9375,584,Intern: Financial Data Analyst,EquipmentShare,"Columbia, MO","EquipmentShare is Hiring an Financial Data Analyst Intern.EquipmentShare is searching for a student intern to join the data analyst team at our Home Office in Columbia, Mo for the 2023 summer.

Your Opportunity to Grow With UsWith 40 interns in 20 different departments in our most recent class, the opportunities to grow with EquipmentShare span far outside traditional construction industry... roles.

Our mission is to build the future of construction, and educate and train interns who have the potential to join our team full-time and help us grow. EquipmentShare has a robust internship program that gives students hands-on opportunities to work and learn in a team environment. Our program equips students with various resources to help shape them into young professionals. From one-on-one mentoring to group education sessions, we are dedicated to investing in the next generation of innovators.

EquipmentShare interns are part of the close-knit group of professionals who all share an interest in providing services and products that improve our customers’ experiences. Our talented and passionate team uses its skills to help interns develop professionally and contribute to our mission. Above all, we care about building something people want, and are looking for interns who share the same passion.

We’re seeking a financial data analyst intern who wants the opportunity to gain professional experience with a rapidly-growing company. The opportunity for growth is unparalleled at EquipmentShare – where you’ll get the chance to build new skills and trailblaze a path to establishing your career.

Responsibilities• Analyze a wide range of data, and turn that data into action, whether that looks like process improvements, best business practices or other data-backed solutions
• Use your strong development and analytical skills to solve business problems across the company
• Produce reports and models for senior leaders and other key team members
• Identify trends, correlations and patterns in data, and present findings to stakeholder
• Perform statistical analysis, predictive and explanatory modeling, and data mining

About You

• Must be qualified to work in the United States - we are not sponsoring any candidates at this time.
• Studying to achieve a bachelor's degree in Statistics, Business Analytics, Economics, Computer Science, Mathematics, or Accounting/Finance or related field
• Expert-level Excel skills
• SQL experience preferred
• Knowledge of an analytical language like Python, R, SAS, SPSS, etc. preferred
• Working knowledge of financial data: forecasting, reporting, and analysis experience, a keen understanding of financial statements and financial data
• Ability to swiftly extract key insights from data
• Proven ability to approach complex problems with curiosity and an analytical mindset
• Eagerness to learn
• Proactive
• Self-Sufficient
• Great communication skills
• You roll with the punches and can adapt quickly, manage competing projects and challenge the status quo

Why We’re a Better Place to WorkEquipmentShare interns have the opportunity to enjoy many perks while working at our Home Office, including:

• Hot breakfast and lunch provided daily
• Healthy snacks, drinks and unlimited coffee bar
• On-site fitness center and group fitness classes
• Weekly professional development sessions
• Mentor and intern happy hours
• End-of-program celebration

About EquipmentShare

Together with our customers and employees, EquipmentShare is building the future of construction by creating a connected jobsite for the modern contractor. We deliver user-friendly solutions that help contractors maximize their equipment uptime, reduce risk exposure and increase productivity. EquipmentShare’s product offerings include an improved equipment rental experience and our T3 technology that encompasses fleet tracking and asset management software, hardware security solutions and predictive service and maintenance applications.

EquipmentShare is the fastest growing, independently-owned construction solutions and equipment rental company in the country. We serve dozens of markets across the U.S., and are building a national footprint in every major market in the country. Our 120+ branch locations are equipped with a wide variety of construction equipment, ranging from 150-foot telescopic booms to 120,000-pound track excavators. Our expansion and customer retention validate the strong contractor demand for the smart jobsite technology we’ve built into our rental fleet. And it’s just the beginning of our journey to establishing a global presence.

EquipmentShare is proud to be a Workplace for All that employs people from all backgrounds and walks of life. We combine the construction and technology sectors to create something incredible – which includes our unmatched work environment. EquipmentShare is a People First company where high tech meets hard work that’s fulfilled by passionate people who have the grit to solve some of the toughest challenges. Prioritizing health and wellness is how we set our employees up for success, both in and out of the workplace. Our team members are also committed to building and bettering the communities we serve through 16 hours of Volunteer Time Off (VTO) and using our giving-back budget to focus on helping those most in need across the country.

Since our founding in 2014 and incorporation in 2015, we’ve had explosive growth — and we’re not stopping anytime soon. Ready to support our mission, invest in yourself and discover your potential? Then we’d love to meet you. Apply today.

