Company Description

Utilimarc is leading the industry in business intelligence solutions for enterprise fleets. We work closely with our customers to ensure their data is actionable and reliable to inform sustainable change within their organization. 22 years of industry experience working with diverse data silos from the nation’s largest utility fleets has driven us to develop our BI platform that connects and unifies fleet data sources into a single environment - expressed through our Fleet Analytics, Benchmarking and Fleet Lifecycle applications. An important layer to Utilimarc’s BI platform - and key to its success - is our people. Our team of data scientists and fleet analysts work closely with our customers building custom scheduled reports and dashboards specific to their needs. Unifying data sources empowers our customers to have a true understanding of the performance and utilization of their fleet assets. Utilimarc is headquartered in Minneapolis with remote teams around the world, currently working alongside North America’s highest performing fleet organizations. For more information visit www.utilimarc.com",2022-02-06,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['snowflake', 'tableau', 'sql', 'looker', 'redshift']"
9389,598,Medical Data Analyst,Classic Westchester,United States,"Job Description

Position Summary: Responsible for data management integrity and reporting for all Electronic Health Records and Practice Management data systems. This individual will support and maintain various data reporting systems including but not limited to: eClinicalWorks, eBO, Epic/SlicerDicer, Ahlers & NYS Family Planning Program...

The Clinical Data Analyst will provide technical, operational and end-user support and is responsible for data collection, integrity and analysis, reporting integrity and analysis, and management of practice related information, including demographic, clinical, statistical and financial data. This position works closely and collaborates with the Director, Revenue Cycle and VP, Information Technology & Facilities Infrastructure to ensure that practice management software is configured optimally and maintained on a current basis, and to improve and optimize data capture and related billing, reporting and benchmarking activities.

The position will also assist in day-to-day administration and support of the eCW application and related software maintenance and upgrades on an ongoing basis and participate in upgrades and new project role outs on an as needed basis.

Essential Functions:
