9411,620,"Senior Data Analyst, Oracle CX Marketing",Oracle,"Oklahoma City, OK","Job Description

Oracle CX Marketing has an exciting opportunity for a Senior Data Analyst...

This is a remote role based anywhere in the US

About the Opportunity

Explore, innovate and develop digital data insights to help Oracle CX Marketing clients leverage the power of email marketing and digital orchestration to drive new customer acquisition, engagement and conversion opportunities. This highly visible role requires a unique combination of skills, experience and marketing acumen.

Responsibilities

What You Will Do

This position reports to the Manager, Analytics & Strategic Services and will work with the team to build and utilize the following skills:
• Reporting Insights. Reports are just another way for you to tell a story (only with data). Youre passionate about translating the data into easy-to-understand visualizations to help you weave a compelling story that helps your customers understand and take action based on your analysis.
• Analytics Acumen. You love working with data and related tools. PivotTables are just the beginning for you as you also understand relational databases and enjoy honing your SQL or similar skills.
• Idea Generation. Identify new opportunities for digital offerings on our team. Spot ways to automate processes and gain efficiencies (and then do it!). Were a team of independent thinkers if someone on the team has an idea, they can pitch it and help make it happen.
• Figure It Out Mentality. Even if youve never done something before, youre comfortable figuring it out. Quickly.
• Team Player. You enjoy working with a smart, entrepreneurial team and fast-growing company to drive impressive results for awesome customers.
What You Will Bring ( requirements)
• Bachelors Degree required.
• Proficiency in Excel required.
• Experience with SQL preferred.
• Experience with R and Python preferred.
• 4-7 years of experience with at least 2 years digital data analytics with large digital data sets (e.g. display, social, web, email, mobile, social, etc.). Experience in consulting capacity preferred.
• Proven experience using your digital marketing analytics skills to identify customer behavior insights and translating data analysis into actionable marketing recommendations and presentations.
• PowerPoint proficiency is required.
• Strong listening and relationship building skills are important.
• High intellectual curiosity, drive, determination, self-confidence and persuasion skills.
• Consulting/agency experience preferred.
• Location flexible but must be within the U.S.
An experienced consulting professional who has a broad understanding of solutions, industry best practices, multiple business processes or technology designs within a product/technology family.

