9427,636,Business Data Analyst II,E Source,United States,"Job Description

Do you love digging into data and bringing actionable insights to life? Can you see trends when you look at numbers? If so, we want you to join our team as E Source’s newest data analyst...

We’re looking for a data analyst who is a problem-solver at heart. We’re looking for someone who is tech-savvy, skilled at finding connections in data, comes to meetings with solutions (not just information), and can ask the big questions to understand what’s missing in a process so we can build better data architecture. This person will join our expanded business intelligence team, building data products for utility clients as well as driving the use of data-driven decision-making across ESource.

E Source is a solutions-based consulting, research and advisory, and data science firm that’s been a change agent in the utility industry for over 30 years.

What you’ll do:
• Partner with utility clients and internal stakeholders to understand business problems and translate those to user stories to be implemented by the team
• Use various data sources to build reports and dashboards that help us provide the best insights to our utility clients and internal stakeholders
• Understand and document the full life cycle of data so it can be efficiently integrated, modeled, and analyzed
• Collaborate with data engineers to define data models and transformations to build sustainable data pipelines for reporting
• Collaborate with data scientists to bring predictive insights to life through interactive dashboards

What will make you a good fit:
• BS or MS in management information systems, computer programming, software engineering, data science, or an equivalent STEM field
• At least two years of relevant professional engineering or analytics experience
• The ability to explore data to extract key insights sourced from a variety of sources including SQL databases, document databases, RESTful Web Services, CSV files, and JSON documents
• Strong analytical skills and the ability to troubleshoot and resolve data issues
• Proven success in communicating ideas, telling stories, and providing recommendations through effective visualization of data
• Experience in Microsoft Power BI, including Power BI data modeling and DAX code
• Experience with SQL, data structures, and databases
• Experience interactively exploring data using languages like Python
• Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written

A little about ESource

Since 1986, ESource has focused on partnering with utilities to help their customers save electricity. That novel approach defined the art of electric end-use efficiency—better known as energy efficiency. We’ve expanded that concept to include a broader perspective of sustainability for utilities that deliver electricity, natural gas, and water.

We work to enhance relationships with the people utilities serve, achieve the next generation of savings, and lead the carbon-reduction effort. We help utilities think differently, make data useful, and learn from the best strategies across the industry. Our people, our insights, and our network help our clients and give them the assurance that the programs they implement are the most effective.

Benefits
• We offer excellent insurance packages, including medical, dental, and vision plans; company-paid life insurance; company-paid long- and short-term disability insurance; and medical and dependent-care flexible spending plans.
• We provide a flexible time off (FTO) program; E Source employees can take as many paid days off per year as they need, with manager approval, while fulfilling their work obligations and ensuring proper coverage of their responsibilities.
• We offer flexible schedules, flexible work locations, and a paid parental leave benefit.
• We provide a 401(k) plan with a 3% employer match.

The budgeted salary for this position is $65,100 TO $89,250+ (INCLUDES BASE + ANNUAL BONUS). Actual pay will be adjusted based on experience.

This person can work remote, a hybrid schedule, or from one of our physical office locations.

Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the US. We’re unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment visas at this time.

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.

