WaterEquity is a purpose-driven company with a culture of innovation. Additional information about WaterEquity is available at _.

Summary

WaterEquity is seeking an Investment Data Analyst who will provide portfolio monitoring and analytical support for the Investment Management team. The role will work closely with a global team to manage and analyze financial, operational, and impact data for WaterEquity's investments. The role is an excellent opportunity for an early career professional with a passion for social impact, a keen eye for detail, strong analytical skills, and comfortable with change. WaterEquity currently manages a portfolio of nearly 50 investments and is growing quickly. Our growing business provides unique opportunities for professional growth. Responsibilities may be expanded to accommodate WaterEquity's strategic priorities and the evolution of the team and this role.

Job Responsibilities

Track investee reporting requirements to ensure compliance with loan agreements
Load reported data into portfolio management software and update data from various external sources
Track country and currency risk data for countries where we have investments or are considering making investments
Analyze financial, operational, and impact data from investees to identify risks and understand trends
Build proactive data validation automation to catch data integrity issues
Manage and maintain datasets, perform data validation/quality assurance analysis for datasets within and across a variety of platforms, including eFront and Salesforce
Serve as a Salesforce administrator and power user for the Investment Management team, including creating new fields, editing page layouts, managing data quality, creating reports, etc.
Cross-collaborate with other departments and understand their data requirements and needs and create useful tools to improve the business process workflow and financial initiatives
Special projects and wider support to the team as needed and determined by Director, Portfolio Management and Risk

Skills and Qualifications

