Benefits : A comprehensive benefits package is available for full-time employees after 60 days of employment, including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. Paid Time Off accrues for all employees beginning with their start date. Employees are eligible for our retirement (401k) benefits after 90 days of employment. Full-time CRMLS employees are expected to work 37.5 hours each week with the opportunity for periodic overtime.

Position Summary: The Data Quality Analyst is an expert in the technical works of MLS data systems, services and support. This is a vital role in the onboarding and data quality maintenance of CRMLS and Datashare systems. Their deep understanding of the MLS operations and data practices are important in order to evaluate and identify data trends to create improvement opportunities. The Data Quality Analyst is also responsible for interfacing with our vendors, call center and other internal departments on data related issues; they will assist with documenting, troubleshooting, resolving those issues. This role will also educate and provide coaching to internal staff on data quality controls and measures to achieve long term results.

Duties & Responsibilities :

Handles data related issues from the IT Services Queue (ITSQ)

Manage the resolution performance of our product vendors and data partners

