9524,733,Data Analyst - ATC,World Wide Technology,Anywhere,"Data Analyst - ATC

Why WWT...

Fueled by creativity and ideation, World Wide Technology strives to accelerate our growth and nurture future innovation. From our world class culture, to our generous benefits, to developing cutting edge technology solutions, WWT constantly works towards its mission of creating a profitable growth company that is a great place to work. We encourage our employees to embrace collaboration, get creative and think outside the box when it comes to delivering some of the most advanced technology solutions for our customers.

We have remained successful and continue to grow through the recent difficult economic conditions. We strive to build a profitable, growth company that’s also a great place to work. With this as our goal we offer a highly competitive benefits package and opportunities for professional development.

At a glance, WWT was founded in 1990 in St. Louis, Missouri. We employ over 8,000 individuals and closed nearly $14 Billion in revenue. We have an inclusive culture and believe our core values are the key to company and employee success. WWT is proud to announce that it has been named on the FORTUNE ""100 Best Places to Work For®"" list for the eleventh consecutive year!

Want to work with highly motivated individuals that come together to form high performance team? Come join WWT today!

Job Summary

A Data Analyst of the Advanced Technology Center is responsible for creating reporting and analytics to support the ATC organization and users across the business that consume its services. The Data Analyst is responsible for having a data-driven mindset and using this mindset to develop solutions that will aid their department’s leadership in decision-making, learning, and business analysis. The Data Analyst is responsible for becoming proficient in ATC data and processes to best serve their stakeholders with valuable and relevant analytical solutions that aid in simplifying the complex and promoting data-driven decision-making.

Responsibilities
• Develop an understanding of ATC operational processes and the data required to develop analytic solutions to support the business
• Understand the data structure supporting ATC applications to communicate between the business and development teams effectively
• Work in conjunction with the business stakeholders to gather and document requirements
• Design and Present analytical solutions that represent the data in a meaningful way using Tableau, ServiceNow, and PowerBi
• Maximize report adoption by Training end users on how to use tools, and answer any questions on reporting and data
• Collaborate with internal customers to meet and exceed their expectations
• Innovate within various analytical platforms to provide quality solutions to the business
• Show a passion for learning and seek certifications as desired for continuous professional improvements
• Supports production issues with reporting and data
• Identify areas of poor data quality and educate respective teams to improve data quality, integrity, and reporting capabilities
• Responsible for testing and validating new data sources, reports, reporting tools, etc.
• Work with IT Data Teams to ensure data integrity and report performance
• Identify areas where a process change will be required to support a reporting need and works with management to implement it
• Monitor internal and external customer support requests when necessary

Education

Bachelor’s Degree required

Work Experience

1-3 years of work experience in a related field preferred

Specialized Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
• Proficiency in reporting and data visualization using Tableau, Amplitude, PowerBi, and ServiceNow
• Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and Outlook
• Ability to work in a fast-paced and deadline-driven environment
• Thoughtful problem-solving skills to meet or exceed goals
• Passion for data and the processes that support it
• Strive for continuous improvement personally and professionally

The well-being of WWT employees is essential. So, when it comes to our benefits package, WWT has one of the best. We offer the following benefits to all full-time employees:
• Health and Wellbeing: Heath, Dental, and Vision Care, Onsite Health Centers, Employee Assistance Program, Wellness program
• Financial Benefits: Competitive pay, Profit Sharing, 401k Plan with Company Matching, Life and Disability Insurance, Tuition Reimbursement
• Paid Time Off: PTO & Holidays, Parental Leave, Sick Leave, Military Leave, Bereavement
• Additional Perks: Nursing Mothers Benefits, Voluntary Legal, Pet Insurance, Employee Discount Program

Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion is more than a commitment at WWT -- it is the foundation of what we do. Through diverse networks and pipelines, we have a clear vision: to create a Great Place to Work for All. We believe inclusion includes U.

Be who U are at WWT!

Equal Opportunity Employer Minorities/Women/Veterans/Differently abled

Some WWT customers have a COVID-19 vaccine requirement. In order to work on projects for these customers, employees must be fully vaccinated or have an appropriate religious or medical accommodation.

