9551,760,Data Analyst,Standleys Systems Llc,"Chickasha, OK","Standleys Systems Llc is now hiring Data Analyst in Oklahoma City, OK 73170. View job listing details and apply now.

Job Title: Data Analyst...

Department: IT Operations

Reports To: IT Operations Manager

FLSA Status: Exempt

Updated: January 11, 2022

Company Profile

To businesses across Oklahoma, Standley means technology. Founded in 1934 as the Fred Standley Typewriter Company in Chickasha, Oklahoma, Standley Systems has continually evolved to remain on the forefront of office technology while maintaining our personal touch. We are currently in our fourth generation as a family-owned, Oklahoma business, serving all 77 Oklahoma counties. We deliver local connectivity and limitless opportunity.

By partnering with Standley Systems, our clients gain a relationship committed to helping them improve their business. From IT and printing solutions to business transformation services, our team focuses on improving our clients productivity, maximizing security, and increasing efficiency. It is our top priority to continue to build a legacy of legendary relationships. We think of our clients as more than just clients and truly want to do what is right by them.

Position Profile

Standley Systems is looking for a skilled Data Analyst to leverage available data, documentation, and expertise to foster a more profitable, relevant, and sustainable operating model. This individual will be responsible for providing ad hoc and recurring reports based off disparate data sources.

The ideal candidate will have experience with T-SQL, Data Profiling, Data Warehousing, and/or ETL (whether using SQL Integration Services, Azure Data Factory, Azure Integration Runtime, etc.).

Primary Responsibilities
• Fully embrace Standley Systems core values
• Understand key business processes that create and utilize key data elements
• Understand data dependencies between teams and ensure processes to share data between teams are documented, repeatable, and reliable
• Manage routine bulk data loads including synchronization between key business systems
• Design the process and facilitate the discussion to define data quality rules
• Collaborate with data owners in developing data metrics and reports to effectively monitor and promote data quality
• Validate and/or cleanse data to ensure reliable output (visuals, dashboards, reports)
• Resolve discrepancies between data to ensure one source of truth
• Develop dataset processes to facilitate analysis of data
• Gather and clarify reporting and analytics requirements for business units
• Develop and maintain reports for departments and upper management to provide perspective, insight, clarity and towards defined business cases
• Conceptualize, propose, design, build, and deliver reporting on key initiatives
• Promote a culture of treating data as an asset organization-wide
• Facilitate discussions with key stakeholders to create and maintain a reliable business data glossary

Qualifications

To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed in following are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.

Technology Skills
• Knowledge of and experience with Extract Transform Load (ETL) processes leveraging APIs, Microsoft SQL Server Instances (On Premises and Azure) required
• Expertise with reporting and analytics tools such as Microsoft Report Builder, Microsoft SQL Server Reporting Services, SAS, Tableau, R, Crystal Reports, and/or Microsoft Power BI required
• Development and Support experience with the Microsoft Power Platform required

Education and/or Experience
• Bachelors degree in applicable field or equivalent experience required
• Experience integrating Line of Business Applications with up/downstream applications preferred
• Prior experience managing and maintaining Sales/ERP data preferred

Certificates, Licenses, and Registrations
• Certifications for reporting and analytics tools preferred
• Database certification preferred, such as MTA, MCP, MCSA or MCSE

Other Skills and Abilities
• Must effectively translate business requirements into data and output requirements
• Self-starter willing to take initiative to identify, define, document, and deliver projects in a reasonable time frame required

Physical Requirements
