9687,896,Data Analyst,CommScope,"Tulsa, OK","In our always on' world, we believe it's essential to have a genuine connection with the work you do.

Does turning data into information, information into insight, and insight into business decisions excite you? We are looking to add a Data Analyst to our team to help develop analyses and reporting capabilities. You will monitor performance and quality to identify improvements present findings... to the management team in a concise and informative format while providing analysis of key KPI indicators and trending. How You'll Help Us Connect the World:

As a Data Analyst, you will do more than collecting and analyzing data. You will also ensure our data is accessible to those who need the information and is presented in a format that streamlines business processes. Accuracy and completeness of data is of the highest importance from this role. Other day-to-day activities of the role may include:
• Using data mining to extract information from data sets and identify correlations and patterns.
• Organizing and transforming information into comprehensible structures.
• Using data to predict trends in the customer base and the consumer population as a whole.
• Performing statistical analysis of data.
• Using tools and techniques to visualize data in easy-to-understand formats, such as diagrams and graphs in a repeatable and consistent manner.
• Must be able to duplicate or replicate the analysis as necessary.
• Using statistical tools to interpret data sets, paying particular attention to trends and patterns that could be valuable for indicative and predictive analytics efforts.
• Understand and track key KPI indicators, both internal and external, to validate compliance and trending.
• Work with Team leadership to understand organizational processes and procedures and ensure Reporting and Dashboards provided reinforce the standards expected of the Support Teams.
• Monitoring data quality and providing recommendations for improvements to data integrity.
• Communicating with stakeholders to understand data content and business requirements.
• Working with MSD Dynamics and Power BI to create and deliver reports, automated subscriptions and dashboards to identify trends and statistics
• To work with Google Analytics tool to export data into PowerBI as additional data reporting metrics as required
• Collaborate within the Business Innovation Team's Reporting group to field new requests, manage revision requests, plan development, and execute on deliverables.
• Maintain the departmental Power BI datasets, dashboards, and reports to meet operational and customer requirements. Minimum Qualifications:

Bachelor's degree from an accredited university or college in mathematics, statistics, computer science, economics or analytics You Will Excite Us If You Have:
• Ability to work with stakeholders to assess potential risks.
• Ability to analyze existing tools and databases and provide software solution recommendations
• Ability to translate business requirements into non-technical, lay terms
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy
• High-level written and verbal communication skills
• Experienced with Microsoft Dynamics, Excel, and Power BI
• Experience with Google Analytics a plus
• In-depth knowledge of statistical methodologies and data analysis techniques
• Strong attention to detail and ability to effectively prioritize

Perks & Benefits: The candidate will be rewarded with a comprehensive benefits package, including paid vacation, medical, dental, and vision plans, life and accidental death insurance, a 401(k) plan, and participation in the Company's Annual Incentive Plan. This position also benefits from eligibility to participate in CommScope's Long-Term Incentive Plan ( LTIP ), as approved by CommScope's Compensation Committee.

For candidates located in the states that require compensation listed in the job description, the anticipated salary range is dependent on experience and qualifications: $67,000 - $83,700 Why CommScope:

CommScope is on a quest to deliver connectivity that empowers how we live, work, and learn. Our employees push the boundaries of communications technology that enables game-changing discoveries like 5G, the Internet of Things, and gigabit speeds for everyone, everywhere. With our unmatched expertise in copper, fiber, and wireless infrastructure, our global clients rely on us to outperform today and be ready for the needs of tomorrow.

If you want to grow your career alongside bright, passionate, and caring people who strive to create what's next come connect to your future at CommScope.

CommScope is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EEO), including people with disabilities and veterans. If you are seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process, please contact us to submit your request at talentacquisition@commscope.com. You can also learn more about CommScope's accommodation process and EEO policy at careers.commscope.com/eeo

