9694,903,Senior Data Analyst,realtor.com,United States (+2 others),"About the job

We have the most comprehensive and accurate coverage of real estate listings and the most engaged users across all the online real estate portals. Our mission is to make buying, selling, renting, and living in homes easier and more rewarding for everyone...

The Data Analytics team at http://realtor.com sits at the heart of this mission. We process and analyze terabytes of data every day that enable decisions for millions of home buyers, sellers, renters, dreamers, and real estate professionals. Our goal is to use this data to make the home-buying experience a breeze for our consumers. We empower them with the most up-to-date information on properties, help them find their dream homes in the least amount of time, and match them with the most suitable realtor to meet their unique, individual needs.

The Role: We’re looking for the best data and analytical minds to help lead a variety of our biggest efforts. Real estate is the largest asset class in the world and we have the best data and visibility into that market. As a member of the Data Analytics team, not only will you be building sophisticated tools, insights, and models, but also you will serve as a trusted advisor to surface data-driven insights to our Finance and Revenue teams. Therefore, we want hands-on executors/do-ers/owners who also possess a strategic, business-oriented mindset.

What will you do?

Responsibilities
• Support the Finance and Revenue organizations at Realtor.com in their analytic and reporting needs
• Apply thought leadership in the application of analytic and statistical methodologies to solve business problems
• Drive insights through rigorous analysis and translate them into strategic recommendations for stakeholders in the Finance and Revenue organizations.
• Collaborate with stakeholders and peers on experimentation ideas, finalize hypotheses, design experiments, synthesize results, and make recommendations based on experiment outcomes.
• Collaborate with teammates to continually enhance and optimize team processes and operating norms.

What will you bring?

Requirements
• Bachelor’s Degree in a business-related or quantitative field
• 5+ years of experience as a Data Scientist, Data Analyst, Business Analyst or similar role
• Experience as an “analytic consultant” highly preferred, with a background in providing data driven recommendations that impact business decisions
• SQL fluency with experience using a scripting language like Python or R.
• Experience building dashboards and using data visualization tools. Tableau experience is preferred.
• Strategic mindset that enables one to learn how the Finance and Revenue organizations operate, understand their pain points and opportunities, and deliver data driven recommendations that drive business value.
• Strong communication skills to effectively communicate complex information and strategies to non-technical audiences.

realtor.com focuses on SaaS, Real Estate, and Consumer. Their company has offices in Austin, Vancouver, and Santa Clara. They have a very large team that's between 1001-5000 employees.

