9696,905,Senior Data Analyst - Web Analytics - UpNest,realtor.com,United States (+2 others),"About us:

Realtor.com®, a leading online destination for real estate services, this role will align with the UpNest team, the newest addition to the realtor.com® network. UpNest (Part of The Realtor.com Network) is an innovative realtor marketplace connecting home buyers and sellers with highly qualified local agents who compete for their business...

The Role

Do you love writing SQL queries, building charts and analyzing data in a database? Do you like to try out new apps and new websites? If you want to pursue your professional interests as you help grow an innovative real estate tech company, this work is for you. In this role you will partner closely with product management and help shape our product. Join us as our newest Data Analyst and help change the world of real estate, one home at a time.

Who you are:

You understand how funnel conversions work and you like to find out why the flow is built in such a way. You are a self-starter with a desire to work in a dynamic, startup environment. You have a great memory and can multi-task. You are organized, good at taking notes and good with Excel. You can follow instructions but also be able to execute with minimal supervision.

What you’ll do:
• Support the Product team in accomplishing the goals and objectives of the Consumer internet businesses.
• Develop and monitor KPIs to drive high-level oversight of business initiatives and company health, and develop regular insights from the data to enable performance management and facilitate accountability.
• Deliver high-quality data-driven business analyses that address business issues with effective solutions, and provide key insights leading to actionable recommendations.
• Partner with the Product organization on data-driven decision making, idea generation, and rigorous measurement.
• Lead exploratory analysis to identify and size product development opportunities to determine tradeoffs between product features that grow and optimize the product offering.
• Develop product learning agendas, design multivariate tests, and synthesize analytical results into practical recommendations that inform key business decisions.
• Partner with the engineering and business intelligence teams to drive improvements to tracking and data quality.
• Conduct deep-dive analyses to understand product performance, conduct complex initiatives that address key strategic questions and drive assorted ad hoc projects.
• Inform OKR development with product leadership.

What you’ll bring:
• Educational Requirements: BA/BS with undergraduate focus in Analytics, Finance, Statistics, Applied Math, Data Science, Economics or related field. Masters a plus. Differentiator: experience within real estate tech, real estate builder communities, market research and/or B2B sales.
• 5+ years' experience with increasing levels of responsibility; online media / consumer audience-oriented / consumer internet experience a plus.
• Strong analytical, critical thinking, decision-making and problem-solving skills.
• Experience in digital tools including Omniture and Google Analytics preferred; SQL experience required.
