9708,917,"Senior Analyst, Advanced Analytics, Sales",Airbnb,United States,"Airbnb is a mission-driven company dedicated to helping create a world where anyone can belong anywhere. It takes a unified team committed to our core values to achieve this goal. Airbnb's various functions embody the company's innovative spirit and our fast-moving team is committed to leading as a 21st century company.

The Location...

This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. Airbnb,Inc. can employ in states where we have registered entities. Currently, employees can not be located in: Alaska, Indiana, Nebraska, North Dakota, Ohio, South Dakota, Wisconsin, Alabama, Mississippi, Oklahoma, Delaware and Rhode Island. This list is continuously evolving and being updated, please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list. If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states yoau are eligible to work from.

Role Summary

We are looking for a Senior Analyst in the Advanced Analytics team to help Airbnb enable travel for our millions of guests and hosts on our platform. This role will support the Sales Organization.

Role Responsibilities
• Data thought partner to business leaders across marketplace teams through providing insights, recommendations, and enabling data informed decisions.
• Create Sales & Marketing Data tools
• Develop a deep understanding of how Airbnb can acquire new hosts or new guests, and set them up for success, through structured and unstructured data sources.
• Partner closely with Business leads to design, execute and evaluate A/B tests. Understand common pitfalls and caveats when designing and evaluating results.
• Define how to best measure the performance of Airbnb product and business through new metrics and dimensions - align on definitions with the business (evaluating tradeoffs and defining guardrails), and prototype metrics through custom data pipelines.
• Empower the team to answer data questions quickly and easily by building high-quality ground truth data sets and dashboards. Collaborate with Product Engineering to spec out logging and with Analytics Engineering to build data tools for mass consumptions within Airbnb.
• Contribute towards advancing the Analytics and Data Science disciplines at Airbnb, including driving data best practices such as improving and automating analytical processes, building new data tools and data sets, data education around the company and mentoring and developing others.

Role Qualifications
• 3+ years in industry experience and a degree (Masters or PhD is a plus) in a quantitative field (e.g., Statistics, Econometrics, Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Operations Research).
• Expert communication and collaboration skills with the ability to work effectively with internal teams in a cross-cultural and cross-functional environment. Ability to conduct rigorous analysis and communicate conclusions to both technical and non-technical audiences
• Experience partnering with internal teams to drive action and providing expertise and direction on analytics, data science, experimental design, and measurement
• Experience in analysis of A|B experiments and statistical data analysis
• Experience designing and building metrics, from conception to building prototypes with data pipelines
• Strong knowledge in at least one programming language (Python or R) and in SQL
• Ability to drive data strategies, with a central source of truth to impact business decisions

The Pay

Our job titles may span more than one career level. The starting base pay for this role is between $118,000 and $148,000. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: education, experience, and skills. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.

Belonging & Accommodation

Airbnb is committed to working with the best and brightest people from the broadest talent pool possible. We believe a diversity of ideas fosters innovation and engagement, and allows us to attract the best people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. If you need assistance, or a reasonable accommodation during the application and recruiting process, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com",2022-11-22,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'sql', 'r']"
9709,918,Business Intelligence Analyst,Lime,United States,"Lime is the world's largest shared electric vehicle company. We’re on a mission to build a future where transportation is shared, affordable and carbon-free. Named a Time 100 Most Influential Company in 2021, Lime has powered 350+ million electric bike and scooter rides in 200+ cities on 5 continents, saving an estimated 75+ million car trips. Learn more about how we help the world #RideGreen at... li.me!

This role is a fantastic opportunity for a Business Intelligence professional with great communication and data skills, and a track record of work experience in Business Intelligence, Analytics, or Insight - preferably in Operations related roles - to join the Global Business Intelligence team at Lime.

What You’ll Do:
• Own projects end to end: define requirements, scope milestones, and timeline, project manage data and other relevant teams, track and report efficiently progress to team lead and effectively communicate to stakeholders.
• Develop impactful BI solutions using SQL, Snowflake, Tableau, Python, Google sheet/ Excel.
• Analyze data and draw actionable insights to enable decision-making for Operations teams.
• Define and document KPIs with Central and Local operations teams.
• Be a key contributor to the team's growth and success: set up best BI and Data best practices in the organization and constantly strive to raise standards.

About You:
• You aim to be an expert on how Business Intelligence can help the business thrive.
• You love interacting with multiple teams and stakeholders.
• You are analytically minded and have a roll up your sleeves attitude: you enjoy wrangling with data, creating dashboards, and delivering analysis and insights to other teams.
• Prioritization, problem-solving, data analysis, and data visualization are second nature to you.
• You have a Degree in Engineering, Data Science, Mathematics, or Economics from a top-tier university/ Business school.
• You have at least 5 years of work experience, with over 3 years working in a Business Intelligence, Analytics, or Insight role in a fast pace environment (Scale-up / Top consulting firm).
• You have an outstanding level of numerical and analytical thinking with a very logical approach.
• You are advanced at SQL, Google sheet, EXCEL, Tableau, and JIRA and have used these technologies on a daily basis in your role(s).
• You are passionate about the ability of BI to change a business and how numbers can be transformed into key insights.
• You are proactive, autonomous, and a true team player.
• You have excellent interpersonal and communication skills with both technical and non-technical individuals.

The anticipated salary range for this position is $82,000.00 - $119,000.00. Equity and benefits may be provided as part of the compensation package, depending on the position offered. Not all candidates will be eligible for the upper end of the salary range. Exact salary will ultimately depend on multiple factors, which may include the successful candidate's skills, experience and other qualifications as well as the candidate's location of residence. In addition to base salary, some roles may be eligible for a variable bonus based on a combination of company performance, employee performance, and management discretion.

