• Developing, and maintaining ongoing metrics, reports, data mining, analyses, dashboards, etc. that drive meaningful and prompt actionable insights
• Documenting and presenting key drivers of business results as well as go forward action plans through reports and presentations
• proactively recommending process improvement opportunities to leadership
• Be responsible for carrying out complex analysis of key Human Resources datasets and conducting appropriate data validation for the Human Resources organization
• Define people data performance indicators and deliver metrics, reporting platforms, dashboards, and analytical models vital for collecting data backed insights as well as tracking and managing our business
• Provide information on analytic results to Human Resource business and functional leaders using visualizations to communicate data and metrics
• Spot vital insights and develop the framework for reporting HR data analytics
• provide direction on maintaining databases through identifying data integrity / data conflict issues and recommended steps toward remediation.
• maintain appropriate documentation and reference materials around business intelligence solutions and systems.
• Facilitate the computerization of analytics and data collection processes for Human Resources
• Support Human Resources business intelligence strategies with quantitative and qualitative data analytics
• Identify HR business challenges and provide active support to leadership on completing process improvement projects
• Work cross-departmentally on data-driven strategies that improve business processes and decision-making
