9903,1112,"Sr.Manager, Healthcare Data Analytics",Cricket Health,Anywhere,"Interwell Health is a kidney care management company that partners with physicians on its mission to reimagine healthcare—with the expertise, scale, compassion, and vision to set the standard for the industry and help patients live their best lives. We are on a mission to help people and we know the work we do changes their lives. If there is a better way, we will create it. So, if our mission... speaks to you, join us!

Interwell Health is looking for a Sr. Manager to join our healthcare Data Analytics team and take over responsibility for managing the dev team that builds data-driven products to improve clinical outcomes for our patients. Our ideal candidate will be an experienced self-starter who can hit the ground running as an independent contributor writing SQL code, while working in parallel to manage a team of healthcare data analysts and engineers in partnership with a data product manager. Your primary responsibility as a dev team lead will be to manage “quality” and “velocity” within your data development team by ensuring that high quality analyses are packaged up and delivered to your internal customers in a timely manner. To succeed in this role you will need to work closely with your Cricket colleagues and with our payor and provider partners to source requirements, plan and structure analytics projects, understand base datasets, review detailed analytic plans, quality check code / results, and communicate key insights using Looker, Excel, and PowerPoint. You will also need to master the ontologies and clinical data definitions related to Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) including disease staging, dialysis modality codes, hospital / ER admits, and transplant procedure codes. Ultimately, as a technical dev lead your goal will be to oversee data-driven projects that distill messy, complex datasets down into meaningful insights to help Interwell Health improve the lives of our patients.

Primary Responsibilities
• Grow and manage a data team responsible for understanding Cricket’s impact on health outcomes and building data products to provide world class kidney care
• As an independent contributor, write and review SQL code to clean and analyze different healthcare datasets, including medical claims, prescription claims, electronic health record (EHR), etc.
• As a team lead, oversee data coding quality and velocity for a team of healthcare data developers, building in the necessary quality control checks so that ad-hoc dev work becomes more scalable over time
• Translate technical challenges and learnings to data product managers and stakeholders to set expectations and plan milestones and deadlines
• Build, QC, and publish performance measurement dashboards that track health outcomes over time using Business Intelligence (BI) software such as Looker
• Build data-driven presentations that translate complex data analyses into crisp insights with clear recommendations, and present your work directly to C-suit
• Communicate within Cricket cross-functionally to make sure the broader Cricket team is aware of any data roadblocks and understands key learnings and takeaways.
• Oversee the development of complex clinical data definitions using clinical ontologies such as ICD-10, CPT, SNOMED, LOINC, NDC, etc.
• Iterate on code bases to streamline query efficiency and automate future work using source code control systems (e.g. Bitbucket) to manage the code development process

Required Qualifications
• 5+ years of healthcare data analytics experience (claims, EHR, Rx, etc.)
• Experience building and leading a team of data analysts and managing healthcare data projects end-to-end
• ExcellentSQL coding skills
• Strong data visualization dev skills using Looker, Qlik, Tableau, and/or R Shiny
• Excellent attention to detail
• The ability to work across multiple projects in a fast-paced environment
• Excellent written, presentation, and verbal communication skills
• Passion for Cricket Health’s mission

