9915,1124,Data Analyst,EMS - Tyler,"Tulsa, OK","Overview

Join our Utica Park Clinic team as a Data Analyst...

Hillcrest HealthCare System (HHS) is a comprehensive health system providing quality healthcare in northeastern Oklahoma, with the system’s flagship hospital, Hillcrest Medical Center, located in Tulsa. Additionally, HHS is comprised of Bailey Medical Center, Hillcrest Hospital Claremore, Hillcrest Hospital Cushing, Hillcrest Hospital Henryetta, Hillcrest Hospital Pryor, Hillcrest Hospital South, Tulsa Spine & Specialty Hospital, Oklahoma Heart Institute and Utica Park Clinic. HHS has 1,180 licensed beds and an expansive network of clinics.

POSITION SUMMARY

The Data Analyst will provide technical and analytical support to the Population Health activities of Utica Park Clinic and to Hillcrest Healthcare System.

New Report Requests: The Data Analyst is responsible for the creation and production of reports using established reporting protocols. The Data Analyst is responsible for reviewing the report requests assigned to them, communicating with the requestor to understand and clarify any questions regarding the report, evaluating the need for a new report creation or modifying an existing report to meet the requestor’s needs and coordinating the due dates and frequency of the report. Creating the query requested and working with the report requestor and the Manager of Data Analytics to generate the report within the timeframe needed. Data validation based on the criteria provided will be done with the requestor and make any need changes.

Standard Report Production : Routine standard monthly reports will also be assigned and will be posted and distributed as established by protocols. Utilize other associated databases that are adjunct to the EPIC electronic records. Utilize Sharepoint and Teams as a report repository for general access for users. Refine and update reports as required for MIPS reporting.

Position reports to:
• Manager, Data Analytics
• Director, Population Health

Position collaborates with:
• Administrative Staff including the Medical Director for Population Health
• Providers, Clinic Managers, Administrative Directors and Care Management Staff
• Members of the Population Health and Quality Improvement department teams

Responsibilities
• Prepares routine monthly data reports and analysis to support quality data reporting to UPC administration, Population Health and QI department, CMMI programs and other value-based programs as defined payers, and other outside reporting agency requirements.
• Provides data aggregation by providers and format the data in graphic representation to present to the providers and administration on a monthly and quarterly basis. Develop clinical dashboards or other data visualization solutions including clinical, cost, and patient satisfaction data.
• Integrates outside databases such as , Care Everywhere, MyHealth or other HIE, and EPIC EMR. Experience working with large clinical and/or administrative databases, including management and analysis
• Demonstrates analytical and statistical abilities to evaluate data, make judgments, and recommendations regarding quality improvement work, including but not limited to resource utilization, physician practice patterns, and clinical pathway effectiveness.

Qualifications

Education:
• Associate/Bachelors in Analytics or equivalent experience

Experience:
• 2+ years of experience with relational databases (SQL)

Licenses, Registrations, or Certifications:
• Will be required to take and pass Epic Cogito Certification during their first 6 months in the Data Analyst position.

Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:
• Analytical Thinking and Problem Solving
• Data Aggregation and analystis as well as generating graphs to help users
• SQL report writing skills
• Excel - Intermediate to Advanced skills
• Epic EMR knowledge
• HEDIS and CMS Quality metrics",2022-01-04,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sql', 'excel', 'sharepoint']"
9916,1125,"Sr. Analyst, Data Analysis",First National Bank of Omaha,United States,"Introduction
Are you looking for the opportunity to do challenging and meaningful work in an environment that encourages ongoing learning, development and career growth? Do you thrive on making a positive impact in our community? Do you believe a company can elevate the spirit and quality of life for others
...
Overview

At FNBO, our employees are the heart of our story—and we’re committed to their success! Please see below the details of this career opportunity and how it fits into our organization’s success.

Our Modern, Flexible Workplace:

At First National, we believe in a Modern, Flexible Workplace, and we are continuously exploring advancements in technology and office environments to make it easier to work from anywhere at any time, allowing for more flexibility in where and how you work. We know that choice and flexibility are important to you. We also recognize that flexible and remote positions can become opportunities for military partners, caregivers, and individuals with disabilities to thrive at First National. We invite you to consider what a Modern, Flexible Workplace can mean for you!

It is anticipated that an incumbent in this role will work onsite for three (3) or more days a week and will have a dedicated workspace when working onsite. Work location is subject to change based on business needs.

Summary of the Job:

The Sr. Analyst, Data Analysis for Fraud Analytics main role is controlling and minimizing fraud loss debit/credit cards while optimizing the customer experience at the point of sale. The role is responsible for monitoring all card activity, creating and maintaining fraud controls through rule writing, which directly helps to decide all card transactions. This role will work with all card products – Debit, Consumer Credit, Commercial Card and Private Label. The role is a subject matter expert in card fraud. This may include working to extract, manipulate, and summarize large amounts of data to provide business insight and intelligence to assigned business units. This role may require utilization of SAS, SQL, and other reporting tools.

Responsibilities

Duties may include:

Perform gap analysis of fraud rules
• Perform trend analysis via ad-hoc queries using SQL, Snowsight, and Power BI
• Develop daily queries to help identify emerging trends
• Create queries and reports to help track performance
• Identify opportunities to apply fraud controls

Maintain fraud rule environments
• Perform frequent rule effectiveness analysis
• Develop necessary rule enhancements, additions, and deletions.
• Responsible for independent decision making
• Document and follow approved change control protocol

Understanding of Snowflake
• Acquire a good understanding of fraud data in Snowflake
• Utilization of disparate fields from multiple tables
• Identify out-of-tolerance conditions and make recommendations

Develop/demonstrate high-level data mining capacity
• Leverage Machine Learning tools and concepts
• Inserting automation in data querying and visualization

Card Fraud subject matter expert
• Participation in industry forums and reporting
• Understanding of industry innovation
• Propose and evaluate system enhancements

Generate fraud accountability metrics and reports for management
• Maintain monthly fraud metrics tracking spreadsheet
• Create management presentations

Understand and comply with bank policy, laws, regulations, and the bank's BSA/AML Program as applicable to your job duties
• Complete compliance training and adhere to internal procedures and controls as required.
• Report any known violations of compliance policy, laws, or regulations
• Report any suspicious customer and/or account activity

Exhibit professional behavior and promote positive working relationships
• Be proactive and respectful in all relationships
• Practice Division values and support the goals and strategic plan
• Complete special projects as assigned within allotted time frames
• Be accountable for continuous best efforts to complete the job assigned

Requirements

The Ideal Candidate for This Role:
• College Degree or Equivalent Work Experience
• Snowsight and SQL knowledge
• Microsoft Office experience (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Power BI)
• Previous fraud analytical experience
• Ability to communicate effectively
• Excellent organizational / time management skills
• Ability to manage multiple complex projects
• Base24 & TBS Experience
• Some on-call/after-hours work required

Equity, Diversity, & Inclusion:

FNBO is committed to belonging, inclusion, diversity and equity. We are committed to intentionally and proactively creating pathways to success for historically underrepresented populations. To accomplish this, we foster a culture of belonging and inclusion so that every employee is valued, and has the opportunity and the ability to make an impact. FNBO strives to reflect the diversity of the communities we serve in the makeup of our workforce.

See the full FNBO Equity, Diversity, & Inclusion Statement here

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or disability status.

