9989,1198,"Senior Data Science - Inference, Payments",Airbnb,United States,"Airbnb is a mission-driven company dedicated to helping create a world where anyone can belong anywhere. It takes a unified team committed to our core values to achieve this goal. Airbnb's various functions embody the company's innovative spirit and our fast-moving team is committed to leading as a 21st century company.Airbnb has become a platform that connects travelers and hosts from over... 81,000 cities around the globe. To power that community, Airbnb is building a world-class payments platform that currently supports over 190 countries, 70+ currencies, connects dozens of payment providers, and transmits billions of dollars per year. Our goal? To empower people and communities to participate in our global marketplace and innovate on a future where payments on Airbnb can be completely trusted, transparent, and simple. As our platform grows, the payments team is building a scalable foundation to support global scale, helping the company grow by bringing new markets and demographics to the platform, protecting our community from bad actors, and enabling new business products to thrive by providing easy to use and trusted payment experience. Our data science team is working to provide statistical insights and intelligent data products that will enable us to scale our platform and empower our entrepreneurs all around the world. About the Role: We are looking for a passionate data scientist to identify and execute scalable ways to improve our platform’s payment experience and to bring a scientific approach to product decision making. This data scientist will perform careful hypothesis generation, causal inference testing, and model development that will drive payment strategies on our platform. Our Inference Data Scientists have deep understanding of causal framework development, statistical analysis/modeling, and the complications of running experiment/quasi-experimental methods in a two-sided marketplace. They also have keen business sense and are able to utilize their findings to inform and drive our product roadmap. Examples of projects you may work on include, development of novel metrics and framework to identify and remediate payment problems, quantification of the impact and informing the structure of new payment products, and building models to optimize guest, host, and business outcomes. Responsibilities: Define novel metrics and their relationships to measure business success. Work with cross-functional partners to design and execute controlled experiment/quasi-experimental methods to quantify the effects of product changes. Develop methodologies to explore and exploit growth opportunities and build data products to optimize product/operational strategies in the payments sphere. Help our business partners understand metric trade-offs and influence business decisions. Qualifications: An ideal candidate should possess a good balance of statistical/technical skills, business acumen, and communication skills. A driven individual who’s keen to solve hard business problems is desired. 5+ years in industry experience and a Master's degree/PhD in a quantitative field Skilled in statistical programming (Python or R) and database usage (SQL) Deep knowledge of casual frameworks (including experimentation and quasi-experimental methods) and statistical modeling Ability to solve business problems by identifying and using appropriate methods and models Ability to communicate clearly and effectively to cross functional partners of varying technical levels and drive impact Ability to translate complex findings and results into a compelling narrative Payments/Risk domain expertise is a strong plus The starting base pay for this role is between $152,000 and $202,500. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: education, experience, and skills. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits. This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. Airbnb,Inc. can employ in states where we have registered entities. Currently, employees can not be located in: Alaska, Indiana, Nebraska, North Dakota, Ohio, South Dakota, Wisconsin, Alabama, Mississippi, Oklahoma, Delaware and Rhode Island. This list is continuously evolving and being updated, please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list. If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from. Belonging & Accommodations Airbnb is committed to working with the best and brightest people from the broadest talent pool possible. We believe a diversity of ideas fosters innovation and engagement, and allows us to attract the best people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. If you need assistance, or a reasonable accommodation during the application and recruiting process, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com",2022-06-16,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'sql', 'r']"
9991,1200,"Staff Data Scientist - Inference, Search",Airbnb,United States,"Airbnb is a mission-driven company dedicated to helping create a world where anyone can belong anywhere. It takes a unified team committed to our core values to achieve this goal. Airbnb's various functions embody the company's innovative spirit and our fast-moving team is committed to leading as a 21st century company. Airbnb is one of the world’s largest marketplaces for unique, authentic places to stay and things to do, offering over 7 million accommodations and 40,000 handcrafted activities, all powered by local hosts. An economic empowerment engine, Airbnb has helped millions of hospitality entrepreneurs monetize their spaces and their passions while keeping the financial benefits of tourism in their own communities. With more than half a billion guest arrivals to date, and accessible in 62 languages across 220 countries and regions, Airbnb promotes people-to-people connection, community and trust around the world. About the Team: Airbnb is a global platform that connects... travelers and hosts from over 81,000 cities. Our mission is to enable a world where anyone can belong anywhere. Using data to help ensure a world class experience for our users is critical to our mission. We are looking for talented Data Scientists to join our Search & Personalization Data Science team. The team works on building a world class search experience for our guests, from the homepage, to search and listing pages, and checkout. You will join a team with 3 other data scientists, responsible for building the data products, inference frameworks, and intelligence to create a personalized search experience. Responsibilities: You will work centrally, with other data scientists, partnering cross-functionally across the search experience. Your initial focus areas in the team: Developing a framework for evaluating the performance of supply categories in search and partnering with product, marketing, engineering and operations to create new categories. Operationalizing a system to detect suboptimal user paths in the product leveraging user behavioral logs. Developing a framework of conversion drivers, connecting input metrics to outputs, to inform strategies, decision-making, and track progress on team goals. Providing technical mentorship to other data scientists, holding a high bar for data products architecture. Minimum Qualifications: 5+ years of relevant industry experience Expert in at least one programming language for data analysis (Python or R) Experience with inference and machine learning techniques Experience in high-dimensional data modeling Proven ability to succeed in both collaborative and independent work environments Passion for scaling data science work Preferred Qualifications: Experience working on a consumer search product or recommender systems Experience with causal inference and structural models Strong skills in SQL and distributed system optimization (e.g. Hadoop, Hive, Spark, Presto) Experience with an ETL framework like Airflow Python skills preferred Experience with technical mentorship of other data scientists Experience with prototyping and writing production code Experience with system design The starting base pay for this role is between $180,000 and $245,000. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: education, experience, and skills. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits. Belonging & Accommodations Airbnb is committed to working with the best and brightest people from the broadest talent pool possible. We believe a diversity of ideas fosters innovation and engagement, and allows us to attract the best people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. If you need assistance, or a reasonable accommodation during the application and recruiting process, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com",2022-02-14,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'sql', 'spark', 'r', 'airflow', 'hadoop']"
9992,1201,Data Analyst,CommScope,"Fairmont, OK","In our always on' world, we believe it's essential to have a genuine connection with the work you do.

Does turning data into information, information into insight, and insight into business decisions excite you? We are looking to add a Data Analyst to our team to help develop analyses and reporting capabilities. You will monitor performance and quality to identify improvements present findings... to the management team in a concise and informative format while providing analysis of key KPI indicators and trending. How You'll Help Us Connect the World:

As a Data Analyst, you will do more than collecting and analyzing data. You will also ensure our data is accessible to those who need the information and is presented in a format that streamlines business processes. Accuracy and completeness of data is of the highest importance from this role. Other day-to-day activities of the role may include:
• Using data mining to extract information from data sets and identify correlations and patterns.
• Organizing and transforming information into comprehensible structures.
• Using data to predict trends in the customer base and the consumer population as a whole.
• Performing statistical analysis of data.
• Using tools and techniques to visualize data in easy-to-understand formats, such as diagrams and graphs in a repeatable and consistent manner.
• Must be able to duplicate or replicate the analysis as necessary.
• Using statistical tools to interpret data sets, paying particular attention to trends and patterns that could be valuable for indicative and predictive analytics efforts.
• Understand and track key KPI indicators, both internal and external, to validate compliance and trending.
• Work with Team leadership to understand organizational processes and procedures and ensure Reporting and Dashboards provided reinforce the standards expected of the Support Teams.
• Monitoring data quality and providing recommendations for improvements to data integrity.
• Communicating with stakeholders to understand data content and business requirements.
• Working with MSD Dynamics and Power BI to create and deliver reports, automated subscriptions and dashboards to identify trends and statistics
• To work with Google Analytics tool to export data into PowerBI as additional data reporting metrics as required
• Collaborate within the Business Innovation Team's Reporting group to field new requests, manage revision requests, plan development, and execute on deliverables.
• Maintain the departmental Power BI datasets, dashboards, and reports to meet operational and customer requirements. Minimum Qualifications:

Bachelor's degree from an accredited university or college in mathematics, statistics, computer science, economics or analytics You Will Excite Us If You Have:
• Ability to work with stakeholders to assess potential risks.
• Ability to analyze existing tools and databases and provide software solution recommendations
• Ability to translate business requirements into non-technical, lay terms
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy
• High-level written and verbal communication skills
• Experienced with Microsoft Dynamics, Excel, and Power BI
• Experience with Google Analytics a plus
• In-depth knowledge of statistical methodologies and data analysis techniques
• Strong attention to detail and ability to effectively prioritize

Perks & Benefits: The candidate will be rewarded with a comprehensive benefits package, including paid vacation, medical, dental, and vision plans, life and accidental death insurance, a 401(k) plan, and participation in the Company's Annual Incentive Plan. This position also benefits from eligibility to participate in CommScope's Long-Term Incentive Plan ( LTIP ), as approved by CommScope's Compensation Committee.

For candidates located in the states that require compensation listed in the job description, the anticipated salary range is dependent on experience and qualifications: $67,000 - $83,700 Why CommScope:

CommScope is on a quest to deliver connectivity that empowers how we live, work, and learn. Our employees push the boundaries of communications technology that enables game-changing discoveries like 5G, the Internet of Things, and gigabit speeds for everyone, everywhere. With our unmatched expertise in copper, fiber, and wireless infrastructure, our global clients rely on us to outperform today and be ready for the needs of tomorrow.

If you want to grow your career alongside bright, passionate, and caring people who strive to create what's next come connect to your future at CommScope.

CommScope is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EEO), including people with disabilities and veterans. If you are seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process, please contact us to submit your request at talentacquisition@commscope.com. You can also learn more about CommScope's accommodation process and EEO policy at careers.commscope.com/eeo

