10251,1460,Data Analyst Product MP,Mercury Insurance,"Oklahoma City, OK","Position Summary

The primary job function, under general supervision, is to work with the various functional areas (UW, Claims, Marketing, Advertising) to provide a data-driven analysis of our many processes. This position will require a solid background in statistical concepts and statistical tools. The incumbent will conduct analysis using statistical techniques to extract data, which will be... of value in process efficiency and product design. Incumbent must have a passion for problem-solving, comfort with ambiguity, and the ability to think conceptually, analytically, and creatively, and will be expected to manage projects and program execution of high complexity.

Essential Job Functions
• Analyzes data available and identify issues and opportunities in different business areas. The successful candidate will understand departments' processes (UW, Claims, Marketing, Advertising, etc.). Creates statistical models to generate insights on different business issues and provides suggestions on approaches to problems. Conducts small-scope project work as assigned and performs ad hoc analyses. Works independently with guidance and direction from advanced-level analysts and management and participates in discussions with colleagues regarding analytical needs. Reviews and discusses analytical results with colleagues and managers as necessary. Supports projects by applying general knowledge of the business area processes, including best practices. Provides analysis to understand options for implementing analytical models and procedures while working closely with other groups through implementation processes.
• Retrieves data from various sources and prepares data for analysis. Reviews data for accuracy and revises methods of data retrieval when necessary. Prepare basic reports, graphs, and charts based on research and analysis. Analyzes algorithms using intermediate SAS programming and MS Excel. Creates procedures to streamline analysis procedures. Provides suggestions for process improvements or goal change and develops and designs presentations to show findings of analyses. Develop tools for use by management including, spreadsheets, presentations, and reports. Serves as primary contact for reporting needs or issues regarding various data.
• Collaborates with MP business intelligence personnel on monthly reporting and working with the team to provide automated monthly reports.
• Communicates proactively and consistently with SME's and Management in the various functional areas to understand each job function. Through clear communication, the incumbent will increase the breadth of their understanding of the processes associated with the listed procedures and various KPI's that drive business results in each area and overall.
• Creates presentations breaking down problems identified and presenting potential solutions. May attend management meetings to present findings and recommendations. The incumbentshall have a strong background in developing and explaining meaningful graphs and assemble and deliver PowerPoint presentations.
• Regular attendance at work on a full-time schedule of at least 8 hours and 40 hours per week.
• Other functions may be assigned.

Education

