10410,1619,Data Analyst - Commissions Focus,Prairie Fire Resources,"Kansas City, MO","Who are we seeking?
We are seeking a dynamic individual who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment, providing a high level of service and welcomes challenges. Responsible for calculating and processing commissions for external clients. This role will be client-facing and balance the priorities of multiple client needs and meeting deadlines.
Who we are...
Advisors Back Office Solution (ABOS) provides back office accounting, budgeting and planning, commissions, payroll and human resources services to a variety of small to mid-size businesses. We handle these day-to-day core activities to allow business to succeed and grow, while providing our expert advice and solutions to the complexities and concerns they face every day. Our clients are located in various states. We are on the hunt for positive people who thrive on hard work and a collaborate team environment.
We celebrate diversity- everyone is welcome here. As an inclusive workplace, our employees feel comfortable to be their authentic self each day. Advisors Back Office Solution is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer.

What we provide:

Fun Culture and a team that values collaboration and high levels of trust
Amazing benefits including medical, dental, vision and 401k
Hybrid and flexible work environment
Continuous personal and professional development opportunities
Paid PTO and Holiday time
Small Company Feel
Room to move up, we are growing!
Open to new ideas- we encourage employee's input for process improvements and employee feedback
Recognition for hard work & exemplary performance
A supportive and engaged management team
Responsible for calculating and processing commissions for all clients. Works closely with team members in this role.

Prepare, calculate and process all Client Commissions; audit and identify inconsistencies; collaborate with team members to correct errors

Fuel continued growth by devising innovative solutions to complex client commission problems. Help keep our business on track to meet (or, better yet, exceed) our goals.

Develop innovative and detailed trackers and workbooks for clients

Review current and future client commission structures; provide guidance and improvement suggestions when applicable.

Partner with client and key client personnel to ensure accurate commission processes. Review processes and implement controls to ensure mitigated risk for the client.

Analyze client commission reports, identify variances and offer feedback

Respond to client inquiries regarding their commissions

Protect our clients by partnering with the members of our team and the client's team to identify and address risks related to client business initiatives.

Manage positive client relationships; respond to client inquiries; provide data as needed

Identify opportunities and implement programs to centralize, eliminate or automate activities.

QUALIFICATIONS/EXPECTATIONS:

Minimum of two years of equivalent practical experience; OR

Bachelor's degree in accounting or other relevant field

Understanding of the functions and operations of the commission calculation process

Progressively improving and expanding accounting knowledge; practices continuous learning and retaining the material learned

Highly analytical

Highly proficient using accounting software and Microsoft Excel

High level of accuracy with minimal errors in all work

Act in a pleasant, professional, courteous and respectful manner to all internal and external customers at all times

Evidence of the practice of a high level of confidentiality

Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with multiple interruptions

Proficient in prioritization and organizational skills

Ability to identify numerical errors and resolve the errors

Communicates clearly both written and verbally

