10461,1670,Data Analyst II - Commercial Payments. Job in Kansas City My...,COMMERCE BANK,"Kansas City, MO","About Working at Commerce

Wouldn't it be great to build your career at a bank that's known for helping people with their financial challenges? That's exactly what you'd be doing when you join the team at Commerce Bank. We're looking for teammates who are ready to do whatever it takes to help our customers with their everyday financial needs. You'd be helping yourself too, because Commerce has a... tradition of recognizing and rewarding team members for their talent, skills and contributions.

No wonder we've been an industry leader for over 155 years and have developed a reputation as a great place to work in the financial services world. If you'd like to be a part of a team and culture that is respected by its peers and in your community, we should talk. We're always looking for the best and brightest.

About This Job

The Data Analyst provides reporting, business intelligence and analysis to the Commercial Payments Line of Business and functional department management. The analyst utilizes database programming (SQL), report design, Microsoft Access/Excel, Power BI, databases and other system tools to lead the business lines with the highest level of service in multiple areas including: sales strategy, business strategy, technical execution, and portfolio management. The incumbent should understand the business issue and its fit with enterprise goals in order to ascertain and consult insightful solutions. Project management skills are needed to develop requirements and project timelines. In addition, the position will require administering databases as well as a mind for automating repetitive tasks/reports and revision of those structures accordingly.

The ideal candidate will continuously ask what they can do to help. They will ask questions to understand customer needs and business goals and apply that understanding to define and evaluate multiple solutions. The ability to manage multiple projects concurrently while streamlining similar tasks across projects for maximum efficiency is expected. The candidate will display a sense of urgency in meeting deadlines and validate findings prior to presentation. The candidate will exhibit commitment and a sense of ownership by anticipating opportunities / issues and taking action to mitigate obstacles. Lastly, the analyst will evaluate emerging trends relative to current technical and leadership skills and request training to enhance those skills.

Essential Functions

Develop and schedule releases for very complex relationship pricing model(s) and customer level profitability

Develop new reports and dashboards ranging from sales metrics to financial trends to portfolio analysis

Setup databases with various levels of complexity for aiding in the explanation of P&L financial variances

Perform data management type initiatives which may require pulling and sending data from one, or more, system(s) or department(s) to another

Ensure data cleanliness and accuracy within the database table/relationship structure

Develop and implement databases, data collection systems/repositories for data analysis and consumption

Plan and facilitate regular meetings with work group and leadership within the company

Simplify very complex data to draw observations for all levels of management

Create new ways to review data differently and articulate findings to management

Coordinate efforts and track progress of multiple groups that are working on related projects or tasks

Actively participate with other data team members to enhance department processes

Provide quality assurance of imported data, working with quality assurance analyst if necessary

Schedule, structure and facilitate working sessions to develop/build consensus on data items or terms with different applications or interpretations in different departments.

Perform other duties as assigned

Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Required

Intermediate knowledge of financial analysis, pricing, profitability and profit/loss statements

Intermediate knowledge of visualization tools such as Power BI and Tableau

Excellent facilitation and negotiation skills

Ability to develop and manage relationships with wide variety of business units

Ability to communicate technical information/concepts to non-technical audiences

Strong analytical and critical thinking skills

Ability to utilize best practices in data design concepts

Ability to establish and meet deadlines consistently

Strong meeting management skills that include scheduling, agenda planning, and decision summaries

Motivated and organized self-starter with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities

Inquisitive, agile and strong team player with excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills

Ability to remain adaptable and resilient to all situations with an optimistic outlook and cast a positive shadow that is aligned with our culture and Core Values

Intermediate level proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, Teams and Outlook

Education & Experience

Bachelor's or equivalent combination of education and experience required

3+ years of work-related experience in systems, data management, data science required

Experience with business intelligence, data warehousing, statistical analysis or visualization platforms required

Experience using querying and visualization tools such as Business Objectives, BI Tools, SAS, SQL, MS Access, etc. required

Experience designing, managing and continually improving business processes preferred

Experience developing organizational policies and procedures and implementing by building consensus and stakeholder commitment preferred

Experience with application management including version control and handling large data sets and relational databases preferred

Experience navigating data warehouses like Teradata or similar preferred

Location: 1000 Walnut St, Kansas City, Missouri 64106

Time Type:

Full time",2022-11-19,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'word', 'power_bi', 'sql', 'outlook', 'sas', 'excel']"
10462,1671,"Expert, Operations Data Analyst (Flexible Location). Job in...",PG&E Corporation,"Oakland, CA","Requisition ID # 137949

Job Category: Business Operations / Strategy...

Job Level: Individual Contributor

Business Unit: Safety & Risk

Job Location: Oakland

Department Overview

The aim of the Risk and Data Analytics team is to enhance the risk practices of PG&E's Electric Operation business and thereby address changing external conditions such as climate change. To this end the Risk and Data Analytics team creates and maintains tools to enable PG&E to close the gap between metrics and electric system performance. These tools provide a multi-layered view of risk across the electric system so that decision-making processes include and empower employees at all levels of the company to manage risk appropriately.

In creating these tools, the team employs a data supported, lean solution process to expand PG&E's ability to assess and manage risk. The result are assessments and mitigations that are more dynamic, quantitative, and customer-focused, with a multi-layered approach for both short-term and long-term time horizons.

Sample activities include:
• Interpretation and representation of meteorological data in models that combine a range data sources such as the electric system asset data, vegetation and meteorology
• Development of computer vision models aimed at accelerating and automating asset inspections processes
• Predicting electric distribution equipment failure before it occurs allowing for proactive maintenance
• Supervised and unsupervised machine learning models using Python and Spark, executed on AWS

Position Summary

We are looking for an Expert Data Analyst to join our growing team. In this role you will have a unique opportunity to be at the forefront of utility industry analytics and their use in tools to asses risk. Working as part of cross functional team, including other data analysts, data scientists, technology experts, and subject matter experts this individual will help develop data driven solutions for decision making and operations. Specifically, in this role you will extract operations data for analysis, leadership, executive support and responses to data requests and analysis. Maintain operational reporting, tools & databases to ensure that it is kept up-to-date. Develop, maintain and enhance operational metric dashboards and database tools for the broader analytics teams. Identify and solve current gaps in data requirements and ease of access to ensure fast and consistent responses to leadership inquiries.

Position is flexible within the PG&E Service Territory.

Job Responsibilities
• Works with all levels of leadership across functions to influence decisions
• Provides new and innovative solutions and recommendations to enhance database(s) with new data sources and improved data processes
• Manages very complex data extracts and list pulls ensuring data accuracy
• Manages extracting data and transferring the data from databases to various analysts to support operational analysis efforts
• Manages complex data analysis projects with limited supervision on only the most complex projects from initial request to presenting data results ensuring that the project is completed on-time and on-budget
• Develops comprehensive reports and communicates clear, concise and actionable data analyses for clients utilizing tools such as PowerBI, Tableau, Excel and/or similar
• Designs data analysis to achieve business objectives, process data, analyze data, write clear and concise data findings and tailor communications to specific audiences
• Creates automated data routines and processes for reporting and data delivery ensuring accurate data manipulation and data cleansing
• Demonstrates and uses broad expertise in data processing and data analysis and applies this knowledge to several different issues
• Analyzes data using various advanced statistical tools to develop complex ad hoc reports, statistics, trends and profiles
• Acts as team lead and provides direction to less experienced employees
Qualifications

Minimum:
• BA/BS Degree in Marketing, Business, Computer Science, Engineering or other related field or equivalent work experience
• 6 years of related work experience
Desired:
• Degree in computer science, engineering, applied sciences, mathematics, statistics, econometrics or similar quantitatively focused subject areas or job-related experience
• Minimum of 6 years of relevant experience in data science or advanced analytics OR Master's Degree and job-related experience, 3 years.
• Knowledge of database and information systems - for example SCADA, EMS, OMT, OIS, SAP, Teradata
• Knowledge of Microsoft Office Products - for example Excel, Word, Power BI, PowerPoint, Access
• Strong oral and written communication skills
• Demonstrated collaboration or paired development work history
• Demonstrated proficiency with relational databases, preferably in SQL

Beneficial Qualifications:
• History mentoring and teaching others as well as desire to continue to do so
• Demonstrated experience with data visualization tools such as Tableau, D3, Plotly, etc.
• Enjoy working on complex multi-stage projects with a diverse team
• Involvement or strong interest in the energy/clean tech industry
• Familiarity with transmission and/or distribution electric system",2022-10-25,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sap', 'word', 'power_bi', 'power_bi', 'python', 'plotly', 'powerpoint', 'sql', 'aws', 'spark', 'excel']"
