10508,1717,"Senior Data Analyst, Mobility","AutoNation, Inc.",United States (+1 other),"AutoNation Headquarters

About AutoNation Mobility...

Mobility is a recently established business unit and a major strategic pillar behind AutoNation’s strategy to unlock new horizons of growth. AutoNation Mobility is developing products and services to address the needs created from several trends such as 1) the shift from vehicle ownership to vehicle access; 2) the electrification of vehicles; 3) the shift to digital car shopping experiences and 4) the increasing importance of fleets.

Mobility will launch new products that provide consumers with more flexible, and convenient ways to access vehicles (compared to financing or leasing), at fair and transparent prices delivered through a seamless digital user experience. AutoNation can leverage its extensive vehicle inventory, nationwide coverage, parts and service, logistics, reconditioning, marketing, and fleet management infrastructure to offer consumers a seamless digital product experience while driving operational excellence and efficiency at every step of the value chain.

Mobility will also bring AutoNation’s full set of existing and new capabilities to partner with the leading fleet operators, marketplaces, and platforms to help them drive efficiencies, scale, and operational excellence in their day-to-day operations. Whether they have a large fleet today or have big plans to scale, AutoNation can be a strategic partner to help fleet operators achieve their goals and objectives.

We are assembling a world-class team of entrepreneurs, operators, and technologists to build new lines of business as well as deliver the best of the AutoNation ecosystem to new customers and segments. If you are excited about building tangible new businesses that cater to the future of mobility and automotive, the time to join us is now!

Position Summary:

As the Data Engineering lead, you will build the data and analytics capabilities for a highly complex Mobility e-commerce, recurring revenue, and fleet management platform from scratch. In this highly visible role, you will serve as the technical expert responsible for design and implementation of BI, Analytics, & Big Data solutions providing high-value, timely analytics and data solutions to the AutoNation Mobility team.

You will work closely with our technology teams to develop our data systems architecture and partner with key leaders across the Technology, Product, Finance, Accounting, Pricing & Inventory, Operations, Marketing and Risk teams to understand their data and analytics needs and translate those into technical specifications, architectures, and implementations.

You will work directly with internal and 3rd party technology providers to implement robust data pipelines and deliver on the data and analytics systems to support our business as it launches and scales.

You will develop the data engineering and business intelligence roadmap and support the evolving needs of the business as we iterate to optimize our overall business model – from pricing, operations, product analytics, conversion to detailed unit economics and marketing campaigns.

You will also build a lean and high-performing Data Engineering organization with a diverse, collaborative, and fun culture as you hire and lead a team of data engineers and analysts.

Job Responsibilities:
• Set overall direction and roadmap for BI, Analytics, & Big Data solutions for Mobility.
• Gather and refine requirements from cross-functional teams / users.
• Verify requirements, define system architectures, develop implementation plans.
• Provide thought leadership for all data solutions, including designing data solutions that meet and exceed customer expectations.
• Provide direction to developers overseeing the development, unit testing and documentation for the developed solution and develop strong customer relationships for ongoing business.
• Evolve and refine BI tools, systems, and capabilities as an area of continuous improvement.

Qualifications (Mandatory):
• 10+ years Data Warehouse/Data Lake Architecture and Development
• 10+ years Data Modeling & Architecture
• Experience building and leading a technical team
• Strong experience with client engagement & aligning others to your ideas/solutions
• Ability to clarify/translate customer requirements into Epics/Stories & remove ambiguity
• Ability to mentor other DE team members
• Ability to present to groups of mixed technical ability

Qualifications (Preferred):
• Prior experience in automotive retailing, marketplace or mobility tech platform.
• Prior “zero-to-one” experience in setting up data, analytics, and BI systems and tools.

Company Overview

AutoNation, a provider of personalized transportation services, is driven by innovation and transformation. As one of America's most admired companies, AutoNation delivers a peerless Customer experience recognized by data-driven consumer insight leaders, Reputation and J.D. Power. Through its bold leadership and brand affinity, the AutoNation Brand is synonymous with ""DRVPNK"" and ""What Drives You, Drives Us."" AutoNation has a singular focus on personalized transportation services that are easy, transparent, and Customer-centric.

Benefits

Click here to learn more about our Benefits.

Join us as we pave the way to moving our company, our communities and our industry forward. Apply today at a location near you or wherever you dream the road will take you.

AutoNation is an equal opportunity employer and a drug-free workplace",2022-07-15,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
