Senior Systems/Data Analyst...

Job Responsibilities

GDIT is your place. You make it your own by bringing your ideas and unique perspective to our culture. By owning your opportunity at GDIT, you are helping us ensure today is safe and tomorrow is smarter. Our work depends on a Senior Software Engineer joining our team to support our customer activities in Washington, DC. This position can be worked Remote.

GDIT supports a system for HHS that collects data from a variety of sources. Data is uploaded directly into the system or entered directly into custom forms. This system also includes a complete case management system. We have hundreds of forms and dozens of data interfaces. There is also a complete data analysis subsystem that is based on Tableau for producing reports and doing analysis of the data.

At GDIT, people are our differentiator. As a Senior Systems/Data Analyst supporting our Customer, you will perform data analysis, interpretation, and management duties. In this role, a typical day will include:
• Developing advanced analytics products using a wide range of statistical and applied mathematical techniques making data-driven conclusions and turning the findings into meaningful and or actionable recommendations to complex business challenges
• Creating data visualizations using Tableau.
• Performing statistical analysis using R or Python.
• Writing SQL queries to extract data for new data analysis reports.
• Performing data extraction, transformation, and loading to support advanced analytics.
• Supporting all phases of analytic work product development, from the identification of key business questions, through data collection and ETL to interpretation of data and analytic results, data reporting, and development and vetting of recommendations.
• Identifying data sources and data integrity, developing internal and external briefings and reports with findings and recommendations.
• Writing and maintaining supporting documentation to include methodologies, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and guidelines for data cleaning and process documentation.
• Supporting data correction efforts to ensure that the users are reporting the required data elements and troubleshooting any end-user technical issues encountered while using the agency system.
• Performing activities related to administration of the Tableau server.
• Responding to time sensitive requests independently
• Working with large amounts of fragmented data in a fast-paced environment.
• Perform other duties as assigned.

Education
• Requires BS/BA degree

Qualifications
• Requires BA/BS with at least 8 years of experience in data analysis and database administration
• Expert user of Tableau, SQL, Python, R, MS Office Suite (including Excel and Access)
• Excellent analytical and writing skills - for this position this is our top priority.
• Strong verbal communication skills
• Highly motivated and collaborative
• Ability to work under pressure in a fast-paced environment

Additional Desired Skills:
• Familiarity with refugee and immigrant populations, a plus.
• Proficiency with social science research, and statistics/statistical software packages.

WHAT GDIT CAN OFFER YOU:
• Full-flex work week
• 401K with company match
• Internal mobility team dedicated to helping you own your career
• Collaborative teams of highly motivated critical thinkers and innovators

The likely salary range for this position is $92,000 - $138,000, this is not, however, a guarantee of compensation or salary; rather, salary will be set based on experience, geographic location and possibly contractual requirements and could fall outside of this range.

