10544,1753,Product Information Management (PIM) Data Analyst,Fortive,United States,"Our vision is to transform the customer experience with industry leading self-service digital tools driven by rich data. We need your help to build and maintain our database and enable best in class solutions with data. You are responsible for executing a structured approach to the collection, creation, and maintenance of master product data in our content management and PIM system supporting the... Business and digital team of Hengstler-Dynapar in the EMEA and US region. You will be a Power User responsible for the integrity of the organization’s master product data systems. You will drive data integrity through data governance, change management, data ownership, and quality assurance.

You will be accountable for maintaining and managing the product information in our content management and PIM systems. You will work Business and digital team of Hengstler-Dynapar. to ensure data is available to be consumed by customer facing systems such as online systems including website, ecommerce and site search systems and offline assets such as product datasheets and catalogs. You will also partner with internal subject matter experts such as product management and engineering to understand key attributes for all product types, collect and implement attribute data for all SKUs.

This is a remote role with limited travel

Core Responsibilities:
• Be the Power User and advocate the use of centralized data/PIM platform
• Acquire and maintain product data from multiple data sources. Manages and executes data requests in support of business processes, new product sales initiatives
• Drives excellence and ensures continuous improvement in quality of data through cleansing and best practices for data construction
• Make data available for use in CMS and front-end website systems by partnering with web developers, agencies, and IT
• Reports KPIs related to material master data management and drives a system of actions to complete requests in accordance with Data management process
• Understand, adapt, and improve document management process to enable more efficient data updates and partner with stakeholders to establish standards, governance, and system administration where no processes are in place
• Upload images and product documents into asset management system with all necessary metadata to maintain system search standards
• Create, review, edit, and upload product content/media with a goal of achieving complete and quality data for all product groups
• Works collaboratively as a data steward within teams to ensure clear understanding of business requirements that are managed in concert with PIM data
• Work with regional teams to ensure that data translations are completed within the required timeframe and to a high standard.

Support and train stakeholders and local users on centralized data platform

Requirements:
• Bachelor’s degree and at least 2 years of experience in e-commerce or PIM systems with a strong track record in working in ecommerce/digital space. Preference given to previous experience with major PIM solutions such as Akeneo, Salsify or Perfion.

Fortive is a diversified industrial growth company comprised of global businesses that are recognized leaders in attractive markets. With more than $6 billion in annual revenues, Fortive’s well-known brands hold leading positions in field instrumentation, transportation, sensing, product realization, automation and specialty, and franchise distribution.

Fortive is headquartered in Everett, Washington and employs a team of more than 24,000 research and development, manufacturing, sales, distribution, service and administrative employees in more than 40 countries around the world. Our team grows by tackling challenges that accelerate progress and further their careers. With a culture rooted in continuous improvement, the core of our company’s operating model is the Fortive Business System. For more information please visit: www.fortive.com.

The position is with Specialty Product Technologies (SPT). Specialty Product Technologies (SPT) has grown to be a global leader as a core technology company comprised of several strong product lines. SPT designs, manufactures, and markets innovative products, services, and technologies to deliver manufacturing/operational efficiencies, cost-effective solutions, and high-quality products demanded by today’s industrial automation marketplace.

Every SPT product line has earned a “best in class” reputation and has been built on a solid foundation of achievement over a long period of time with proven reliability in the most rigorous and demanding applications. Each product line is considered essential components in the markets and applications they serve.

Founded in 1901 as the Veeder Manufacturing Company, the company joined the Danaher portfolio in 1986 and has continued to grow. Today, SPT is part of the Fortive Corporation. The SPT product lines encompass the solid brands of Eagle Signal, Joslyn Clark, Namco Controls, Superior Electric, Thomson Nyliner, and Veeder-Root. SPT product lines can be found in a wide variety of applications and industries.

We Are an Equal Opportunity Employer

Fortive Corporation and all Fortive Companies are proud to be equal opportunity employers. We value and encourage diversity and solicit applications from all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, religion, sex, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristics protected by law. Fortive and all Fortive Companies are also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for applicants with disabilities. Individuals who need a reasonable accommodation because of a disability for any part of the employment process should ask to speak with a Human Resources representative to request an accommodation",2022-11-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
10545,1754,Data Analyst & Reporting Specialist,Revinate,United States,"About Us

Revinate is one of the largest and most innovative providers of direct revenue-generating solutions in the hospitality industry. Revinate's mission is to deliver hoteliers scalable direct revenue and profits from data-driven solutions that cultivate deeper relationships with guests. Revinate’s Direct Booking Platform helps capture, convert and retain guests with strategies and services... that maximize direct booking revenue. This combination maximizes the lifetime value of each guest through personalized and targeted campaigns across the guest journey.

THE ROLE

As the Data Analyst and Reporting Specialist, you will collect and analyse complex business and application data and create reports that drive efficiencies and improvements for Revinate and our customers. You develop, deploy and maintain complex dynamic dashboards to support the business strategy. You collect and interpret business and application data to inform management and operations about current situations and identify and interpret patterns and opportunities for improvement. Ultimately you will be able to forecast trends for decision makers.

You are able to work independently, as well as with your team members, cross functional peers and (senior) management. Also you have the skill to operate effectively across geographies, which needs a cultural awareness. You are inquisitive and can work with confidential data.

What You'll Do
• Liaise with internal stakeholders to understand reporting need and gather business requirements
• Translate business requirements into technical requirements
• Assess and understand data stored in our Data Warehouse
• Interpret results by using statistical techniques and translate the relevant information into reports and data visualisation solutions
• Help roll out new dashboards and processes
• Effectively communicate complex findings into actionable and understandable results for both operations and discussions with management

What you'll Bring
• Master’s degree in Data Analytics, Statistics or another relevant study, with strong affinity for numbers and information systems
• 1-3 years of work experience
• English fluency
• Familiarity with Python and Machine Learning
• Experience working with SQL
• Experience working with Looker, Tableau or other BI/Dashboarding tools
• Strong analytical, mathematical, and reasoning skills to collect and interpret data

Excited?! Want to learn more? Apply Now!

Our Core Values:

One Revinate - United & Strong, on a single mission together

Built on Trust - It’s the foundation of everything we do

Expect Amazing - We think, dream & deliver big

Customer Love - When the customer wins, we win

Make it Simpler - Apply it to everything we do

Hungerness - Feel it, follow it, be relentless about our success

Grounded in Gratitude - We’re glad to be here & make the most of every day

Revinate Inc. provides Equal Employment Opportunity to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender identity or expression, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, amnesty, or status as a covered veteran in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Revinate complies with applicable state and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities.

Revinate is not open to third party solicitation or resumes for our posted FTE positions. Resumes received from third party agencies that are unsolicited will be considered complimentary.

If you are in need of accommodation or special assistance to navigate our website or to complete your application, please send an e-mail with your request to recruiting@revinate.com.

By submitting your application you acknowledge that you have read Revinate's Privacy Policy (https://www.revinate.com/privacy",2022-10-26,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'python', 'sql']"
10546,1755,Data Analyst II,Children's Mercy KC,"Kansas City, MO","Thanks for your interest in Children's Mercy!

Do you envision finding a meaningful role with an inclusive and compassionate team? At Children’s Mercy, we believe in making a difference in the lives of all children and shining a light of hope to the patients and families we serve. Our employees make the difference, which is why we have been recognized by U.S. News & World Report as a top... pediatric hospital, for eleven consecutive years.

Children’s Mercy is in the heart of Kansas City – a metro abounding in cultural experiences, vibrant communities and thriving businesses. This is where our patients and families live, work and play. This is a community that has embraced our hospital and we strive to say thanks by giving back. As a leader in children’s health, we engage in meaningful programs and partnerships throughout the region so that we can improve the lives of children beyond the walls of our hospital.

Overview

A Data Analyst II is responsible for analyzing trends and insights in the data, and enabling stakeholders to make data-driven decisions and take action. The Data Analyst II will partner with business and clinical stakeholders across the enterprise. This position is part of the Enterprise Intelligence team.

At Children’s Mercy, we are committed to ensuring that everyone feels welcomed within our walls. A successful candidate for this position will join us as we strive to create a workplace that reflects the community we serve, as well as our core values of kindness, curiosity, inclusion, team and integrity.

Additionally, it’s important to us that we remain transparent with all potential job candidates. Because we value the safety of the patients and families we serve, as well as the Children’s Mercy staff, we want to let you know that the seasonal influenza and COVID-19 vaccines are a condition of employment for all employees in our organization. New employees must be willing to be vaccinated if found non-immune to measles, mumps, rubella (MMR) and chicken pox (varicella) and/or without evidence of tetanus, diphtheria, acellular pertussis (Tdap) vaccination since 2005. If you become a finalist for this position, and have any concerns about receiving these vaccines, medical and/or religious exemptions can be further discussed with Human Resources.

Responsibilities
• Conducts data analysis to produce actionable insights
• Partners with stakeholders to understand business needs and present insights and solutions
• Partners with Data Engineering (DE) team and Data Architects (DA) to identify new data sources for the Modern Data Platform (MDP)
• Discovers emerging analytic techniques and applies them to the business

Qualifications
• Bachelor's Degree 5-7 years experience Background in data analytics and history of using analytics to drive action. Experience presenting insights to non-technical stakeholders.
• Expert SQL skills
• Expert Tableau and/or Power BI skills, both in technical competency and design aptitude
• Exposure/expertise in using Python or R for data analysis
• Ability to identify, analyze and interpret trends or patterns in complex datasets
• Ability to prioritize and meet multiple deadlines for the volume of work expected without supervision
• Ability to produce work that is accurate, neat and adheres to standards
• Ability to work as part of a multi-disciplinary team or independently
• Excellent written and verbal communication skills in a narrative story format with a business mindset

Remote Work/Work from Home

This position is entirely remote or work-from-home. The person hired must live in the Kansas City metro area and may attend on-site meetings, as scheduled.

EEO Employer/Disabled/Vet

Children’s Mercy hires individuals based on their job skills, expertise and ability to maintain professional relationships with fellow employees, patients, parents and visitors. A personal interview, formal education and training, previous work experience, references and a criminal background investigation all are factors used to select the best candidates. The hospital does not discriminate against prospective or current employees based on the race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, creed, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, ancestry or veteran status. A drug screen will be performed upon hire. Children’s Mercy is smoke and tobacco free.

Our commitment to Diversity & Inclusion

CM is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. Our patients and families come from all walks of life, and so do we. We know that our greatest strengths come from the people who make up our team so we hire great people from a wide variety of backgrounds, not just because it’s the right thing to do, but because it makes our hospital stronger and our patient care more compassionate.

If you share our values and our enthusiasm for service, you will find a home at CM. In recruiting for our team, we welcome the unique contributions that you can bring, including education, ideas, culture, ethnicity, race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, national origin, age, languages spoken, veteran status, color, religion, disability and beliefs",2022-12-09,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'power_bi', 'python', 'sql', 'r']"
10547,1756,Data Analyst,Bartlett & West,"Overland Park, KS","Overview

POSITION SUMMARY: The GIS Analyst position provides expanded geospatial technical leadership on one or more projects. Technical leadership will include higher-level expertise in leading data modeling methods, a deeper understanding of spatial and other enterprise databases, data quality assurance, and quality control or other data management techniques. In addition, the position will... involve understanding client needs and requirements, existing processes and workflows, and supporting the development of technical solutions preferred by the client.

This will include working with internal teams and with the client. The GIS Analyst will develop a current understanding of data state, workflows, and processes used to provide solutions that meet the client and project’s needs. Solutions will require the configuration of web maps, field collection tools, and dashboards. 

This role requires demonstrated ability to solve complex problems and recommend or make decisions regarding the best path for data development, processing, and analysis. Project work will involve process improvement, quality control, data creation from spatial and tabular sources, conversion, migration, and maintenance. Project work will apply the following analytic skills: thematic map creation, preparation of GIS and tabular data, use of analytical tools, database creation, data modeling for manipulation, and transformation.

Veterans encouraged to apply.

Responsibilities

Essential Functions & Responsibilities:

Design, Analysis & Documentation
• Develop and lead integration and deployment of new methods or processes for data sourcing, development, and management on client systems and internal to Bartlett & West
• Data conversion, migration, and map production in a layered environment, including analysis support
• Edit and create new feature classes within the map environment
• Import and convert CAD, GPS, LiDAR, or other feature data types into a GIS environment
• Development and support of geographic databases
• Develop methods and perform quality assurance/quality control on GIS and non-spatial data to meet quality goals
• Document workflows and business procedures.
• Attend client meetings, as needed, and document key information relative to business processes, workflows, and system requirements.
• Create mockups, workflows, design documents, and any other documentation
• Assist in advanced GIS data creation, editing, analysis, and the configuration of map services and system workflows

Coordination
• Prepare, conduct and document all requirements assessments, progress reviews, and other meetings
• Oversee the process used by GIS Technicians assigned to the project to meet project deadlines
• Participate in the training of employees and clients, including designing and developing a training program
• Develop and participate in ongoing client maintenance and support opportunities such as presentations and relationship-building activities
• Provide proposal support by designing new processes to meet the proposal preparation needs and estimating hours required to complete individual production tasks

Innovation
• Primary support or lead initiatives to develop new methods or processes for data sourcing, development, and management
• Perform research into emerging GIS technologies
• Stay abreast of new geographic information trends and technologies
• Participate in professional organization(s) in the analyst’s area of expertise or client focus

Qualifications

Knowledge, Skills, Abilities:
• Analytical thinker
• Detail-oriented
• Customer-focused (internal and external)
• Presentation skills
• Active listening skills
• Strong organizational and time management skills
• Ability to work independently and within a team successfully
• Ability to train, mentor, and lead others
• Exhibit initiative, responsibility, flexibility, and leadership
• Practical interpersonal communication skills to maintain client and employee relationships
• Demonstrate ability to solve complex problems and make decisions
• Ability to embrace new technology and processes
• Ability to reduce complex data management challenges to practical workflows, processes and methods in verbal and written communication
• Expanded knowledge of GIS practices and methodology
• Understanding of Esri data editing workflows, ArcGIS Enterprise or ArcGIS Online, GIS web services, and ArcGIS web/mobile application configuration
• Basic understanding of Python and Esri Arcade scripting
• Ability to assess spatial and non-spatial data, database models and client needs to develop data management solutions
• Familiarity with locating and using public GIS data sources
• Strong proficiency in Microsoft Office and ArcGIS software
• Possess unquestionable integrity, ethics, and the values appropriate to the company’s culture; and actively models those values internally and externally

Education:

An associate’s degree or equivalent coursework from an accredited school in GIS, Geography, or a related field is required. Bachelor’s degree preferred.

Experience:

5 years’ experience working with GIS. Experience using ESRI or Bentley software products. Familiarity with ArcGIS, specifically ArcPro and ArcGIS Online or ArcGIS Enterprise. Strong experience in Geographic and Spatial methodologies required. Background in wastewater collection systems, stormwater collection systems, and water systems, specifically rural water networks, is desriable.

Travel Expectations:

Must be able to travel in-state and out-of-state on occasion, which usually would consist of visiting other office locations, project sites, attending seminars or business meetings. Minimum travel is 10-20% of the time depending on projects. Certain positions will require more travel. Travel expectations will be communicated through the employee-owner’s manager, and for newly open positions, travel expectations will be reflected in the job posting announcement. Driver’s license with clean driving record required.

This job description is not designed to cover or contain a listing of all functions and responsibilities that are required of this position. Employee owners are expected to take on additional responsibilities as requested.

Bartlett & West is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, sexual orientation, status as a protected veteran or status as a qualified individual with disability.

An offer is contingent upon successfully passing the pre-employment drug screen. Drug screen will need to complete within 48 hours of being contacted.

Nearly all positions at Bartlett & West can require employee-owners to operate a motor vehicle on public roads in the course of their duties. Accordingly, all employees may be required to have acceptable driving records and to provide an authorization to the Company to periodically obtain MVR reports”.

Bartlett & West partners with businesses and communities to build smarter, stronger, more connected infrastructure. From railroad GIS to industrial parks and city planning, we provide innovative technology and engineering solutions to clients worldwide. With deep industry knowledge and a passion for creative problem solving, we engineer better tomorrows.

Bartlett & West is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, sexual orientation, status as a protected veteran or status as a qualified individual with disability",2022-12-17,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['python']
10548,1757,Consumer Intelligence Analyst,Barkley,"Kansas City, MO","The Consumer Intelligence Analyst is responsible for helping execute consumer research for current clients and prospects, synthesizing research results, and making recommendations that ultimately impact strategic business decisions. In this role you will partner with key members of the Barkley Strategy and Intelligence teams and support primary and secondary consumer research efforts, data... analysis, data mining, data visualization, brand performance tracking and measurement, and other quantitative research initiatives that deliver results against the client’s specific business and marketing related goals and objectives.

This role is an excellent opportunity for an individual with the right attitude and abilities to strengthen his or her research skill set by working collaboratively with more senior research analysts. To be successful, you need to be passionate and excited about consumer research and data and curious about new techniques and methodologies for generating insights. Agency work is fast-paced and collaborative, so you’ll also need to be a fast learner, pay attention to detail, manage your time effectively, and communicate effectively with a wide range of colleagues, collaborators, and clients.

Responsibilities
• Work with clients and brand strategists to design and execute research that answers critical business questions and helps them grow the business.
• Prepare summaries and reports of findings from consumer analyses and share with internal teams and clients.
• Highlight critical insights from research and help translate findings into strategy and concrete actions.
• Create, program, and launch surveys designed to gather consumer information that drives client strategy. Examples include consumer segmentation studies, new brand or product concept screens, and brand health trackers.
• Clean, reorganize, and recode data to prepare it for analysis.
• Analyze data using a variety of univariate and multivariate statistical techniques to uncover insights that help inform strategic decision-making.
• Prepare crosstabs reports that help summarize survey data.
• Synthesize and summarize data from secondary sources to inform survey content or to make decisions in lieu of primary research (e.g., Census data, Mintel, Gartner/Iconoculture, Euromonitor, etc.)
• Prepare summaries and reports of findings from consumer analyses and share with internal teams and clients.
• Serve as a key partner research resource for internal and client-side brand leaders and marketing teams.

Qualifications
• BS/BA in Marketing, Market Research, Data Analytics, Statistics, Psychology, Sociology or related degree. Graduate degree preferred
• 3 years of experience in a marketing, consumer insights/research, or professional consulting role, prefer experience in the consumer packaged goods, restaurant, retail, travel, finance, or healthcare industry.
• Ability to navigate, utilize and analyze raw data files using analysis software (SPSS or R)
• Ability to deliver actionable business recommendations, influence decisions, and drive results.
• Ability to work with third-party suppliers ensuring they are aligned to our deliverables and are driving impactful outcomes.
• Strong oral and written communication skills, especially the ability to explain difficult concepts and opportunities in simple, applicable business terms.
• Experience with data mining, segmentation, or predictive modeling using large, research or marketing databases.
• Ability to use software to develop crosstabs from raw data files (e.g., Q, MarketSight, Wincross, etc.)
• Experience with data visualization and information design to communicate results for impact.
• Experience with survey design and programming (e.g., Alchemer/SurveyGizmo, Decipher/Forsta, Sawtooth, Qualtrics, SurveyMonkey, etc.)
• Strong analytic thought process and ability to interpret findings.
• Ability to use all MS office software with proficiency and advanced skills in Excel",2022-07-02,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['excel', 'r', 'spss']"
10549,1758,Senior Data Analyst Manager,Tyson Foods,"Springdale, AR","Job Details:

The Senior Data Analyst position requires knowledge of the biological, physical, and engineering sciences that make possible safe and wholesome food products; of food industry facilities, methods, processes, equipment capabilities and limitations; and of relevant laws, regulations, and governmental oversight. This position is responsible for involvement with the planning... development, implementation, and administration of systems for the acquisition, storage, and retrieval of data within the data-based applications and business systems for the internal/external users of the portfolio of the Product Development Management (PDM) systems used across the Enterprise. The Senior Data Analyst may also have responsibility for designing, developing, and implementing training materials including facilitator guides, participant guides, job aids, and computer-based training/learning options. The Senior Data Analyst operates as an internal consultant to IT project teams to provide analysis and definition of data requirements; development and administration of data standards; policies, and procedures; development and implementation of data mining programs; evaluation and recommendations on new database technologies; and ensuring the rigorous application of information security/information assurance policies, principles, and practices in the delivery of data management services. The Senior Data Analyst performs duties with wide latitude for the exercise of independent judgement to perform responsible work of considerable difficulty requiring somewhat extended professional and technical training and experience which has demonstrated important attainments and marked capacity for independent work. Additionally, the Data Manager needs to have knowledge of, and skill in, applying network principles and concepts; systems administration methods and procedures; customer support principles; IT security principles; troubleshooting methods; and utilize communication methods and techniques in providing guidance to our internal/external customers.

REQUIREMENTS:
• Collaborate with IT staff and other technical staff to ensure that the delivered solution and/or system(s) meet the needs of the business.
• Proactively analyze and resolve software, system, or application errors in a timely and accurate fashion.
• Provide status reports as requested and escalate items to decision makers as needed.
• Create and maintain documentation for systems and procedures related to the deliverables expectation.
• Train customers and other team members on usage of systems and solutions.
• Identify cross-functional opportunities to automate the execution of repeatable tasks and simplify system workflows.
• Demonstrate problem-solving skills within area of responsibility and adjacent technology areas.
• Build, maintain, and improve systems to support business processes.

EDUCATION:

Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD in related field of study. Equivalent work experience may be acceptable.

EXPERIENCE:

Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD with a minimum of 2 years relevant experience. No degree with a minimum of 4 years relevant experience.

COMPUTER SKILLS:

Requires strong PC skills including Microsoft Office, project management system(s), graphic management system(s) and all other web-based discipline specific systems.

COMMUNICATION SKILLS:

Requires robust collaboratory and relational ability to work cross-functionally across the Enterprise, with external customers, and consultants. Positive customer service and a team approach are required.

SPECIAL SKILLS (if applicable):

Critical thinking and problem-solving skills required. Strong time-management and organizational skills needed.

SUPERVISORY:

None

TRAVEL:

3+ Trips Per Year

Relocation Assistance Eligible:

Yes

Work Shift:

1ST SHIFT (United States of America)

Hourly Applicants ONLY -You must complete the task after submitting your application to provide additional information to be considered for employment.

