10558,1767,United Healthcare Careers – Data Analyst,United HealthCare,United States,"Job Description:

As a Data Analyst you will be responsible for reporting on operational and business metrics and indicators using a standardized approach. You will create specifications, data models, and solutions to develop actionable insights on business performance. You will partner with business stakeholders to define requirements and develop reports that are meaningful and useful to the... business. You will assist with creating data models. You will work to create report output suited to different needs such as dashboards, data visualizations, and data summarization. You will work collaboratively and provide guidance and input based on what you learn in data review and during the development and test process. This role will also assist with data validation and data analysis.

[ads1]
Job Responsibilities:
• Gather and document requirements from the client/business while focused on process improvement, workflow, benchmarking and/or evaluation of business processes.
• Interact with internal customers to effectively design, implement, operationalize and document reporting that accurately captures business requirements.
