Job Purpose

The primary purpose of the Data Analyst is to provide support to the IT Operations team by analyzing integrated and extensive datasets to extract value which directly impacts and influences business decisions.

The data analyst will be responsible for creating and modifying database structures, establishing guidelines for database design, provide reports and recommendations based upon identified trends.

The ideal candidate should have a natural analytical way of thinking and exceptional attention to details and should be committed to transforming data into readable, goal-driven reports for continued innovations and growth.

Essential Duties and Responsibilities
• Support business and technology needs by creating and modifying database structures as needed
• Recommend improvements to the database structure or Indexing methods to improve performance
• Design solutions for business problems along with plans on deploying them
• Create database schemas that are compatible with existing systems
• Establish guidelines for database design, including database security measures
• Write optimized queries, views and triggers for integration with other applications
• Commissioning and decommissioning of data sets.
• Manage data pipelines and evaluate performance needs
