10631,17,Workday Reporting/Data Analyst,Corporate,"Jefferson City, MO","You could be the one who changes everything for our 26 million members. Centene is transforming the health of our communities, one person at a time. As a diversified, national organization, you'll have access to competitive benefits including a fresh perspective on workplace flexibility. Position Purpose: Responsible for analytic data needs of the business unit. Handle complex data projects and... acts as a lead for other Data Analysts. Provide advanced analytical support for business operations within Workday and external reporting.
Extract, load, model, and reconcile large amounts of data across multiple system platforms and sources within Workday.
Review data to determine operational impacts and needed actions; elevate issues, trends, areas for improvement and opportunities to management.
Develop reports and deliverables and make recommendations to management
Model data using MS Excel
Assist management in driving business decisions based on data
Ensure compliance with federal and state deliverable reporting requirements by performing data quality audits and analysis.
Assist with training and mentoring other Data Analysts.
Assist with determining work load and related activities for other Data Analysts
• This position is offering a one time sign on bonus*

Education/Experience: Bachelor's degree in related field or equivalent experience. 6+ years of statistical analysis or data analysis experience. Workday experience Required. Workday Reporting, Prism Analytics and Integration knowledge. Modules: Core HCM, Recruit, Benefits and Comp are a plus to know. Healthcare experience preferred but not required. Advanced knowledge of Enterprise Reporting and Analysis within Workday and Microsoft Office applications, including Excel and Access. Experience managing projects or heavy involvement in project implementation.

Our Comprehensive Benefits Package: Flexible work solutions including remote options, hybrid work schedules and dress flexibility, Competitive pay, Paid time off including holidays, Health insurance coverage for you and your dependents, 401(k) and stock purchase plans, Tuition reimbursement and best-in-class training and development.

Centene is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity, and values the ways in which we are different. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or other characteristic protected by applicable law",2022-06-24,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['excel']
10632,18,Data analyst ii,Cox Communications,"Tulsa, OK","Description

The Data Analyst II, Cox Mobile role, is part of the Cox Mobile team at Cox Communications. In this role you will be responsible for creating and maintaining high-quality reports, analysis, and ad hoc requests to support the Mobile team...

This position reports to the Director of Cox Mobile Analytics and interacts with a variety of other internal teams (e.g.

Finance, Customer Care, Sales, Marketing, Logistics, Fraud) to set, document, and maintain standards for reporting and analytics.

In this role you will work closely with a data engineer to incorporate new data sets into a single source of truth, as well as review logical data models for long-term data asset growth.

Responsibilities & Essential Functions

Runs analysis on an as-needed or ad hoc basis for partner teams such as Finance, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Customer Care

Acts as a storyteller to uncover insights to business audiences, with actionable next steps or opportunities for improvement

Ability to write complex SQL queries and filter for specific conditions out of existing structured environments

Able to perform data exploration in any environment with targeted problem statements

Identifies analytics solutions to address problems in the domain demonstrating the following abilities :

Correct application of hypothesis testing (T-Tests, Chi-Squared, One-Way ANOVA)

Correct application of simple graphical analysis tools (i.e. Scatterplots, Simple Control Charts (I-MR, P, U)

Conduct simple regression / correlation analyses to understand the relationship between 2+ variables

Conduct basic exploratory data analysis and develop testable hypotheses based on observations

Creating reusable analytical models

Follows best practices and standardizations

Other duties as needed or required

Minimum

Bachelor’s degree in a related discipline and 2 years’ experience in Finance, Customer Care, Sales, Marketing, Logistics, and / or Fraud data sources.

The right candidate could also have a different combination, such as a master’s degree and up to 2 years’ experience; or 6 years’ experience in a related field

2+ years of related data analysis experience.

2+ years with Finance, Customer Care, Sales, Marketing, Logistics, and / or Fraud data sources.

Advanced knowledge and experience with business intelligence & data visualization systems (e.g. Microstrategy, Microsoft Power BI, Qlik, Google Data Studio and / or Tableau).

Strong communication skills, including experience in clearly and effectively presenting to internal stakeholders.

A drive to learn and master new technologies and techniques.

Ability to anticipate stakeholders’ needs and recognize the opportunity to provide proactive insights to build tight thought partnership

Strong organizational skills and the ability to effectively multi-task and prioritize in a deadline-driven atmosphere.

Preferred

Advanced Degree a plus

Experience in the Mobile / Wireless industry

Logistics background is a plus

