10634,20,Data analyst ii,Cox Communications,"Springdale, AR","Description

Cox Communications is seeking analysts who are experienced or interested in learning about ...

Data mining, modeling, analysis, and visualization

Analytical capabilities building and continuous improvement

Using data analysis to assess the results of structured tests

In this role you are part of a team responsible for CCI’s efforts to develop and expand an analytically driven business performance evaluation framework.

You will support the testing, analysis, and reporting function in projects across multiple functional areas of the business, currently including Marketing and Operations Communications, but with potential to scale to other parts of the business as well.

This role is a unique opportunity to help deliver on the vision for a critical analytical capability from the ground up, driving significant and swift impact across the organization, and meaningfully influencing the future of our learning and continuous improvement culture at Cox.

What You’ll Do

Serve as a data mining, visualization, and data analysis subject matter expert, reporting to the Manager or Sr. Manager of Business Optimization

Write reports, creates charts and presentations

Work closely with cross functional partners to establish the necessary process and data infrastructure and requirements to support reporting & analytic needs

Utilize a variety of data, visualization, dashboard and Microsoft Office tools to assemble analysis and storytelling with actionable insights

Represent the team in various cross functional work streams and ad hoc analytical projects

Identifies, researches, and resolves discrepancies in data or analytical methods

What’s In It For You

At Cox, we reward your hard work with meaningful benefits.

First, we offer a highly competitive compensation package, 401(k) with a generous company match, comprehensive healthcare, life, and disability benefits, plus numerous other benefits, including adoption assistance, pet insurance, and discounts on travel and cars!

We value people more than technology. That means you’ll work within a culture and with a team that values your leadership, your experience, your contributions, and you yes, you as a person.

We believe recognition is important, and Cox strives to celebrate those who help make us successful every day. We also encourage diversity and support inclusion;

we want you to do you and feel comfortable doing so.

You’ll find the potential for lateral or upward career growth within the Cox family businesses, including the innovative startups in transportation mobility, clean tech and more.

Minimum

At least one of the following- High school diploma / GED and 6 years of related experience, OR BA / BS degree and 2 years of related experience, OR MS degree and up to 2 years of related experience

Strong collaborative skills to work effectively with teams across the organization to deliver, and potentially present, complex analysis projects

Strong internal client and relationship management emphasis

Creative thinker with a keen attention to detail

Deadline driven : ability to work with a sense of urgency

Proficiency with quantitative tools including Excel and presentation tools such as PowerPoint and willingness to learn new tools that may be valuable to the team

Continuous learner mindset

Preferred

Familiarity with financial modeling techniques

Interest in learning (or prior experience with) statistical analysis methods

Hands on experience with BI and dashboarding tools (MicroStrategy, Tableau, Thoughtspot, etc.)

Hands on experience with data acquisition tools and languages (SQL, etc.)

Bachelor’s degree in engineering, computer science, economics, finance or similar analytical or technical field

Join the Cox family of businesses and make your mark today!

