10651,37,Data Analyst (Marketing),Entain,United States,"About The Role

About Us...

We’re Entain. Our vision is to be the world leader in sports betting and gaming entertainment by creating the most exciting and trusted experience for our customers, and revolutionizing the gambling space as we go. We're home to a global family of more than 25 well-known brands, and with a focus on sustainability and growth, we will transform our sector for our players, for ourselves, and for the good of entertainment.

In 2021, Entain acquired unikrn to launch the company’s esports practice. Unikrn is one of the world’s preeminent esports betting platforms. Unikrn paved the wave in the sports betting industry by offering esports odds across 35 titles, as well as virtual esports and streamer betting. Unikrn also boasts a skill-based betting platform that allows players to wager on themselves in ranked matches in the world’s most popular gaming titles.

Objective of the role:

Performing detailed analysis of the Unikrn business for stakeholders including insights, reporting, modeling, and business intelligence for all products and Marketing activities.

Along with the Head of Quantitative Trading & Analytics, support the roadmap and direction of

Analytics within Unikrn with a focus on innovating and optimizing our product offering, marketing, and business activities. Utilizing analytical and modeling techniques, you will build and optimize existing and new products, Marketing channels, and promotional activities.

On a day-to-day basis, you will work closely with stakeholders across all functions of the business to gather KPI, reporting, data intelligence, optimization, and analysis requirements and execute on those to drive business outcomes. Working closely with our world-class Marketing team, you will scope out tracking and modeling requirements and see them through the development until tested and implemented into production, reporting on outcomes and optimizing where necessary.

Role Responsibilities
• Support strategy and roadmap for Analytics that supports the overall Unikrn business strategy as well as the overall Entain Group strategy
• Support business functions including Marketing, Product, Finance, and Compliance with ad hoc and periodic reporting, insights, and analysis
• Support customer and risk management outcomes by undertaking detailed analysis of business and Marketing performance
• Develop and update Customer segmentation models and reports for the purpose of identifying high-risk and high-value customers
• Develop models to determine the success of business initiatives, past or proposed, including relevant marketing activities
• Develop and maintain business performance reports along with automated self-service BI in Tableau
