10670,56,Accounting Data Analyst,"Koch Industries, Inc.","Wichita, KS","Description

Koch Companies Services is seeking multiple Data Analysts to join our Data Management and Enablement team! The Data Management and Enablement team is focused on safeguarding and maximizing the current and future value of Koch Finance Data Assets...

The ideal candidate is self-motivated, works well through ambiguity, is a creative problem solver with the aptitude to drive change and partner with customers.

By applying to this role, you will be considered for one of the following data product teams:
• Master Data
• Intercompany

What You Will Do In Your Role
• Partner with multiple business groups to understand processes, help determine requirements, develop data quality business rules, and key performance indicators to ensure ongoing and consistent data management
• Partner with customers to understand data problems to support insights and analysis to drive business decisions
• Standardize data structures and finance processes from multiple business groups into an enterprise data platform
• Lead and manage the development process from an end-to-end perspective and support the ongoing management of the requirements in detail
• Facilitate and support testing, identify ingestion errors and identify the SMEs to support testing
• Ensure our data products are updated to meet changing requirements such as evolution of audits, regulatory/government requirements, compliance, etc.
• Knowledge share with other data management analysts across products
• Responsible for documentation to support the Data Team including: the data governance model, requirements, decisions, process flows, etc.
• Assist in developing an enterprise-wide culture of data as an asset
• Design, execute and seek continuous improvement of data products, along with identify other Finance processes or groups with opportunities to leverage the data, share value of data products to other teams and processes and influence change
• Act as a change agent related to business and technical changes within the environment as related to data product
• Work in a SAFe Agile environment

The Experience You Will Bring

Requirements:
• Accounting, tax, and/or finance domain knowledge
• Enterprise-wide data management and analytics experience
• Experience communicating and presenting to various levels within an organization

What Will Put You Ahead
• Specific domain knowledge (trial balance, master data, etc) with a strong understanding of how the data is used in various accounting, finance, and tax processes
• Scrum frameworks and methodology
• Experience building business knowledge through meaningful partnerships at the individual contributor and leadership levels
• Excellent attention to detail and ability to create synergies/draw connections across multiple platforms/disparate systems to drive consistency and reuse in data
• Demonstrate deep curiosity and willingness to trace gaps in metadata (and ultimately quality) back to the originator to address and resolve issues proactively at the source
• Understanding of the data development life cycle and data management principles (ETL/ELT process, SDLC (Software development lifecycle), metadata management, data quality, etc.)
• Experience in understanding and correcting data discrepancies, identifying data anomalies, and root cause analysis
• Experience communicating and presenting to various levels within an organization
• Experience working in finance systems such as ERPs, Alteryx, AtScale, SQL, Tableau, tax provision tools or consolidation tools

