Data Analyst (Entry) BAY1JP00015874

Positions Requested 2

Total Hours 4,160.00

Description:

Data Analyst

YOUR TASKS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

The primary responsibilities of this role, Data Analyst, are to:

Partner with Breeders, Data Scientists and Software Developers to drive data alignment and consistency across the Breeding organization.

Deliver key datasets to enable our delivery of the product pipeline

Develop data assets needed to provide breeding insights to the global organization

Support analytic models and report creation to drive product decisions

Provide analytics and pipeline data support during peak harvest times

Provide framework to support new IT tool implementation and testing

Willingness to support a fast pace and highly critical data flows in shorts amounts of time

Create ad-hoc reporting datasets to leadership

WHO YOU ARE

Your success will be driven by your demonstration of our LIFE (Leadership Integrity Flexibility Efficiency) values. More specifically related to this position, Bayer seeks an incumbent who possesses the following:

(Rate yourself on each line item in Yellow with a score of 1 to 5

5 being the highest-

followed by a slant bar and then a number that represents years of experience with that item i.e; 4/3)-

In addition, anything you show as having a rating should also be in the resume

the higher the rating you give yourself the more enhanced that item should be within the resume

Required Qualifications:

Bachelor of Science with minimum of three years relevant experience; or a Master of Science with one year of relevant experience in life sciences or data analytics fields

Experience with R and/or Python, Java, Linux or other computing languages

Solid experience with PL-SQL a must.

Ability to prioritize tasks and projects

Ability to work as part of multidisciplinary/multicultural team

Excellent oral and written communication skills

Ability to excel in ambiguous environment; thinking objectively and leveraging information to develop corporate strategies and guidelines that effectively balances compliance and operations.

Preferred Qualifications:

Preferred degree in Plant Breeding, Agronomy, Molecular Biology or related discipline.

Two years of experience with Python and R

Project management experience with the ability to drive projects to completion while working under tight timelines.

Proficient in Bayer's enterprise data management and analysis software.

Experience leading IT strategies and building solutions to meet changing business needs.

Additional Information

2 positions

1 backfill

1 new

Duration: 12 months with the potential to go beyond

Site Location: Chesterfield

Remote or Hybrid:

Preference is hybrid - 1 day a week in the office

Open to 100% remote (must be able to work core business hours of 9:00 AM CST - 3:00 PM CST)

Must Haves:

Python is preferred over R; Must have a minimum of 2+ years of experience

SQL is a must: They must be able to do scripting, pulling data out of databases, SQL writing to help reporting, automate data processes, ensure data is set up correctly. Must have a minimum of 2+ years of experience

Reporting tools are preferred: Tableau, Spotfire, etc; We are moving away from Spotfire and we currently have an inhouse reporting that is written in R

Must have excellent communication skills

Interview process:

Phone interview week of the 21st

Interview Panel week of the 28th

Is travel required for this position?

No

Will any tasks within this assignment support Pharma or Consumer Health efforts?

No

Will the work location for this assignment be remote?

Yes

Will work location for this assignment be remote after activation of the hybrid model (post COVID)?

Yes

Worker Shift Start Time

AM - 08:00 AM

Is driving required for this position?

1. No - No driving on a regular basis for company business is required for role

Subcontractor Submittals Allowed?

No

Is Filtered Assessment Required?

No

