10796,182,Lead Business / Data Analyst,"Perficient, Inc",United States,"Overview

At Perficient you’ll deliver mission-critical technology and business solutions to Fortune 500 companies and some of the most recognized brands on the planet. And you’ll do it with cutting-edge technologies, thanks to our close partnerships with the world’s biggest vendors. Our network of offices across North America, as well as locations in India and China, will give you the... opportunity to spread your wings, too.

We’re proud to be publicly recognized as a “Top Workplace” year after year. This is due, in no small part, to our entrepreneurial attitude and collaborative spirit that sets us apart and keeps our colleagues impassioned, driven, and fulfilled.

Perficient is on a mission to help the Healthcare industry take advantage of modern digital solutions, data and analytics architectures, and patterns to improve the quality and affordability of care. We are a fast-paced, innovative team and we take pride in the quality of our people as well as our work. We are a relationship based and people focused environment. We are committed to creating a welcoming and rewarding workplace for clients and employees alike. This is an excellent opportunity for the right individual to assist Perficient and its customers to grow the capabilities necessary to improve care through integrated digital solutions and, in the process, take their career to the next level.

Perficient currently has a career opportunity for a Healthcare Lead Business / Data Analyst as part of our national healthcare team. This job can be remote from any location in the continental US.

Job Overview:

The role of the is reserved for individuals who are passionate about identifying and delivering the right business solution for each client. Our Senior Business Analysts have a keen business orientation with an industry understanding of how technology can be effectively applied to meet a variety of healthcare business needs.

Our Healthcare Lead Business/Data Analyst fills several different roles on our project teams, working with hospitals, health plans, and similar organizations to develop customer-centric digital solutions, leveraging a variety of business processes and technologies. The specific responsibilities vary for each client and each project. Key to the success of our Senior Healthcare Business Analyst is the willingness and desire to quickly learn the client’s business, the unique requirements of each engagement and to fill whatever role may be required to best support our client’s needs.

A Healthcare Lead Business/Data Analyst thrives in challenging environments and accomplishes difficult assignments without significant supervision and instruction. Our Senior Business Analysts can handle the stress of being accountable for supporting delivery and: complete goals on time, practice strong attention to detail, persevere through tough obstacles, and does not get easily discouraged.

The Healthcare Lead Business/Data Analyst is a key delivery point of contact and will be involved in supporting the strategic planning of an engagement or helping the client make decisions about their future business objectives. The Senior Healthcare Business Analyst works directly with the entire project team and assists with daily operations exercising time management, communication, and collaboration in a fast-paced environment to ensure the successful delivery of projects. The Senior Healthcare Business Analyst will interface with Perficient leadership, technical and business delivery personnel, as well as vendors and customers on a regular basis.

Responsibilities

Key Responsibilities
• This is a hands on business analyst role working on a data lake, warehouse, and analytics solution project.
• This role has responsibility for leading the business and data analysis function for a 2 to 5 person analysis team focused on a single workstream of a large data and analytics program.
• This role requires leading the planning and execution of the direct analysis team, hands on creation of reporting/analytics and data requirements documentation, and initial profiling of source data
• This role requires interaction and collaboration with end users, executive stakeholders, business analysts, solution architects, and technical architects.
• This role requires planning, strategizing, organizing and leading facilitated requirements discovery and elaboration sessions (JAD-style sessions)
• This role requires aggregating status from the direct team and communicating status to project leads/managers, architects, and business stakeholders.
• This role requires collaborating with data architects, modelers, other analysts, and business users/stakeholders to elaborate requirements which represent project data requirements, business process models, and complex business hierarchies
• This role requires using Jira to articulate assigned work/tasks/stories, and provide project status to lead architects, project managers, and business stakeholders

Qualifications

Qualifications
• 5+ years collective experience working as a hands on business data analyst for a data warehousing BI Analytics project with similar description as provided above
• 2+ years experience working with accounting department reporting business data analysis (complex manufacturer/supplier sales and fulfilment contract hierarchies)
• 1+ year experience and reasonable comfort working with healthcare PBM or traditional healthcare Payer/Plan product or data and terminology
• Very strong experience creating and documenting business requirements for a reporting and analytics solution
• Strong Experience creating data requirements for reporting solutions
• Experience and comfort working within an Agile Scrum structure with the ability to seamlessly use Jira and confluence for work articulation and tracking
• Must have good SQL skills (6 out of 10) required
• Must have experience working within an Agile Scrum structure with the ability to seamlessly use Jira and Confluence for work articulation and tracking
• Must have extremely strong communication, collaboration, and consulting skills and be very proactive in planning and problem solving

Perficient full-time employees receive complete and competitive benefits. We offer a collaborative work environment, competitive compensation, generous work/life opportunities and an outstanding benefits package that includes paid time off plus holidays. In addition, all colleagues are eligible for several rewards and recognition programs including billable bonus opportunities. Encouraging a healthy work/life balance and providing our colleagues great benefits are just part of what makes Perficient a great place to work.

More About Perficient

Perficient is the leading digital transformation consulting firm serving Global 2000 and enterprise customers throughout North America. With unparalleled information technology, management consulting and creative capabilities, Perficient and its Perficient Digital agency deliver vision, execution and value with outstanding digital experience, business optimization and industry solutions.

Our work enables clients to improve productivity and competitiveness; grow and strengthen relationships with customers, suppliers, and partners; and reduce costs. Perficient's professionals serve clients from a network of offices across North America and offshore locations in India and China. Traded on the Nasdaq Global Select Market, Perficient is a member of the Russell 2000 index and the S&P SmallCap 600 index.

Perficient is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national, origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.

