Our culture is entrepreneurial, team-oriented, collaborative, and fast-paced. If you get excited about stretching yourself in new ways, developing yourself to your fullest potential, and care about working with smart colleagues; we want to talk to you!

Position Overview

The Data Analyst will be a key member of the Data Analytics Team, which finds ways to digest, understand and analyze the complex data derived from its medication management and secure communications platforms. This data combines provider and patient information, allowing our team to understand both the doctor’s intentions and the patient’s actions. Since our products intervene at the critical time between when the doctor writes a prescription to when the patient picks it up at the pharmacy, we can uniquely identify and influence patient behavior.

Your work will primarily focus on client facing analyses and reports . Our ideal candidate drives continuous improvement and brings a strong sense of ownership over the quality of their deliverables. They effectively prioritize and manage multiple projects, deliver results while balancing competing priorities and timelines, and communicate technical integration concepts across business and technical audiences.

Who Will Love This Job
• A Trusted advisor : with strong technical acumen who always strives to do better tomorrow than today, and continuously improve their team’s analysis knowledge and skills
• An Innovator : who thinks outside the box to introduce new methods, ideas and products, and loves building and creating new tools and approaches to improve healthcare
