10851,237,Senior Business Data Analyst,Intuit,"Mountain View, CA","Overview

The CRM Analytics team on the Small Business Data Analytics & Science organization's mission is to deliver delightful customer experiences and drive business impact by surfacing the right messages to the right customers at the right time across all customer touchpoints (web app, in-app, notifications, sms, email, direct mail, sales, customer care etc.). We partner with marketing... product management, design and engineering teams to guide better decisions, automated and human, using data analysis, machine learning and experimentation.

As a Senior Business Data Analyts on the analytics team, you will dive deep into our data to uncover actionable insights and make recommendations that will influence the company's strategic decisions. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in quantitative analysis using large data sets, and in data-driven decision making..

What you'll bring
• BS or MS degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Operations Research, Computer Science, Econometrics or related field
• 5+ years industry experience with a proven track record of leveraging analytics to drive significant business impact
• An advanced degree (M.S., PhD.), preferably in Statistics, Computer Science, Physical Sciences, Operations Research, Economics, or a related technical field
• Advanced SQL skills and proficiency in visualization tools such as Tableau, Plotly Dash
• Strong track record of performing data analysis and modeling using Python (for its rich suite of statistical and modeling libraries like numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, etc.) and SQL
• Quick learner, adaptable, with the ability to work independently or as part of a team in a fast-paced environment
• Outstanding communication skills with the ability to influence decision makers and build consensus with teams
• Experience using statistics and machine learning to solve complex business problems within go-to-market and marketing areas, e.g., propensity for feature adoption, customer health scoring to identify customers at risk to cancel, next best action models etc.
• Familiarity with Linux/OS X command line, version control software (git), and general software development

Preferred Additional Qualifications
• Experience solving growth problems at consumer or SMB technology companies a plus

How you will lead
• Help build the next generation of data products for the QuickBooks Online ecosystem
• Conceptualize business problems or opportunities, formulate hypotheses and goals, define KPIs and make appropriate recommendations
• Partner with Marketing, Product, Engineering and Design teams to:
• Drive data efforts for all customer lifecycle stages, using all the tools in our data science toolkit - personalizing and targeting in our onboarding experiences, recommending features and product experiences that drive retention and monetization
• Develop success criteria and optimize new products, features, and models
• Lead and drive cross functional machine learning/data science projects from beginning to end
• Build relationships with partner teams
• Frame and structure questions
• Collect and analyze data, research, prototype, and build out data science pipelines and models in production
• Develop, deploy and apply advanced predictive models using advanced data machine learning techniques across customer lifecycle
• Summarize and present methodology with key insights driving actions
• Design and measure A/B/n or multivariate experiments to learn and optimize
• Work with our Product Development, Go-to-market Technology, Data Engineering and Machine Learning Platform teams to develop and deploy critical technology for driving growth, such as audience segmentation, communications platforms, experimentation frameworks etc",2022-05-10,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'pandas', 'git', 'scikit-learn', 'python', 'plotly', 'numpy']"
10852,238,Data Analyst - Secret clearance - Remote,GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY,"Fort Smith, AR","Type of Requisition: Regular

Clearance Level Must Be Able to Obtain: Secret...

Public Trust/Other Required: NACLC (T3)

Job Family: Data Analysis

GDIT is seeking an Data Analyst to help support the Duplicate Identity Resolution Processing Team (DIRP-II).

As an Data Analyst for the Duplicate Identity Resolution Processing Team (DIRP-II) , you will contribute to a fast-paced team responsible for monitoring and maintaining Data Quality within very large Oracle production databases at the Defense Manpower Data Center (DMDC) containing military identification information used for healthcare benefits. Work includes both responding to urgent data quality issues as they arise as well as proactive analysis to discover and research previously unknown problem areas. Role has potential for advancement for high-achieving individuals.

This position is 100% remote with minimum travel possible.

In this role, a typical day will include:
• Develop SQL and PL/SQL to find, investigate, and map out strategies to correct data quality issues
• Work closely with other data quality team analysts, management, project managers, business analysts, developers, quality assurance and DBAs to determine root causes for data quality issues
• Devise remediation plans that both prevent future occurrences and restore data that has already been affected
• Actively collaborate with others on business rules underlying the data
• Develop in-depth understanding and knowledge about the variety of data stores, data sources, applications and tiers that make up the DEERS architecture
• Design and administer data collection tools; clean, merge and manage existing data sets as well as establish and maintain data quality procedures to ensure accuracy and timeliness of data
Required Qualifications:
• Active Secret clearance or higher
