10956,342,Data Analyst and Statistics Tutoring Specialist,Adtalem Global Education,Anywhere,"Opportunity at a Glance

Walden’s Office of Academic Support and Instructional Services (OASIS) provides instruction to help students develop academic and professional skills for success. OASIS houses seven teams: the Walden Library; Content Management; Content Operations; Instructional Strategy; and Undergraduate, Graduate, and Doctoral Academic Support. Following Walden’s Success by Degree... framework, we align our instructional support with university-wide, degree-level learning outcomes. Everyone in OASIS collaborates with teams across Walden to ensure we connect students with flexible, seamless instructional support where and when they need it.

Across OASIS, we offer a variety of instructional services and resources to support students’ skill development at all stages of their studies. The Data Analyst and Statistics Tutoring Specialist plays a pivotal role by providing data collection and analysis for OASIS services and resources. This person also offers direct student support as the content lead of OASIS’ team of statistics peer tutors, Walden graduate students who hold synchronous online tutoring appointments with students seeking help in their Walden statistics courses. The person in this role will report to the Associate Dean for Doctoral Academic Support in OASIS.

This role includes opportunities for communication and collaboration with other teams at Walden related both to data analysis and statistics support. Key traits sought for the person in the Data Analyst and Statistics Tutoring Lead role include being creative, strategic, organized, and caring. The person in this role will bring heart to their work with students and with colleagues.

Walden’s Values and Mission

Walden University provides a diverse community of career professionals with the opportunity to transform themselves as scholar-practitioners to affect positive social change. Walden’s commitment to social change began with our founders. Students, faculty, and staff choose Walden because of that commitment, and we keep our values in mind with every action we take.

We are a teaching institution. Online higher education is our specialty, and we emerged early on as pioneers in this field. We are committed to inclusive teaching and learning in all our academic endeavors with intentionality, using a framework of shared accountability to enhance and advance the equitable health and wellbeing of communities, systems, and organizations. The philosophy of our institution is not sink or swim: We meet students where they are and accompany them as they strive to move forward on their academic pathways.

Responsibilities

The Data Analyst and Statistics Tutoring Specialist will perform day-to-day operations in OASIS related to data collection and statistics peer tutoring. Duties include:
• Working with other academic data specialists across the academic team to aggregate degree-level and academic skills outcomes data related to student progress, retention, and graduation
• Using degree-level and academic skills outcome data to determine ongoing academic support improvements. If possible, this same data and other efficacy data should be tracked for specific OASIS products and services.
• Developing and sharing data best practices, both internally to OASIS and externally to the academic team.
• Designing, developing, and maintaining course-based statistics instructional resources for students across all degree levels.
• Tutoring students in statistics and SPSS in synchronous, one-on-one and group sessions.
• Leading statistics peer tutor training, regular meetings, and ongoing professional development.
• Communicating well with students by establishing online rapport and maintaining a friendly, helpful, patient, and interested attitude and demeanor.
• Assisting students in developing their skills by asking questions, helping them understand components of statistics and academic assignments, giving constructive feedback, and referring students to appropriate instructional resources in and beyond OASIS.
• Keeping accurate records showing student contact and progress.
• Contributing to building a positive team culture and a healthy workplace in OASIS and beyond.
• Other duties as assigned.

Based on their experience, the Data Analyst and Statistics Tutoring Specialist will provide instructional support as needed based on students’ needs and team priorities. Support can include:
• Designing engaging and effective instruction in audio, video, or self-paced tutorials.
• Leading and/or co-presenting live instructional sessions, including at online academic residencies required in some Walden doctoral programs, via Microsoft Teams, Zoom, or other platforms.
• Providing instruction in concert with OASIS priorities based on student needs.

The Data Analysis and Statistics Tutoring Specialist also can join OASIS and/or university working groups, engage with university faculty, and participate in professional development opportunities.
Qualifications

Qualified candidates for this role will:
• Have a commitment to advocating for the learning and development needs of adult students earning their degrees in an online, distance-learning environment; experience in providing instructional support to students in online educational programs, preferred.
• Value working with individuals from diverse cultural and professional backgrounds.
• Have demonstrated expertise in advanced statistical concepts, tests, and tools and in using SPSS, Microsoft Excel, and other statistical software programs for data analysis.
• Have demonstrated expertise in data analysis; experience in data visualization preferred.
• Have experience working on a team providing support to students in a university cocurricular instructional department; people management experience in that or related setting, preferred.
• Be flexible in adapting to new responsibilities, initiatives, and priorities based on students’ needs during the academic year and across degree programs.
• Value intellectual curiosity and creativity for staying current in data analysis and statistics tutoring literature and trying new approaches in online academic support.
• Have strong collaboration, problem-solving, organizational, and communication skills.
• Have experience with learning management (e.g., Blackboard, Canvas, Brightspace), customer management (e.g., Banner, LEAP, Salesforce), and/or data management (Tableau, LEAP, Qualtrics) systems and virtual communication tools (Microsoft Teams, Zoom).
• Have experience training graduate assistant staff, preferred
• Have a master’s degree, with educational background and/or professional experience in statistics, research, and data analysis required; past or current doctoral program enrollment, completed doctoral degree, or experience teaching doctoral students, preferred.

TECHNICAL, MANAGERIAL, and PEOPLE SKILLS REQUIRED

To perform this job successfully an individual must be able to perform the range of essential duties satisfactorily. Candidates will be evaluated, in part, based on capabilities related to the range of essential functions. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions.

EEO

We are proud to be an EEO employer M/F/D/V. At Adtalem, we welcome everyone and have a strong commitment towards diversity and inclusion. We encourage our Colleagues to be their true authentic selves and support laws that prohibit discrimination everywhere we do business. We also maintain a drug-free workplace",2022-06-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'spss', 'excel']"
