10977,363,REMOTE BI SQL Developer / Data Analyst,Tential Solutions,Anywhere,"REMOTE BI SQL Developer Job Description

As a Data Analyst / BI SQL Developer on the Assurance Technology Metrics & Reporting team you will play a critical role in the data investigation, wrangling, and visualization processes within our reporting delivery pipeline. Working directly with our business and internal stakeholders you will be responsible for managing the reporting request intake... process, scheduling and leading requirements gathering and data onboarding sessions with various stakeholders, creating final reporting deliverables, and managing report update and decommission requests.

You will be expected to adhere to all internal and external data and privacy guidelines, and to maintain a broad knowledge of various data extraction techniques and Assurance Technology data sources. You will also be expected to maintain a broad knowledge of various data visualization and reporting techniques, leveraging human centered design principles in report creation and delivery.

Our aim is to ensure we deliver value from our client’s data using innovative approaches that improve their data capabilities, analytics and data governance.

REMOTE BI SQL Developer Requirements
• Experience or appetite in building dashboards/reports for clients, using tools such as Microsoft Power BI Desktop and Online (Report and Dataset development and management).
• Experience working with data warehouses, including data warehouse technical architectures, infrastructure components, ETL/ELT and reporting/analytic tools and environments.
• Power BI development experience includes using Power Query and Microsoft DAX (Data aggregation, filtering, lookups, etc.).
• Microsoft Transactional SQL (Data aggregation, transformation, relational table joins, etc.).
• Experience of building, enhancing and utilizing Data Warehousing through SQL, providing Data Analytics, complex data queries and joins and subsequently use of Power BI to present the results.
• Experience in using SQL is essential coupled with other analytics tools, e.g. Power BI.
• Knowledge in SSRS.
• Problem-solving, troubleshooting & analytical skills.
• Ability to juggle multiple projects simultaneously.
• Excellent attention to detail and ability to work to tight deadlines.
• Preferred: Experience with Microsoft Data Factory, Azure Storage Accounts, Microsoft Power Platform, On-Prem data Gateways and Data Flows.

REMOTE BI SQL Developer Benefits
• Collaborative team environment.
• Long Term Opportunity.
• Opportunity for growth in a Big 4 Consulting Firm.
• Working on a Global Project.

REMOTE BI SQL Developer Responsibilities
• Designing and building modern data pipelines and data streams using Azure Data Factory.
• Engineer and orchestrate data flows & pipelines using high quality, easily deployable, repeatable and extensible codebases that ingest and integrate data from many disparate data sources in a cloud environment using a progressive. tech stack. e.g. SQL, Logic Apps, Azure Functions, ADLS, Parquet
• Be able to write and perform SQL scripts to filter and join varied data sets for reporting or querying purposes. Improve existing reporting, code, and procedures.
• Develop Power BI reports and dashboards that connect to various on- and off-premise data sources, ensuring data is optimized.
• Delivering data and reporting requirements to business users and investigating and resolving reporting errors, data discrepancies and queries.
• Collaborating with team members to collect data and produce exception reports to cleanse data at the origin.
• Communicate effectively with internal teams and stakeholders both virtually and in-person, including communication with both technical and non-technical team members.
• Creating and maintaining documentation that includes the design, requirements and user manuals for the organization.
• Create, analyze and support the delivery of regular and ad hoc reports, suggesting improvements and changes where necessary.
• Monitoring of existing data feeds to ensure data integrity.
• Proactive investigations into any data discrepancies or anomalies.
• Your responsibilities will include exploring the data available and looking for trends and valuable analysis that might be useful for the team / Business.
• Conduct unit testing and troubleshooting.
