10980,366,Quantitative Analyst,VGM,United States,"Job Description - Qualitative Analyst

VGM, a leading global market research firm and the largest provider of custom research to the video game industry, is looking for a quantitative analyst to join our team. We provide services for companies such as Amazon, Google, Sonic, and Zynga. Do you enjoy video games or are you interested in the business side of the games industry? Come be a part of a... passionate team of researchers that are experts in this field!

The candidate we are looking for will approach problems and tasks by utilizing their analysis and communication skills. Under general direction, the quantitative analyst cleans, summarizes, and analyzes raw survey data, and also assists in creating reports for clients based on recommendations derived from their analysis. Successful completion of projects involves working with a cross-functional team to provide well-rounded conclusions for key stakeholders.

Responsibilities

Clean, summarize, and analyze raw survey data
Build and review survey drafts to ensure the questions asked will address client objectives
Use quantitative analysis to back up and explain conclusions (often in conjunction with qualitative data), as well as make or support recommendations for clients
Partner with team members from other departments, including qualitative analysts, in creating and peer-reviewing deliverables that offer actionable insights and a cohesive narrative

Requirements

Bachelor's degree in statistics, economics, market research, or related field with 3-4 years of professional analysis/reporting on data driven insights
Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Excel, including use of formula writing, logic statements, pivot tables, and macros
Strong survey writing and logic skills (highly prioritized)
Demonstrated competency in data analysis and visualization
Experience with R and/or Python a plus
A strong interest in the video game industry, with an understanding of how a wide variety of games work and an ability to clearly explain their strengths and weaknesses
Be able to maintain a diligent and flexible working schedule while working from home, working evenings and Saturdays as needed
Communicate effectively and punctually with all team members
A willingness to learn and open to changing project goals
Excellent written and verbal communication skills
Reliable high-speed internet
Candidates including a cover letter are highly prioritized

