10992,378,Data Governance Analyst,Zoox,"Foster City, CA","The Data Governance Analyst position is a business-focused role primarily responsible for implementing and managing relevant Master Data of SAP S/4HANA covering end-to-end Supply Chain areas. The ideal candidate will have working experience with data governance standards, policies, and practices for master data management in SAP S/4 HANA, Product Lifecycle Management, and other manufacturing... systems. This person will be strong in corresponding business processes and related project implementation pertaining to Master Data Governance. The candidate will use in-depth analysis skills, business knowledge, and technical expertise to implement effective Master Data and provide support services to end-users. This person will be strong in execution capabilities and will report directly to Senior Program Manager for Data Governance.

Responsibilities
• Able to completely understand and manage SAP Master Data objects like Material Master, Bills of Material, Routings, Work Centers, Production Versions, Business Partner (Supplier), Engineering Change Management, etc
• Ensure data quality, metadata management, compliance, and consistency of master data across business systems (PLM, SAP, MES, and other systems) to achieve a scalable digital ecosystem
• Create/ support a master data governance framework and rules
• Educate users on the basics of data governance and master data management including data dictionaries, business glossary, 6Ws, data standards, lineage, etc.
• Support the business with required master data management procedures and submit incidents and change requests when needed to comply with the Master Data governance rules
• Assist business process experts in defining standard operating procedures, process flows, and related documentation
• Work collaboratively with the Technology team for data management and governance across enterprise solutions like 3DX(PLM), SAP S4/HANA, SAP-ME
• Completely understand the lineage of master data of an automotive manufacturing industry (or similar industries)
• Centralize data collection among multiple business areas. Measure and report data volumes and growth. Establish and communicate data governance standards and expectations.
• Facilitate training sessions for the users wherever appropriate.
• Ensure appropriate support to projects and new development is followed (i.e. scope, design, test plans, issues, cutover, project plans, go-live, etc).
• Demonstrate effective team skills with strong oral and written communication on deliverables and facilitate the issue resolution process by tracking the status of issues in the process.
• Flexible and able to adapt to a high-growth environment. Comfortable working in a dynamic and ambiguous startup environment.
• Excellent communication and presentation skills

Qualifications
• Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, related field, or equivalent work experience
• A minimum of 7 years of experience with Data Management solutions such as Collibra, IBM IGC/ UG&I, Talend, or any equivalent toolset
• SAP experience in MDM/MDG (Master Data Management) dealing with MM, PP, QM, WM/EWM modules (like Material Master, Bills of Materials, Routing, Change Management, Work Centers, Production Versions, Business Partners, etc)
• Previous experience of full life-cycle of Master Data Management project experience with expertise in PLM integration and MM / PP / QM / WM / EWM Modules with a strong understanding of Master Data integration points involved in all these areas.
• Experience with SAP S/4HANA implementation is highly desirable.
• Understanding of functional and technical objects in SAP Master Data
• Understands SAP best practices, business processes, operational procedures, and the relationships between various SAP Modules in a manufacturing establishment.
• Should be able to prepare Master Data Specification for SAP Master Data if required for the business with strong tracking, coordination, and project participation skills and proven ability to follow change management procedures and internal guidelines
• Demonstrated initiative with commitment and ability to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines while still maintaining high-quality standards
• Strong communications to work with business users and management from across the company for Master Data projects, and to collaborate with external consultants and vendors.

Vaccine Mandate

Employees working in this position will be required to have received a single dose of the J&J/Janssen COVID-19 vaccine OR have completed the two-dose Pfizer or Moderna vaccine series.In addition, employees will be required to receive a COVID-19 booster vaccine by the earlier of (1) April 15 or (2) within two months of becoming eligible for the booster vaccine.

Employees will be required to show proof of vaccination status upon receipt of a conditional offer of employment. That offer of employment will be conditioned upon, among other things, an Applicant’s ability to show proof of vaccination status. Please note the Company provides reasonable accommodations in accordance with applicable state, federal, and local laws.

About Zoox

Zoox is developing the first ground-up, fully autonomous vehicle fleet and the supporting ecosystem required to bring this technology to market. Sitting at the intersection of robotics, machine learning, and design, Zoox aims to provide the next generation of mobility-as-a-service in urban environments. We’re looking for top talent that shares our passion and wants to be part of a fast-moving and highly execution-oriented team.

Follow us on LinkedIn

A Final Note:
You do not need to match every listed expectation to apply for this position. Here at Zoox, we know that diverse perspectives foster the innovation we need to be successful, and we are committed to building a team that encompasses a variety of backgrounds, experiences, and skills.

