11116,502,Senior Data Analyst I,Unite Us,United States,"About the Role:

Unite Us seeks an experienced Senior Data Analyst ready to tackle an array of data challenges and advance data-driven decision making across the business. Unite Us brings health care and social services together into a single, integrated network. We believe the network creates value beyond the sum of its parts, and our Analytic mission is to measure and enhance that impact...

The Senior Analyst will work with internal and external stakeholders to solve the company’s most pressing data and analytics challenges. This includes measuring and improving product outcomes, delving into usage dynamics and deeply understanding our user base. This role will also include a heavy customer-facing component including gathering requirements, evaluating and improving current processes and data storytelling to internal and external stakeholders. The Analyst must be both highly quantitative and possess strong business acumen and communication skills while being a team player across the company. The Analyst will independently decompose amorphous problems, gather and analyze data, and go ‘beyond the numbers” by creating synthetic output and recommendations. If you love numbers, driving practical application of analytics in a growth environment and want to work with a passionate and growing team, this is the role for you.

What You’ll Do:
• Design and build client reporting in Tableau, from the ground up
• Work with cross-functional teams to understand current client reporting, needs and define critical outcome measures
• Design, build and maintain a set of client-facing as well as internal dashboards and reports, refining over time to improve and scale across audiences
• Work with other teams at Unite Us to understand and support ad-hoc data needs
• Support key accounts and company initiatives proving a strategic and operational data lens, providing solutions and adding to the overall vision
• Work with customers, internal stakeholders and leadership to understand and evaluate priorities and objectives; ensuring our Insights products are rolled out successfully
• Drive data-driven decision making across Unite Us
• Deeply understand business opportunities and constraints, then specify analytic work to solve them
• Be self-sufficient at extracting and manipulating data; work creatively to solve data challenges
• Go beyond running the numbers: interpret what they mean and recommend actions
• Communicate learnings and Unite Us impact to the entire company, customers and industry players; ensure that stakeholders, customers and executives are informed about our findings and contributions
• Partner with customers and Insights team members on how to turn analytic products and tool into a community action, identify use cases for sharing with stakeholders

You’re A Great Fit For This Role If You Have:
• Strong analytical, problem-solving skills and a passion for turning data into actionable insights
• You like to teach others, are an active listener who can break down complex ideas and tailor your message to a specific audience, and have experience briefing leadership on outcomes and recommendations
• You are flexible and excited to work in a fast-paced environment with evolving needs
• At least 4 years of work experience as a Quantitative Analyst
• Experience with healthcare data is preferred; background in public health is a plus
• Bachelor’s/Master’s degree in a quantitative field strongly preferred
• Ability to self-serve data and work with multiple modern data tools & technologies including SQL and BI platforms (Tableau, Looker)
• Broad and deep quantitative skills, ranging from basic to cutting edge. Experience with analytics and scripting tools like Python and R is expected
• Expert with Google G Suite, Microsoft Office Suite

Environmental Job Requirements & Working Conditions:
• This position is remote, U.S. based
• Our target range for this position is $85,000-95,000
• ***This salary range represents our national target range for this role. Some geographic areas may have higher target ranges.*
• You will only be contacted by a Unite Us team member with a Unite Us email address regarding any Unite Us job openings. We will never contact you through a third party.

Unite Us is committed to building a diverse team and fostering an inclusive culture, and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We embrace and encourage our employees' differences in race, religion, color, national origin, gender, family status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, veteran status, disability, pregnancy, medical conditions, and other characteristics. If you require assistance in applying for open positions due to a disability please email us at peopleops@uniteus.com to request an accommodation.

