11165,551,Strategy Analyst II - Financial Planning and Analysis,EDWARD JONES,"Bruner, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.
The Financial Planning & Analysis area is seeking a Strategy Analyst II to support our firm's Digital function team. We are responsible for financial planning & analysis, management reporting and evolving financial planning processes.
The successful candidate will be a self-starter who partners well in a collaborative manner to support our Finance and Digital area stakeholder's ability to make timely financial impacting decisions while championing financial stewardship.

Role Responsibilities
• Develop an internal network of relationships in current function, to act as a trusted partner for stakeholders to rely on.
• Advanced analysis skills, forecasting/outlooking, reporting and complex modeling.
• Conducting analysis that facilitates the transformation of complex data/information into actionable insights.
• Understand and identify opportunities to apply different types of statistics and advanced analytical concepts.
• Prepare customized management-level reports and dashboards in support of the Firm's initiatives or programs.
• Summarize complex information and concepts and clearly communicate up to Senior Management
• Verbal & written presentation of analysis, as well as presentation of firm financial information and analytical insights to senior Firm leaders. Educate Firm Leaders on analytical concepts and best practices.
• Develop and manage business relationships with Finance associates, project team members and senior leaders across the organization. Participate in cross-functional teams responsible for implementing projects in support of divisional and firm-wide business objectives; occasionally lead cross-functional teams responsible for divisional objectives.
Education and Experiences
• Bachelor's degree in a related field
• Advanced Degree (MBA / MSF) / Comparable Certifications (CFA, CPA, etc.) preferred
• 4+ years of relevant work experience
• Experience in Technology or Digital financial planning is a plus
Skills and Abilities
• Creation of financial budgets, proactive cost management, and financial estimating
• Understanding operating and capital expenditures
• Ability to connect the dots to ensure processes are integrated
• Ability to operate in ambiguous situations, create processes enhancements that address short term needs while moving us closer to the more longer-term vision
• Identify trends and present recommendations to Senior Leadership in order to influence decision making
• Ability to plan and organize efficiently and effectively
• Ability to analyze problems and recommend solutions to divisional and firm-wide leadership for a broad spectrum of business improvement opportunities in a clear and concise manner.
• Ability to collaborate well with associates and leadership throughout the firm, including external vendors.
• Strong written and verbal communication
• Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) required, including demonstrated ability to utilize pivot tables, advanced charting, advanced formulas, and conditional formatting
• Working knowledge of PeopleSoft Financials, OneStream or a financial planning tool is a plus
