11183,569,Senior Financial Analyst / Business Analyst / Data Analyst – Remote,Four Pillars Talent,United States,"Senior Financial Analyst / Business Analyst / Data Analyst - Finance Team - Remote

Are you innately curious, passionate about building impactful analyses and a truth seeker using data? Are you a SQL, PowerBI, data mining and reporting whiz that can synthesize data to help make meaningful business decisions? Our client is looking for an individual to join its Global Finance and Business Analytics... team to boost it's growing business. The Finance team ensures data driven decision-making throughout the company. You're a problem-solver, who uses both quantitative and qualitative methods to get things done. And most importantly, you are an individual who wonders ""What if?"" and are passionate about seeking out the solution.

You will play a meaningful role in how they bring data to everything with your expertise and passion to help address the data and analytical needs of our client. Your knowledge of data, along with deep business context, and willingness to take action will ensure our client's finance organization and Business Leaders are well-informed and able to make decisions backed by data.

Location: Remote within the US (Excluding Alaska and Hawaii)

Benefits for you:
• 100% Remote position with occasional travel as needed (less than 5%)
• Excellent compensation package, comprehensive medical benefits, generous vacation, plus paid holidays
• Ability to fast track your career vertically in a dynamic and growing company
• Broad scope of responsibilities so you won't get bored or pigeonholed into one area of finance
• Work with a dynamic progressive team and collaborate with some of the best minds in the business
• Opportunity to work with an exceptional Finance Leadership team that truly values and appreciates their team
• Have great mentors to help push your personal growth & development
• Stability and job security within a larger organization

Responsibilities that you'll oversee
• Support our strategic and financial planning processes, financial forecasts as well as the underlying financial planning models, systems and tools.
• Develop and monitor key performance indicators and analyzing causes of unexpected variances. Work with team members to enhance global operational performance trends (historical and forecasted) using appropriate metrics.
• Manipulate and analyze large and complex data sets to distill insights from data; connect disparate ideas into cohesive, well-grounded recommendations using creative, effective, structured and analytical thinking.
• Design, develop and automate dashboards and business analytics for Executive Leadership and Business Managers at scale.
• Orchestrate expert level data visualizations and internal presentations that translate analytic insights into tangible, measurable solutions for business partners to implement.
• Understand the requirements of business partners and map them with the data sources/data warehouse
• Execute high priority (i.e. cross functional, high impact) projects to improve operations performance
• Partner with Sales, Product, Engineering, Marketing, Finance and other Operational teams to define the data elements and data structure that the team should use to enable analytical capabilities
• Collaborate with business customers for requirements and delivering complete reporting solutions.
• Standardize data and report consumption across all operations groups.
• Make recommendations for new metrics, techniques, and strategies to improve the operational metrics.
• Automate reporting to save time and enhance decision making process real time for executive leaders across the organization

Ideal Background Profile
• This role is for doers; be able to get into the details and get the job done while at the same time being able to see the forest for the trees
• High degree of intellectual curiosity and forward thinking, wants to understand the ""why"" of what's driving the business or underlying issues as they occur
• Articulate with excellent verbal and written communication skills. Capable of communicating complex information in an easy to understand format. Able to interact comfortably with the cross functional leadership
• Ability to think creatively; Builder who is ambitious. Highest standards of accuracy and precision; highly organized
• Collaboratively-focused and able to work well with others in a fast-paced and growing business
• Data Warehouse data mining and manipulation experience is needed
• Experience with SQL, Python, R or coding in general a huge plus
• Experience with business and data analytics and visualization tools (Tableau, Power BI, Business Intelligence, Advanced Excel) with hands-on experience using SQL across different relational databases
• Experience owning complex projects involving multiple teams
• Bachelors in Accounting, Finance, MIS, Business or Data Analytics

Salary is commensurate with experience and expertise.

Exploratory conversations are currently being conducted, for immediate consideration or interest, please let us know.

Though we'd love to see your resume, we don't need to in order to have a conversation. Send me an email to shane (at) and let me know what is appealing to you about this role, and why you feel you're qualified. Please give me some real life tangible examples to illustrate the key objectives this position is trying to achieve relating to your experience with SQL, PowerBI and using data and business analytics to analyze operations and reporting that you've created to help executive leadership make informed business decisions. Get me excited to represent you! Tell me about the impact you made.

Please note that we have been receiving an extremely high level of interest in our remote opportunities. We are trying to review everyone's background and appreciate your patience. We may not be able to respond to everyone individually and are not trying to be rude and apologize in advance. We would encourage you to follow the Four Pillars Talent LinkedIn company page as new opportunities are posted as there will likely be future roles that align. You are welcome to send invites to connect with Shane Fairchild as well as I believe that helps alert you when new opportunities are posted.

All applicants applying for U.S. job openings must be authorized to work in the United States. These positions are not eligible for sponsorship.

© 2022 Four Pillars Talent. An Equal Opportunity Employer M/F/Disability/Veterans",2022-11-11,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'power_bi', 'power_bi', 'python', 'sql', 'excel', 'r']"
11194,580,Data Analyst III - Full Time - Days,Mercy,"Springfield, MO","We’re a Little Different

Our mission is clear. We bring to life a healing ministry through our compassionate care and exceptional service...

At Mercy, we believe in careers that match the unique gifts of unique individuals – careers that not only make the most of your skills and talents, but also your heart. Join us and discover why Modern Healthcare Magazine named us in its “Top 100 Places to Work.”

Overview:

Responsible for a variety of functions that are specific to drug management for Mercy. The person in this position participates in formulary management, drug use care management projects, database design and development, data query for clinical and administrative reports, customer service related to pharmacy claims, and education distribution for physicians, patients, and other health professionals. Performs related duties as assigned. Performs duties and
responsibilities in a manner consistent with our mission, values, and Mercy Service Standards.

Qualifications:
• Preferred Education:Bachelor of Science (BS) or Arts (BA)
• Preferred Experience:Minimum 3 years experience in related field
• Other: Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities: Possess highly proficient
customer-relations skills with ability to communicate properly
with a wide-variety of professional sources (e.g. physicians,
nurses, patients, administration, etc.). Experience with Microsoft
Windows XP and strong working knowledge of Office
applications (Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint), with high
emphasis on Microsoft Access and Excel. Able to learn other
software to support assigned tasks.
• Must be highly motivated,task-oriented and possess proper time-management and organizational skills with ability to adhere to crucial timelines.
• Proficient in general mathematics and basic statistical analysis.
Good working knowledge of medical and pharmaceutical
terminology.
• Outstanding oral and written communication skills.
Commitment to accuracy, thoroughness, and excellence. Must
have a demonstrated history of excellent work attendance and
dependability.

We Offer Great Benefits:

Day-one comprehensive health, vision and dental coverage, PTO, tuition reimbursement and employer-matched retirement funds are just a few of the great benefits offered to eligible co-workers, including those working 48 hours or more per pay period!

We’re bringing to life a healing ministry through compassionate care.

