11215,601,Senior Data Analyst,Cypress.io,United States,"*This position is eligible to be hired virtually within the US or locally in Atlanta, GA

At Cypress.io, we're on a mission to make software testing delightful and effective and thus dramatically improve the efficiency and quality of modern software development. Today, Cypress provides better, faster, and more reliable testing for anything that runs in a browser. Hundreds of thousands of... developers and QA professionals use Cypress to write better code faster and release with confidence.

Cypress is currently used in over 90 countries by hundreds of thousands of developers across more than 30,000 organizations. Cypress has over 2,500 customers in more than 60 countries across 45 industries and includes marquee names like Atlassian, Crunchbase, GitHub, PayPal, and Slack.

The company was founded in 2015 and has raised $55M in capital to date, including a $40M Series B financing in November 2020, led by OpenView Partners, with participation from Bessemer Venture Partners, Battery Ventures, Sapphire Ventures, and Stripes.co.

Who You are:

This Senior Data Analyst role will increase our speed to insight around key business questions from our various stakeholders and expand the data team capabilities in many critical areas of Cypress.

This person will work with our existing team of Data Scientists and across Cypress partnering with RevOps, Marketing, Sales, Finance, Product and Support functions. You will be responsible for providing data insights, reporting as well as providing accurate and timely data for ad hoc/one-off requests to support and enable data driven decision-making for various stakeholders.

Successful candidates will work cross-functionally with key business partners and will come prepared with new ideas and a unique point of view. You have the ability to execute and can manage multiple projects, fulfill priorities and meet deadlines. You are a data junkie that knows what quality data means and what will help to improve it.

Responsibilities:

• Partner with leadership on the best approach for what data is needed and the methodology required to solve complex root cause analysis on business problems to identify insights that inform and drive key business decisions.
• Standup reports/dashboards that deliver a high degree of quality, timeliness, and accuracy in reporting as well as clearly showcasing any discovered insights to help drive better decisioning.
• Ability to extract data (from a variety of sources like Redshift, Postgres and Salesforce) and perform detailed data analysis on internal processes and productivity.
• Lead goal setting, tracking and defining reports, and supporting company-wide metrics (Board reviews, QBRs, and OKRs (Objectives and Key Results)) through a regular cadence for daily, weekly, monthly reporting and analytics.
• Process monthly and quarterly sales commissions and support the Sales Organization with commission inquiries/requests.
• Support quarterly and annual sales comp plan review, providing research on best practices of incentive plan design, metrics, and quota setting.
• Manage the annual and quarterly budget planning processes, including the development of operating models resource allocation and market segmentation.
• Engage in ad-hoc projects, month-end close activities, and reconciliations as needed.
• Enable effective decision making by retrieving and aggregating data from multiple sources and compiling it into a digestible and actionable format.
• Work cross-functionally with our Product team to reconcile, identify/define problems to implement processes and standards that inspire trust with data and provide consistent metrics across the organization.
• Create presentations that capture key operational metrics, articulate results, and convey actionable business insight for both sales management and executive audiences.
• Provide and support ad-hoc reporting services for non-standard issues and analysis.

Qualifications:

• 5+ years of relevant sales/business/finance operations experience with solid understanding of SaaS business models.
• Past experience building complex financial and forecast models.
• Advanced experience working with various BI tools (Tableau, Looker etc.) **required**
• Advanced experience with SQL **required**.
• Demonstrated ability to partner with various stakeholders in building intuitive and actionable dashboards and data visualizations that drive business decisions.
• You are able to breakdown down fuzzy business questions into actionable and useful data insights
• Attention to detail, accuracy, resourcefulness, and ability to follow-through
• Ability to thrive in a changing environment and to manage and prioritize multiple initiatives
• Intermediate ability in statistical analysis preferred.
• Strong technical skills are preferred in order to better understand the Cypress product.
• Ability to understand/write python/R scripts (Pandas/dyplr) is a bonus.
• Experience with DBT is also a bonus.

Talent Attributes - what we look for in all hires at Cypress

• Self awareness: you seek to understand your own behaviors, actions, emotions and traits in an effort to continually improve and develop.
• Collaboration: you work together towards a shared goal, not in service of individual needs.
• Stage Appropriateness: you have experienced growth and scale and understand the impact it has on individual roles, decision making, prioritization and our vision.
• Intrinsic Motivation: you are driven by an internal desire to achieve, succeed and contribute
• Intellectual Curiosity & Agility: you have a perpetual need to learn new information, and with exposure to it you’re able to adopt and modify your thoughts, solutions and outcomes.

#LI-Remote

Although we list out what we generally look for, we are very likely missing other attributes and skills that you have that could make you a great fit, and are not currently listed. Research has shown this especially applies to women and other marginalized groups, who tend to apply if they check 100% of every box, versus men who apply if they hit roughly 60%. The point we’re getting at, it doesn’t hurt to take a chance and apply!

We are an inclusive employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status",2022-07-17,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'atlassian', 'looker', 'postgres', 'sql', 'redshift', 'github']"
