11224,610,"Sr PX Data Analyst, Support & Delivery",Zoom,"Jefferson City, MO","Work Styles at Zoom

In most cases, you will have the opportunity to choose your preferred working location from the following options when you join Zoom: in-person, hybrid or remote. Visit this page for more information about Zoom's Workstyles () ...

About Us

Zoomies help people stay connected so they can get more done together. We set out to build the best video product for the enterprise, and today help people communicate better with products like Zoom Contact Center, Zoom Phone, Zoom Events, Zoom Apps, Zoom Rooms, and Zoom Webinars.

Were problem-solvers, working at a fast pace to design solutions with our customers and users in mind. Here, youll work across teams to deliver impactful projects that are changing the way people communicate and enjoy opportunities to advance your career in a diverse, inclusive environment.

Description

Zoomies help people stay connected so they can get more done together. We set out to build the best video product for the enterprise, and today help people communicate better with products like Zoom Contact Center, Zoom Phone, Zoom Events, Zoom Apps, Zoom Rooms, and Zoom Webinar.

Were problem-solvers, working at a fast pace to design solutions with our customers and users in mind. Here, youll work across teams to deliver impactful projects that are changing the way people communicate and enjoy opportunities to advance your career in a diverse, inclusive environment.

Zoom's Senior People Data Analyst, Delivery & Support will be an expert and strategist who partners with peers across the Talent Acquisition, People Experience (PX), and business Leadership teams to provide novel insights that support business decisions. You will report to the Head of PX Data & Insights.

You will leverage your stakeholder and request management expertise with your understanding of analytics and insights development to deliver on requests and provide research to stakeholders across Talent Acquisition (TA), People Experience (PX), and the business. As a foundational member of the PX Data & Insights team, Your knowledge and expertise in support and training will be critical to delivering on the near-term project management and request delivery strategy. As you are producing near-term request deliverables, your consultation will guide strategic and long-term plans for both support and delivery. You will collaborate with many customers to propel business changes driven by insight interpretation and stakeholder engagement.

About the Role
• Develop, implement, and drive the Delivery & Support portion of the overall PX Data & Insights strategy and roadmap
• Contribute to the process of initially evaluating and continually maintaining current-state and future-state documentation around metric availability, analytic solution availability, and the associated roadmap driving the continued expansion of available PX Data & Insights solutions
• Consult stakeholders, customers, requestors, and the team on maximizing the utilization of available solutions in a standardized and efficient manner while also keeping a record of solutions that have been requested and should be slotted for development or placed in the backlog
• Design analytic solutions through requirements intake for requests, developing wireframes, and engaging in a feedback/sign-off process with the stakeholders for each respective solution, where applicable
• Manage prioritization of planned deliverables through continual additions and iterations of all data visualization and reporting solutions applicable to people functions
• Maintain business ownership of Support & Delivery involving cross-functional partnerships and strategies with Talent Acquisition, People Experience, each business vertical, and the corporate systems and IT team supporting the people function
• Deliver on-time, accurate data visualizations (both request-driven and strategy/roadmap-driven) and insights through partnership, requirements receipt, and resulting development - working with peers on the PX Data & Insights team and in coordination with stakeholders
• Deliver ad-hoc requests that are driven by business needs and reconcile these requests against existing solutions and infrastructure to determine existing self-service options and the need to deliver an automated solution for continued usage
• Drive adoption of analytic solutions and evangelism around the TA data function ranging from operational influence for better data generation to training and troubleshooting solutions with end-users and stakeholders
About You
• 4 6 years of analytical experience with 2+ years in HR/Talent Acquisition specific functions
• Experience reporting and dashboarding critical business data throughout its lifecycle and among its applications
• Experience collaborating cross-functionally and driving successful initiative implementation
• Experience supporting ad-hoc requests and project work in addition to stakeholder management
• Knowledge of the following domains, systems, and technologies:
• Source System/ External Data Technologies (e.g. Workday, EZHire, Clinch, GoodTimes, LinkedIn, .Gov, Glassdoor, Finance, Textio, SFDC, Anaplan, and more)
• Integration Technology/Applications (e.g. APIs, Informatica, Mulesoft, Alteryx, Knime)
• Database Technologies, SQL/ DB Applications (e.g. Snowflake, OracleDB, Postgres, Redshift, SAP HANA, Google Big Query, Hadoop)
• AI/ML technologies
• Data Science principles and applications
• Data Modeling applications
• Solution Systems (e.g. Tableau, PowerBI, Anaplan)
• Server Technology/Applications (e.g. S3, 2012R2, Virtualization)
• Data Modeling and Science technologies (e.g. dataIKU, Knime, Alteryx, R, Python)
• Security Standards (e.g. TLS1.3+, Technology Security Review Process, Role & Permission Lineage)

