11255,641,Data analyst – finance,PlayStation,United States,"Why PlayStation?

PlayStation isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Today, we’re recognized as a global leader in entertainment producing The PlayStation family of products and services including PlayStation®5, PlayStation®4, PlayStation®VR, PlayStation®Plus, acclaimed PlayStation software titles from PlayStation Studios, and more...
PlayStation also strives to create an inclusive environment that empowers employees and embraces diversity. We welcome and encourage everyone who has a passion and curiosity for innovation, technology, and play to explore our open positions and join our growing global team.
The PlayStation brand falls under Sony Interactive Entertainment, a wholly-owned subsidiary of Sony Corporation.

Role Overview

The Strategic Insights Analyst will be a crucial pillar of PSS Finance’s data-driven business support capabilities. Capitalising on the collective skillsets, KPI standards and data sources already established within the PSS Finance division, they will work alongside the Strategic Insights Lead to ensure enthusiastic delivery of PlayStation Studios’ strategic objectives.
Together, they will mould Strategic Finance into a proactive, high integrity and indispensable resource. This is a rare opportunity for a trustworthy, entry-level candidate to join PlayStation Studios at a more senior level. The ideal candidate will have knowledge of and a passion for the gaming industry, alongside technical skills gained at graduate level or above.
The Strategic Insights Analyst will report to the Strategic Insights Manager/Lead, housed within the PlayStation Studios Finance. Given the fast-changing nature of the industry and its technologies, the right candidate should expect new responsibilities to emerge over and above those listed below. Location is flexible, with the option to work remotely, provided work can also be carried out on-site at PlayStation Studios offices when required on key projects, in-person work meetings etc.

What you’ll be doing:
• Undertake standardised reporting functions (in particular, those previously carried out by the Senior Business Analyst, PSS Financial Planning & Analysis, e.g. weekly digital sales reports)
• Become fluent with PSS Finance and wider SIE metadata, undertaking master data management to underpin their knowledge for higher-level tasks
• Provide ad-hoc analysis for PSS Finance and studio directors, producers and analysts, as well as the wider SIE, as signalled by the Strategic Insights Manager/Lead
• Transform neutral data into useable insights, helping to provide PSS titles with a competitive edge from the perspective of PSS Finance
• Become a subject matter expert over time on data points and sources available within the team to PSS (and the wider SIE on behalf of PSS), both in terms of their definitions and their appropriate usage
• Assist the Strategic Insights Manager/Lead to develop the capabilities of the Strategic Insights team
• Understand and undertake some of the duties of the Strategic Insights Manager/Lead in their absence
• Represent the team as appropriate in cross-functional meetings
• Continued development of analytical- and advanced SQL skills and Snowflake
• Promote the value of PSS & DSO metadata and best practices
• Contribute to a healthy team environment in which everyone can share in their success

What we’re looking for:
• Data Science undergraduate degree or similar including SQL skills, Snowflake and/or two years+ of practical business intelligence experience inc. with SQL
• Extensive videogame knowledge, able to demonstrate a fluent understanding of genre, gameplay, monetisation methods and industry trends
• Self-starter, showing initiative and the ability to work with minimal supervision, as well as within a team
• Enthusiasm for forensic exploration of data, data discovery and interrogation
• Ability to translate data into analysis, and analysis into insights
• Knowledge of best practice with regards to data integrity, consistency and cleanliness
• Strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills
• Proficiency in MS Excel and MS PowerPoint
• Fluent English speaker, able to write in a highly professional manner to the highest levels of the business
• Strong work ethic and adherence to maintaining strict confidentiality essential
• Ability to solve problems creatively and implements workable solutions
• Ability to manage multiple projects, in high profile and time-pressured environments

Desirable Skills:
• Exposure to or understanding of basic financial concepts such as P&L
• Familiarity with visualisation tools e.g. Tableau, Looker
• Familiarity with BI tools e.g. Cognos, MicroStrategy, PowerBI

Equal Opportunity Statement:

Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy or maternity, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.
We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.
PlayStation is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.

Tagged as: Business, Curiosity, Data Management, Financial Planning, Innovation, Metadata, Sales, Trustworthy",2022-03-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'microstrategy', 'looker', 'snowflake', 'power_bi', 'cognos', 'powerpoint', 'sql', 'excel']"
11256,642,Senior BI & Data Analyst,"Charles River Laboratories, Inc.",United States,"At Charles River, we are passionate about improving the quality of people’s lives. When you join our global family, you will help create healthier lives for millions of patients and their families.

Charles River employees are innovative thinkers, who are dedicated to continuous learning and improvement. We will empower you with the resources you need to grow and develop in your career...

As a Charles River employee, you will be part of an industry-leading, customer-focused company at the forefront of drug development. Your skills will play a key role in bringing life-saving therapies to market faster through simpler, quicker, and more digitalized processes. Whether you are in lab operations, finance, IT, sales, or another area, when you work at Charles River, you will be the difference every day for patients across the globe.

Job Summary

We are seeking an experienced Senior Business Intelligence (BI) & Data Analyst for our Enterprise Data Analytics Team.

There’s never been a more exciting time to be on the Enterprise Data Analytics team at Charles River Labs! We are on a mission to make the Enterprise Data Analytics team be the backbone of today’s business, as data-driven decision-making enables business leaders to make informed choices quickly to boost revenue, improve productivity, and stay a step ahead of the market. We have already launched our own Enterprise Data Hub, the digital backbone of this company, and we need more experts and leaders in the data analytics discipline who are forward thinking, self-guided and innovative to continue to build out the hub across our lines of business, integrating all of our data, mastering data and focusing on data quality to fundamentally shift the way Charles River operates through data science and advanced analytics.

You will be joining a team with an unyielding dedication to the company purpose; Together We Create Healthier Lives. This laser focus on the patient makes the boarder Global Technology Team so exciting. As we look to our company’s future, we are embarking on a reimagination of how we do business through a Digital Journey. Our Digital Journey is about sustaining and advancing our position to unlock our next horizon of growth and become a leading ‘digitally-powered’ CRO enabling our clients to deliver innovative, safe, and effective treatments to patients as quickly and effectively as possible. In the process, we want to continue to be at the forefront of the drug development and discovery process, ultimately reducing the early-stage drug development timeline by a full year. Our collective focus over the coming, multi-year journey is to enable this extraordinary group of people - our 18,000 colleagues - to execute and achieve our ambitious business goals. We are taking Charles River to a place where Enterprise Data Analytics team will be applying the techniques of data management, data engineering, and strategy development, as well as the use of analytics techniques that range from forecasting and simulation to linear programming and optimization and we want you to join us.

This role will work collaboratively, in a consultative way, across the business units and IT, owning the modern analytics solutions that are built by the team, supporting and training business users, as well as advising on best approaches to solve business problems, automate manual solutions, or simply bring to life ‘the art of the possible’ leveraging modern analytics as a competitive advantage.

Job Responsibilities

The following are responsibilities related to the position:

•Engage Business Stakeholders at all levels to identify requirements for current and future products through ongoing interaction

•Data Profiling, mining, and data validation to ensure data is fit for use by the business

•Ability to see big picture and then identify key areas for deep analysis to support sound solutions

•Perform ad-hoc analysis and present results in a clear and user-friendly manner

•Perform testing, resolve issues and work with developers to automate testing/data validation

•Lead requirements workshops and User Acceptance Testing for new data and analytics solutions

•Build strong business relationships that foster a collaborative and trusting approach and partnership

•Act as scrum master for the team and prepare detailed stories for developers

Job Qualifications

The following are minimum requirements related to the Senior Business Intelligence / Data Analyst position.

•BS/BA degree in Business Management, Computer Science (or related field), MBA Preferred

•7+ years of experience in writing SQL queries, data mining, data profiling, and data validation/testing

•7+ years of experience as a Business Systems Analyst / Data Analyst specializing in the Data & Analytics discipline

•7+ years of experience organizing and running User Acceptance Testing cycles and training with business users and stakeholders

•5+ years of experience with Data Governance processes to ensure consistent implementations of data sets, terminology and reporting structures for optimal data integrity

•5+ years of experience with Data Visualizations tools such as Power BI, SSRS, or Tableau

•3+ years of experience supporting users with OLAP solutions in SSAS (MDX or DAX)

•3+ years working in Agile Software Development Methodology

•Ability to translate requirements to well-written user stories to bridge the gap between business and technology

•Strong business mindset with ability to collaborate with business partners to identify needs and opportunities for improved data management and delivery

The following are strongly desired:

