11556,942,Marketing Database Manager/Data Analyst - Remote US,Marvel Marketers,United States,"At Marvel Marketers, it is our goal to make clients incredibly successful through Expert Services, Strategic Partnerships, and Training. We work with some of the largest brands across the globe and need the best and the brightest to make them successful.

As a Marketing Database Manager, you will have held database marketing positions and are well versed in business acumen outside of Marketing... and Marketing Automation. You have the technical aptitude, database management and analysis experience for marketing data. You are comfortable analyzing the key causes of data integrity issues (accuracy, duplication and completeness), drive processes/systems that solve these issues and communicate them with confidence to the internal team. You are also comfortable moving a strategy forward with confidence.

In return, you get an awesome opportunity to work with amazing clients and awesome people who love to have fun while getting stuff done! We are growing fast, which means you grow with us! We also typically have large scale ongoing engagements, so you have the opportunity to really understand the client's business firsthand.

To be successful in this role, you will be someone who learns quickly, thrives in fast-paced environments, and appreciates the strength in using data to drive decisions. Experience with Marketo, Salesforce, Pardot is highly preferred.

Essential responsibilities, include but are not limited to:

Manage, maintain data quality and normalize marketing database(s).
Segment data, build target audience marketing lists.
Conduct analysis on marketing data for trends, insights and recommendations.
Work closely with stakeholders providing campaign reports & dashboards.
Pull data from different data sources i.e. Pardot, GA, normalize it, enrich data and make it read for analysis and insights.

Minimum Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:

5+ years relevant marketing database experience
Working knowledge of Marketing Automation platforms such as Pardot, Marketo or Hubspot.
Experience analyzing, maintaining and normalizing large datasets.
Experience with CRM such as building reports & dashboards.
Experience with 3rd party reporting/visualization tools such as Tableua or Domo
Excellent verbal, written, presentation and storytelling skills.
Process and quality orientation with exceptional attention to detail
Ability to collaborate and work in a cross-functional environment
Thrive in a fast-paced, iterative, deadline driven environment

Nice to Have / preferred qualifications:

Experience with Marketo, Pardot, Salesforce highly preferred
MCE Marketo Certification preferred
Well-rounded marketing technologist familiar with/passionate about industry best practices
Experience with other automation platforms
Experience in working in a remote position

Who thrives with us:

People who want to learn, but are self motivated in learning from their projects.
People who enjoy the really hard problems.
People who enjoy having too much vs. too little to do.
People who like creating from nothing (We still need a lot built to support our growth).
People who understand how to build and maintain relationships with their coworkers and their clients.
People who like making others successful and understand the value of that as much as making themselves successful.
People who leave their ego at home and really enjoy working with other brilliant people.
People who not only can thrive in ambiguity but prefer informing frameworks and structures themselves.

About Marvel Marketers:

Marvel Marketers () is a global Marketing Automation, Digital Marketing, Experience Management and ABM Consultancy. Our clients are sophisticated so we only hire the best to keep up and add value along the entire Digital Marketing Maturity Curve. We also partner strategically on custom digital marketing roles to help support all areas of our client's Digital Marketing Strategy.

As we continue to grow and expand our service offerings, we are looking for the best and brightest to join our team. If you applied for a previous role, apply again! Our needs continuously change and evolve.

Marvel Marketers is an Equal Opportunity Employer",2022-11-18,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
11557,943,NDE Data Analyst,"Audubon Engineering Operations, LLC","Tulsa, OK","This job was posted by https://okjobmatch.com : For more information, please see: https://okjobmatch.com/jobs/2602096

Audubon is currently seeking an NDE Data Analyst to join our team in our Tulsa, OK Office. The NDE Data Analyst will be responsible for the quality control of all data gathered during inspection jobs, delivery of data to specified client timelines, and client interactions... post-report delivery. These responsibilities will be carried out from their base location. While not performing data analysis, responsibilities will also include but are not limited to assisting with ongoing training activities, quality control functions, and special projects. Responsible for ensuring that safety and quality take priority over any other aspect of the job.

PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES:

Key Areas of Responsibility will include:

+ Follow and adhere to all Audubon and Client safety rules and regulations.

+ Adhere to Audubon Core Values.

+ Must be able to interpret and apply all applicable procedures associated with quality procedures per client and Audubon requests.

+ Review all data/reports completed on assigned inspection projects/jobs for accuracy and validity.

+ Track all assigned projects/jobs to ensure that all data is completed and meets specified delivery timelines.

+ Ensure that all data was completed per Audubon or client specific processes/procedures.

+ Maintain all record retention for inspection projects/jobs per Audubon guidelines.

+ Communicate with NDE technicians.

+ Communicate with clients for post-job requests as required.

+ Must be able to complete computerized reports, research procedural requirements, file paperwork, and fill out required reports.

+ Assist in quality control functions, as assigned.

+ All other assigned duties.

EXPERIENCE AND SKILL REQUIREMENTS:

The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required for the position:

+ Requires high school diploma or equivalent.

+ Complete all required Company safety and job related training and demonstrated proficiency of the methods, procedures, and tools used to accomplish the task being performed.

+ Ability to perform a variety of tasks, often changing assignments with short notice.

+ Must possess a valid driver’s license.

+ Proven ability to prioritize and complete work assignments by specific deadlines.

+ Proven ability to communicate with customers, supervision, and co-workers.

+ Proven ability to follow precise directions and procedures as directed by supervision.

+ Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite.

+ Knowledge of pipeline integrity operations and maintenance processes.

+ Coding experience.

+ Ultrasonic inspection and magnetic particle inspection experience.

Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled",2022-03-08,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
