11573,959,Senior Data Analyst,Gopuff,United States,"The Senior Data Analyst will join as an analytical leader within the 3 Way Match program at Gopuff. 3 Way Match program is critical for Gopuff to properly manage the procurement process, inventory, and financial reporting. The expectation for this role is to understand the end-to-end data flow across Supply Chain, Inventory, and Finance systems, perform root cause analysis, and build reports and... dashboards to provide visibility across the team.
You Will:

• Have a strong analytical toolkit. SQL, Sigma, Looker
• Having domain knowledge of Supply Chain, Inventory Management, and 3 Way Match is a strong plus
• Have a strong sense of ownership and entrepreneurial spirit with relentlessly high standards and high attention to detail
• Be a collaborative, cross-functional team player and comfortable partnering with a variety of teams from Product to Ops to Finance

You Have:

• 3+ years in an analytical role supporting a business team
• Curiosity around data and willingness to continue to go deeper and learn about our business
• Expert-level SQL and excel knowledge
• Python experience is a plus
• Root cause analysis, able to use data to diagnose any problem in front of you
• Experience building intuitive dashboards, reports, and analyses for easy dissemination
• Expert presentation skills
• Ability to synthesize complex datasets and topics into actionable insights
• Ability to generate buy-in from stakeholders

#LI-Remote

Benefits
We want to help our employees stay safe and healthy! We offer comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance, optional FSAs and HSA plans, 401k, commuter benefits, supplemental employee, spouse and child life insurance to all eligible employees.*

We also offer*:
-Gopuff employee discount
-Career growth opportunities
-Internal rewards programs
-Annual performance appraisal and bonus
-Equity program
• Not applicable for contractors or temporary employees.

At Gopuff, we know that life can be unpredictable. Sometimes you forget the milk at the store, run out of pet food for Fido, or just really need ice cream at 11 pm. We get it—stuff happens. But that’s where we come in, delivering all your wants and needs in just minutes.

And now, we’re assembling a team of motivated people to help us drive forward that vision to bring a new age of convenience and predictability to an unpredictable world.

Like what you’re hearing? Then join us on Team Blue.

Gopuff is an equal employment opportunity employer, committed to an inclusive workplace where we do not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, gender, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital or familial status, age, ancestry, disability, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws. We believe in diversity and encourage any qualified individual to apply",2022-07-15,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sql', 'excel', 'go', 'looker', 'python']"
11574,960,Financial Data Analyst,Life.Church,"Edmond, OK","The Financial Data Analyst will visualize data and ensure integrity, support Financial Operations Group systems, and lead through process implementations in support of Life.Church and YouVersion.

You care about the missing digits, the decimal points, and a balanced spreadsheet. Life.Church cares about numbers the same way you care about numbers, because to us, every number is a story. That’s why... we’re looking for someone like you. Someone who knows the bottom line is never measured in dollars—it’s measured in lives forever changed by the love of Christ.

The Finance Team partners with the organization to facilitate the payroll, accounting, and forecasting needs of Life.Church. We equip the organization with the tools needed to plan for, understand, and steward the resources God has provided for our ministry.

Do you make Tableau dashboards for fun? Are you passionate about excellence in the details? If so, continue reading for more details!
Who you are:

• A team player who loves to collaborate as well as work independently
• Well-organized and equipped to adapt at a moment’s notice
• Passionate about organizing and visualizing data
• A gifted problem solver who thoroughly appreciates checking things off your to-do list
• A curious thinker who asks questions and learns rapidly and eagerly

What you'll do:

• Use tools such as Tableau and SQL to organize and visualize data
• Support and evaluate systems used by the Financial Operations Group to drive efficiency
• Be a technical advocate for the Financial Operations group with internal teams and external vendors
• Develop reports and dashboards that inform leadership and empower them to make strategic financial decisions

For bonus points:

• You’re excited to work in a fun, fast-paced atmosphere where everyone takes the mission seriously, but no one takes themselves too seriously
• You’re a whiz with numbers, but you love people
• You are passionate about building systems and simplifying processes

To view the expectations and responsibilities of this role, please review the job description.

Work Perks:
When you join the Life.Church team, our prayer is that your family will be closer, your leadership will be sharper, your finances will be stronger, your faith will be deeper, and your heart will be larger. And while the biggest perk to working at Life.Church is doing work that makes an eternal difference, you'll find that's not the only benefit we offer:

Office hours are from 8-5, but flexible work arrangements are available
Generous and immediate time-off
Industry-leading medical, dental, and vision coverage
Unparalleled employer 401K contribution match
Childcare benefits
Casual dress code
Professional development funds
And so much more!

Learn More:
Learn more about what it’s like to work at Life.Church: www.life.church/careers. This role is located at Life.Church Central Offices in Edmond, OK",2022-01-16,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'spreadsheet']"
11578,964,Senior Data Analyst (Remote),Talentify.io,Anywhere,"Talentify helps candidates around the world to discover and stay focused on the jobs they want until they can complete a full application in the hiring company career page/ATS.

The Analytic Consulting Group partners with internal and external clients and data providers, leveraging predictive analytics and advanced statistical techniques to drive strategic thought and effective decision making... The Senior Data Analyst helps support all aspects of analytic initiatives from conception to completion.

Responsibilities
• Participate in presentation of reports to key internal and external stakeholders, effectively communicating the key findings and recommendations
• QA/QC data and report output to ensure accuracy
• Appropriately account for the timeliness and quality of all assignments
• Provide SAS/SQL programming, under general direction, in the execution of data analysis that will contribute to the final project deliverables
• Prioritize and monitor project progress relative to timeline and scope
• Assist in development of reports, providing content and writing of key observations
• Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to manage data logistics - including data transfers, understanding data structures, business rules, etc. - to enable project execution
• Manage multiple projects concurrently

Minimum Qualifications
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills
• Proficient in SAS/SQL; minimum 3 years’ experience
• Solid planning, priority setting, and project management skills with experience managing multiple projects concurrently
• Successful developing relationships within and across functional teams (including statistical, technical, and marketing resources)
• Minimum 2 years of experience in marketing analytics field
• Proficient in MS Office, including PowerPoint, Word, Excel and Outlook
• Strong technical skills
• Bachelor or Master’s degree in a quantitative discipline (statistics, economics, mathematics, marketing analytics)

Desirable Qualifications
• Ability to display data visually, creating powerful presentations which effectively demonstrate the value of analytic deliverables; proficiency with business visualization tools (e.g., interactive dashboard software)
• Advanced degree (Master’s/PhD) in Statistics, Economics or other quantitative discipline
• Ability to program in newer and emerging languages such as R and Python; working knowledge of Hadoop and other big data technologies

About

Check out a few of these resources to learn more about what makes Epsilon so EPIC

When you’re one of us, you get to run with the best. For decades, we’ve been helping marketers from the world’s top brands personalize experiences for millions of people with our cutting-edge technology, solutions and services. Epsilon’s best-in-class identity gives brands a clear, privacy-safe view of their customers, which they can use across our suite of digital media, messaging and loyalty solutions. We process 400+ billion consumer actions each day and hold many patents of proprietary technology, including real-time modeling languages and consumer privacy advancements. Thanks to the work of every employee, Epsilon has been consistently recognized as industry-leading by Forrester, Adweek and the MRC. Positioned at the core of Hiring Company, Epsilon is a global company with more than 8,000 employees around the world.
• Life at Epsilon: https://www.epsilon.com/us/about-us/epic-blog
• DE&I: https://www.epsilon.com/us/about-us/diversity-equity-inclusion
• CSR: https://www.epsilon.com/us/about-us/corporate-social-responsibility
