11589,975,Data Analyst,Genuent,Anywhere,"Job Description

Title: Data Analyst...

Location: Fully Remote

Duration: 6+ Months

Compensation: $50-60/hr W2

Industry: Financial Services, Mortgage

Work Requirements: US Citizens, GC Holders or Authorized to Work in the US

Job Description:

The Data Analyst is a key technical position and plays an important role in the organization by performing a number of activities related to the company's Information Technology functions. The role is primarily responsible, under limited supervision, for executing the data strategy and analysis efforts within the company's enterprise data platform by eliciting business requirements for data & analytics, identifying Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), documenting functional requirements for various business functions, validating data analysis and collaborating across the enterprise data team to deliver actionable insights to key stakeholders. Responsibilities include working with key stakeholders to assess their data and analytics needs, reviewing and updating logical data dictionaries and other supporting documentation, assessing the availability and quality of data, and researching internal and external data sources.

Essential Functions:
• Partner with key stakeholders, including the business unit leaders, Product, Data & Technology teams, to assess their data and analytics needs by eliciting data requirements, esearching internal systems of record and publicly available data sources ,and assessing their qdata quality
• Requisition and obtain private data sources to support business needs for data and insights.
• Identify translation or transformation requirements for sourced data into the data warehouse.
• Improve the quality of sourced data by data curation and validation rules as well as maintaining the Master Data tables.
• Maintain the Logical Data Dictionary (LDD) with data lineage information (field definition, domain, source system, intermediary and destination system(s), translations, transformation rules, display screens, referenced reports, etc.), Data Stewards, and Data Custodian info along with versioning for historic analysis and audit trail.
• Ensure consistent delivery of high-quality insights to key stakeholders by reconciling and validating dashboards and reports in a timely manner.
• Document functional / non-functional business requirements for collecting, loading, transforming, curating, and processing data, and for visualization and distribution of insights.
• Identify internal process improvements for automating manual processes, optimizing data delivery, re-designing infrastructure for greater scalability, etc.
• Provide actionable insights using analytics tools into customer acquisition, operational efficiency, and other key business performance metrics.
• Identify Personally Identifiable Information data in primary data sources as well as in data architecture, define masking and other data processing rules for special handling of PII data as well as maintain access control lists for visibility of PII data on a need-to-know basis.
• Identify and document the Business Continuity Plan/Disaster Recovery (BCP/DR), and technical requirements for high availability and recoverability for the data architecture.
• Improve the quality of data used for analysis by assessing the accuracy of new data sources and the effectiveness of new data-gathering techniques.
• Define Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and document technical processes to monitor and analyze data warehouse performance and data accuracy.
• Contribute to the team of data professionals by using expertise to answer questions and share templates, and reusable artifacts with less experienced teammates, enhancing skillsets and competencies of team members, and sharing business domain knowledge throughout the team.
• Participate in stakeholder reviews, and design sessions.
• Provide data, reports, and information to management as needed.
• Identify, track, and monitor trends and avoidable technology-related errors; work across functions to develop complex solutions, improvements, and stop-gaps.
• Focus on the continual improvement of policies, procedures, and processes falling under the scope of authority.
• Use expertise to resolve high-level issues that cannot be solved by teammates.
• Stay abreast of the latest technology trends and participate in high-level decisions impacting the direction of the Information Technology function.
• Consistently monitor and model platform usage, database sizes, compute resources, and third-party costs to ensure that the data team's spend is as cost-efficient as possible.
• Champion data transformation to new ways of working and generating insights.
• Drive strong communications, partnerships, and stakeholder management with senior leaders, functional managers, and staff.
• Perform other duties as assigned.

Qualifications:
• Bachelor's degree, BS in Statistics, Computer Science, Data Science, or related quantitative field is required, Master's degree in business administration (MBA) is preferred, along with a minimum of five years experience in a Data Analyst related role(s) and at least two of those years spent in a senior technical level role(s) required.
• Highly proficient with eliciting business requirements, documenting user stories, analyzing data sources, and assessing data quality.
• Highly proficient in data analysis, technical documentation, logical data dictionary, data validation rules, acceptance criteria, and software development lifecycle (SDLC) such as Scrum and IT Service Management (ITSM) ITILv4.
• Experience in identifying data integration needs using Extract, Transform and Load (ETL) tools and modern data pipes.
• Proven experience with querying and analyzing data from SQL relational databases such as AuroraDB, IBM DB2, MemSQL, MS SQL Server, MySQL, Postgres, Snowflake, and NoSQL Databases such as Cassandra, DynamoDB, Redis, MongoDB.
• Experience collecting structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data in various popular formats and sourced from internal core systems as well as 3rd partner providers such as Google Analytics, Facebook Insights, Zillow, CoreLogic, MLS Data, Public Records, and Property Data.
• Experience using collaboration tools such as Microsoft Office or Google G-Suite as well as Jira, Confluence, and Microsoft SharePoint.
• Experience performing root cause analysis on internal and external data and processes to answer specific business questions and identify opportunities for improvement.
• Strong analytical skills to document processes supporting data transformation, data structures, metadata, dependency, and workload management.
• Strong data governance skills to ensure the highest quality of data is made available for data analysis and accuracy in reporting.
• Problem solver with the ability to work as a team towards a solution.
• Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a deadline-driven environment, a strong sense of urgency, and responsiveness.
• Strong detail orientation and highly organized with proven ability to lead effectively and drive results in a matrixed management environment.
• Ability to think critically, including the ability to evaluate facts and data to draw conclusions, and determine the downstream impact of decisions and associated risks.
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills plus demonstrate strong leadership capabilities.
• Strong interpersonal and team-building skills.
• Self-starter with the demonstrated ability to learn/adapt to new technologies and techniques.
• Ethical, with a commitment to company values.

Our benefits package includes:
• Comprehensive medical benefits
• Competitive pay, 401(k)
• Retirement plan
• and much more!

About INSPYR Solutions:

TekPartners and Genuent are becoming INSPYR Solutions. As a leading information technology partner, we connect top IT talent with our clients to provide innovative business solutions through our IT Staffing, Professional Services, and Infrastructure Solutions divisions. We understand and value the unique needs of highly-skilled information technology professionals in the industry and always strive to stay above the curve. Our company was founded on the following core values: Be the Best, Understand the Urgency, Never Ever Give Up, Have the Courage to Excel, and Make a Contribution. We take pride in our business model and strive to create a positive workplace environment through an exemplary culture.

INSPYR Solutions provides Equal Employment Opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, or genetics. In addition to federal law requirements, INSPYR complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities",2022-06-10,Contractor,data analyst,United States,"['snowflake', 'sharepoint', 'postgres', 'sql', 'mongodb', 'nosql', 'excel', 'redis', 'mysql', 'jira']"
