11607,993,"Data Analyst, Education & Services",UNAVAILABLE,United States,"Boiler

How many people can answer the question, ""What do you do for a living?"" with the answer, ""I help find cures for cancer."" At LLS, employees take our mission seriously. Whether you work in one of our chapters, are an accountant at the national office or a specialist in our Information Resource Center, you work each day on making our mission a reality: Cure leukemia, lymphoma, Hodgkin's... disease and myeloma, and improve the quality of life of patients and their families. Join us and give new meaning to the word, ""job.""

Overview

The Data Analyst, Education & Services (E&S) ensures that E&S is utilizing data to maximize reach, improve the delivery of programs and services, and communicate impact. The individual in this position will collaborate with E&S staff to optimize measurement of program and services, including special initiatives such as Hispanic Outreach and Myeloma Link. They will develop reports and create dashboards - including visual tools - that can help staff and other stakeholders easily digest and act upon data, while building the data teams’ working knowledge of analytics tools. The analyst will also manage the yearly development of E&S’ widely used and annually created booklet on blood cancer statistics.

All employees and temporary workers are required to provide proof of vaccination for COVID-19 in connection with performing in-person work at an LLS office or other location, or before attending any LLS sponsored event, unless a reasonable accommodation is approved, consistent with applicable law.

While employees may be permitted to work remotely, travel to the assigned office, HUB or Satellite Offices may be required as determined by the employee’s manager and the employee’s Strategic Talent Partner.

Additional Position Information
Reports To: Senior Director, Analytics and Quality Improvement All employees are required to provide proof of vaccination for COVID-19 in connection with performing in-person work at an LLS office or other location, or before attending any LLS sponsored event, unless a reasonable accommodation is approved, consistent with applicable law.
Responsibilities

Duties and Responsibilities:
• Determine characteristics of patients, caregivers, and healthcare professionals served, including developing profiles by disease type and other characteristics.
• Describe the various patient journeys through E&S, including breadth of engagement.
• Utilize program and service delivery data to identify patterns and trends, identify areas of unmet need and types of patients not being reached.
• Contribute to LLS’s ongoing reporting of available US and Global incidence, mortality, survival and prevalence statistics of hematologic malignancies.
• Integrate existing publicly available data (e.g., Census poverty data) with our datasets to enhance understanding of the constituency we serve and to better target services.
• Assist with determining analysis frameworks, including developing templates/programs that are reusable and easily updated for various subsets of data and time periods.
• Generate reports that include visual tools (e.g., graphs, charts, tables, maps) that help others easily track and digest complex data, in order to drive decisions about any needed programmatic changes to maximize reach and impact.
• Validate the data prior to performing analytical procedures. Give feedback on data quality issues to E&S Data Manager and Director of Training and Quality Improvement.
• Support implementation of health services and quality of life research with external collaborators by contributing to development of study methodology, survey instruments, data capture systems, data analysis, and reporting.
• Respond to internal data requests.
• Contribute to the creation of presentations for internal stakeholders to communicate the impact of LLS programs.
• Support work with external collaborators by preparing different kinds of data for presentation at meetings, local and national conferences, and for publication in professional journals as appropriate; respond to external data requests.

#LI-Remote

Qualifications

Requirements:
• Master’s degree in a relevant discipline, such as such as sociology, community engagement, health economics, data science, or public health (e.g., with a focus on biostatistics, health services research, or epidemiology).
• At least 3 years of relevant experience.
• Extensive experience in data presentation and reporting for a variety of audiences, including the development of visual presentations of data (graphs, charts, maps, etc.).
• Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to present data in a simple and straightforward way for non-technical audiences.
• Commitment to advancing diversity, equity and inclusion.
• Advanced knowledge of statistical practices, including experience with analyzing and interpreting incidence and prevalence data.
• Proficiency with statistical operations package such as R, SAS or SPSS required.
• Experience with data visualization packages such as Tableau strongly preferred.
• Experience with Salesforce and/or Salesforce CRM Analytics preferred.
• Outstanding written and oral communication skills.

Physical Demands & Work Environment:
• Position may require occasional night and weekend work as well as occasional travel.
• Physical demands are minimal and typical of similar jobs in comparable organizations.
• Average hourly rate is $40-47/ hour.

Disclaimer
LLS is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusion in its workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender, gender identity and expression (including transgender status), sexual orientation, pregnancy, age, race, color, creed, national origin/ancestry, citizenship, religion, genetic predisposition or information, physical or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LLS seeks such skilled and qualified individuals to share our mission and where they will join a cohort of others who have chosen to call LLS home. LLS complies with all applicable laws which prohibit discrimination and harassment in the workplace, and is committed to maintaining a diverse and inclusive environment supportive of all of our employees and the communities we serve. **All LLS employees are required to provide proof of vaccination for COVID-19 before beginning work at LLS unless a valid medical, religious, or other exemption is approved consistent with applicable law",2022-04-09,,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'word', 'spss', 'sas', 'r']"
11608,994,Enterprise Portfolio Data Analyst,Children’s Mercy Kansas City,"Kansas City, MO","Thanks for your interest in Children's Mercy!

Do you envision finding a meaningful role with an inclusive and compassionate team? At Children’s Mercy, we believe in making a difference in the lives of all children and shining a light of hope to the patients and families we serve. Our employees make the difference, which is why we have been recognized by U.S. News & World Report as a top... pediatric hospital, for eleven consecutive years.

Children’s Mercy is in the heart of Kansas City – a metro abounding in cultural experiences, vibrant communities and thriving businesses. This is where our patients and families live, work and play. This is a community that has embraced our hospital and we strive to say thanks by giving back. As a leader in children’s health, we engage in meaningful programs and partnerships throughout the region so that we can improve the lives of children beyond the walls of our hospital.
Overview

The Enterprise Portfolio Data Analyst, reporting to the Portfolio Manager, will assist the organization in making data informed decisions surrounding project requests as well as monitoring the success of approved projects. Through partnership with end users and project requestors, the data analyst will identify metrics helping to move the needle of organizational KPIs.

At Children’s Mercy, we are committed to ensuring that everyone feels welcomed within our walls. A successful candidate for this position will join us as we strive to create a workplace that reflects the community we serve, as well as our core values of kindness, curiosity, inclusion, team and integrity.

Additionally, it’s important to us that we remain transparent with all potential job candidates. Because we value the safety of the patients and families we serve, as well as the Children’s Mercy staff, we want to let you know that the seasonal influenza and COVID-19 vaccines are a condition of employment for all employees in our organization. New employees must be willing to be vaccinated if found non-immune to measles, mumps, rubella (MMR) and chicken pox (varicella) and/or without evidence of tetanus, diphtheria, acellular pertussis (Tdap) vaccination since 2005. If you become a finalist for this position, and have any concerns about receiving these vaccines, medical and/or religious exemptions can be further discussed with Human Resources.
Responsibilities
• Data exploration, project metric development data analysis
• Research and identify organizational data sources to support metric development and tracking
• Act as the data subject matter expert in the EPMO connecting people, tools, and data sets to facilitate data driven decision making
• Liaise between EPMO and data intelligence team when/if a new data collection tool/report needs to be developed
• Explore year-over-year milestone setting with requesters and help align milestones and metrics to industry standards
• Remain up-to-date on industry data analytical innovations and data use best practices
• Work with intake analysts to ensure project metrics have been developed and included in project proposals
• Through partnership with end users and project requesters, the data analyst will identify metrics which help move the needle of organizational KPIs.
• Project Metric Development
• Assist project requestersin pulling current state relevant metrics
• Work with EPMO leadership to define, build and track performance metrics to measure the efficacy and efficiency of EPMO processes.
• Work with EPMO staff and requesters to define, build and track project level metrics to measure project level of success and inform project status.
• Assist project requestersin analyzing current state data and setting yearly targets for improvement
• Provide updated data for program and project looks backs (in collaboration with program and project managers) as directed by Portfolio Manager
• Develop visualizations/dashboards depicting metric progress per project
• Liase between EPMO and finance team to ensure financial metrics are on track
• Synthesize and analyze data sets to present to stakeholders and EPMO leadership
• Project requester/ end user education
• Provide education to project requesters on tools leading to self-service data pulling
• Educate end users on the importance of tracking metrics and how to set yearly targets based on historical/contextual data
• Communicate to stakeholders if yearly targets are not on track to be met
Qualifications
• Bachelor's Degree Required and 3-5 years experience knowledge of modern analytic tools, stakeholder management, project management, data analysis business analysis, business case development.
Starting Pay

Our pay ranges are market competitive. The pay range for this job begins at $27.87/hr, but your offer will be determined based on your education and experience.

Remote Work/Work from Home

This is an intermittent remote position, which means that the person hired will work with his or her manager to determine a schedule that includes both at home and on-site hours at a Children’s Mercy location. The incumbent must live in the Kansas City metro area.

EEO Employer/Disabled/Vet

Children’s Mercy hires individuals based on their job skills, expertise and ability to maintain professional relationships with fellow employees, patients, parents and visitors. A personal interview, formal education and training, previous work experience, references and a criminal background investigation all are factors used to select the best candidates. The hospital does not discriminate against prospective or current employees based on the race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, creed, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, ancestry or veteran status. A drug screen will be performed upon hire. Children’s Mercy is smoke and tobacco free.

Our commitment to Diversity & Inclusion

CM is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. Our patients and families come from all walks of life, and so do we. We know that our greatest strengths come from the people who make up our team so we hire great people from a wide variety of backgrounds, not just because it’s the right thing to do, but because it makes our hospital stronger and our patient care more compassionate.

If you share our values and our enthusiasm for service, you will find a home at CM. In recruiting for our team, we welcome the unique contributions that you can bring, including education, ideas, culture, ethnicity, race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, national origin, age, languages spoken, veteran status, color, religion, disability and beliefs",2022-03-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
11609,995,Analytics Engineer - Architecture,Fivetran,United States,"From Fivetran’s founding until now, our mission has remained the same: to make access to data as simple and reliable as electricity. With Fivetran, customer data arrives in their warehouses, canonical and ready to query, with no engineering or maintenance required. We’re proud that more organizations continue to leverage our technology every day to become truly data-driven.Overview As an Analytics Engineer on Fivetran’s internal Analytics team, you will be the standard-bearer for data quality and efficiency on a high-performance, industry-leading team. You will ensure that our analytics warehouse and codebase is designed to support our growing enterprise business reliably, accurately and affordably. You will work closely with our fantastic Data Analysts, bringing an informed, opinionated viewpoint to frameworks, tools, templates and code reviews in order to elevate code quality teamwide. You will identify opportunities for refactoring existing code, you will implement the refactoring... and you will lay the guardrails for fewer refactors in the future. What You'll Do Champion our core values of #one-team-one-dream, #get-stuck-in, #do-the-right-thing. Be the standard-bearer for data quality and efficiency on a high-performance, industry-leading team. Ensure that our analytics warehouse and codebase is designed to support our growing enterprise business reliably, accurately and affordably. Work closely with our fantastic Data Analysts, bringing an informed, opinionated viewpoint to frameworks, tools, templates and code reviews in order to elevate code quality teamwide. Identify opportunities for refactoring existing code Implement the refactoring Lay the guardrails for fewer refactors in the future. What You'll Bring A mastery of SQL An informed, opinionated stance on SQL style, normalization, Kimball, etc. A deep understanding of ERDs, DAGs and ETL/ELT An ability to take end-to-end ownership of data product delivery, from design through implementation You want to solve problems the RIGHT way, and you can clearly articulate why to a technical audience Bonus Skills Deep experience working with dbt Core, including macro development and maintenance Experience scaling an ETL or other analytics codebase across several years and 10+ collaborators Good understanding of data governance and data security We’re honored to be valued at over $5.6 billion, but more importantly, we’re proud of our core values of Get Stuck In, Do the Right Thing, and One Team, One Dream. Fivetran brings together high-quality talent across the globe to make data access as easy and reliable as electricity for our customers. We value and recognize that our customers benefit from having innovative teams made of people from many backgrounds, experiences and identities. Fivetran promotes diversity, equity, inclusion & belonging through attracting, recruiting, developing and retaining a diverse workforce, not only because it is the right thing to do, but because it helps us build a world-class company to better serve our customers, our people and our communities. To learn more about Fivetran’s culture and what it’s like to be part of the team, click here and enjoy our video. To learn more about our candidate privacy policy, you can read our statement here",2022-08-28,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['sql']
