Costco IT is responsible for the technical future of Costco Wholesale, the second largest retailer in the world with wholesale operations in twelve countries. Despite our size and explosive international expansion, we continue to provide a family, employee centric atmosphere in which our employees thrive and succeed. As proof, Costco consistently ranks in the top five of Forbes “America’s Best Employers”.

Data Analysts are responsible for importing, transforming, and validating or querying data with the purpose of understanding or drawing conclusions from the data to drive decision-making. They may use modeling techniques to form data in ways that can be analyzed and/or queried to identify data quality issues, anomalies or deviations. Data Analysts generate ad hoc reports and regular datasets or report information for end-users using system tools, database or data warehouse queries and scripts. They also integrate data from multiple sources to produce requested or required data elements. The Data Analysts work closely with business groups, IT verticals, and governance teams to provide information to drive data quality and usage decisions.

In this position, the Data Analysts are responsible for querying data sources to import and transform private and/or sensitive data requested by the legal departments, which includes generating ad hoc reports. They work closely with Legal, Human Resources, and PayRoll departments as well as the IT Data and Analytics teams.

If you want to be a part of one of the BEST “to work for” companies in the world, simply apply and let your career be reimagined.

ROLE

