Defines and ensures adherence to new process improvement opportunities.
Performs testing and validation of data and data sources.
Applies best practices and data governance to database and reporting solutions.
Performs data mapping and tracing from system to system in order to solve a given business or system problem.
Supports initiatives for data integrity and normalization.
Provides technical expertise on migration, mining, and cleansing of data.
Supports and informs data stewards and custodians to ensure quality of master data changes and additions.
Prepares documentation of relationships, integration, and flow of data.
Supports tooling for capturing and maintaining metadata elements within a repository.
Identifies and resolves problems often anticipating issues before they occur or before they grow; develops and evaluates options and implements solutions.

REQUIRED

1-3 years’ writing SQLs queries, report writing and presenting findings.
Strong
with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy. * Detail oriented and possess strong problem solving skills, with the ability to analyze a situation for potential future problems.

Strong technical documentation and writing skills.
Strong written and verbal communication skills and able to work effectively with all levels of the business and IS.
Responsible, conscientious, and possess a passion for excellence.
Self-motivated and able to work independently with little supervision.
Demonstrates an ability to grow technical skills and learn new technologies.
Able to support off-hours work as required, including weekends, holidays, and 24/7 on call responsibilities on a rotational basis.

