Description & Qualifications

Description

UKG Global Delivery Services (GDS) is looking for an experienced, inquisitive, strategically-oriented Business Improvement Data Analyst to play a central role in realizing UKGs long term goals related to financial growth, profitability and customer and employee satisfaction. In this highly influential, cross-functional role, you will be working with GDS leadership to identify, evaluate, recommend, monitor and report on internal projects that are focused on continuous improvement within our Service Delivery functions. We are looking for a data guru who can not only provide insights on complex, strategic challenges, but who also has the experience and vision to help GDS leadership uncover opportunities to improve our business.

Responsibilities

Using data-driven approaches, evaluate, size and prioritize business improvement initiatives

Produce detailed analysis and presentations to GDS Leadership to provide guidance and recommendations on business improvement initiatives

Produce regular reporting on the performance of in-flight business improvement initiatives

As needed, deliver ad-hoc data and reporting on strategic questions and topics from the business

Work with UKGs Data Governance team to identify data gaps, errors, inconsistencies with a view toward establishing a single set of trusted performance data for Global Delivery

Regularly interact with GDS Teams and Leaders to communicate, publicize, and market initiatives and their impact on the business

Seek out and proactively identify business improvement opportunities

Serve as a key member of our Continuous Improvement Governance Board where CPI initiatives are evaluated for investment

Qualifications

5-7 years of experience working as a strategic Business Analyst. The ideal candidate will have experience working with Professional Services delivery teams and will be familiar with the KPIs such as Revenue, Project Profitability, Time-to-Live, Project Budget vs Actual, etc.

Must have extensive experience with Power BI

Extensive knowledge of data analysis and reporting tools is required to include Excel, Smartsheets, Tableau, etc. The ability to transform and combine disparate sets of data together to tell a story is essential.

Experience developing reporting and analytics on Sales and Professional Services Automation applications such as , FinancialForce, OpenAir and Mavenlink is desired

Strong business acumen with experience in P&L Management, Financial and Resource Productivity analysis

Ability to engage and build relationships across many functions and levels within GDS. The ideal candidate is comfortable both in the weeds as well as in the C-Suite.

Predictive modeling experience with development and analysis

Prior experience in a process improvement role or project(s) is desired

Ability to travel up to 25%

