• Ensure data accuracy for audits and reporting.
• Create and maintain network records.
• Record electronic files for storage.
• Prepare customized reports for local school needs.
• Work with management to prioritize business and information needs.
• Develop and execute professional development to ensure teachers are able to utilize database and software applications.
• Maintain, generate, and distribute student demographic, scheduling, and grading information.
• Support and respond to general troubleshooting inquiries for hardware/software problems.
• Manage network IT solutions, establishing a working relationship with vendors as needed.
• Performs other duties as assigned.

Requirements
• Bachelor's Degree or higher with a concentration in IT, Information Management, Mathematics, Computer Science, Statistics, or another relevant field.
• At least 2 years of professional experience.
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, compile, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy.
• Adept at queries, report writing, and presenting findings.
• Knowledge of statistics and experience using statistical packages for analyzing datasets.
• Technical expertise regarding data models, data mining, and segmentation techniques.
• Ability to troubleshoot hardware and software problems, managing network IT solutions.
• **THIS POSITION REQUIRES YOU TO BE FULLY VACCINATED AND YOU MUST PROVIDE PROOF OF VACCINATION.**
• Note: This is a 12-month position.

Candidates who do not meet the above requirements will not be considered.

Benefits
