Hillcrest HealthCare System (HHS) is a comprehensive health system providing quality healthcare in northeastern Oklahoma, with the system's flagship hospital, Hillcrest Medical Center, located in Tulsa. Additionally, HHS is comprised of Bailey Medical Center, Hillcrest Hospital Claremore, Hillcrest Hospital Cushing, Hillcrest Hospital Henryetta, Hillcrest Hospital Pryor, Hillcrest Hospital South, Tulsa Spine & Specialty Hospital, Oklahoma Heart Institute and Utica Park Clinic. HHS has 1,180 licensed beds and an expansive network of clinics.

POSITION SUMMARY

The Data Analyst will provide technical and analytical support to the Population Health activities of Utica Park Clinic and to Hillcrest Healthcare System.

New Report Requests: The Data Analyst is responsible for the creation and production of reports using established reporting protocols. The Data Analyst is responsible for reviewing the report requests assigned to them, communicating with the requestor to understand and clarify any questions regarding the report, evaluating the need for a new report creation or modifying an existing report to meet the requestor's needs and coordinating the due dates and frequency of the report. Creating the query requested and working with the report requestor and the Manager of Data Analytics to generate the report within the timeframe needed. Data validation based on the criteria provided will be done with the requestor and make any need changes.

Standard Report Production: Routine standard monthly reports will also be assigned and will be posted and distributed as established by protocols. Utilize other associated databases that are adjunct to the EPIC electronic records. Utilize Sharepoint and Teams as a report repository for general access for users. Refine and update reports as required for MIPS reporting.

Position reports to:
