• Integrates outside databases such as , Care Everywhere, MyHealth or other HIE, and EPIC EMR. Experience working with large clinical and/or administrative databases, including management and analysis
• Demonstrates analytical and statistical abilities to evaluate data, make judgments, and recommendations regarding quality improvement work, including but not limited to resource utilization, physician practice patterns, and clinical pathway effectiveness.
Qualifications

Education:
• Associate/Bachelors in Analytics or equivalent experience

Experience:
• 2+ years of experience with relational databases (SQL)

Licenses, Registrations, or Certifications:
• Will be required to take and pass Epic Cogito Certification during their first 6 months in the Data Analyst position.

Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:
• Analytical Thinking and Problem Solving
• Data Aggregation and analystis as well as generating graphs to help users
• SQL report writing skills
• Excel - Intermediate to Advanced skills
• Epic EMR knowledge
• HEDIS and CMS Quality metrics
