12399,1785,AVP - Senior Data Analyst,Citi,United States,"Come Work with us This is an exciting opportunity for individuals with passion for Data Science.

Citi, the world's leading global bank, has approximately 200 million customer accounts and a presence in more than 160 countries and jurisdictions worldwide. Citi provides consumers, corporations, governments, and institutions with a broad range of financial products and services, including consumer... banking and credit, corporate and investment banking, securities brokerage, transaction services, and wealth management. Citi enables clients to achieve their strategic financial objectives by providing them with cutting-edge ideas, best-in-class products and solutions, and unparalleled access to capital and liquidity.

Institutional Clients Group Technology (ICG-IT) features a diverse, inclusive team of professionals in approximately 90 countries around the globe . A career in ICG Technology offers the chance to experience being part of a global organization that features the best talent in the industry and creates a positive impact for each other, our clients and our communities where we live and work. The Wholesale Credit Risk Technology team within ICG-IT is responsible for ensuring that the data received from various front office applications into the reporting platform contains the authoritative data as expected by the Risk Managers. We are looking to build a team of enthusiastic and skilled Data Science / Data Analysts, who can combine data analysis, business knowledge and technical capabilities with existing tools - to take a significant part in innovative analytical projects and generate timely insights for credit risk data sets.

The Senior Technical Data Analyst position is responsible for providing oversight and facilitation of the various application, technology, and architecture processes liaising between business users and technologists to exchange information in a concise, logical, and understandable way in coordination with various other collaborating technological teams within ICG-IT. In this role, the data analyst must demonstrate critical thinking, analytical and problem-solving abilities, hands-on intelligence or data analysis skills, and must have strong technical skills - must be able to write complex SQL, perform data mappings and provide technical solutions on complex projects. The candidate should understand data science methods, and visualization techniques to leverage internal and external data to identify and develop ways to systemically detect inefficiencies and gaps. The incumbent is required to engage and work with global and regional business partners, IT-operations, and other internal technology partners to deliver.

Who you are:
• You've got positive energy. You are optimistic about the future and determined to get there. You appreciate open and direct communication. You are both - an active communicator and an eager listener.
• You can switch context & pivot on the fly. Our group is a horizontal organization and regulations are constantly changing. What you worked on yesterday may not be what you work on today. You should be flexible to accommodate the constantly changing regulatory landscape into your projects by translating the business requirements into technical specifications.
• You want to be part of a winning team. We build & grow with one another and you're a person who does not shy away from being pushed out of your comfort zone.
• You are often cited as inspiration for the junior colleagues, and they feel that they can learn something from you.
• You have a ""can do"" attitude. We assure that data of pristine quality is available to the business users for filing various Regulatory & Risk reports. Owning a problem does not scare you but empowers you to take 100% ownership.
What will you do?
• Apply curiosity and critical thinking in data mining, data analysis and analytics to drive optimization and improve data quality. Detect data anomalies and identify source of data problems. Recommend data quality solutions.
• Conduct strategic data analysis across relational databases, provide insights & implications to make strategic recommendations, develop data displays that clearly communicate complex analysis.
• Participate in the development, testing, and training of new or enhanced tactical solutions or strategic system applications. Write complex test cases during release sprints and ensure accurate delivery in line with technical requirements.
• Be an active contributor to Data Tracing Projects and assist in various Data Governance Program related data analysis requests from the Chief Data Office.
• Collaborate with business partners to analyze complex system issues/problems through in-depth evaluation of business processes, systems and industry standards; design new workflows to transform business requirements into concrete insights
• Create new transformations, mappings, workflows and data loading procedures to implement business rules using the best practices to achieve high performance.
• As applicable, lead systems change process from requirements through implementation; provide user and operational support of applications to business users.
• Formulate and define systems scope and objectives for complex projects through research and fact-finding combined with an understanding of applicable business systems and industry standards
• Document and reference key facts uncovered during research and analysis process. Understand the global implications & applicability of the recommendations and effectively communicate them to stakeholders
Basic Requirements :
• 8-10 years Business and/or Data analysis experience using tools and techniques for modeling of large data sets. Comprehensive knowledge of the principles of business and data analysis.
• BS or MS in Computer Science or related technical field or a degree in Finance with strong technical skills
• Intermediate to advanced SQL skills querying relational databases, ability to create complex DDL, DML, DQL scripts. Experience querying multiple large data sets.
• Data Warehouse or Business Intelligence experience including experience with data sourcing, data integration and data quality projects
• Advanced Excel skills, strong experience using Power Query.
• Extensive experience working in Waterfall and Agile project methodologies; using JIRA. Experience with all phases of Software Development Life Cycle.
• Experience with process and data modelling (UML) and knowledge of ETL
• Ability to han dle multiple projects simultaneously and analyze large sets of complex data, draw meaningful conclusions, and make recommendations based on analysis.
• Ability to create metrics and reports using the extracted data.
Preferred Qualifications
• Prefer 3+ years of experience in Finance, Risk and Regulatory Reporting. Strong knowledge of credit risk, market risk concepts
• Knowledge of reporting tools like: Cognos, Tableau, Power BI is preferred.
• Experience using tools like: Python, R or similar is a plus
Development Opportunities:
• Opportunity to widen your knowledge of the investment banking industry and key control processes
• Chance to build an exceptional global network of professionals across different business areas, technology teams and 2nd line functions, including Finance and Risk
• Long-term career path across geographies and business lines
• Competitive compensation package and flexible work arrangements.
