12478,3,Data Analyst,"Government Employees Health Association, Inc. - GEHA","Lee's Summit, MO","GEHA (Government Employees Health Association, Inc., pronounced G.E.H.A.) is a nonprofit member association that provides medical and dental benefits to more than two million federal employees and retirees, military retirees and their families. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.

GEHA has one mission: To empower federal workers to be... healthy and well.

Offering one of the largest medical and dental benefit provider networks available to federal employees in the United States, GEHA empowers health and wellness by meeting its members where they are, when they need care. We serve our members with products they value and a personalized customer experience, sustained by a nimble and efficient organization.
Job Description Summary

Under supervision within the Analytics function. Develops analytical insights for all business units using written or oral instruction of what is needed. Super user of analytic solutions supported by the Analytics division and has a strong knowledge of enterprise accepted reporting, data and systems.
SKILLS
• Develops reports, data files and dashboards based on requirements through direct interaction with designated business unit.
• Conducts research and analysis to provide insights, identify trends and patterns, and share results back with members of business and management.
• Thorough knowledge of enterprise accepted analytical and data sources in order to satisfy business requests and maximize efficiency.
• Create new insightful metrics to help enterprise track and analyze data.
• Prepare report writing documentation.
• Collaborates alongside business team and management to contribute to growing business needs.
• Communicates data analysis and data solutions with business and analytic teams

Minimum Requirements
• Requires a Bachelor's degree in Healthcare, Business Administration, Computer Science, Statistics or a related discipline.
• Additional year relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education
• Requires 4-6 years of experience in a Data Analytics or Data Management role (internally or at another company.)
• 2 years of SQL
• Strong communication and collaboration skills within varied business and analytics teams
• Confident presentation skills

Preferred Qualifications
• Healthcare experience
• Experience with PowerBI

Work-at-home requirements
• Must have the ability to provide a non-cellular High Speed Internet Service such as Fiber, DSL, or cable Modems for a home office.
• A minimum standard speed for optimal performance of 30x5 (30mpbs download x 5mpbs upload) is required.
• Latency (ping) response time lower than 80 ms
• Hotspots, satellite and wireless internet service is NOT allowed for this role.
• A dedicated space lacking ongoing interruptions to protect member PHI / HIPAA information

How we value you
• Competitive pay/salary ranges
• Incentive plan
• Health/Vision/Dental benefits effective day one
• 401(k) retirement plan: company match - dollar for dollar up to 4% employee contribution (pretax or Roth options) plus a 6% annual company contribution
• Robust employee well-being program
• Paid Time Off
• Personal Community Enrichment Time
• Company-provided Basic Life and AD&D
• Company-provided Short-Term & Long-Term Disability
• Tuition Assistance Program

Please note that the salary information is a general guideline only. GEHA considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and business considerations when extending an offer.
The annual base salary range for this position is $69,639 - $97,561 USD.

GEHA is an Equal Opportunity Employer, which means we will not discriminate against any individual based on sex, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, age, military status, genetic information, veteran status, pregnancy, marital status, gender identity, and sexual orientation, as well as all other characteristics and qualities protected by federal, state, or local law. GEHA will not discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their compensation or the compensation of another employee or applicant. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. Our diversity drives innovation deepens connections and strengthens our organization.

GEHA is headquartered in Lee's Summit, Missouri, in the Kansas City area. We recognize the importance of balance and flexibility and offer hybrid and work-from-home options for many of our roles.

An Executive Order was released stating that federal contractors must require COVID-19 vaccinations for all US employees. As a company that works on federal contracts, we have a legal requirement to comply with the executive order, if it is enforced",2022-10-18,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'sql']"
12506,31,Senior Data Analyst,StartupJobs,United States,"🍪 Privacy Notice

Senior Data Analyst - Remote...

United States / Engineering / Full-time / Remote Mattermost is an open source platform for secure collaboration across the entire software development lifecycle. Hundreds of thousands of developers around the globe trust Mattermost to increase their productivity by bringing together team communication, task and project management, and workflow orchestration into a unified platform for agile software development.
Founded in 2016, Mattermost's open source platform powers over 800,000 workspaces worldwide with the support of over 4,000 contributors from across the developer community. The company serves over 800 customers, including European Parliament, NASA, Nasdaq, Samsung, SAP, United States Air Force and Wealthfront, and is backed by world-class investors including Battery Ventures, Redpoint, S28 Capital, YC Continuity. To learn more, visit .
We value high impact work, ownership, self-awareness and being focused on customer success. If these values match who you are, we hope you'll learn more about and apply
Mattermost is seeking a passionate data enthusiast to solve data analytics and engineering problems in the Marketing, Sales, Finance, Product and Engineering organizations. As a data-driven organization, Mattermost relies on our data team to drive marketing insights, ensure accurate data across systems, iterate on current key business metrics, and dive into complex datasets to answer business-critical this role, you will work closely with the Finance, Marketing, Sales, Product and Engineering organizations to deeply understand customer trends, analyze marketing activities, product adoption, and sales results in order to surface insights that impact the health of the overall business. If you are data-obsessed, love connecting the dots, thrive in an iterative environment, and aren't afraid to get your hands dirty, this is the role for you.
About Our Tools ● Tool Stack: Marketo, Salesforce, Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, Google Optimize, Clearbit, Rudderstack, Snowflake, dbt, airflow, Stitch, Hightouch, Looker, Google Sheets/Excel, etc. ● Coding Languages: SQL, Python, LookML

Responsibilities:

Proactively identify data-related issues, investigate root causes, and drive them to resolution across Finance, Marketing, Sales, Product, and Engineering functional areas

Participate in the development process for our Finance, Marketing, Sales, Product and Engineering analytics reporting. This includes meeting with internal customers to understand their needs, understanding the core data models, writing code to enrich and transform raw data to analytics data and designing and iterating dashboards

Build and maintain models that will help the functional teams predict results and report on performance

Work with the other Data Engineering team members to ensure relevant data is centralized into our data warehouse and modeled for performant analytics, while meeting our high-quality standards

Be hands-on with monitoring tools, work with large data sets, and provide insights into our performance(e.g. Finance). This includes writing queries to access data, performing analysis, utilizing your technical expertise as well as a variety of internal tools and/or collaborating with other teams as needed

Effectively communicate insights and make recommendations and decisions in line with business objectives

Help project manage the end to end process to triage and resolve anomalies in various functional areas; this includes leading investigation efforts to identify root causes which may include changes in sales pipeline, product releases and/or system related issues

Become an expert at maintaining a variety of internal data systems and automate and script repetitive tasks where needed

Required Background/Skills:

5+ years of demonstrated experience in data analysis or analytics engineering

Experience with schema design, data modeling and metadata management

Experience applying Software Engineering best practices to data analytics including CI/CD, version control, etc.

Experience with building and maintaining data pipelinesIn-depth knowledge of (at least) one data warehouse system

Experience with building reports to various stakeholdersStrong SQL skills

Excellent written and verbal communication skills

Demonstrable teamwork skills and resourcefulness",2022-12-08,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sap', 'looker', 'snowflake', 'python', 'sql', 'airflow']"
12520,45,Product Data Analyst,Parts Town,United States,"Position at Parts Town

See What We're All About...

As the fastest growing distributor of foodservice equipment parts, we like to do things a little differently. We believe our team should be like family. Not like a second cousin, twice removed, but more like the family you choose to be with every day. First, youmustdemonstrate our core valuesand keep safety as your #1 priority, that's key. But we're also looking for unique enthusiasm, high integrity,courage toembrace if you know a few jokes, that puts you on the top of our list.

About Red Lightning Group

Red Lightning Group is a new and separate division of PT Holdings focusing solely on innovation to support the foodservice industry and beyond. We are accelerating the pace of breakthroughs to expand and grow our business faster than ever before

Perks
• Parts Town Pride - check out our and
• Red Lightning Group sponsored employee training and development opportunities
• Team member appreciation events and recognition programs
• Volunteer opportunities
• Casual dress code
• On-demand pay options: Access your pay as you earn it, to cover unexpected or even everyday expenses
• All the traditional benefits like health insurance, 401k/401k match, employee assistance programs and time away - don't worry, we've got you covered.

The Job at a Glance

The Product Data Analyst (Internally known as the Product Data Wizard) will be responsible for taking a lead role in our product data initiatives related to the Parts Town Marketplace. This includes adding and updating all product data such as, images, digital media, category landing pages and categorization of information that supports the Parts Town Marketplace. Examples of projects include working directly with Marketplace sellers to obtain content about new categories being added into the marketplace such as product descriptions, images, product specs, manuals, etc. which will enhance the unique search functionality of the Parts Town website, mobile app, and mobile-optimized website as well as improves organic search ranking. Competitive research and analysis of Marketplaces is a must

A Typical Day
• Partner with the Marketplace Onboarding Manager as well as Marketplace sellers to collect product content specific to the seller's product categories
• Analyze collected data from multiple sources to ensure accuracy before loading onto our website as well as our ERP
• Develop a process to ensure that collected product data from multiple sellers for the same offer is accurate as well as differentiating.
• Establish and maintain an ongoing data analysis to ensure product content is currently up to date regards to product descriptions, images and other product content
• Maintain a relationship with the Red Lightning Digital analyst to develop and track the effectiveness of any product data that is loaded onto our website
• Analyze other marketplace competitors and provide suggestions on optimizations or additions to our product data strategy.
• Continually manage replacement or obsolescence items
• Work on our product image strategy which can include optimizing seller provided images, working with photographers, etc.
• Utilize numerous ecommerce tools such as Google Analytics, Hotjar, Hybris, etc.

To Land This Opportunity
• You have strong project management and organizational skills - demonstrated through your ability to think on your feet, work with limited resources, and manage multiple projects at once
• You know MS Office (Access and Excel), heck you consider yourself a pro
• You're adaptable and self-motivated to quickly pick up new skills and learn new tasks
• You have the desire to build and lead our product data efforts as well as providing additional ideas ways to achieve our team goals
• You demonstrate a passion and knowledge for analytical skills and basic vendor management
• You have experience with e-commerce product data management and product information management
• Basic knowledge or strong desire to learn and utilize scripting languages such as Python and Powershell
• You are often referred to as a unicorn as you possess all of these features and would be the ideal future team member

Extra awesome
• You are familiar with SEO and analytics tools, such as Google Analytics, BrightEdge, Google Search Console, SEMrush, etc.
• Remember, just be yourself. Unless you can be a unicorn. Then always be a unicorn.

About Your Future Team

How do lightning bolts laugh? They crack up Yes, we love puns. Most of us enjoy a pot of java each day while some just stick to sweets for a quick pick me up. Some can bake and some can cook but when in doubt, we all know how to order out. Most of us should go back to driving school to learn a few things about parking and drive thru-s though. We all love sports whether we played at some point in our lives, or currently watch our kids throw. One member of our team actually worked at Super Bowl XL, assisting former NFL athletes. Some of us have four legged furry friends as their ""other"" coworkers. They always seem to chime in during conference calls, begging for some treats. BEST of all - we love to innovate

