Job Description

The Corporate Audit Services Senior Data Analyst supports internal audit with data analysis projects designed to improve the effectiveness and efficiency of audit engagements of U.S.
Bancorp (USB), affiliates, wholly owned subsidiaries and entities where USB owns a majority (controlling) interest.

The Senior Data Analyst is also expected to develop and deepen relationships with key internal and external stakeholders that include, but are not limited to:
CAS leadership, regulatory agencies; business line and risk management peers; external subject matter experts; and industry peers.

The Senior Data Analyst is responsible for performing assigned data analysis projects in accordance with U.S. Bank Human Resources policies and internal audit policies and procedures to support the audit teams completing their engagements.

Responsibilities:

Responsible for working on advanced big data/analytics projects that gather and integrate large volumes of data to perform analysis, interpret results and develop actionable insights and recommendations for use across CAS.

Collaborates with the CAS audit teams to promote the use of data analytics, building more effective tests of controls, enabling more comprehensive audit testing, providing efficiencies that cannot be achieved through manual testing, and increasing the use of data analytics overall.
Includes assisting CAS audit teams to better understand their data.

Acquires complex data from multiple data sources, including emerging distributed database platforms, in order to perform sophisticated analyses that will provide insights about the risk and control environment.

Identifies, analyzes and interprets trends or patterns in data in order to provide answers to business questions, as well as provide recommendations for action.
Interprets complex data and analyzes results using various statistical techniques and tools.

Presents data and analysis in a clear and concise manner, allowing the audience to quickly understand the results and recommendations, so they may act upon them and make data driven decisions.
Collaborates with various partners to provide a holistic view of the analysis.

Measures and monitors results of applied recommendations and facilitates adjustments.

Ensures all data acquisition, sharing and results of applied recommendations are compliant with company standards.

Provides technical coaching and assistance to others as needed, sharing expert-level knowledge of tools and languages.

Basic Qualifications
• Bachelor's degree in a related field, or equivalent work experience
• Five to seven years of statistical and/or data analytics experience

Preferred Skills/Experience:
• Relevant technical knowledge: 2 3 years of work experience with Tableau or Power BI, and 5 or more years of significant work experience with one or more of the following: SQL, SAS, Python, R/R-Studio, WebFOCUS, or ACL
• CIA, CISA, or other relevant professional designation or advanced degree.
Public accounting or other relevant experience
• Ability to independently translate complex business scenarios into efficient and effective data analytic solutions
• Internal audit experience
• Demonstrated project management skills
• Effective interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills
This role is hybrid. Team members who are in a hybrid role typically spend three days a week at a U.S. Bank location, while having flexibility on their work location for the other working days.

