About the team

We are a Product focused business unit focused on Knowledge Management and Collaborative Work Management themes. Today the majority of our customer base and value add is via Confluence and Trello Apps. We have 3 main product teams and a management structure to support that as well a number of key roles working across those 3 product teams.

We cover the usual Product functions so Engineering, Marketing, Product Management, UX etc. Today the team is approx 30 people.

About the role

The purpose of the Senior Data Analyst role is to provide actionable, data-driven, insights to the business. The portfolio of digital products this role would cover are diverse and insights required relate to user interaction, user sentiment, financial performance, license statistics and other product and user-related metrics. The team are the 'Front Door' for end users into the wider Analytics Team (comprising of Analytics Analyst & Analytics Engineers), leveraging excellent stakeholder management and analysis skills to improve the outcome of business decisions.

Contributing to the Presentation layer of our Data Stack (BI reports, Presentation Layer, Kimball Models) the Analyst role has a significant impact on the ability of the organisation to access information and insights.

They work closely with the organisation to understand Business Issues which require reporting or information, translate these into requirements, and then, working alongside Analytics Engineers, deliver solutions.

The Analytics Analyst is a hybrid role, combining skills around problem-solving and understanding stakeholder's needs, alongside the implementation of Technical Solutions (Modelling, SQL, coding, Databases etc). They look to leverage our 'Data Estate', focussing on reusability of Models, ease of access to information for end users and evangelising the use of our Data Assets.

