13184,709,Category Data Analyst,Cookies,United States,"Category Data Analyst

Yea, I do a hundred mil annual...

Dope game, I damn near wrote the manual

—Berner

Cookies sells iconic cannabis, with roots that stretch back to garage grows in San Francisco, before the industry was an industry. Our breeders developed many of the world's most famous strains, from GSC to Gary Payton, and we have flagship stores and infrastructure operating on multiple continents.

At Cookies your work will have a personal impact at truly global scale —in Los Angeles, Detroit, and Barcelona, the quality of our products affect our customers' lives for the better. We know cannabis can be a force multiplier for equity, economic inclusion, diversity and community, and we are on a mission to bring that culture to the world.

We're looking for a fully-remote Data Analyst who can jump in with both feet and help us select, develop, and deploy strategic solutions that support all aspects of the Cookies vision and mission. This role will involve cross-functional requirements gathering, ideation, synthesis of those requirements into solutions, and then deployment of those solutions throughout Cookies and our network of partners, constellation of vendors, and footprint of stores, sites, brands, and lines of business.

Major Areas of Responsibility:
• Understand how Cookies can leverage our data to prioritize Product category opportunities and make faster decisions by defining metrics and identifying data needed.
• Combine external market data points with internal sales data points to help guide our category management team to select the best products to grow, manufacture and distribute in our growing Cookies Retail network.
• Build scalable tools and creative solutions, working with leadership to implement them.
• Ability to work with vast and ambiguous data sets to create business visualizations leading to create action-oriented solutions
• Contribute during data architecture discussions.
• Work cross-functionally with Cookies commercial team to deliver data insight to help guide business decisions.
• Write unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and other QA code.
• Design, perform and analyze A/B testing data (exposure to experimental design is a plus).
• Manage and own work in Jira sprints.

You have:
• SQL experience required - know how to interpret and package data so our team can deliver innovative analysis to streamline our operations.
• Bonus points: Python and/or R, Tableau, Superset, Metabase and similar data visualization tools
• Any experience with CRM, PIM and GS1 GDSN are a plus.
• Excellent analytical thinking - you'll connect dots between data and operations and gut check the numbers you use.
• Passion for frontier hyper-growth industries, particularly legal cannabis.
• Experience implementing data-driven decisions with measurable results.
• Healthy curiosity and spirit of an innovator for learning new tools and applying them to drive efficiency in day-to-day activities.
• Ability to break down complex problems into manageable pieces, strong organizational & project management skills.

Cookies is a fast-paced, dynamic environment. We are looking for team members who are kind but driven, and who know how to get stuff done. We are a fun, entrepreneurial group focused on culture, community and quality.

We believe that in diversity is strength. We encourage all to apply, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability status. We will ensure that people with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process.

This is a full-time position with the ability to work remotely. While our team and company-operated retail locations are primarily located in California, we are open to applicants who are willing to work west coast business hours.

Come join our team",2022-01-22,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'python', 'sql', 'r', 'jira']"
