13210,735,Intern: Financial Data Analyst,EquipmentShare,"Columbia, MO","EquipmentShare is Hiring an Financial Data Analyst Intern.

EquipmentShare is searching for a student intern to join the data analyst team at our Home Office in Columbia, Mo for the 2023 summer...

Your Opportunity to Grow With Us

With 40 interns in 20 different departments in our most recent class, the opportunities to grow with EquipmentShare span far outside traditional construction industry roles.

Our mission is to build the future of construction, and educate and train interns who have the potential to join our team full-time and help us grow. EquipmentShare has a robust internship program that gives students hands-on opportunities to work and learn in a team environment. Our program equips students with various resources to help shape them into young professionals. From one-on-one mentoring to group education sessions, we are dedicated to investing in the next generation of innovators.

EquipmentShare interns are part of the close-knit group of professionals who all share an interest in providing services and products that improve our customers experiences. Our talented and passionate team uses its skills to help interns develop professionally and contribute to our mission. Above all, we care about building something people want, and are looking for interns who share the same passion.

Were seeking a financial data analyst intern who wants the opportunity to gain professional experience with a rapidly-growing company. The opportunity for growth is unparalleled at EquipmentShare where youll get the chance to build new skills and trailblaze a path to establishing your career.

Responsibilities
• Analyze a wide range of data, and turn that data into action, whether that looks like process improvements, best business practices or other data-backed solutions
• Use your strong development and analytical skills to solve business problems across the company
• Produce reports and models for senior leaders and other key team members
• Identify trends, correlations and patterns in data, and present findings to stakeholder
• Perform statistical analysis, predictive and explanatory modeling, and data mining About You
• Must be qualified to work in the United States - we are not sponsoring any candidates at this time.
• Studying to achieve a bachelor's degree in Statistics, Business Analytics, Economics, Computer Science, Mathematics, or Accounting/Finance or related field
• Expert-level Excel skills
• SQL experience preferred
• Knowledge of an analytical language like Python, R, SAS, SPSS, etc. preferred
• Working knowledge of financial data: forecasting, reporting, and analysis experience, a keen understanding of financial statements and financial data
• Ability to swiftly extract key insights from data
• Proven ability to approach complex problems with curiosity and an analytical mindset
• Eagerness to learn
• Proactive
• Self-Sufficient
• Great communication skills
• You roll with the punches and can adapt quickly, manage competing projects and challenge the status quo Why Were a Better Place to Work EquipmentShare interns have the opportunity to enjoy many perks while working at our Home Office, including:
• Hot breakfast and lunch provided daily
• Healthy snacks, drinks and unlimited coffee bar
• On-site fitness center and group fitness classes
• Weekly professional development sessions
• Mentor and intern happy hours
• End-of-program celebration About EquipmentShare Together with our customers and employees, EquipmentShare is building the future of construction by creating a connected jobsite for the modern contractor. We deliver user-friendly solutions that help contractors maximize their equipment uptime, reduce risk exposure and increase productivity. EquipmentShares product offerings include an improved equipment rental experience and our T3 technology that encompasses fleet tracking and asset management software, hardware security solutions and predictive service and maintenance applications. EquipmentShare is the fastest growing, independently-owned construction solutions and equipment rental company in the country. We serve dozens of markets across the U.S., and are building a national footprint in every major market in the country. Our 120+ branch locations are equipped with a wide variety of construction equipment, ranging from 150-foot telescopic booms to 120,000-pound track excavators. Our expansion and customer retention validate the strong contractor demand for the smart jobsite technology weve built into our rental fleet. And its just the beginning of our journey to establishing a global presence. EquipmentShare is proud to be a Workplace for All that employs people from all backgrounds and walks of life. We combine the construction and technology sectors to create something incredible which includes our unmatched work environment. EquipmentShare is a People First company where high tech meets hard work thats fulfilled by passionate people who have the grit to solve some of the toughest challenges. Prioritizing health and wellness is how we set our employees up for success, both in and out of the workplace. Our team members are also committed to building and bettering the communities we serve through 16 hours of Volunteer Time Off (VTO) and using our giving-back budget to focus on helping those most in need across the country.

Since our founding in 2014 and incorporation in 2015, weve had explosive growth and were not stopping anytime soon. Ready to support our mission, invest in yourself and discover your potential? Then wed love to meet you. Apply today.

EquipmentShare is an EOE M/F/D/V",2022-09-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'sql', 'spss', 'sas', 'excel', 'r']"
13241,766,(Senior) Data Analyst,Stanford University,"Stanford, CA","(Senior) Data Analyst🔍Vice Provost for Student Affairs, Stanford, California, United States📁Information Analytics📅Nov 08, 2022 Post Date📅96909 Requisition #Stanford University has an immediate opening for a full-time Senior Data Analyst. This position will provide reporting, data analysis and forecasting for academic space planning and scheduling. This is a key role in the success of... Stanford Classrooms Reimagined, the 10-year strategic plan for learning spaces campus-wide. This position will initially support two teams within the division of Student Affairs: Learning Technologies and Spaces (LTS) and Curriculum Management and Scheduling (CMS). This position works on a high-performing, cross-functional team of experts ranging from curriculum management and scheduling, to audio visual technologies, learning space design, project and operations management. Student AffairsLTS and CMS are part of Student Affairs, which supports a variety of student experiences inside our learning spaces and outside the classroom in our residences, community centers, student organizations, health center, and career education center. Student Affairs aspires to ""educate students to make meaningful contributions as citizens of a complex world."" This is Our Most Important Work. About CMS:
The Curriculum Management and Scheduling team within the Registrar's Office is responsible for maintaining the integrity of information about over 300 programs, nearly 20,000 active courses, scheduling 29,000 class sections per quarter, managing nearly 200 classroom and other event spaces, with over 8,000 events being scheduled yearly into the spaces that we manage. About LTS:
Learning Technologies & Spaces (LTS) facilitates exceptional teaching and learning. We design, implement, provision, operate, and support an ecosystem of platforms, tools, services, and technology-rich classrooms and learning spaces. Our aim is to provide great experiences for faculty and students in the use of instructional technology and classrooms to create engaging and accessible learning experiences for all our students. About the Position:Reporting to the Senior Director, Learning Spaces, the Senior Data Analyst will help shape strategic campus learning space design and planning and inform how we use classroom and learning spaces across the Stanford campus. This position works very closely with both the LTS and CMS teams, contributing experience and expertise in all facets of learning space design and scheduling as well as classroom information system development and use, database integrity, reporting, and data analysis. The Senior Data Analyst will leverage a range of data sources, quantitative and qualitative methods, and technical tools in independent and collaborative projects ranging from improving routine reporting to deep dives into specific questions. You want to make an impact by leveraging data-driven insights and enjoy working collaboratively in an innovative environment. You are a problem solver with a passion to deliver advanced data-driven solutions. You are curious, collaborative, and creative, with an eagerness to learn about new topics and new analytic techniques, and an ability to communicate results effectively to a wide variety of audiences. You are passionate about data and IT, conversant with space planning, teaching, and have experience in integrating data sources and systems, preferably in higher educational environments. You are people- and solutions-focused; bring a positive outlook; and thrive equally when working as an individual contributor and collaboratively with a cross-unit team. Inclusion and diversity are integral to Stanford's commitment to excellence. We are interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience engaging with diversity through activities such as fostering an inclusive environment, working with students and staff from diverse backgrounds, or incorporating diverse perspectives in their work. Your responsibilities include:Data Analysis and ReportingFoster a continuous-improvement and insight-driven environment that supports Stanford's instructional mission:
• Ensure decision-makers across the University have well-curated, consistent, transparent, high-quality data assets and reporting.
• Produce highly polished, audience-appropriate deliverables (e.g., tables, charts, interactive dashboards, narrative reports) for division leadership, other school and university audiences, and external agencies as applicable.
• Build, implement, and manage classroom and learning space data infrastructure and program
• Support the development and implementation of KPI's and dashboards across data sources.
• Identify patterns, trends, and other insights in datasets using a variety of qualitative and quantitative techniques.
• Serve as a resource for inquiries about data and reporting across a wide range of functional areas. Data Management, Database Design and Performance Tuning
• Identify relevant data sources; creating and maintaining datasets for analysis; recommending and implementing new processes around data collection, management, reporting, and analysis as needed.
• Establish and integrate systems for maximizing the efficiency and accuracy of reporting, monitoring data integrity, facilitating integrations across data sources, and documenting processes.
• Collaborate with technical staff and end users to standardize, systematize, and automate routine reports, dashboards, and metrics, as well as with partners throughout the university on the development of shared or central solutions as appropriate.
• Contribute to the design, development, and maintenance of databases.
• Develop algorithms and statistical models; and perform statistical analyses appropriate to complex data and reporting requirements. Leading Projects
• Meet with campus partners to understand problems that would benefit by leveraging of university data
• Requirements gathering. Scoping and defining projects and data and metadata sets to meet reporting needs
• Apply security best practices. Other duties as assigned Other duties as assigned To be successful in this role, you will bring:
• Bachelor's degree and three years of relevant experience or combination of education and relevant experience. Experience in a quantitative discipline such as economics, finance, statistics or engineering.
• Ability to design, create, refine meaningful research questions, datasets, analyses, and reports.
• Strong ability to evaluate data quality, and to identify appropriate methods for working with imperfect data sources.
• Ability to work with data of varying levels of quality and validity.
• In-depth knowledge and experience using and applying analytical software, database management system software, database reporting software, database user interface and query software, and data mining software.
• Expert ability to collect, clean, manage, analyze, visualize data using a variety of methods.
• Basic statistical ability.
• Strong listening, verbal and written communication skills.
• Ability to manage multiple activities in a deadline-oriented environment; highly organized, flexible and rigorous attention to detail.
• Ability to work effectively with multiple internal and external customers.
• Ability to take a leadership role on projects and with users/clients. In addition, our preferred requirements include:
• Experience with reporting, analytical, and visualization tools such as Tableau, SAS, OBIEE, SQL, R, Python, or similar.
• Experience in a social science discipline, e.g., sociology, anthropology, linguistics, psychology, especially when this includes a quantitative component.
• Experience in integrating data sources and systems
• Experience working in higher education, including familiarity with data, systems, business processes, space planning, or in a relevant functional area.
• Familiarity with institutional research, assessment, program evaluation, or business intelligence.
• Experience serving in a leadership role on projects and with users/clients.
• Conversant with space planning, teaching. Physical Requirements:Constantly perform desk-based computer tasks.Frequently sit, sort, file paperwork or parts, grasp lightly, and use fine manipulation, lift, carry, push and pull objects that weigh 10 pounds or less.Occasionally write by hand, twist, bend, stoop and squat.Rarely stand, walk, reach or work above shoulders and use a telephone. Working Conditions:May work extended hours during peak business cycles.The university requires all staff to be fully vaccinated for COVID-19 and provide proof of vaccination prior to their start date, unless granted a medical or religious accommodation.This position is designated as fully onsite or hybrid, working onsite a minimum of 2 days per week. Work Standards:Interpersonal Skills: Demonstrates the ability to work well with Stanford colleagues and clients and with external organizations.Promote Culture of Safety: Demonstrates commitment to personal responsibility and value for safety; communicates safety concerns; uses and promotes safe behaviors based on training and lessons learned.Subject to and expected to comply with all applicable University policies and procedures, including but not limited to the personnel policies and other policies found in the University's Administrative Guide, Why Stanford is for you:Imagine a world without search engines or social platforms. Consider lives saved through first-ever organ transplants and research to cure illnesses. Stanford University has revolutionized the way we live and enrich the world. Supporting this mission is our diverse and dedicated 17,000 staff. We seek talent driven to impact the future of our legacy. Our culture and unique perks empower you with:Freedom to grow. We offer career development programs, tuition reimbursement, or audit a course. Join a TedTalk, film screening, or listen to a renowned author or global leader speak.A caring culture. We provide superb retirement plans, generous time-off, and family care resources.A healthier you. Climb our rock wall, or choose from hundreds of health or fitness classes at our world-class exercise facilities. We also provide excellent health care benefits.Discovery and fun. Stroll through historic sculptures, trails, and museums.Enviable resources. Enjoy free commuter programs, ridesharing incentives, discounts and more The job duties listed are typical examples of work performed by positions in this job classification and are not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, tasks, and responsibilities. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary depending on department or program needs without changing the general nature and scope of the job or level of responsibility. Employees may also perform other duties as assigned. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodation to any employee with a disability who requires accommodation to perform the essential functions of his or her job. Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by lawAdditional Information
• Schedule: Full-time
• Job Code: 4745
• Employee Status: Regular
• Grade: I
• Requisition ID: 96909",2022-02-11,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'python', 'sql', 'outlook', 'sas', 'r']"
13252,777,Financial Data Analyst,LifeChurch,"Edmond, OK","The Financial Data Analyst is primarily responsible for providing data analysis via data visualizations.

At Life.Church, we exist to lead people to become fully devoted followers of Christ. It's been our mission since 1996 and has guided us every day. Leading people isn't just an expectation; it's a necessity. It's a cornerstone of our culture. That's why we're always seeking leaders-leaders... like you-to bring your skills to life. We are one church meeting in multiple locations, and we want to help you become the person God made you to be.

The Finance Team partners with the organization to facilitate the financial reporting needs of Life.Church, including payroll, accounts payable, giving operations, accounting, forecasting, and data analytics. We equip the organization with the tools needed to plan for, understand, and steward the resources God has provided for our ministry.

This role will use SQL and other programming languages to query, summarize, and analyze key metrics and develop data visualizations for the Financial Operations Group (FOG) in support of Life.Church and YouVersion. This position ensures data integrity and provides technical support & maintenance across all Financial Operations Group Systems. The Financial Data Analyst acts as an advocate and vital technical resource for all FOG teams through implementing new processes and maintaining operational integrity in partnership with both internal departments and external service providers or vendors.

What You'll Do
• Perform investigative analysis with FOG data residing in MSSQL and BigQuery.
• Manage and ensure the functionality of key systems used by the Finance team (RockRMS, Coupa, Sage Intacct, Tableau, etc.)
• Develop reports and dashboards that answer business operation questions submitted by FOG team leaders, Financial Operations Group Leader, or Life.Church Directional Leadership.
• Develop new, reinvent existing, add features to, and optimize data structure for new and existing data analytics in Tableau.
• Provide internal technical support and act as the main point of contact for external contact support.
• Develop and train the team on process improvement initiatives to drive efficiency.
• Properly document system processes and procedures to ensure successful knowledge transfer.
Skills Needed to Succeed
• SQL, Python or other related programming language skills and experience.
• Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills to maintain relationships and partnerships.
• Maintain a systematic and organized approach to completing assignments accurately, thoroughly, and timely.
• Clearly explain complicated and detailed processes concisely.
• Ability to self-motivate, take initiative, make independent decisions, and problem-solve.
• Ability to collaborate in a team environment and work independently.
• High School Diploma or GED.
• 1-3 years of related work experience.
Benefits We Offer
• Paid parental leave, including maternity, paternity, and adoption leave.
• Generous employer-paid leave for use of vacation, sick time, and other qualifying reasons.
• Innovative and comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance that provides team members with useful resources and savings to navigate their holistic health.
• Life insurance policy provided for all staff members at 2x annual salary at no cost. Additional life insurance coverage is available to purchase.
• Short-Term and Long-Term disability covered at 100% for full-time qualified staff members.
• Comprehensive wellness and mental health benefits allow staff to proactively invest in their physical and emotional health.
• Generous 401(k) retirement plan allowing a team member to have up to 12.5% (including employee contribution, employer match, and employer discretionary contribution) contributed into their account in their first year. It doesn't stop there-the more years on staff, the greater the investment
• $160 annually in development dollars for team members to invest in their professional growth.
• Casual dress and work environment.
• Flexible work schedule.
• And much more
Our Beliefs, Culture, and Commitment to Diversity

At Life.Church, every staff member, and intern is a minister and is expected to engage in the church's ministry fully. We consider ministry readiness and an individual's capacity to represent Life.Church's beliefs as a minister during the selection process for all staff and intern positions. An essential function within every position held by a staff member or intern at Life.Church is to uphold and represent the beliefs of Life.Church. Learn more about what we believe at Life.Church.

While we unite around our mission, we know unity doesn't mean uniformity. Our calling is too great, and our mission is too important not to be intentional about strengthening our team through diversity. We know that diverse perspectives in race, ethnicity, background, age, and gender are essential to reaching the world for Christ. To learn more about how we strengthen our team through diversity, visit our careers page.

All data collected in our application process, from resume collection to application questions, is used for recruitment purposes only",2022-10-17,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'mssql', 'python', 'sql', 'bigquery']"
