? Manage projects from start to end: build timelines and important milestones, provide regular updates to Analytics Management partners and achieve delivery against agreed upon specs

• Directly produces datasets and reports for analysis using databases and reporting tools, mapping to business requirements

• Create Sales & Marketing Data tools

? Partner closely with Business leads to design, execute and evaluate A/B tests. Understand common pitfalls and caveats when designing and evaluating results.

? Define how to best measure the performance of Siemens Digital Industries product and business through new metrics and dimensions - align on definitions with the business (evaluating tradeoffs and defining guardrails), and prototype metrics through custom data pipelines.

? Empower the marketing team to answer data questions quickly and easily by building high-quality ground truth data sets and dashboards.

Qualifications:

• Master's or Bachelor's degree in a relevant field of study

• 10+ years top tier analyst or consulting experience in business analytics

• Expert communication and collaboration skills with the ability to work effectively with internal teams in a cross-cultural and

cross-functional environment. Ability to conduct rigorous analysis and communicate conclusions to both technical and nontechnical

audiences

• Hands-on experience with one or more language(s) used for querying (e.g., SQL, Python)

• Advanced Excel skills including pivot tables, macros, charts, functions, vba modeling

• Experience with Analytics platforms/languages like Snowflake, Python, R a big plus

• Experience with Tableau or similar BI platform to develop reports and dashboards a plus

• Experience with Advanced Analytics (modeling, optimization, forecasting, experimentation) a plus

• Experience with marketing or sales analytics a huge plus

• Excellent communication skills with the ability to distill complex subjects to a wider audience, technical and non-technical

• Experience with delivering analytics recommendations to senior leadership and executive level audiences

• Hands-on to get things done fast and ability to work without continual guidance

• Excellent time management skills, attention to detail and ability to prioritize work

