13404,929,Client Engagement Data & Insights Analyst,Lincoln Financial Group,"Oklahoma City, OK","Alternate Locations: Work from Home

Work Arrangement: Work from Home...

Relocation assistance: : is not available for this opportunity.

Pay Range: $63,100 - $137,900

Bonus Potential: 5%

Requisition #: 70917

The Role at a Glance

We are looking for a passionate team member committed to serving others to join our team as the Client Engagement Data & Insights Analyst of the Retirement Plan Services Client Engagement Group. Our continued growth and ongoing commitment to providing a high tech/high touch experience requires a strategic thinker who is adept at relationship building, problem solving, and identifying opportunities for process improvement and continued growth. You will consult/analyze and deliver on more complex assignments/projects for our team.

As an Client Engagement Data & Insights Analyst, you will have a large role in identifying insights and managing reporting for senior leadership and ultimately making a meaningful impact in the lives of others through selfless service. We all are dedicated to helping our clients on the journey to retirement readiness and financial wellness.

What you'll be doing
• Researches and analyzes complex performance data for business and analytical value by applying concepts such as probability, statistics, modeling, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical solutions
• Consults and acts as a subject matter expert for specific processes to maximize the efficiency of our team's efforts, departmental capabilities and/or return on investment
• Maintains knowledge on current and emerging developments/trends for Retirement Plan Services, assesses the impact, and collaborates with management to incorporate new trends and developments in current and future solutions
• Maintains tracking, measurement and accountability programs for various initiatives and looks to maximize our technology's capabilities to best track performance relative to our team's goals
• Collaborate with internal stakeholders, clients, and intermediaries to improve participant outcomes, retirement readiness, and financial wellness

What we're looking for

Must-haves:
• 3 - 5+ Years experience in data/reporting/insights experience that aligns with the responsibilities
• 4 Year/Bachelor's degree or equivalent work experience (4 years of experience in lieu of Bachelor's)
• Strong presentation skills at all levels of management through clear, informed and logical discussions/presentations
• Proven ability to develop creative solutions that finds common ground and builds consensus to ensure resources are aligned and achieve success
• High proficiency w/Microsoft Excel
• Working knowledge of Tableau and Data Management

Nice-to-haves:
• Retirement plan administration experience
• Experience w/Salesforce, Python, SQL, Process Automation

