13429,954,Data Analyst,Change Healthcare,"Topeka, KS","Change Healthcare is a leading healthcare technology company with a mission to inspire a better healthcare system. We deliver innovative solutions to patients, hospitals, and insurance companies to improve clinical decision making, simplify financial processes, and enable better patient experiences to improve lives and support healthier communities.

What will I be responsible for in this... job?

Position Summary:

The Data Analyst will utilize data analysis techniques and healthcare domain knowledge to analyze and synthesize data, construct data analytics processes, and develop information necessary to guide Change Healthcare's clients in their business decision making process. The position involves the ability to learn risk adjustment and submissions for Medicare, Medicaid, or Commercial ACA, along with database structures to do analytical work on behalf of our health plan clients. This position requires analytical skills and the ability to independently research business, technical, and application-related questions. This analyst will be responsible for the creation of custom reports and custom analytics using SQL and Python as well as other data analysis and visualization tools. The candidate should have good communication skills to work with clients and internal resources.

Essential Duties and Responsibilities :
• Create simple and complex analytics and reports requested by clients
• Coordinate the research of client data and collaborate with business leaders to provide actionable insights, design strategies, or recommend changes
• Participate in the advancement of improved efficiency and effectiveness of Change Healthcare's risk analytics algorithms
• Collects, cleanses, and automates data flow into a central repository
• Creates data visualizations for end users or for analysis including the use of dashboards (Tableau, Spotfire, etc.)
• Facilitates cross-functional teams and uses an inclusive approach to understanding current operations
• Demonstrate good judgment and analytical skills to conduct option analysis and present recommendations
• Actively works to overcome project barriers, and follows up with stakeholders on status
• Perform other duties as assigned

What are the requirements?
• Years of experience:
• 1-3 years of applicable work experience is desirable, preferably in analytics, data science, business intelligence, or similar field. Healthcare background is preferred
• Recent college graduates with relevant course work will also be considered
• Must have experience with SQL and at least one object-oriented programming language (Python, etc.)
• Strong personal computer literacy required including working knowledge of relevant software statistic packages and visualization suites

Education:
• BA or BS degree in a quantitative discipline such as Management Information Systems, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, Analytics or Computer Science
• Other majors will be considered if candidates have relevant experience or coursework that shows analytics skills What critical skills are needed for you to consider someone for this position?
• Experience with Python, visualization suites- Power BI, Spotfire, Tableau, etc. preferred but not required
• Ability to work with large amounts of data, including checks for integrity, summation
• Effective communication (written and verbal) to internal and external constituents
• Experience with relational databases is a plus What other skills/experience would be helpful to have?
• Healthcare industry knowledge
• Excellent organizational, communication and interpersonal skills
• ""Self-starter"" attitude with the ability to excel in dynamic work environments
• Ability to manage multiple priorities
• Outstanding problem-solving skills How much should I expect to travel?
• No travel expected

New York and New Jersey Residents Only: The salary range for New York City, NY and Westchester County, NY is $43,815 - $76,200. The salary range for Ithaca, NY is $38,100- $76,200. The salary range for Jersey City, NJ is $45,720 - $76,200. Pay is based on several factors including but not limited to education, work experience, certifications, etc. In addition to your salary, Change Healthcare offers benefits such as a comprehensive benefits package, incentive and recognition programs, equity and 401k contribution (all benefits are subject to eligibility requirements). No matter where or when you begin a career with Change Healthcare, you'll find a far-reaching choice of benefits and incentives.

Diversity, Equity & Inclusion :

•At Change Healthcare, we include all. We celebrate diversity and inclusivity, respect each other and value our unique experiences. By being our authentic selves, we bring different perspectives into our work and relationships.•Business Resource Groups (BRGs) play a central role in advancing diversity and inclusion at Change Healthcare. They deepen our understanding of different cultures, people, and experiences, and help foster an inclusive workplace. Change offers eight (8) BRGs. Learn more at ~~~ Feeling Inspired? Ready to #MakeAChange? Apply today!

COVID Vaccination Requirements

We remain committed to doing our part to ensure the health, safety and well-being of our team members and our communities. As such, some individuals may be required to disclose COVID-19 vaccination status prior to or during employment. Certain roles may require COVID-19 vaccination and/or testing as a condition of employment. Change Healthcare adheres to COVID-19 vaccination regulations as well as all client COVID-19 vaccination requirements and will obtain the necessary information from candidates prior to employment to ensure compliance.

Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Statement

Change Healthcare is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, disability, or veteran status. To read more about employment discrimination protections under federal law, read EEO is the Law at ~~~ and the supplemental information at ~~~.

If you need a reasonable accommodation to assist with your application for employment, please contact us by sending an email to ~~~ with ""Applicant requesting reasonable accommodation"" as the subject. Resumes or CVs submitted to this email box will not be accepted.

Click here ~~~ to view our pay transparency nondiscrimination policy.

California (US) Residents: By submitting an application to Change Healthcare for consideration of any employment opportunity, you acknowledge that you have read and understood Change Healthcare's Privacy Notice to California Job Applicants Regarding the Collection of Personal Information (~~~) .

Change Healthcare maintains a drug free workplace and conducts pre-employment drug-testing, where applicable, in accordance with federal, state and local laws.

