13499,1024,"Data & BI Analyst I, FIN",EDWARD JONES,"Houstonia, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.

The Data & BI Analyst II works in collaboration with other analysts and stakeholders on the formulation of an appropriate analytic approach to solve ambiguous business. In the Banking Business Unit the Data and BI Analyst will provide actionable insights to support business decisions related to product development, delivery, and adoption strategies to drive the future of banking at Edward Jones.

• Maintain a strong understanding of division results & key business drivers, as well as an understanding of key business strategies & priorities, apply business knowledge to analytic approach to address business questions

• Build and maintain a strong knowledge of data sets available to the analyst. Extract, cleanse and transform data to support analysis needs. Pressure test and validate logic and outputs against known sources and business acumen. Proactively identify data quality issues

• Define business and data requirements for analytic deliverables and serve as liaison with IS support teams. Lead collaboration with IDM for data improvements and proactively identify data enhancements in conjunction with division data stewards

• Understand and apply beginning statistical concepts

• Provide actionable insights to support business decisions, primarily by performing root cause, exploratory, sensitivity and scenario analysis, hypothesis testing, economic modeling, and data visualization to identify patterns/trends/insights etc. on ambiguous business problems

• Independently generate and incorporate insights into a cohesive story that clearly addresses business questions. Effectively communicate with business partners and non-technical audiences regarding analytic ideas, approach, key takeaways, and actionable insights

• Develop and manage business relationships with project team members and leaders across the organization. Consult with business owners to understand the business problem. Collaborate to identify the appropriate analytic approach to solve the problem

• Document, monitor, and proactively recommend improvements to processes and controls related to areas of responsibility

• Lead the development and monitoring of KPIs and benchmarks. Must be able to communicate results to senior leaders

• Serve as a technical and functional data subject matter expert

Experience Required:

• 3-5 years' experience in relevant field

• At least 2 years of analytics experience

Education Required:

• Bachelor's Degree with an emphasis in business, economics, math, engineering, or analytics preferred (or relevant work experience)

• Advanced Degree or Certification preferred

Functional Knowledge:

• Requires conceptual knowledge of theories, practices, and procedures within a job discipline

• Requires expanded conceptual knowledge in own job discipline and broadens capabilities

• Proficiency interacting with various database and file storage systems (e.g. Oracle, Hadoop, NoSQL)

• Understanding of join types

• Experience with data manipulation languages, such as SQL, required
