13504,1029,Product Analyst II - Predictive Analytics,EDWARD JONES,"Linn, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.

A driven business professional with exceptional analytical skills, critical thinking, systems thinking and interpersonal skills eager to work in a supportive, collaborative environment.
What you'll do:
• Liaison between Data Science, Business Stakeholders, and Product Owners to maintain, enhance or integrate firm systems and ML Models by serving on cross functional project teams in support of Advanced Analytics for the Firm.
• Identify current and future potential enterprise use cases of Advanced Analytics (Machine Learning Operations) solutions by interfacing with data & analytics teams as well as business units across the enterprise.
• Serve as subject matter experts of ML models automation.
• Support strategic communications with Product Owners and Business Stakeholders.
• Create, maintain, and review business process models, data flows, prototypes, business requirements, use cases and test cases.
• Execute and present written and verbal business systems impact analysis resulting in identification of new features, data integrations, and software recommendations that enable self-service analytics and reporting for the Firm.
• Generate communication, process, and educational plans to mitigate the disruption of change.
• Understanding of cross divisional systems and impacts of change.
• Follow moderately complex data analytics and Machine Learning Use Cases to interpret specific requirements in support of designing best fit business solutions.
• Write requirements for platform engineers and solution architects in a manner that reflects a working understanding of the data and products that will make up the solution.
• Build trust with business areas and ask probing questions to uncover unknown requirements.

What you'll need:
• Bachelor's degree is required, with emphasis in Computer Science, MIS, Business Analytics, or other quantitative area highly preferred.
• Understanding of Agile with experience with Jira or similar Agile workflow tool.
• Ability to conduct exploratory research, understand and interpret business needs, and translate needs into a solution using established patterns.
• Ability to multi-task and work with cross functional senior leaders to prioritize assigned tasks / projects.
• Basic understanding of Machine Learning and/or coursework in Data Science.
• Self-starter, resourceful, team-oriented, and compassionate about cooperating in dynamic teams and changing environments is a must.

What will set you apart:
• 3-5 years of experience with hands on experience in automating Data Science models
