13505,1030,Data Scientist II,EDWARD JONES,"Lenox, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.

Opportunity overview:

Come join us in Firm Analytics, where we strive to unleash the full potential of data and analytics to address business challenges. As a Data Scientist on our team, you will design, develop and deliver data science solutions requiring advanced mathematical methods, statistical and machine learning models, data-driven strategies and deliver business outcomes. You will combine data from multiple sources to develop innovative solutions to business problems and collaborate with other data scientists to develop tailored analytic solutions that inform and influence business decisions across the firm.
What you'll do:
• Use statistical modeling, machine learning and numerical optimization to discover and explain patterns in data
• Define data needs and evaluate data quality for applicability to posed problems
• Create features and develop models beyond standard toolset libraries to meet unique business challenges
• Independently and proactively interpret and communicate findings and insights from the data to business partners
• Execute projects from design through implementation and final delivery to internal business partners

Position Qualifications:
• Master of Science Degree in Statistics, Applied Mathematics, Industrial Engineering, Computer Science or related field required. PhD degree desired.
• 5+ years professional experience with predictive statistical models or numerical optimization, and working with typical data used in such analyses
• Experience with one or more programming languages (Python, R, Scala)
• Ability to derive insights or novel ideas from data and mathematical models using a hypothesis driven framework. Connect insights to desired research or business outcomes.
• Demonstrated ability and interest in learning new algorithms and tools, including optimization, natural language processing and graph analysis.
Persons requiring sponsorship for an employment visa are ineligible for this position
