14034,1559,Data Analyst - Consultant,Origin,Anywhere,"Description:

Origin Teams with Modernizing Utilities to Deploy and Operate Key Business Systems. Origin offers software, services, and managed solutions that suit the modernizing utility; is steadfast in delivering the kind of trusted collaboration that utilities need; and is proven in navigating industry change smoothly and efficiently...

Origin is partnering with Infor, makers of the Infor Public Service (IPS) and Infor LN (ERP) software solutions. We have an incredible opportunity to help consolidate and modernize the Customer Information, Meter Data Management, Billing, and Payment systems, as well as ERP and Asset Management systems, for all the Water Councils across New Zealand. This job opportunity is contingent on closing that deal. The project is anticipated to last 2 years with a high potential for post-implementation support services. Most roles will be offered as a contract for a duration to complete the overall project, plus any service extensions, as needed. Training will be provided in the software systems being implemented.

As a Data Analyst - Consultant, you will
• Manage data mapping, conversion, and load, using ETL, to the WSL template model.
• Provide advisory services around data transformation and cleansing requirements to meet template structure
• Provide advice on system processes, changes, and improvements to align with the WSL model
• Work with the solution architect and offshore Infor teams to coordinate configuration enhancements to meet local variations
• Provide on-call ad-hoc services throughout the engagement phase of the program.

This role is to be located in Auckland, New Zealand for the duration of the project. When the project is complete, for those candidates hired on as full time employees, work can be done fully remote.

Requirements:

Our Ideal Candidate Brings the following to the table:
• Bachelor’s (4-year College/University) Degree in a Business or Technology discipline
• 4+ years progressive IT Software implementation experience, primarily in roles as Data Analyst, Data Consultant, Data Engineer, or Business Analyst.
• Strong technical skills in Data Mapping, ETL and various data conversion technologies
• Experience supporting successful large-scale projects and programs across an enterprise utilizing external providers, offshore resources, and internal staff.
• Excellent interpersonal and communication skills
• Experience and understanding of the Utilities sector or related IT systems for businesses such as telecom, banking, or healthcare.
• Understanding of the Meter-to-Cash business processes, customer information systems, ERP systems and Asset Management systems used in these sectors is a plus
• Experience specifically with the Infor IPS and LN platforms is a plus. Training will be provided in the software systems being implemented.

Additionally, it is especially helpful if you have specialized knowledge in one or more of the following:
• Utility billing (meter to cash), Water meter management, or related public sector business processes and customer management
• Standard financials processes including Procurement, General Ledger, and Inventory, especially as they relate to the implementation of an ERP system.
• Enterprise Asset Management systems for Linear assets, management of utility assets, and asset financials (valuations, capitalization).

Training will be provided in the software systems being implemented.

This role is to be located in Auckland, New Zealand for the duration of the project",2022-08-24,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
