14040,1565,Jr. Data Analyst,ASG,Anywhere,"Description:

Company Description...

ASG is a Minority Woman Owned, Physician owned small business with over 10 years' experience in federal government contracting. ASG offers data collection, statistical analysis, health program evaluation, technical and health program implementation support. ASG provides a broad range of healthcare technology related services such as software development and integration, mobile apps, AI/ML, Analytics, Data Science, Bigdata, DevSecOps, Digital transformation, cloud, and cybersecurity. ASG is CMMI Level 3 certified for Development and Services, and holds ISO certifications 9001:2015, 20000-1:2011, and 27000:2015.

Job Description:

ASG is seeking a motivated Jr. Data Analyst with good organizational and communications skills with experience in data analytics and written communications to join an exciting program in support of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Health Insurance Marketplace. This program assists agents and brokers who in turn guide Americans and small businesses in determining the most appropriate health insurance products and services for their needs. The success of the program depends upon rigorous planning and analysis, business-driven technical support, a customer-focused help desk, and robust training for agents, brokers, and vendors. The Junior Data Analyst will have the ability to make a strong positive impact on a program in support CMS’s mission.

The Jr. Data Analyst will have the opportunity to utilize their analytics, communications, reporting, problem-solving and relationship-building skillsets across a variety of tasks on this contract for the Agent and Broker supporting the following functional areas:
• Web-based marketplace consumer assistance request system
• Agent and broker registry
• Data analytics
• System monitoring
• Agent and broker training vendor support
• Development and revision of guidance documents and standard operating procedures
• Technical Escalations
• Monthly Sprint Development
• Help On demand
• Agent Broker Help Desk
• Program Management

What You Will Do:

A typical M-F 8:30Am-5:30PM workday may include the following types of responsibilities:
• Provide support across multiple tasks within the Agent and Broker contract to collect and analyze data for the purposes of creating reports and documents (these can be in the form of email summaries, creating visuals such as graphs, tables, and charts, assisting with the Annual Open Enrollment Period and Special Enrollment Period reports, drafting memos, developing PowerPoint decks, Tableau dashboards, and other documents or forms deemed appropriate by CMS) that can be used by CMS to illustrate agent and broker registration, enrollment, compliance trends and other activities.
• Utilize agent, broker, and web-broker data to develop program metrics, strategies, and solutions.
• Collaborate with internal team and CMS to continue to identify new areas of interest for analytics and enhance visibility into agent broker performance and performance drivers.
• Support the creation of Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Ad-hoc dashboards to highlight enrollment and registration metrics.
• Support the creation of Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Ad-hoc workbooks, to support system monitoring.
• Revise Standard Operating Procedures as processes are updated.
• Review/Update Escalations Responses, Knowledge Base Articles and Resources that are shared with Agent Broker community.
• Memorialize key take-aways, decisions, action-items in client meetings in minutes, as requested.
• Propose and scope new data analytics use cases based on availability of data sources, including, but not limited to AB survey data, MIDAS, MLMS, and NIPR data, and validate applicability and utility with CMS.
• Support CMS with ad hoc requests, analysis, results, and key takeaways, including:

- Pulling enrollment history, registration, licensure, and contact information for agents and brokers

- Support business requirements, documentation, and development for new capabilities
• Provide assistance across multiple tasks within the Agent and Broker contract based on Marketplace Agent and Broker Program annual activities including Help Desk surge periods, Open Enrollment, Special Enrollment, Marketplace Learning Management System Go Dark and Go Live periods, and others as necessary.
• Work with Microsoft Access Database and analyzing and resolving technical issues using SQL-VBA, as needed.
• Run ingests to be able to provide updated information to CMS, as needed.
• Test and verify that deliverables meet CMS’s established requirements, as needed.
• Other tasks as assigned by your manager.

Requirements:

What We Need:
• Bachelor’s Degree and 2 or more years of experience.
• Ability to create, update intermediate to advanced SQL and VBA Queries as needed.
• Experience with complex MS Access concepts to meet client requirements and build advanced visualizations (Table Calculations etc. in multiple formats. Example, SQL, VBA, Excel, CVS).
• Strong written and verbal communications skills.
• Ability to interpret data trends and to summarize that information into plain language.
• Ability to thrive in a work environment that requires strong independent problem-solving skills, self- direction, and innovative thinking.
• Possession of agile mindset and the willingness to perform in a cross-functional team.
• Ability to foster collaboration both inside and outside the team, evangelize and promote inclusive experiences within the company, and juggle several projects with high quality.
• Flexibility to work occasional nights and weekends to meet client deadlines.

Even Better:
• Experience with Tableau design, development, and deployment and/or Tableau Server administration.
