14062,1587,Master Data Analyst,Lozier,United States,"Lozier Corporation is an industry leader in providing store fixtures to major retailers across the U.S. and around the world. Headquartered in Omaha, Nebraska, Lozier began manufacturing fixtures in 1956, and originated the basics of today’s shelving systems. Today, Lozier has over 4 million square feet of manufacturing and distribution space across facilities located in five states. We are... committed to quality and service, building our business around integrity and respect, and investing in our people and communities.

We continue to invest in technology and people to ensure we remain competitive in the industry. That means opportunities for you to grow and develop as an employee and individual. Whether you have a clear idea of where you see yourself in your career or not, Lozier has a diverse range of departments with their own challenges and opportunities for growth to explore. You will find a welcoming and team-oriented environment where employees strive to not only help the company succeed but also help each other succeed, too.

POSITION SUMMARY

The Master Data Analyst is responsible for providing ongoing management of data governance processes and operations. This position performs analysis to ensure the completeness and correctness of data to ensure compliance of our data policies within our Oracle system. Responsibilities include working with business subject matter experts to design data mapping, development of Golden Record rules and overall support of our Oracle master data governance processes. The Analyst also partners with the Data Governance Team members and may support multiple data domains.

ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS
• Perform routine data quality analysis to ensure data adheres to data governance rules and policies; provide recommendations when a new rule or enforcement of a rule may be required
• Manage accuracy of golden record for designated data domains
• Create and maintain all Business Process Procedures documentation for master data transactions and data fields
• Partner with business data owners to develop new data policies
• Provides business partners day to day support for MDM applications through monitoring of metrics, reports and documentation of new requirements
• Supports the Data Architect with testing systems to support data rules, policies and guidelines
• Collaborate with data and analytics leaders, technical solution developers and business domain stakeholders, such as data stewards and business analysts
• Produces analytical data and ad hoc reports as directed with good communication skills to translate reporting requests and accurately meet the actual information and deadline needed
• Troubleshoots issues and errors detected in business processes and/or systems caused by master data issues
• Partner with data owners to improve and streamline processes regarding data flow, data quality, data accuracy and value
• Determine the meaning of data and explain how various teams and leaders can leverage it to improve and streamline their processes
• Demonstrate regular attendance and timeliness in reporting to work, meetings, and completing assignments.
• Ability to work and interact well with others.

JOB QUALIFICATIONS

Education:
• Bachelor degree with an emphasis in Computer Science/Business Analytics//Finance/Accounting or equivalent work experience

Experience:
• Minimum of 2 years experience managing master data in an ERP system if degreed
• Or 5 years master data management experience in an ERP system if non-degreed
• Knowledge of relational databases and reporting tools

Required Skills:
• Experience in defining Master Data Management strategies using MDM services and capabilities, Metadata Management, Data Governance, and Data Quality solutions.
• Expert knowledge and proficiency with Microsoft Office programs (Excel, Word, Outlook, and Access)
• Experience with enterprise level data analysis and integration work and/or providing data focused systems integration solutions
• Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills to facilitate clear communication of information, ideas, procedures, and processes in a logical sequence, at an appropriate level to the audience
• Ability to adapt quickly to new technologies and changing business requirements
• Solid problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and critical thinking abilities
• Must be able to organize with the ability to prioritize work and keep accurate and detailed records
• Must have excellent time management skills with the ability to use independent judgment effectively
• Experience in requirements definition, mapping and gap analysis
