14144,1669,Workforce Management Analyst - Data Analyst,Wollborg Michelson Recruiting,Anywhere,"Workforce Management Analyst - Intraday Analyst - Data Analyst
• Fully Remote
• Must be Covid 19 Vaccinated...
• If not near an office, must have your own Windows Based Equipment, High-Speed Internet, and a Quiet Space to work
• $23/hour
• Shifts Available:

- 6AM-3PM EST
- 8AM-5PM EST
- 2PM-11PM EST

The Intraday Analyst is a key player supporting the Intraday Management practice within the Workforce Management (WFM) Organization. This position will be responsible for assessing and improving contact and agent real-time performance metrics, net staffing levels, rerouting strategies, intraday reporting, and root cause analysis for various business lines within Enterprise Operations. The Intraday Analyst also participates cross-functionally with Performance Analytics, Forecasting, and Scheduling practices within the WFM Organization.

How you will make an impact:
• Responsible for the intraday management function end-to-end, including but not limited to queue threshold monitoring, daily net staffing outlooks, root-cause analysis, agent adherence/conformance monitoring, unplanned attendance process, schedule exception process, and applicable reporting for WFM-supported business lines.
• Monitor services levels, contacts in queue, abandonment rates, etc. for all WFM-supported queues and follow the KPI threshold model for contacts and agents, including driving corresponding actions to address variances.
• Perform the attendance call-out process, handle schedule exceptions, and execute permissible schedule changes as needed to reduce agent overtime and follow the excess capacity strategy for overstaffed timeframes for Operations and WFM.
• Utilize intraday performance (IDP) reports to provide proactive communications regarding attendance, net staffing, cautionary periods, excess capacity, and scheduled offline events coupled with relevant action plans daily.
• Execute intraday applicable Automatic Call Distributor (ACD) routing strategies and changes within routing profiles.
• Collaborate with the WFM Forecasting and Scheduling Analysts regarding new volume and staffing trends that could impact future forecasts; partner with the WFM Sr. Performance Analyst to identify agent and volume behaviors for intraday management strategies.
• Supply inputs by collecting, analyzing, and summarizing information, data, and trends for the WFM Efficiency Model tracking and convert recommendations into cost savings and monthly and quarterly business reviews.
• Execute continuous optimization and improvement aligned with industry best practices for the WFM Intraday Management practice.
• Maintain relationships with stakeholders by meeting and educating them on the nuances of Intraday Management to foster credibility and partnership.
• Perform other duties as requested or assigned.

What we look for:
• 2+ years of relevant experience w/Bachelors degree.
• 2+ years of relevant Contact Center experience; 1+ years in Intraday or Real Time Analyst (RTA) role within Workforce Management; Experience with Workforce Management systems (e.g., Aspect eWFM, Genesis, NICE IEX, etc.) and Contact Center functionality, reporting, and analytics.
• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.
• Highly collaborative and solution-focused.
• Proficient with Microsoft Office applications.
• Professional approach, good judgment, creative problem-solver.
• Strong problem-solving, critical thinking and analytical skills.
• Ability to maintain confidentiality in a variety of matters.
• Time management skills with an ability to multi-task and to manage priorities and workflow.
• Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records, files, and reports.

