14383,1908,Data Analyst,Healthcare Training Leader,Anywhere,"Fast-growing entrepreneurial online training company needs to add an experienced Data Analyst to its team. Your primary focus will be email deliverability in the healthcare industry by preventing and resolving deliverability challenges with the company’s high volume email campaigns. This is a perfect opportunity for someone who loves maintaining, analyzing, auditing, and interpreting data on the... technical side of an email marketing environment.

You will identify opportunities for optimizing overall email pipeline health, contact flow, domain reputation, email deliverability, and engagement. Your goal will be to transform data from multiple sources into actionable insights that promote organizational growth, and informed decision-making at all levels.

Key Responsibilities include:
• Analyze data from our email and digital marketing pipelines to identify opportunities for optimizing overall pipeline health, pipeline flow, domain reputation, email deliverability, engagement, and conversion, while mitigating risk.
• Generate intuitive reports for executive leadership and non-technical team members that effectively communicate trends, patterns, and predictions using relevant data extracted from multiple repositories and platforms.
• Audit data stored and accessed by disparate platforms including internal databases, Email Service Providers (ESP’s), CRM systems, website CMS, Power BI, and Excel spreadsheets.
• Design, manage, and optimize complex queries and stored procedures using efficient code to support new and existing reporting requirements with a high degree of accuracy. Assist with data management by developing workflows, automations, and ETL procedures. Assist with the migration of data from legacy systems to new solutions.
• Work with leading ISPs, email blacklist operators and antispam providers to resolve deliverability issues.
• Track and report on overall email deliverability metrics and take appropriate action on emerging issues.

Requirements:
• Expert level proficiency with MS SQL Server (5+ years), including SSMS, SSRS, and SSIS.
• Ability to write complex queries, stored procedures, and ETL processes for reporting, auditing, and cleansing. Ability to find and correct data errors by interacting directly with relational databases and third-party data sources.
• Expert level proficiency with MS Excel and the ability to create complex pivot tables, charts, and formulas with large underlying datasets.
• Ability to derive business intelligence from complex datasets and provide comprehensive actionable insights, enabling management to readily draw conclusions and make well informed business decisions.
• Values data integrity and has exceptional attention to detail such that inconsistencies are identified, prioritized, and addressed early on. Compelled to notice and act upon erratic data and illogical/inefficient processes.
• Ability to anticipate end-user needs, and consistently produce relevant, useful end user experiences.
• Strong problem solving and critical thinking skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with all levels of the organization. Ability to be readily understood by non-technical team members by expressing technical issues in common terms and vice-versa.
• Familiarity with MySQL, Dynamics CRM, Visual Studio, C#, REST API’s, and DAX programming is a plus.

Healthcare Training Leader Values:

Healthcare Training Leader is a small, customer-centric and entrepreneurial minded team producing the most current, relevant and actionable content focused on solutions for small practices within the healthcare industry.

The culture at Healthcare Training Leader is built on our shared core values – People First, Own It, Tenacious Optimism, and Results. It is important that we all hold each other accountable to these values with every decision we make. These values should demonstrate who we are, not who we hope to be. They are defined as follows:

PEOPLE FIRST: Every decision we make should have some level of positive impact on our customers and/or team. We work hard and strive for balance between our lives in and out of the company.

OWN IT: When things are good, we celebrate. When mistakes are made, we stand up and are accountable for them, we work together to ferret out the issue and tackle it head on. We never hide from the truth.

TENACIOUS OPTIMISM: We do the best we can every time, and when that isn’t enough, we work harder & never give up on a project or mission if we believe in it. However, this doesn’t mean we wear blinders

RESULTS: The outcomes we achieve allow us to grow, identify opportunities, help our customers, and ensure a strong, supportive where we want to be.

We hire, fire, review, reward, and recognize our teammates based on these characteristics, so it’s essential that you share these values in order to be part of our team. We work hard to live and breathe these values, so if you don’t embody them, it will seriously stand out. Better to know now.

