KVLR Capital is a healthcare-focused investment and advisory firm, headquartered in New York City. Our firm's mission is to execute partnership structures with physicians and healthcare groups nationwide that complement our goal to maximize positive impact. With a strict acquisition criteria, data analytics, and a robust M&A team - our foundation offers options for operational optimization throughout the healthcare ecosystem. KVLR has a proven ability to create value through nonclinical management, serving as an Management Services Organization (MSO) and capital partner with a long-term approach across most medical specialties and verticals.

KVLR prioritizes creating enduring market value for the benefit of the healthcare ecosystem including patients, providers, private HC companies, staff, and investing partners. We firmly believe in the transformative power of subdividing the clinical responsibilities within operations of a company from the financial responsibilities to drive growth and efficiency.

Upon applying, you will automatically receive a link to an online phone assessment to be considered for the position. You must complete it within 48 hours.

The Data Analyst Internship Program provides access for students to gain further experience in the utilization of Python, SQL, C++, and other common languages. During this 3-month program, you will engage in assignments evolving data mining, building automations, and discovering sources of information valuable to private equity healthcare, sourcing prospective industry opportunities, and delivering value around the rapidly changing healthcare sector. Interns will be part of roundtable discussions, participate in case study monthly learning sessions, and given the opportunity to suggest their own work for projects that involve their full creative control. At then end of the program, an individualized performance feedback overview will be provided and a meeting scheduled for discussion. This internship will best fit a candidate who has an entrepreneur spirit and is self-motivated to enhance their knowledge with the goal to achieve a greater understanding of healthcare-related data work and the general process of investment decisions made by private equity firms, specifically by KVLR Capital.

