Responsibilities
• Develop, maintain, and troubleshoot complex scripts and reports developed using SQL, Microsoft Excel, PowerBI, or other analytics tools
• Interpret and analyze data from multiple sources including electronic health records and third-party vendors. Identify and assess the current performance and historical trends in care delivery and patient outcomes
• To develop and update dynamic dashboards within PowerBI, leveraging various data sources (including Azure Data Lake) to visualize data insights for Ivy operators to manage performance and drive functional change within the organization
• Update and evolve weekly Key Performance Indicator (KPI) reports and integrate into the PowerBI platform
• Identify data irregularities, perform quality assurance checks, and present findings and proposed solutions to leadership
• Apply experience with statistical analysis and modeling to gain key insights into drivers of improved care delivery and patient outcomes
• Contribute to the planning and execution of large-scale projects with limited direction from leadership
