• Partner cross-functionally at all levels of the organization and effectively, both verbally and visually, communicate findings and insights to non-technical business partners
• Assist the Director of Clinical Outcomes & Research in preparing business proposals and monthly performance reports for senior leadership and key business stakeholders.
• Collaborate with key internal stakeholders and external 3rd party vendors (data engineers and developer teams) to create, implement, and manage databases, reporting dashboards, and data collection systems
• Enhance capabilities of various data systems and manage organization-wide user accessibility

Ivy Incentives
• Competitive pay and bonus incentives
• Premium benefits package, including 401(k) match, medical, dental, vision and PTO
• Industry-leading professional development
• Accelerated career growth and advancement
• Community outreach and service initiatives

Regardless of position, whether you are an enthusiastic clinician, dedicated support staff, or an accomplished business leader, we all come together to be One Ivy!
Ivy is a Leading Provider of Outpatient Rehabilitation
Ivy Rehab is an extraordinary network of 450+ best-in-class outpatient physical, occupational, speech and ABA therapy clinics in the Northeast (CT, NJ, NY, PA, DE), the Midwest (IL, IN, MI), and the Southeast (NC, SC, VA). With over 4,300 teammates and growing rapidly, our network consists of multiple brands in 14 states. Clinics within our network are dedicated to providing exceptional care and personalized treatment to 7,500+ patients - both adults and children - every day.
“It’s All About The People” at Ivy —our teammates, our patients, our referral sources, and the communities in which we operate.
