15073,544,Solve linear programming problems (data analytics),Upwork,Anywhere,"Few tips for calculation for Linear Programming Problem : Fabric Mill Scheduling

Obj Function: 13 Decision Variables for both Maximum and Minimum (For each 5 fabric purchased and produced by Draw (5) and Regular (3...

For Maximum – find the profit for each fabric by using Selling price and Variable cost (8 variables), Also, similar by using Selling price and Purchase price (5 variables)

For Minimum – Use cost of purchase (5 variable) and variable cost (8 variable) for each fabric Constraints - Total 7 constraints

There are 5 Demand Constraints

2 constraints for hrs each Draw loom and Regular loom Calculate total hrs available for RHS for both looms Calculate time (hr) for each fabric by dividing 1 by loom rate for both looms, please use 3 d.p. at least for more accuracy.

Solve using either Excel or The Management Scientist and answer questions by using the output for Profit and sensitivity analysis to complete the management report by answering questions and making changes with additional Draw loom etc.

