15160,631,Shiny App/NLP expert,Upwork,Anywhere,"Hi! Here is some information about the project. My son really loves sports, especially college basketball and he wanted to make an interactive shiny app to spread awareness about gender bias in the college basketball landscape. He was inspired by a project that looked at the way that white vs black players were being described and it was found that white players were often praised for their... high-IQs, “sneaky athleticism”, good work ethics and smarts while black players were often praised for their physical attributes, strong bodies, dominance, aggression, etc.

He wanted to conduct a similar study but look at women vs men and see if there were any biases in articles describing the players. The premise of his shiny app would be to analyze the ways that women basketball players and men basketball players are being described from ESPN articles.

So far, he has web-scraped all of the players from all of the 363 collegiate teams in both the men's and women's leagues, their stats from the 2021-22 season and the articles that are written for each of the teams and has them stored in data files. So, he has done all the web-scraping needed for this project already. He now just needs help with the NLP and text analytics coding required to find the biases in sports journalism. One thing that he really wants to do is to use the player's names as keywords and then use a keyword extractor to find the sentiment scores of adjectives around the keywords (this is pretty complex and thus he needs help with this).

