15429,900,"Freelance Data Analyst – Short Term Project due January 5, 2023",Upwork,Anywhere,"ABOUT GOBEL GROUP

GOBEL is the leading consulting firm working exclusively in healthcare philanthropy. We are internationally recognized for our best-in-class grateful patient and family philanthropy program with active clinician engagement and we also offer counsel and assistance for every step of the development process, including proven and comprehensive solutions for campaign planning and... management, data analytics, systems and information services, development audits, hospital and system philanthropy office integrations, and ongoing counsel.

Over 11 years, GOBEL has had the privilege of working with 550 hospitals and health systems. Our growing team includes 45 employees who are seasoned healthcare development professionals and clinicians from the top medical centers in the nation. Collectively, our consultants bring 500 years of healthcare philanthropy experience to our client engagements, having led billion-dollar campaigns, and raised hundreds of millions annually.

More information on the Gobel Group can be found on our website at www.gobelgroup.com.

ABOUT THE PROJECT

GOBEL is looking for a detail-oriented, organized, and experienced Data Analyst to work on a short-term project, estimated to be around 20-30 hours and is due by January 5, 2023. A team meeting will be scheduled to ensure that the individual is given the specific deliverables of the project and internally, who they will work with.

The Data Analyst will work with both fundraising data that has been exported from a philanthropy CRM and patient data sets that has been received to identify past trends in various donation ranges and then project future philanthropic donations in each of the donation ranges.

Our ideal candidate is a go-getter, has a strong team-oriented working style, and enjoys working with colleagues and clients to ensure clients have a superior experience. The candidate enjoys both collaboration with a team as well as a strong commitment to work independently to meet objectives.

•Meet with key stakeholders to clarify project requirements and create a written plan of action.

• Take large, complex sets of data to analyze and identify past philanthropic trends.

