16371,1842,How much predictors add on the outcome,Upwork,Anywhere,"Hi Ahmad,

I have attached a snippet of my data and hope you be able to get an idea of all of the data and I can send the full dataset to you. This analysis will be in SAS...

Here is the detail of the data.

sub_id = subjects, measurement is taken on subject at different time point.

position: where measurement is taken (anterior or posterior)

time_in_seconds: time to apply treatment

resistant:

force: force of treatment application

The y variable is whether there is a block after treatment has been applied i.e. y =1 or there is a gap y= 0

The main question to address is how much these predictors add on the outcome?

1)At first step just use all the data set without considering the position (ant or post) (one unique dataset).

2)then re-run the same analysis by dividing the dataset in Post=Posterior and Ant=Anterior segments (two datasets)

3)Then the interpretations.

