17177,2648,Operations Analyst in maritime Industry,Upwork,Anywhere,"ABOUT eeSea

eeSea is a global container shipping data solutions provider that offers industry stakeholders a full suite of tools via web-app, Tableau, and API. Our services and user approach are modular; we host an extensive relational database of interconnected and simultaneously robust stand-alone products...

JOB DESCRIPTION

The team of operations analysts is responsible for researching information about the industry, organizing it, and uploading it to our database. You will learn how to contribute through a variety of tasks including but not limited to online research, use of eeSea’s business intelligence tools, data verification through multiple public sources, and the process of structuring historical and forward-facing vessel movement data. The information is eventually the product that we market towards our customers, so high-quality work is required.

Examples of tasks you will be mastering are:

- Web research on container carrier and port & terminal websites, from news sites and other relevant sources of industry information

- Understand and verify the information collected – the human element. You will come to understand the industry from the top down, and gain valuable business insights and methods in the process

- Structure the data and insert it into our database, ensuring quality input and output

SKILLS

As a person you:

- Are proactive, self-driven, and eager to learn.

- Take ownership over tasks assigned to you; drive them to completion on time and with an assurance of quality.

- Are structured and able to keep up with multiple tasks and timelines.

- Communicate effectively in English; are able to learn to understand and utilize technical terminology used by the rest of the team.

- Are committed to the work and experience for a long period of time; you are not just looking for a short-term project.

- Enjoy working closely with a team of international peers.

- Have your own computer, access to a reliable internet connection, and enough bandwidth to participate in regular Zoom/Microsoft Teams/Google Meet meetings with team members.

- (Not required but a plus) are familiar with Tableau.

- (Not required but a plus) have previous work experience in the transport & logistics industry or in a reputable data-oriented company.

WHAT'S IN IT FOR YOU?

- The benefit of building new paradigms for data-oriented visibility in an exciting industry with massive growth opportunities.

- Having clear insights into the results of your hard work; you get end-to-end visibility on the development of our products and client relationships.

- The excitement of working in a start-up with a team of close peers. We are not a large company and don't have a rigid corporate structure - beyond making time for necessary peer communications, you are free to work on your own schedule as long as the work gets done!

- The opportunity to gain a valuable knowledge base through the support and training of your peers; you bring the motivation and discipline and we will equip you with the tools you need to succeed.

- Starting in a junior position with the opportunity to shape the processes and growth of eeSea. If you perform exceptionally and are motivated to grow alongside our company, we are happy to grant you greater roles & responsibilities.

