Employment Type: Part Time
...
The Brink’s name is a promise to respect the trust we’ve earned in over 150 years in business. Every employee honors that promise by offering the highest levels of service and support to our customers. We take pride in our work, and we share a passion about our future. Learn why so many people have made the choice to join our team – and stay here.

Job Title

Data Analyst Intern

Job Description

Are you passionate about ensuring end users are delivered the highest quality product possible? Do you thrive in an environment that is fast-paced and do whatever it takes to deliver a quality product?We do!The Data Analytics Intern will be responsible for supporting customer operations, creating reports, troubleshooting data issues, and ad hoc projects.

What we are looking for this role to do:

Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

·Create daily, weekly and monthly reports*

·Communicate with third parties on a daily basis*

·Implement processes to identify, analyze, and interpret trends or patterns in complex data sets*

·Retrieve data from various reporting systems and use tools to generate recommendations

·Research discrepancies and identify root cause of errors

·Place orders with banking partners

·Make recommendations for process improvement opportunities and recommend system improvements by studying current practices

What you need to bring to the table:

·Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy

·Organizational skills, attention to detail and accuracy

·Proficiency with Microsoft Office programs, especially Excel and Outlook skills. Experience with common data analytics tools (R, Tableau, Python,SAS, Spark,etc.) and/or database software is a bonus

·Ability to identify and communicate discrepancies in information

·Good interpersonal, communication and customer service skills

·Excellent written and verbal communication skills

·Willingness and ability to make phone calls to banks to provide them with required data

·Ability to effectively prepare materials andcommunicate your insights

·Must be available most mornings (7-10 am) and for 1 hour most afternoons (between and 3-5 pm)

About Brink’s

Brink’s is the global leader in security and logistics services, trusted by banks, financial institutions and businesses in both public and private sectors. We deliver the currency of the world to businesses in our communities. We do it because we’re needed. We do it because we’re trusted and valued. We do it because it makes us proud. Brink’s Proud.

What’s Next?

Thank you for considering applying for a job at Brink’s U.S. To be considered for this position, you must complete the entire application process, which includes answering all prescreening questions and providing your eSignature.

Upon completion of the application process, you will receive an email confirming that we have received your application. We will review all candidates and notify you of your status should we deem you fit for a job. Thank you again for your interest in a career at Brink’s U.S. For more information about future career opportunities, join our talent network, Like our Facebook page or Follow us on Twitter.

Brink’s is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, marital status, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information or history or any other characteristic protected by law. Brink’s is also committed to providing a drug free workplace.

We are an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, sex, age, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, status as a veteran, and basis of disability or any other federal, state or local protected class",2022-11-05,Part-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'python', 'outlook', 'spark', 'sas', 'excel', 'r']"
