18065,3536,Research Data Analyst 3,Oregon Health & Science University,United States,"Department Overview

This position exists within the Pacific Northwest Evidence-based Practice Center (EPC), a research program of the Department of Medical Informatics & Clinical Epidemiology (DMICE), OHSU School of Medicine. The Pacific Northwest EPC is a collaboration of OHSU, the University of Washington, and Aggregate Analytics, Inc. Designated by the Agency for Healthcare Research and... Quality (AHRQ) as one of nine Evidence-based Practice Centers, the Pacific Northwest EPC conducts systematic evidence reviews for the AHRQ Effective Health Care Program and the U.S. Preventive Services Task Force, the Brain Trauma Foundation, other foundations, professional associations, and other state and federal government agencies. As a part of producing systematic evidence reviews, the EPC completes comparative effectiveness reviews, meta-analyses, technology assessments, and clinical guideline development.

This position currently allows for telework. Telework is subject to change based on the needs of the organization.
Function/Duties of Position

This position applies standard systematic review methods, drafts portions of evidence reports and manuscripts, engages stakeholders and experts; performs basic meta-analyses; collaborates with EPC investigators, project managers, and staff in planning evidence reviews; contributes to stakeholder and expert reviewer engagement processes; and when applicable, manages, trains, and mentors students and junior staff. This position does not manage staff or projects; however, the position independently provides high level assistance to PIs in conducting reviews.
Required Qualifications

Education and Experience:
• PhD in relevant field
• OR Master's Degree in relevant field AND 4 years of relevant experience
• OR Bachelor's Degree in relevant field AND 6 years of relevant experience
• OR Equivalent combination of training and experience

Job Related Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (Competencies):
• Knowledge of clinical research methods, study design, and basic biostatistics.
• Exceptional organizational skills and ability to manage research teams.
• Excellent communications skills, including verbal, written, interpersonal, and email.
• Ability to work independently and as a contributing member of multidisciplinary teams.
• Able to attend to detail, work with a high degree of accuracy, and perform well under deadlines.
• Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint).
Preferred Qualifications
• Statistical and research coursework.
• Experience in systematic reviews or comparative effectiveness research.
• Experience in appraising medical literature.
• Knowledge of:
• epidemiology
• biostatistics
• study design
• systematic review methods
• reference management and systematic review software (e.g., EndNote)
• statistical and data visualization software and methods

All are welcomeOregon Health & Science University values a diverse and culturally competent workforce. We are proud of our commitment to being an equal opportunity, affirmative action organization that does not discriminate against applicants on the basis of any protected class status, including disability status and protected veteran status. Individuals with diverse backgrounds and those who promote diversity and a culture of inclusion are encouraged to apply. To request reasonable accommodation contact the Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Department at 503-494-5148 or aaeo@ohsu.edu. As an organization devoted to the health and well-being of people in Oregon and beyond, OHSU requires its employees to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19",2022-02-08,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['powerpoint', 'excel', 'word']"
18077,3548,Data Analyst,KellyMitchell,Missouri,"Data Analyst

4 City Place, Missouri | Business Intelligence & Data Management...
Job ID: 122900
Listed on 12/6/2022
Job Summary: We are seeking a highly motivated and agile Data Analyst to join our team and help lead our efforts in making our data pipeline process more efficient and robust. You will work collaboratively with our Alpha and Protocol Management teams to create new, automated ways to streamline the search, quality check and ingestion of field trial data into our pipeline. The goal is to drive efficiency in processing, analyzing and deliver quality agronomic data to our modeling teams that is developing novel & integrated agronomic models for sustainable recommendations on seeds, agronomic traits, and crop protection solutions for farmers.

Duties:
• Partner with Data Engineers to implement and maintain processes to search for and identify instances where designed field trials are missing data and/or contain data anomalies that inhibit our ability to properly process the field
• Ensure alignment of correct crop/year in FieldView and our database
• Ensure alignment of the correct boundary/UUID in FieldView and our database
• Coordinate with Research Data Engineering, the Engineering department, and Protocols team with submitting requests, tracking status and with resolution of tickets when issues emerge
• Partner with domain experts to collaborate in the development and maintenance of a trial monitoring tool
• Make sure the data flow between the Alpha/Protocol Management and Operational Effectiveness teams is consistent and of an acceptable quality to enable faster turnaround for our data deliverables
• Learn and leverage existing tools or infrastructure developed by Data Analytics, Engineering and Product teams to support our data pipeline needs
• Serve on the Protocol Review Committee with responsibility for ensuring that protocols are well-designed from an implementation perspective and requirements are properly translated to the Science Data Pipeline team

Desired Skills/Experience:
• Bachelor’s degree in a STEM discipline (preferably in data science, statistics, computer science, physical sciences or agricultural sciences)
• 2+ years of experience working with data management, QA/QC processes and/or automation/coding
• Basic coding skills developing new solutions and visualizations
• Decent skills working with Microsoft Excel
• Understanding of agricultural, environmental data, and/or geospatial data concepts
• Experience with oral presentation and technical writing
• Eager to learn new topics, develop new skills and use new tools
• Coding experience with Python (preferred)
• Experience working with geospatial data (preferred)
• Experience working with agricultural and/or environmental data (preferred)
