18085,3556,Business Data Analyst,Randstad USA,"Kansas City, MO","job summary:

Randstad Technologies is seeking an experienced Business Data Analyst for a remote opportunity. The Business Data Analyst is responsible for the implementation and support of business information systems across multiple departments. They collaborate with Product Owners and business leaders to manage team backlogs and help define and deliver strategic visions. They affect change by... helping leaders articulate business needs to facilitate working sessions with architects in creating transformational solutions. They operate in a solution-oriented environment and are encouraged to identify process improvement opportunities to drive systemic change in the organization.

Requirements:
• 6 years of experience gathering and creating software development requirement documents
• 3+ years of experience in the healthcare or health insurance industry
• 1+ years of experience working with claims data or facets

location: KANSAS CITY, Missouri
job type: Contract
salary: $55 - 60 per hour
work hours: 8am to 4pm
education: Bachelors

responsibilities:
• Create detailed business requirements documents, project charters, and other analysis documentation to facilitate IT project management and IT product and program development teams in understanding, scheduling, and tracking product development projects
• Serve as a liaison between product and program development teams, business stakeholders and product and program owners to determine business need of software products and the technical delivery of business requests
• Lead backlog refinement sessions to manage priority of Operational and Strategic work for the development teams
• Lead sessions with business stakeholders and product owners to define, prioritize, and track annual road maps of product development initiatives
• Engage with business stakeholders and product owners to guide project decisions; assess the risks of various solutions and facilitate prioritization of competing business needs
• Facilitate User Acceptance Testing (UAT) including, but not limited to: Creating UAT plans, facilitating identification of UAT participants, creation of UAT Issues Document to track identified bugs, priority, and resolution
• Use project and task management software to track software development progress, and monitor production issues
• Manage company-wide communications regarding software enhancements and project statuses
• Conduct research and analysis on healthcare/user data
• Plan and manage multiple assignments of varying scope
• Assist in the research, analysis, problems, and coordination of production software issues
• Serve as Subject Matter Expert on at least one program or product supported by development teams

qualifications:
• Experience level: Experienced
• Minimum 6 years of experience
• Education: Bachelors

skills:
• Business Analysis (6 years of experience is required)
• SQL (4 years of experience is required)
• Healthcare (3 years of experience is required)
• Equal Opportunity Employer: Race, Color, Religion, Sex, Sexual Orientation, Gender Identity, National Origin, Age, Genetic Information, Disability, Protected Veteran Status, or any other legally protected group status.

At Randstad, we welcome people of all abilities and want to ensure that our hiring and interview process meets the needs of all applicants. If you require a reasonable accommodation to make your application or interview experience a great one, please contact HRsupport@randstadusa.com.

Pay offered to a successful candidate will be based on several factors including the candidate's education, work experience, work location, specific job duties, certifications, etc. In addition, Randstad offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health, an incentive and recognition program, and 401K contribution (all benefits are based on eligibility).

For certain assignments, Covid-19 vaccination and/or testing may be required by Randstad's client or applicable federal mandate, subject to approved medical or religious accommodations. Carefully review the job posting for details on vaccine/testing requirements or ask your Randstad representative for more information",2022-02-02,Contractor,data analyst,United States,['sql']
