18154,3625,Communications Data Analyst,Infinity Consulting Solutions,"Pacifica, CA","Our client, a worldwide media & entertainment brand is looking for a Communications Data Analyst who will be an integral part of the External Communications team, working collaboratively to support a broad range of activities and day-to-day operations across all key lines of business. The role will work in tandem with the Manager of Communications to support the reputation through external... communications strategies in support of the organization’s strategic goals. This role will provide critical monitoring support with a focus on escalating media alerts, traditional and social media monitoring and analysis, and marketplace intelligence.

Responsibilities:
• Read, watch, listen, and engage with traditional and social media to stay apprised of and be the first to identify evolutions and trends in the consumer and media landscapes that relate to business priorities - working to anticipate and proactively address any key issues or opportunities that may arise.
• Support business communications efforts tied to competitive insight analysis and marketplace monitoring.
• Manage daily monitoring of traditional and social media, identifying anticipated stories and potential issues and flagging to key stakeholders across the business to drive awareness and deliver actionable qualitative and quantitative insights reports to assist in issues management and crisis response.
• Track performance and sentiment, report on key metrics and insights, and interpret data from multiple sources across communications campaigns
• Develop holistic media recaps that are distributed to key leaders across the business, utilizing tools and research to analyze key coverage, sentiment and engagement analytics to deliver a deeper understanding of the impact our announcements and campaigns are driving.
• Conduct ad hoc research, develop media audits and provide recommendations as necessary tied to storytelling opportunities and key program launches.

Qualifications:
• Prior experience with data analysis and marketplace monitoring, including use of tools such as Crimson Hexagon, Cision, Critical Mention, Muck Rack and NetBase.
• Ability to execute within tight timeframes with relentless attention to detail, accuracy and excellent project management and research skills.
• Demonstrated ability to synthesize complex information and present in a clear, concise, and readable manner with actionable insights.
• Experience with problem solving and coming up with creative solutions.
• Enthusiastic, proactive, eager to learn attitude and are willing to take on new challenges.
• Ability to take direction from multiple stakeholders, balance numerous projects simultaneously and prioritize deadlines
• Effectively work in a fast-paced environment with a can-do attitude, being comfortable with pivoting priorities, adapting to constantly changing news cycles and shifting focus based on business needs.
• Ability to manage confidential information.
• Experience supporting data analytics and monitoring in a communications-related field (preferred, but not required).
• Familiarity with the media landscape, as well as issues management data analysis",2022-02-26,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
18155,3626,Data Analyst II,EDWARD JONES,"Rolla, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.
Firm Analytics partners with business areas to provide analytical and financial insights for firm decision making and strategic planning. We use advanced data manipulation techniques, data visualization and statistical analysis to provide actionable insights to the enterprise.

Key Responsibilities:
• Design and execute measures, KPIs and descriptive analytic analysis by leveraging business acumen and analytic acumen.
• Design and develop technical and functional prototypes to uncover business questions, validate use cases and capture key requirements.
• Query, manipulate and validate data across multiple domains using database technologies and querying languages (SQL, Snowflake etc.)
• Analyze the effectiveness of programs, perform calculations, summarize, and present insights to enhance future efforts using appropriate descriptive statistical methods.
• Conduct meaningful descriptive data analysis to inform business decisions. Primarily by performing root cause, exploratory, sensitivity and scenario analysis, hypothesis testing, economic modeling, and data visualization to identify patterns/trends/insights etc. on ambiguous business problems.
• Create data visualizations that simplify complex information in a robust, accurate, and appealing visual story that engages end users and drives them to action.
• Collaborate with cross-functional teams responsible for implementing projects in support of divisional and firm-wide business objectives; occasionally lead cross-functional teams responsible for divisional objectives while following an analytics development lifecycle.
• Communicate across a wide range of audiences with specialized subject matter expertise including Finance, Compliance, Marketing, Products, Branch Development, and Technology.
• Work with stakeholders throughout the organization to identify opportunities for leveraging data & analytics to drive business outcomes.
• Proactively recommend improvement to processes and controls related to area responsibilities while quantifying the impact of changes for leaders.
• Maintain a good understanding of business objectives, key business drivers, strategies and priorities, to inform an analytic approach to address business questions.
• Strong analytical and critical thinking required.
• 5+ years of experience in data analytics required.
• Undergraduate degree required. Mathematics, Sciences, Engineering, Finance, and Information Systems preferred. Advanced degree is a plus.
• Ability to extract and analyze large amounts of data using at least one data manipulation language required (SQL preferred.)
• Ability to prioritize and execute on multiple tasks as well as adjust to changing priorities with minimal leader oversight required.
• Strong analysis skills, primarily investigating and explaining trends and variances using statistical techniques required.
• Works effectively in both an independent or team environment required
• Ability to effectively communicate with associates and leadership in cross-functional settings using verbal, written and presentation skills required.
• Technical proficiency in the following: SQL, Oracle Database, Tableau–preferred.
• Data manipulation languages such as Snowflake, Hive, Pig, XML a plus.
• Visualization tools such as Power BI, Qlikview, or Birst a plus.
• Statistical tools such as SAS, SPSS, R, Python, or Dataiku, a plus.
• Microsoft Excel – experience using pivot tables, formulas, macros/VBA a plus.
