18220,3691,"Data Analyst, Office of Medicaid Inspector General",The State of Kansas,"Shawnee County, KS","Data Analyst, Office of Medicaid Inspector General Jobs in Shawnee County, KS at The State of Kansas

Title: Data Analyst, Office of Medicaid Inspector General...

Company: The State of Kansas

Location: Shawnee County, KS

Important Recruitment Information for this vacancy:

Job Posting closes: November 30, 2022

Required documents uploaded by: December 2, 2022

Office of the Kansas Attorney General

The Office of the Kansas Attorney General (OAG) is an organization that values individuals who strive to work in a team environment, where a positive attitude and willingness to assist others is critical. We seek to hire individuals who exemplify the highest standards of integrity, efficiency and professionalism. You should be well-organized, self-motivated, and punctual. A high degree of accuracy and attention to detail, strong work ethic and superb team building ethos are required.

You can learn more about our office on our website.

About the Position:

Who can apply: Anyone

Classified/Unclassified Service: Unclassified

Full/Part-time: Full-Time

FLSA: Nonexempt

Location: Topeka (Shawnee County)

Eligible to Receive Benefits: Yes

Veteran Preference Eligible: Yes

Search Keywords: data analysis, system analysis, research, audit, Medicaid

Compensation:

Hourly Salary Range: $22.50-$31.50

Salary can vary depending upon education, experience, or qualifications.

Employment Benefits:

Comprehensive medical, mental, dental, vision, and additional coverage

Sick & Vacation leave

Work-Life Balance programs: parental leave, military leave, jury leave, funeral leave

Paid State Holidays (designated by the Governor annually)

Fitness Centers in select locations

