18225,3696,Sr Data Quality Analyst,Honeywell,"Overland Park, KS","Join the industry leader to design the next generation of breakthroughs

Innovate to solve the world's most important challenges...

Honeywell is a Fortune 100 company that invents and manufactures technologies to address critical challenges linked to global macrotrends such as safety, security, productivity, global urbanization and energy. With approximately 129,000 employees worldwide, including more than 19,000 engineers and scientists, Honeywell has an unrelenting focus on quality, delivery, value, and technology in everything they make and do. Honeywell has been named a Top 100 Global Innovator for seven years in a row, recognizing the company’s global reach of portfolio and invention influence.

In Kansas City, Honeywell Federal Manufacturing & Technologies (FM&T) manages and operates the U.S. Department of Energy/National Nuclear Security Administration’s (NNSA) Kansas City National Security Campus. This state-of-the-art engineering, manufacturing, and sourcing facility produces a wide array of intricate components to deliver trusted national security products and government services primarily for the NNSA. Honeywell FM&T’s culture of integrity, commitment and continuous improvement enables them to deliver responsive, collaborative, and innovative management and technology services and products that translate into cutting edge solutions to complex national security issues.
• **This position will be in Kansas City, MO***

Summary:

The Senior Data Quality Analyst works closely with business teams to develop and drive governance maturity across the organization. This position helps to facilitate data assessment and data quality activities in the governance program and contributes to the development of policies and standards. The Senior data governance analyst works closely with data governance analysts, data stewards, data ambassadors to improve data quality and ensure data is managed effectively.

Duties and responsibilities:
• Lead data governance strategy and policy development within the enterprise
• Develop and maintain a collaborative relationship with data stewards and ambassadors in assigned business units
• Develop and maintain strong understanding of the data landscape in the assigned areas of the enterprise
• Identify, understand and document data usage characteristics to drive alignment of data standards
• Lead development of and changes to data governance policies and strategies
• Chairing and facilitating working sessions with business leaders, stakeholders, and data consumers.
• Tracking, managing, and reporting on data governance initiatives and progress towards team goals and objectives
• Lead the implementation and integration of a new, integrated data model

You Must Have:
• Bachelor's Degree in a Business or Science discipline (e.g., Math, Statistics, Computer Science, Information Science, Engineering or Economics) or 6 years equivalent work experience
• 5+ years’ work experience in data management, data quality or business applications function
• US citizenship to obtain US Dept. of Energy """"Q"""" level security clearance

We Value:
• Hands-on experience in data catalog technologies, Collibra experience is a plus
• Mastery of data quality management
• Deep understanding of information and process integration management
• Policy and standards drafting experience
• Ability to implement change by mentoring and motivating others, driving consensus, and executing through others.
• Experience working in sensitive/classified data environments
• Experience working with a US government contractor
• Strong working knowledge of engineering, manufacturing, program management, and/or financial data operations
• Strong organizational skills: managing several complex initiatives simultaneously in a fast-paced, demanding
• Environment

FMT2021
Additional Information
• JOB ID: req381876
• Category: Information Technology
• Location: 9221 Ward Parkway,Kansas City,Missouri,64114,United States
• Exempt
• Must have or be eligible for a security clearance due to contractual requirements.

Honeywell is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will be considered without regard to age, race, creed, color, national origin, ancestry, marital status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, nationality, sex, religion, or veteran status",2022-09-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
18226,3697,Clinical Nurse Informatics Data Analyst,Swope Health,"Kansas City, MO","Position Summary

The Healthcare Clinical Data Analyst will be uniquely positioned to gather and analyze healthcare data from multiple sources to extract trends and business insights. This role will assess current and future technology needs. Will integrate clinical information process and education to maximize front line staff and providers' efficiency and skills. The incumbent must be an... excellent communicator who's able to tell the story behind raw data to non-technical audiences. This role will adhere to nursing policy, practice and regulatory standards when designing in the current system and will provide assistance and technical guidance to the clinicians in both the medical clinics and the behavioral health settings. This role will function both as a health informatics resource and as a reporting resource.

Primary Functions
• Pull and integrate data from disparate sources
• Build models that capture a wide range of health care operations
• Evaluate and preprocess raw information
• Present and explain information in an accessible way
• Proficient in SQL and analysis tools
• Performs a QA function for the data integration processes and repository metrics
• Collaborates with other staff to document data needs and metric definitions
• Validates data load processes and the quality of the data loaded into clinical data repositories
• Responsible for maintaining, storing, mapping and analyzing medical, lab and any other health data in compliance with HIPAA policies and procedures
• Provides consultative services to customers and application and development teams as to workflow processes and technological solutions
• Knowledge of Extract, Transform and Load frameworks.
• Coordinates the changes in workflow process needing to be made with the system changes, specific to policy and practice standards and following change management protocols.
• Works with members of the clinic staff and IT Department staff to design and develop clinical documentation based on workflow and regulatory standards
• Assists in the testing and implementation of new applications and upgrades
• Works closely with end users in the clinical environment to optimize their use of clinical systems. Develops and coordinates a team of interdisciplinary super-users. Responsible for facilitating communication across the patient care departments
• Provides project leadership and direction. Coordinates meetings and ensures appropriate expertise is applied to projects/tasks; resolves all issues.
• Recommends innovative ideas, processes, and/or procedures for enhancements, additions, and modifications to improve existing systems
• Researches patient data across multiple applications to resolve discrepancies and/or improve work flow
• Utilizes various tools to capture EHR data and compile into reports that are meaningful to end users.
• Facilitates meetings and brings working groups to consensus in relation to the clinical record.
• Provides leadership to team when manager is not available
• Provide technical support, diagnosis of application errors and troubleshooting with system issues.
• Understands testing concepts including different types of testing and their objectives. Develops and executes tests scripts based on future state workflows and software enhancements/fixes. Works with others to create test scenarios (stories) for integration testing incorporating new features and workflows. Directs project team members throughout the testing event.
• Provides onboarding EHR training for providers and staff as needed
• Other duties as assigned within the Health Informatics & Data Analytics Team

Education/Qualifications
• Graduate of an accredited School of Nursing
• Active RN license required
• Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree preferred
• eClinicalWorks certification required within 1 year of hire
• At least 3 years of experience in healthcare required, with at least 2 years of experience in data analytics, data science, or informatics. Certification in Informatics is a plus",2022-01-04,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['sql']
