18228,3699,Senior Data Analyst Manager,Tyson Foods,"Springdale, AR","Job Details:

The Senior Data Analyst position requires knowledge of the biological, physical, and engineering sciences that make possible safe and wholesome food products; of food industry facilities, methods, processes, equipment capabilities and limitations; and of relevant laws, regulations, and governmental oversight. This position is responsible for involvement with the planning... development, implementation, and administration of systems for the acquisition, storage, and retrieval of data within the data-based applications and business systems for the internal/external users of the portfolio of the Product Development Management (PDM) systems used across the Enterprise. The Senior Data Analyst may also have responsibility for designing, developing, and implementing training materials including facilitator guides, participant guides, job aids, and computer-based training/learning options. The Senior Data Analyst operates as an internal consultant to IT project teams to provide analysis and definition of data requirements; development and administration of data standards; policies, and procedures; development and implementation of data mining programs; evaluation and recommendations on new database technologies; and ensuring the rigorous application of information security/information assurance policies, principles, and practices in the delivery of data management services. The Senior Data Analyst performs duties with wide latitude for the exercise of independent judgement to perform responsible work of considerable difficulty requiring somewhat extended professional and technical training and experience which has demonstrated important attainments and marked capacity for independent work. Additionally, the Data Manager needs to have knowledge of, and skill in, applying network principles and concepts; systems administration methods and procedures; customer support principles; IT security principles; troubleshooting methods; and utilize communication methods and techniques in providing guidance to our internal/external customers.

REQUIREMENTS:
• Collaborate with IT staff and other technical staff to ensure that the delivered solution and/or system(s) meet the needs of the business.
• Proactively analyze and resolve software, system, or application errors in a timely and accurate fashion.
• Provide status reports as requested and escalate items to decision makers as needed.
• Create and maintain documentation for systems and procedures related to the deliverables expectation.
• Train customers and other team members on usage of systems and solutions.
• Identify cross-functional opportunities to automate the execution of repeatable tasks and simplify system workflows.
• Demonstrate problem-solving skills within area of responsibility and adjacent technology areas.
• Build, maintain, and improve systems to support business processes.

EDUCATION:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD in related field of study. Equivalent work experience may be acceptable.

EXPERIENCE:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD with a minimum of 2 years relevant experience. No degree with a minimum of 4 years relevant experience.

COMPUTER SKILLS:
Requires strong PC skills including Microsoft Office, project management system(s), graphic management system(s) and all other web-based discipline specific systems.

COMMUNICATION SKILLS:
Requires robust collaboratory and relational ability to work cross-functionally across the Enterprise, with external customers, and consultants. Positive customer service and a team approach are required.

SPECIAL SKILLS (if applicable):
Critical thinking and problem-solving skills required. Strong time-management and organizational skills needed.

SUPERVISORY:
None

TRAVEL:
3+ Trips Per Year

Relocation Assistance Eligible:
Yes

Work Shift:

1ST SHIFT (United States of America)

Hourly Applicants ONLY -You must complete the task after submitting your application to provide additional information to be considered for employment.

Tyson is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, national origin, color, religion, age, genetics, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability or veteran status.

