18270,3741,Senior Analytics Consultant (Remote),Experian,Anywhere,"Descrizione dell'azienda

We are the leading global information services company, providing data and analytical tools to our clients around the world. We help businesses to manage credit risk, prevent fraud, target marketing offers and automate decision making. We also help people to check their credit report and credit score and protect against identity theft...

We employ approximately 17,000 people in 37 countries and our corporate headquarters are in Dublin, Ireland, with operational headquarters in Nottingham, UK; California, US; and São Paulo, Brazil.

Experian is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, age, or veteran status.

We are committed to building an inclusive culture and creating an environment where people can balance successful careers with their commitments and interests outside of work. Our flexible working practices support our belief that this balance brings long-lasting benefits for our business as well as our people. Some roles lend themselves to flexible options more than others, and if this is important to you, we are open to discussing agile working opportunities during the hiring process.

Descrizione del lavoro

ROLE: Senior Analytics Consultant

Location: Both Rome or Milan

This successful candidate will be part of a very dynamic, highly motivated and fast-growing Analytics team in Italy and will develop analytical solutions to the benefit of our clients’ and their customers. He / She will be based in our Rome or Milan office.

The role holder must have significant experience (4-5 years at least) in the development of analytical projects in the field of credit risk management, anti-fraud modelling and or Marketing. Knowledge and experience of regulatory-driven analytics (AIRB, IFRS9 etc.) will be a major plus.

Job Description – Consultancy and Analytics

· Support and manage a team of analytical staff (Consultants Jr. Consultants, Analysts) in the development robust analytical solutions for different clients, primarily in the financial sector – this includes the development of statistical models and ad hoc data analysis

· Be responsible for understanding the project’s requirements and for communicating them to more junior staff

· Ensure that project deliverables are accurate and meet project scope and objectives

· Question results through applied intelligence in a proactive way and interpret them into conclusions and recommendations to clients

· Present the project results to clients and/or to more senior members of Experian

Job Description – Pre-sales and Sales support

· Participate in pre-sales and sales meetings with clients and prospects to describe and position Experian’s analytics projects and propositions

Job Description – Project Management

· Plan, organize and complete project work to meet team commitments within agreed timescales

Qualifiche

Job requirements and qualifications – The successful candidate will have:

· Strong personal motivation and commitment to results

· Degree in quantitative subjects (mathematics, economics, statistics, engineering, physics)

· Strong technical and analytical skills

· Good experience in the design and implementation of credit risk models

· Strong knowledge of statistics and how statistical methodologies are employed in model development

· Good knowledge of SAS or other major statistical packages (e.g. WPS, SPSS, R)

· Established track record (at least four years) of delivering complex analytical projects

· Fluent in English – both written and spoken with working proficiency

Informazioni aggiuntive

The following abilities and skills will be considered a further advantage:

· Previous experience in Advanced Analytics/Machine Learning projects

· Working knowledge of Python and / or other relevant programming packages

· Previous experience in analytics on Big Data platforms (e.g. Cloudera, Databricks) and related programming frameworks (e.g. Apache Spark)

· Working experience of minimum capital regulation (i.e. Basel AIRB) and/or of accounting regulation like IFRS 9 and how it is applied to products and services like those provided by Experian

· Working experience in Marketing Analytics

Experian Careers - Creating a better tomorrow together

