18321,49,"Sr. Marketing Data Analyst, REMOTE",Thermo Fisher Scientific,Anywhere,"Job Description

As part of the Thermo Fisher Scientific team, you'll discover meaningful work that makes a positive impact on a global scale. Join our colleagues in bringing our Mission to life every single day to enable our customers to make the world healthier, cleaner and safer...

Position Summary:

Are you passionate about how data and analytics converge to drive strategic decision-making within a global life science company? Then this is the role for you. You are inquisitive, by nature, and tend to always ask ""why."" Your curious demeanor fuels your insatiable appetite for learning and a fascination for analytics and data-driven decisioning within a large, complex organization. You also need to be a critical thinker with the ability to work with imperfect data and continuously test and learn.

This role is an individual contributor position and is highly visible. The successful candidate will have a broad background in marketing analysis, business systems analysis, presentation and influencing skills with expertise in the reporting process for full-funnel lead-generating marketing campaigns. You must also be able to translate your findings and turn them into useful business insights that get results and return on investment. You have strong business acumen, combined with a marketing and/or commercial analytics background, digital analytics experience, and project management skills.

Key Responsibilities:
• Independently synthesize automated reports and visualizations that provide useful insights in close partnership with marketing and commercial teams to expose opportunities that improve commercial funnel and marketing metrics.
• Lead the development of measurement frameworks and dashboards to measure performance of marketing campaigns, tactics, and investments.
• Develop and maintain digital channel reports and ad hoc deep dives to help marketing team optimize efforts.
• Support ongoing business marketing, sales, and digital channel reports/dashboards and support ad hoc deep dives to help marketing and commercial leaders optimize efforts.
• Develop and own weekly, monthly, and quarterly metrics reporting for marketing activities to business leaders. Provide clear metrics with guidance and insights on opportunities for optimization and improvements
• Lead projects from start to finish, and present findings and recommendations across a wide array of team members and settings, including strategic marketing, commercial, product management, and senior leadership.

Minimum Requirements/Qualifications:
• 5+ years of hands on experience in marketing analytics, digital marketing analytics, and business intelligence reporting
• Experience in writing scripts to extract and manipulate data, using SQL, Python, and/or Databricks for report automation
• 3+ years of experience with data visualization tools, such as Power BI, Tableau or Looker.
• Experience in marketing data systems such as web/digital (Adobe Analytics), SFDC and email (Silverpop, Eloqua, etc)
• Advanced knowledge of Excel (i.e. pivot, vlookups, macros)
• Proven experience in marketing analytics tools, such as A/B testing, statistical inference, and process control analysis (pre/post analysis)
• Excellent communication skills
• Ability to present executive summaries of practical insights and recommendations to executives
• Bachelors degree in a STEM field with a strong background in math, operations research, business analytics, or statistics
• MBA with a strong technical background or graduate degree preferable
• Minimal travel required < 25>
• Excellent ability to articulate complex data to a wide variety of non-technical audiences.

At Thermo Fisher Scientific, each one of our 100,000 extraordinary minds have a unique story to tell. Join us and give to our singular mission-enabling our customers to make the world healthier, cleaner and safer

