18327,55,"Data Analyst (St. Louis, MO)",Thermo Fisher Scientific,United States,"Job Description

When you join us at Thermo Fisher Scientific, you will be part of a team that shares your passion for exploration and discovery. With revenues of more than $40 billion, we provide our people the resources and opportunities to make meaningful contributions to the world...

The Data Analyst will learn and understand the data architecture of our computer systems in order to provide information to the business that drives action, effective root cause analysis, process monitoring, and identifies barriers to operational efficacy. This role will monitor data quality, integrity, and usability for applications and analytics for ERP and stand-alone systems in order to identify trends and opportunities to improve through analysis of data sets, and create insightful reports based on data mining, analysis, and effective data visualization. The Data Analyst must follow all company data security and privacy practices and standards while meeting the needs of end-users. This role will work closely with leaders from across the value stream to provide data-driven insights on PPI projects as well as coordinate with other functional areas assigning master data to steward standard best practices and maintain data integrity.

What will you do?
• Collaborate with multiple departments to understand and maintain focus on their analytical needs, including identifying critical metrics and KPIs, and deliver useful insights to relevant decision-makers
• Proactively analyze data to answer key questions from business partners or out of self-initiated curiosity with an eye for what drives business performance, investigating and communicating areas for improvement in efficiency and productivity
• Build and maintain rich interactive visualizations through data interpretation and analysis integrating various reporting components from multiple data sources
• Define and implement data acquisition and integration logic, selecting appropriate combination of methods and tools within defined technology stack to ensure efficient scalability and performance of the solution
• Develop and maintain databases by acquiring data from primary and secondary sources, and build scripts that will make our data evaluation process more flexible or scalable across data sets
• Data maintenance and auditing of critical fields of various tools and databases

How will you get here?
• Bachelor's degree or higher
• Proficient skill level in Excel, Power query and SQL preferred
• Analytic skills, including mining, evaluation, analysis, and data visualization
• Strong analytical experience with database in writing sophisticated queries, query optimization, debugging, user defined functions, views, indexes etc.
• Skills in processing, cleansing, and verifying the integrity of data used for analysis
• Good communication skills and the ability to influence senior leadership, along with all levels of the organization

Knowledge, Skills, Abilities
• Ability to clearly explain data insights to Operations team
• 2 + years of proven track record in data management and analysis
• Experience with various data collection methods and in coordinating efforts of multiple groups
• Practical experience in statistical analysis using statistical tools such as Excel, Power BI, SPSS, etc.
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills
• English language proficiency (verbal and written)

Key hiring criteria will include but are not limited to:
• Ability to work successfully in a collaborative, team-oriented business environment
• Excellent organizational, project, and collaboration skills with ability to multi-task
• Project management skills with demonstrated ability to take initiative, supervise and handle own deadlines, drive projects to completion
• Highly analytical with attention to detail
• Creative problem solver who looks for ways to improve processes as well as improve data visualizations to provide clarity to business partners
• Ability to apply analytical thinking and problem-solving with data providers and category leaders to achieve high data accuracy, data integrity, and provide data insights
• Clear communicator who maintains a high level of integrity with internal and external business partners",2022-05-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'sql', 'spss', 'excel']"
