• Assist with authoring Pratt roadmap for the software application as it relates to broader strategy, including technologies and industry best practices
• Seek mentoring and coaching opportunities from existing members of the team, including technical exposure and broader cross-functional learning

Experience/Qualifications:
• Five or more years of IT experience, with sensitivity and commitment to business problem solving
• Past exposure to architecture design, application integration, product road mapping, delivery, and support
• Possess exceptional written and oral communication skills, can develop clear, concise, and logical business communications, as well as deliver recommendations effectively to demanding audiences
• Demonstrated effectiveness working in a complex, service-intensive, deadline-driven environment
• Ability to build strong relationships to leverage information and insights across key groups
• Strong personal leadership, organizational, relationship-building, and negotiation skills
• Self-starter with self-confidence, enthusiasm, and strong customer service orientation

Basic Qualifications:
• U.S. Citizen (required due to Government contractual requirements)
• Bachelor's Degree with 2+ years of experience Preferred fields include Computer Science, Engineering, MIS or related technical discipline(s) OR HS Diploma and 6+ years of experience.

Preferred Qualifications:
• Good communication skills, work ethic and a high level of personal integrity and accountability
• Willingness to learn new technologies & take on new projects to grow experience
• Highly self-directed and able to learn quickly with a solid ability to drive and deliver results
• Strong analytical skills, demonstrated organizational and leadership skills, examples of effective teamwork, a track record of consistently meeting deadlines and due dates
• You're comfortable working with minimal daily supervision and to balance numerous priorities
• Ability to remain calm and composed under pressure, in a fast-paced environment of rapidly changing demands

What is my role type?

In addition to transforming the future of flight, we are also transforming how and where we work. We've introduced role types to help you understand how you will operate in our blended work environment. This role is:

Remote: Employees who are working in Remote roles will work primarily offsite (from home).

