18350,78,Principal Healthcare Data Analyst - Remote,Optum,Anywhere,"Optum is a global organization that delivers care, aided by technology to help millions of people live healthier lives. The work you do with our team will directly improve health outcomes by connecting people with the care, pharmacy benefits, data and resources they need to feel their best. Come make an impact on the communities we serve as we help advance health equity on a global scale. Here... you will find talented peers, comprehensive benefits, a culture guided by diversity and inclusion, career growth opportunities and your life's best work.(sm)
As a Principal Data Analyst in OptumCare Advanced Analytics group, you will lead efforts to manipulate and analyze data to support program evaluations and drive effectiveness of palliative care and end of life programs. You will partner with stakeholders to define data requirements to conduct data-driven analyses and establish efficient data aggregations to help tell the story of how OptumCare are making a difference. You will become a subject matter expert on the data and present results to our internal customers. You'll work closely with business leaders and other analysts and researchers in the team to develop innovative analytic solutions to achieve business objectives.
You'll enjoy the flexibility to work remotely * from anywhere within the U.S. as you take on some tough challenges.
Primary Responsibilities:
• Develop and implement appropriate business requirements for dataset creation for research projects in collaboration with research analysts and Advanced Analytics leaders
• Conduct Data Feasibility and Sample Size analyses for Program Evaluation Studies
• Develop code to extract and manipulate health insurance claims data, health care operational data, and clinical data from a variety of data sources
• Perform highly complex data cleansing, transformation, aggregation, and summarization and output datasets for analysis
• Identify and investigate data quality issues and lead efforts to research data anomalies
• Lead team efforts in documenting data and programming processes
• Serve as a data SME across multiple internal data sources
• Coach and assist other researcher and analysts regarding data sources and code usage
• Work collaboratively with other teams to develop standard code and data protocols to be used across Advanced Analytics team
• Interact directly with customers to gather specifications for research projects and ad hoc requests
• Lead analytic and data visualization projects within team or across teams
• Apply advanced and complex SAS programming techniques

You'll be rewarded and recognized for your performance in an environment that will challenge you and give you clear direction on what it takes to succeed in your role as well as provide development for other roles you may be interested in.
Required Qualifications:
• Undergraduate degree in mathematics, statistics, computer science, public health, health services research, economics, or related field
• 5+ years of experience in analyzing health insurance claims, transactions data, biometric, health assessment, or similar types of clinical, program or employer data
• 5+ years of experience integrating data from large relational databases
• 5+ years of experience SAS, SQL, or equivalent programming experience
• 5+ years of experience writing advanced Data Step SAS program or other equivalent programming language
• Excellent time/project management and problem-solving skills
• Experience using data visualization tools such as Tableau

P referred Qualifications:
• Demonstrated self-motivation and initiative in order to excel in a fast-paced environment, pivot priorities as business needs shift
• Excellent presentation skills and professional communication style (verbal and written)
• Proficiency in statistical techniques such as logistic regression, multivariate analysis, and linear models
• Working knowledge in Medicare, commercial, and/or Medicaid claims

