Job Description Summary...
As a Data Analyst at Venmo, you will apply your strategic and analytical skills to major company challenges. You will act as a business consultant to drive recommendations and implement solutions that ultimately impact the bottom line.

You will collaborate closely with a global team of colleagues across risk, sales, operations, product, data science, and finance in an environment that values your insight, encourages you to take on new responsibility, promotes continuous learning, and rewards innovation. Our team members are excited about solving analytical problems. They are bright, they are responsible, and they know how to follow through. If you're also like that, we'd love to hear from you.

Job Description:

Your way to impact

You will provide business impact around developing expertise in specific areas by leading analytical projects independently, while setting goals, providing benefit estimations, defining workflows, and coordinating timelines in advance.

On top of that, your work will also include discovery of new opportunities to grow and optimize business and risk/reward trade-offs through analytics.

Your day to day
• Usingmodeling and analytics to understand how business decisions impact our bottom line. This may include assessing risksof new products,determiningfraud policies, oridentifying inefficiencies in existing operations.
• Ensuringthe team is delivering on our KPIsby using various data mining and datavisualizationtools tomonitor portfolio performance andidentifyimprovementopportunities
• Developinghypotheses and set up your own problem frameworks to test for the best solutions. You will also scope the operational feasibility, lead implementation efforts, and monitor the success of your solutions.
• Creatingnew solutions rooted in empathy and research that assist all customers as they work to better manage their finances.
• Translate quantitative information into presentations that are easily understood by general management on a regular basis. Communicate and interact with partners, verbally and written, in a professional manner.
• Manage the enablement of new or high-risk vertical projects by way of collaboration with cross-functional teams, including sales, compliance, and product.
• Conduct post-live reporting on newly enabled verticals in which PayPal conducts businessthrough understandingthe customer payment flows, exposure and chargeback risks to PayPal.
• Collaborating in ateam environment. As part of our crew, you will learn to energetically rally diverse groups in pursuit of a common goal.
• Stay current on merchant industry trends that impact theLargeEnterprise Merchant segment.
• Lead special strategic projects and perform other duties as assigned.

What do you need to bring
• Bachelor'sdegreeor higherin a quantitative field (Business, Math, Economics, Finance, Statistics, Science, Engineering)
• 3+ years of experience in solving problems using a data-driven approach or Master's degree and 2+ years.
• High proficiency in fundamental SQL. Other technical skills are a plus (Python; Hadoop; R)
• The ideal candidate is inclusive, innnocative and curious, analutical and action-oriened, collaboraive and team oriented.

We're a purpose-driven company whose beliefs are the foundation for how we conduct business every day. We hold ourselves to our One TeamBehaviors,which demand that we hold the highest ethical standards, to empower an open and diverse workplace, and strive to treat everyone who is touched by our business with dignity and respect. Our employees challenge the status quo, ask questions, and find solutions. We want to break down barriers to financial empowerment. Join us as we change the way the world defines financial freedom.

