18510,238,Specialist on statistical treatment and analysis of the data...,FAO,"Home, KS","Organizational Setting

UTF/BRA/085/BRA...

Food and Nutritional Security (FNS) is understood as ""the realization of the right of all to regular and permanent access to quality food, in sufficient quantity, without compromising access to other essential needs, based on health-promoting food practices that respect cultural diversity and are environmental, cultural, economic and socially sustainable"".

It is a comprehensive concept that sets the challenge of measuring and monitoring the dimensions associated with SAN. Above all, it is one of the fundamental aspects for ensuring social protection, care and promoting integral development.

In order to ensure the Human Right to Adequate Food (DHAA), Brazil established the National Food and Nutritional Security System (SISAN) through the Organic Law on Food and Nutrition Security (LOSAN), Federal Law No 11,346 of 2006, implementing and coordinating policies for the promotion and access to healthy food, access to water, promotion of production, marketing and consumption of food from family farming.

The SISAN aims to formulate and implement food and nutritional security policies and plans, stimulate the integration of efforts between government and civil society, and promote monitoring, the monitoring and evaluation of the country’s food and nutritional security.

The organizational structures of SISAN are now institutionalized in a model that decentralizes management, towards the state and municipal levels. Through this decentralized federative system, government agencies (municipal, state, district and federal) must act together to carry out the National Food and Nutritional Security Policy, with a view to promoting and ensuring the progressive realization of DHAA.

Food and nutritional security actions have taken place throughout the national territory, for example, from the National School Feeding Policy (PNAE), the public facilities of SAN (community restaurants, community kitchens and food bank) actions to promote family farming, urban and periurban agriculture, food and nutrition education (EAN) actions, among others.

All states and the Federal District made the adhesion to SISAN, forming a group of technicians and managers committed to the consolidation of this system. The current challenge of the federal government is to strengthen the performance of these state bodies, as well as promote the adhesion of municipalities, which today has a total of 479 municipalities.

Among the strategies to improve the management of SISAN, it is considered essential to have diagnoses about the existence and condition of operation of the state and municipal components of SISAN to support the planning of strategies for its strengthening. And it is in this context that, in 2014, MapaSAN emerged, as a self-reported and voluntary response research of municipal and state managers, with the aim of collecting information, within the states, the Federal District and municipalities, management of the System and the SAN actions developed by them.

Reporting Lines

Assistente do Representante na FAO Brasil – Programas

Technical Focus

The products expected from the incumbent as a result of the developed activities are described below:

Product 1: Technical document in the form of a research report with the results achieved by the research at the end of the online data collection stage

Product 2: Technical document containing tabs and reports with research data, including publication of the resulting database.

Product 3: Technical document in the format of executive summary and final research report, including the publication of online database access tools.

The Specialist shall ensure that the services performed are performed with quality, meeting all specifications and within the deadline established in this term of reference.

Tasks And Responsibilities

The activities to be performed are as follows:
• Draw up a Work Plan, in a model established by the FAO - Food and Agriculture Organization, containing the strategy for developing all consultancy products, which must be delivered together with the first product to be presented;
• Hold technical meetings and information gathering with the technical teams of the National Secretariat of Social and Productive Inclusion - SEISP and the Secretariat of Evaluation and Information Management SAGI, regarding the methodology of information collection and the results of SAN mapping in the municipalities;
• Perform database extraction and statistical processing of data collected in MapaSAN in 2022 in municipalities;
• Define the scope of the executive summary and final publication of MapaSAN 2022;
• Systematize and analyze the data and information to compose the analysis of the results of MapaSAN 2022 for each axis;
• Draw up a final technical document containing tabulations and reports containing research data, including publication of the resulting database;
• Present text content for other areas of SEISP;
• Develop other activities necessary for the execution of the consultancy .

CANDIDATES WILL BE ASSESSED AGAINST THE FOLLOWING

Minimum Requirements
• University degree or Master’s degree (desirable) in the areas of Applied Social Sciences, Health Sciences, Agrarian Sciences and/or Human Sciences, according to CAPES Knowledge Table, with diploma duly recognized by MEC
• Minimum experience of 5 (five) years in the formulation and/or implementation and/or execution of public policies aimed at the federal government and/or state/district/municipal governments
• Working knowledge (level C) of Portuguese; basic knowledge (level A) of English would be an asset.
• Brazilian Nationality or other legally authorized to work in Brazil

FAO Core Competencies
• Results Focus
• Teamwork
• Communication
• Building Effective Relationships
• Knowledge Sharing and Continuous Improvement

Technical/Functional Skills
• Minimum 2 (two) years' experience in monitoring public policies;
• Experience in actions and programs that have contributed to the organization and/or structuring of public systems (example: Sisan, SUS, SUAS and others);
• Experience in diagnostics, construction and analysis of public policy data aimed at the federal government and/or state/district/municipal governments.

