18513,241,Data Analytics Analyst/Trainer,Metric5,"All, MO","Description

a Data Analytics Analyst/Trainer to perform analysis and validation activities supporting an enterprise data warehousing program. The United States Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS), Office of Information Technology (OIT), Data and Business Intelligence Support Services (DBIS) has been tasked with implementing Enterprise Data Warehouse and Business Intelligence (DW/BI... solutions. The Data Analytics Analyst/Trainer will be a member of the Center of Excellence (COE) team and will support the program by working with the end-user community to ensure that they are able to use the data analytics tools and that their resulting reports are accurate.

Program Details

The program you will be supporting has a mission to provide development, security, and operations (DevSecOps) support to U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) with a focus on development, operations, and modernization of the Agency’s Enterprise Data Warehouse/Data Lake. The team utilizes open-source, AWS Cloud, and Big Data technologies, agile project management practices, and modern DevSecOps delivery to provide the business intelligence support systems to meet the reporting, data analytics, and machine learning/artificial intelligence needs critical to USCIS leadership, data/business analysts, data scientists, and other decision-makers.

Required Skills
• 2-3 years of experience with SQL skills
• Working knowledge of Agile development and best practices
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills and the ability to interact professionally with a diverse group, executives, managers, and subject matter experts.
• Experience reviewing, preparing and/or maintaining system, operations, and training documentation with input from team members
• Ability to deliver high quality documentation and pay attention to detail
• Ability to quickly grasp technical concepts and make them easily understandable for non-technical audiences through text and other media
• Ability to manage own work, multi-task, and prioritize; highly organized, deadline oriented, quality focused

Desired Skills
• Working knowledge of Oracle Business Intelligence Enterprise Edition (OBIEE), Databricks, SAS, and/ or Tableau preferred
• 1-2 years of experience with JIRA or similar tool
• Experience of working with Maestro Confluence
• Understanding of technical and technology terms and processes

Responsibilities
• Work closely with Scrum Masters, technical leads, architects, and developers to communicate any data inaccuracies, defects, delays, and inconsistencies and support the Agile development process
• Provide support and training to the end-user community; provide resolutions for users by walking the user through a series of root cause analyses (RCA) to determine the cause of a problem
• Triage requests to identify data quality issues and query data using SQL and other methods. This role ensures problem ownership and promotes end-user satisfaction
• Create and maintain training resources (manuals, job aides, reference guides, webinars, websites, knowledge base articles) to support ongoing training using a number of mediums: Adobe, PowerPoint, video, Word, SharePoint, etc.
• Interface with other teams on behalf of the Center of Excellence team to improve processes and relationships, ensuring end-user buy-in and satisfaction
• Assist to create training tailored to the end users' needs by utilizing in-class training, webinars, or any other training methods
• Provide the business and data analyst community with knowledge, skills, and abilities to utilize data analytics reporting tools effectively
• Execute change management effectively by promoting the systems’ usefulness among the user community
• Analyze and address any end user reporting requests
• Evaluate training needs to support the development of learning objectives; collaborate with managers and subject matter experts on the learning objectives, content, and delivery of proposed courses
• Support the development of learning objectives; collaborate with managers and subject matter experts on the learning objectives, content, and delivery of proposed courses
• Create ad hoc reports as needed
• Gather, analyze, translate, and compose technical information into clear readable documents to be used by technical and non-technical personnel

Education: Bachelor’s degree in a technical discipline preferred – Computer Science, Mathematics, or equivalent technical degree, or the equivalent combination of education, professional training, and work experience.

Location: Reston, VA – Currently fully remote due to COVID-19

Clearance: Must be a US Citizen and be able to obtain a government agency Suitability Clearance. USCIS Entry on Duty (EOD) preferred",2022-01-20,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'word', 'sharepoint', 'powerpoint', 'sql', 'aws', 'sas', 'jira']"
18520,248,SPACES Data Analyst,State of North Dakota,United States,"The ND Department of Health and Human Services (DHHS) is seeking a Data Analyst for its Economic Assistance Division .

As th e Data Analyst , you will be responsible for evaluating and reporting the quality of the data from the Self-Service Portal and Combined Eligibility System (SPACES) by collaborating with programmers, engineers, and organizational leaders to identify opportunities for... process improvements, recommend system modifications, and develop policies for data governance. On a daily basis you will perform statistical tests on large datasets to determine data quality; identify corrupt data and code errors to improve data quality and integrity; use statistical tools to interpret data sets. In addition, you will document and report for immediate data changes or future data planning.

To succeed in this role, you should have a strong understanding of database architecture of an eligibility system and have performed data quality analysis, data modeling, reporting and governance. You should be highly organized, able to manage your time and priorities effectively with minimal direction. Furthermore you have demonstrated the ability to discuss data analysis and governance with all levels of data users. Most importantly, you are effective at influencing the adoption of data-driven recommendations that will improve the quality of the services provided to North Dakotans.

To be considered for this position, you must have a bachelor’s degree and three (3) years of experience in data analysis, data quality monitoring for an integrated eligibility system and management of data integrity, OR combination of equivalent related education and experience.

Working For ND DHHS

Careers with DHHS include 100% employer-paid family health insurance and an excellent retirement package! In addition to the exceptional health insurance and retirement benefits, DHHS values continued learning and career enhancement. Therefore, we offer varying continuing education formats, including in-person and online, as well as tuition reimbursement.

ND DHHS utilizes a blended workplace model. This is a remote position; the hired individual could work from anywhere.

Application Procedures

For more details about this position, please contact Monica Clark by email: moclark@nd.gov or phone: (701) 328-4879
• Please make sure that your resume includes information to demonstrate how you meet the minimum qualifications as posted. Your work history will not be given credit if the Department’s Human Resource Division cannot determine that you meet the minimum qualifications
• Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. The Department of Human Services does not offer or provide sponsorships.
• All application material must be received on or before the closing date by 11:59 pm.
• A copy of your qualifying degrees transcript and any applicable certifications or licensures must be provided at the time of an interview.

Employing Unit: DHHS Economic Assistance

TTY Number: ND Relay Service 1-800-366-6888 (text); 1-800-366-6889 (voice)

If you are experiencing technical difficulties with the Application Process or uploading attachments, please contact recruiter@nd.gov or (701)328-3290.

Equal Employment Opportunity

The State of North Dakota and this hiring agency do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex (including sexual orientation and gender identity), genetics, religion, age or disability in employment or the provisions of services and complies with the provisions of the North Dakota Human Rights Act.

As an employer, the State of North Dakota prohibits smoking in all places of state employment in accordance with N.D.C.C.
