https://app.brazenconnect.com/a//s/4DJxY/next/login

Qualifications

Other... information:Bachelors in a data and analytics affiliate field such as Business Statistics and Analysis, Business Administration, Finance, Information Systems, Computer Science or related. Four or more years of experience in data compilation, reporting and analytics utilizing data and analytics tools. Demonstrated skills in leading a team through standard processes or projects. Must demonstrate strong analytical skills/capabilities and communication skills (verbal and written). Strong working knowledge and/or experience with Microsoft Office products and other analytical tools such as SAS, Business Objects, Tableau etc. Prior Business Objects, relational databases, and health care experience preferred. Excellent written and oral communications is a MUST.

Responsibilities

Responsibilities:Project Management and Execution:* Make prioritization decisions concerning individual or team tasks and assignments, maintain communications with customers to manage expectations, and escalates appropriately to management* Interface with internal business units and external entities (i.e. vendors, regulatory agencies) to manage requirements gathering, maintain work plan, coordinate activities, maintain effective communication in support of reporting/analytics* Manage customer requirements and identify most efficient and accurate approach to structuring solutions to complex reporting/analytics needs * Present, process, analyze, interpret, and assess impact to internal and external stakeholders for cross-departmental or enterprise initiatives that are accurate, complete, timely, and effective in support of business initiatives, accreditation, and regulatory compliance* Discern patterns and correlate diverse set of information, conceptualize and then translate ideas from abstract to concrete, determine appropriate level to conduct analysis, and navigate efficiently between levels of detail to transform data into an audience appropriate story that can be used to support business decisions, identify solutions to problems, or answer questions* Maintain reporting/analytics foundation through coordination of business definitions, data marts and BI tools (i.e. BO), translation into technical requirements, annual maintenance for any updates, and testing to ensure accuracy* Review data provided by the business operator and manage execution of reporting/analysis, perform interpretations and conclusions, and prepare recommendations* Accurately interpret, understand, evaluate, select, and recommend appropriate alternate reporting/analytics that are innovative and sophisticated achieving quality and work/process improvements to support the business decision * Validate reports/analysis to ensure accuracy via comparison to internal and external benchmarks and use of peer review as appropriate* Act as a data steward maintaining and ensuring data integrity; manage research concerning data anomalies, work with other departments to identify solution or workaround, and communicate outcomes and impacts to other departments as appropriate* Perform, monitor and manage other ad-hoc/ advance reporting/analytics functions as and when requiredTraining and Guidance:* Serve as a resource/educator to internal/external customers and peers regarding appropriate use of data and BI tools ensuring accurate and advanced understanding/use of reports/analytics/data and increase technical capability of tools* Perform audit and monitor progress of team members supporting the reporting/analytics process and providing feedback to manager*Assist managers in determining the best content to share with others; support other team members in knowledge sharing best practices* Responsible for the work flow of the analytics associates ensuring reliability, integrity, and timeliness of end products*Coach and assist team members to ensure continuous",2022-06-18,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sas']"
18546,274,"Senior Data Analyst [Remote or San Diego, CA]",EDF Renewables North America,Anywhere,"The Pre-Construction Estimating Team at EDF Renewables is seeking a dynamic individual to conduct detailed data analysis to support all aspects of estimating Utility-Scale Solar PV, Energy Storage and Wind Engineering Procurement Construction (EPC) projects. With the primary strategic focus to provide innovative analytical insights on project profitability and constructability to support pricing... strategies developed to maximize profits. The Senior Data Analyst will also provide data solutions and tools to help assess fair market value of project costs and change orders requests during project execution.

Responsibilities

Applications and database development and maintenance
• Maintain and continuously improve custom internal cost estimating software, data structure, and analytics around the Utility-Scale EPC estimating processes.
• Develop and implement databases, data collection systems, data analytics and other strategies that optimize statistical efficiency and quality.
• Coordinate with various internal cross-functional teams to design the proper interface, touch points, and inputs for the estimating software. Design the workflow and system data architecture.
• Maintain and continuously improve the Monte Carlo risk assessment software and communicate results.
• Maintain centralized databases of market costs, historical projects costs, labor productivities, value engineering, and cost efficiencies.

Data analytics and reporting
• Gather and build analytics of external market data and insights to improve and update internal cost estimate methodologies and assumptions.
• Identify, analyze, and interpret trends or patterns in complex datasets.
• Work with management to prioritize business and information needs.
• Facilitates effective communication and coordination with Development, Product Management, Strategic Procurement, Pre-Construction, Portfolio Management, Engineering, and Project Management to produce project analytics to support the most competitive EPC cost estimates.

Other duties as assigned.

Qualifications
• Extensive experience in SQL.
• Proficient with tools and reporting packages including Tableau Desktop, Tableau Server, Power BI, MySQL, and ETL tools (Tableau Prep).
• Experience in advanced LOD calculations, custom data visualizations, data cleaning and restructuring.
• Extensive experience in Python (libraries such as pandas and numpy).
• Proficient in Microsoft Suite (Excel, PowerPoint, Project, Outlook, Word, etc.)
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy.
• Excellent written and oral communication skills.

Education/Experience –
• Minimum five (5) years of experience in data analysis.
• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Statistics, Engineering Technology or related study.

Skills/Knowledge/Abilities –
• Proven working experience as a data analyst or business analyst.
• Technical expertise regarding data models, database design development, data mining and segmentation techniques.
• Practical knowledge of data in various forms such as data warehouses, SQL, and unstructured data environments.
• Knowledge of statistics and experience using statistical packages for analyzing datasets.
• Understanding of Agile development methodologies, software design patterns, network design and architecture.
• Ability to understand complex data processes and evaluate opportunities for efficiencies and streamlining.
• Excellent teamwork and communication skills with the ability to work in a very dynamic environment.
• Demonstrates excellent organizational skills with good time management.
• Ability to work in a matrix organization with the mindset of taking a holistic cross-functional approach.

Working Conditions:

90% of time is spent in the office environment, utilizing computers (frequent use of various Microsoft software/programs), phones, and general office equipment. 10% of time is spent outside of the office visiting projects, vendors’ and/or internal customers’ sites in additional to attending various conferences and meetings.

