Position Requirements

Job Summary

The RCM Data Analyst is responsible for helping manage the software resources of Hiring Company (NAPA) related to Medical (Anesthesia) Claims, Provider Enrollment, Eligibility, Payment Posting, and Patient Financial Services processes. This will be achieved by conducting a thorough analysis of data to create reports identifying trends by division, provider, payer, and individual staff members within the organization and by in maintaining/optimizing system software to reduce payer enrollment turnaround times and subsequent claims processing for onboarding providers and post-claim adjudication workflows. The RCM Analyst will regularly compile reports/data from various software platforms. This position will look for opportunities to enhance workflow processes and will provide consultation on provider enrollment & reimbursement practices to mitigate denials and revenue leakage in the Revenue Cycle Division. This position reports to the RCM Director of Revenue Cycle Management.

Duties & Responsibilities

Principal Duties and Responsibilities
• Reviews current software platform functionality to optimize performance by users, creates report templates for users, evaluates and ensures data integrity across credentialing and billing platforms
• Creates variance reports to identify and trend payment discrepancies (e.g., denials, underpayments, and write-offs etc.), reporting results to leadership on a regular basis
• Conducts ongoing analysis of contract compliance and financial performance for third-party payers to provide leadership with support during payer contract negotiations
• Develops performance dashboards with key performance indicators, formulas, and other reimbursement-related data to track reimbursement trends for both individual staff members and the overall department
• Interprets compiled dashboard data and develops regular reports to explain trends and identify root causes of financial performance for the organization’s financial leaders
• Analyzes dashboard data to identify potential gaps in the department’s reimbursement and workflows
• Helps design and implement improvements to established or proposed provider data collection methods and reimbursement process flows in an effort to maximize potential revenue
• Stays apprised of current industry best practices and aligns departmental processes with applicable practices as needed
• Identifies and works with IT to rectify any claims data transmission issues as they arise
• Regularly evaluates departments’ performance both qualitatively and quantitatively as it relates to minimizing provider enrollment denials and write-offs
• Supports the coordination of cost reports or other information as required by the government and other payers
• Identifies potential sources of revenue leakage and assists in developing data-driven initiatives to resolve any issues
• Honors the organization’s mission statement, vision statement, and values

Qualifications

Education
• Bachelor’s degree in business, accounting, healthcare administration, or finance required

Experience
• At least 2-3 years of experience in healthcare accounting or finance required

Knowledge, Skills, Abilities
• Knowledge of third-party payer regulations, reimbursement, and payment policies
• Understanding of billing practices and operational workflows
• Understanding of medical terminology and medical record coding
• Proven analytic and problem-solving skills
• Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills
• Proficiency in utilizing Microsoft Excel and other database management software
• Ability to extract and analyze relevant data
• Ability to self-manage and prioritize multiple tasks

