At Hatch, we're dreaming up new ways to help everyone sleep better. We’ve helped over a million families get the sleep they need and we’re just getting started. Originally inspired by new parents and their babies, Hatch has evolved our suite of smart sleep products to help humans of all ages and stages develop and maintain natural, healthy sleep habits...

The Opportunity

We are looking for our first Growth Analyst to help drive a data-first culture and support our Growth team. Reporting to the VP of Growth, you will deeply understand the ecomm and product experiences and how they relate to our company objectives. You’ll synthesize and communicate growth insights, and empower others to work effectively with data so that we can achieve our mission of helping everyone sleep better. You will deep dive into our Hatch Sleep Membership and identify opportunities to continue growing the program. You will support the expansion of AB testing across the organization and lead the analysis and recommendations. This is a great opportunity to join a rapidly growing team and have an immediate impact on the customer experience and business.

This person must be based in the United States or Canada. Hatch is based out of California, so this role would be asked to be available during PST/PDT hours

What You’ll Do

Within 3 Months:

Build a solid understanding of our ecomm experience, product experience and current data streams.
• Complete an audit of our current web and mobile subscription analytics and identify discrepancies, redundancies, and oversights in our taxonomy.
• Drive the monitoring, optimizing, and reporting on growth metrics and split-test results, making recommendations based on sound analytics, experimentation, and test findings.
• Look for areas of growth, and start to think about how we can use data better to get to where we want to go as a company, revamping company wide dashboards reporting on subscription growth

Within 6 Months:
• Drive the monitoring, optimizing, and reporting on growth metrics and split-test results, making recommendations based on analytics, experimentation, and test findings.
