• People Planning Strategies and Programs designs, implements, and supports workforce management solutions globally, collaborating with partners across the Company to develop retail programs that enable teams and customers to receive a truly world class experience.

Overview of Role: In this position, you will be responsible for collaborating with cross-functional business partners to analyze data, design solutions, build processes and support programs.

What We Are Looking For

Droisys is seeking a Data Analyst to lead and manager strategic programs to assist and benefit our employees and customers –
• Onsite in Austin, TX or Cupertino, CA on a hybrid schedule (remote is possible but not preferred and will result in lesser Pay Rate)
• Long-term assignment of 1 year with possibility of extension

Requirements
• 5+ years of experience as a Data Analyst
• Project management experience
• Some travel required
• Strong data analysis skills, with ability to efficiently identify trends and root causes and then to analyze and transition insights into actionable projects
• Strong excel modeling skills, with ability to work with sophisticated formulas and macros
• Fluency in SQL for data access, manipulation, and validation
• Passion for data visualization and information design (Tableau proficiency preferred)
• Ability to clearly communicate complex analyses to non-technical audiences and experience presenting to management and/leadership groups
• Consistent track record in prioritizing, planning, and implementing strategies
• Ability to operate both at strategic and at tactical levels

Preferred Experience:
• Experience and understanding of management principles related to: strategy, resource allocation, human resources modeling, leadership technique, production methods, and coordination of people and resources
• BA/BS

Description of Responsibilities:
