18869,597,Senior Research/Data Analyst (4214018),State of Missouri,"Jefferson City, MO","Job Location: This position will be located at 920 Wildwood, Jefferson City, MO 65102

Why You’ll Love This Position...

As a Senior Research/Data Analyst, you will have the opportunity to develop, lead, and conduct a broad and complex range of investigative and analytical studies. This position will gain diverse experience while applying technical concepts and methodologies to support chronic disease programs such as Missouri’s Breast & Cervical Cancer Early Detection Program (Show Me Healthy Women), Comprehensive Tobacco Control Program, Missouri Cancer Registry, and WISEWOMAN Program.

Excellent Benefits Package That Includes
• Health insurance 1st of the month following start date
• Generous amounts of annual and sick leave each month
• 14 paid holidays
• Retirement and deferred savings programs
• Ongoing opportunities for training and professional development

What You’ll Do
• Provide analytical expertise to meet grant reporting and evaluation needs for chronic disease programs including, but not limited to, Show Me Healthy Women, Comprehensive Tobacco Control, WISEWOMAN, and the Missouri Cancer Registry.
• Develop methods and tools for data collection and analysis in addition to creating and/or updating data dissemination products such as grant-related reports, maps, presentations, factsheets, or dashboards.
• Serve as a liaison between programs and data systems, knowledgeable in the analysis of data from multiple chronic disease programs and existing surveillance systems (such as the Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System) to support program needs.
• Collaborate with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders working to reduce the incidence and mortality of cancer and associated projects.
• Analyze risk factors associated with chronic disease, specifically cancer, and provide context to facilitate planning and policy decisions.
• Work independently, as an experienced team member, or as a mentor to facilitate complex analyses/research that furthers program goals and supports the mission of public health organizations in Missouri.

All You Need For Success

Minimum Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree and 4-6 years of relevant experience and/or appropriate certification (Master’s Degree preferred, transcripts required).
• A high degree of technical expertise, and the ability to use substantial independent judgment when applying technical concepts and methodologies
• Ability to plan and execute complex research studies, conduct comprehensive data analysis, and interpret data
• Knowledge of data management, research design, and current analytical/statistical methods
• Experience with SAS, SQL, or other analytical software and general programming techniques
• Experience with ArcGIS and SQL Server and/or Tableau (or similar) is preferred but not required
• Experience with programs such as Excel, Access, and Word as well as other PC desktop resources
• Strong and effective communication skills, both written and verbal

If You Have Questions About This Position Please Contact

Anthony Belenchia, anthony.belenchia@health.mo.gov, 573-526-6660

