This position reports to

US Spare Parts & Repair Center Manager

Your responsibilities
• Master Data records: Ensures that Master Data is maintained efficiently and accurately in all systems within scope of responsibility
• Advice and guidance: Understands the impact of the Master Data maintained and provides guidance to others regarding Master Data
• Documentation: Documents, reviews and updates all work procedures pertaining to all aspects of system maintenance
• Data quality assurance: Assists in the overall solution to quality issues by participating in the elimination of non conformance and adopting the approach of ""doing it right the first time""
• Super User duties: May act as Master Data Super User, providing support and training to other Master Data Specialists and Master Data professionals in own area of responsibility and suggesting improvements concerning Master Data creation, maintenance and archiving/deletion processes

Your background
• Bachelor’s degree preferred and minimum 5 years Master Data experience within SAP
• Ability to demonstrate SAP expertise, master data characteristics, variants and reports
• General knowledge in change management processes. Strong written and verbal communication skills
• Ability to influence others and support projects
