18874,602,Senior Supply Chain Data Analyst,CenterPoint Energy,United States,"CenterPoint Energy is looking for a Senior Data Analyst to join our Supply Chain Team, located in Houston, TX.

Summary...

You are responsible for the development, support, maintenance, and implementation of supply chain data analytics. Knowledge of analytic tools and systems are required. You should be able to work as an independent team member, capable of applying judgment to plan and execute your tasks. You should have advanced knowledge of Tableau/SQL. Ability to respond to technical queries/requests from stake holders and business.

In this role, you should be an visualization expert with Tableau with exposure in the application of standard software development principles. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills are essential for interpreting data. Constant, self-motiviated pursuit of learning systems, organizational structure, processes, data sets and techniques.

We want you to know

CenterPoint Energy and its predecessor companies have been in business for more than 150 years. Our vision to lead the nation in delivering energy, service and value drives our strategy and performance. We have an unwavering commitment to safely and reliably deliver electricity and natural gas to millions of people.

Diversity and Inclusion

CenterPoint Energy is committed to creating an inclusive work environment where business results are achieved through the skills, abilities and talents of our diverse workforce.

At CenterPoint Energy, individuals are respected for their contributions toward our company objectives. We strive for an inclusive work environment across all levels that is reflective of the available workforce in the communities we serve.

What We Bring To You
• Competitive pay
• Paid training
• Benefits eligibility begins on your first day
• Flexible work schedule, paid holidays and paid time off
• Professional growth and development programs including tuition reimbursement
• 401(k) Savings Plan featuring a company match dollar-for-dollar up to 6% and a company contribution of 3% regardless of your contribution with immediate 100% vesting.

Your Background Includes

To be successful in this role you will:
• Develop dashboards, scorecards, and other visualizations to support business requests using Tableau.
• Leverage established guidelines and custom designs to create complex formulas and calculations to meet the needs of business
• Strong data analysis and data quality skills such as SQL, reporting and data visualization, trouble shooting, validation and cleansing
• Leverage expertise in business systems, processes, and data sets to serve as a champion for improved data quality and accurate data use across the organization.
• Development of formal documentation including process maps, data dictionaries, metadata, architecture diagrams.
• Develop test strategies for implemented efforts to optimize collection and use of data to improve efficiency, improve data quality, improve customer service, and reduce costs.
• Operate with moderate supervision, guidance, and direction from leadership and senior staff.
• May provide training and guidance to less experienced professionals.

Basic Qualifications

Education
• Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university in Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, Economics, or a related field.

Experience
• Requires a minimum of 7 years of related analytics experience
• 5 years of advanced Tableau expertise
• Prior experience with SAP
• Experience with data warehousing technology like SAP HANA, Oracle database Google BigQuery, etc.
• Programming experience in languages including SQL
• Proven success in a collaborative, team-oriented environment

Preferred Experience
• Supply Chain Knowledge
• Good Communication skills

