18893,621,"Director, Data Enablement Strategy & Analytics",SelectQuote Insurance Services,"Overland Park, KS","Founded in 1985, SelectQuote (NYSE: SLQT) provides solutions that help consumers protect their most valuable assets: their families, health and property. The company pioneered the model of providing unbiased comparisons from multiple, highly rated insurance companies allowing consumers to choose the policy and terms that best meet their unique needs. Two foundational pillars underpin... SelectQuote’s success: a strong force of highly trained and skilled agents, who provide consultative needs analysis for every consumer, and proprietary technology that sources and routes high quality leads. The company has three core business lines: SelectQuote Senior, SelectQuote Life and SelectQuote Auto and Home. SelectQuote Senior, the largest and fastest-growing business, serves the needs of a demographic that sees 10,000 people turn 65 each day with a range of Medicare Advantage and Medicare Supplement plans.

Job Summary:

The Data Enablement Strategy & Analytics Director will support all Selectquote divisions creating, implementing and optimizing cross-sell and lead level reporting and procedures. This role is responsible for managing our customer lifecycle data team, providing strategic decision making driven by effective reporting and analysis and managing our strategic partnerships reporting.

Essential Functions:
• Create, prepare, and analyze reports and metrics to identify opportunities where desired processes are not meeting fundamental operational goals or pacing towards success and take action
• Effectively project manage and execute on strategic initiatives
• Drive the evolution of SelectQuote’s cross-divisional strategies through innovative process design, technology solutions, and cross-functional leadership
• Product execution owner and data SME
• Continuously assess department for process improvement opportunities and lead the implementation of solutions
• Effectively summarize and communicate department results and ad hoc initiatives weekly to various stakeholders
• Partner with business and technical leaders across the company to execute on various projects ranging from lead plans, tech development, etc.

Knowledge, Skills & Abilities:
• Quick to learn complex integrated systems, quick to understand how to interpret and utilize disparate data sets
• Extremely strong analytical skills – must be able to understand KPIs and use data to identify issues and make decisions
• Excellence in operations and executing new initiatives quickly
• Strong communication skills and a proven ability to influence peers
• Strong project management skills
• Strong technical skills in SQL, Microsoft office, etc.
• Excellent executive presence as this role will have C-suite visibility
• Entrepreneurial spirit – creativity to identify opportunities when others may not see them and a willingness to “roll up your sleeves” to execute
• Proactive, impatient nature, taking ownership of projects and acting as a driving force for progress
• Flexibility to adapt and change as priorities evolve
• Ability to manage multiple priorities at the same time

Training & Experience:
• BA / BS computer science/MIS, mathematics, marketing, finance, preferred with strong undergraduate track record
• 7+ years of experience in a heavy analytical role
• 5+ years of experience in an operational discipline (sales operations, supply chain, etc.) with responsibility for delivering against a set of KPIs
• 3+ years of experience in SQL or comparable language
• Proven track record of managing to a set of operational KPIs and hitting performance objectives
• Proven experience as both a player and a coach – ability to execute while also leading and influencing others
• Proven success managing and executing large cross-department initiatives

Benefits:

It’s an exciting time to join SelectQuote. We became a publicly traded company in 2020 with the first 100% virtual IPO (non-biotech) in American history. We have also been recognized nationally on the 2021 Top Workplaces USA list and by the Kansas City Business Journal as a 2020 Best Places to Work honoree.

Full-time employees are eligible for medical, dental, vision, voluntary short-term disability, company-paid long term disability, company-paid life insurance and accidental death & dismemberment (AD&D), 401(k) + company match and 100% vesting after 4 years, discretionary profit sharing, employee stock purchase program (espp), paid time off, floating holidays, paid maternity leave, paid parental bonding leave, tuition reimbursement, jury duty pay, and other paid leaves vary based on work location",2022-06-27,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['sql']
18894,622,"Sr. Financial Data Analytics, Reporting Analyst",Cochlear,United States,"Position Spotlight
• We are looking for a candidate with a financial analytics and reporting background.
• Are you able to tell the story from the data with little direction...
• Tableau or other data visualization platform experience required
• Considering Colorado Candidates. Hybrid role, 2 days in our Lone Tree office, 3 days working from home!

Change people’s lives and love what you do! Cochlear is the most recognized brand in hearing health care.

About The Role

If you know Data analytics and reporting and are good at telling the story of the data then this is a fantastic opportunity to join the Finance team as the global leader in implantable hearing devices! Cochlear is helping people hear, and be heard, all over the world. In this role, you will be based in our Americas head office in Lone Tree, CO.

In alignment with our organizational principle of providing a safe work environment, employees of Cochlear are required to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19. The only allowable exceptions include qualifying medical and religious accommodation. Proof of your COVID-19 vaccination will be required prior to your start date.

Your success in this role is measured by your ability to help to develop and enhance analytic capabilities in the organization. This position will partner with the business to develop insights that drive actionable outcomes and continue the development and maintenance of our tableau dashboard reporting.

Key Responsibilities
• Analytics - Identify opportunities to use data to help drive new strategies and improve business performance; utilize analytical techniques to produce outputs that can be used to ""tell the story"" and provide business recommendations; Help create dynamic models that are streamlined and meet business requirements; Use critical thinking skills to independently plan and execute analysis
• Tableau Development and Administration - Develop dashboards and views that reflect business priorities; Maintain existing tableau reporting and optimize performance; Ensure tableau server structure and reporting is in line with best practices; Work with BI team to administer access and security on Tableau sever
• Data Management and Automation - Understand data structure of the organization and utilize data cleansing and blending tools to create sources for reporting platform; Identify data gaps and recommend data to be added to master sources; Partner with IT team to facilitate new and existing solutions; Support process flow automation for various business partners in the organization
• Reporting - Proactively and reactively provide reporting solutions for the business; Work with business to define reporting requirements and utilize business acumen to suggest best solutions: Recommend when reporting can be added to standardized reporting in Tableau & use automation techniques to streamline
• IT Business Partnering - Work with IT to manage the finance departments major initiatives; Partner with IT business to monitor progress and identify potential risks or opportunities as initiatives progress through the pipeline; Work closely with the global business intelligence team to identify and implement new solutions

Key Requirements

To add value to Cochlear in this role you'll be able to meet and demonstrate the following knowledge, skills and abilities in your application and at interview:
• Bachelors or Equivalent Work Experience
• 3-5 Years of Experience
• Demonstrated proficiency using data visualization tools (preferably Tableau)
• High proficiency using Microsoft Excel to build models and perform analysis
• Ability to ""tell the story”, with data and proven track record of presenting findings to management
• Experience extracting, transforming and loading data for analysis; Ability to automate repeatable processes to create efficiencies and reduce errors; Experience with Tableau Prep or Microsoft Power Query preferred but no required
• Strong business acumen with ability to understand operating models
• Ability to meet deadlines and re-prioritize as directed
• Knowledge of basic statistical analysis techniques; Understanding or experience of Python or R a plus but not required
• Basic knowledge of database principles a plus but not required

Total Rewards

In addition to the opportunity to develop your knowledge and grow professionally, we offer competitive wages and benefits.
• Target Salary Range: $80,000 – $90,000 based upon experience, as well as an annual bonus opportunity of 7.5% of base salary
• Benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance and disability insurance as well as 401(K) matching with immediate vesting, Paid Time Off, tuition reimbursement, maternity and paternity leave, Employee Stock Purchase Plan and pet insurance.

Who are we?

Human needs have always been our inspiration, ever since Professor Graeme Clark set out to create the first multi-channel cochlear implant because he saw his father struggle with hearing loss. We always start with people in mind – thinking about their needs.

For this reason, our products, services and support will continue to evolve and improve. We are by our customers’ side through the entire hearing journey, so they can experience a life full of hearing. Our employees tell us that the number one reason they enjoy working for Cochlear is the opportunity to make a difference to people’s lives and working in an organization where they can be part of bringing the mission to life each day.

Physical & Mental Demands

The physical and mental demands described below are representative of those that must be met to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.

While performing the duties of this job, the individual is regularly required to be in a stationary seated position; utilize business technology for work product delivery, communicate orally and in writing with others internal or external to the organization, utilize problem solving skills to discern and convey information. Specific vision abilities required by this job include ability to adjust focus. The individual is regularly required to utilize comprehension, critical thinking, communication, problem solving, organization reasoning, relating to others and discernment of items such as product specifications, procedures and processes to customers. Influence, organization/classification of information and planning are also required.

The work environment is a hybrid home/office environment and represents those an individual encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.

Apply now by completing your application form online. Applicants must meet the job specific application criteria to be considered. Visit our careers site at www.cochlear.us/careers to learn more.

Cochlear Americas is an Equal Opportunity, Affirmative Action Employer and provides equal employment opportunity (EEO) to all persons regardless of age, color, national origin, citizenship status, physical or mental disability, race, religion, creed, gender, sex, sexual orientation, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local law . In addition, Cochlear will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation with completing the online application, please contact us via web or phone at 303-264-2549",2022-08-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'python', 'excel', 'r']"
