18916,644,Data Analysis Instructor,LaunchCode,,"LaunchCode is a non-profit solving the tech talent gap and paving new pathways to economic opportunity through education, apprenticeships, and job placement in technology. We're seeking a hyper-motivated Lead Instructor to lead our Women+ Data Analysis class.

Are you passionate about sharing your coding skills with others? Have programming chops and communication skills? Does the thought of... preparing people for employment sing to your soul? Then you, my friend, should contract with us.

Lead Instructor Responsibilities

As Lead Instructor, your responsibility is to broadly ensure the overall success of the class alongside your team of Teaching Assistants (TAs). You will plan and deliver lectures, provide insight to TAs, and have final say in coordination with LaunchCode's Candidate Engagement Manager on what happens during each class session. You will also be the primary liaison with LaunchCode staff, communicating feedback and any changes you plan to make.

Qualifications
• Ability to empathize and work with learners from a wide variety of backgrounds and skill levels
• Strong communication skills
• Proficiency in topics covered (See our syllabus here.)
• Willingness to learn in-depth the topics they are less familiar with
• General alignment with LaunchCode's educational philosophy
• Ability to lead and coach Teaching Assistants

The work is fast-paced and multi-faceted. It's also super fun. A pretty sweet deal, if you ask us.

You're perfect for this role if you
• Have substantial work experience as a developer and/or experience teaching at the college level
