Description
Company Description:
A Square Group (ASG) is a Minority Woman Owned, Physician owned small business with over 10 years' experience in federal government contracting. ASG offers data collection, statistical analysis, health program evaluation, technical and health program implementation support. ASG provides a broad range of healthcare technology related services such as software development and integration, mobile apps, AI/ML, Analytics, Data Science, Bigdata, DevSecOps, Digital transformation, cloud, and cybersecurity. ASG is CMMI Level 3 certified for Development and Services, and holds ISO certifications 9001:2015, 20000-1:2011, and 27000:2015.

Job Description:
ASG is seeking Systems Data Analysts in support of our new VIPER program delivering innovative software solutions for our customer the US Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS). Systems Data Analysts will work on leading edge integration solutions to meet the mission.

Use strong technical and analytical skills to explore and examine data from disparate systems with the goal of discovering patterns and hidden insights that can enhance mission capabilities. Work collaboratively with an Agile DevSecOps team within a large environment consisting of several (on-prem and cloud-based) data models, interacting with government stakeholders and teaming partners to gather requirements and propose analytic solutions for the United States Citizenship and Immigration Service (USCIS) which is a part of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS). The Data Analyst will provide expertise in data collection, data analysis, data mapping, data profiling, data mining and data modeling. Collect relevant data and provide meaningful analytics and insights for incidents to resolve service requests.

What You Will Do:
• Inspect, cleanse, transform, and model data and address issues related to data completeness and quality.
• Conduct data profiling and predictive analysis using a variety of standard tools.
• Analyze and model structured data using advanced statistical methods and implement algorithms and software needed to perform analyses.
• Collaborate, coordinate, and interface with, and provide knowledgebase data, scripts, and procedures to, the USCIS Tier-I Service Desk for their responses to internal USCIS technical service requests.
• Provide scheduled (i.e., recurring) and unscheduled reports derived from data contained in Verification applications and generate reports and charts so that user stories, defects, and tasks and their status are available to government customer.
• Ability to analyze large, complex data sets or develop mathematical models to address various USCIS problems.
• Other duties as assigned.
Requirements
What We Need:
• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, or related field. In lieu of degree, will consider combination of training, certifications, and years of experience.
• Minimum four (4) years of experience in data science data mining, and/or data analysis.
• Experience with AWS (Amazon Web Services) and cloud-based systems.
• Experience in large-scale, high-performance enterprise big data application deployment and solution architecture on complex heterogeneous environments in AWS (Amazon Web Services).
• Possess strong architecture & design experience, including at least three (3) years of experience working with production enterprise applications in AWS (Amazon Web Services) that use large scale data elements.
• Experience with data visualization tools and methodologies.
• Experience with studying and interpreting large data sets in support of real-world operations.
• Candidates must possess effective communication skills and problem-solving abilities.
• Excellent customer skills are necessary as well as strong aptitude to learn and adapt to modern technologies.
• Ability to adapt well to diverse environments and work collaboratively in a dynamic team setting.
• Strong attention to detail and ability to prioritize work.
• Ability to be self-organized and motivated to work independently and as part of a team.
Certifications:
• AWS (Amazon Web Services) Certification (any)
Even Better:
