18974,702,EDI Integration Data Analyst,Versant Health,Anywhere,"EDI Integration Data Analyst

Who are we...

Versant Health is one of the nation’s leading administrators of managed vision care, serving millions of our clients’ members nationwide. We are driven by our mission to help members enjoy the wonders of sight through healthy eyes and vision.

As a Versant Health associate, you can enjoy a comprehensive Total Rewards package, which includes health and dental insurance, tuition reimbursement, 401(k) with company match, pet insurance, no-cost-to-you vision insurance for you and your qualified dependents. We are also invested in your success. There are many opportunities for advancement and development throughout all stages of your career with us.

See how you can make a difference with the support of strong leadership and a team environment.

See Everything, Be Anything™.

What are we looking for?

The role of the EDI Data Integration Data Analyst is to support the Versant Health EDI team in implementing and maintaining EDI X12 solutions and is responsible for assisting the ongoing operational excellence of the enterprise technology environment. This includes the development, design and maintenance of inbound data processing and outbound data processing using the tools within the business.

Where you will have an impact:
• Design, develop, implement, maintain, and analyze EDI solutions using IBM Transformation Extender Advanced (ITXA) and IBM GenTran tools
• Perform complex healthcare EDI X12 mapping activities related to standard formats including 837 inbound claims, 837 outbound encounters, 834 inbound enrollment and 835 remittance advice
• Migrate and convert existing maps from IBM GenTran to IBM ITXA technology base
• Integrate EDI X12 files with Optum Transaction Validation Manager (OTVM) for compliance checks and validation
• Develop SQL queries and stored procedures and automate integration with EDI X12 processes
• Develop EDI transaction processing and validation reporting solutions
• Participate in the full Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) of various components and systems that are required to be highly efficient, robust and scalable
• Design, develop and implement system-monitoring tools for all inbound and outbound data transmissions with customers and partners that adhere to organizational compliance standards
• Design, develop and implement automation tools and processes for all inbound, internal and outbound data transmissions with systems, customers and partners
• Identify, analyze and communicate recurring problems and develop remediation plans
• Review and enhance documentation for troubleshooting and resolution procedures for all levels of support
• Produce comprehensive documentation of all developed software & repositories
• Automation of routine processes with appropriate monitoring controls
• Support the development of technical EDI implementation documentation, technical reports, and payer companion guides
• Other duties as assigned

What’s necessary to do the job?
• Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of experience and education required in a Computer Science, Technology or Engineering program
• 5+ years’ experience in healthcare EDI
• 5+ years with XML data mapping and/or XSLT transformations with IBM ITXA and/or IBM GenTran
