Job Description

The largest coffeehouse in the world is looking to bring on a Data/Business Analyst. While in this role, you will be required to wear multiple hats. You must have a strong blend of analytical skills, project management, presentation skills, and the ability to develop strong and effective working relationships.

You will be working independently and/or as part of a cross-functional team engaged in the many moving pieces associated with today’s global supply chain challenges. To do this, you will utilize your data mining experience to seek out data and then establish the foundation of a data-driven mindset across the organization, via your expertise across the various tools needed to make it happen.

You must be able to build relationships with other organizations, to gain access to data they may own, then access and manipulate large amounts of data, extract key insights from the data, and then clearly and concisely communicate actionable recommendations based upon your insights. In many cases, you will participate in projects at various stages from idea or hypothesis generation to development and/or implementation. You will be expected to contribute as a data mining expert, data analytic specialist and data modeling guru, as tasks will varies across each of these skillsets.

Day-to-Day Responsibilities:
• Provide a consultative approach when working with stakeholders, communicating best practices to achieve each workstream's goals.
• This person will be flexing their program management skills, but all within the subject of data
• Working with lots of different product owners to tease out the questions that need to be answered
• Ensuring that data (all ambiguous forms of data) is thought of as early as possible, across all engagements, becoming a data champion
• Able to tease out actionable insights in an efficient manner
• Daily meetings, talking to people they don’t have existing relationships with

Must Haves:
• 3+ years experience as a Data Analyst or Business Analyst, specifically improving business processes and solving complex business problems
• Extensive experience querying in SQL
• Advanced user in Excel - building pivot tables, if statements, macros
• Experience building extensive dashboards and data models in Power BI (Tableau may be considered)
• Experience utilizing PowerQuery

Plusses:
• Experience customizing within SharePoint
• Ability to automate manual data
• ETL and Data Warehousing
• Predictive modeling and forecasting of demand
• Experience data mining & modeling within an enterprise-level corporation
• Experience with Oracle, specifically with the ability to execute SQL queries across multiple databases",2022-10-11,Contractor,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'excel', 'sharepoint', 'power_bi']"
19086,814,Sr. Quality Data Analyst - U.S. Remote,ACS Solutions,Anywhere,"ASAP Solutions, an ACS Company, is hiring for a Senior Quality Data Analyst for a client in the pharma industry. Position is 100% remote from the U.S. working ET Zone business ours. If interested, please submit your resume today for immediate consideration.

Senior Quality Data Analyst (Remote, 6 Month Contract...

This senior quality data analyst contractor, under Quality Data Analytics and Insights, is responsible for developing novel approaches to understand various types of data including but not limited to Quality Systems data (e.g. Deviations, CAPAs), operational data as part of the manufacturing lifecycle, and financial data (e.g. capital and operational expenses) using analytics and advanced modeling techniques.

In addition, the current role is expected to interact with key stakeholders (e.g. GxP subject matter experts (SMEs), business process owners (BPOs) and Quality Business Partners, etc.) to help design leading quality KPIs to enable enhanced performance.

The Senior Quality Data Analyst will report to the Senior Manager in Quality Data Analytics, a group that is focused on transforming our QMS through innovative, creative, and scalable approaches. This role will be an active member of a community of Data Scientists, that share ideas, information, techniques, and best practices across different functional areas.

Principal Responsibilities:
• Provide support in QMS data analytics and advanced programing to the Quality Data Analytics team and / or project stakeholders within and beyond the Central Quality System and Compliance (CQSC), which includes:
• Appropriately framing questions to be answered / issues facing the organization
• Choosing an analytical methodology that is situationally appropriate
• Understanding data correlations across databases and developing data mapping strategies for standardization
• Applying data cleansing and data QC techniques to leverage data integrity
• Visualize results / data with experience in tools such as R, Python, Power-BI, Tableau, Qlik Sense or equivalent
• Interrogating data with in-depth analyses and extracting right information to support metrics reporting
• Present and explain analysis and options
• Developing appropriate analysis models (including machine learning and / or artificial intelligence (AI) as appropriate) to conduct analysis, interpret results and determine potential risks, time impact, costs, and value
• Work with various stakeholders (e.g. quality process owners) to derive leading KPIs to drive performance
• Ability of utilizing advanced programing/coding to automate analysis/business pipelines is a must. Support ad-hoc data query requests
• Develop predictive / forecasting dashboards to support Management Reviews

Required Skills:
• 3-5 years of data science / analytics or related field experience, experience working in a pharmaceutical / life science company preferred.
• Must have strong R coding skills. Skillful data manipulation and visualization expertise through BI tools such as Power-BI, Qlik Sense, EXCEL Macros; advanced programing capabilities and coding techniques in R and experience with R-shiny
• Prior knowledge in Quality & Compliance and/or existing experiences in understanding quality management system (QMS) components considered a big PLUS
• Understanding of industry trends in analytics, database technologies, machine learning, and statistical analysis
• Comprehensive understanding and use of experience with quantitative principles, concepts, practices, and standards
• Ability to present data, ideas, and rationale clearly to a broad audience and strong communication skills

Education:

· BS with education/training from a strong analytical field such as statistics/biostatistics, information science, applied mathematics, quantitative engineering or computer science",2022-08-04,Contractor,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'excel', 'r', 'python', 'qlik']"
