19098,826,Junior Data Analyst,HyreCar,United States,"Join the Movement!

Are you interested in the mobility technology sector, but are also looking for an opportunity to make a direct impact on the lives of others? How about playing a critical role in redefining the meaning of vehicle ownership and helping some of the world’s largest companies empower individuals to become entrepreneurs in the growing gig economy...

About The Role

We are looking for a Junior Data Analyst to join our team to help the business make data-driven decisions by delivering meaningful insights from data and adding values to customers. If you are passionate about data with great analytical skills, it is your time to shine!.

What You'll Do
• Guide decision-makers with insights from data and analysis, by creating reports and dashboards to perform advanced analysis.
• Work closely with one or multiple functions of the business to support business growth as a go-to source.
• Help improve customer retention and experiences by identifying opportunities and areas for improvement.

What You'll Have
• 2+ years of experience working in the analytical field in a team environment within a business..
• Advanced proficiency in SQL and Tableau (or similar tools); advanced expertise in using databases and creating data visualizations.
• Expertise in data analysis from exploring and creating complex data sources, to data cleaning and processing, to performing statistical analysis and delivering results.
• Great communication skills to effectively partner and collaborate with team members and cross-functional teams on a frequent basis to understand requests and deliver results.
• Growth-minded with a passion to always accept new challenges, picking up new skills.
• Process driven with great work ethic and ability to make sure tasks are on track and delivered on time.
• Solid background in Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Economics, or related fields.

What Makes you Stand Out
• Ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines
• Ability to define and document business processes
• Experience in quality improvement, relational databases, SQL, and reporting tools
• Specialization in one or multiple areas within a business such as Marketing, Sales, Product, Operations, Finance, etc.
• Creative, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills
• Ability to work independently and as a team in a fast-paced environments

What You’ll Get
• Competitive salary and company stock grants
• Medical, Dental, and Vision benefits
• 401K
• Unlimited PTO and paid company holidays
• Professional training and education reimbursements

About HyreCar
• HyreCar is a carsharing marketplace that is powering the gig economy. Using the HyreCar platform, drivers who need vehicles for rideshare and other gig work are able to connect with owners and fleet operators who have vehicles to rent. By providing drivers with access to vehicles and owners with access to demand, HyreCar empowers both sides of the marketplace to participate in and benefit from the growing gig economy",2022-03-27,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql']"
