Our client is looking for someone aware of the outcomes/ results that their work led to, not just the work they did (# of hours saved, % improved, $ grown or saved, etc.) And not just in the resume, but you'd need to be able to speak to this in an interview.

Our client is also looking for a true data analyst, not a data scientist. We want the assigned job duties & responsibilities here to be understood in this way. -Chameleon Tech**

Job #2684: Chameleon Technologies is looking for an experienced and passionate product data analyst to help drive deeply understanding our customers and users, to provide our customers with higher value while engaging and delighting them. Ultimately achieving the business goal of increasing the profitability and retention of existing products and developing new product revenue.

Key responsibilities include:
• Help us build a quantitative and data-based decision making culture
• Help us understand our users, how we make product decisions, design, engineer and ship features. This includes creation of queries, reports, and data sets.
• Work closely with Engineering Leadership, Product Management, Software Engineers, UX, and Quality Assurance Engineers to plan and deliver on the product roadmap.
• Deep analysis of data for actionable insights. Data includes including usage from our 250k+ agent users across the US and Canada, millions of consumers, home listings, national and local economic/real estate data
• Perform segmentation to develop user personas that will be leveraged for further research and product decision-making
• Build reports and dashboards for specific efforts and for general ongoing use by product, engineering and other business groups
• Basically, make everyone smarter and help them make better decisions

RESPONSIBILITIES:
• Great communication and collaboration skills. Demonstrated ability to work on small, cross functional teams to achieve goals. Work collaboratively with product managers, creative designers, technical leads, and business executives. Ability to explain and write concisely and effectively.
• Understands Business, Research, and Analytics perspectives and needs.
• Thinks about issues broadly. Comfortable asking “Why” and saying “No”. Must be a critical thinker and problem solver while considering technical and business needs, requirements, and trade-offs. Able to calmly and objectively deal with challenges.
• Strong attention to detail, enjoys deep focused analysis of data and finding insights and trends. Possess a healthy skepticism of data and findings
• Ability to independently and quickly explore datasets and product functionality to sidestep dirty data, identify key data components and transform data for analysis to find key actionable insights
• Goal driven, self-motivated, and a strong advocate for outcomes. Focused on meaningful achievements and goals. Biased toward taking action.
• Must learn how our business works and be able to “speak business” and translate into analysis requirements
• Full analytical lifecycle work, performing all stages spanning:

o Inception

o Design and execute research and analysis plans with strong focus on achieving business/product goals

o Focused, heads down analysis of data to develop insights

o Working with product and engineering on details and issues

o Build dashboards, reports, processes, approaches, and toolsets that will be leveraged to accelerate all future efforts

QUALIFICATIONS:
• 3+ years of quantitative data experience, including pulling data and creating analyses independently
• Comfortable with start-up environment where tools and systems are being built out, and often a scrappy approach is needed
• Proven track record of performing high quality analysis and delivering helpful insights
• Strong technical skills and experience with advance SQL such as windowing functions and one other language/toolset such as PySpark (preferred), R, Scikit Learn, Tensor Flow/Keras Pandas, NumPy, SciPy, MatplotLib. Experience with Databricks or Spark is a strong plus.
• Demonstrated ability to work effectively both within a team and cross-group.
• Must demonstrate a strong passion for and commitment to results and quality.
• Excellent communication and collaboration skills, ability to make and influence decisions, and drive open discussions to a closure.
• BS with strong quantitative core or related field required. MS a strong plus",2022-05-13,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['pandas', 'pyspark', 'matplotlib', 'numpy', 'sql', 'spark', 'r']"
