19148,876,Data Analyst,"HeartLand, LLC",,"The Company:

We are a Private Equity backed strategy and progressive organization dedicated to building relationships and delivering exceptional service through leading commercial landscape firms across the US. We deliver the ordinary in extraordinary ways, by operating our business with a shared vision of excellence – combining best practices and the right tools for the job with ongoing... training and support. We acquire companies in attractive markets who share a common culture of excellence and success. Our landscape companies are the first choice for employees and clients in the markets they serve.
• Please note, this role will have hybrid capability, but must be local to Kansas City*

The Opportunity:

Are you looking for a data visualization opportunity with a growing company in the business services industry? In this dynamic role, you will wireframe and develop reports for leadership and operational teams across HeartLand’s business portfolio. The Data Analyst will be responsible for visualizing financial and business data by developing user-friendly reports, dashboards, and apps in the Microsoft Power Platform. If you are passionate about storytelling through data visualizations, are a self-starter, and enjoy challenges while interfacing with clients, this may be the opportunity for you. This is a direct hire position with an engaging office location in the heart of downtown Kansas City. If you’re interested in this opportunity and are excited about joining one of the fastest-growing companies in the U.S., please apply, even if you don’t meet all the Requirements below.

The Data Analyst will:
• Convert raw data into actionable business reports and dashboards in Power BI. The Data Analyst will define report needs while interfacing with clients, model and visualize data in Power BI, and implement the tools in the organization.
• Analyze and visualize financial, safety, operational, sales, weather, and other business data to track key performance indicators (KPIs), model predictions, and enable data-driven decisions.
• Automate and modernize manual reports using Power BI, Power Apps, and/or other analytical tools.
• Establish a Business Intelligence training program in the company Learning Management System for key users of the tools.
• Create scorecards in Power BI to track progress of business metrics.
• Optimize reports and dashboards for mobile devices.
• Participate in external software rollouts and internal software development. This may include communicating and collaborating with third parties to effectively facilitate new data connections or pipelines in Power BI for reporting.

If this sounds exciting to you, we are seeking a leader with these qualifications:
• 2+ years of experience deploying Power BI or similar business intelligence software such as Tableau.
• 1+ year of experience designing reports and developing interactive, real-time dashboards that enable more informed decision making.
• Bachelor’s degree in business intelligence, data analytics, data science, data warehousing, or similar field. Microsoft Certified Data Analyst preferred.
• Expertise in wireframing and modeling intuitive, engaging data visualizations using best practices for User Interface (UI) and User Experience (UX) elements.
• Comprehensive knowledge and experience developing DAX queries and measures, SQL scripts, performing ETL in Power Query, Power Automate, Power BI, Power BI Embedded, row-level security, data modeling, and creating user-friendly BI tools. Experience using Microsoft Azure and Power Apps is a plus.
• Effectively communicate with clients to implement advanced business intelligence solutions across business segments. Experience scripting using R and/or Python to develop custom visualizations in Power BI is a plus.
• Creative problem-solver, strong work-ethic, attention to detail, and passionate about data storytelling.

As HeartLand’s Data Analyst, you will enjoy:
• Competitive salary, plus a performance-based incentive program.
• Paid vacation and holidays.
• Full suite of health insurance – medical, dental, vision, etc.
• 401(k) with company match.
• Professional development opportunities.
• Exceptional company culture.
• Corporate HQ office on highest floor of downtown skyline with a brand-new rebuilt floorplan",2022-10-19,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'dax', 'power_bi', 'azure', 'python', 'sql', 'r']"
