19188,916,Data and Image Analyst Team Leader,Optelos,Anywhere,"Position Title: Data and Image Analyst Team Leader

Job Description: Lead a team of Data and Image Analysts to deliver accurate, robust data analysis through the Optelos software platform to our clients...
• ********

About Optelos

Optelos is the leading enterprise platform for enabling the digitalization of asset inspections. Utilizing patented image transformation technology, Optelos leverages Computer Vision AI and Machine Learning, advanced image modeling/visualization and enterprise system and workflow integrations to enable enterprises to fully operationalize their visual asset inspections. Optelos allows Enterprises to lower inspection costs while increasing safety, speed and accuracy of inspections in the oil/gas, process manufacturing, energy, telecom and virtually any other industry where asset inspections are required.

Job Description

We’re seeking a skilled candidate for the role of Data and Image Analyst Team Leader. The ideal candidate will have strong data management and communication skills with an analytical mindset. As a strong communicator and skilled data analyst, you will make it your mission to lead our team of image and data analysts in the production of high-quality deliverables to our clients.

You will help ensure existing staff of image and data analysts are producing accurate data deliverables including image labeling, image annotations, 3D point cloud measurements, and image selections per prescribed workflows through the Optelos software platform.

Roles Responsibilities
• Perform data analytics and data management assessments in accordance with Optelos SOPs, Training, and Image Analyst procedures
• Build and develop a team culture dedicated to the pursuit of accurate results.
• Lead your team to achieve outputs to meet the customer requirements.
• Develop talent within your team to build depth of management.
• Conduct Initial training of new Image Analysts (IAs).
• Conduct Quality Assurance of work performed by Image Analysts.
• Display exceptional attention to detail to draw annotations and take measurements on asset Point Clouds.
• Proficient in Excel to be able to track output and task assignments.
• Participate in Slack and other communications media to facilitate workflow coordination.
• Communicate status and be an active participant in a team environment.
• Be willing to learn from the mistakes of others, as well as share your own errors to improve the overall outcomes.

Location: Remote. Must be based in the continental US, Houston area highly preferred

