19206,934,Senior Data Intelligence Analyst,Quest Star Recruiting INC,Anywhere,"Senior Data Intelligence Analyst

Our client is seeking a Senior Data Analyst that supports client objectives by providing analysis and analytic consultation for email campaigns; this includes design and backend analytics and interpretation of findings to make data-based recommendations aligned with company and marketing goals. This position requires the ability to assess and evaluate the... performance of calls to action as driven by direct mail, email and other campaigns. The Senior Data Analyst, in addition to generating insights and test designs is responsible for collating and developing best practices for email marketing. And where applicable, the Senior Data Analyst, should have awareness of company key performance indicators (KPIs) and integrate them in report narratives for further perspective. This role also provides mentorship for other team analysts.

In addition to the Senior level role, there is a Manager of Data Intelligence position open as well. These positions are not backfill positions, but new positions out of growth!

ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS

Campaign Insight and Optimization
• Monitor and analyze campaign results across channels to understand the effectiveness of strategies and tactics for optimization – this includes ability to assess website actions and performance
• Provide regular cadence of reporting with insights and recommendations for improving campaign performance
• Perform data visualization to illustrate trends and data relationships
• Collaborate to brainstorm campaign optimization tactics to drive effective response

Campaign Testing
• Partner with stakeholders to develop email testing strategies and tactics; including all elements (i.e., creative, copy, segmentation, personalization, product, subject lines and messaging)
• Develop and manage weekly, monthly and quarterly reports that highlight key insights and strategic learnings

QUALIFICATIONS
• Bachelor’s Degree in Marketing, Statistics, Finance, Information Management or Business/Marketing related fields preferred
• Minimum 3-5 years of experience in the analysis and performance measurement of email campaigns preferred
