19256,984,Product Data Analyst,VerticalScope Inc.,Anywhere,"WHO WE ARE

VerticalScope (TSE: FORA) operates one of the 10 largest online community platforms in the US. Our platform includes over 1,000 websites and 100 million monthly visitors. Our mission is to enable the world to share expertise and discover knowledge on subjects they love. We operate at the intersection of community, content, and commerce; and believe in the power of enthusiasts to... inform and inspire.

THE ROLE

At VerticalScope, we are reimagining the future of online forums and are looking for a Product Data Analyst to join our team. As a Product Data Analyst, you will work closely with the Design, Engineering, and Product teams to iteratively define the team’s product direction via experimentation, prototyping, validation, and analysis. Your unique contribution will bring sound quantitative analysis and reasoning to team decisions.

With your expertise in data analysis, you will develop a strong and nuanced understanding of user needs and behaviors, and the impact of the features and experiences your team builds. You will help define the metrics that accurately measure team progress toward desired outcomes, and you will be a key contributor to setting the team’s quarterly goals and key results.

Ideally, you are curious about what data from multiple sources tells you about user behavior. You will perform exploratory quantitative research to help drive decisions. You will develop hypotheses and experiments that will validate them, and you bring a healthy skepticism to observations and assumptions. You will help your team make decisions based on solid quantitative processes and statistically significant outcomes. This is an exciting opportunity to join a mission-focused public company with a startup mentality.

WHAT YOU’LL DO
• Collaborate closely with Engineering, Design, and Product Management to understand user behaviors and funnels, discover and size new opportunities, and develop and run experiments to test how users adopt features and products
• Define and track metrics that monitor your team’s progress toward desired outcomes, and make sure these are accurately represented when the team is making decisions or communicating results outwardly
• Dive deep into the raw results of the experiments you helped design: analyze the data in a reproducible and well-documented way, set up dashboards and visualizations to describe the findings, facilitate discussions among your team to come up with recommended directions, and help communicate the findings
• Teach and share data analysis techniques and tools with others in order to empower people in other functions to participate in quantitative research. Encourage people to explore and question your team’s results and incorporate their feedback into future tools, analysis, and visualizations
• Other related responsibilities and ad hoc projects as negotiated and needed to meet the ongoing needs of the company

ABOUT YOU
• Strong background in quantitative analysis & statistical methods, including hypothesis testing, linear regression, confidence intervals, significance testing, sampling distributions, bias, probability functions
• Fluency in Python, R, or other data-oriented scripting languages
• Strong relational database skills (eg, MySQL, Postgres) including query optimization, intermediate functions such as case logic, joins to query large data sets from multiple sources

YOU’RE A GREAT FIT IF YOU ALSO HAVE
• 2+ years of experience as a Product Data Analyst or similar role
• Bachelor's Degree in Data Analytics, Data Engineering, Statistics or other related field
• Experience with A/B testing, experiment design, funnel optimization, cohort analysis
• Familiarity with user analytics platforms (Google Analytics, MixPanel, Amplitude, or similar)
• Awareness of PII and sensitive information, GDPR, data privacy, security, local and global compliance standards

LIFE AT VERTICALSCOPE

We believe that competitive benefits are an important investment in our people and culture. In addition to joining a passionate and collaborative team culture, your benefits and perks include:

Benefits:

- Full suite of health benefits (medical, dental, vision), including fertility options

- Retirement savings program and HSA/FSA programs

- Flexible working hours and unlimited vacation

- Parental leave top up pay

- Life insurance, long-term disability, AD&D

- Employee Stock Option Program (ESOP)

- Career development stipend

Perks:

- Employee referral bonus

- Employee discounts

- High-tech office space and remote work options

- Virtual social events

- Inclusive culture

EEO

Our company values diversity of thought and believes diverse teams make innovation possible. We work on complex, difficult problems with no linear or clear solutions. We believe that a diverse team can bring different perspectives and approaches, and whose experiences reflect the full set of clients we seek to serve. As such, VerticalScope is committed to a diverse representation among our employees.

If you require disability-related accommodation during the application, recruitment, and interview process, please let us know and we will work with you to make all possible adjustments to suit your needs",2022-12-14,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'postgres', 'r', 'mysql', 'gdpr']"
19257,985,Data Scientist,Integra Connect,Anywhere,"About Integra Connect:

We are a value-based, precision medicine company specializing in solutions for providers, patients, life science and EMS companies. With the emergence of value-based care, Integra Connect’s mission is to help specialty care providers succeed both clinically and financially. We accomplish this through a comprehensive offering of technology and services, unified by our... cloud-based platform, combined with unmatched industry expertise. We are looking for like-minded individuals committed to making a difference in healthcare. Come join our growing team!

Job Description:

The Data Scientist will be a key member on the Data Science and AI team within the precision oncology organization. The Data Science and AI team is responsible for developing innovative analytical solutions and products that benefit the entire enterprise. The team generates insights for providers, payers, pharma, and biotech by leveraging the available health care data from electronic medical records, healthcare claims, pharmacy claims and genomics data for oncology, urology, and other patients via the Integra precision oncology platform. Utilizing analytical, statistical, and programming skills to collect, analyze, and interpret large data sets, the Data Scientist will extract meaningful information from all patient data from our rapid growing network of healthcare practices. The solutions created by the Data Scientist will positively impact patient outcomes, while reducing cost of healthcare.

Come join one of the hottest companies that is revolutionizing healthcare!

Responsibilities:
• The Data Scientist will work with stakeholders throughout the organization to identify opportunities for leveraging company data to drive beneficial solutions to patients, providers, pharma, and payers.
• Apply predictive modeling to increase and optimize customer experiences, revenue generation, and other business outcomes. Mine for insights and analyze available healthcare data via the precision oncology platform to drive optimization and improvement of product development, marketing techniques and business strategies.
