19414,1142,Finance and Data Analyst,Florida Hospital Association,United States,"Position Summary

Reporting directly to the AVP of Hospital Finance & Data Analytics, the Finance and Data Analyst will be responsible for researching, and analyzing complex data sets associated with Hospitals across Florida. This position will assist prepare executive-level presentations and dashboards that showcase the Association’s leadership using data analytic tools and databases...

Essential Duties and Responsibilities
• Manage master hospital data, including creation, updates, and deletion
• Assist in collecting data for media inquiries, press releases, and interviews
• Create and share surveys from Survey Monkey or a similar data collection application
• Assist to import financial and hospital data onto SAP Analytics Cloud
• Assist to build dashboards with backend data models and daily support of data warehouse and troubleshooting data anomalies
• Process confidential data and information
• Research & gather data on current issues and focuses relating to hospital finance and policy issues
• Create and maintain rich interactive visualizations through data interpretation and analysis from multiple data sources
• Support initiatives for data integrity and normalization
• Create management-level dashboards, presentations, and reports
• Provide management with statistical findings and conclusions by analyzing trends in financial and hospital data
• Improve processes regarding data flow and quality to improve data accuracy, viability, quality assurance, validation, and value
• Educate end-users towards self-serve reporting models and dashboards
• Prepare, analyze and distribute hospital-specific data

Minimum Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree in a business-related field, preferably management information systems, statistics, or business
• Work experience as a data analyst or in a related field
• Ability to analyze existing tools and databases and provide recommendations on process improvement
• Demonstrated experience in handling data sets and analysis with data sets
• Ability to create visualizations with large data sets
• High-level written and verbal communication skills
• Ability to research highly complex healthcare topics

Physical Demands and Work Environment

The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the functions.
• While performing duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, sit, talk, or hear. The employee is occasionally required to walk; use hands to manipulate, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. The employee must frequently lift and/or move up to 10 pounds and occasionally lift and/or move up to 20 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, and the ability to adjust focus.

Note

This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee(s) incumbent in this position. Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform any other job-related duties requested by any person authorized to give instructions or assignments. All duties and responsibilities are essential functions and requirements and are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. To perform this job successfully, the incumbents will possess the skills, aptitudes, and abilities to perform each duty proficiently. Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health or safety of themselves or others. The requirements listed in this document are the minimum levels of knowledge, skills, or abilities. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an “at will” relationship",2022-01-27,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['sap']
19415,1143,Network Data Comm Analyst,Leidos,United States,"Description

Job Description...

Responsibilities

Supporting the SENS3 management team, the selected individual will be responsible for providing monitoring of customer network data, applications, and operational architecture through a 24/7 Operating Center environment to ensure Service Level Agreements are met, including

The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) has a continuing requirement for Secure Enterprise Network Systems, Services & Support (SENS3) for the continued operations, maintenance and evolution of the Homeland Secure Data Network (HSDN) and the Classified Local Area Network (C-LAN).
• Working with Telco providers, LECs, and customers in troubleshooting circuit and data issues
• Answering queries by telephone and e-mail in support of customer hardware, software, network, and telecommunication systems and execution of network procedures
• Provide operational support for all network components and conducts problem determinations, escalations and provides problem resolution

Primary Responsibilities
• Monitoring, installation, modification, testing and servicing of network equipment.
• Assisting and training lower level support employees
• Resolving networking/customer related concerns and issues
• Supporting engineers in troubleshooting network instability
• Communicating to customers and Leidos leadership of any impact to operational continuity
• Possessing a comprehensive understanding of network and device relationships
• Ability to effectively balance priorities and customer needs during periods of outages or moments of degradation of services

Basic Qualifications
• HS Diploma and 3+ years of experience working with networks and performing Network administration/Troubleshooting
• 3+ years of experience working with networks and performing Network Administration/Troubleshooting
• Must be familiar with Windows Systems administration tools and processes such as adding and removing user accounts and configuring / correcting profile issues
• Knowledge in coordinating problem resolution and working across IT functional areas
• Proven ability to manage multiple tasks/events simultaneously and deliver on time

Preferred Qualifications
• DHS Experience
• Networking Certification
• Microsoft Certification
• Security+
• CCENT
• Bachelors degree from an accredited college in a related discipline, or equivalent experience/combined education with 2 years of professional experience

Pay Range

Pay Range $50,700.00 - $78,000.00 - $105,300.00

