19441,1169,Senior Data Analyst,Walmart,"Bentonville, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

Lead the team in the 2 to 6 week planning horizon, managing the transit strategy and continuous improvement efforts. Collaborates with stakeholders to identify loss opportunities and priorities. Work closely with product and tech teams to conduct and/or coordinate discovery, design, and development efforts. Deploy basic project management to ensure objectives are met while leveraging technical problem solving and critical thinking to participate in and accelerate solution design and development.

About The Team

As a part of the Walmart Supply Chain organization, you will contribute to the success of our Transportation Network! Why? Because Sam Walton founded our company with the belief that the customer is #1. It is not just a belief, but our way of doing business. With our Supply Chain Team at the forefront of retail transformation you can work on a team that is ultimately focused on delighting our customers, saving them both time and money in unexpected ways. As the biggest player in the game, we trust our associates to innovate the future of Supply Chain!

Centrally controlling master data, optimization configuration and automation for our best-in-class transportation management systems is critical to enabling the business to meet customer demand efficiently and effectively. This team is at the crossroads of operations and technology to optimize transportation shipments for the best cost and service. To do this, the team manages data, works with operations for improvement, and drives changes and enhancements to system configurations and optimization parameters.

If you are motivated by complex, purposeful challenges, this role, with the world's largest retailer, could be the fit you have been looking for. Do you possess any of the following skills and experience?
• Transportation shipment optimization or operations research. Experience in Blue Yonder (JDA) TMS a plus!
• Collaborative analytics and project management to improve business operations.
• Data processing and data quality validation to ensure the best possible data inputs are driving systemic solutions.

You'll Make An Impact Through The Following Job Functions
• Advanced Analytics: In-depth investigation of key drivers of transportation dynamic optimization and data quality. Work with large, messy, disparate datasets and conduct ad hoc ""back of the envelope"" analyses to quickly inform critical business decisions. Develop data visualization to monitor and quantify the impact of changes and unique business challenges.
• Partnership and Collaboration: Engage with team members and cross-functional teams on a periodic basis and establish credibility. Analyze stakeholder needs and partner with them to share relevant information.
• Data and Data Processing: Leverage data analysis tools to explore and process complex data. Develop and test hypotheses, uses data to influence strategic work, builds and presents insights.
• Modeling: Develop and improve upon our methodology with A/B testing for continuous improvement of transportation shipment management. Execute on exploratory and scenario analysis to shape future changes and product improvements.
• Continuous Improvement: Seeks to implement ideas for process improvement for the group by leveraging lean manufacturing principles, time studies, and collaborative efforts with operations teams.

About You
• You understand transportation or supply chain, whether in Retail ecommerce environment or similar industries
• You are a problem solver and creative thinker: you think about finding the best solution that will work in days, instead of the perfect one that requires weeks.
• You learn and adapt quickly, and are excellent at working on multiple cross-functional projects concurrently
• You have excellent general modeling and data processing skills.
• You are customer-centric in spirit and in execution.

The above information has been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed in the role. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities and qualifications required of employees assigned to this job. The full Job Description can be made available as part of the hiring process.

Perks and Benefits

Beyond competitive pay, you can receive incentive awards for your performance. Other great perks include 401(k) match, stock purchase plan, paid maternity and parental leave, PTO, multiple health plans, and much more.

Who We Are

Join Walmart and your work could help over 275million global customers live better every week. Yes, we are the Fortune #1 company. But you'll quickly find we're a company who wants you to feel comfortable bringing your whole self to work. A career at Walmart is where the world's most complex challenges meet a kinder way of life. Our mission spreads far beyond the walls of our stores. Join us and you'll discover why we are a world leader in diversity and inclusion, sustainability, and community involvement. From day one, you'll be empowered and equipped to do the best work of your life.

Walmart, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer - By Choice. We believe we are best equipped to help our associates, customers and the communities we serve live better when we really know them. That means understanding, respecting and valuing diversity- unique styles, experiences, identities, ideas and opinions - while being inclusive of all people.

Minimum Qualifications...

Outlined below are the required minimum qualifications for this position. If none are listed, there are no minimum qualifications.

Option 1: Bachelor's degree in Business, Engineering, Statistics, Economics, Analytics, Mathematics, Arts, Finance or related field and 2 years' experience in data analysis, data science, statistics, or related field. Option 2: Master's degree in Business, Engineering, Statistics, Economics, Analytics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Information Technology or related field. Option 3: 4 years' experience in data analysis, data science, statistics, or related field.

Preferred Qualifications...

Outlined below are the optional preferred qualifications for this position. If none are listed, there are no preferred qualifications.

Data science, data analysis, statistics, or related field, Master's degree in Business, Computer Science, Engineering, Statistics, Economics, Analytics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Information Technology or related field, Related industry experience (for example, retail, merchandising, healthcare, eCommerce), Successful completion of assessments in data analysis and Business Intelligence tools and scripting languages (for example, SQL, Python, Spark, Scala, R, Power BI, or Tableau)

Primary Location...

311 NORTH WALTON BOULEVARD, BENTONVILLE, AR 72716, United States of America",2022-01-24,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'power_bi', 'scala', 'python', 'sql', 'spark', 'r']"
19443,1171,"Data Analyst, Strategic Operations","PLBY Group, Inc.",United States,"Playboy is now part of PLBY Group. What was once a legacy brand that catered to the male gaze has transformed into an innovative lifestyle and sexual wellness consumer goods and tech company with robust physical and digital assets. With 97% global recognition, the Playboy brand is universally known, yet is hardly recognizable today. Along with our other brands – Yandy, Lovers and Honey Birdette –... PLBY Group aims to be the place to celebrate pleasure for all, creative freedom, artistic expression, and sex positivity.

We have a strong global brand with the unique ability to play in both the physical and digital worlds across consumer products, experiences, NFT and blockchain, and gaming.

PLBY Group’s team is top-tier talent to continue the company’s dramatic transformation; and with a renewed commitment to women’s empowerment, inclusion, and social advocacy, today’s Playboy is committed to using its platforms to advance social change. From investing in employees through wellness, fertility, health, and parental benefits, to investing in women’s rights and LGBTQIIA+ organizations around the globe, there’s a wealth of impactful work being done.

Who We Seek:

PLBY Group is looking for a Data Analyst to join our strategic operations team. This person will work with brands across the entire omnichannel ecosystem – including Playboy, Yandy, Lovers, and Honey Birdette – to build highly visible reporting tools, extract actionable insights, and deliver recommendations to drive operational improvements. The ideal candidate’s success will not only be measured by the development or deployment of dashboards, but also by the business successfully using and embracing these measurements to make key decisions.

What You’ll Do:
• Effectively gather, organize and synthesize data relevant to consumer product operations activities: ask appropriate questions to understand hypotheses and requests, and illustrate and present complex data to senior leaders of the organization
• Maintain and validate data visualization tools or automated reports for business departments across C-Suite, Finance, Marketing, Merchandising, and Operations.
• Champion the build-out and management of Dashboards and Reports for the business built in modern data visualization tools
• Lead the continued development of a data warehouse architecture within BigQuery
• Use advanced data techniques to analyze user behavioral data to identify patterns and uncover opportunities and present to fellow team members.
• Partner with business leaders to build new tools that use data to solve complex business problems.
• Assist in the development of new data pipelines, data sanitization and/or consolidation
• Train co-workers on how to best utilize new or existing data tool sets
• Maintain a “data dictionary” that enforces a unified terminology across multiple businesses
• Contribute to the implementation of 3rd party systems reliant on operational, sales, and customer data, including merchandise planning tools, marketing automations, and sales reports
• Build statistical models to analyze KPI trends and provide insights to our stakeholders
• Develop and execute A/B testing testing modules, and provide actionable analysis to senior management
• Contribute to a positive working environment by building solid relationships with team members, proactively seeking guidance, clarification, and feedback

What You’ll Bring:
• Strong proficiency with SQL (BQ Standard SQL, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, PostreSQL).
• 4+ Years work experience as a Data Analyst or similar role
• Experience in Marketing, Merchandising or Ecommerce data analysis a plus
• Experience with data warehouse architecture and implementation through dbt
• Expertise in Google Analytics
• 3+ Years experience working with data visualization tools (Looker, Tableau or similar)
• Preferred experience with Salesforce data integrations and architecture
• Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel
• Strong proficiency in data languages such as LookML, Python, and SQL
• Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills
• Must have unrestricted access to work in the U.S.

What We Offer:
• Competitive salary
• Medical, dental, vision, life, and pet insurance for you and your family
• Generous paid parental leave and fertility benefits
• Access to coaching and legal support
• 401k+ matching
• Flexible Time Away
• Professional growth opportunities

This job description has been approved by the Company. Please note this job description is intended to convey information essential to understanding the scope of the job and the general nature, level, and expectation of the work to be performed. It is not designed to cover a complete list of qualifications, skills, efforts, duties and responsibilities or activities associated with this position, as they may change at any time, with or without notice.

PLBY Group is an equal-opportunity employer and is committed to providing a workplace free from harassment and discrimination. We are committed to recruiting, hiring, training and promoting qualified people of all backgrounds, and make all employment decisions without regard to any protected status. The right talent for us innately embodies our values. Come as you are",2022-04-03,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'python', 'sql', 'excel', 'bigquery', 'mysql']"
19446,1174,Associate Consultant - Data Analyst,"SES, Inc.","Lenexa, KS","SES is looking for a Data Analyst with a mastery of applying Excel and R software to analyze data. Additional experience with life cycle analysis projects and SimaPro software puts your resume on the top of the list. Strong technical writing and verbal communication skills are a must.

The ideal candidate has intellectual curiosity, loves to learn, and understands the balance between... sustainability and real-world needs. We are looking for a team player who enjoys participating in a company culture that is based on objective science and diverse thinking and problem-solving. The right person will thrive best working autonomously and enjoys the dynamic of a small but growing company.

Position Overview:
• Develop and maintain Excel-based spreadsheet calculators and tools for carbon intensity scoring, environmental reporting, greenhouse gas accounting, and carbon offset verification
• Life cycle analysis for agricultural commodities and packaged goods
• Survey response analysis
• Literature reviews and report development
• Develop and manage Microsoft Project databases for data collection, analysis, and project reporting
• Integrating data sets from multiple sources for analysis
• Data analysis and visualization
• Potential for cross-training in field work including environmental auditing and carbon offset verification

Minimum Qualifications
• B.S or M.S. degree in Statistics, Data Analysis, Agricultural Economics, Agronomy, Environmental and Climate Science, or similar.
• 2-5 years’ work experience conducting data analysis and technical writing.
• Strong technical writing and verbal communication skills
• Collaborative mindset and a “self-starter” – can-do attitude

What We Do

SES offers an opportunity to work on a diverse range of projects while addressing some of the most critical challenges today. Our company helps the agriculture industry and regulatory communities build resiliency for disease and other emergencies. We conduct climate consulting to help clients reduce their greenhouse gas and environmental impact, making their operations more sustainable. Our full suite of environmental consulting services also includes verification of carbon offsets and insets for voluntary and regulatory markets.

