Workstyle: Hybrid...

What Makes a Honda, Is Who Makes a Honda

Honda has a clear vision for the future, and it’s a joyful one. We are looking for individuals with the skills, courage, persistence, and dreams that will help us reach our future-focused goals.

At our core is innovation. Honda is constantly innovating and developing solutions to drive our business with record success. We strive to be a company which serves as a source of “power” that supports people around the world who are trying to do things based on their own initiative and that helps people expand their own potential. To this end, Honda strives to realize “the joy and freedom of mobility” by developing new technologies and an innovative approach to achieve a “zero environmental footprint.”

We are looking for qualified individuals with diverse backgrounds, experiences, continuous improvement values, and a strong work ethic to join our team.

If your goals and values align with Honda’s, we want you to join our team to Bring the Future!

About This Position

In collaboration with procurement associates (directly) and business stake holders (indirectly), the NAIP Procurement Data Analyst will mine existing indirect procurement ERP systems for relevant spend and transactional data, constructing that data into information, information into insights, and insights into the development of business strategies designed to improve company profitability and performance characteristics.

Responsibilities Include
• Ability to gather needed data, analysis, etc. to help shape procurement-based business strategies
• Clearly presents and articulates the value to digital transformation to all associates within the Division
• Collaborates with and forms effective relationships with internal (NAIP) and external (AHM-HDMA BU) stake holders in order to encourage broader use of analytics for business enablement.
• Leads the development of standard processes, procedures, and outputs for digital solutions. Ensures effective change management across the Division.
• Provides training for all NAIP associates on how to access and interprep analysis, reporting, models, etc. produced.
• Compiles Division and Department level KPI's on a monthly and quarterly basis. Presents to BU, Divison and Company leadership as required.
• Maintains SAP Analytics Cloud (SAC) ecosystem as the ""source of truth"" for indirect procurement data, information, dashboards, executive summaries, reporting, etc. Collaborates effectively with Finance-COE Department to optimize the SAC platform.
• Leads opportunities for process, system, and analytics improvements across the Division, which align with company needs and direction. Develops specific activities needed to achieve those strategic objectives and ensures their completion.
• Ensures data, analysis, reporting, models, etc. quality and integrity by working with internal/external stake holders to confirm/PDCA requirements received.

Required Work Experience

Who we are seeking:
• 3-5 Years of experience as a data analyst or business data analyst (or related field)
• 3-5 Years of experience building data/cost models, reporting dashboards and executive summaries, and segmentation models

Required Education
• Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain or Purchasing Field (or related field of study)

Desired Skills
• Strong Analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy
• Experience working with the SAP suite of products, including ECC, ARIBA, and Supplier Analytics Cloud (preferred)

Additional Position Factors
• Hybrid (office and remote) job work style
• 3-5 hours of overtime expected per week
• Limited inter-state travel (1-2 times per year)

At Honda, you will play a key role in our journey to become a company that society wants to exist now, and in the future. Your endless curiosity will drive innovation and your courageous spirit will challenge the status quo. We believe having a workforce made up of diverse thinkers and innovators makes us a better Honda. Respect for each other and respect for diversity each and every day drives our associates to contribute at the highest level and work effectively in a team environment. We make the dream of mobility a reality with our innovative and high-quality products. Together, we Bring the Future to our customers, associates, and communities. We are Honda!

