19458,1186,"Data Analyst, Legal",Safeway,"Pleasanton, CA","About The Company

Albertsons Companies is at the forefront of the revolution in retail. With a fixation on innovation and building culture, our team is rallying our company around a unique vision: forging a retail winner that is admired for national strength, deep roots in the communities we serve, and a team that has passion for food and delivering great service...

Albertsons is one of the largest retail employers, providing approximately 300,000 jobs across 2,200 stores, 22 distribution centers, 20 food and beverage plants and various support offices. We operate in 34 states and the District of Columbia under the Albertsons banner, as well as Safeway, Tom Thumb, Jewel Osco, Shaw’s and many more recognizable names.

Albertsons Companies recently rolled out our Presence with a Purpose work model. Placing a premium on adaptability, safety and family well-being, Presence with a Purpose will help us build a hybrid work environment between remote work and office time. A one-size-fits-all approach does not apply to everyone, and teams are allowed to make decisions that are best for them.

What You Will Be Doing

The Data & Insights Center of Excellence (COE) is a new, exciting group created to accelerate the transformation of Albertsons into a data-driven enterprise. We leverage our rich data around the customer, our stores, and the marketplace to create new data products, analytic tools and capabilities supporting company goal to delight our customers and associates with rich and relevant experiences, in-store and digitally.

The Data Analyst, Legal will be responsible for doing in-depth analysis and compilation of data sets needed to support the Legal team as they respond to various case needs. Data sets will span across multiple business domains such as Customer, Product, Marketing, Finance, HR, etc.

The position will be based in Pleasanton, California and a secondary location of Phoenix, Arizona may be considered.

Main Responsibilities
• Developing in-depth subject matter expertise in datasets requested by Legal teams
• Running complex SQL queries and procedures and compiling results
• Good understanding of database management and concepts
• Applying data quality principles to day-to-day analyses
• Summarize findings for Legal team and business stakeholders
• Lead meetings to resolve data issues/challenges by factoring input from diverse stakeholders

A copy of the full job description can be made available to you.

What We Are Searching For
• 5+ years of experience in data analysis, data quality, business intelligence and reporting or data-related issue management and remediation efforts
• Excellent SQL and Data analysis skills
• Experience in data privacy, legal or compliance needs would be a plus
• Knowledge of data classification, cataloging, lineage, data quality techniques preferred
• Excellent written, verbal communication and presentation skills with ability to effectively communicate with senior management
• Retail / Grocery / Ecommerce would be a plus

What it is like at Albertsons?

Albertsons Culture Principles

Compassion: We always treat each other with kindness and respect

Team: We always support and recognize each other

Inclusive: We always value everyone’s perspective

Learning: We always strive to grow and develop ourselves and others

Competitive: We always act with integrity to win over the customer

Ownership: We always take actions to drive our success",2022-02-26,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['sql']
