19508,1236,Lead Data and Insights Analyst,Goodway Group,Anywhere,"Who We Are

Goodway Group is a an independent and remote-first media and marketing services firm with a 90+ year history and a start-up feel. With leading data-driven and technology-enabled digital media and marketing services firm with teams in the U.S. and the UK, our diverse team of digital strategists, media practitioners, technologists and data scientists have won the most prestigious awards... for innovative marketing technology, impactful work and inclusive remote-first places to work including being honored as a multiyear winner in Ad Age Best Places to Work, Ad Exchanger's Best Use of Technology by an Agency Award and two MarTech Breakthrough Awards and a certified service partner to The Trade Desk.

We are looking for a Lead Data Analyst, preferably with hands-on experience working on a wide range of data and insights problems in ad-tech, including ranging from lift measurement to conversion attribution.

The ideal candidate should also show technical acumen and chops with tools of the trade, including (and not limited to) SQL, Python, and R.

What You’ll Do

The Lead Data Insights Analyst role is a leading member of the Analytics and Data Science team at Goodway. This team utilizes advanced tools and innovative techniques to maximize advertising results for our clients and demonstrate thought leadership within the digital advertising industry. You will be at the center of data analysis and modeling at the forefront of the ad-tech space and be taking and communicating the learnings and insights that matter to clients and stakeholders.

Although not strictly required, an ideal candidate will have hands-on experience working on a wide range of data and insights problems in ad-tech, including ranging from lift measurement to conversion attribution. The ideal candidate should also show the technical acumen and chops with tools of the trade, including (and not limited to) SQL, Python, and R.

Analytics and Insights
• Lead various types of statistical analyses to drive actionable client and internal business insights in paid media planning, execution, and measurement
• Drives actionable and innovative analytical solutions to key prospect/client and internal business questions by utilizing various datasets and statistical techniques
• Provides a combination of thought-leadership and hands-on implementation for bespoke client solutions (e.g., measurement) utilizing Goodway and vendor platform capabilities
• Works closely with key internal stakeholders as well as external partners and vendors to enhance the application of both newly sourced and existing raw / aggregated data across all channels and mediums
• Collaborates with Goodway Product and Tech. leaders to identify, understand and resolve technical challenges related to data ingestion, data access, and data accuracy
• Leads by example: demonstrates hands-on functional knowledge to develop/mentor new analysts.
• Facilitates and provides both individual and team industry and technology learning opportunities
• Actively mentors Data Analysts on Analytics and Account teams to drive team members’ career / professional development.

Client Engagements
• Be an active contributor in strategic client acquisition and retention opportunities in all aspects of the client life-cycle ranging from initial prospect RFP response to existing client QBR discussions
• Manage and resolve ambiguous/uncertain client demands in a positive and forward-looking manner
• Be the go-to expert for client teams to call on for client analytics and insights opportunities.

Expertise and Evangelize
• Be the go-to experts at Goodway Group for business intelligence and analytics-related topics.
• Stay at the forefront of digital marketing and advertising technology and its relevance in data analysis; shares learnings with immediate and account teams as appropriate.
• Align with the Learning and Development (L&D) team as appropriate to broaden organizational analytics and insights competency via targeted training and learning modules

You’ll Be Successful Because You Are

Knowledgeable: Undergraduate degree or equivalent training in computer science, math, statistics, or a similar technical subject area is required
• Seasoned / Experienced:
• Previous analytics-focused experience (4-7+ years minimum) is required
• Previous experience in digital advertising or ad-tech industry is preferred
• Previous client-side (advertiser) and/or agency - engagement experience is preferred
• Working knowledge of SQL is required; experience with or a desire to learn Python and comfort operating in a Linux OS environment is preferred
• Familiarity and experience with business intelligence tools (e.g., Tableau, Looker) is required
• Familiarity with big-data tools such as Hadoop, Hive, Athena, or Qubole is required
• Exposure to modern software engineering processes (e.g., version control, automated testing) is preferred
• Right Radio Frequency: You can effectively listen and communicate to a variety of audiences. The ability to communicate the right “radio frequency” with precision and concision is critical
• Agile: You know how to get things done both through formal and informal channels. You understand Goodway’s culture, including the origin and reasoning behind key policies, practices, and procedures
• Multi-Lensed: You can look at a piece of information or problem through different lenses

#usremote

Check us out at www.goodwaygroup.com to learn more!

If you identify as a female candidate, and feel you can do this role even if there are a few things perhaps you've not done, please apply anyway! Goodway Group is 70% Female! We realize that men tend to apply for jobs when they can meet around 60% of the requirements for the role, where women tend to only apply when they know they meet 100% of the requirements.

