19554,1282,Senior Healthcare Data Analyst / Engineer,Empassion Health,Anywhere,"Empassion is Complete Care for patients with Advanced Illness. We manage unique care programs, and the people that power them, to deliver more good days.

Role & Team...

Empassion is seeking an entrepreneurial data analyst or analytics engineer to architect, build, and own analytics that deliver actionable data to healthcare providers and our company leadership. This high-impact role will serve as a subject matter expert on healthcare claims data and drive the implementation of a custom Medicare risk adjustment model using a combination of proprietary and open source SQL code. This role is critical in enabling care teams to drive targeted, high quality care for seriously ill patients and reports directly to the VP of Data & Analytics.

The Data & Analytics team is a rapidly growing, high-impact, high-visibility team that works cross-functionally across the entire organization. We are creating a robust, flexible, and modern data platform that is core to delivering the company’s technology and service capabilities. We pride ourselves on delivering accurate, timely, and actionable data to our downstream users. We hold ourselves to a high standard that respects the impact our data and analytics can have on a patient’s course of care.

This is a rare opportunity to support the buildout of the Empassion’s technology platform, and to be part of a passionate, skilled, and committed team working together to realize our important vision.

Responsibilities
• Learn the needs of leadership, operations, and care teams, then leverage technical expertise to translate these needs into requirements
• Calculate traditional and novel healthcare metrics from claims data (HCCs/RAF, readmit rates, PMPM cost, etc.) using SQL
• Evaluate opportunities to leverage third-party and open source solutions for common healthcare analytics challenges
• Act as a healthcare data SME on a rapidly growing Data & Analytics team
• Develop reports and dashboards that enable data-driven decision making by the business operations and care teams, with a focus on cost, utilization, and care improvement opportunities
• Create documentation and training materials for technical and non-technical users of our data products

Requirements
• 2+ years experience in healthcare analytics, delivering actionable insights from big data analytics environments to Clinical and Operations teams
• Familiarity with healthcare data and standards (Claims, Eligibility, Labs, HL7/FHIR)
• Strong SQL skills
• Experience with BI / reporting tools (Looker, Tableau, etc.)
• Excitement about working in a fast-moving startup environment
• Excellent communication abilities around highly technical data topics and the ability to work with a diverse set of technical and non-technical audiences (peers, engineers, operations, external customers)

Nice to Have
• Proficiency with Looker (administration, reports, dashboards)
• Experience with dbt and templated SQL
• Experience with statistical analysis software (Python/pandas, R, etc.)

Company Background

Beneficiaries with serious illness (also called “advanced illness”) account for 4 percent of the Medicare population but 25 percent of its costs. Serious illness refers to late-stage chronic illness, when one or more conditions become serious enough that general health and function decline and treatments begin to lose their impact – a state that progresses to the end of life.

As many have unfortunately experienced, loved ones with serious illness often undergo unwanted, avoidable, and costly hospitalizations near the end of life, resulting in a poor patient experience, low quality of care and high costs. Empassion Health is a Management Services Organization (MSO) that enables serious illness providers to improve quality of care and manage rising costs through value-based models. The business will improve upon earlier generations of seriously ill platforms by enabling increased access and alignment, to deliver superior outcomes for patients and their communities, the healthcare system, and society. To realize this mission, we are building a world-class team of mission-driven, passionate, and committed team members",2022-08-21,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'sql', 'r']"
19555,1283,Senior Data Analyst,Allied Benefit Systems,Anywhere,"Description

Would you like to be part of a growing national healthcare solutions company? Are you looking to positively affect thousands of lives each day via health benefits? Do you have experience storytelling using data by use of BI tools...

We are hiring for a Senior Data Analyst to join our team.

Who We Are

Allied is a national healthcare solutions company that supports healthy workplace cultures.

What We Do

We are problem-solvers, innovators, and collaborators. Our purpose is to work with employers to take care of their employees and their families every day – and it all starts with the Allied family. 

What’s in it for you?

Allied supports an inclusive culture focused on developing employees to succeed, innovate & impact the community.

Here’s How We Do It

Training and Development: Allied offers tailored learning and development curriculums for all employees and a Learning Management Database with thousands of courses for professional and personal development.

Career Mobility: Growth opportunities are endless at Allied. In 2021 alone, one in five employees had a job change. 75% of these job changes were promotions!

Employee Engagement: We pride ourselves on employee engagement! With our recognition program, employees recognize their colleagues monthly or donate to charities with cash rewards. Allied has a dedicated committee planning monthly engagement activities to create endless opportunities to get to know your peers and destress in this new remote world.

Employee Feedback: We regularly survey our employees throughout the year to seek continuous feedback, ideas and suggestions on new initiatives.

Community Outreach: We have dedicated committees focused on fundraising efforts supporting our employees and their families, furthering education goals and providing funds for charitable organizations outside of Allied.

What will you be doing?

The Senior Data Analyst role establishes and conducts auditing, creation of medium to complex reports and reporting tools including regular analysis, data models, dashboards, hosts presentations and provides summaries to leadership regularly. This position is responsible for examining, auditing, integration, management, and reporting of all data essential to contact center operations. This position also facilitates and implements new data connections and standard data extracts.

Essential Functions
• Establishes auditing, analysis and data reconciliation procedures
• Writes and revises quality assurance procedures and processes. Conducts internal daily audits of all reports and data.
• Creates custom reports through the use of Power BI, SQL server queries, excel and access.
• Develops MS Power tools, SharePoint sites, etc.
• Reformats data reports into loadable formats
• Reviews and addresses eligibility file data errors with appropriate parties/vendors
• Examines, reconciles, and manages vendor reporting
• Reports audit and trend findings and develops recommendations for remediation of any identified findings
• Develops recommendations for improvements to existing systems and/or processes
• Participates in reviewing data for departmental and divisional projects as assigned
• Oversees the daily management of data file processes
• Acts as Allied’s internal and external point of contact for all data file related items
