19567,1295,"Lead, HR Data Analyst (People Analytics)",Paylocity,Anywhere,"Job Type

Full-time...

Description

Paylocity is a cloud-based software company that creates customized HR solutions for small to mid-sized organizations. Our workplace enhances communication and enables employees to connect, collaborate, and create from anywhere. Our award-winning culture ensures everyone has a voice and feels truly welcome. Join Paylocity as we shape the future of technology and the workplace!

We give our employees what they need to succeed, including great benefits and perks! We offer medical, dental, vision, life, disability, and a 401(k) match, as well as perks that support you, your family, and your finances. And if it’s career development you desire, we provide that, too! At Paylocity, people matter most and have always been at the heart of our business.

When you feel like you belong, work is no longer work – it's personal. At Paylocity, we believe better employees lead to better companies. Workplaces and cultures that care will build the future, and at Paylocity, we’re doing just that. Join us as we change the future and transform your career!

There are jobs and then there are careers. Since 1997, Paylocity has been hiring talented people, giving them big challenges, and providing the right resources to help them succeed. Our award-winning culture ensures all employees feel truly welcome, appreciated, and free to be themselves. While other companies talk about it, we make it happen. Join Paylocity and launch your career!

Position Overview

You will report to the Director of People Analytics & Insights to build and expand the reach and role of people data among leaders and stakeholders at Paylocity. As a People Analytics Lead, HR Data Analyst you will be an integral part of the People Analytics team to deliver solutions that empower People leaders to integrate data into their daily workflow to drive business outcomes. You will have the opportunity to build data solutions that leverage your expertise on how data, when actioned, helps improve people strategy and the employee experience including diversity and inclusion, talent acquisition, retention, and talent development.

The Lead HR Data Analyst is responsible for researching and presenting assigned data, developing ad hoc reports or metrics, meeting with HR Leaders and stakeholders to address issues and offer recommendations, produce insights, troubleshoot operating models, measure the effectiveness of people initiatives, and ensure full compliance with data privacy guidelines.

Responsibilities

The below represents some of the primary responsibilities of the position. Other duties may be assigned as needed.
• Data Management: Data accuracy is an integral part of scaling People Analytics capabilities and solutions. You will be working with employee data every day. Whether it is demographic information, compensation, performance data, the ability to perform exploratory data analysis to assess the overall quality of the data is essential for this role. Ensure high quality, accurate, insightful data is produced and maintained, partnering with HR peer teams to identify process controls and data integrity. Advises peers on how the People Analytics team consumes data. Drives a standardization philosophy to help democratize knowledge of how people data is consumed for analytics and solutions.
• Data Asset Migration to BI: A key component of the role in the first 9 months will be partnering with team members to assess, scope and scale the migration of data assets that aligns with the People Analytics Master Data Model methodology. You should have a sound understanding of ETL (Extract, Transfer, Load) methodologies, data modelling best practices including an understanding of cardinality and star schema as well as the ability to write complex measures that incorporate time-intelligence in a BI platform. You will be expected to have a complete deployment phase plan; create, and validate, deploy, support, and monitor all data assets. The preferred tool is Power BI.
• Reporting: Business leaders rely on the People Analytics team to provide employee information to support their decision-making. You will convert data into insights through standard reporting and ad-hoc analysis. Accurately produce all required HR data reports, displayed in appropriate formats, in agreed timeframes. Partners with different HR functions to provide process improvements and tools that drive data accuracy and efficiencies to improve reporting. Work closely with the business to create new reports and dashboards; and develop processes for program evaluation and reporting.
• Process Improvement: Advise on best practices to scale People Analytics in close partnership with the Director of People Analytics. Partner with team members to identify opportunities and make recommendations to migrate solutions to models and methodologies that will effectively reduce time to refresh as well as improve the overall health of production ready solutions.
• Project Coordination: Across HR, new capabilities and resources are constantly being added. To broaden your exposure to multiple parts of HR, on some projects you will be part of the launch team to get to know the area of HR and key stakeholders in the business.
• Day-to-day Support: As a fast-growing organization, things come up that are not planned. Everyone in HR approaches work with a low ego and ‘How-can-I-help?’ spirit.

Requirements
• Bachelor’s degree is required in Industrial & Organizational Psychology, Social Psychology, Statistics/Mathematics, Business, Human Resources/Organizational Behavior or a related field with 3+ years of experience providing human capital analytics and insights services at an enterprise level.
• Working knowledge of managing and analyzing structured and unstructured data using at least 2-3 of the following tools such as tools; R, SQL, Power-BI, and Excel to drive analytics
• Preferred to have at least 5-7 years of related experience in an HR or data processing environment
• Previous experience working within an HR function, HRIS systems, possess an understanding of HR processes and administration
• Demonstrated ability to handle multiple tasks effectively, prioritize requests, and adapt well to change
• Requires strong attention to detail, management of deadlines, and accuracy of processing data while working in a fast-paced environment
• Expert knowledge of Microsoft Office, especially Excel
• Detail-oriented mindset resulting in high-quality work and a strong, proactive follow-through.
• Collaborative problem-solving approach with the ability to work individually and as a team
• Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to build “trust” with internal and external stakeholders
• Ability to gather, analyze, interpret, and translate data into meaningful insights
• Delivering data, information, and insights in a secure manner
• Strong organization and time management skills
• Ability to work in a fast-paced, high-volume environment
• Ability to effectively manage tasks and meet deadlines

Paylocity is an equal opportunity employer.

Paylocity is committed to the full inclusion of all individuals. We comply with federal and state disability laws and make reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the job application or interview process, please contact accessibility@paylocity.com.

This role can be performed from any office in the US. The pay range for this position is $87,366 - $120,000/year; however, base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. This position is eligible for an annual bonus and restricted stock unit grant based on individual performance in addition to a full range of benefits outlined here. Base pay information is based on market location. Applicants should apply via www.paylocity.com/careers.

This job description has been written to provide an accurate reflection of the current job and to include the general nature of work performed. It is not designed to contain a comprehensive detailed inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of the employees assigned to the job. Management reserves the right to revise the job or require that other or different tasks be performed when circumstances change",2022-11-19,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'sql', 'excel', 'r']"
19568,1296,Pricing and Contract Data Analyst,SHI International Corp.,Anywhere,"Job Summary

Reporting to the Manager Pricing and Contract Analytics, this position provides strong analytical support to the public sector team around pricing reports, membership list analysis, and contract analysis. This will primarily be achieved by gathering, transforming, and integrating multiple data sets to attain analytics that drive action. This position will help perform quantitative... analysis to model impact to profitability and growth based on various data sets.

As the Pricing and Contract Data Analyst for Public Sector support, you will be responsible for designing, managing, and implementing regular monthly reporting and analysis. In this role, you will collaborate with the Capture & Development team, Contracting, and Sales teams to perform both routine and ad hoc analysis to gain insights. Additionally, you will conduct market research to present in-depth analysis in a clear, concise, and comprehensible fashion. This position will encompass a combination of technical and analytical skills to assist with regular monthly reporting requirements and additional special projects.

About Us

Founded in 1989, SHI International Corp. is a $12 billion global provider of IT solutions and services, and currently has over 5,000 dedicated employees worldwide.

To learn more about SHI International Corp, visit our website: www.shi.com/careers

What SHI Can Offer:
• World Class Facility includes on site gyms and cafeterias
• Ongoing opportunities for personal and professional growth and development due to our strong promote from within philosophy
• Work in an up-beat, creative, and fun environment
• Benefits including medical, vision, dental, 401K, and flexible spending

Responsibilities

Include, but are not limited to:
• Organize and clean data that impacts contract alignment
• Analyze contract usage to help improve profitability
• Assist in analyzing, tracking, and reporting on contract usage
• Create reports of regular and ad hoc results on departmental requests
• Troubleshoot problems and research cause of variances between various data sets
• Interpret data and recommend appropriate course of action
• Develop systems and procedures to enhance data tracking as needed
• Maintain data sets and membership lists related to contract usage and eligibility
• Help maintain compliance with applicable contracts and associated sets of data
• Operate with direct guidance on work assignments which are generally straightforward and of moderate complexity
• Work closely with Contracts Specialists and Capture Manager to understand data needs and organize accordingly

Qualifications
• Bachelor's Degree in Finance, Math, Business, or relevant field
• At least 1 year of experience in a Sales or Support role
• Proven experience using Microsoft Excel to analyze data
• Understanding of how to use CRM

Required Skills
• Exemplary analytical and problem-solving skills
• Excellent organizational, written, and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate both internally and externally
• Excellent project management and execution skills, including clear methods for tracking action items, consistently following up with involved parties, and leading executive briefings on opportunities and progress
• Ability to manage and report on tasks
• Strong ability to multitask and prioritize assignments
• Ability to work in a dynamic, results driven and fast-paced culture

Unique Requirements
• Extended hours are required to complete some special projects

Additional Information
• FLSA Status: Exempt

