• Analyze and transform data sets from multiple file and database formats to optimize dashboard flexibility and performance.
• Established best practices for the creation of dynamic and effective dashboards across departments.

This Role is a Good Fit if You
• Have a Bachelor’s degree in Business, Business Analytics, Statistics, or Information Management, preferred
• 5+ years of progressive Business Intelligence or analytics experience
• Advanced experience in SQL and other comparable data analytics tools
• Experience analyzing data used in forecasting and performance guarantee management is a plus
• Proficient in Microsoft Office with a strong knowledge of PowerPoint, SharePoint, Access, Excel (including the use of formulas, vlookups, pivot tables, macros, etc.)
• Experience in the healthcare industry is a plus

The Perks
