19584,1312,"Sr. Analyst, Data Intelligence and Business Insights",Motorola Solutions,Anywhere,"Company Overview

At Motorola Solutions, we believe that everything starts with safety. It’s the constant that empowers people to confidently move forward. It can fill a flight or sell out a stadium. It can care for a patient or graduate a class...

As a global leader in public safety and enterprise security, we create and connect the technologies that help to keep people safe where they live, learn, work and play. Our integrated technology ecosystem unifies critical communications, video security and access control, and command center software, enabling collaboration in more powerful ways.

At Motorola Solutions, we’re ushering in a new era in public safety and security. Bring your passion, potential and talents to a career that matters.

Department Overview

Motorola Solution's Video Division company, is defining the future of the security industry through innovative end-to-end-solutions. We’re changing the landscape of the surveillance industry through advanced award-winning AI based surveillance systems. Artificial Intelligence is transforming the world and our team is advancing the field as it applies to the intersection of computer vision and real-time video analysis. We are proud to be industry leaders in video analytics with features such as Appearance Search and Unusual Motion Detection along with our innovative cloud service platform. Unlike a startup, we’re part of a company that has the resources to do great things now.

Job Description

Primary Function:

The Sr. Analyst, Data Intelligence and Business Insights will be responsible for leading the implementation and ongoing management of tools and solutions that enhance the data and analytics made available to the Motorola Solutions Sales teams worldwide. He/she will be responsible for providing primary support to cross functional teams and will work in a consultative role with Senior Sales Management. Work will require successful implementation of Data Integrity processes and tools, and integration of analysis results into the flow of work, that leverage across relevant functions including Sales Operations, Finance and Forecasting. The position requires working with internal constituencies, such as sales, Customer Success and other analytics teams as well as external service providers.

Responsibilities:
• Develop and maintain reporting on performance metrics for senior sales management within Tableau and/or other tools
• Provide analysis, insights, and strategic recommendations to support ongoing business and the financial planning process
• Translate complex, technical information into simple, engaging visuals that a less-technical audience will easily understand and use for actionable insights
• Communicate project status, risks, dependencies, and roadblocks for technical and business audiences
• Provide input on topics like data access, data ingestion, data transformation, database design and implementation
• Develop business-oriented presentations with appropriate level to detail to have strategic discussions with cross-functional teams

Skills:
• Proficiency in SQL and can independently mine data to translate business data needs into creative and actionable visualizations. Python coding a plus
• Expertise is the design and development of Tableau dashboards, reports and front-end visualizations and analysis with ability to tell stories with data
• Experience with various types of data repositories (e.g., data warehouses, data lakes, data marts), master data management, and ETL/integration
• Technical aptitude with Google Suite, Salesforce and broad awareness of other analytical tools
• Experience in SaaS sales industry or a subscription based sales a plus

Qualifications:
• Undergraduate Degree in Business, Computer Science, Statistics, Economics, or a related field
• 5+ years work experience in Business Insights, Sales Operations, or Data Management
• 3+ years of experience with Tableau, Salesforce, Power BI or related tool
• 3+ years of experience in visual reporting development, including hands-on development of analytics dashboards and working with complex data sets

Basic Requirements
• Bachelor Degree and 5+ years experience of Business Insights, Sales Operations, or Data Management analysis/reporting

Vaccine Requirement

Motorola Solutions has implemented a voluntary COVID-19 vaccination policy. We strongly encourage all employees to be fully vaccinated. Additionally, certain local governments or Motorola Solutions' customers may have vaccine requirements that apply to some of our employees. These employees are required to submit proof of vaccination to Motorola Solutions and maintain compliance with these requirements.

Travel Requirements

10-25%

Relocation Provided

None

Position Type

Experienced

Referral Payment Plan

Yes

Our U.S. Benefits include:
• Incentive Bonus Plans
• Medical, Dental, Vision benefits effective Day 1
• 401K with Company Match and Day 1 vesting
• 9 Paid Holidays
• Generous Paid Time Off Packages
• Employee Stock Purchase Plan
• Paid Parental & Family Leave
• and more!

EEO Statement

Motorola Solutions is an Equal Opportunity Employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran's status, or, any other protected characteristic",2022-07-25,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'power_bi', 'python', 'sql']"
19585,1313,Reporting Data Analyst,Exos,Anywhere,"WHO WE ARE

Exos provides certified coaches, therapists, dieticians, psychologists, and instructors for over 400 locations globally, ranging from corporate sites and community programs to military and athlete training centers. By leveraging science, technology and engaging programming, we impact hundreds of thousands of people, from professional athletes and military operations, to employees at... Fortune 100 companies. The launch of our new suite of digital products has allowed us to expand our reach even further, bringing our coaches and methodology to the virtual and hybrid employee, and truly enabling us to meet each performer where they are.

THE ROLE

The Reporting Data Analyst on the Exos Service Delivery team will be a data specialist who contributes to operational improvement and efficiency by gathering and analyzing data, preparing reports, and introducing process improvements throughout the reporting process for a large, global client.

The ideal candidate has excellent analytical and technical skills, as well as a keen ability to determine specifications and standards for business reporting and maintaining data integrity. The Reporting Data Analyst will leverage their knowledge, problem solving skills, and passion about analytics to inform the evolution of our digital and on-site experiences and keep our operations running as efficiently as possible.

JOB RESPONSIBILITIES
• Report: Provide regular reporting on our operational health and provide program recommendations that showcase impact and efficiency of our global operations.
• Analyze: Use critical thinking to conduct comprehensive analysis of the data, surface actionable insights, and design powerful visualizations that help communicate information in a meaningful way.
• Communicate: Effectively tailor both written and verbal communication style and adapt approach for business partners, client liaisons, and EXOS teams to maximize effectiveness; ability to clearly convey complicated concepts and strategies to others.
• Collaborate: Work with executive stakeholders and program management to identify and create metrics and KPIs that enable leaders to manage their areas.

QUALIFICATIONS
• Bachelor’s degree in a business, data, or technology-related field.
• Proven ability and success working with cross-functional teams.
• Strong understanding of database query languages.
• Experience with data mining and visualization techniques, preferably in Looker, Tableau and/or Google Data Studio.
• Proven record in supporting business leaders with data to make decisions (business intelligence).
• Experience working with multiple unstructured data sources.
• Reflective and independent learner (e.g., learns from mistakes, asks good questions).
• Detail-oriented, with the ability to effectively multi-task in a deadline driven atmosphere.
• Excellent written communication and presentation skills to diverse stakeholders.
• The ability to see the big picture, work on the details and think analytically
• Curious, consistent, reliable, and work quickly to find solutions - you seek to understand multiple perspectives, always asking questions about the patterns you are seeing and wondering what might be the cause.

WHAT WE OFFER

Exos strives to create a workplace culture that prioritizes health, wellness and recovery. We believe that the concepts of happiness and productivity are not mutually exclusive. They feed one another. We cultivate an environment that allows for all team members to feel and perform at their best in work and in life outside of work.

We offer:
• Competitive salary and incentive opportunities
• Benefits after 30 days - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision packages
• 401(k) match with access to financial advisors and seminars
• Paid time off
• Recovery Week – Corporate offices close the last week of the year
• Parental leave benefit with up to 12 weeks of 100% paid leave
• Daily access to Exos Coaches on all aspects of personal development
• Employee interest groups for BIPOC, Women, LGBTQ and Caregiver communities
• Discounts with our partners for apparel, equipment & supplements
• Education reimbursement, pet insurance and partner discounts
• Flexible work schedules that encourage and emphasize employee wellness
• The opportunity to grow with us as we expand with newly launched digital products

To prevent the infection and spread of COVID-19, and as an integral part of its public health and safety measures, Exos requires that all successful applicants shall be required to show proof of full vaccination by an FDA-approved COVID-19 vaccine before beginning employment, unless an exemption from this policy has been granted as an accommodation or otherwise. Applicants believing they need an accommodation of this policy because of a disability, sincerely-held religious belief, or otherwise should inform People Operations after an offer of employment is extended; please do not include any medical, genetic, or religious information on your application materials.

To learn more about us and this role, please visit us at www.teamexos.com",2022-03-02,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker']"
