19607,1335,Clinical Data Analyst,Tata Consultancy Services,Anywhere,"Job Title: Clinical Data Analyst

Work Location: Cincinnati, OH / Austin, TX/ Detroit, MI...

Technical/Functional Skills:

Google Cloud Platform, HL7v2, FHIR, CPCDS, CCDA, and OMOP

Experience Required:
• We’re looking for a small team of vendors familiar with healthcare data standards such as HL7v2, FHIR, CPCDS, CCDA, and OMOP. It’s important they also have some technical skills, specifically the ability to write python-like code in our proprietary language to map data between different schemas and to submit their code for review. The main responsibilities will be to write mappings between medical ontologies. Quarterly, there will be a need for video call interactions on Eastern time zone.
• Experience in EHR and claims ETL Knowledge in clinical informatics Healthcare interoperability Excellent communication skills
• Desired - Experience working with EHR (Epic, Cerner, etc) or pharmaceutical data. Software coding or design experience (but project does not involve writing programs, but will require writing configuration files to express mapping rules)

Roles & Responsibilities:
• Create data mappings from one data format to another in the customer’s proprietary format (Whistle) and submit them using internal tools like cider, critique and piper. At the beginning, client will provide spreadsheets to be translated to our mapping language. Over time we expect the agency to source the spreadsheets and build the mappings. Examples include:
• HL7v2 -> FHIR
• CPCDS -> FHIR
• CCDA -> FHIR
• FHIR -> OMOP
• OMOP -> FHIR
• Participate in answering one-off customer questions via one-off video meetings coordinated by client’s SWEs, approximately quarterly.
• Provide eng and UX feedback on the tooling and the process, approx quarterly",2022-11-03,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['spreadsheet']
19608,1336,Bilingual Web and Social Media Data Analyst (Spanish and English...,"Cascades Technologies, Inc.",Anywhere,"CTI is a recognized award-winning provider of information technology and professional services. Focused primarily on the Federal Government, CTI delivers technology enabled, results oriented solutions. CTI has built long term business relationships by ensuring the availability of highly skilled and certified resources providing a broad range of capabilities that meet the unique needs of all... customers. With a 100% referenceable client base, CTI leverages industry best practices and business innovations to provide measurable results.

