19853,1581,Senior Data Analyst,Thentia,"Oklahoma City, OK","About Thentia

Thentia Cloud is a fast-growing, venture capital-backed software as a service (SaaS) company that is emerging as a world leader in government technology with a platform that is transforming and modernizing how regulatory organizations are conducting business. A company of builders, thinkers, and owners, Thentia gives employees the opportunity to create amazing solutions, showcase... their talents, and benefit from our shared success as we scale up in the U.S., Canadian, and global markets. Further, Thentia Cloud’s solutions directly impact the public trust and regulatory integrity, helping regulators and agencies meet 21st century standards by leveraging predictive analytics, Big Data, AI, and other innovative capabilities. Internally, our culture fosters collaboration, inclusivity, intellectual curiosity, and professional development.

About the role:

Data Analysts support Product Delivery by identifying tools and processes to enable faster mapping of data from clients and legacy platforms to the target platform. Taking a product-oriented approach, you will assist the client by features and functions that set our product as a leader in the marketplace.

Having a thorough understanding of data management, visualization, and data migration tools is very helpful for success in this role. Understanding licensing processes and procedures is extremely beneficial to this role.

Responsibilities:
• Independently map data from legacy to target platform accurately and with speed.
• Identify tools and processes that will enable efficiency in data mapping and movement.
• Collaborate with client subject-matter experts to meet the regulatory requirements of the organization.
• Gain a firm knowledge of the modules, features, processes, and capabilities of the company’s product (Thentia Cloud) to assist the client through the product delivery
• Communicate and create visual representations of our data structures
• Plan and facilitate data movement and collaborate with the project team and the client for their identified projects
• Document all mapping information in the appropriate tools for traceability
• Identify and lead the resolution of issues; devise effective ways of reaching project objectives in the most cost/time-effective manner while taking into account unique business conditions for the client
• Provide data driven insights and analytical support in solving strategic and operational problems.
• Work with QA to ensure they are able to conduct thorough testing

Qualifications:
• Must have education, experience, and/or training in the field of Data Analysis
• Strong interpersonal skills and at least 2 years of experience in client-facing communications.
• Regulatory experience and technical knowledge are a plus
• Knowledge and experience with agile work environments.
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills
• Work well with a diverse team in a fast-paced environment.
• Excellent time management, written and verbal communication skills.
• Exceptionally organized with strong attention to detail.
• Comfortable in a remote-first work environment
• Experience with task scheduling and resource allocation.

Assets:
• Familiarity with the Office 365 suite.
• Experience with the AGILE project management model.
• Familiarity with JIRA projects, boards and stories.

We thank all applicants in advance for applying. Only individuals selected for interviews will be contacted.

Compensation:

Thentia provides employees with a competitive base salary along with:
• Full Health Insurance coverage,
• Flexible paid-time-off, including vacation and sick leave,
• Employee Stock Options Plan
• Year-end bonus
• Remote or Hybrid working options,
• Professional development & training

Our Commitment:

Thentia is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are building products for a diverse world and are committed to building and fostering an environment where our employees feel included, valued, and heard, which enables us to make commerce better for everyone. We strongly encourage applications from racialized people, people with disabilities, people from gender and sexually diverse communities and/or people with intersectional identities. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, provincial, or local laws in the regions we operate. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, or internships",2022-06-11,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['jira']
