19921,1649,Data Privacy Analyst,ISG (Information Services Group),Anywhere,"Data Privacy Analyst - Remote

Wanted: dynamic and creative individuals ready to connect with a like-minded team. You’ll enjoy all the autonomy you need to help our clients make their digital infrastructure faster and more effective. Free reign for free spirits doesn’t mean you’ve got to go it alone. Over 1400 teammates from around the globe are eager to help you out when things get down to wire... Their expertise will put you on the winning path and keep you there. So get ready to kickstart your career with a team that’s connected – connected by freedom.

Position Overview

The purpose of this position is to support the development, integration, and execution of all aspects of the Data Privacy Operations Office for client. The potential candidate should have the requisite background, as well as advanced analytical skills, and proficiency in various technology suites. The role will reside in the client’s Customer Data Privacy Operations Office and will specifically provide guidance and assistance with client’s support of California Consumer Privacy Act (“CCPA”) compliance.

Responsibilities
• Assisting the Customer Data Privacy Operations Office with ongoing activities related to the development, implementation and ongoing maintenance of the Client’s Privacy policies, standards, and procedures in accordance with privacy laws, regulations and industry best practices and standards.
• Supporting Customer Privacy & Data Management Operations
• As part of ongoing operations, the candidate will support Data Subject Requests, including Right-to-Know, Right-to-Opt-Out of Sell, and Right-to-Delete, and ongoing analysis of client’s current privacy policies and terms and conditions. This role will also assist with customer database operations, Data Transfer Requests, marketing campaign reviews & certifications, Privacy Impact Assessments (“PIA”), and data incident management.
• As part of the PIA process, the team makes decisions regarding lawful basis, records of processing, data inventory, data minimization, privacy notices, consent, and cross-border transfer.
• Understanding and providing guidance around data lifecycle, data maps, retention, data destruction best practices and data governance.
• The resource will need the ability to interpret and understand laws, regulations, complex issues, and documents.
• Investigating and solving problems, and providing workable recommendations and solutions.
• The resource will ultimately be responsible for working with global Data Owners, Compliance, IT, Legal, Security, and the Data Protection Officer to ensure privacy requirements are being implemented and enforced consistently throughout the organization and its operations.
• The candidate is required to remain current with regulatory updates and maintain an understanding of basic compliance topics and how they affect the company.
• Initiating, facilitating, and promoting activities to foster data privacy awareness within the client and related entities.
• Serving as a subject matter expert on global privacy and data protection laws and regulations.
• Escalating key data privacy issues accordingly.
• Maintaining strict confidentiality and privilege when required.
• Performing additional duties as required.
• Negligible travel may be required. Any travel will be domestic.

Required Skillsets
• Strong interpersonal, presentation, verbal, and written communication skills with the ability to effectively interact with internal and external business partners at all levels
• Minimum 3 to 5 years of experience with legal and regulatory standards (e.g. CCPA, California Privacy Rights Act (“CPRA”), General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”), Gramm–Leach–Bliley Act (“GLBA”), et al)
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to effectively resolve moderately complex situations and issues
• Ability to create, interpret and understand data flow diagrams
• Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite and other business-related software systems, including processing systems and applications
• Detail-oriented with strong project management, organization, and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple projects effectively
• System end-user acceptance testing

Education
• Bachelor’s degree in related field
• 3 to 5 years of experience with legal and/or regulatory standards (e.g., CCPA, CPRA, GLBA, State privacy laws, GDPR, et al)
• Certified Information Privacy Professional designation (or equivalent experience or willingness to certify)
• CCPA and CPRA specific knowledge and experience
• Data Governance Experience
• Data Analytics Experience

