19984,1712,Senior Data Analyst,Exos,Anywhere,"Exos, a coaching company powered by technology, gets our members ready to achieve what’s most meaningful to them. We do this by building mobile and web apps that use a coaching system that has evolved over 20 years. A team passionate about creating human-centric products, we use technology to empower our world-class coaches and make coaching accessible to everyone. Professional and elite athletes... as well as employees at Fortune 100 and Fortune 500 companies around the world, have improved their lives through Exos.

We’re looking for a Senior Data Analyst who is energetic, a team player, and self-driven with strong data analytics skills. This role will be responsible for executing and evolving the Exos data strategy at a global corporate wellness client.

What we Offer:

Exos strives to create a workplace culture that prioritizes health, wellness and recovery. We believe that the concepts of happiness and productivity are not mutually exclusive. They feed one another. We cultivate an environment that allows for all team members to feel and perform at their best in work and in life outside of work. We offer:
• Competitive salary and incentive opportunities
• Benefits after 30 days - Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision packages
• 401(k) match with access to financial advisors and seminars
• Paid time off & Recovery Week – Corporate offices close the last week of the year
• Parental leave benefit with up to 12 weeks of 100% paid leave
• Daily access to Exos Coaches on all aspects of personal development
• Employee interest groups for BIPOC, Womxn, LGBTQ and Caregiver communities
• Education reimbursement, pet insurance and partner discounts
• Flexible work schedules that encourage and emphasize employee wellness
• The opportunity to grow with us as we expand with newly launched digital products

Responsibilities:
• Use best practices in continuous integration and delivery.
• Help drive optimization, testing and tooling to improve data quality and our ability to use data to make product decisions.
• Collaborate with key stakeholders to understand data requirements necessary for building new data pipelines, and optimize existing data streams, so that analysts can seamlessly connect to data through Looker and/or Google Data Studio, among other tools.
• Collaborate with other software engineers, ML engineers and stakeholders, taking learning and leadership opportunities that will arise every single day.
• Collaborate with the analytics team to support their BI tools and initiatives to deliver the reliability, speed, and scalability of a data platform they’ll love working with.
• Work in multi-functional agile teams to continuously experiment, iterate and deliver on new product and infrastructure objectives.
• Collaborate with the data engineering team to optimize the existing data warehouse which will create a single version of the truth and standardize data into coherent formats so that it can be queried by users by leveraging query languages.
• Create and maintain pertinent datasets aligned to business needs, including gathering client report requirements to execute to highest possible standards.
• Ensure data structures, reports and any other data-related item meets standards and guidelines outlined by Exos Data Governance.
• Find trends in data sets and develop algorithms to help make raw data more useful to the enterprise.
• Identify, design and implement internal process improvements, including automating manual processes, optimizing data delivery, re-designing infrastructure for greater scalability, etc.
• Work within multidisciplinary teams to identify client needs, define critical success indicators, identify and maintain data flows that fuel operations, and supply data.
• Keep abreast of new analysis, visualization, reporting techniques and software to develop a more powerful analytics platform.
• Be a trusted technical advisor to customers and solve complex data challenges.

Qualifications:
• Bachelor’s degree in a technology-related field (data science, computer science, software engineering, etc.), with 3-5 years’ data analysis experience.
• Must have experience with the visualization software, Looker.
• Experience in database query languages (SQL, MySQL, Snowflake) and substantial knowledge in analytical approaches.
• Knowledgeable about data modeling, data access and data storage techniques
• Experience contributing to client-facing projects, troubleshooting technical issues, working with cross-functional stakeholders.
• Experience in working with/on data warehouses.
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.

Who We Are:

Exos, a coaching company, was founded in 1999 and became the industry leader in human performance by preparing elite athletes for their sport. Over two decades later, we have evolved into a company with a goal to ignite the hero in all of us by getting our members ready to achieve what’s most meaningful to them. Whether that’s having energy to chase kids at the playground, coming up with a breakthrough idea at work, getting back into a running plan, or other moments that matter most -- Exos gets our members ready.

We provide coaches who empathetically and expertly guide, programs that are personalized, and teams to support members along the way. By leveraging science, technology and engaging programming, we impact hundreds of thousands of members at 400 locations world-wide; ranging from corporate sites and community programs to military and athlete training centers.

Exos is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming workplace for all. We invite applicants from a wide variety of identities, ideas, perspectives and experiences and encourage people from underrepresented backgrounds to apply. Exos offers reasonable accommodations to job applicants with disabilities",2022-05-01,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['looker', 'snowflake', 'sql', 'mysql']"
