19990,1718,"Data Engineer I, Data Analytics",FiscalNote,Anywhere,"About The Position

At FiscalNote, we build platforms that connect people to their governments, and our Data Analytics team builds tools, processes, and reporting capabilities to integrate operational data and enable enterprise decision-making. As a Data Engineer on the Data Analytics team, you recognize the value of properly collecting, managing, analyzing, and reporting data to improve... operational efficiencies, customer experience, and financial performance, and want to be the architect of a centralized data warehouse and enterprise level analytics and reporting platform that impacts decision making across the company. You will work closely with our product, engineering, and operations teams to build a robust and scalable analytics stack and perform various data analysis projects on how our business is performing, how we interact with our clients and prospects, and how they use our products.

About The Team

The Research and Development (R&D) Department at FiscalNote is where the magic happens. The Data Analytics team provides cross-functional data insights to leaders across the organization to power data-driven decision-making. The team is responsible for collecting and analyzing data to provide insights into improving business operations, product usage and customer experience across multiple platforms and thousands of clients, and financial performance. Our data stack currently consists of Stitch, Databricks, Snowflake, and Looker.

About You

You understand that business teams need to have trust in the accuracy of incoming data in order to shape their decision making around it, and choose to relentlessly seek solutions when you notice anything is amiss. You believe that data and analytics need to be relevant, actionable, and timely and that the most comprehensive data collection and accurate analytical model that does not change action is useless. You’re comfortable around ambiguity with a high degree of autonomy, and are excited about solving complex, open-ended problems by distilling the complexity as simply as necessary to build solutions that work. Along the way, you’re capable of communicating what you’re thinking to both technical and non-technical audiences, taking in others’ ideas as well as expressing your own.

What To Expect In This Position
• As an individual contributor on the Data Analytics team, you will work closely with the Data Infrastructure team and collaborate with stakeholders across the Business Development, Account Management, Finance, and Product teams to gather data and reporting requirements and drive the development of data models, pipelines and platforms to extract and consume data for reporting and analysis tools
• Work closely with the Product & Engineering teams to manage product usage requirements and analytics
• Create reporting and conduct ad-hoc analyses on financial, operational, and product data
• Work with business and engineering teams to build and maintain integration points and efficient ETL pipelines
• Build, test, and maintain a scalable and robust analytics stack
• Write documentation and reporting requirements
• Create and govern data warehouse architecture and data quality and integrity
• Serve as an analytics expert to establish and communicate best practices internally to both technical and non-technical stakeholders

What Sets You Apart
• 1-3 years combined as a data engineer or data analyst
• 1-3 years of database expertise, including intermediate SQL
• 1+ years of experience in data analysis and business intelligence
• 1+ years of programming experience (Python)
• Experience with cloud data warehousing (AWS Redshift, Snowflake, etc.)
• Experience with data ingestion/transformation tools (DBT, Stitch, Fivetran, etc.)
• Demonstrated experience developing with data reporting and visualization tools (Looker, Tableau, Domo, Thoughtspot, etc.)
• Experience working with product analytics (Mixpanel, Amplitude, Heap, Segment, Pendo, Gainsight, etc.)
• An independent motivation to solve problems
• Ability to communicate with technical and non-technical stakeholders to understand business and technical processes
• Experience in establishing, implementing, and socializing analytics best practices with both technical and non-technical stakeholders
• Experience with distributed computing data platforms (Databricks, Spark, Glue) is a plus

Excited about this role, but don't meet 100% of the expected qualifications listed above? We'd still love for you to apply! FiscalNote is committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce where unique experiences are valued and everyone has the opportunity to contribute. Research has continuously shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet all of the listed qualifications. We want to help overcome this trend and seek to make space for unique and relevant skills and attributes. So, when applying to FiscalNote, rest assured that your application is reviewed by a living, breathing human being and evaluated based on key competencies needed for success in the position. Our Recruiting team maintains awareness of all open roles which means your application may be assessed against multiple positions and we will reach out to gauge your interest in other opportunities as appropriate. Questions or concerns? Contact recruiting.team@fiscalnote.com, we'd be happy to connect!

As part of FiscalNote's commitment to creating an accessible and inclusive hiring process, we strive to provide reasonable accommodations for persons with medical conditions or disabilities that will enable their access to the hiring process. If you need an accommodation, please send an email to recruiting.team@fiscalnote.com to let us know the nature of your request.

About FiscalNote

FiscalNote is the premier information services company focused on global policy and market intelligence. By combining AI technology, expert analysis, and legislative, regulatory, and geopolitical data, FiscalNote is reinventing the way that organizations minimize risk and capitalize on opportunity.

Home to CQ, Roll Call, Oxford Analytica, and VoterVoice, FiscalNote empowers more than 5,000 clients worldwide to monitor, manage, and act on the issues that matter most to them. To learn more about FiscalNote and its family of brands, visit FiscalNote.com and follow @FiscalNote.

At FiscalNote, we Lead with Values

Know your Audience ∙ Find the Truth ∙ Drive Alignment ∙ Level Up ∙ Own the Job ∙ Bias for Action ∙ Support the Family

FiscalNote is continuing to hire new talent, with all interviewing and on-boarding done virtually due to COVID-19. New team members, along with our current staff, will temporarily work remotely (unless communicated otherwise).

Company Benefits

FiscalNote offers competitive salaries, equity packages, and retirement accounts to ensure we’re all FN owners. We work hard, so our open vacation policy helps us ensure you’re getting the R&R you need. We offer comprehensive health, vision, and dental insurance options supplemented by a flexible spending account (FSA). We have a slew of other benefits which you can check out at careers.FiscalNote.com .

FiscalNote values diversity. We are committed to equal opportunities and creating an inclusive environment for all our employees. We welcome applicants regardless of ethnic origin, national origin, gender, race, religious beliefs, disability, sexual orientation or age. FiscalNote is an EEOC employer.

FiscalNote uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all new employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.DHS.gov/E-Verify ",2022-05-23,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'snowflake', 'python', 'sql', 'redshift', 'aws', 'spark', 'r']"
19991,1719,Business Analyst/Healthcare Data Analyst,Alaka`ina Foundation Family of Companies,Anywhere,"The Alaka`ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) has a need for a Business Analyst/Healthcare Data Analyst to support the Defense Health Agency. Preferred locations are San Antonio or TX, Falls Church, VA, however this position can be remote as well.

Alaka`ina has partnered with the Defense Health Agency (DHA) to deliver world class, data-driven decision science analytics of military... healthcare operations and the delivery of healthcare services worldwide. Alaka`ina and its partners will lead with way for DHA to expand its current analytical services to incorporate leading-edge technologies and advanced skills.

Successful candidates will have an extensive background in the Military Healthcare System, in-depth knowledge of the Military Healthcare data marts, experience developing healthcare delivery standards, and analyzing operations at both the headquarters and military treatment facility levels.

DESCRIPTION OF RESPONSIBILITIES:
• Access, validate and analyze information about the MHS population by developing, validating, and linking various medical, safety, environmental, occupational and personnel databases.
• Aggregate and analyze population health data to respond to questions from the various Congressional inquiries, DoD senior leaders, Service-specific Headquarters agencies, and the MTFs.
• Coordinate and attend meetings for Service and Enterprise/Tri-Services groups and record/report/ communicate back to Government leadership items of discussion especially relevant to Analytics.
• Collaborate with DHA and other applicable agencies to link program data with other health and personnel data to support a longitudinal database.
• Conduct financial on Business Case Analysis (BCA) associated with government programs.
• Conduct research and perform analysis (including development/use of predictive models for improving clinical operations and evaluating clinical currency, efficiency, and productivity) to support a variety of clinic practices initiatives focused on improvement of clinical operations.
• Coordinate and arrange for program data transfer from DHA, MCSCs, MTFs, and other users of various programs.
• Identify, troubleshoot, and conduct data import, analysis, and display errors from multiple data sources.
• Provide analytical support regarding the integration, access, and development of data to support the documentation, comparative analysis, and outcomes analysis necessary to demonstrate the efficacy of clinical pathways designed and implemented in the MTFs.
• Provide data analysis and decision support using research expertise as well as literature review/evidence-base to develop clinical and business measures and prototypes of health information technology (IT) tools, programs, procedures, services, or databases to support DHA’s goal of building a managed healthcare system that considers and optimizes safety, quality, cost, and access.
• Provide technical expertise in the areas of prevention, managed care, medical readiness issues, health promotion, clinical safety and quality, and other health Service-related issues in order to support the DHA’s vision of becoming the healthiest and highest performing segment of the US.
• Research, develop, analyze, monitor, and report annual Performance Plans.
• Research, identify and apply, when available, national/standardized benchmarks and thresholds to DHA/MHS metrics as appropriate or the Contractor shall identify reasons why the established benchmarks/thresholds/methods are not appropriate/relevant.
• Support the Government as the lead clinical and business information resource in the documentation, plan, design, build, implementation, and maintenance of clinical and business information systems for the DHA and its internal/external customers.

REQUIRED DEGREE/EDUCATION/CERTIFICATIONS:
• Master’s Degree in Healthcare or Business Administration, Economics, Accounting, Management, or 8 years of equivalent health care work experience.

REQUIRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:
• Demonstrated knowledge of CHCS and/or M2 file and MHS data table structures; Minimum of 3 years’ experience data mining and conducting detailed analysis within the Military Health System (MHS) Data Warehouses.
• Expert level skills in SQL or SAS.
• Demonstrated knowledge of internal MTF processes related to the execution of health care, e.g., admissions/dispositions process, patient scheduling and appointing, financial reimbursements through Third Party Collections, and outpatient and inpatient throughput.
• Demonstrated knowledge of medical coding practices and processes (ICD-9/10 and CPT/HCPS).
• Five (5) years of technical experience in data presentation software and concepts associated with presentation of quantitative information.
• Five (5) years demonstrated ability conducting thorough and comprehensive system-wide business case and return on investment (ROI) analysis for healthcare operations within the DHA, MHS, Veterans Administration (VA) or private sector.
• Five (5) years of experience in communicating and writing complex concepts and their effects/impacts on the target environment, such that a lay audience is capable of understanding.
• Five (5) years of experience using MHS Medical Expense and Performance Reporting System (MEPRS) / Defense Medical Human Resources System Internet (DMHRSi), Manpower, Program Objective Memorandum (POM) processes, Finance, and Referral Management/Access to Care.
• Five (5) years of experience with integration of performance planning goals to meet the objectives of the DHA.
• Proven ability to identify and implement solutions to improve data quality (medical coding, MEPRS usage).
• Three (3) years’ experience working in a leadership role within Resource Management, Group Practice Management, or TRICARE Operations.

GENERAL SKILLS AND RESPONSIBILITIES:
• Ability to acquire skills/capabilities necessary to meet growing needs/demands of systems/software/hardware.
• Ability to critically examine and evaluate, problem-solve.
• Ability to deliver products on time, on schedule, within budget. Flexibility and ability to adapt to rapidly changing and often time-constrained environment.
• Able to read, write, speak, and understand English.
• Demonstrated ability to communicate analytical discoveries and appropriate recommendations/mitigation strategies effectively and clearly to all levels of customers including Senior DHA leadership.
• Demonstrated ability to organize/participate/lead working groups to develop analytic products and byproducts or to develop/understand processes leading to effective optimization of analytic efforts.
• Demonstrated ability to provide accurate and timely analytical products containing well-reasoned and cogent discussion points providing leadership with substantiated options or courses of action.
• Demonstrated ability to undertake and complete multiple tasks with multiple deadlines simultaneously.
• Demonstrated advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office products PLUS additional software/hardware skills and capabilities.
• Proven ability to synthesize disparate data from multiple sources and coalesce into an accurate and useful analytic product, incorporating Service and MHS strategic goals for use by leadership in both tactical and strategic decision making.

DESIRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:
• Minimum of 10 years’ experience within the Military Health System (MHS)

REQUIRED CITIZENSHIP AND CLEARANCE:
• Tier I background check or National Agency Check with Inquiries (NACI) Equivalent
• US Citizenship Required

The Alaka`ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) is a fast-growing government service provider. Employees enjoy competitive salaries. Eligible employees enjoy a 401K plan with company match; medical, dental, disability, and life insurance coverage; tuition reimbursement; paid time off; and 10 paid holidays.

We are an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. We are proud to state that we do not discriminate in employment decisions on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, or disability status. If you are a person with a disability and you need an accommodation during the application process, please click here to request accommodation. We E-Verify all employees.

The Alaka`ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) is comprised of industry-recognized government service firms designated as Native Hawaiian Organization (NHO)-owned and 8(a) certified businesses. The Family of Companies (FOCs) includes Ke`aki Technologies, Laulima Government Solutions, Kūpono Government Services, and Kapili Services, Po`okela Solutions, Kīkaha Solutions, LLC, and Pololei Solutions, LLC. Alaka`ina Foundation activities principally benefit the youth of Hawaii through charitable efforts which includes providing innovative educational programs that combine leadership, science & technology, and environmental stewardship.

For additional information, please visit www.alakainafoundation.com .

