19992,1720,Data Analyst Intern (Spring / Summer 2023) (Virtual),"Stride, Inc.",Anywhere,"• Meet Stride
• Success Stories
• Responsibility and Inclusion...

Over 20 years ago, Stride was founded to provide personalized learning — powered by technology. We reached students where they were in their own journeys. We knocked down their barriers to great education. And we gave every learner equal opportunity to succeed — however they defined success. Stride innovated the learning experience with online and blended learning that prepared them for their lives ahead.

Stride is a community of passionate leaders. Whether teachers, engineers, curriculum writers, or financial managers — whatever your expertise or role, we all work to empower futures through learning. And changing the trajectory of learning itself is one of our greatest missions. Join us in developing more effective ways to learn and helping learners build the skills and confidence they need to make their way forward in life.

Product Effectiveness Team Data Analyst Intern gathers data on product use and uses it to create actionable reports, dashboards, and views to shape product design and improvement decisions. The ideal candidate is actively pursuing a degree with an eye toward a career in data analysis, analytics, or data visualization and is interested in getting hands-on experience in a corporate environment. You’ll be presented with real business challenges and provide solutions that make a difference across our product development teams while learning the skills needed to successfully navigate the modern virtual workplace.

ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential duties.
• At the direction of Product Management team, assist in defining, developing, and maintaining reports and data views that give insight into academic outcomes, user engagement and satisfaction, and business objectives of Stride curriculum products;
• Support analysts in mining data from multiple data sources, including Snowflake, AWS, MongoDB, SQLServer, and others;
• Write and revise SQL queries to acquire data;
• Help establish data pipelines in DBT, Fivetran and PowerBI;;
• Create report or dashboard mockups and prototypes to help validate business requirements and UX prior to development;
• Proactively investigate, report, and where possible, address data quality issues;
• Create data extracts or reports, primarily in Microsoft PowerBI or Excel;
• Collaborate closely with stakeholders on curriculum and engineering product development teams, finance, marketing, and school implementation teams to ensure reporting requirements are well defined and that solutions meet stakeholder needs;
• Create and maintain product documentation including requirements, data dictionaries, and use manuals, and other training collateral that clearly and concisely communicates what data products offer and how they can help users realize their goals;
• Participate and contribute to cross-organization data efforts to standardize reporting and increase ability of business stakeholders to self-serve their data needs;
• Attend and actively participate in daily Agile development processes and ceremonies including standups, sprint planning, PI planning, and retrospectives.

Supervisory Responsibilities: This position has no formal supervisory responsibilities.

MINIMUM REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:
• Strong analytical abilities (research, conceptual, quantitative skills)
• In pursuit of degree in Computer Science, Learning Analytics, Educational Data Mining, Information Technology, Data Informatics, or similar (non-technical disciplines, such as IT Analyst, Project Management, Process Analyst)
• Experience and/or coursework in creating SQL queries, generating reports or dashboards in Microsoft PowerBI or similar software, and building data narratives or reports
• Intermediate knowledge of at least one programming language, ideally Python or R
• Strong drive for results and taking initiative
• Ability to be resourceful and adaptable
• Strong written and verbal communication skills: ability to tell story through data
• Ability to interact with business partners and drive the conversation
• Flexible and adapts well to change

Certificates and Licenses: None required.

OTHER REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:
• Demonstrated experience in Microsoft PowerBI reporting and visualizations. A review of your portfolio of visualizations will be part of the interview process, with an emphasis on any prior work related to learning analytics or school data.
• Basic experience with online collaboration tools such as Slack, O365, Google Docs, Aha, Trello, StoriesOnBoard, etc.
• Basic experience with basic office software tools such as Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Project, Visio, etc.); Web proficiency.
• Basic familiarity with Agile software development teams and practices (especially Scrum and/or Kanban)
• Ability to pass required background check

DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS:
• Enrolled at a 4-year accredited college or university, rising senior or master’s level education status at the start of the internship, graduating August 2023 – May 2024 or no more than 12 months past your graduation
• Demonstrated working knowledge and expertise in visualization techniques for Learning Analytics strongly preferred
• Exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills
• Excellent listening, communication, and presentation skills. You can tell a story about data and walk stakeholders through a complex report or dashboard in a concise and compelling manner.

Work Environment: The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.
• This position is virtual and open to residents of the 50 states and D.C.

Compensation & Benefits: Stride, Inc. considers a person’s education, experience, and qualifications, as well as the position’s work location, expected quality and quantity of work, required travel (if any), external market and internal value when determining a new employee’s salary level. Salaries will differ based on these factors, the position’s level and expected contribution, and the employee’s benefits elections.

We anticipate this position will pay between $17.20 to $27.53 per hour. The upper end of this range is not likely to be offered, as an individual’s compensation can vary based on several factors. These factors include, but are not limited to, geographic location, experience, training, education, and local market conditions. Eligible employees may receive a bonus. Stride offers a robust benefits package for eligible employees that can include health benefits, retirement contributions, and paid time off.

The above job is not intended to be an all-inclusive list of duties and standards of the position. Incumbents will follow any other instructions, and perform any other related duties, as assigned by their supervisor. All employment is “at-will” as governed by the law of the state where the employee works. It is further understood that the “at-will” nature of employment is one aspect of employment that cannot be changed except in writing and signed by an authorized officer.

Stride, Inc. is a Federal Contractor, an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and a Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected Veteran status age, or genetics, or any other characteristic protected by law",2022-08-28,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['word', 'snowflake', 'power_bi', 'python', 'visio', 'powerpoint', 'sql', 'mongodb', 'aws', 'outlook', 'excel', 'r']"
