20164,1892,Data Steward Analyst- AVP,Mindlance,United States,"Job Title: Data Steward Analyst – CDE Registration & DQ Metrics - AVP

Location: Jersey City, NJ (Hybrid role, 2-3 times a week onsite...

Position Type: Fulltime (Direct Placement)

Our client, one of the largest Investment Bank, is seeking a Data Steward Analyst – AVP for their Jersey City, NJ location. Looking for local candidates. This is a fulltime direct placement role, offering high visibility and competitive salary.

Job Description:

The Data Steward function is a new team within the Client’s organization that will provide oversight for the use, management, and integrity of the data across its lifecycle with a focus on improving siloed approaches to data. The function will be responsible for governance and oversight of Client’s data set in order to improve and maintain the completeness, accuracy and timeliness of the data. The team will work closely with business process owners, operations and data custodians in the client’s technology organization to ensure that Corporate, ICG and ISG data governance processes are followed for their respective subject-areas and domains. As such, the right resource will have experience acting as a point of accountability for data content and quality that is consumed, processed and distributed. The candidate will provide oversight of the change management processes for data models and data distribution channels. The candidate will have experience with products that support the governance process e.g. data dictionaries, logical and physical lineage tracing, CDE identification and registration, and governance workflow.

Key Responsibilities:
• Responsible for production of monthly Critical Data Element (CDE) scorecards, gathering approvals, dispositioning red metrics, and archiving documents for audit
• Partnering with data consumers and tech owners to establish scope of request and gather/review CDE data and metadata including profiling to ensure data is fit for purpose
• Working with technology team to test CDE rules before implementation
• Gathering approvals from both consumer and technology teams for CDE registration
• Registering CDE data and metadata in an Enterprise Chief Data Office (ECDO) tool known as Collibra
• Submitting change control documentation to the ECDO including approved profiling and test scorecards, as well as any other necessary requirements in support of the registration process
• Organizing and archiving required audit artifacts for future retrieval and reference in support of audit
• Ensuring tech teams add new rules accurately to the monthly scorecard
• Effectively tracking data quality exceptions working to properly disposition against defined SLAs

· Responsible for quality control of own work

Skills Required:
• Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Business, Finance or Information Technology with minimum 5 years or relevant work experience in a corporate environment with demonstrated ability to meet the job requirements through comparable work experience.
• Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office (PowerPoint, Excel and Word) with a proficiency in advanced formulas, such as nested IF statements, VLOOKUP’s, pivot tables, etc.
• Working knowledge of JIRA/Confluence for project status tracking

· Strong interpersonal, customer service and communication skills (oral and written)
• Excellent project management skills
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills
• Strong ability to communicate information, business process and system wide changes to a technical and nontechnical audience
• Ability to work under pressure and manage conflicting priorities
• Knowledge of Oracle SQL to query large data sets preferred
• Knowledge of Python to automate recurring data cleansing processes preferred
• Prior Data Governance experience is preferred

Education:
• Bachelor's degree/University degree or equivalent experience

