20172,1900,Data Research Analyst,University of Kentucky,Anywhere,"UK

The University of Kentucky (UK) is hiring a Data Research Analyst...

UK has been recognized as a Higher Education Excellence in Diversity (HEED) Award recipient for the sixth (6th) consecutive year and has earned Forbes ranking for Best Employers for Diversity, Best Employers for Women, and recognition as a Military Friendly School.

UK has also been recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for the fifth (5th) consecutive year, in large part due to compensation and benefits, shared governance, and faculty experience.

In addition to your take-home pay, your benefits package is a major component of your total compensation at UK. These benefits include flexible work arrangements; our 200 percent match on eligible retirement contributions; competitive health, dental, and vision coverage; tuition benefits for classes at UK, and much more.

Job Summary

The Data Research Analyst will provide analytical support to help manage the research enterprise at the University of Kentucky. In the Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR), this position will work independently with colleges, departments, and support units across campus to gather requirements and influence how our services are measured by assembling dashboards, self-service tools, and reports to analyze and deliver information on extramural research data, operations, and strategic decision-making.

This position requires advanced proficiency in using Tableau Desktop, including creating and designing dashboards, connecting to and joining various data sources, constructing complex calculated fields and level of detail expressions, and using formatting and layout options.

The Data Research Analyst will be required to periodically develop, coordinate, and provide training and materials on extramural research data. Training may be delivered in person or virtually, depending on our customers’ needs. The successful candidate will be able to work effectively with various stakeholders across the university while also managing timelines to ensure reports are timely and accurate.

This position will also be independently accountable for producing and maintaining metadata, preparing flowcharts and other documentation to illustrate data flow through systems and procedures, writing technical documentation, and assisting with archiving obsolete reports.

Our office may consider hybrid or remote work opportunities for the successful candidate.

COVID-19

The University of Kentucky considers the health, safety and well-being of our entire community to be a top priority. In alignment with this priority, all new hires must provide proof of COVID-19 vaccination or obtain an approved medical or religious exemption as a condition of employment. For areas that fall under the federal CMS mandate, start of employment cannot occur until two weeks after receiving the full COVID-19 vaccination series or upon obtaining an approved exemption. Only vaccines approved by the World Health Organization can be accepted.

Equivalencies

The University of Kentucky uses equivalencies in determining if a potential applicant meets the minimum education and experience. Related experience can be substituted for education. Click here for more information about equivalencies: http://www.uky.edu/hr/employment/working-uk/equivalencies

Required Edu./Exp.

Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree and five (5) years of experience OR equivalent (below)
• High School diploma or GED and nine (9) years of experience
• Associate's degree and seven (7) years of experience
• Master’s degree and three (3) years of experience
• Doctorate degree and no experience

Required License/Registration/Certification

None.

Diversity/EEO

The University of Kentucky is committed to a diverse and inclusive workforce by ensuring all our students, faculty, and staff work in an environment of openness and acceptance. We strive to foster a community where people of all backgrounds, identities, and perspectives can feel secure and welcome. We also value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.

The University of Kentucky is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from veterans, individuals with disabilities, women, African Americans, and all minorities",2022-12-21,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['tableau']
