20329,2057,Scientific Data Analyst,McKesson,Anywhere,"Summary

The Scientific Data Analyst drives the implementation of complex biomedical data modeling projects. As a member of the data science and product teams, the Scientific Data Analyst works on a wide variety of highly detailed scientific and medical data projects related to specific customer implementations as well as core product development...

Duties and Responsibilities:
• Partner with colleagues and customers to achieve meaningful discussions regarding data outputs and feedback
• Extract data from primary sources reliably
• Develop expertise in working with clinical and genomic data
• Hold discussions and prepare materials for colleagues and superiors.
• Lead debate and problem solving.
• Use formal methodologies to understand and solve complex problems
• Determine root causes, and apply the scientific method to test, validate and reformulate hypotheses. Form recommendations.
• Escalate program issues and risks to identify solutions.
• Develop and implement project plans and timelines
• Create procedures to transform, harmonize, and model project data
• Prepare and perform customer training
• Work closely with the product development team on the definition, testing, and evaluation of new products and features

Skills:
• Working knowledge of genomics including tools, technologies, and data resources
• Understanding of data transformation operations such as string operations, numerical scaling, terminology mappings, etc.
• Knowledge of one high level scripting or programming language
• Working knowledge of MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint).
• Solid understanding of the biomedical domain with an emphasis on fields related to precision medicine including molecular biology, genetics, cancer biology, medical terminologies and coding systems, biomedical ontologies
• Strong analytical and technical skills with ability to analyze issues, assess technical risks, and recommend sound solutions in a timely manner
• Works independently with general supervision and act as a resource for colleagues with less experience.

Education:

Bachelors Degree or Masters Degree

At McKesson, we care about the well-being of the patients and communities we serve, and that starts with caring for our people. That’s why we have a Total Rewards package that includes comprehensive benefits to support physical, mental, and financial well-being. Our Total Rewards offerings serve the different needs of our diverse employee population and ensure they are the healthiest versions of themselves. For more information regarding benefits at McKesson, please click here.

As part of Total Rewards, we are proud to offer a competitive compensation package at McKesson. This is determined by several factors, including performance, experience and skills, equity, regular job market evaluations, and geographical markets. In addition to base pay, other compensation, such as an annual bonus or long-term incentive opportunities may be offered.

Our Base Pay Range for this position

$71,000 - $118,400

