20385,2113,Data Analyst,Crain Communications,Anywhere,"Description

Crain is looking for a Data Analyst to join our team. The Data & Analytics team supports all the Crain brands with actionable intelligence that helps drive revenue. The team supports brands like AdAge, Automotive News, and Crain’s Chicago—among others...

Data is the lifeblood of our business. It helps ensure we’re tracking towards our goals and is the foundation of our decision making. As a data analyst, you’ll be a steward for our data so we can extract actionable insights and drive the business forward.

As we continue to evolve the data and analytics role at Crain, we are in the process of building a data warehouse to allow for deeper analyses and more sophisticated reporting. We’re looking for someone that’s excited to be a part of this new evolution in data and analysis here at Crain.

The perfect candidate will be able to analyze data and discuss that analysis in a concise, impactful way to ensure it's well received and implemented. Join a team that’s constantly identifying ways to leverage our best-in-class content to continue the expansion of our fast-growing subscription business.

Responsibilities
• Develop ad hoc reports, dashboards & visualizations from multiple data sources to support business operations using Tableau and Excel
• Ensure clear definition of reporting and data requests before beginning implementation
• Analyze trends to identify experiments for our optimization team
• Help drive a data-first culture that builds data literacy and curiosity throughout the company
• Assist in the advancement of data governance principles and initiatives with various stakeholders
• Be a thought partner for all matters related to data and overall strategy for those brands
• Troubleshoot and analyze reporting and data warehouse issues' root causes

Requirements
• 5 years experience in analyzing data and communicating insights in a clear, concise way without sounding like a robot
• Experience creating dashboards in Tableau
• Must be fluent in Microsoft Excel
• Familiarity with a subscription-model business (traffic, conversion rate, churn, etc.) is a plus
• Stellar written and verbal communication skills
• Ability to tell the story in a clear, compelling way
• Exceptional attention to detail
• Experience working with a centralized data warehouse, including data mining and extraction
• Basic SQL skills; experience with Postgres (PostgreSQL) preferred
• Exposure or working knowledge of Alteryx is a plus
• Experience manipulating data; joining multiple sourced data, basic “cleaning” of data, creating metrics from multiple fields, etc.
• Ability to manage multiple priorities
• Experience with a “consultative” approach and drawing from the fact that you are the data subject matter expert
• Ability and desire to be proactive with data insights
• Ideal candidate would get excited about data and technology

This position is exempt under the Fair Labor Standards Act and is not eligible for overtime pay.

Pay Transparency Disclosure:

The estimated salary range for this position is $45,000 to $80,000.

The final salary offering will take into account a wide range of factors, including experience, accomplishments and location. The salary range provided should not be considered as a salary limit or cap. In addition to base salary, Crain also offers competitive benefits including retirement plan savings contributions and bonus opportunities based on individual and company performance.

