20564,13,Program Analyst - Data Scientist,U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs,United States,"Summary

This position is remote. The primary purpose of this position is to serve as a data scientist who provides analytical, data architecture and data visualization and reporting support to the evaluation of VA specialized mental health systems nationally. This position supports program evaluation of these services through the application of data science and informatics theory and principles... to the development of databases, evaluation reports, dashboards and other data visualization needs.

Learn more about this agency

Help

Duties

This position is REMOTE (location to be determined) and salary will be adjusted based on General Schedule locality of selection.

Major duties include, but are not limited to:
• Conducting these projects requires a versatile skill set relying on elements of computer programming in SQL and other languages, database architecture, clinical informatics, and data optimization. Some projects may require expertise with natural language processing to analyze data and interpret results.
• Creating and refining highly complex health care system-level databases to provide efficient, integrated automation, governance, and standardization to secure data warehouses.
• Creating sets of complex performance and quality measurements and evaluating their consistency in the degree to which they follow OMHSP business rules. An aspect of such work would be helping to migrate measurements to use of data associated with the new electronic health record, as discussed below.
• Uses multiple software packages and operating system environments suitable for working with large datasets.
• Contributes to and maintains a transparent and reusable data architecture for mental health data.
• Provides NEPEC staff with technical training as deemed necessary by the Director.
• Represents NEPEC on OMHSP, VHA wide, or interagency work groups in lieu of the Director or Associate Directors, attends conference calls or briefings, reviews materials, and reports on these activities Monitor compliance with data security requirements and regulations and facilitate the protection of large volumes of highly sensitive patient information.
• Verify that projects follow patient information protection rules and work with the Information System Security Officers and facility Privacy Officers as needed.
• Facilitate and actively manage sharing of specific data tables across VHA and partner organizations when approved.
• Confirm that any researchers they are in contact with are following procedures specified in the OMHSP data use agreement process and the procedures required by VA Informatics and Computing Infrastructure (VINCI) staff.
• Attend conference calls or briefings about relevant research activities in lieu of the Director or Deputy Director, review materials, and report on these activities.

Work Schedule: Monday to Friday, 8am until 4:30pm

Recruitment & Relocation Incentives: Not authorized

Financial Disclosure Report: Not Required

Help

Requirements

Conditions of Employment
• You must be a U.S. Citizen to apply for this job
• Selective Service Registration is required for males born after 12/31/1959
• You may be required to serve a probationary period
• Subject to background/security investigation
