Job Description

At FIS, you’ll have the opportunity to work on some of the most challenging and relevant issues in financial services and technology. Our talented people empower us, and we believe in being part of a team that is open, collaborative, entrepreneurial, passionate and above all fun.

About The Role

FIS is looking for a Marketing Analytics Data Analyst. Ideally, this person would be located on the East Coast. You will be responsible for providing best-in-breed analysis tools and insights on client needs and motivations to our Marketing and business stakeholders. You will work closely with our internal stakeholders to give them access to actionable insights, as well as work closely with our data engineers and visualization experts to implement our marketing data strategy roadmap.

About The Team

The Marketing Analytics team delivers enterprise-wide analytics products (datasets, models, reports, dashboards) to our internal customers across Marketing, Sales and Client Engagement. Join us in building out our Data Platform and that will directly impact the operations and decisions for our stakeholders, ranging individual contributors to senior management. Satisfy your curiosity and desire to learn while applying your technical acumen to building analytic data products that will help articulate and answer business questions that matter.

What You Will Be Doing

You will contribute to all delivery aspects of our analytics products~
• Analyzing large and complex datasets through multiple data transformation layers, proposing data modelling/transformation to answer business questions
• Engaging with cross functional teams (IT, Finance, Sales, Marketing etc.) to build data domain subject matter expertise
• Contributing to the development and support of data flows/pipelines in our Marketing Data Platform
• Gather and document requirements, including process analysis, working with internal clients and stakeholders to understand business requirements, create technical requirements and work with back-end developers to ensure details are well understood and executed properly
• Supporting testing processes (ensure changes made by back-end developers are correct and meet business needs)
• Identifying strategies as well as improvement opportunities while also reengineering processes for greater efficiency both within the team and across the Marketing technology platform (raising new opportunities for data capture or data integration to improve business processes)
• Data Mapping & ETL activities, investigating data issues

What You Will Need
• An understanding of end-to-end systems development life cycles
• A bachelor’s in computer science or information systems or equivalent experience
• Exposure to cloud technology, data warehousing and relational database design
• Advanced data management and data wrangling expertise that includes SSIS development, solid SQL skills and a good understanding of the intricacies of building data flows/pipelines. A very strong grasp of SQL and data management through relational databases is a must have
• Ability to analyze source data systems to identify and document complex data mapping, business rule analysis, functional and non-functional requirements
• Ability to contribute in Marketing Data Platform governance and data management efforts
• Exposure and experience with business intelligence/visualization tools (Tableau, PowerBI) and integration aspects to various data sources. Strong Tableau development skills is a must have
• Programming experience in SQL
• Experience working in projects within cross-functional teams (marketing, finance, data engineering, data science etc.)

Added Bonus If You Have
• Knowledge of financial services industry
• Experience doing Marketing analytics/data modeling
• Experience with Marketing technology stack (Marketo, Google Analytics, Sprinklr etc)
• Other programming language experience, Python, Regex expressions etc
• Microsoft Azure experience (Data Factory, Data Bricks, SQL, Synapse)
• Familiarity with working in the Agile/SCRUM framework (JIRA experience)
• CRM / ERP experience (Dynamics, Salesforce)

