20619,68,Sr. Clinical Operations Data Analyst,"Cardiovascular Systems, Inc.",Anywhere,"Putting a new spin on your career

Working at CSI means being a part of something greater than ourselves. We think big and move fast. From creating revolutionary technologies, to working with world class physicians and teams, we don’t simply work, we save lives. We have big company drive and small company vibe where your daily impact can be felt company-wide. If you are curious, ambitious and... dedicated, you will love our community. Grow with us!

Job Summary

Job Description:

The Sr. Clinical Operations Data Analyst leads system administration activities for assigned systems within the Clinical Affairs department and is responsible for developing reports to support trial activities and oversight for multiple stakeholders. This role will prioritize, gather requirements, develop or validate, and train users on reports. The Sr. Clinical Operations Data Analyst will manage upgrade activities and lead aspects of vendor qualifications, evaluations, and audits. All responsibilities will be conducted in compliance with regulatory guidelines, policies, and internal procedures.

Essential Duties And Responsibilities

Reporting/Analytics
• Prioritizes opportunities, gathers requirements, and creates or validates reports for various Clinical stakeholders
• Provides data interpretation and training of reports to Clinical Affairs team
• Identifies reports and tools to increase efficiency and quality within and across studies, functions (e.g. CEC, Monitoring, Payments), and leads implementation efforts

System Administration
• Defines process flows and develops templates and/or metrics to support system qualification, evaluation, usage, and oversight
• Responsible for system configuration and/or configuration validation, system updates/upgrades and access management for assigned systems
• Works across Clinical to define optimization opportunities, builds technical solutions, develops supporting processes, and trains users
• Serves as the technical systems support contact for assigned systems
• Serves as a Subject Matter Expert for Clinical technology projects and vendor audits
• Leads semi-annual Clinical system security review activities
• Provides input to solution roadmap to include system upgrades and innovations

General
• Manages system and reporting deliverables to meet overall trial timelines and objectives
• Leads or participates in ad hoc process improvement or solutions teams to deliver on specified project objectives
• Supports CAPAs as needed
• Serves as Subject Matter Expert for one or more CSI Standard Operating Procedures

Qualifications
• Four (4) Year / bachelor’s degree preferably in life sciences, physical sciences, statistics, information technology or related field or experience
• Six (6) years professional experience in information technology systems, clinical data management or reporting/analytics in medical device or drug clinical trial operations
• Demonstrated ability to recognize complex problems and apply creativity to analyze solution, develop technical solutions, process, and procedures
• Ability to coordinate multiple tasks and reprioritize based on changing demands in a fast-paced environment
• Knowledgeable on relational databases
• Advanced skills in Microsoft Office, Word, Visio, Power Point, clinical database management and data visualization or other reporting software (e.g. Tableau)
• Established experience with Structured Query Language (SQL), design of user interface for data collection, and database architecture
• Extensive knowledge of applicable CFR (including part 11) and ISO requirements as well as governing procedures, policies and regulations
• Prior experience with developing test plans for application and/or report testing

Specifications/Other
• Must be able to lift 25 lbs
• Work is performed on-site in an office environment with exposure to electrical office equipment.
• Must be able to look at a computer screen for up to 8 hours per day

CSI is an EEO/AA company: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are a job seeker with a disability and require accessibility assistance or reasonable accommodation to apply for an open position, please contact the Recruiting Department at Cardiovascular Systems, Inc., 1225 Old Hwy 8, New Brighton MN 55112, or call (651) 259-1600",2022-08-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'word', 'visio', 'sql']"
