20689,138,Client Excellence Business Analyst,TrueAccord,Anywhere,"Why TrueAccord?

TrueAccord, a wholly owned subsidiary of TrueML, is a category-defining company. We combine machine learning with a human-based approach to transform debt resolution and to get people on the path towards financial health. Every year, more than 70 million Americans have negative experiences dealing with debt. We are changing this by providing personalized digital experiences that... guide lenders and consumers through this challenging financial process.

With a world-class leadership team, passionate team members, and proprietary predictive models trained on years worth of transactional data, TrueAccord is well-positioned to deliver on a huge opportunity: helping millions of consumers to regain and keep their financial footing while lowering the cost of doing business for creditors across many industries.

The Opportunity:

TrueAccord’s Client Excellence team is responsible for improving business processes and client operational impacts through data-driven continuous process improvement using best practices and methodologies. The Business Analyst will join a team of highly motivated people who take the TrueAccord mission seriously and are determined to succeed. The ultimate objective of this role is the development and delivery of reporting and analysis to cultivate TrueAccord’s strategies and process optimization.

As a Business Analyst on our team, you will take ownership of multiple complex/sensitive reports. You will create reports that provide insight into key data points including client data and requests, inventory management, root cause evaluation and population scoping. This is an exciting role that can have a real impact on TrueAccord's success.

What You'll Do:
• Create reports that provide insight into key data points including historical account data, inventory management, root cause evaluation and population scoping
• Partner with Client Success, Product, Engineering, Sales, Finance, and Operations to supply actionable analytics and reports supporting a broad range of tactical and strategic objectives.
• Help manage team business intelligence initiatives; Including everything from the coordination of data extraction/transformation/loading processes to the design and development of reporting and visualizations to support business operations
• Translate stakeholder requests into the correct analytical framework, including accurate problem identification
• Write clean and concise queries to manage large tables and extract the relevant data efficiently
• Routinely present findings, insights, and recommendations to key stakeholders within TrueAccord
• Ensure data integrity through the development and use of system controls
• Regularly examine data reports to locate and resolve mistakes throughout

What We're Looking For:
• A minimum of 3 years of experience as a reporting or business analyst
• BS/MS degree in an analytical discipline: finance, statistics, applied mathematics, computer science, etc.
• Fluency in SQL, along with strong proficiency in data visualization and storytelling, is necessary
• Ability to build complex models, perform deep analyses, and turn raw data into useful information and actionable insights
• A deep understanding of statistical analysis, modeling, and common pitfalls of data analysis
• Demonstrated pattern of being analytically curious, drilling into root causes and business impacts to answer not only “Why” but also “So What”
• Ability to present complex information and deliver insights to non-technical business partners clearly and concisely
• Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively, both in a team environment and across functions
• Attention to detail and accuracy, while maintaining a solid awareness of the big picture, are extremely important
• Must be able to work effectively with little direct supervision and in the face of ambiguity, shifting priorities, and multiple deadlines
• General knowledge of business operations, objectives, strategies, processes, and information flow

You might also have:
• 5 years of relevant analytical experience
• Experience in the Financial Services industry--with major bonus points coming from relevant experience in the debt collections space
• Prior experience providing data analysis solutions in an inventory management environment
• Competency with data visualization or business intelligence tools such as Looker, Tableau, or Power BI
• Familiarity with a statistical language, such as R or Python
• Familiarity with a Snowflake data warehouse
• Experience with scenario planning (i.e., “What if” analyses), including the successful use of assumptions in place of key data points
• Ability to use data-driven insights to influence process improvements and controls

Benefits, Perks, and Culture

- Everything you need to work remotely

- Medical/dental/vision insurance, 401k (with match), flex spending plan, and life insurance

- Family-friendly policies - parental leave, remote positions

- Unlimited PTO

- Transportation benefits

- Employee assistance program (EAP) + Wellness Coach for you and 5 others

- Paid time off to do volunteer work in your community!

We are a dynamic group of people who are subject matter experts with a passion for change. Our teams are crafting solutions to big problems every day. If you’re looking for an opportunity to do impactful work, join TrueAccord and make a difference.

Our Dedication to Diversity & Inclusion

TrueML and TrueAccord are equal opportunity employers. We promote, value, and thrive with a diverse & inclusive team. Different perspectives contribute to better solutions and this makes us stronger every day. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status",2022-12-15,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'power_bi', 'snowflake', 'python', 'sql', 'r']"
20690,139,Data Analyst,GPRS,Anywhere,"What is it like to be a Data Analyst?

Ground Penetrating Radar Systems LLC, is the nation’s largest company specializing in the detection of underground utilities, video pipe inspection, and the scanning of concrete structures. GPRS has an extensive nationwide network of highly trained and experienced project managers in every major U.S. market. When clients hire GPRS, they have the peace of... mind of knowing that they have the most reliable scanning technology on their job site and they'll receive the assistance of a project manager who can provide them with the most accurate data. For over a decade, GPRS has been the industry leader by providing outstanding service and cutting edge technology, keeping projects on time, reducing safety risks, and putting our relationships with our clients before profit.

GPRS Purpose Statement

Our purpose, as an organization, is to create possibility for our team members and clients by intelligently visualizing the built world.

GPRS Core Values
• Integrity
• Teamwork
• Mutual Respect
• Growth Mindedness
• Safety

A GPRS Data Analyst collects and analyzes internal and external data in order to recommend, support and guide various business decisions. The person fulfilling this role will be responsible for gathering, analyzing and producing usable data for GPRS leaders.
• Collect and analyze internal and market data to generate useful business reports, recognize business trends and patterns, and identify new business opportunities
• Coordinate with other business division leaders to provide data-driven insight to assist with enterprise business projects
• Develops knowledge of data sources content and structure to assess the quality of data
