• Leading BI software development, deployment, and maintenance
• Develop, maintain, and optimize organizational data modeling systems and policies
• Connect and build pipelines between various data sources
• Support operational improvement and business decision making through ad-hoc statistical analysis of curated enterprise data and self-constructed data sets
• Develop, maintain, and optimize automated data reporting functions to empower real-time decision making by stakeholders
• Assists in the development and maintenance of department databases and assesses quality of data used in routine report

Here Are The Requirements (what We Need From You)
• Bachelor’s degree in statistics, computer science, or related quantitative field of study
• One to two years of analytical experience
• One to two years’ work experience using SQL
• Experience with Python/R or other statistical programming language
• Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Power BI, SQL, or other enterprise reporting tools
• Effective data validation and quality assurance skills
• Excellent analytical, quantitative, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities
• Ability to think strategically, analyze and interpret market and customer information
• Intense curiosity, high intellectual and analytical ability, passionate pursuit of analytics driven insights

Desired Characteristics
• Excellent reporting and data visualization skills
• Ability to communicate with all levels within an organization
• Willingness to work independently (after proper training) and be a self-starter
• Ability to effectively manage time
• Strong analysis skill
• Adaptable and flexible to manage deadline pressure, ambiguity, and change

We offer full medical, dental, and vision insurance with day-one coverage, 401k with company matching beginning on day one, Life, Short-Term, and Long-Term Disability at no cost to our employees, paid holidays, paid time off, leadership development training programs and additional benefits to support our strong commitment to the development of each team member.

