20891,340,Data Business Analyst,Ikano Bank,"All, MO","Are you passionate about data and information management? Are you a motivated, organized person seeking an exciting and rewarding opening in a fast-paced environment? Do you have Analyst experience within data and/or financial services industry? If you're looking for change and ready to make changes … we're looking for you!

As our Business Analyst Data, you will strengthen our Data Delivery... function within the area of Data & Analytics. You will be part of Ikano, where we create possibilities for a better living by providing financial services to the many people. We do it with different perspectives, natural curiosity, and long-term focus. A unique chance for greater responsibility and future opportunities. Let’s achieve great things together.

Together we create solutions that simplify life for the many people

As a Business Analyst for Data Delivery, you have a key role in the success of data product deliveries in the bank. You work closely with different business stakeholders to create efficient data solutions.

You are responsible for maximizing value delivered by working together with business stakeholders to design data products iteratively and incrementally. You collaborate with data product owners and data delivery team in understanding and develop features through our Agile Release Trains.

As a Business Analyst for Data Delivery, you will be creating and expanding our data solutions that will supply the bank with the data that will fuel our digital transformation. The solutions covered ranges from traditional data warehouse solutions for reporting / BI to more modern solutions (data lakes and streams) to handle real time reporting and advanced analytics.

Ikano Bank’s Digital organization is on an exciting transformation journey to advance our mindsets, ways of working and solutions. Our vision is to establish user friendly digital capabilities for the many people by unlocking the full potential of our co-workers and partners.

We offer you

This is a unique opportunity to join our team as we are on an exciting journey delivering awesome services for the many people. As a Business Analyst in the Data Delivery team you will have a great platform to expand your career and continue to develop your skills. You will work in a diverse and friendly team in a fast-paced environment.

Operating at the center of events, you will have an active role in various decision forums to create a great foundation for further development. This position is more than what meets the eye. You will get the chance to push boundaries and influence your daily work. All as part of a caring and open culture where we live our values, work hard, have fun, and operate with a long-term perspective. Because here opportunities arise, and growth follows.

Are you the one for Ikano?

Key Responsibilities
• Defining the requirements and features that will create our capabilities in line with the overall bank strategy
• Creating features with relevant acceptance criteria
• Build trust and effective relationships with relevant stakeholders by analyzing their needs and find solutions
• Reviewing features to make sure that they are in line with the objectives
• Preparing documentation and presentations
• Support the Data & Analytics product team to create, maintain and prioritize the data product backlog and roadmap
• Understand Ikano Bank’s strategic initiatives working closely with Product Management, to deliver products that helps the Bank in achieving the desired objectives
• Drive the planning of product releases, communication, learning and set expectation for delivery of new features and functionalities

Key Qualifications
• 3-5 years’ experience as an analyst or similar preferably within financial services industry specifically within finance or risk.
• You have a passion and drive to work with technologies in a team-oriented environment.
• You have a basic understanding of the different steps of software development.
• Experience and knowledge of Agile frameworks, preferably SAFe
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills
• Excellent English communication skills (written and verbal), including facilitation
• You have good technical writing skills with the ability to produce documentation of complex ideas and solutions.
• Experience within / knowledge of data, and technical architecture for Data & Analytics
• Preferred but not a must is experience in provisioning of data through modern technology
• You have Ikano’s values, common sense, simplicity and daring to be different at heart.

We want our customers, partners and co-workers to choose us for what we stand for, what we deliver and how we deliver it. Three basic values guide our work: common sense and simplicity, working together, and daring to be different. These values should feel natural to you.

Join us now – together we will find a better way

This position is a full-time employment, located in Malmö/Nothingham. More information about the position can be provided by Regy Jackers

We look forward to receiving your application with a CV and cover letter. Please note that we are unable to accept applications via email.

About Ikano Bank AB (publ)

Ikano Bank creates possibilities for better living by offering simple, fair and affordable services, enabling a healthy economy for the many people. Our offer includes savings and loan products for consumers, sales support services for retailers, and leasing and factoring solutions for businesses. We conduct business in Sweden, Denmark, Finland, Norway, the UK, Poland, Germany and Austria. Ikano Bank is a part of the Ikano Group who owns 51 % of Ikano Bank. Ingka Group, the largest IKEA retailer representing about 90% of IKEA retail sales and operates IKEA sales channels under franchise agreements with Inter IKEA Systems B.V., owns the remaining 49 % of the Bank. Ikano Bank’s head office is located in Malmö, Sweden and the company is registered in Älmhult, Sweden where the business was once founded",2022-12-07,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
20892,341,Senior Research/Data Analyst (0500004),State of Missouri,"Higginsville, MO","Senior Research/Data Analyst

Division Of Developmental Disabilities...

STATE OPERATED PROGRAMS

Salary: $73,200

The State Operated Programs (SOP) of the Division of Developmental Disabilities (DD), with the Missouri Department of Mental Health (DMH), seeks a Research/Data Analyst to serve in the role of Data Analytics and Development Statewide Lead. This position will provide state-wide services and development to the State Operated Programs Team and can be based remotely within the state of Missouri, with domicile to be determined. Travel is required.

The position will: Support the DD State Operated Programs, including both Intermediate Care Facilities for Individuals with Intellectual Disabilities (ICF/IID) and Community Based Waiver, by developing procedures and methodology used in researching/querying; analyzing, organizing, evaluating and reporting performance and quality outcome data related to program efficiencies, consumer care and staffing management; ensuring data governance; as well as training for various levels of facility staff. Examples of work in this area may include performing specialized and analytical studies by researching policies and practices consistent with the ICF/IID and Medicaid Waiver regulations, CMS standards of care and current best practices related to care of individuals with IID. It will include participation in the long term implementation, operation and enhancements of a new DMH electronic medical record system, becoming a subject matter expert to better support evolving SOP research and data needs, in support of data-driven programmatic decision making.

Job Duties
• Provides essential and critical research, data and analysis to guide Division’s management in decisions and determinations.
• Serves as a member of the DD SOP Executive Team.
• Ensures data governance for DD SOPs as a whole, as well as within each individual facility.
• Evaluate data collection and reporting methods within DD SOPs on an ongoing basis.
• Meets regularly with DD SOP executive team, facility management teams, quality assurance teams and other staff as a leader in driving data driven decision making.
• Provides training to facility staff in regard to collecting, managing and utilizing data.
• Leads and provides technical oversight to team members responsible for collecting data.
• Manages data within the event management tracking system to ensure best outcomes for consumers supported within DD SOP.
• Provides and presents quarterly and annual reports on quality measures to SOP leadership.
• Compiles critical health care data reports to the Division, the SOP leadership and the Chief Medical Director as needed.
• Develops, monitors and reports on SOP targeted measures of the DMH Strategic Direction Plan.
• Coordinate, monitor and report on the progress of the implementation of the DD SOP Electronic Health System, in order to identify successful execution, as well as ongoing needs and system issues to produce desired outcomes.
• Coordinate and provide the overall research, analysis and data display to support various DD facility programs and initiatives; including: the crisis program and the facility staffing patterns, as related to recruitment and retention.
• Provides assistant and support to division-wide needs, as necessary.
• Works closely with other research analysts in DD/DMH on a wide variety of data analysis projects.
• Advises on policy, conduct policy research, and serve as technical consultant related to Medicaid data.
• Performs other work and special projects related to research analysis, data reporting and supporting the electronic medical record as needed.

Qualifications

Bachelor’s Degree and 4-6 years of relevant experience and/or appropriate certification. Data analysis of programs involving mental health, social services, intellectual disability/developmental disability, public health and quality assurance services preferred.

Is highly efficient in SQL, Visual Studio, Excel, Tableau and/or other reporting programs.

To Apply

Upload a resume, cover letter, and transcripts to Ashlea Thompson, Human Resources, Northwest Community Services, 1547 W Commerce, Marshall, MO 65340, fax 660-831-3066, email ashlea.thompson@dmh.mo.gov, and complete the online application at https://mocareers.mo.gov/ no later than December 2, 2022 ",2022-05-21,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'excel']"
