Job Description...

This role will support multiple business units within operations and is tasked with the development, maintenance and analysis of current reports as well as the creation of new reports as deemed necessary in order to improve department effectiveness, monitor business and agent trends, support compliance and collections, and to maintain procedural controls where appropriate. This position is also accountable for analyzing and reporting on a wide variety of departmental data for processing and collection management.

Key Responsibilities:
• Create, maintain, analyze and distribute reports/queries from databases (ad-hoc and scheduled) to support the business objectives. This would include scheduled and adhoc policy/agent data, debt information, control reports, time service, quality, time studies, compliance reporting’s, DOI audit data, AWD queries, telephony data, etc.
• Assist in completion of quality controls at a macro level. Develop and maintain SSRS reports, Access databases, and Tableau reports to manage various departmental needs.
• Participate in project work and communicate necessary information to the business units.

Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:
• Excellent knowledge or ability to learn Americo data systems including DSS, Oracle, Navision, AWD, and other pertinent systems
• Expert Knowledge in Microsoft Excel, Tableau, SSRS, Microsoft Access, and/or other reporting tools
• General Commission and Collection Knowledge
• General understanding of life insurance, annuities and accounting principles
• Displays big picture thinking and an above average business acumen
• Excellent verbal/written communication skills
• Proven success working directly with top level management
• Ability to multi-task
• Superior time management skills
• Professionalism when dealing with others
• Ability to self-start and operate independently minimal supervision
• Excellent attention to detail
• Strong technical aptitude
• Ability to analyze data, identify trends, and recommend appropriate course of action
• Ability to operate with a sense of urgency, meet deadlines, and multi-task
• Ability to react and change direction as needed to meet objectives
• Ability to be a team player and foster collaborative relationships
• Ability to design reports and modify approach as needs change
• Ability to be responsible and accountable for actions and results

Education:

Four-year degree or equivalent professional experience

Americo: We’re in this for life!

The roots of the Americo family of companies date back more than 100 years. Americo is a life insurance, annuity, and Medicare Supplement Insurance company providing innovative products to our customers. At Americo, it’s the people who make things work, so we hope you join us!

What you’ll love about working at Americo:
• Compensation: You’ll feel valued with our competitive pay and robust bonus program that’s offered to all associates.
• Learning and development: We prepare you with a comprehensive, paid training program that will get you ready for success. Additionally, our Talent Development team creates a variety of development opportunities for associates at every stage of their careers.
• Work-life balance: We place true value on work-life balance with our generous paid time off; you begin accruing hours right off the bat every month and it increases with tenure. All new hires earn over 4 weeks of paid time off annually, plus 11 paid company holidays! We also support new parents with a generous new child leave program, along with paid STD and LTD.
