20950,399,Enterprise BI and Analytics Analyst Sr,Medical College of Wisconsin,United States,"Position Description:

Every great life-changing discovery begins the same way—with new knowledge. It can change everything, from a single life to the future of entire communities. That’s why academic medicine, and the continuous pursuit of knowledge, is at the center of everything we do at the Medical College of Wisconsin (MCW...

In the role of Enterprise BI and Analytics Analyst Sr you will bridge the communication between Stakeholders, Internal customers, BI Developers, Reporting Analyst, Data Management and IT. This position requires a unique combination of knowledge of business operations, requirement analysis, project management and data analysis. Leveraging the knowledge of business operations and quality to perform requirement analysis, data analysis, develop data transformation logic and functional specifications for building analytics dashboards and data products. Enhances analytics experience by providing inputs for dashboard design, analyses data and perform data presentation using modern styles and techniques. Collaborates with units across MCW to service analytics requests as well as improve analytics footprint. Assist in design and implementation of analytics dashboards, applications and ad-hoc and standard reports.

Responsibilities:
• Formulate calculations, transformation logic, data analysis and rapid prototyping to aid BI and Analytics Applications/Dashboards/Reports.
• Develop requirement analysis, functional specifications and solutions design for analytics and data visualization in analytics dashboards and BI reports.
• Work closely with project teams, operational leaders, BI developers, data analyst and reporting analysts to analyze data requirements, data mapping and analytics needs.
• Provides technical and functional documentation on project requirements and deliverables.
• Collaborate across all MCW’s Missions, departments and operational partners, to present analytics, value creation and insights.
• Collaborate and partner with units across clinical enterprise and MCW clinical departments, (including practice groups MCP & CSG) to develop analytics footprint across the organization.
• Assist and support adoption of Enterprise Analytics Intake and Triage process.
• Analyze and propose improvements to gain efficiency on Enterprise Analytics Intake and Triage process.
• Experience in data modeling and integration.
• Advanced SQL scripting skills for data acquisition and manipulations in SQL-compliant or other data sources.
• Coordinate quality control and accuracy of information by creating recommendations for data quality.
• Knowledge in QlikView/ QlikSense or other equivalent visual presentation tools.
• Construct new and redesign existing SSRS reports to be deployed on a (SQL Server Reporting Services) server.
• Construct new and maintain SSAS OLAP cubes deployed on (SQL Server Analysis Services) server.
• Participate in project teams as necessary and assist with timely delivery and project timelines.
• Perform other duties as assigned.

Knowledge – Skills – Abilities
• Excellent interpersonal communication skills and team player attitude.
• Strong oral and written communication skills, strong critical thinking and problem-solving and attention to detail required.
• Strong analytical abilities and software knowledge in the areas of spreadsheets, power point presentation, word documentation, databases, electronic records and graphics.
• Ability to work independently.

Preferred Schedule:

Position Requirements:

Minimum Qualifications:

Appropriate experience may be substituted for education on an equivalent basis
• Bachelor’s degree
• 8 years

Preferred Qualifications:
• Preferred Experience: Extensive knowledge of SQL programming, Qlik development and other BI Tools.

Why MCW?
• Outstanding Healthcare Coverage, including but not limited to Health, Vision, and Dental. Along with Flexible Spending options
• 403B Retirement Package
