20964,413,Finance & Data Analyst,LHH,"Palo Alto, CA","LHH is working with a well funded biopharmaceutical client in Palo Alto to hire a Finance & Data Analyst. This position will support traditional FP&A, forecasting, and analysis in addition to data analysis. This includes data mining & analytics, modeling, decision support, and building out dashboards & reporting tools for executives. The right candidate will have strong analytical skills and... exposure to Tableau, Snowflake, Alteryx, SQL, Python, and advanced Excel. This is a great opportunity for someone that has a big picture mindset and enjoys rolling up their sleeves to work in the details. This company is based in Palo Alto and offering a hybrid (in-office/remote) work arrangement.

Primary Duties and Responsibilities:

• Bring a product mindset to building the tools and visualizations for optimal decision making

• Shape and continuously improve both standard reports and customized analyses to deliver ongoing insight to leaders

• Communicate and partner with our key leaders to deeply understand the business questions and apply data techniques to support high quality decision-making

• Join financial and operational data as needed to enable good decisions

• Build our data infrastructure and support scripts and updates needed to ensure timely, accurate data flows

• Enhance operational excellence within the team by creating useful data automation wherever possible

• Support our enterprise systems & processes in relation to data

• Build and extend data quality processes

Skills and Competencies:

• 2+ years of experience in an FP&A or data function preferably within a biotech or biopharma company

• Experience with analytics and visualization tools (Tableau, Snowflake), and data modeling techniques

• Familiarity with cloud data warehouses, SQL, Python, and the ability to query, join and transform data from multiple sources

• Proven ability to build strong relationships of trust & influence

• Strong modeling & analytics, demonstrated business acumen, and great communication skills

• Solid experience with regression analysis, cohort analysis, and other conventional statistical modeling techniques

• Experience working with financial data sets and clinical data a big plus

