Job Description

Clinical Ink is seeking a Data Quality Analyst to join our Study Quality team based remotely across the United States! This role is a contract position and is responsible for performing statistical tests and assessments on large datasets to ensure data quality and integrity. The ideal candidate will have prior experience in data quality (i.e., report and export) combined with the ability to write simple to complex SQL queries. The Data Quality Analyst's responsibilities include:
• Perform statistical tests on large datasets to determine data quality and integrity
• Undertake and Conduct Data Quality Management activities such as (but limited to):
• Identify, compare, and resolve data quality problems
• Evaluate large dataset for quality and accuracy
• Determine business impact level for data quality issues
• Work with Programmers to correct data quality errors
• Determine root cause for data quality errors and make recommendations for long-term solutions
• Research and determine scope and complexity of issue to identify steps to fix issue
• Develop process improvements to enhance overall data quality
• Provide cross-functional support to Study Quality, as needed, to ensure the correct functioning of clinical trial software with focus on patient safety and integrity of clinical study data
• Ability to influence others to improve ways of working and buy into new processes
• Experience on a number of Data Management projects using SSRS and/or Tableau
• As required, assist with the execution of platform testing
• Perform other related duties as assigned/needed

Qualifications
• Associate’s degree
• 5+ years of experience in data quality/testing (Report and Export)
• Experience with SQL queries and demonstrate writing simple to complex SQL queries
• Exceptional analytical skills and problem-solving skills
• Experience with Tableau and SSRS Report is plus
• Experience in clinical trial space is plus
• Relevant experience or coursework in statistics, data management, SQL, and/or clinical trial design
• Strong written/verbal communication skills; ability to communicate with personnel at various levels
• Exceptional computer skills; proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, etc.
• Detail oriented and analytical reasoning skills
• Sense of ownership and proactive approach to work
• Effective prioritization, time management, and organizational skills

Additional Information

