As a Marketing Data Analyst, you will:
• Evaluate enterprise-wide customer data systems and manage the process of marketing data integration, analysis and output.
• Evaluate and append external data to support customer relationship management and conduct opportunity analysis.
• Capitalizes on data and technology to accomplish three main objectives; to effectively communicate with our customers, to enhance their customer experience, and to provide long-term profitability to the bank through customer retention.
• Collaborate with line of business managers, market managers and other primary data users to prioritize where data can best be used to support business development efforts. Develop an action plan for deployment and use of key marketing data.
• Direct development, creation and integration of data to assist in executing marketing campaigns.
• Develop dashboards and reports to share desired information in a consistent, concise, accurate and timely manner.
• Assist the Marketing Director in managing the annual marketing budget.
• Manage the bank’s Voice of the Customer program, deploying customer surveys, analyzing responses and providing timely reports at the market and bank wide level.
• Gather, analyze, and distribute accurate information in recognizing and retaining the bank’s most profitable customers, as well as customers with the potential for high profitability.
• Use customer data, along with analysis of demographics and psychographics, to assist in delivering relevant marketing offers and sales contact to key business development segments.
• Play a key role in administering CRM software to expand the bank’s cross sales success.
• Understand and practice data quality and maintenance best practices, ensure data security and integrity are met and in line with the bank’s data governance guidelines.
• Mine and segment data bases for direct mail marketing campaigns.
• Develop and maintain internal policies and procedures related to email usage.
• Develop, create, manage and maintain email lists and distribution.
• Work to minimize list decay and unsubscribes while increasing productivity of email sends.
• Performs other miscellaneous duties as assigned by the Marketing and Communications Director.

Interpersonal Skills and Competencies Required
• Excellent verbal and written communications skills for effective interactions with marketing team, departmental and banking associates.
• Demonstrated expertise in modeling and customer segmentation, managing analytics, lead generation, database management, and personal computing.
• Ability to clearly express ideas in both written and oral communications.
• Ability to work efficiently and effectively both independently and in collaboration with others, commitment and ability to meet deadlines.
• Must be self-motivated and also work in a team environment.
• Must be organized with excellent project and time management skills.
• Requires a high energy level and strong sense of urgency.

Education and/or Experience
• Bachelor’s degree in marketing, marketing analytics, business analytics, data management or related field. Applicable experience and/or related certifications may be considered in lieu of degree.
• Master’s degree is preferred.
• Three to five years applicable experience preferred.
• Three to five years of banking or finance marketing preferred.

The Bank of Missouri is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability",2022-08-13,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
