21109,558,Data Governance Analyst I - Remote,Ultra Mobile,Anywhere,"ULTRA MOBILE is seeking a talented Data Governance Analyst I to join our Enterprise Data Team! Individual reports to Manager, Data Governance. Role is remote – must reside in the United States.

About The Role...

The Data Governance Analyst I role within the Data organization is responsible for assurance that data is appropriately governed from various sources to ensure data integrity and information usability for decision making. This is accomplished by applying data management principles in cross functional settings across both business and technical stakeholders.

In this hybrid business-technical role, you will work closely with other enterprise teams to support the operations of Data Governance by ensuring system metadata, dictionaries, business glossaries, data lineage, and data security is maintained/monitored. This is an opportunity to interact with both technical partners (ETL developers, integration developers, data stewards, DBAs, architects), business stewards.

We’re looking for a hands-on person who’s capable of driving the importance of data governance and passionate about data quality for “data driven” decisions.

Your usual day of awesomeness includes:
• Support metadata management processes and standards across all of the data domains to ensure data integrity and standardization.
• Creates, documents, maintains and oversees Data governance processes and data catalog- partner with business stewards to define the data standards, certify data assets and maintain the data assets, business Glossary and asset relationships in DG tool.
• Support data governance council and working group discussions as subject matter expert of DG tools and processes, meeting coordinator.
• Promote a culture of data governance by developing partnership with data stewards to promote data governance best practices.
• Identify data issues and collaborate with business and technical stewards to address the issues and improve internal processes.
• Support the documentation of requirements for data governance related projects by analyzing systems and data.

What You Bring
• A self-starter and able to operate independently and manage multiple priorities and tasks with minimal supervision.
• Ability to work in a team environment and lead cross functional teams.
• Effective verbal and written communication with stakeholders across various levels of organization.
• Business Analysts type skills in gathering and presenting information to management.
• Knowledge of common data governance, data management and metadata management practices.
• Experience in creating data standards, procedures.
• Knowledge of Agile Project management methodologies.
• Knowledge of data structures such as columnar, unstructured data, data lakes, APIs, data virtualization, data warehousing, data visualization, predictive analytics, statistics, and analytic models.
• Problem solving skills – Anticipates potential obstacles and develops contingency plans to overcome the same.
• Experience in one of the data governance tools like Collibra is preferred.
• SQL, Python or experience in any other programming languages a plus.
• Proficiency in MS Excel and experience in data visualization /reporting tools like Looker, Tableau, is a plus.

WE ARE ULTRA & MINT MOBILE

We connect people to what’s most important in their lives: Easily, affordably and reliably. We strive to be California’s Preeminent Destination Employer. Oh yeah, we get it too! We understand what matters to you most. You’re an individual with unique needs, and we’re prepared to exceed any expectations you have for an ideal employer.

We’re smart, strategic, and get things done without a lot of red tape or unnecessary politics. Everyone matters here and everyone has a voice. Expect to spend your time contributing to projects that really matter. We obsess over the employee experience. To start, we provide some of the most competitive salary, benefits, family leave, vacation, retirement and equity options in Southern California. We believe in you and invest in you. Not just your career aspirations, but your life.

In addition, we’ve got a laundry list of perks you’ll brag about on insta -- Lunch every day prepared by our very own chef, healthy snacks, onsite gym, free massages, car wash services, and most importantly, a team atmosphere. We even raise the bar on well bars, including Espresso/Cappuccino/Nitro/Cold Brew/Kombucha Bar, Froyo Bar, Breakfast Bar, Snack Bar and a, well, you know, bar (after 5 pm).

And if you feel intrigued right now reading, imagine the co-workers we have already attracted. This is the kind of team you’ll want to take home to mom or invite to your kid’s next birthday party. This is the kind of close-knit community happening here. Come check out how you can be part of Ultra & Mint!

OUR VALUES – LET’S MAKE LIFE ULTRA TOGETHER!
• Ownership: We are all owners; be the outcome and get the job done.
• Action Biased: Be brilliant, proactive, and act with urgency.
• Embrace the Adventure: Be agile, adaptive, and thrive on change.
• Invent and Simplify: Never accept good enough.

$1,000 REFERRAL BONUS

Take a look at this job description, if you are the right person, please apply. If Ultra Mobile doesn't appear to be a fit for you, refer a friend or colleague and get $1,000. Let your friend or colleague know to provide your full name and email when applying to the job. If we hire them and they stay for 90 days, you get $1000. For more details of restrictions and rules, please email recruiting@ultra.me.

