21424,873,Data Health Analyst,Arcadia,Anywhere,"Serve as a member of Arcadia's product development team for our high growth Population Health and Analytics software. Will analyze large and diverse data sets on our customized data model and systems to support a wide variety of customers in the healthcare space.

What Success Looks Like...

In 3 months

- Gain familiarity with Arcadia’s data integration process and data quality tools

- Begin completing data integration implementation tasks with the assistance of a senior data quality and implementation analyst

- Develop cross-team relationships (Account Management, Implementation Management and Data Management)

In 6 months

- Take ownership of a customer and the data quality and implementation tasks associated with the customer

- Complete most data integration and data quality tasks with minimal assistance

- Begin contributing to process improvement conversations

- Share subject matter expertise in health care data with fellow Arcadians

In 12 months

- Take ownership of a portfolio of customers

- Work independently in completing data quality and data integration tasks for customers in your portfolio

- Have customer facing conversations independently on a regular basis. Be able to articulate data quality nuances and issues to the customer so that the customer can understand the root cause and any resolution necessary.

- Develop innovative approaches to data quality management and implementation, by using your deep industry experience, and then share these innovations across teams

What You'll Be Doing
• Prepare, analyze and visualize tens of millions of healthcare data records to support marketing and Return on Investment (ROI) analyses, customer requests and product Research and Development (R&D);
• Balance and deliver on multiple ad-hoc data analyses for customers;
• Take ownership of content creation over specific domains including: Readmissions and Social Determinants of Health (SDOH);
• Build content for Arcadia's proprietary technical foundry database and systems;
