21426,875,Data Privacy and InfoSec Contracts Associate,Applause,Anywhere,"Job Description

Data Privacy and InfoSec Contracts Associate - US Remote...

Applause seeks a client-supporting Data Privacy and InfoSec Contracts Associate to join our team.

You will:
• Coordinate with Legal, InfoSec, Sales and Customer Operations teams internally, as well as the company’s clients, to map data workflows regarding the company’s deliverables and ensure that commercial contracts and Data Processing Agreements are redlined, negotiated approved and signed efficiently and in compliance with InfoSec and Privacy policies
• Support Legal and InfoSec teams in onboarding, managing new and existing supplier commitments and associated contracts to confirm compliance with customer-facing commitments
• Act as an escalation point for a dedicated team which handles client-sourced data privacy and InfoSec inquiries and onboarding requests

Key Responsibilities:
• Review and complete Applause-populated InfoSec and Privacy elements within time-sensitive contracts affecting deal closure, such as Master Services Agreements, Scopes of Work, and Data Processing Agreements and Addenda
• Expeditious review of InfoSec and data handling terms within such contracts, ensuring that the terms are acceptable by Applause, escalating where terms may require a unique approach or alteration of existing policy and/or process
• Track, monitor and escalate customer and vendor unique requirements in aggregate, ensuring company’s compliance efforts converge on commitments
• Proactively work with the InfoSec and legal teams to effectively manage suppliers, ensuring regulatory and contractual commitments are enforced, fulfilled, and updated when needed
• Support customer, RFP and vendor onboarding processes, handling escalations from cross-functional teams on new/non-standard intake questions, helping to develop standardized resources addressing recurring client-facing needs, and attending client InfoSec (and/or legal) meetings to facilitate approval

Qualifications:
• 4+ years of information security and technical compliance experience
• 4+ years of contract management/vetting experience, or equivalent vendor management responsibility
• Proven corporate experience having proactively supported legal, InfoSec and sales working cross functionally to expeditiously review, redline and negotiate customer and vendor contracts
• Experience working directly with customers, preferentially in both services-delivery and sales contexts
• Experience working with multiple external parties to achieve consensus on expectations
• Ability to work independently and as part of a team
• Ability to work in a fast changing environment, be well organized, manage multiple projects with competing priorities and deadlines
• Understanding of technical controls supporting SOC2, GDPR, CCPA and other privacy regulations
• Excellent verbal and written communications skills to effectively engage with stakeholders at all levels
• Certified Information Privacy Professional (CIPP) certification or equivalent
• BS degree or equivalent experience

Salary range for this position is included in accordance with current state/local pay transparency legislation. Please note that salaries may vary for different individuals in the same role based on several factors, including but not limited to location of the role, individual competencies, education/professional certifications, experience, and performance in the role.

Base Salary Range: $75,000 - $120,000

Who We Are:

Applause leverages its worldwide community of on-demand digital testing professionals to create curated and vetted testing teams who provide our clients with a full suite of testing and feedback solutions. Our white glove approach seamlessly integrates with any SDLC process, enabling leading brands across all industries to increase development velocity and deliver high-quality digital experiences to their customers.

Applause is a place where everyone belongs and where we believe everyone deserves the exceptional. Since our founding, we have continued to celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment. We have a global workforce that, like our crowd, embraces diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and abilities. Our employees bring their true self to Applause. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, religion, national origin, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, veteran status, genetic information, disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. If you are qualified to perform the essential functions of this job, but believe you require a reasonable accommodation to do so, please click here to complete an accommodation request. Please note Applause will only review requests for applications that have been submitted. We will review your qualifications and follow up with you regarding your request if your qualifications meet our current needs",2022-07-19,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['gdpr']
21427,876,Data Analytics Security Manager,Cardinal Health,Anywhere,"Headquartered in Dublin, Ohio, Cardinal Health, Inc. (NYSE: CAH) is a global, integrated healthcare services and products company connecting patients, providers, payers, pharmacists and manufacturers for integrated care coordination and better patient management. Backed by nearly 100 years of experience, with more than 50,000 employees in nearly 60 countries, Cardinal Health ranks among the top... 20 on the Fortune 500.

We are currently seeking a Data Analytics Security Manager to join our growing augIntel team.

Department Overview

augmented Intelligence (augIntel) builds automation, analytics and artificial intelligence solutions that drive success for Cardinal Health by creating material savings, efficiencies and revenue growth opportunities. The team drives business innovation by leveraging emerging technologies and turning them into differentiating business capabilities.

Job Overview

The Data Analytics Security Manager will be responsible for Security and Compliance of various Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions. The Manager will be responsible to oversee all aspects of Security and Compliance for AugIntel team by acting as a liaison with Enterprise Security, Audit and Compliance teams. Responsible for translating SOX, HIPAA and GDPR controls to technical requirements and operating procedures to ensure compliance across Data Platforms and Analytics solutions. The ideal candidate for this role will have blend of Security, Compliance and Data Analytics skills.

The Manager brings in a product mindset and leverages agile practices to craft and drive iterations building new Security controls, addressing gaps and incorporate automations to improve efficiency and usability of the technologies.

Additionally, the Manager brings in a Service Provider mindset, demonstrate exceptional interpersonal skills, strong leadership, relationship management to build a strong and cohesive team that focuses on security, compliance, and usability

Responsibilities:
• Maintain a comprehensive set of policies, standards, processes, and procedures to achieve compliance across Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions
• Maintain governance program that ensures security policies, standards and process are being adhered to by new products and Analytics consumers
• Ensure healthcare information security best practice controls are in place and they adhere to HIPAA utilizing a common control framework (i.e., NIST, HITRUST CSF)
• Involved in completing security questionnaires and representing the security and privacy of the Data Solutions in a professional manner
• Serve as liaison to Cardinal Health Enterprise security and audit teams and help influence the policies and processes to be tailored for modern day analytics and self-service analytics
• Work with the engineering and operations teams to ensure that the infrastructure design meets Cardinal Health, and industry security requirements
• Monitor security trends for Data lakes, Data Operations, and drive adoption of best practices
• Conduct risk analysis and advise senior management on appropriate remediation
• Investigate, drive resolution, and document security incidents
• Manages expectations with key stakeholders, builds and fosters relationships
• Participates in the development of policies and procedures to achieve specific goals
• Leverages understanding of Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions to tailor security policies, standards, and processes, to secure Analytics systems

Qualifications:

Required
• Proven information security related work experience.
• Experience with HIPAA/HITECH regulations and guidelines for securing ePHI data
• Proficient working in multiple Security domains (e.g., Cryptography, Authentication, Authorization, OWASP, Vulnerability Management, Threat Modeling, Identity Management)
• Knowledge of Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions and Knowledge in Big Data systems, Data Lakes and Analytics related field managing Build & Run teams
• Understanding of ML/AI concepts and compliance implications for ML/AL in the industry
• Aware of common security vulnerabilities like OWASP Top 10 and Ransomware with the ability to successfully communicate the remediation to the business
• Experience advising and mentoring diverse teams.

Preferred
• Professional certification in the information security space (e.g., CISM, CISSP, CISA, GIAC) or other security certification at a similar level.
• Familiarity with security frameworks associated with one or more industry standards (e.g., HITRUST CSF, COBIT, COSO, HIPAA/HITECH, ISO, ITIL, NIST, PCI DSS, SOC or SOX)
• Involvement or knowledge of several aspects related to a SSAE 16 SOC 2 Audit
• Understanding of protocols underlying security domains (e.g., FIDO, U2F, Web-Auth, SSO, SAML, OAuth
• Understanding of Data Analytics solutions in Cloud

Covid

For any onsite, non-remote employees

A Covid-19 vaccination is required in order to be employed in this position. This includes either:

2 doses of the Moderna or Pfizer vaccine

1 dose of the Johnson & Johnson vaccine

Cardinal Health is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, veteran status, marital status, creed, status with regard to public assistance, genetic status or any other status protected by federal, state or local law",2022-12-21,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['gdpr']
