21482,931,Financial Data Analyst,Public Consulting Group,Anywhere,"Overview

Public Consulting Group (PCG) is a leading public sector management consulting and operations improvement firm that partners with health, education, and human services agencies to improve lives. Founded in 1986 and headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts, PCG has over 2,500 professionals in more than 60 offices worldwide. PCG’s Human Services practice helps state, county, and municipal... human services agencies to achieve their performance goals to better serve populations in need. PCG’s seasoned professionals offer proven solutions to help agencies design programs, services, and systems; increase program revenue; cut costs; and improve regulatory compliance with state and federal regulations. To learn more, visit http://www.publicconsultinggroup.com/humanservices/ .

PCG is committed to a diverse workforce; a reflection of our clients and the people they serve. Our organizational culture attracts and rewards people who are results-oriented and interested in making an immediate impact on their community as well as their own career.

Responsibilities
• Understands and is an expert in complex federal regulations and requirements for long-term services and supports (LTSS) programs, including home and community-based services (HCBS) waivers, Program of All Inclusive Care for the Elderly (PACE), skilled nursing facilities (SNF), and intermediate care facilities for individuals with intellectual disabilities (ICF-IID)
• Designs and calculates optimal purchasing strategies for LTSS programs
• Understands available services and program goals and develops program rates that support desired outcomes
• Identifies federal funding support and calculates reimbursement rates
• Analyzes data and effectively communicates findings
• Collects cost data and other information from providers and analyzes and manipulates data sets.
• Provides administrative support for various projects, including data entry for and quality assurance of cost reports, time studies, and survey data
• Serves as primary contact for time study help lines and email accounts
• Conducts financial and data analysis using Excel and Access, including reviews of financial cost reports and time study data
• Understands and evaluates current rate setting methodologies
• Evaluates rate structures for specific programs and makes recommendations for improvements
• Analyzes and interprets federal and state laws and regulations
• Understands program requirements and associated costs
• Participates in both internal and external client discussions
• Prepares other written reports and materials for consultants and clients (e.g., deliverables, policy summaries, status reports, invoices)
• Travels as needed for projects
