21539,988,Senior Data Analyst,Zipline,Anywhere,"About Zipline

Do you want to change the world? Zipline is on a mission to transform the way goods move. Our aim is to solve the world’s most urgent and complex access challenges by building, manufacturing and operating the first instant delivery and logistics system that serves all humans equally, wherever they are. From powering Rwanda’s national blood delivery network and Ghana’s COVID-19... vaccine distribution, to providing on-demand home delivery for Walmart, to enabling healthcare providers to bring care directly to U.S. homes, we are transforming the way things move for businesses, governments and consumers. The technology is complex but the idea is simple: a teleportation service that delivers what you need, when you need it. Through our technology that includes robotics and autonomy, we are decarbonizing delivery, decreasing road congestion, and reducing fossil fuel consumption and air pollution, while providing equitable access to billions of people and building a more resilient global supply chain.

Join Zipline and help us to make good on our promise to build an equitable and more resilient global supply chain for billions of people.

About You And The Role

Zipline’s Data team is responsible for powering data-driven decision making across the entire organization.

We are hiring a talented and experienced Senior Data Analyst to join our small, but growing Data team and play a critical role in empowering all team members to make decisions with data. Doing our job well means that we enable the entire organization’s ability to make more informed decisions, innovate faster, and serve our customers better.

In this role, you will work directly with our Data, Engineering, Operations, Go-to-Market, and Finance teams to support the organization's data analytics needs.

What You'll Do
• Deep dive into our data, create intuitive visualizations, and present actionable insights to a variety of stakeholders.
• Create high quality metrics and reporting in order to continuously improve our daily operations and processes, root cause problems, and measure the success of projects and initiatives.
• Build predictive models that help us improve the performance of our drones and reduce stockout rates at our distribution centers.
• Maintain the integrity of our data by proactively identifying issues and working with our engineering and operations teams to implement robust solutions that will enable us to scale and operate more efficiently.
• Share your knowledge across the company by mentoring and managing other analysts and leveling up our collective technical expertise.

What You'll Bring
• Advanced knowledge of SQL and comfort with Python and libraries commonly used for data analysis and visualization, e.g., Pandas, Numpy, Scipy, and Matplotlib
• Strong understanding of descriptive statistics, probability, and statistical modeling
• Experience with BI tools such as Mode, Tableau, Looker, or similar tools
• Adept at summarizing large datasets visually that make complex results understandable at a glance
• Adept at triaging analysis requests and balancing multiple projects, deadlines, and stakeholders at once
• Extremely high standards and obsession for data accuracy
• Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain complex topics in simple language to different types of audiences
• Passion and excitement to serve as a technical mentor and thought leader at Zipline
• Nice to have:
• Experience in schema design and dimensional data modeling, ideally using tools like dbt
• Experience with tools commonly used in data orchestration and processing such as Airflow and Spark

What Else You Need to Know

Location: This is a remote friendly role, but you do have the option to come into our South San Francisco office if you’re based in the Bay Area. If you are full-time remote, you must be able to travel to South San Francisco (Headquarters) to work with stakeholders approximately once a quarter and overlap working hours with both GMT and Pacific time zones.

Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.

We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply",2022-03-02,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'pandas', 'looker', 'matplotlib', 'numpy', 'python', 'sql', 'spark', 'airflow']"
21562,1011,Data Analyst (Marketing & Growth),Kraken Digital Asset Exchange,Anywhere,"About Kraken

As one of the largest and most trusted digital asset platforms globally, we are empowering people to experience the life-changing potential of crypto. Trusted by over 8 million consumer and pro traders, institutions, and authorities worldwide - our unique combination of products, services, and global expertise is helping tip the scales towards mass crypto adoption. But we’re only... just getting started. We want to be pioneers in crypto and add value to the everyday lives of billions. Now is not the time to sit on the sidelines. Join us to bring crypto to the world.

To ensure Kraken is the right fit for you, please ensure you read Kraken Culture Explained to find out more about us!

We are looking for a Data Analyst who is innovative, highly-motivated, and proactive to understand the various aspects of the marketing funnel and to help scale spend and user growth.

For this role, you will have the opportunity to work with a team that builds cutting-edge trading products and guides sound data-driven decision making in the cryptocurrency industry. You will transform large datasets from complex systems, generate actionable insights, and share the results with stakeholders at all levels of the company. You will also partner and lead projects with brand and marketing leaders, product management, engineering, client engagement, finance and other enterprise level teams.

In your day to day, you can easily go from coding, to coaching, to sharing the results of your team’s efforts with stakeholders at all company levels. You will collaborate and lead projects to understand the impact of marketing spend using various techniques including but not limited to media mix modeling with recommendations on optimization strategies.

Great benefits, amazing perks, remote work, stock incentives, and a flexible PTO policy make Kraken a great place to work. If you value having a seat at the table and want to make a big impact on guiding the direction of marketing and growth at one of the top crypto exchanges in the world, this role is for you.

Responsibilities
• Be a foundational member of the growth analytics organization within Kraken.
• Conduct data analysis and generate actionable insights and make recommendations for improving, developing and launching products
• Communicate key results with self-serve tools (dashboards, analytics tools) for your product teams and key stakeholders
• Develop and automate reporting of key performance indicators of various Kraken’s products and services at scale, solving for business priorities
• Partner with growth and marketing leaders to design experiments to test hypothesis and help with idea generation and refinement
• Collaborate with engineering teams and stakeholders to build key datasets and data pipelines using Python/ETL frameworks

Qualifications
• 5+ years industry experience in data analytics field
• 5+ years of experience with SQL, scripting languages and database concepts
• 3+ years of experience using Python, R, SQL, distributed data warehouses and computing platforms
• Proven track record of and career growth
• The versatility and willingness to learn new technologies on the job
