EBSCO’s Product Management team is looking for a creative and motivated individual who, like us, has a passion for data reporting, innovation, problem-solving, and financial acumen to drive cost savings along with continuous improvement. The ideal candidate will be a passionate problem-solver with excellent analytical skills, who is comfortable navigating large data sets from multiple sources, and clearly connects technology solutions with measurable business value. The analyst will constantly seek ways to improve and automate day-to-day operations for the team and build reporting with key KPIs to inform business decisions. The position is a great fit for a motivated self-starter who loves to drive sustainable solutions for real business problems.

Primary Responsibilities:
• Provide reporting and analytical support by creating and maintaining key reports and self-service dashboards using Tableau to provide relevant information on third-party production to business stakeholders and support leadership in making effective, data-driven decisions.
• Responsible for the development and tracking of key financial metrics, including key KPIs and staffing models, across all external partners to ensure that financial cost savings are measured, tracked, and meet the needs of the business.
• Assist in the management of product management financial review revenue and costs across the business operations, which includes a monthly review of costs with analysis and explanation of variances, forecast projections at a product level, and participation in the budget process.
• Provide and support the implementation of business solutions by building relationships and partnerships with key stakeholders in product management, identifying business needs, determining, and carrying out necessary processes and practices, implementing key metrics that drive operations, monitoring progress and results, and driving improvement opportunities.
• Identifies new opportunities and solutions and determines new and improved methods and tools that could lead to future process improvements (in particular, ways to automate manual processes and develop automation solutions across product management).

Required Qualifications:
• Bachelor’s degree or equivalent years of experience
• 5+ years of experience in a business analyst role
• Working and development knowledge of data visualization tools such as Tableau
• Data Analysis – Must have proficiency with relational databases, SQL, Microsoft Excel
• Strong communication skills – both written and verbal
• Experience extracting and analyzing large data sets

Preferred Qualifications:
• 3+ years’ experience with Tableau
• Knowledge of the Publishing Industry
• Strong organization and time management skills and the ability to manage multiple projects

Target Annual Compensation Range: $78,150 - $111,640. The actual salary offer will carefully consider a wide range of factors including your skills, qualifications, education, training, and experience, as well as the position’s work location. EBSCO provides a generous benefits program including medical, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, flexible spending accounts, a retirement savings plan, paid parental leave, holidays and paid time off (PTO), as well as tuition reimbursement. View more about EBSCO’s benefits here: https://www.ebsco.com/about/benefits",2022-11-10,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'excel']"
21743,1192,Senior Data Analyst,Pierce County,Anywhere,"Why It's a Great Opportunity:

We are using data to make a difference! Our Research and Data Analysis Team is looking for an accomplished Senior Data Analyst with a proven record of conducting complex quantitative analysis and supplying accessible insights to non-technical audiences. Working with the elected officials and various groups throughout the community, your role will evaluate programs... and policies that impact the daily lives of Pierce County residents.

Why It's a Great Department:

The Finance Department proudly serves the great communities of the County and has received awards recognizing its performance and dedication to the public. It’s a team that provides real solutions and assists all County departments meet goals as defined by their mission.

How to be Successful in the Role:

We are looking for someone who enjoys analyzing complex issues and has professional experience conducting quantitative and qualitative research. An academic research background with strong statistical analysis skills, including causal inference research experience using R and Python for statistical analysis is preferred. The successful candidate will complete projects that generate insightful, timely, and relevant research to support the County’s strategic priorities.

Your Future in this Role:

As a Senior Data Analyst, you can immediately contribute to the team’s success. You will be guided through the process with coaching-focused support, a team that wants you to be successful in your role, and an organizational culture that encourages continuous learning and professional development.

Core Daily Responsibilities:
• Work with Finance Department colleagues, other County department staff, and management to proactively develop models and analytic approaches that can be reliably applied in a timely and effective manner.
• Consult and coordinate with County departments and external agencies to identify data sources, analysis tools and requirements, and appropriate methods and analytic approaches to examine research questions and topics with County-wide significance.
• Write feasibility studies for multi-departmental projects, project briefs, progress reports, proposals, and final reports.
• Report status of project activities and resources to mitigate risk and assess business value achievement.
• Conduct presentations and/or briefings on all aspects of assigned projects

Minimum Qualifications:
• Bachelor’s degree in data science, statistics, computer sciences, business/public administration, or related field.
• Four years of data analysis, statistics, or business analysis experience; AND
• One year of experience in a project lead role is required.

Preferred Qualifications:
• Experience in programming or system integration work is preferred.

As a condition of employment, the applicant will need to authorize and complete a background check. Information received from the background check is reviewed case-by-case and will not necessarily remove an applicant from consideration.

Supplemental Information: This is a competitive selection process. Your application form will be reviewed and evaluated for the quality and quantity of education/experience in the areas listed. Applicants whose qualifications most closely correspond to the County's needs will be eligible for further consideration. Notification of application status normally occurs 2 to 3 weeks after the closing date. Short notice may be given to applicants to participate in further selection processes which may include written, oral and performance examinations, and final interviews.

At Pierce County, diversity, equity, and inclusion means commitment, not a single step. We strive to foster an inclusive environment that supports equitable access to opportunities throughout your career. We want to recruit, develop, and maintain a talented workforce from various backgrounds, cultures, lifestyles, and perspectives, committed to our vision.

Employees of the County have local, direct, and visible impact in our diverse community. Will you join us in keeping Pierce County a great place to live, work, and raise a family",2022-04-21,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['python', 'r']"
21744,1193,Catastrophe Modeling Underwriting Data Analyst,"MSIG Holdings (U.S.A.), Inc. - Mitsui Sumitomo Marine Management (U.S.A.), Inc.",United States,"Company Overview:

Mitsui Sumitomo Marine Management U.S.A., Inc. is one of the world’s top ten property/casualty insurance carriers with over 40,000 employees worldwide...

Position Overview:

As an expanding and important field in the insurance industry, this is an exciting entry-level opportunity within our catastrophe modeling team to be on the forefront of protecting insureds from the devastating impacts of climate change. MSMM is seeking a hardworking, driven individual eager to learn with an interest in quantitative analysis.

The Catastrophe Modeling Analyst will work alongside experienced modelers to learn catastrophe modeling concepts and perform account-level modeling for the company’s property units utilizing our vendor software (AIR) and internal tools to provide underwriters result outputs needed to make informed risk decisions. This consists of the collection, analysis and quality control of MSMM’s property book of business.

The individual will work with the catastrophe modeling team for data analysis related to property aggregations, PML calculations, portfolio level profitability and trend indications.

This is a hybrid position based in Warren, NJ but are open to considering other locations within the country where a MSMM office is accessible.

Essential Functions
• Perform account-level property catastrophe modeling under the direction of experienced modelers
• Identify and track aggregate exposures in order to assist in the prevention of undue loss potential to the company from extreme events, such as hurricanes, earthquakes, and wildfires
• Track and monitor underwriting data by working with CAT modeling team to develop and provide analysis on the data necessary to manage MSMM’s property portfolio
• Maintain and control quality of property catastrophe data by monthly/quarterly/annual file and portfolio reviews and completion of QC checklists
• Collaborate with catastrophe modeling team, underwriting, reinsurance and management teams to develop and implement “best practices” for ensuring data quality across the property portfolio
• Provide support to field underwriters in the use of and problem resolution in areas of catastrophe modeling
• Assist in the creation, delivery and/or coordination of internal or external training programs related to MSMM’s Catastrophe Management activities
• Assist with various ad hoc reports as assigned

Education & Experience:
• High school degree required. Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree preferred.
• Strong knowledge of Excel
• Prior AIR software or CAT modeling experience a plus, but willing to train

If you would like to apply for this position please send your resume to resumes@msigusa.com

The Company is an Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action employer, all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or protected veteran status",2022-09-02,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['excel']
