21842,1291,Data Analyst - Finance,Drip,Anywhere,"At Drip, we believe any ecommerce brand should have the tools to connect with their customers and compete online. Learn more about Drip and how we empower independent brands to grow beyond their wildest dreams.

Look through our Careers Page to see our story, learn about our team and browse some of our benefits. Diversity at Drip is more than welcomed. It’s celebrated...

About the opportunity:

Drip is looking for a Data Analyst to join our Data team. You will play a key role using data to test, iterate and drive product outcomes. As a data team representative you will work with the VP of Finance and the Head of Engineering to create and implement best data practices across multiple platforms. In this role, you will be the data team emissary to the finance team and maintain KPI reports. You will also have the opportunity to learn about data processes across a wide swath of the company and to backstop the data team’s collaborations with multiple departments. Data is core to who we are at Drip, and you will play a crucial role in helping multiple teams be successful.

To get a sense of how Drip’s Product Machine operates, check out our blog at https://DripShips.gold.

Some of your contributions will include:
• Design experiments to validate hypotheses and translate data into insights that the finance team can use to improve internal process
• Create and maintain self-service BI solutions for SaaS Business Metrics and additional ad hoc self-service reports for the senior leadership group
• Create insightful automated dashboards and data visualization to track progress
• Develop a thorough understanding of how business processes affect the financial situation of the company. Show the findings through well designed descriptive analytics reports
• Collaborate with the Data team to ensure data quality and partner in the development of sustainable data practices and processes
• Use data to find and promote the best performing marketing of Drip customers
• Backstop Data Analysts specializing in other organizational capacities
• Drive Business Intelligence process across or within multiple departments, and understand the company’s data movement as a whole
What You’ve Done:
• 3+ years of experience in a data science or analytics role turning data into insights and recommendations
• 2+ years of professional experience using SQL on a daily/weekly basis
• Strong analytical and communication skills with the ability to synthesize insights into compelling stories
• Good business acumen, marketing, sales and acquisition domain knowledge plus knowledge of SaaS industries' models and metrics
• Experience with a Business Intelligence tool (e.g. Metabase and Quicksight)
• Experience working with Chargebee a plus
• Overall excitement to discuss and evaluate business processes and approach data insight from a SaaS business perspective, comfort with solving ambiguous problems and providing insight with data driven answers
• Building and maintaining formula driven spreadsheets for displaying data
The Interview Process:
• Apply, nice to meet you!
• Recruiter Phone Screen - 30 min
• Assignment - expected duration
• Hiring Manager Video Screen - 30 min
• Team Video Interview - 3-4 hours
• Team Debrief, we will meet to discuss openly about our conversations and share feedback for the hiring managers final decision. Regardless of outcome, every candidate will get an update from Drip on their interview status quickly
• Offer, we will call the candidate that we hope will be the next Dripster hire!
What We Offer:
• Competitive pay, benefits, and equity
• Challenging and meaningful problems to solve - you will invariably make a difference and impact
• The chance to learn from some of the best people in the business, including our wildly talented and in-touch leadership team
• A vibrant and devoted team, who still finds time for fun
• Digital first culture - many of our crew members work remotely. We have a hub in Minneapolis, MN and a European Hub in Aarhus, Denmark for in person collaboration
• Finally, just good humans...no jerks!
Compensation: $80,000 - $100,000

In order to create a space of trust with our crew, we publicize quite a bit, including compensation ranges for each of our positions. We select our initial range through national compensation survey data. And then factor in things like tenure, performance, and geographic location to come up with the most accurate numbers. Are you outside the range we’ve provided above? No problem. We encourage you to still apply, and provide us with your compensation expectations when you do. We’re big on open conversations, so, let’s have one.

