21974,1423,"Data Analytics Manager, Valuation & Internal Partnerships",Upstart,Anywhere,"About Upstart

Upstart is a leading AI lending platform partnering with banks and credit unions to expand access to affordable credit. As we transitioned to being a public company, we’re now poised to leverage our domain expertise and revolutionize every aspect of lending and credit risk evaluation. We’ve recently expanded our offerings to include automobile refinancing and we plan to take on... more verticals as the business grows.

By leveraging Upstart's AI platform, Upstart-powered banks and credit unions can have higher approval rates and lower loss rates, while simultaneously delivering the exceptional digital-first lending experience their customers demand. Upstart not only supports a large remote workforce, but also has offices in San Mateo, CA; Columbus, OH; and Austin, TX.

Most Upstarters join us because they connect with our mission of enabling access to effortless credit based on true risk. If you are energized by the impact you can make at Upstart, we’d love to hear from you!

The Team

The Data Analytics team plays the critical role of providing analytical capability across Upstart's organization to enable data-driven decision making. We leverage our analytical and technical skills to support our partners with a multitude of services, some of which include understanding our underwriting models and presenting on trends in our loan performance, analyzing market size opportunities, creating financial models, developing our business intelligence pipeline to enable self-service reporting, and architecting/automating of work processes.

As the Data Analytics Manager of the Data Analytics - Valuation & Internal Partnerships team at Upstart, you will lead and coach the team in fair value model and cross-functional reporting initiatives through building repeatable, scalable, and auditable analytics.

Position Location - This role is available in the following locations: San Mateo,CA LI-REMOTE

Time Zone Requirements - This team operates on the East/West Coast time zones.

Travel Requirements - This team has regular on-site collaboration sessions. These occur 4-5 days per Month at the San Mateo, CA office. If you need to travel to make these meetups, Upstart will cover all travel related expenses

How you’ll make an impact:
• Develop a deep understanding of AI consumer lending marketplace economics and underlying analytics infrastructure supporting various internal partner teams
• Build tools and enhance methodologies for the asset valuation and forecasting models, informing business decisions with accurate, transparent, and speed delivery of financial impacts
• Define and execute strategy in data modeling and reporting process automation initiatives for financial reporting and SOX control activities. Drive data infrastructure and architecture discussions, while influencing data products roadmap
• Partner with Accounting, Audit, Product, and Engineering teams to support monthly financial reporting and deliver an accurate, consistent, and efficient data reporting process
• Implement and maintain a suite of reports and dashboards in BI tools such as Looker. Monitor trends in relevant key metrics and report on key insights on a daily basis
• Work with data service providers to explore APIs, analyze and forecast impact of integrating new data sets, while partnering with Engineering throughout the entire process of on-boarding new data sets

What we’re looking for:
• Minimum requirements:
• 3+ years of professional experience in leading analytical team and coaching talents
• 7+ years of professional experience in developing asset valuation, cash flow forecast, credit loss, econometrics, and/or other quantitative models (e.g., fixed income, structured product)
