Description

Who is SimSpace:

SimSpace Corporation launched in 2015 with a singular purpose – addressing the most demanding cybersecurity challenges to reduce organizational cyber risk. Our exclusive cyber range provides the best platform for product testing, real-world attack simulations, and extensive individual and team readiness training.

We are a fast-growing leader in the cyber range market and enable organizations to ensure that their people, processes, and technology are all ready to operate in harmony. SimSpace is disrupting the status quo for cybersecurity risk and readiness. Our advanced cyber security stack evaluations, automatic attack/defend bots, and cyber range technologies are changing the way security teams learn, grow, and work. We are a hybrid remote/in-person company with offices in Boston's Fort Point and Laurel, Maryland. We also have distributed teams across the country. We do value in-person collaboration, so if you're located in Boston or Maryland, we'd love to have you visit our teams on site when possible!

Summary of the Role: Our directorate is seeking data science engineers with strong data science, machine learning engineering, and computer science/software engineering experience to enhance and automate cybersecurity systems and to fully test, integrate and deploy those systems into the broader SimSpace software ecosystem. The focus of the department is to innovate, prototype, and deliver new capabilities that advance SimSpace's core activities. We are searching for people who can help incorporate machine learning, data science, information science, statistics, applied mathematics, analytics, and more to build systems that significantly enhance capabilities in several application areas. Several of our current and future initiatives include:
• Advancing cybersecurity assessment of organizations, teams, and individuals
• Improving assessment analysis and scoring and automation
• Developing AI-enhanced attack and defensive agents
• Predictive Modeling for Cyber Risk Estimation
• Characterization of cyber range defensive complexity, attack sophistication, and deception networks
• Statistical analyses and Design of Experiments for Candidate Assessment and other efforts
• Enhancing existing user emulation tools

Who We’re Looking For

Candidates should possess strong analytical and programming skills and have a background that includes academic coursework and project experience that demonstrate aptitude and enthusiasm for problem solving, computer science, machine learning, statistics, applied mathematics, and related topics. Prior cybersecurity expertise is not required.

What You Will Do
• Design and develop software to support new AI/ML capabilities that advance SimSpace's core activities
• Integrate these capabilities into the broader company software ecosystem
• Upgrade and maintain these systems
• Interact with provided cyber tools and other component services
• Work closely with a passionate team of other data science engineers and software developers
• Demonstrated enthusiasm and aptitude for software architecture, design, test suites, and system maintenance

Requirements

What You Will Bring:
• At least 6 years of professional Data Science experience or a PhD in a relevant field and significant professional computer science / software engineering experience
• Capable of producing high quality software that is well-written, well-instrumented, tested thoroughly, and securely designed and implemented
• Familiar with machine learning and related topics and with common libraries and tools (e.g., TensorFlow, PyTorch, Numpy, SciPy, Seaborn, Scikit-Learn)
• Experienced with writing efficient and highly optimized code to accelerate intensive tasks.
• Fluent in Python, git, GitLab/GitHub, container systems, databases, CI/CD, multithreading/multiprocessing, messaging, and modern team software development and testing tools and best practices
• Strong oral and written communication skills
• A problem-solver that is highly self-motivated, accepting of others’ opinions, and can work effectively in a team

SimSpace is an Equal Opportunity Employer and provides extensive Benefits including:
• Competitive salary and benefits (medical, dental, company-paid vision, 401k, savings and spending accounts, Employee Assistance Program, company-paid Life and AD&D Insurance)
• Unlimited paid time off
• Salary Range $180,000 - $240,000
• Equity options at hire and potential for additional based on performance
• Generous employee referral bonus program
• Peloton Interactive Wellness Program
• Semi-flexible hours, with the expectation that you overlap the main part of the day to meet deadlines, collaborate with colleagues and attend key meetings.

In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire.

SimSpace does not and shall not discriminate based on race, color, religion (creed), gender, gender expression and identity, age, national origin (ancestry), disability, marital status, sexual orientation, or military/veteran status, in any of its activities or operations. We are committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all members of our staff, clients, volunteers, subcontractors, vendors, and clients. Research shows that women and people from underrepresented groups only apply to jobs if they meet all of the qualifications. However, no one ever meets 100% of the qualifications. SimSpace encourages you to break that statistic and to apply. We look forward to your application.

