22212,1661,Senior Data Analyst I,Continental Resources,"Oklahoma City, OK","Job Summary

The Senior Data Analyst is primarily responsible for leading projects to automate manual processes and produce data driven insights for the team and other stakeholders across the organization. A successful candidate will also actively seek out and generate new and innovative ways to retrieve, visualize and analyze data across a variety of operational, geological and financial data... sources.

Serves as a resource for multiple projects across multiple work areas. Performs tasks to solve complex issues; may lead specific projects in areas of expertise. Fundamental knowledge of theories, principles and practices of Petroleum Engineering. Solves complex problems without precedent and/or structure; takes a broad perspective to identify solutions. Works independently, with guidance in complex situations.

Duties And Responsibilities
• Discover and troubleshoot data issues across sources, drive issues to resolution
• Create complex datasets, visualizations and tools
• Mentor and train staff in data management and analytics solutions; creates training content and executes across the team, department and company.
• Collaborate with varying levels of engineers, geologists and management to effectively gather data and build datasets for analytics, visualizations and reservoir modeling
• Own, maintain and enhance critical Spotfire Tools
• Own, maintain and enhance key Geographix projects for all basins
• Implement automated solutions to streamline manual team processes
• Perform data capture processes as necessary to support engineering and analytics efforts
