22213,1662,EHS Data Analyst,Chord Energy,United States,"Position Summary

The EHS Data Analyst is responsible for development and maintenance of the Intelex ACTS and V6 database architectures to provide the necessary functionalities and efficiencies to the EHS team in order to monitor and maintain compliance. This position is also responsible for managing the data quality of EHS information, and providing EHS data insights to users through reports... visualizations and dashboards. Identification, development, and implementation of large and often complex process improvements through automation and artificial intelligence is led by this position. This position is also responsible for coaching and training the appropriate users on all tools implemented for EHS data management. This person should be flexible enough to complete the technical work when time permits but have strong project management skills to delegate and managers others to complete these tasks. A subject matter expert understanding of relational databases, visualization tools, and SQL is critical to success in this position, along with basic knowledge of several EHS rules and regulations. The position will report to the Director of Environmental and will be located in downtown Houston, TX. Level and salary commensurate with background and experience.

Essential Job Functions
• Serves as lead in the development, configuration, implementation, management, maintenance, and support of the EHS data systems and users, including but not limited to databases, dashboards, data processing and analytics, reporting, and mobile tools
• Interprets core environmental regulations and company policies in order to identify and mitigate environmental issues using the ACTS Database
• Lead and direct the Greenhouse Gas (GHG) reporting programs, including EPA mandatory reporting and external organizational ESG reporting
• Conducts periodic audits of the ACTS database to ensure compliance with environmental regulations, data integrity and validation, and user functionality
• Develops and manages systems to collect, analyze, and maintain EHS data.
• Develops standardized procedures for entering data into the database while maintaining a high degree of data quality
• Serves as liaison between the company and external vendors regarding database solutions
• Provides coaching and training to employees regarding usage and maintenance of the database; ensures understanding and compliance with applicable company policies
• Effectively creates insights from large volumes of related and unrelated data

This job description is not intended to be an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities of the position. Selected candidates will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and duties outside of their normal responsibilities as assigned by their supervisor.

Minimum Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree in science, engineering or computer science
• Minimum 7 years of related experience
• Must have proficient environmental experience as a degreed professional or equivalent related environmental experience and training as a non-degreed professional
• Possesses basic working knowledge of oil and gas exploration and production technologies, including production process and equipment
• Must have advanced mathematical, science and analytical abilities
• Must possess effective analytical, graphical, written and oral communication skills
• Experience working Intelex ACTS Database
• Experience working with SQL Management Studio
• Experience working with data visualization software
• Strong knowledge of MS Office, including Word, Excel, and Outlook
• Must be able to travel, prepare written communications, present information to others, enter data into various programs
• Communicates effectively with colleagues, superiors, vendors, and regulators
• Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must possess the ability to work in a standard office setting and to use standard office equipment, including a computer, copier, files, telephone, and fax; maintain attention to detail despite interruptions; vision to read printed materials and a computer screen, and hearing and speech to communicate in person and over the telephone

The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.

Preferred Qualifications
