New York, NY...

Who You Are:

The Senior Analyst, Digital Data will join a team of global analysts leveraging digital data to deliver insights to business stakeholders and drive the ecommerce division of Michael Kors. The Senior Analyst, Digital Data will work closely with the Senior Manager, Digital Data in the data collection processes for the Michael Kors’ web sites and native mobile applications. The Analyst will provide support in the implementation, testing and maintenance of data layer and analytics tagging. Qualified candidates will have a background working in Ecommerce and hands-on experience with a tag management solution, Analytics testing and Data validation.

What You’ll Do:
• Work closely with the Senior Manager to interpret business objectives and requirements into technical requirements with input from stakeholders and digital marketing analysts
• Design and develop the analytics code base, data layer, and tag management solution for accurate and efficient data capture
• Define and design data layer requirements/specifications and coordinate with the dev team on implementation
• Support the Adobe Launch tag Implementation/development and maintenance
• Maintain technical documentation and data dictionary to account for evolving business needs and requirements
• Develop, document, execute and maintain analytics test cases and data validation
• Test the Site/App with test cases and validate data layer and javaScript beacons to ensure adherence to high data quality
• Leverage best practices and make recommendations for improvements in the existing tag implementation
• Support for appropriate tagging is functioning for all A/B tests.
• Support the pixel tags implementation for measuring campaign performance and retargeting
• Support analytics testing for IOS/Android app

You’ll Need to Have:
• Bachelors from a four-year college or equivalent
• 3-5 years of experience with digital analytics, preferable in Ecommerce
• Hands-on experience implementing tags through tag management solutions (Adobe Launch, Adobe SDK, Google Tag Manager)
• Experience of javaScript, jQuarry, JSON, HTML and CSS
• Working knowledge of reporting and insights suites (Adobe Analytics Reporting, Google Analytics) is a plus
• Experience implementing Mobile SDKs and tagging a plus
• Experience in working with JIRA, Confluence, etc
• Strong written and verbal communication skills
• Demonstrated ability to work in a fast-paced, “self-starter” environment
• Highly organized and detail-oriented
• Team-player with excellent relationship-building

MK Perks:
