You’ll enjoy the flexibility to telecommute* from anywhere within the U.S. as you take on some tough challenges. Boston, MA preferred.

Primary Responsibilities
• Support external and internal clients with diverse backgrounds, including health systems and life science companies, with expertise attaining value from real-world datasets through cloud-based environments and tools
• Support strategies to develop and internalize data assets for key internal and external stakeholders
• Work with a team of experienced healthcare data analysts
• Collaborate and work effectively across a large matrix organization
• Apply client real-world data requirements into data analytics, tools and dashboard solutions for clients using Optum data assets
• Support support strategies to develop and internalize data assets for key internal and external stakeholders
• Serve as point of contact for Client Support to explain data elements, structure, sourcing, and triage client questions
• Provide scientific and technical guidance on best practices, including standardized workflows, SOPs and related documentation, for real-world data utilization across multiple domains and stakeholder groups over a range of therapeutic areas and diseases state

You’ll be rewarded and recognized for your performance in an environment that will challenge you and give you clear direction on what it takes to succeed in your role as well as provide development for other roles you may be interested in.

Required Qualifications
• Master’s degree in data analytics, statistics, computer science or other related discipline using 'real-world data'
• 3+ years of experience, with at least 50% healthcare experience
• 2+ years of AWS experience (working within an AWS cloud using native or other tools)
• 2+ years of consulting experience (healthcare data and/or services)
• Demonstrated experiencing conducting analytics with claims and EMR/EHR data ('real-world data')
• Demonstrated experience utilizing effective communication, motivation, cooperation and conflict resolution skills
• Background in client management or program and project management
• Demonstrated proficiency in python, SQL, R, SAS
