22340,1789,"Data Analyst, Platform Analysts",Decide,Anywhere,"Decide is an AI company that crowdsources decisions to achieve better outcomes. Our flagship product, the Decision Marketplace℠, is an ever-growing marketplace of intelligent models that gets smarter with every addition. Today, the Decision Marketplace is powering our ad platform to offer brands and publishers a future-proof solution for a cookieless world, but in the coming years, we expect that... the scope of our work will expand.

Decide powers the future of advertising on the open web and automates decisions for the real world. Our flagship technology, the Decision Marketplace℠, delivers results for brands and publishers across our distributed advertising network without the crutch of third-party cookies or behavioral targeting. The Decision Marketplace is an entirely composable ecosystem that enables contributors to rapidly develop machine learning models to make intelligent predictions and more importantly, to render automated decisions.

As a Data Analyst on the Platform Analysts team, you will leverage Decide's homegrown analytics tools and techniques to assess and process performance data. Working closely with our sales team, you’ll create solutions that maximize success for both Decide and its partners. Additionally, you’ll contribute to Decide's code base, working with large datasets within our platform and supplemental client data to build tools that are reusable and tie directly into our data science models.

This role reports to the Director, PlatformAnalysts. The responsibilities of this position may be done remotely from anywhere in the United States. There are no in-person requirements, but you may choose to work in one of our hub offices in Austin, Texas, or St. Louis, Missouri.

What You’ll Do
• Manage and analyze various internal and external data sets, identifying performance trends and flagging anomalies in the data
• Execute routine optimizations to maximize return on investment and yield for both Decide and its partners
• Work closely with Decide's sales team to package data and create solutions for clients, leveraging Decide's homegrown analytics tooling and techniques
• Contribute to Decide's code base
• Tie in to external data sources to further improve our algorithms and internal processes
• Execute ad hoc needs, such as developing new tooling or defining new processes as we scale
• Generate regular and ad hoc reports on projects for leadership and organization

Your Skills And Qualifications Should Include
• Up to 4 years experience in Data Analytics, with a portfolio of data projects for entry-level candidates
• Degree in a scientific or quantitative field, or proven proficiency in these areas
• Strong command of statistics and other analytical tools
• Strong technical ability in a data-focused programming language, such as Python or SQL
• Strong business intuition
• Proficiency with version control software, such as Git
• Strong verbal and written communication
• Ability to solve unique or complex problems and explain your findings in a concise, actionable manner
• Ability to learn new skills and information sets quickly
• Working knowledge of the performance-based marketing and digital media landscape is a plus

