22650,2099,Data Governance Analyst,Honeywell,"Overland Park, KS","Join the industry leader to design the next generation of breakthroughs

Innovate to solve the world's most important challenges...

Honeywell is a Fortune 100 company that invents and manufactures technologies to address critical challenges linked to global macrotrends such as safety, security, productivity, global urbanization and energy. With approximately 129,000 employees worldwide, including more than 19,000 engineers and scientists, Honeywell has an unrelenting focus on quality, delivery, value, and technology in everything they make and do. Honeywell has been named a Top 100 Global Innovator for seven years in a row, recognizing the company’s global reach of portfolio and invention influence.

In Kansas City, Honeywell Federal Manufacturing & Technologies (FM&T) manages and operates the U.S. Department of Energy/National Nuclear Security Administration’s (NNSA) Kansas City National Security Campus. This state-of-the-art engineering, manufacturing, and sourcing facility produces a wide array of intricate components to deliver trusted national security products and government services primarily for the NNSA. Honeywell FM&T’s culture of integrity, commitment and continuous improvement enables them to deliver responsive, collaborative, and innovative management and technology services and products that translate into cutting edge solutions to complex national security issues.
• **This position will be in Kansas City, MO***

Summary

The EIM Governance Analyst works closely with business teams to develop and drive governance maturity across the organization. This position helps to facilitate assessment activities in the governance program and contributes to the development of policies and standards. The data governance analyst works closely with data stewards and data ambassadors to improve data quality and ensure data is managed effectively.

Duties And Responsibilities
• Drive data governance strategy and policies within assigned areas of the enterprise
• Develop and maintain a collaborative relationship with data stewards and ambassadors in assigned business units.
• Develop and maintain strong understanding of the data landscape in the assigned areas of the enterprise
• Identify, understand, and document data usage characteristics to drive alignment of data standards
• Reviewing and proposing changes to data governance policies and strategies
• Chairing and facilitating working sessions with business leaders, stakeholders, and data consumers.
• Tracking, managing, and reporting on data governance initiatives and progress towards goals and objectives
• Help drive the implementation and integration of a new, integrated data model

You Must Have
• A bachelor's degree in MIS, IT, Business, or 6 years of equivalent experience
• At least 2 years of related work experience in data governance, data management, GRC (Governance, Risk & Compliance) or similar areas
• US citizenship to obtain US Dept. of Energy """"Q"""" level security clearance

We Value
• Hands-on experience in data management and technologies
• Understanding of data quality management
• Deep understanding of information and process integration management
• Policy and standards drafting experience
• Ability to implement change by motivating others, driving consensus, and executing through others
• Experience working in sensitive/classified data environments
• Experience working with a US government contractor
• Strong working knowledge of engineering, manufacturing, program management, and/or financial data operations
• Strong organizational skills: managing several complex initiatives simultaneously in a fast-paced, demanding environment

FMT2021

