22720,2169,Data Analyst / Underwriter,Bar Down Investments LLC,Anywhere,"Who Are We?

Bar Down Investments is a real estate investment firm that was founded by former professional and Division 1 athletes who know what it takes to be successful. In sports, a shot that hits the crossbar and goes down into the goal is almost impossible to stop, and it takes thousands of hours of practice and hundreds of shots to achieve. This is known as a ""Bar Down"". At Bar Down... Investments, we have put in those hours and taken those shots to make sure that when we offer an investment, it is as close to unstoppable as possible. In addition to our holdings, partners Ashley Wilson and J Scott train aspiring real estate investors to reach unstoppable success in their careers through multifamily.

What is the Multi-Family Data Analyst / Underwriter Role?

The ideal candidate is analytical and logical. This individual will be capable of gathering data from multiple sources (including determining market rents based on area comps), assimilating it into our financial model, modifying assumptions to generate optimal outputs and then making recommendations to the team on how to proceed on potential deals.

In addition to the above, the ideal candidate has high attention to detail, is professional, flexible, discrete and must be willing to sign a confidentiality agreement, as much of this role will involve communication regarding large financial investments.

Job Duties and Core Responsibilities:
• Determine rental comps
• Track each property within our database
• Create and manage all documents within our filing system
• Perform research and analysis for properties and markets being considered for acquisition, development, or disposition.
• Perform detailed financial analysis using our proprietary models
• Make recommendations to the team on whether to pursue individual projects based on output from financial models.

Essential Qualifications/Skills:
• Previous professional experience in real estate and/or analysis
• Certificate, Associates or Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in Real Estate, Business, Math, Finance, Accounting or similar field, required
• Excellent computer skills with MS Office Suite, must be extremely proficient in Excel
• Exceptional verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills

Location:
• This is a remote position, so candidate can be located anywhere. The role will require work on a schedule based on the Eastern time zone.

Hours & Pay:
• This is a full-time position
• Pay is commensurate with experience and qualifications

To Apply For This Position:

To apply for this position, please submit a resume/CV plus a short (1-3 minute) video introducing yourself and providing a quick background and overview of your qualifications to jen@bardowninvestments.com",2022-11-08,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['excel']
