22781,2230,"Data Analyst , Value-based Care Services Client Analytics",Signify Health,Anywhere,"How will this role have an impact?

The Data Analyst contributes to the overall success of our organization by applying data mining techniques and statistical modeling to population health data to better understand cost, utilization, and quality of care for a defined patient population typically part of an Accountable Care Organizations (ACO) or similar environments. Through analyzing patient... claims, EHR, and organizational data, the Healthcare Data Analyst will contribute to identifying progress, performance, and opportunities for improvement on program, financial, quality, patient experience, and other metrics. The analytic findings will help healthcare providers in various value-based and pay-for-performance programs understand and identify methods to maximize reimbursement and improve population health. This work contributes to the development of new strategies and tactics to improve overall health care delivery and transform rural health systems across the country as they adapt from volume-based to value-based models of care.

This role will report to our Director, Analytics for VBC Client Analytics.

What will you do?
• Prepare a variety of reports including statistical analyses for stakeholders to assist with decision-making and tracking accountability.
• Respond to Ad hoc reporting requests by creating reports as needed for specific situations.
• Develop new reports, dashboards and other means to enable transparency and to monitor system-wide performance of program progress, total cost of care and clinical quality.
• Monitor trend of cost, utilization and quality of care for a defined patient population, identify factors driving the changes, and predict future trends.
• Support acquisition and implementation of new information sources, data collection strategies, data governance, and analytics.
• Help staff with data manipulation and analytic methods to improve analytic deliverables when required.
• Other duties as assigned.

We Are Looking For Someone With
• Bachelor’s Degree with concentration in health informatics, computing, epidemiology, statistics, or related field
• 3-5 years relevant experience.
• Strong SQL, Python, or R skills, ability to perform effective querying involving multiple tables and subqueries. Experience with SQL and Power BI strongly preferred.
• Ability to examine, interpret and report results of analytical initiatives to stakeholders.
• Preferred understanding of health data formats including Medicare claims, EMR, ADT feeds, lab and pharmacy. Previous experience analyzing medical claims or EMR data is strongly preferred
• Excellent oral and written communication skills; ability to present complex information in an understandable and compelling manner

