22907,97,Healthcare Data Analyst,Komodo Health,Anywhere,"We Breathe Life Into Data

At Komodo Health, our mission is to reduce the global burden of disease. And we believe that smarter use of data is essential to this mission. That’s why we built the Healthcare Map — the industry’s largest, most complete, precise view of the U.S. healthcare system — by combining de-identified, real-world patient data with innovative algorithms and decades of clinical... experience. The Healthcare Map serves as our foundation for a powerful suite of software applications, helping us answer healthcare’s most complex questions for our partners. Across the healthcare ecosystem, we’re helping our clients unlock critical insights to track detailed patient behaviors and treatment patterns, identify gaps in care, address unmet patient needs, and reduce the global burden of disease.

As we pursue these goals, it remains essential to us that we stay grounded in our values: be awesome, seek growth, deliver “wow,” and enjoy the ride. At Komodo, you will be joining a team of ambitious, supportive Dragons with diverse backgrounds but a shared passion to deliver on our mission to reduce the burden of disease — and enjoy the journey along the way.

The Opportunity At Komodo Health

The Healthcare Data Analyst will be responsible for the development, analysis and compilation of timely research findings using Komodo’s comprehensive Healthcare Map. The role will leverage both public and proprietary data sources to generate external reports and other thought leadership materials in support of marketing, communications, and media engagement.

The ideal candidate has experience identifying and implementing novel approaches to healthcare informatics analyses, collaborating in cross-functional teams, and summarizing findings in an understandable format.

Looking back on your first 12 months at Komodo Health, you will have…
• Designed and executed analytical projects for external thought leadership programs, including white papers and research briefs that shed light on key trends in the healthcare industry.
• Collaborated closely with Marketing and Clinical Innovations and Research teams to identify timely, data-driven research projects, complete data analyses, and help interpret findings.
• Become proficient in advanced database concepts and the application of SQL to query and evaluate trends in data.
• Developed an in-depth understanding of Komodo’s Healthcare Map, as well as Komodo’s proprietary software applications such as Prism and Aperture

What You Bring To Komodo...
• Understanding of the third party payment system in the United States and how this system affects the claims data
• A terminal degree in a healthcare related field with clinical experience treating patients
• Comfort reviewing data and running analysis in SQL/Snowflake
• Ability to communicate complex clinical data analysis to non-clinical and non-technical audiences

#LIRemote

Where You’ll Work

Komodo Health has a hybrid work model; we recognize the power of choice and importance of flexibility for the well-being of both our company and our individual Dragons. Roles may be completely remote based anywhere in the country listed, remote but based in a specific region, or local (commuting distance) to one of our hubs in San Francisco, New York City, or Chicago with remote work options.

What We Offer

On top of our commitment to providing competitive, fair pay for all roles at Komodo Health, we’re proud to offer robust and inclusive benefits to all Dragons at Komodo Health. We offer global time off programs, extensive internal and external career development and learning opportunities, multiple affinity groups celebrating our team’s diversity, and an annual wellness and productivity stipend to support you in being your healthiest, best self.

Equal Opportunity Statement

Komodo Health provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any type with regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws",2022-06-02,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['terminal', 'sql']"
22908,98,North America Product Supply Decision Analytics Data Manager,Bayer,Anywhere,"At Bayer we’re visionaries, driven to solve the world’s toughest challenges and striving for a world where ,Health for all, Hunger for none’ is no longer a dream, but a real possibility. We’re doing it with energy, curiosity and sheer dedication, always learning from unique perspectives of those around us, expanding our thinking, growing our capabilities and redefining ‘impossible’. There are so... many reasons to join us. If you’re hungry to build a varied and meaningful career in a community of brilliant and diverse minds to make a real difference, there’s only one choice.

North America Product Supply Decision Analytics Data Manager

Your Tasks And Responsibilities

The primary responsibilities of this role, NAPS Decision Analytics Data Manager are to:
• Create and manage all incoming data files from SAP, Data One, Teradata, Oracle and other databases and standardize data for use in analytics;
• Perform database design, logic and complex data joins; automation of data pipelines;
• Perform data quality/hygiene management (collection, cleaning and preparing large volumes of data;
• Review data for inconsistencies or anomalies that could skew analytical results;
• Manage data definitions and business rules, and related documentation in SmartSheet collaborative software and firm data dictionaries;
• Manage Decision Analytics Knowledge repository/project management folders including project deliverables, model and variable documentation, workpapers, data management templates, significant correspondence from subject matter experts, major data sources and points of contact, project code and model management;
• Generate and review documentation for all database changes or refinements;
• Maintain Decision Analytics Time Series and related databases, conducting routine maintenance as needed to ensure data integrity and data capture in provide analysts with access to essential data sets;
• Stream processes for data collection and analysis procedures to ensure fast access to metrics;
• Communicate with analysts about data changes or requirements;
• Make recommendations for software, hardware and data storage upgrades;
• Manage internal client expectations, related processes, workloads and time.

Who You Are

Your success will be driven by your demonstration of our LIFE values. More specifically related to this position, Bayer seeks an incumbent who possesses the following:

Required Qualifications:
• Bachelor’s/Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or related field;
• Minimum of one years’ of experience in data management or analysis; (Desired min 3yrs exper)
• Experience with SAP, Teradata and SQL databases, Python and other related applications;
• Ability to work with large data sets;
• Excellent organizational skills and emphasis on project completion.

YOUR APPLICATION

Bayer offers a wide variety of competitive compensation and benefits programs. If you meet the requirements of this unique opportunity, and want to impact our mission Science for a better life, we encourage you to apply now. Be part of something bigger. Be you. Be Bayer.

