With strategic leadership, develop and implement processes to identify National University (NU) intelligence needs. Researches related information, analyzes relevant facts, create, sustain useful visualizations and reports for NU. Champion the NU Tableau dashboard portfolio to provide timely and reliable data for informed decision-making and builds capacity and tools to enable... stakeholders at various levels of the organization to use data to drive continuous improvement. Apply advanced statistical analysis, data mining and various predictive modeling techniques to provide information, knowledge, collaboration and tools to substantiate growth and continued success of the University. Partner with senior leadership on vision, objectives and projects to expand the analytics projects.

Essential Functions:
• Partners with senior leadership to design, sustain and expand the NU analytical metrics and infrastructure program.
• Designs and sustains a system for managing institutional knowledge accumulated across the University. Collaborates closely with other analyst to support the analysis and reporting of data and/or information.
• Builds and executes data extraction, transfer and loading from various sources, as well as, implements appropriate security measures to ensure data integrity.
• Facilitates the transmission and understanding of data to enable fact-based decisions to various stakeholders such as leadership, faculty, administrators and staff.
• Champions the metadata management and data quality assurance to ensure data accuracy, reliability and documentation.
• Applies advanced predictive modeling, data mining, machine learning and statistical techniques to enable informed decision-making, student support and strategic initiatives.
• Builds relationships and liaises with various internal departments to drive guidance, collaboration and project success including interacting with and responding appropriately to urgent requests from multiple internal and/or external stakeholders.
• Provides reliable and well-timed data supporting strategic planning, student success initiatives and educational and operational value-added services.
• Utilizes various software applications and reporting tools to deliver actionable data to end-users in an understandable format.
• Other duties as assigned.

Supervisory Responsibilities: N/A

Requirements:

Education & Experience:
• Bachelor’s degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Social Sciences or related filed.
• Five (5) years’ relevant experience conducting data analysis, data mining or data visualization or, equivalent combination of education and experience.

Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills:
• Actively seeks opportunities to influence, build and sustain successful relationships and gain alignment with peers, functional partners and/or external partners to accomplish business objectives. Ability to participate as an active team member of the team and organization and work toward a common goal.
• Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company and oneself.
• Develops new insights into situations; questions conventional approaches; encourages new ideas and innovations; designs and implements new or cutting-edge programs/processes. Ability to generate and/or recognize imaginative or creative solutions that generate successful outcomes.
• Superior working knowledge in data collection, classification and analysis, techniques and methodologies with proven ability to independently synthesize, implement, analyze and report findings on research investigations.
• Working knowledge of information technologies including high-level proficiency and understanding of data visualization, data mining, statistical analysis, cloud computing and analytical programming languages such as SQL, R and/or Python.
• Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite Applications such as Word, Excel, Power Point, Outlook and other software applications such as Azure, Redmine; PeopleSoft, Relational Database Management, Tableau/Power BI and statistical analysis (R, Python or equivalent), required.
