Data Analyst, Medicare Advantage, Remote...

Bethesda, MD /

Product – Impact Analytics /

Full Time

/ Remote

Apply for this job

We are seeking a new member of our Impact Analytics team at Hiring Company to create and analyze datasets that answer pressing business and policy questions and work closely with stakeholdersacross Hiring Company to communicate and implement the team’s insights. This person will support analyses that leverage Medicare and commercial data, quality reports, and other data sources as appropriate. They will work in cross-functional teams to clarify key performance and policy questions facing the business and bring data to inform strategic and tactical decision making. The successful candidate will have experience with healthcare data sources, strong critical thinking and programming skills, and a passion for the intricacies of value based care.

We are flexible with respect to geographic location. The ideal candidate will be comfortable working remotely within the US, with occasional travel for in-person meetings–roughly 3-4 times per year for 2-3 days at a time. There are several regional office options for those who prefer to work in person.

As An Analyst, You Will Be Responsible For
• Utilizing Medicare reports and claims data, payer reports, and other sources as appropriate to track key measures of ACO performance and identify opportunities to improve Hiring Company’s management of shared savings contracts.
• Executing and managing descriptive analyses to identify opportunities to improve care delivery, strengthen performance measurement, and support population health product development in collaboration with Impact Analytics research scientists.
• Partnering with colleagues in Finance, Policy, Performance, and Product domains to develop and clarify business questions, think critically about solutions, and contribute to cross-departmental performance efforts.

Preferred Qualifications
