23118,308,Summer 2023 Data Intelligence Intern [Data Science/ Data Engineer],Salesforce,"San Francisco, CA","To get the best candidate experience, please consider applying for a maximum of 3 roles within 12 months to ensure you are not duplicating efforts.

About Futureforce University Recruiting...

Our Futureforce University Recruiting program is dedicated to attracting, retaining and cultivating talent. Our interns and new graduates work on real projects that affect how our business runs, giving them the opportunity to make a tangible impact on the future of our company. With offices all over the world, our recruits have the chance to collaborate and connect with fellow employees on a global scale. We offer job shadowing, mentorship programs, talent development courses, and much more.

Job Category

Intern

Job Details

Data Intelligence (Di) is the force that propels Salesforce into the 4th Industrial Revolution informing through trusted data and artificial intelligence the path forward to be smarter in every dimension. From financial forecasting, customer health, adoption insights to the utmost trusted and curated data, the Data Intelligence team is the unbiased partner to all data trailblazers at Salesforce.

Success in the Role: What would it look like?

As a Summer Intern, you will
• Learn our development process, culture, and code base then improve practices
• Collaborate and work with the Program managers, Data architect and fellow engineers on a wide range of problems from forecasting business metrics
• Work on an exciting project to build new features our customers will love, adopt and use while keeping our trusted platform stable and scalable using agile development practices
• Learn how Salesforce data collected, stored, consumed & managed.
• Have an opportunity to co-architect, design and develop strategies to deliver highly scalable products through high impact projects
• Ensure compliance with governing standards, data quality & protection principles, coding standards, workflows, tools, and product automation
• Lead the charge on taking our core products to the next level in terms of engineering maturity and architecture.
• Refine and develop new data science products, workflows, tools, and automation.
• Build tools to monitor data pipeline performance, data quality and models in production.
• Scale the operations of the data science team by building automation and libraries
• Peer review code and participate in architecture design and reviews

The Work: Typical day for Summer Intern in Data Domain
• To start with, you will have global on-boarding, engineering-specific training, and intern-specific on-boarding to ensure you are set up for success
• Days are filled with collaboration and contributing to the team goals building scalable data pipelines for both real time and batch using best practices in data modeling, ETL/ELT processes using various technologies such as Spark, Trino, Airflow.
• Hands-on development work on all aspects of building frameworks, data analysis, data provisioning, modelling, performance tuning, and optimization using version control and CICD systems such as GIT, GitFlow, Bitbucket, Jenkins etc.
• Build data solutions in AWS ecosystem and operate large-scale, high-volume, high-performance data structures for analytics
• Opportunities to participate in Executive Speaker Series, Asking me anything, Volunteer Time Off, Workshops, and team engagement.
• recruiter check-ins, general guidance and support from your team and mentors to make the most of your internship experience.
• Lastly, you have access to participate in any of our 13 Employee Resource Groups of your choice and cause that motivates you
• In addition, you will have access to resources and events to help you grow both professionally and personally.

Qualifications
• Enrolled and working towards BS or MS in Computer Science, Data Science, Machine Learning or related field.
• Please note that in order to be eligible for an internship, we require that you be returning to school the following quarter/semester to work towards completing your degree
• Must be attending a school in the U.S.
• Strong technical foresight, understanding of object-oriented programming/design, algorithms, and data structures and how to efficiently implement them into a solution
• Curiosity about how things work and tenacity to learn and bring new perspective
• A strong work ethic, customer success and quality first, self-awareness and desire to challenge and solve problems
• Strong communication skills, ability convey complex ideas, a positive approach, continuous learner and empathy to others
• Experience deploying, monitoring and maintaining data science products in cloud environments such as AWS or Microsoft Azure
• Good understanding of Machine Learning methods and Statistics, including ML project lifecycle and associated challenges at each stage of development
• Can demonstrate written production quality, well-documented and tested, scalable code in Python. Experience with tools like mlFlow, Airflow, Docker and Cloud Platforms such as AWS/GCP is ideal.
• Strong understanding of data transformations and analytics functions using tools/languages like Pandas, Sklearn, SQL and Spark

What is the leadership like for this role? What is the culture of the team like?

The Data Science and Engineering team enables various data personas with robust and scalable frameworks, services and brings data to life. We partner with data producers and platform engineers to empower data engineers and data consumers (data scientists, data analysts and Business Intelligence engineers) with data, services and APIs for data science applications, data products and business analytics. We pride ourselves in being data curious (one who has an intrinsic need to understand a data point) and passionate about improving reliability and throughput of analytics and machine learning solutions at Salesforce. We are a globally distributed inclusive team that builds and relies on trust, constantly innovate and work towards one common theme - Customer Success.

