23125,315,Market Data Compliance Specialist,Cboe Global Markets,United States,"Job Description

Cboe is one of the world’s largest exchange holding companies, offering cutting-edge trading and investment solutions to investors around the world. Cboe’s culture is unique. Our associates come to work inspired, knowing they can be part of the next market-defining breakthrough, whether they are writing code for the next technology release, paving the way for a new product... launch, or advocating for a market reform. We strive to efficiently use innovation to better serve customers and the broader marketplace.

Please note: We lead with a flexibility first work model. Ideal candidate would be available to come on site a few times per year for all hands team/department meetings (either our Chicago or NY office) but this role is mostly remote.

About The Role

The candidate selected will perform data compliance reviews and audits of data recipient compliance with the Cboe data agreement and policies.

Responsibilities
• Perform audits of Cboe data recipients to verify compliance with the Cboe data agreement and policies, including but not limited to: Review of systems using Cboe data; Understanding entitlement and permission systems for data; Verify reporting of data usage and qualification; Review external distributor subscriber agreements for disseminating data
• Communicate with the data recipient frequently to get information necessary to conduct the audit
• Use and enhance tools and techniques to verify, analyze and validate the information provided by the data recipient including but not limited to identifying unauthorized use of the Cboe data
• Prepare audit reports detailing the audit and findings
• Perform quarterly internal reviews of market data and access tracking tools to check completeness and accuracy
• Performs other duties as assigned

Required Skills
• 3-5 years of compliance/regulatory/audit experience
• Knowledge of writing scalable code using Python programming language and creating ad hoc Tableau dashboards
• Proven PC skills within the work environment that include frequent use of Microsoft Word and PowerPoint and advanced skills in Excel
• Highly organized with strong analytical skills
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills to include previous work experience that required preparing written analysis and documents
• Self-motivated, inquisitive, and the ability to complete projects and work assignments both working independently and as a member of a team within deadlines
• Prioritize work to meet objectives of multiple or competing priorities/projects; shift focus quickly relative to changing priorities; identify, communicate and strategize regarding situations that may impact successful execution
• Respond to inquiries or requests for assistance promptly and courteously; identify customer needs through active listening and clarifying questions; meet commitments and check for customer satisfaction; manage difficult or emotional customer situations
• Ability to make rational judgments on complex matters

Preferred Qualifications
• Ability to make rational judgments on complex matters
• Knowledge of commercial entitlements control systems such as Refinitiv’s Data Access Control System (DACS), Bloomberg’s EMRS etc.
• Knowledge of the market data business specifically index and derivatives product development, modeling, and management
• Financial Information Associate certification a plus
• Experience in conducting onsite and remote audits of the trading systems, databases, entitlements systems, cloud technologies, etc.
• Generic knowledge of market data contracts and policies

Education Requirement
• Bachelor’s Degree in Finance, Technology, or related subject

Cool Benefits At a Glance
• $20K per year MBA tuition reimbursement after 6 month waiting period (up to $60k)
• 401k match up to 8%
• Free lunch, snacks and beverages during all in-office workdays

The Cboe Experience

Whether you are just beginning your career or are a senior-level professional, working at Cboe will offer you countless opportunities to develop skills, make an impact through meaningful contributions, and gain rich experiences at an accelerated pace. By working collaboratively with smart, genuine and hardworking colleagues, you will build enduring relationships through frequent collaboration that will serve you well throughout your career, regardless of your chosen path. And, along your exceptional career journey at Cboe you’ll receive amazing benefits and robust rewards.

