23127,317,Data Analytics Security Manager,Cardinal Health,"Jefferson City, MO","Headquartered in Dublin, Ohio, Cardinal Health, Inc. (NYSE: CAH) is a global, integrated healthcare services and products company connecting patients, providers, payers, pharmacists and manufacturers for integrated care coordination and better patient management. Backed by nearly 100 years of experience, with more than 50,000 employees in nearly 60 countries, Cardinal Health ranks among the top... 20 on the Fortune 500.

We are currently seeking a Data Analytics Security Manager to join our growing augIntel team.

Department Overview

augmented Intelligence (augIntel) builds automation, analytics and artificial intelligence solutions that drive success for Cardinal Health by creating material savings, efficiencies and revenue growth opportunities. The team drives business innovation by leveraging emerging technologies and turning them into differentiating business capabilities.

Job Overview

The Data Analytics Security Manager will be responsible for Security and Compliance of various Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions. The Manager will be responsible to oversee all aspects of Security and Compliance for AugIntel team by acting as a liaison with Enterprise Security, Audit and Compliance teams. Responsible for translating SOX, HIPAA and GDPR controls to technical requirements and operating procedures to ensure compliance across Data Platforms and Analytics solutions. The ideal candidate for this role will have blend of Security, Compliance and Data Analytics skills.

The Manager brings in a product mindset and leverages agile practices to craft and drive iterations building new Security controls, addressing gaps and incorporate automations to improve efficiency and usability of the technologies.

Additionally, the Manager brings in a Service Provider mindset, demonstrate exceptional interpersonal skills, strong leadership, relationship management to build a strong and cohesive team that focuses on security, compliance, and usability

Responsibilities:
• Maintain a comprehensive set of policies, standards, processes, and procedures to achieve compliance across Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions
• Maintain governance program that ensures security policies, standards and process are being adhered to by new products and Analytics consumers
• Ensure healthcare information security best practice controls are in place and they adhere to HIPAA utilizing a common control framework (i.e., NIST, HITRUST CSF)
• Involved in completing security questionnaires and representing the security and privacy of the Data Solutions in a professional manner
• Serve as liaison to Cardinal Health Enterprise security and audit teams and help influence the policies and processes to be tailored for modern day analytics and self-service analytics
• Work with the engineering and operations teams to ensure that the infrastructure design meets Cardinal Health, and industry security requirements
• Monitor security trends for Data lakes, Data Operations, and drive adoption of best practices
• Conduct risk analysis and advise senior management on appropriate remediation
• Investigate, drive resolution, and document security incidents
• Manages expectations with key stakeholders, builds and fosters relationships
• Participates in the development of policies and procedures to achieve specific goals
• Leverages understanding of Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions to tailor security policies, standards, and processes, to secure Analytics systems

Qualifications:

Required
• Proven information security related work experience.
• Experience with HIPAA/HITECH regulations and guidelines for securing ePHI data
• Proficient working in multiple Security domains (e.g., Cryptography, Authentication, Authorization, OWASP, Vulnerability Management, Threat Modeling, Identity Management)
• Knowledge of Data Platforms and Analytics Solutions and Knowledge in Big Data systems, Data Lakes and Analytics related field managing Build & Run teams
• Understanding of ML/AI concepts and compliance implications for ML/AL in the industry
• Aware of common security vulnerabilities like OWASP Top 10 and Ransomware with the ability to successfully communicate the remediation to the business
• Experience advising and mentoring diverse teams.

Preferred
• Professional certification in the information security space (e.g., CISM, CISSP, CISA, GIAC) or other security certification at a similar level.
• Familiarity with security frameworks associated with one or more industry standards (e.g., HITRUST CSF, COBIT, COSO, HIPAA/HITECH, ISO, ITIL, NIST, PCI DSS, SOC or SOX)
• Involvement or knowledge of several aspects related to a SSAE 16 SOC 2 Audit
• Understanding of protocols underlying security domains (e.g., FIDO, U2F, Web-Auth, SSO, SAML, OAuth
• Understanding of Data Analytics solutions in Cloud

Covid

For any onsite, non-remote employees

A Covid-19 vaccination is required in order to be employed in this position. This includes either:

2 doses of the Moderna or Pfizer vaccine

1 dose of the Johnson & Johnson vaccine

