23204,394,Third Party Risk Program Data Analyst - Remote,Red Hat,Anywhere,"About The Job

The Red Hat Global Resilience Management team is seeking a Third Party Risk Program Data Analyst to join us remotely or in Raleigh, NC, USA. In this role, you will collaboratively support the global Business Resilience team to help ensure data quality and accuracy of our Third Party Risk Management (TPRM) and Business Resilience programs. TPRM at Red Hat establishes and supports... the framework for identifying, categorizing, monitoring and mitigating risk associated with doing business with third party organizations.

In this role, you’ll support Red Hat’s success by analyzing complex data from internal and external systems to identify and interpret trends, strengths and weaknesses (issues). You’ll work with and support key global stakeholders including application development, information security, procurement, risk and compliance teams as well as third parties to bring issues to a timely, satisfactory conclusion.

What You Will Do
• Monitor TPRM life cycle activities and data (risk assessment & due diligence, supplier validation/onboarding, risk conclusion and termination) to identify process or data issues.
• Develop metrics and reports that ensure issues are identified, analyzed, reported and controlled throughout the third-party life cycle to ensure compliance with policies and regulations.
• Ensure appropriate TPRM activities are completed on time, identifying and managing issues to a timely and satisfactory conclusion.
• Serve as a key point of contact supporting global stakeholders and third parties engaging with the TPRM process using ServiceNow’s Vendor Risk Management (VRM) and other internal and external data sources.
• Raise and monitor TPRM enhancements through the development lifecycle to meet scheduled releases.
• Update TPRM procedures and education materials to align with TPRM guidelines.
• Assist in the education of Red Hat associates on TPRM and their role in the process.
• Work with the business owners through the risk escalation process to document appropriate corrective action plans and monitor to conclusion.
• Such other activities as may be assigned by your manager.

What You Will Bring
• One+ years of experience or equivalent college level course work in a risk, issue management or related control function, understanding of Third Party Risk Management a plus.
• Command of data analysis and reporting tools/applications (aka. Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Microsoft Office or Apache OpenOffice) required
• Highly organized and detail oriented individual with ability to work independently with little direction and/or supervision in a global, remote environment.
• Knowledge of ServiceNow and/or Vendor Risk Management platform a plus.
• Flexibility to support a global audience and work with a remote, global team is a must.
• Excellent communication, facilitation and presentation skills.
• Understanding of information security, data privacy, business controls and business continuity requirements are a plus.
• Ability to communicate technical security and operational risks to non-technical business stakeholders.
• Bachelor's degree preferred, or equivalent combination of education and experience.
• Minimal (up to 10%) international travel is possible",2022-07-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
23205,395,"Principal Analyst, Data Science & Analytics",Zillow,Anywhere,"About The Team

The Zillow Analytics organization is passionate about understanding the customer journey on our platforms through deep analysis and measurement. We relentlessly advocate for a seamless and delightful home shopping experience from dream to reality! The team works closely across the organization to discover strategic opportunities in areas spanning the search and discovery process... membership and re-engagement, evaluation and curation of potential homes, and personalization for both the Zillow and Trulia brands. We scale this work by partnering with engineering teams to build and maintain key analytics tools and infrastructure.

About The Role

Zillow is looking for Principal Analyst to join a growing world-class analytics group dedicated to excellence. In this role you will:
• Lead analytical efforts across the organization.
• Define, measure, and report on success metrics for complex projects and pilots.
• Use data to identify large opportunities for product and operational improvements.
• Partner with product, marketing, and operations leaders across the organization to deliver impactful solutions to business problems.
• Partner with customers to understand and clarify requirements to creatively solve complex business problems with analytic solutions.
• Recruit, hire, and mentor extraordinary analysts and data scientists.

In addition to a competitive base salary this position is also eligible for equity awards based on factors such as experience, performance and location. Actual amounts will vary depending on experience, performance and location.

Who you are
• 8-10 years experience in an analytical role.
• 3-4 years of experience communicating regularly with executive stakeholders.
• Strong bias for action and impact informed by your data insights.
• Ability to design and communicate your analytical roadmap to peers and stakeholders.
• Strong business acumen, communication skills and the ability to work cross-functionally and connect customer problems to business strategy.
• Expert at applying the “80/20” rule and estimating the impact and relative priority of a potential analysis project.
• Deep, intuitive understanding of core statistical concepts, such as probability, randomness, correlation and sampling distributions.
• Expert in SQL, Excel, and either Tableau, Mode, or other visualization software. Scripting and automation experience is preferred.
• Experience leading self and mentoring junior data analysts and/or data scientists.

Get to know us

Zillow is reimagining real estate to make it easier to unlock life’s next chapter.

As the most-visited real estate website in the United States, Zillow® and its affiliates help movers find and win their home through digital solutions, first class partners, and easier buying, selling, financing and renting experiences. Millions of people visit Zillow Group sites every month to start their home search, and now they can rely on Zillow to help make it easier to move. The work we do is helping people move from dreaming to transacting — and no matter what job you're in, you will play a critical role in making this vision a reality.

Our efforts to streamline the real estate transaction are supported by a deep-rooted culture of innovation, our passion to redefine the employee experience, a fundamental commitment to Equity and Belonging, and world-class benefits. We’re also setting the standard for work experiences of the future, where our employees are supported in doing their best work and living a flexible, well-balanced life. But don’t just take our word for it. Read recent reviews on Glassdoor and recent recognition from multiple organizations, including: the 100 Best Companies to Work For in 2022 list, Glassdoor Employees’ Choice Award, honoring the Best Places to Work in 2022, Bloomberg Gender-Equality Index 2022, Human Rights Campaign (HRC) Corporate Equity Index and Best Place to Work for LGBTQ Equality 2022, and TIME 100 Most Influential Companies list.

