Job Summary

The Marketing Analytics Manager will be responsible for establishing and tracking marketing KPIs & metrics, analyzing marketing and customer data to discover insights, and providing dashboards and reports for CMO and marketing leadership teams to monitor and analyze marketing performance.

Essential Duties/Responsibilities
• Own the marketing analytics function.
• Manage and coach junior data analysts.
• Review and complete the definitions of marketing KPIS and metrics.
• Maintain and enhance the CMO dashboard.
• Build BI dashboards and reports for marketing leaders to make data-driven decisions.
• Provide weekly marketing performance reports & updates.
• Conduct deep analysis of marketing data to discover insights about campaign performance, channel effectiveness, demand gen efficiency and pipeline conversion, etc.
• Benchmark performance across all online channels and advising on KPIs, conducting trending analysis.
• Analyze customer segments and their journey against target KPIs, such as funnel conversion and digital engagements, providing optimization recommendations.
• Create PowerPoint slides and narratives to share insights across sales, marketing and product teams.

Education

JOB REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS
• Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience.

Training Requirements (licenses, Programs, Or Certificates)
• Tableau certification a plus.

Experience
