23294,484,Data Conversion Analyst,ABC Fitness Solutions,Anywhere,"Company : ABC Fitness Solutions

It's fun to work in a company where people truly BELIEVE in what they're doing...

We're committed to bringing passion and customer focus to the business.

Job Description

ABC Fitness Solutions is seeking to add a Data Conversion Analyst to our team. This role is responsible for facilitating the manipulation of data from multiple software platforms in order to convert a database from an existing billing system to ABC Fitness Solutions IBM iSeries and the Oracle based software, Datatrak. Processing the conversion using different software tools, such as, Actian, Excel, MS Access, SQL,etc. is a tedious job requiring extreme attention to detail. This position will evaluate the data during the conversion process, identifying exceptions, anomalies, and variations in the data; and document/communicate to the clients.

The Data Conversion Analyst will work with the client throughout the conversion process, continuing the evaluation and review of the data. As well as prepare the data, make the necessary adjustments at an account level, preparing the account to be activated and billed. That Data Conversion Analyst will remain assigned to the client for the entirety of the transitional period to assist them with their acclimation to our company.

WHAT YOU’LL DO:
• Maintain consistent review of the data conversion schedule. Must be constantly aware of all recent and future conversion outlined on the schedule.
• Review formatted data to ensure all records, fields and tables have been formatted appropriately.
• Verify all necessary backup and supporting tables are included in the file.
• Is responsible for verifying the required documentation from the Project Manager has been received according to the timelines established.
• Review all data conversion documentation provided by the Project Manager and the client. Identify any pre-conversion questions or concerns. Communicate this to the Project Manager.
• Communicate with the Project Manager and Data Conversion Architect to ensure the success of the conversion.
• Using Actian, MS Access, SQL and MS Excel; create detailed documentation outlining any and all variations, exceptions, and anomalies in the data.
• Communicate with the Project Manager and the client regarding all variations and exceptions in the data.
• Communicate any specific instructions, procedures or processes needed based on requirements of each specific client in the areas of Data Processing, Client Services and any other relevant division of the company
• Provide post conversion and post amendment documentation to client.
• Communicate the finalization of the transition period

WHAT YOU’LL NEED:
• High school diploma or equivalent
• College degree (preferred)
• Must have minimum 2 + year experience as a Data Conversion Analyst

But wait, there’s more…

BONUS SKILLS:
• Knowledge of I-Series database platform
• Knowledge of SQL
• Advanced in Microsoft Office products
• Self starter: Ability to multi-task projects with multiple deadlines
• Flexible schedule
• Excellent organizational skills
• Must be able to excel in a fast-paced work environment
• Ability to make independent decisions and take calculated risks
• Must be able to accurately and effectively communicate both verbally and in writing
• Must be extremely detail-oriented and able to make sound decisions
• Professional Phone Skills

WHAT’S IN IT FOR YOU:
• A work environment built on ideation, collaboration, and our Core Values of integrity, excellence, results, respect, team & community.
• A fast-growing & fast-paced start-up culture prime for the picking. It’s a vibe!
• People-focused benefits including Medical, Dental, Vision, 401K, Best Life & more.

ABC’S COMMITMENT TO DIVERSITY, EQUALITY, BELONGING AND INCLUSION:

ABC is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We are intentional about creating an environment where employees, our clients and other stakeholders feel valued and inspired to reach their full potential and make authentic connections. We foster a workplace culture that embraces each person’s diversity, including the extent to which they are similar or different. ABC leaders believe that an equitable and inclusive culture is not only the right thing to do, it is a business imperative. Read more about our commitment to diversity, equality, belonging and inclusion at abcfitness.com

ABOUT ABC:

ABC Fitness Solutions (abcfitness.com) is the premier provider of software and related services for the fitness industry, and has built a reputation for excellence in support for clubs and their members. ABC is the trusted provider to boost performance and create a total fitness experience for members of clubs of all sizes whether a multi-location chain, franchise or an independent gym.

Founded in 1981, ABC helps nearly 16,000 clubs and facilities globally perform better and more profitably offering a comprehensive SaaS club management solution that enables club operators to achieve optimal performance. ABC Fitness is a Thoma Bravo portfolio company, a private equity firm focused on investing in software and technology companies (thomabravo.com).

