23307,497,DPR Data Analyst,Clearlink,Anywhere,"Job Posting Title

DPR Data Analyst...

Who We Are

Job Description:

At Clearlink we value a people-first mentality by providing our employees with resources and flexibility to live their best lives, strive to build brands that guide users to decisions, and excel in the ever-changing digital marketing and tech industry. We believe in opening doors for new opportunities and empowering our people.Our team of Clearlinkers are highly driven, inquisitive, diverse, empathetic, and exceptionally passionate individuals.

Since we opened our doors in 2003, Clearlink has been committed to growth and opportunity. We’re not afraid to go against the grain and spark innovation in uncharted territory. Our passion for people is changing the way businesses are built and acquired to help grow digital brands and elevate user experiences. We do this by creating a culture of belonging and inclusion, inviting everyone to Be an Owner—to speak up, share ideas, and safely bring their whole selves to work!

Why Work For Us

We care deeply about hiring the best talent and supporting the wellbeing of our people by working together in an environment where everyone can make an impact, no matter what your area of expertise is. As Clearlinkers we value the meaning of community and we celebrate our diversity through our Employee Resource Groups. Our ever-expanding reach means we’re always finding more ways to help people make better decisions that improve their everyday lives, which is why we need you!

Who We're Looking For - DPR Data Analyst

Clearlink is looking for a Data Analyst to join the Digital PR team and assist in the creation and production of data-centric content for earned media marketing campaigns. This role sits right at the intersection of data analytics, digital PR, and brand storytelling.

Alongside a team of Digital PR Specialists and designers, you will be responsible for ideating, researching, compiling, analyzing and telling stories through data, which will then be crafted into promotional campaigns for public relations and marketing. These data visualizations will vary in format — maps, surveys, charts, reports — and will be pitched to journalists and publications in varying industries with the end goal of earning media coverage, increasing brand awareness, and driving traffic to our web properties. The ability to give direction on how to best visualize data is crucial.

You will be expected to utilize our own proprietary data as well as scrape, submit records requests, or compile data sets from scratch to help our Consumer Trends reporter and Digital PR Specialists tell clear, compelling visual stories about a wide range of topics. If you think you can transform raw data sets into compelling stories and help designers create meaningful visual illustrations to accompany those stories, this is the job for you!

Our ideal candidate loves data and is able to coherently “speak data” to others. In addition, this individual has a strong sense of what it takes to use data to create a story that will garner media attention. To be successful in the role, you must be passionately curious, equal parts creative and analytical, resourceful, and self-motivated.

The Impact You Will Make
• Advanced knowledge of Microsoft PowerPoint, Word, and Excel
• Experience working in a data-centric environment
• Experience with using data to tell stories
• Knowledge of how media properties operate
• Understanding or work experience in data journalism
• Detail-oriented and organized
• Strong SQL, R, SAS, or equivalent data management and analytics software.
• Ability to influence and advance projects in a cross-functional, matrixed environment
• Basic understanding of statistical methods and predictive analytics
• Ability to leverage BI tools such as Google Data Studio and Lookr
• Experience querying APIs to gather data
• Experience with HTML5 , CSS and/or Python
• Preferred but not required: Knowledge of programming languages like Javascript, digital production and development experience working with Adobe Creative Suite, and familiarity with common statistical and data visualization libraries

What You Need
• Bachelor’s 4 -year BS/BA degree (preferably in data journalism, data-visualization and storytelling, business analytics, statistics, information design)

Perks Just For You
• Medical/Vision/Dental - Clearlink offers employees competitive health coverage options for you and your family. (Yes, this includes domestic partners too!)
• 401k Matching - After one year of employment, employees are eligible for a 401k company match.
• Flexible time off - Time off starts at 20 days annually accrued on a weekly basis, and increases with tenure.
• Paid Parental Leave - Employees can benefit from 2 weeks paid parental leave during their first year, and up to 6 weeks following one year of employment.
• Tuition & Conference Funding- We have a dedicated budget for tuition reimbursement and work-related conferences.
• Learning and Development - Clearlink offers a choice-based learning program focused on development (skills, career path, leadership), our business, and your well-being (boundaries, communication, work-life balance).
• Home office assistance - Corporate new hires get up to a $200 desk reimbursement.
• Pick your perks allowance - Clearlink partners with Fringe to offer employees the greater benefit of exploring their hobbies and interests with a monthly accrual of points to spend on things they love! (AirBnB, InstaCart, Cruises, etc.)

More About Us

As an equal opportunity employer, we believe everyone is a part; no one is apart.

We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment.

