DB&A’s Managed Services Team focuses on developing and implementing long-term solutions for our clients. Our customizable resource management software provides additional support for continued

growth and improvement after the completion of any engagement. Once this proprietary software is installed at a client’s facility, DB&A’s Managed Services Team offers ongoing analytical, coaching, and leadership development services. Our goal is to ensure clients are able to promote continuous improvements and sustain the results of the consulting project.

Responsibilities
• Utilize DB&A’s proven methodology to drive the sustainability of performance improvements through the implementation of management tools and processes This includes gathering, compiling, and analyzing data, as well as requirements for the Project and Managed Services Teams to implement WorkSite
• Partner with clients to conduct periodic audits and identify client performance improvement opportunities
• Provide ongoing analytical feedback and coaching to clients with a focus on action planning and execution while maintaining a culture of continuous improvement
Requirements:
• Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering, Business, or related technical field
• Strong analytical ability to conduct trend analysis and draw conclusions for required actions
• Experienced problem solver, defining root causes through a variety of problem-solving tools
• Ability to work cross functionally, gathering information from multiple areas and driving alignment
• Demonstrated ability to learn and utilize client systems to access and analyze pertinent information
• Working knowledge of software implementation process is a plus
• Ability to collect and verify pertinent client information relating to performance management, including organizational structures, KPIs, metrics, etc.
• Strong data analytics and Excel capabilities including statistical analysis, pivot tables, graphing, etc.
• Ability to rapidly and frequently learn new industries and environments in a short period of time
• Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to meet the milestones and deadlines on schedule as outlined
• Ability to develop and present leadership workshops to clients
• Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to interact with all levels of client’s organization
• Strong client management experience

The Equal Employment Opportunity Policy of this corporation is to provide a fair and equal employment opportunity for all job applicants regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability. Our corporation hires and promotes individuals solely on the basis of their qualifications for the job to be filled.

This corporation believes that all employees should be provided with a work environment which enables each team member to be productive and to work to the best of his/her ability. We do not condone or tolerate an atmosphere of intimidation or harassment based on race, color religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability.

