23468,658,Enterprise Automation Sr Data Analyst,Northwestern Mutual,United States,"At Northwestern Mutual, we are strong, innovative and growing. We invest in our people. We care and make a positive difference.

The mission of the Enterprise Automation function is to relentlessly pursue seamless experiences for our clients, field, and employees by integrating experience-led process improvement methodologies and workflow automation capabilities. Our function takes a... collaborative, end-to-end, process-first approach to automation as we drive sustainable process improvements for existing experiences, and design and deliver processes that drive new experiences.

As a member of the Discovery, Insights, and Analytics team within Enterprise Automation, this role provides impactful data visualization and analysis to inform this mission.

Job Description

Primary Duties and Responsibilities
• Develops and implements user-friendly data visualization solutions which inform, guide, support, and enable data-driven decisions.
• Accesses and prepares data from various internal and external sources for visualization and analysis.
• Utilizes appropriate statistical and analytical methods to perform quantitative and qualitative data analysis.
• Researches and evaluates process and task mining solutions to assist with automation discovery work.
• Performs current state- future state modeling of business processes.
• Innovates new metrics to describe and analyze complex business processes.
• Provides consultation to business partners and participates in cross-functional teams to address visualization and analytical needs.
• Applies knowledge of key performance indicators, objectives and key results, and other metrics to understand business performance and outcomes.
• Summarizes analysis into user-friendly deliverables by translating detailed data into audience-appropriate communication and recommendations.
• Applies new perspectives, creative problem solving, and inter-departmental connections to improve analytical capabilities.
• Influences and shares best practices with peers through coaching and mentoring around core methodologies, standards and processes.
• Effectively manages and prioritizes multiple concurrent projects.

Qualifications
• Bachelor's degree in a field that emphasizes data analysis (e.g., Data Science, Computer Science, MIS, Mathematics, Statistics, Business).
• 5+ years of progressively responsible experience in data analytics that support business decisions/outcomes.
• Experience in visualization tooling like PowerBI or Tableau.
• Experience with data querying and analytical tools such as SAS, SQL, MS Excel, SPSS, R or other tool.
• Demonstrated ability to deliver results and recommendations in written, verbal and presentation form at an appropriate level for a variety of business audiences.
• Proven excellence in problem solving, research, quantitative analysis and analytical working techniques.
• Strong aptitude and desire for learning new platforms, analytic and presentation tools; modeling, analytic and quantitative techniques.
• Demonstrated ability to gather information systematically; consider a broad range of issues or factors; grasp complexities and perceive relationships among problems or issues; use accurate logic in analysis.
• Initiative to independently design and develop own deliverables while still being a team player.
• Ability to be adaptable to changing business needs, manage and prioritize concurrent assignments, and handle ambiguity.
• Ability to generate new insights and go beyond the status quo; recognize the need for new or modified approaches.
• Strong analytical capability with ability to meet deadlines.

