23475,665,DWC Senior Research/Data Analyst,State of Missouri,"Jefferson City, MO","Senior Research/Data Analyst

Salary Range: $45,000 - $65,000...

Why You Will Love This Position

The Division of Workers’ Compensation offers a dynamic, energetic and engaging environment to flourish and to demonstrate operational excellence. The Division is modernizing its internal and external processes and procedures and there is immense opportunity to contribute to an exciting, forward-thinking, fast-moving, collaborative environment. As part of the team, you will enjoy the genuine spirit of cooperation and shared goals all revolving around helping the citizens of Missouri.

The Enterprise Functions Unit supports functions Division wide by providing data analytics, statistical reporting, training and reviewing processes for improvement and standardization. As the Division moves forward with modernizing, the unit will also provide technical assistance and communications for both internal and external stakeholders.

What You Will Do
• Use Statistical Analysis System (SAS) and Tableau to collect, tabulate, and assemble raw data to be used when completing research projects and compiling data and visualizations for the Division’s various constituents and internal requestors.
• Develop, lead and conduct complex research studies and/or assess impact of proposed legislation and presenting findings to Division and Department management and other stakeholders.
• Plan, develop, and present new ideas, concepts and strategies related to systems and techniques.
• Analyze, organize, and present data requested by the Division’s various constituents and internal requestors.
• Work with minimal direction in responding to a variety of ad hoc requests via tables, charts, data visualization, written summaries and verbal presentations.
• Assist with the accurate and timely production of ongoing reporting required by the division and its stakeholders
• Advise on policy, conduct policy research, serve as technical consultants, and may also advise or review the work of lower-level staff.
• Provide statistical and analytical support to the Division including conducting research, compiling and analyzing data and preparing numerous reports

Qualifications

All you need for success:
• Bachelor’s degree and 2 or more years of relevant experience and/or appropriate certification (Substitutions may be allowed.) Title and salary will be determined based upon candidate’s relevant experience and certifications.

Desired Attributes
• Knowledge of methods and techniques of collection, compilation, and analysis of research data.
• Knowledge of research design and ability to plan and execute research studies and present information in a clear and concise manner.
• Ability to effectively communicate a story from data through graphics such as flows, diagrams, and Tableau visualizations.
• Advanced knowledge of research methods and analysis, computer information systems, and statistical software
• Skilled in SQL and/or Statistical Analysis System (SAS) and have other relevant database related experience. Tableau experience highly preferred.
• Moderate to high degree of technical writing and reporting skills
• Ability to use substantial independent judgment when applying technical concepts and methodologies.

More Reasons To Love This Position

The State of Missouri offers an excellent benefits package that includes a defined pension plan, generous amounts of leave and holiday time, and eligibility for health insurance coverage. Your total compensation is more than the dollars you receive in your paycheck. To help demonstrate the value of working for the State of Missouri, we have created an interactive Total Compensation Calculator. This tool provides a comprehensive view of benefits and more that are offered to prospective employees. The Total Compensation Calculator and other applicant resources can be found here .

If you have questions about this position, please contact: Amber Bauer at amber.bauer@labor.mo.gov .

The State of Missouri is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees",2022-08-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'sas']"
