Job Description...

OPIS, a Dow Jones company, provides price transparency across the global fuel supply chain, including the Spot, Wholesale Rack and Retail markets. OPIS enables customers to buy and sell energy commodities with confidence via multi-platform access to accurate data, real-time news, powerful software and educational events. Our commitment to reliability is reinforced by personalized customer service and constant innovation. OPIS listens to what energy stakeholders need and responds with flexible and easy-to-use products. Navigating world fuel markets is complex – OPIS makes it simpler.

Your Role

Do you have a passion for data governance and understand how it creates substantial value to a business? Do you believe that the quality and integrity of trusted data can transform an entire organization in its ability to deliver best-in-class information and analytics products? If so, come join an excellent team to achieve our data governance mission!

We are looking for a Senior Data Analyst, I to work closely with our broad data assets across the organization as we launch an exciting new enterprise governance program. This role will be empowered to provide leadership and management of key governance activities related to metadata management for our oil pricing business unit.

Your Main Responsibilities
• Perform application front-end work related to metadata management
• Create a business glossary of terms and identify all enterprise data assets
• Apply proven communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills to help support the implementation of new metadata management processes
• Document business rules, transformation rules, calculations, and derivations
• Document data security/privacy levels according to existing policy and standards
• Become a subject matter expert with our metadata management software and support implementation efforts, including training colleagues to leverage system capabilities
• Create accurate impact and lineage capabilities
• Document stewardship to enable accountability
• Ensure metadata quality, consistency, currency, and security
• Leverage KPI metrics to increase utilization and adoption

Your Expertise
• University degree (Bachelors or equivalent) in Business Administration, Operations Management, Quality, Computer Sciences, or related fields
• Typically requires 5+ years industry related experience
• Technical and/or business writing experience
