23609,799,"Associate Manager, Medical Affairs Field Data Analyst",Seagen,Anywhere,"Description

Position at Seagen...

Seagen is a global, multi-product biotechnology company dedicated to developing and commercializing transformative cancer medicines. As the industry leader in antibody-drug conjugate (ADC) technology, we pioneered a new generation in the science of harnessing antibodies to deliver cell-killing agents directly to cancer cells. Seagen’s dedication to improving the lives of cancer patients goes beyond science, and we believe that every employee has a role in contributing to this mission. By working together with a shared dedication and diverse perspectives, we are able to reach our full potential and make a real difference in the world. Seagen is a fast-growing company and has an abundance of opportunities available for you to grow your career. Put your passion to work at Seagen and join us!

Summary

The focus of this role is to provide support to the Field-Based Medical Affairs team with data analysis, activity tracking report generation and optimal utilization of multiple databases and resources including our Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system. The Associate Manager, Field Operations Analyst will report to the Director of Scientific Engagement and work closely with the US field Medical Science Liaison (MSL) / Clinical Value & Outcomes (CVO) medical leadership team. This individual will be the point of contact with our IT Department and will be accountable for helping to create tools and reports to track MSL/CVO Key Opinion Leader (KOL) / Key Decision Maker (KDM) engagement.

Principal Responsibilities
• Partner with MSL/CVO leadership to understand IT / database business needs, propose solutions and lead the development of projects
• Provide technical expertise for existing tools and platforms for KOL/KDM identification, profiling and engagement including CRM tools, KOL/KDM management databases & data visualization tools for tracking and reporting KOL/KDM engagement metrics
• Optimize MSL/CVO and management’s use of Veeva CRM via:
• Maintain current call entry options for MSL/CVO teams
• Create, run, and analyze manager reports to appropriately capture the team’s KOL/KDM engagement
• Develop and maintain appropriate MSL/CVO and manage Dashboards
• Support Veeva Link utilization, training, and enhancements
• Continue development of the HCP Dashboard to maximize comprehensive tracking of Seagen KOL/KDM activities
• Understand and maximize MSL/CVO use of additional resources as needed including Power BI reports and Veeva Vault
• Provide additional database support / analysis to other Medical Affairs functions i.e., Scientific Alliances
• Collaborate with key internal stakeholders including IT, Commercial, Clinical Development and external vendors to support Medical Affairs databases and data analysis

Required Qualifications
• Bachelor’s / Master’s Degree preferred (or equivalent experience) with specialization in Computer Science, MIS, IT, or other computer related disciplines
• Veeva CRM expertise
• Prior pharmaceutical company experience preferred (Medical Affairs, Clinical Development or Commercial)
• Familiarity with KOL databases and engagement tracking tools
• High level of proficiency with Excel, PowerPoint, and Word
• Strong communication skills with an ability to work successfully in a complex, global, matrix organization
• Collaborative nature and flexibility with shifting priorities
• Ability to assess and optimize existing systems and tools to drive results
• Proven track record of strong teamwork, innovation, and project management

As the leading employer in our industry in the Pacific Northwest, Seagen is proud to offer a competitive total compensation package as well as a comprehensive benefits program designed to support the whole lives of our employees and their families. Benefits include medical, vision and dental coverage, group and supplemental life insurance, 401(k) with company match, tuition reimbursement, relocation assistance and much more. To learn more about Seagen, please visit www.seagen.com. 

Seagen is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applications will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, age, gender identity, sexual orientation, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, protected veteran status, disability status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law. 

To prevent the spread of COVID-19, and as an integral part of its public health and safety measures, Seagen requires that all newly-hired employees be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 before commencing employment, subject to reasonable accommodation and other requirements of applicable federal, state, and local law",2022-08-16,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['word', 'power_bi', 'powerpoint', 'excel']"
23616,806,Data Analyst,National Veterinary Associates,Anywhere,"The Company

Based in Greater Los Angeles, National Veterinary Associates (“NVA”) is the largest private owner of unbranded freestanding veterinary hospitals in North America, with over 1,500 companion animal and equine veterinary hospitals, and pet resort locations in the United States, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, and Singapore...

NVA has grown rapidly over its history via a combination of acquisition, de novo and same-store initiatives. NVA competes in a $30 billion industry that has grown faster than GDP over 20+ years with few exceptions. The industry is highly fragmented with approximately 22,000 veterinary hospitals; fewer than 5,000 are part of large chains. Advancing medical sophistication and technology combined with the evolving human-animal bond is driving greater spend per pet and veterinarians will look to partner with companies that have the capital, expertise and management talent as the industry evolves.

A cornerstone of the NVA culture is a servant leadership approach to our business, our hospitals, our pet resorts and our teams. We find people who exemplify the same servant leadership approach are best suited for NVA. We are a community dedicated to the love of animals and the people who love them.

The Role

NVA is seeking a Data Analyst to support the Client Service Center (“CSC”) in their strategic initiatives. The Client Service Center is an extension of our locations by assisting our sites with outbound calls, inbound calls, wellness plans and other administrative tasks.

Specifically, the Data Analyst will support the CSC on cleansing data, managing several key reports, identifying strategic insights from the data, and presenting these findings to management. Key reports consist of productivity, performance, and revenue reporting as well as maintaining the monthly budget and chargeback reporting. Chargebacks are the process of allocating the cost of the CSC’s resources to the individual locations or departments which use them.

The ideal candidate has 1 to 3 years’ experience in transforming raw data sets to useable reports and outputs, with an interest in building tools that systemize and create reporting efficiencies. The Data Analyst must demonstrate a mastery of Excel and be able to articulate insights to Manager – C-level audiences. This role has a high level of leadership exposure. A bonus would be knowledge of call center operations and software. The role is remote.

Job Description
• Possess business understanding needed to conduct analysis through collaboration with business experts, field partners, and other team members.
• Analyze large amounts of information to discover hospital and/or program trends and patterns.
• Create standard re-occurring reports that improves overall department performance.
• Conduct data cleaning, and data quality management. Maintain appropriate documentation.
• Plan work activities thoughtfully to ensure project and deliverable deadlines are met.
• Perform ad-hoc analysis to evaluate key business issues and develop results-driven solutions
• Support monthly budgeting and forecasting process

Qualifications
• Bachelor’s Degree in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Computer Science, Business Analytics, Economics, Marketing, Mathematics, Healthcare Administration, or equivalent work experience.
• Experience and working knowledge of Excel, PowerPoint, QuickBase, PowerBI, MicroStrategy.
• High level of motivation and a strong desire to find creative solutions to challenging situations.
• Demonstrated experience with projects that require both attention to detail and an ability to deliver on deadline.
• Excellent communication skills. Able to translate information into insights management may act on.

Personal Attributes

The successful candidate will be adaptable, solution-oriented, and curious. They demonstrate a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion through personal development, modeling inclusive behaviors, and managing bias. A collaborative team member, who is adept at defining performance measures and navigating ambiguous situations.

Location: US Remote

Why You’ll Love Working Here
• The people. You will be surrounded by talented, supportive, smart, and kind leaders/teams - people you will be proud to work with and who also have fun.
• The business. We work for the love of animals and the people who love them. We enjoy driving a successful business while living our values and our “why”.
• The opportunity. Your days and projects will offer variety with the opportunity to gain operational, cross-functional, and executive leadership exposure as a trusted internal business partner. You would have the opportunity to help build and shape a fast-growing, global company within a high-growth, exciting industry.

Compensation

Starting salary is competitive with excellent benefits including health insurance, 401k, and vacation time

EEOC

NVA is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Hiring is contingent on candidate verifying their eligibility to work in the United States and passing a complete background check and drug screen.

This role is not open to receiving agency candidates and any contingent submissions will not be honored",2022-01-28,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['microstrategy', 'power_bi', 'powerpoint', 'excel']"
23617,807,SaaS Support Data Analyst (IRIS CRM),NMI,Anywhere,"Description

We are recruiting for a talented SaaS Support Data Analyst to provide a first-class service to our customers who are using our IRIS CRM product. IRIS is an NMI company...

About Us

IRIS CRM is a cloud-based platform, accessed through a secure website built and hosted by IRIS CRM, a certified PCI Level 1 Compliant Service Provider. IRIS CRM customers are payment processing organizations registered with Visa and MasterCard, called ISOs, whose job is to compete with names like Stripe, Square, and PayPal for their market share of electronic commerce in North America. This CRM is responsible for providing the business management CRM along with transaction reporting services that ISOs rely on to manage more than 350,000 active businesses each month.

This is a fully remote role (work anywhere in the US), however, if you live within a reasonable commutable distance, we’d love to see you in the office from time to time!

We are open to candidates from the following US States: Arizona, Arkansas, California, Florida, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Michigan, New Jersey, New York, Utah, Texas, Wyoming, Virginia, Kansas, Tennessee.

A great place to work!

We believe that having a diverse group of employees strengthens both our work and our workplace. We’re focused on making NMI more diverse and welcoming with initiatives like having a dedicated Diversity, Equity & Inclusion action group, diversity goals for hiring, anonymized resume screening, affinity groups such as our Women's network and LGBTQ+ Network, open forums for discussions on diversity and social justice, and measuring inclusion and belonging as part of our regular employee engagement surveys.

What will I be doing?

Responsibilities:
• Acting as the subject matter expert within the IRIS Support team for handling tasks and requests pertaining to the Residuals module;
• Solving residual calculation tickets accurately through the use of Excel and IRIS CRM;
• Interacting with clients by phone, chat, and email that have questions pertaining to residual calculations, proof of concepts, and configuration updates;
• Creating new mathematical formulas and verifying existing formulas to ensure that residual income calculations are being reported correctly on client sites;
• Professionally and effectively answering questions about using and configuring IRIS software for clients' needs in a concise way while understanding clients may possess different levels of technical understanding;
• Logging software issues, bugs or inconsistencies that are reported by clients using JIRA and Zendesk tools;
• Creating visual mockups and written descriptions of suggestions for the development related but not limited to the Residuals functionality;
• Training and coaching new clients on the richness of IRIS features to ensure maximum adaptability and stickiness;
• Creating and analyzing internal reports pertaining to Employer’s billing, revenue KPIs, client pricing adjustments and general reporting as requested by management or the support team;
• Taking interest in and educating yourself about the payments industry to be able to provide the most accurate information

Requirements
• Minimum completion of a Bachelor’s degree
• 2+ years of experience implementing or supporting SaaS software
• Experience working in a ticketing system on a daily basis
• Excellent verbal and written communication and problem-solving skills
• Strong sense of curiosity and interest in learning the ins-and-outs of the product in detail
