23670,860,"Senior Analyst, BI & Analytics",WorldRemit,Anywhere,"Who we are

We’re global, we’re growing and we’re going to need talent to keep up the pace. We’re making payments simpler for over 4m customers worldwide, in over 90 currencies. We’ve been around for 10 years, disrupting the market with a digital payment platform that aims to make sending money abroad as easy as sending a text message...

There’s almost 1,200 of us already hard at work and we love welcoming new people. We’ve got offices across the world, from London to Sydney and 15 locations in between - they’re open for business but right now lots of us are working from home. Want to be part of our global growth story - read on…

About the role

Data, Insight, and Analytics is an integral part of our business and you will be part of an ambitious team delivering impactful data-driven solutions to some of our trickiest problems - partnering closely with our Technology, Commercial, Operations and Finance teams. Our mission is to enable the best human and machine-driven decision making, and this role will have a huge impact in achieving that mission and helping our business grow and succeed.

We are looking for an experienced analyst that is passionate about storytelling and impact using data in its wonderful diversity and depth. We have roles open across different teams and encourage the building of subject matter expertise in multiple business areas or just one depending on your interests.

You will be a passionate advocate for using data to create insightful and actionable insight using a wide range of products and tools. You thrive in dynamic and collaborative environments where the learning curve never flattens.

You enjoy finding creative solutions to complex problems using structured thinking and an ability to see the bigger picture: a problem solving approach that gets to the underlying business questions, using a variety of data sources and information

On the technical side, you will be working with a wide variety of technologies (e.g. Tableau, SQL, Python or R, Excel…), data sets, and techniques to drive real business value. You’ll need to be comfortable choosing the right tool for the job.

As a member of WorldRemit’s Analytics team you will aim high, embrace challenge and always do what’s right; acting with integrity and building trust as you contribute to the company’s technical direction and long term decision making.

Reporting to the Senior Manager, Analytics you will:
• Champion the use of data to derive insights and drive action, ensuring our customers are at the heart of every business decision
• Understand the key growth and financial drivers of our business model and provide recommendations of how best to meet business objectives
• Work collaboratively with senior stakeholders to prioritise and translate business questions into analytical projects
• Identify opportunities for improvement through data - setting targets, understanding drivers, assessing performance, and modelling scenarios
• Present results back to the business in a structured, data-driven manner - simplifying complex concepts for non-technical audiences
• Set and improve on analytical best practices in our team and in the wider business

What we’re looking for from you
• Experience in an analytics or data science role. Experience in a fintech or fast-growing data-driven B2C companies would be a bonus but not essential.
• Strong problem solving abilities; using structured thinking to identify root causes, opportunities and risks and implementing effective solutions
• Strong SQL skills, able to handle large, complex data structures from multiple sources
• Strong Storytelling skills using a range of mediums (documents, presentations, verbal)
• Experience with using other coding languages (e.g. R, Python) to analyse complex datasets
• Understanding of the fundamentals of Data Architecture, Governance and Quality
• Strong skills using Data Visualisation/BI tools (e.g. Looker, Tableau, Periscope, Excel/Gsheets)
• Experience using data and analytics as a central part of your role either as a user or creator

What you’ll get from us
• Pension scheme offering 8% matched contributions
• 25 days of holiday plus bank holidays, rising to 28 after 3 years
• Income Protection
• Life assurance worth 3 x your salary
• Private medical and dental care plans
• Cycle to work scheme

This role can be based in the UK, Krakow or the Philippines. Benefits for Krakow and the Philippines will be discussed on application",2022-02-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'looker', 'python', 'sql', 'r']"
