23724,914,Senior Procurement Analyst,Mimecast,United States,"A key function of Procurement is to create data processes, dashboards & other visualizations that will give Procurement and business colleagues visibility into key spend categories and actively guide their strategies in delivering cost-savings and operational efficiency. The analyst will collaborate heavily with both business facing teams and with Finance, and a key aspect of the role is... combining solid technical abilities with strong business acumen & communication skills to coherently combine both sets of requests.

The analyst is expected to independently conduct analysis in Excel, SQL & Viz tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI, etc.) and take over key workstreams to support Procurement, Strategic Sourcing, Vendor Onboarding and Travel which includes Concur, credit card and Travel Management) teams. Analysis must be reproducible and timely. The analyst would be expected to paint a picture of Mimecast spend by category factoring in growth as well as other scenarios for all levels of the company including Executive Committee. The analyst will be responsible for allocating time to both build out internal Procurement insight and delivering clear messaging internally and externally as needed.

Some examples of job requirements: Analyze spend data to support Sr Managers in category planning, generate savings tracking reports, conduct data analysis on usage data for Business Applications to drive insights into renewal strategies, developing code to automate processes. Support the RFP process by providing summary results and scenario planning.

Essential Requirements
• Exemplary academic background in STEM or demonstrated excellence in analytics via independent project work
• Proficiency in Excel and SQL
• Expert in research, problem-solving, communication, & analysis
• Experience building dashboards
• Experience in a position focused on delivering analytics solutions in a business context, such as but not limited to: Procurement, Travel, SaaS/Technology company, business/operations/data analyst at a leading firm.
• Record of leadership
• Experience in stakeholder management

Desirable Requirements
• Experience managing complex projects with several teams & partners
• Strong visual & oral communicator with experience independently leading presentations on complex analytical topics to audiences of different backgrounds
• Experience visualizing data: PowerPoint, Tableau, PowerBI
• Solid academic background in or independent understanding of fundamental programming concepts
• Experience in other coding languages: Python, Java, R, Matlab

Education
• Bachelor’s degree – preferably in a business or science related industry
• 5-year experience as an analyst
• 2+ years preferred in Technology company
• Experience working in Procurement is preferred

Why Mimecast?

We’re fast thinking. We go big to reach our cyberattack-disrupting goals. And we do what we need to protect the world of business from getting important (and potentially compromising) data stolen. We never leave anyone behind. We deliver quickly – and outstandingly. We’re big on honesty because it makes us better. We’re empowered by our mission. And if cybercriminals have a good day, we work twice as hard to make the rest of their days a nightmare. That’s The Mimecast Way.

And the Mimecast way is also a hybrid-working way. We empower our people to balance their time between home and the office in a way that works best for them, their team, and our stakeholders.

Become a Mimecaster and put corporate data under your protection. Fill our teams with respect. And bring cybercrime-obstructing energy to your work. Be passionate. Be powerful. Be alive with purpose.

DEI Statement

Cybersecurity is a community effort. That’s why we’re committed to building an inclusive, diverse community that celebrates and welcomes everyone – unless they’re a cybercriminal, of course.

We’re proud to be an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer, and we’d encourage you to join us whatever your background. We particularly welcome applicants from traditionally underrepresented groups.

We consider everyone equally: your race, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, ability, marital status, nationality, or any other protected characteristic won’t affect your application.

If you require any adjustments or accommodations due to a disability, or any other reason that may help you in your interview process, please let us know by emailing careers@mimecast.com.

