23783,973,Senior Recruiting Data Visualization Analyst,Dropbox,"Kansas City, MO","Company Description

Dropbox is a leading global collaboration platform that's transforming the way people work together, from the smallest business to the largest enterprise. With more than 700 million registered users across more than 180 countries, our mission is to design a more enlightened way of working. From our headquarters in San Francisco to eight dedicated Studios and a worldwide team... of employees who choose where they work best, our Virtual First approach is leading the way into the future of work.

Team Description

The People team are ambassadors of enlightened work, delivering meaningful experiences that empower us all to do our best work.

Role Description

At Dropbox, our leaders, our People team, and our business stakeholders understand the power of using data to shape our HR and Recruiting strategies. Our People Analytics team has made significant investments in our data warehouse and infrastructure, and we’ve launched a suite of HR and Recruiting dashboards to empower our internal customers. Now, we’re looking for someone to take our self-service dashboarding capabilities to the next level through world-class visualizations, proactive alerts, enhanced performance, and multi-data source metrics. You bring the ability to take a holistic approach to the wide-variety of People data needs across Dropbox. You’re able to balance multiple priorities, deep analytical rigor, and excellent interpersonal skills that can be tailored to cross-functional audiences at every level. You also love what you do, possess a positive, “let’s make it work” mindset, and can thrive under pressure.

Responsibilities
• Lead Tableau dashboard development efforts within Dropbox’s People Analytics team, specifically focused on Recruiting dashboards
• Partner with stakeholders across Dropbox to understand data needs, define solutions, and visualize a wide variety of Recruiting & HR metrics
• Answer business questions through independent investigation/data forensics. Identify operational inefficiencies, data quality issues, and behavioral trends
• Develop prototypes, mock-ups, and conceptualization of ideas that bring simplicity and context to complex design challenges
• Build analytics capabilities through data literacy trainings focused on storytelling with data, and leveraging dashboards to take action
• Leverage and improve upon our internal data warehouse through partnership with other technical teams at Dropbox and external consultants
• Develop, consolidate, and improve our self-service HR and Recruiting dashboards based on user feedback

Requirements
• 3-5 years of experience building data visualizations in Tableau with a portfolio of intuitive, interactive dashboards (multiple role experience)
• Expertise in leveraging complex data sources to visually represent business metrics
• Ability to quickly prototype and transform ideas into high-quality work product
• Strong communication skills and ability to articulate complex solutions well to both technical and non-technical audiences
• Low ego attitude with a willingness to shift from high-level critical thinking to stepping in and helping to drive implementation alongside functional teams
• Knowledge of HR and Recruiting processes
• Ability to think creatively and critically and thrive in a fast-paced, multifaceted, and often ambiguous work environment

Total Rewards

For candidates hired in Colorado, the expected salary/On-Target Earnings (OTE) range for the role is $101,200 - $119,100 - $137,000.
This salary/OTE range represents the low, middle, and high end of the salary or OTE (Sales roles) range for this position, and is subject to change. To determine a Dropboxer’s starting pay we carefully consider a variety of factors, including primary work location and an evaluation of a candidate’s skills, experience, market demands, and internal parity. This position may be considered a promotional opportunity.
Salary/OTE is just one component of Dropbox’s total rewards package. All regular employees are also eligible for the corporate bonus program or a sales incentive (target included in OTE) as well as stock in the form of Restricted Stock Units (RSUs).
Dropbox is committed to investing in the holistic health and wellbeing of all Dropboxers and their families. Our benefits and perks programs include, but are not limited to:
• Competitive medical, dental and vision coverage
• (US Only) Competitive 401(k) Plan with a generous company match and immediate vesting
• Flexible Time Off/Paid Time Off, paid holidays, 11 Company-wide PTO days, Volunteer time off and more
• Protection Plans including; Life Insurance, Disability Insurance and Travel benefit plans
• Perks Allowance to be used on what matters most to you, whether that’s wellness, learning and development, food & groceries, and much more
• Parental benefits including; Parental Leave, Child and Adult Care, Day Care FSA (US Only), Fertility Benefits (US Only), Adoption and Surrogacy support and Lactation Support
• Mental Health and Wellness benefits
• Free Dropbox space for your friends and family

Additional benefits details are available upon request.

Dropbox is in the process of updating our technology to provide pay ranges in New York City based on the recent amendments to the New York City Human Rights Law (NYCHRL). If you are based in NYC and have any questions about the pay range for this role, please contact paytransparency@ and provide your name and the job title to which you are interested in applying.

Dropbox is an equal opportunity employer. We are a welcoming place for everyone, and we do our best to make sure all people feel supported and connected at work. A big part of that effort is our support for members and allies of internal groups like Asians at Dropbox, BlackDropboxers, Latinx, Pridebox (LGBTQ), Vets at Dropbox, Women at Dropbox, ATX Diversity (based in Austin, Texas) and the Dropbox Empowerment Network (based in Dublin, Ireland",2022-02-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['tableau']
23788,978,Data Analyst,Parity Group PLC,Anywhere,"Data Analyst

Remote working – US BASED...

Parity Group are working closely and exclusively with our new client. A private equity backed, global powerhouse helping clients to optimise and manage their IT, software, and investments. They have a new opportunity for a Data Analyst to join their Development team on a permanent basis.

This role would be an exciting but challenging step for someone looking to dip deeper into their career in Data and for you to start a career in Licensing. Whether you have been exposed to Licensing before, or just have a genuine interest, this role will be a great way to develop your skills through a company that offer you the experience and the resources to grow your career in the industry.

What they can offer you:
• Up to $75k
• Unlimited holidays
• Pension contributions
• Life Assurance
• Flexible working
• Private healthcare
• Days off for charity and volunteering

The Role:

Your role will play an active part in the success of our client. You will collect, analyse, format and present new and existing data sources for our customers software and cloud investments driving optimisation recommendations and value-based data insights.

Responsibilities:
• Analytical and problem-solving. Apply basic techniques for analysis of research data and synthesis of findings and present these findings in a way that colleagues can understand and make use.
• Communication. Translate and communicate accurate information to technical and non-technical stakeholders, set clear requirements needed to carry out accurate and high-quality analysis.
• Data management. Understand data governance and how it works in relation to other organisational governance structures.
• Data modelling, data cleansing, and data enrichment. Produce data models and understand where to use different types of data models. Understand different tools and compare different data models.
• Data visualisation. Use the most appropriate approach to visualise data to tell compelling and actionable stories relevant for business goals.
• Quality assurance, validation, and data linkage. Manage your own data preparation and cleansing with minimal guidance. Create appropriate documentation that allows stakeholders to understand the steps of the data analysis process and duplicate or replicate the analysis if necessary.
• Statistical methods and data analysis. Understand how and when to practically apply existing best-practice solutions.

Knowledge and Experience:
• Strong analytical skills related to working with a mixed variety of both structured and unstructured datasets, finding relationships in the data.
• Solid current experience of using a software language to obtain, extract and manipulate data, such asPython, C#, Java or equivalent.
• Software language skills to call APIs
• Experience working within AWS environment.
• Experience with Amazon QuickSight.
• Azure DevOps.
• Strong project management and organizational skills",2022-05-06,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['c', 'azure', 'aws', 'java']"
23791,981,Senior Marketing Data Analyst,BOLD,Anywhere,"BOLD is an established and fast-growing technology company that transforms work lives. Since 2005, BOLD has delivered award-winning career services that have a meaningful and positive impact on job seekers and employers. BOLD’s robust product line includes professional resume and cover letter writing services, scientifically validated career tests, and employer tools that help companies hire... onboard, and communicate with their staff.

Position Summary

The Senior Marketing Data Analyst plays a key role within the Finance and Marketing teams of our fast-paced, rapidly growing, high-tech company. The role requires a multi-faceted individual willing to dive into details, ensure accurate and timely work yet with the ability to work across multiple functions, be proactive with shifting priorities, and have the drive to deliver results. This role is a remote US role, with the East Coast as the preferred location.

The Senior Marketing Data Analyst will work with the Senior Director of Finance and the Head of Marketing with data interpretation and financial analysis. This role will serve as a strategic partner to the Marketing organization. The analyst will dive into the details of marketing performance KPIs, form a solid understanding of Marketing initiatives, and provide insights and advice from a data and finance perspective. This role will also assist in the long-term strategic planning and budgeting process for the Marketing organization.

Position Responsibility
• Support the Marketing organization in long-range strategic planning, budgeting, and short-term forecast.
• Analyze marketing campaign data and performance KPIs, to understand the competitive landscape of a market, and the success of campaigns, to provide insights to the Marketing team on the performance and action plans
• Assess/analyze deviations from key metric targets and provide insight to leaders
• Build financial models to analyze business opportunities for new markets and Marketing initiatives, and conduct variance and scenario analysis
• Evaluate, help prioritize and recommend proposals to maximize market growth based on market insights – with an understanding of marketing channel performance, website performance, customer segment performance and product performance for the region
• Develop financial analysis that challenges & evaluates all marketing strategic decisions and contributes to overall roll out strategies.
• Liaise between the Marketing team and the rest of the Finance team, which runs monthly financial analysis, reporting, and rolling forecast. Make sure the Finance team understands Marketing initiatives and plans, and the Marketing team understands the financial performance and trends.

Required Qualifications
• Degree in Finance, Business, Statistics, Mathematics, or related fields; advanced degree preferred
• Experience building complex financial models, conducting quantitative and qualitative financial analysis and scenario analysis
• Minimum of 3+ years of progressive experience in finance or related fields
• Ability to translate numerical data into business language and convey key messages clearly
• Strong desire to learn and be challenged
• Strong persuasion ability and influencing skills
• Ability to create practical, workable solutions for changing forecasting needs
• Strong presence and presentation skills
• Experience presenting analyses to senior executives and working as a business partner across all departments
• Ability to set and monitor priorities and meet deadlines
• Advanced knowledge of Excel and PowerPoint

Desired Qualifications
• Knowledge and experience in digital marketing
• Knowledge and experience working with marketing analytics tools such as Google Analytics, Google Adwords, etc.
• Experience with subscription-based business
• Experience with NetSuite, Anaplan

About BOLD

BOLD is a fast-paced, innovative company full of smart, committed people who are passionate about our products and love helping people find the career of their dreams. We balance work and fun, while continuing to build a successful, fast-growing company that is changing the way people get jobs.

Our vision is to revolutionize the online career world by creating transformational products that help people find the careers they love and reach their full potential.

