23852,1042,Data Analyst,"KARL STORZ Endoscopy-America, Inc.",Anywhere,"Company: KARL STORZ Endoscopy-America, Inc. (KSEA)

Job Code: 12605...

Pay Grade: US-C15

Description

KARL STORZ SE & Co. KG based in Tuttlingen, Germany, is a family-owned, global company committed to benefiting humanity by advancing medical technology through innovation and education.

For more than 75 years, KARL STORZ has been dedicated to earning its international reputation as a leader that designs, engineers, manufactures, and markets all its products with an emphasis on visionary design, precision craftsmanship, and clinical effectiveness.

KARL STORZ is currently seeking a highly motivated Data Analystto join the Sales Analytics team. The ideal candidate has expertise in big data, data analytics, Tableau and predictive modeling. They are passionate about creating business value by designing and developing robust and performant data models. They have strong problem-solving skill, a keen attention to detail, ability to work in a fast-paced environment with ambiguous situations, and solid skills in project management.

Reporting to the Sales Analytics Manager, the Data Analyst will collaborate across marketing, sales and operations teams to design and develop datasets and reports in Tableau, as well as perform analysis which provides actionable insights to help stakeholders in decision-making.

This role will be based out of our El Segundo office but offer the opportunity to work remotely full time.

This opportunity will get you working on large scale structured and unstructured data sets, applying various data engineering and modeling techniques on real-world datasets to build and deploy models. A well-qualified candidate will be highly technical with strong business acumen. The successful candidate is a self-starter with abundant intellectual curiosity who excels at framing problems analytically, is comfortable working through ambiguity, and has a proven track record of leveraging analytical insights to drive impactful decisions.

Responsibilities
• Mine data, perform quantitative analysis and create clear and actionable narratives about our customers, their behaviors, and drivers of retention and engagement.
• Collaborate with internal business partners to design, build and automate data pipelines, datasets, reports and dashboards in Tableau to provide actionable insight into business metrics, customers, products, and sales force.
• Leverage data wrangling, engineering and analytics techniques to investigate internal data and external data (e.g., health claims data) to boost our understanding of the medical devices market or to generate new customer leads.
• Partner with Marketing and Sales teams to understand business context, develop metrics to measure performance, iterate and improve on data insights and solutions to deliver actionable information to the business.
• Collaborate with stakeholders including marketing, sales, customer service, finance etc. on initiatives that improve our company-level KPIs and match our business priorities.
• Develop and deploy solutions for solving business problems using predictive modeling techniques.
• Build intuitive interfaces, infographics, and visualizations to tell stories with data.
• Create presentations with analysis and insights for both technical and non-technical audiences.
• Be constantly curious and continue to pursue in-depth explorations of our datasets.
• Communicate complicated data findings in a clear and concise manner to stakeholders.
• Ad-hoc analysis to address urgent high impact analysis for business stakeholders

Required Qualifications
• A Bachelor's degree in a quantitative discipline (e.g., Finance, Economics, Statistics, Computer Science, Math, Engineering) or equivalent consulting experience.
• A minimum of three years of experience in data analytics, including building and deploying enterprise-wide data pipelines and models with applications to real-world problems.
• A minimum of three years of experience with data exploration and visualization like Tableau, Looker, PowerBI, etc. It is a plus if you can share a portfolio of clear, intuitive and insightful visualizations.
• A minimum of two years of professional experience in designing, developing, and scripting data pipelines, data sources and dashboards in Tableau. (Tableau Desktop, Tableau Prep and Tableau Server)
• Proficient in SQL and/or other data query languages. Experience of handling large scale data with efficiency. Familiar with Python or R is a plus.
• Strong knowledge about ETL process, data modeling and data wrangling.
• Understanding of statistics concepts (e.g., hypothesis testing, regression analysis).
• Effective written and verbal communication skills to translate technical solutions and methodologies to executive leadership.
• Demonstrated success working in a collaborative, service-oriented team environment.
• Experience working in a cross-functional setting, managing the full lifecycle of projects.
• Experience working well with ambiguity, prioritizing needs, and delivering results in a dynamic environment.
• Attention to detail with self-discipline and a drive for results.
• Advanced problem-solving, organizational, analytical and critical thinking skills.
• Proven experience with tolerance for ambiguity working through incubation to actual product definition.
• Pragmatic attitude and ability to rapidly iterate and evolve ideas into practical implementations.
• Experience in medical device or healthcare industry is a plus.

