• Partner across HR to develop a standard set of key performance indicators, robust self-service reporting capability and manager dashboards in appliance ERP / HCM solutions.
• Transform large amounts of data into compelling visual stories to facilitate analysis and business decision-making, using data visualization tools. Ensure that the information is presented in a visually clear, concise, and business-relevant manner to senior leadership level stakeholders.

Minimum Qualifications
• Strategic thinker with superior business and financial acumen.
• Experience in delivering executive level presentations.
• Demonstrated experience developing and implementing department and enterprise level capital and operating budgets.
• Demonstrated success in repurposing raw data into actionable information.
• Demonstrated acumen with metrics and/or KPI development, tracking and evaluation.
• Demonstrated business process management experience. Experience leading large scale company-wide programs and initiatives.
• Demonstrated ability to work in a partnership environment and cooperatively with a cross section of stakeholders.
• 10+ years of professional experience in a quantitative or analytics role such as Workforce Analytics, Data Science, or People Analytics.
• 10 years of HR SAP management (or equivalent HCM) experience.
• Knowledge of predictive analysis and advanced visualization techniques.
• Possess the ability to mage across various HR disciplines and integrate solutions within various disparate tools/ processes.
• Exposure and understanding of reporting and HR systems. Specific experience with the SAP/SF reporting and Power BI analytics tools a plus.
• Experience synthesizing quantitative and qualitative analysis into understandable, actionable recommendations and connecting Human Resources insights to business impact.
• MA or MS or MBA with concentration in data theory, digital analytics, data scientist a plus
• 10 years of leadership experience developing professional staff and leading cross functional project teams.

Preferred Qualifications
• Master’s degree.
• Experience with SAP or enterprise Human Resource data structures.
• Experience with quantitative and qualitative analysis.
• Direct or indirect experience with both financial planning, analysis, and headcount management.

Communications And Interpersonal Skills
• Must have excellent oral and written communication skills.

The salary/hourly range is $148,000 - $209,950. Pay is based on several factors including but not limited to education, work experience, certifications, etc. Depending on an employee’s assigned worksite or location, Amtrak may consider a geo-pay differential to be applied to the employee’s base salary. Amtrak may offer additional incentive and pay programs to recognize and reward our employees, including a short-term incentive bonus based upon factors such as individual and company performance that is commensurate with the level of the position and/or long-term incentive plan compensation. In addition to your salary, Amtrak offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes health, dental, and vision plans; health savings accounts; wellness programs; flexible spending accounts; 401K retirement plan with employer match; life insurance; short and long term disability insurance; paid time off; back-up care; adoption assistance; surrogacy assistance; reimbursement of education expenses; Public Service Loan Forgiveness eligibility; Railroad Retirement sickness and retirement benefits; and rail pass privileges. Learn more about our benefits offerings here .

