23885,1075,"Senior Business Data Analyst, SOLAR",Levi Strauss & Co.,Anywhere,"Purpose

JOB DESCRIPTION...

The Sr Business Data Analyst provides leadership and direction to the SOLAR Business Data Analysts for future proofing, converting/migrating and cleansing data. The Sr Business Data Analyst is responsible for identifying the impacts and requirements for global master data, its respective business areas, owners and systems. The Sr Business Data Analyst has ownership of the project deliverables for their respective business areas and ultimately will ensure that the solution will fulfil the needs of their representative process scope and LS&Co business. The Sr Business Data Analyst reports to the SOLAR Business Data Architect and works in close partnership with the SOLAR functional leads (OTC, DTC, FICO, P2P, WO, IMP & SCS) and functional product owners in their respective area.

Key Results
• Strategic future proofing; define the future “best practice” attribution of either Material, Vendor, Customer, or FICO master data based on industry standard and best practices commonly applied to an omnichannel (apparel) retailer.
• Tactical future proofing; Assist with data cataloging efforts to ensure clear visibility of data elements across Levi's S4 landscape. Maintain field mapping documentation to highlight cross functional gaps in field definitions and usage to decrease data defects in each Cutover Rehearsal and drive towards 0 defects at Go Live.
• Operational future proofing; ensure clean and efficient data by keeping our records current and closing old unused records while updating values based on current and future business decisions.

Key Responsibilities
• Gather requirements for each release of SOLAR in discover and explore phases
• Manage defects that stem from new requirements during testing cycles
• Participate in and lead cross functional workshops for master data
• Provide guidance and direction to data analysts within respective domain
• Own master data design for respective domain
• Collaborate with data owners on non master data objects related to respective domain
• Support building and staffing within respective domain based on skills required for project success
• Assist in coordinating the day-to-day activities of the business data analysts to ensure that milestones are achieved
• Resolve business issues that impact the ability of the business data analysts to deliver project goals and escalate issues as appropriate
• Accountable for the deliverables for respective functional areas (Requirements, BPD’s, Functional Specs, etc.)
• Assist in driving the execution of testing, identification of transactions and data to be tested, and managing test problem resolution
• Lead business process definition and ensures business processes are effectively mapped in the software configuration
• Conduct and/or participate in workshops and presentations to validate business processes and requirements
• Provide strategic leadership for the data proofing area and ultimately ensures that the application fulfills the needs of the global LS&Co business areas + the integration points with other areas
• Maintain ongoing communication with business partners as part of stakeholder engagement program
• Partner with functional leads, functional product owners and project leadership to plan, set priorities, and resolve issues and conflicts
• Communicate progress and status on a regular basis
• Monitor issue management procedures and resolution
• Monitor delivery of agreed functional scope within budget and timeline, and take corrective action when necessary
• Participate in planning and execution of organizational readiness activities
• Work closely with the functional leads, functional product owners & technical team to facilitate the completion of development objects in support of the business processes
• Proactive management of project risks on an ongoing basis including the identification, analysis, and response to risks
• Participate in the development of risk mitigation and contingency strategies

