23888,1078,Business/Data Analyst REMOTE,"RealPage, Inc.",Anywhere,"Who We Are

RealPage is changing the technology real estate industry and our teammates know how to think big and leave their mark. If you want to join a globally progressive and inclusive company devoted to excellence, we are looking for you...

We are the leading global provider of software and data analytics to the real estate industry. We navigate clients toward the right decisions with data and technology insights they can only get from RealPage. Serving our clients is our highest priority and RealPage teammates are our greatest asset.

Come join a team where your work makes an impact every day!

About The Team

We’re passionate about helping hard-working entrepreneurs grow their property management businesses. We’re a collective of uniquely talented people who are at the top of our game and are determined to get better at what we do every day.

Our determination to make our customers’ lives better and break records is contagious—you find yourself becoming intensely passionate about the work that we do, even if the property management industry was never on your radar before you got here.

What You’ll Do

We are looking for a data guru to join our Business Analytics team to assist the Mixed Use division by providing actionable insights regarding business operations, product features, and customer behaviors by retrieving, sanitizing and testing the data from the source. As a Business Analyst IV, you will report to the Director, Program Management Office and Business Analytics.

The Business Analytics team works with company management to define, collect and present the metrics used to make good decisions. The team is a collection of analysts that facilitate the network of data between our internal and external sources of data.

This role is geared toward someone who is passionate about asking and answering questions about the business through large data sets. A desire to provide actionable insights and experience with SQL coding is essential while knowledge in SaaS business metrics is a plus.

Primary Responsibilities

Responsibilities for this position include but are not limited to the following:
• Be the go-to analyst for the Mixed Use Team
• Develop a deep understanding of our intelligence platform and the sources of data that populate it.
• Coordinating with our offshore teamin India (intermediator)
• Complete ad-hoc analysis for business problems and present to stakeholders to provide actionable insights
• Assist with prioritization of incoming requests and manage team sprints
• Be at the core a team player, assisting other team members and helping them to learn
• Consistently deliver results on time and within the expected margin of task completion
• Responsible for Mixed Use analytics reporting working with various departments to provide business metrics
• Write SQL code to pull data from our database
• Build visualizations and dashboards

Required Knowledge/Skills/Abilities
• 3+ years analytics experience
• Proficiency with SQL
• Experience with Looker or other Business Intelligence tool
• Demonstrated ability to think analytically and solve problems
• Excellent organizational and time-management skills
• Strong verbal and written communication skills, collaboration and influencing skills
• Experience working in a fast-paced environment
• Enthusiastic and goal oriented

Preferred Knowledge/Skills/Abilities
• Python/R experience preferred
• Experience working with a datawarehouse preferred

What We Offer

At RealPage, we’re always looking for talented professionals who thrive in a learning work environment that continually supports individual greatness. We foster a culture of innovation and creativity. It is the things you do that bring out the best of you and RealPage.

RealPage considers qualified applicants without regard to gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, race, national origin, age, veteran, or disability status. We celebrate diversity and are committed to building an inclusive work environment where all teammates feel a sense of belonging while bringing their authentic self to the table and being valued for it",2022-07-28,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['looker', 'sql']"
23889,1079,Lead Data Analyst,OpenText,Anywhere,"Opentext - The Information Company

As the Information Company, our mission at OpenText is to create software solutions and deliver services that redefine the future of digital. Be part of a winning team that leads the way in Enterprise Information Management...

The Opportunity

We are currently seeking a Lead Data Scientist with deep technical expertise to join our Business Insights and Analytics team. Individuals should demonstrate intellectual curiosity and passion for solving problems with an eye for optimization and efficiency. This role will support application development for multiple lines of business within the SMB/C organization, including Sales, Renewals, Business and Revenue Operations, and Finance.

You Are Great At

Our professionals need to work across multiple database systems to provide a holistic view of multiple business divisions. Your deep technical expertise in SQL or SQL Server, combined with the strong business acumen of SaaS metrics in a subscription business model, will enable you to quickly and accurately model, query, and wrangle data in preparation for application development.

Application Development

You will work both independently, and in partnership with other BI Developers and Business Analysts, to manage the application development experience throughout its lifecycle: from gathering report requirements and meeting with stakeholders, to develop the data model and specific applications, to ongoing tuning and enhancements as required.

This position requires the individual to provide planning, estimation, scheduling, prioritization, and coordination of technical activities related to application development with multiple stakeholders. Accountable to business and technical stakeholders for end-to-end application scoping, planning, development, and delivery that meets and exceeds quality standards.

Data Visualization, Reporting, And Storytelling

Your applications will include a variety of data visualizations enabling business analysts and end users to employ various data analysis technics including, including but not limited to exploratory, descriptive, diagnostic, cohort, time series, moving average, and forecasting.

Experience developing applications containing more advanced analytical techniques such as predictive, prescriptive, clustering, classification, optimization, regression, Niave Bayes, neural networks, decision trees, and text analysis is not required. However, skills such as these will add value as organizational data readiness matures. Similarly, technical skills with respect to QlikView, R, or ggplot2 would be helpful.

Your applications will be used to transform business processes, improve internal controls, improve the efficiency of operations, and increase transparency and performance management. Our environment requires self-motivated individual who is willing to develop solutions on their own or in a team of highly skilled professionals.

What It Takes

Persona
• 5-7 years of application development experience
• Intellectually curious, conceptual, and analytical thinker
• Conscientious and organized with strong problem-solving skills
• Results-oriented with thoughtful actions, flexible and collaborative

Technical Skills
• Proven experience with querying, wrangling, and analyzing data in SQL
• Proficiency in writing and debugging SQL queries
• Proficiency with BI tools such as Tableau, Excel, and Power BI
• Experience with leveraging data from CRM and ERP systems
• Experience designing and implementing data models
• Proficiency in navigating data architecture
• Ability to work concurrently across multiple technologies
• Experience in optimizing dashboards with a focus on usability, performance, flexibility, and standardization
• Experience in end-to-end implementation of BI projects for developing a portfolio of scorecards, KPIs, reports & dashboards

Analytical Skills
• Experience in synthesizing SaaS analytics themes and key performance indicators – storytelling with data
• Have a working understanding of data visualization best practices, development processes, and knowledge of typical BI & analytics tools and technologies
• Ability to integrate reporting components from multiple data sources

Project Management Skills
• Knowledge and experience with driving projects, facilitating BI tool demos, and managing stakeholders across different levels
• Provides technical expertise in the diagnosis and resolution of an issue, including the determination and provision of workaround solution or escalation to owners
• Comfortable fulfilling ad-hoc requests as needed
• Good written and verbal communication skills
• Ability to manage multiple parallel assignments and meet specified milestones
• Ensures delivered solutions meet technical and functional/non-functional performance requirements within.
• Manage day-to-day technical challenges and communicate to project manager/stakeholder any risks or issues associated with the development activities

For Colorado residents, this job is expected to pay in the range of $99,000 to $148,0000 USD in addition to a comprehensive and competitive group benefit and healthcare plan. Individual compensation will be determined based on skills and experience comparable to the job requirements.

