Description

Director, Reporting & Data Analysis: Responsible for planning, directing, and controlling the resources and efforts of reporting and data analysis team to accomplish the company objectives through information management.

Primary Duties May Include, But Are Not Limited To
• Providing leadership in motivating subordinates to accomplish reporting and data analysis goals and objectives.
• Developing a strong team through training and effective organizational development practices.
• Obtaining resources (people, funding, material, support) to support business unit information needs and strategic initiatives.
• Reporting project status and progress to business unit senior management.
• Ensures accuracy and timeliness of output and deliverables for assigned functional areas.
• Implements the policies, practices, and procedures of the company and business units supported.
• Has fiscal responsibility for area budgets.
• Establishes relationships with business users both internal and external.
• Hires, trains, coaches, counsels, and evaluates performance of direct reports.
• Oversees entire reporting/analysis/consulting unit on all aspects of a centralized function.
• Participates with other executives to establish strategic plans and objectives.
• Coordinates project management across department and divisional line.

Minimum Qualifications
• Requires Bachelor's degree and 10+ years experience leading technical teams, or any combination of education and experience, which would provide an equivalent background.

Preferred Skills, Capabilities And Experiences
• Prior leadership or management experience.
• Technical knowledge.
• Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills.
• Effective communication skills, including facilitation, consultation, negotiation, and persuasion.
• Prior experience supporting operational teams.

For candidates working in person or remotely in the below locations, the salary* range for this specific position is $122,720 to $220,896

Locations: Colorado; Nevada, Jersey City, NJ; New York City, NY; Ithaca, NY and Westchester County, NY

In addition to your salary, Elevance Health offers benefits such as, a comprehensive benefits package, incentive and recognition programs, equity stock purchase and 401k contribution (all benefits are subject to eligibility requirements). The salary offered for this specific position is based on a number of legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the company. The company is fully committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, and local pay equity laws .
