23949,1139,Data Admin Analyst SR (Reporting/Data Analytics),Elevance Health,United States,"Description

Title: Data Admin Analyst SR (Reporting/Data Analytics...

Location: Remote/WFH; candidate not required to reside in posted state but must be able to access Elevance Health Pulse Point location.

Build the Possibilities. Make an extraordinary impact.

The Data Admin Analyst SR is responsible for creating a reporting structure for Provider data as new applications and processes are deployed to ensure these applications provide appropriate reporting capabilities / insights. Will also drive true value realiza t ion where decisions are made based on performance metrics. This role will also work with X-functional reporting and analytics teams to define the reporting criteria and analyze and forecast future performance based on changes in the business.

How You Will Make An Impact
• Designs and constructs difficult data reports and analytics.
• Conducts implementation, upgrade and maintenance of vendor supplied data management, data management and information and other third-party software.
• Collects, cleans, catalogs, maintains, and delivers data with minimal guidance and supervision.
• Performs system administration duties with little supervision.
• Performs data profiling analysis and data analysis with guidance and supervision.
• Creates impactful, quality reports for internal constituents.

Minimum Requirements
• Requires an BA/BS degree in Information Technology, Computer Science or related field of study and a minimum of 5 years’ experience in information systems with 3 years’ experience in data administration; or any combination of education and experience, which would provide an equivalent background.

Preferred Skills, Capabilities, And Experiences
• Prior experience with ASG, Rochade Evoke, Data Foundations/Kalido or similar, UNIX, JAVA, PowerBuilder, Oracle, DB2 UDB, Teredata, Sybase, C# and SQL servers strongly preferred.
• PowerBi/Alteryx, Telerak experience preferred.
• Experience in health care industry strongly preferred.
• Master’s degree preferred.

