The First Destination Survey is conducted campus-wide at the end of each term (spring, summer and fall). The data compiled from the FDS is used by academic units and the campus as a whole to assist prospective and current students with their career planning and to report to national publications post-graduation outcomes.

Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others.

