Summary of Job Duties:MC Retention Programs aims to increase retention and graduation for program students while providing an inclusive environment and a community of support. The Data Analyst Graduate Assistant (GA) for MC Retention Programs supports the professional staff in planning, implementing, and assessing programs and services offered through the Academic Enrichment Program (AEP), Freshman Commuter Student Success (FCSS), and TRIO Student Support Services (SSS).

The Data Analyst GA will develop, analyze, maintain, and revise various data collection and reporting processes that will allow our programs to make data-informed decisions that increase student retention and program outcomes. The Data Analyst GA may also provide mentoring, advisement, and supervision to undergraduate students and student staff.

The Data Analyst GA is expected to be student-centered, administratively sound, and both task and relationship oriented.

Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others.

