• Excellent oral and written communication skills
• Presentation and facilitation skills
• Excellent customer service and public relations skills
• Proficiency in MS Excel, PowerBI, Forms or other data management and analytic software
• Skills with word processing, basic design software, including experience with Microsoft Office Suite, cloud-based storage applications, Zoom and other video conferencing and online meeting tools
• Ability to learn and manage various technology platforms such as student information systems (e.g. UASuccess), learning management software (e.g. BlackBoard) and other required software that supports program operations
• Ability to contribute to and thrive in an inclusive work environment
• Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment
• Apply judgment, discretion, and maintain confidentiality in performing complex tasks.
• Ability to effectively organize and prioritize multiple work priorities
• Ability to work some evenings and weekends, based on office needs
