As a global business, (that hasn’t lost its family feel) we can offer opportunities in locations such as the United Kingdom, Europe, United States & Asia. We also offer a great work life balance, remote working or you are welcome to work in our offices, dedicated Cultural Ambassadors – even if you are a remote worker, you don’t need to feel like it! Excellent pay and benefits, generous pension scheme, equity & generous holidays

Description

Dotmatics is seeking a fully remote Data Analyst, Finance to join its growing Strategic Finance team and serve as the analytical engine for a fast-growing, highly acquisitive, mission driven SaaS business executing on a global growth strategy. In this force multiplier role, you will support the Director of FP&A in delivering value-added analysis and relevant financial and operating metrics that help drive sound business decisions. The ideal candidate is intellectually curious, has excellent analytical skills, and possesses a passion for digging into data and building models.

In this role you will get to
• Be an analytical partner to key leaders. Research ways of modeling data to unlock actionable insights or improve processes.
• Collaborate cross-functionally to support the forecast and help maintain the strategic operating plan.
• Develop and maintain financial and operating models and reporting metrics.
• Consolidate data across business units and acquisitions with different definitions and measurement.
• Lead financial data processes and support the rhythm of consistent reporting and of timely, accurate data flows.
• Prepare variance reports, forecast updates, and support the close cycle as needed.
• Deliver executive-ready presentations and analyses and create dashboards and reports to guide business decisions.
• Shape and continuously improve both standard reports and customized analyses to deliver ongoing insight to leaders.
• Enhance operational excellence within the team by creating useful data automation wherever possible.
• Develop a deep understanding of industry trends and benchmarks

We are looking for people who have 3+ years of experience in data analytics and/or finance, preferably within a dynamic and high growth business environment. You should also demonstrate:
• Bachelor’s Degree in Mathematics, Data Engineering, Finance or related quantitative background
• Experience working with large datasets; proficiency in SQL; ability to connect to multiple data sources
• Familiarity with cloud data warehouses (Snowflake)
• Experience using reporting and visualization tools (Expert Power BI, Tableau, Google Workspace, Smartsheets, PowerPoint, Excel)
• Ability to self-start and self-direct work in an unstructured environment
• Must be extremely collaborative and comfortable dealing with ambiguity
• Strong modeling & analytics, high attention to detail, and great communication skills
• Experience working with financial data sets and a general understanding of 3 statement financial modeling considered a big plus

