Responsible for the holistic assessment of enterprise fraud losses and trends identified by the 1st line of defense (1LOD), resulting from fraud incidents and investigations. Develops and clearly, concisely presents enterprise fraud loss reporting for the Bank's Board of Directors and/or senior management risk governance committees with a business centric view of the Bank's Fraud risk profile. Solves complex analytical problems by using statistical methods to analyze data of fraud incident reviews for control gaps, failures, and enhancement opportunities for by providing recommendations to the 1LOD. Collaborates in an advisory function with multiple areas in the Bank on complex fraud prevention projects requiring experienced analytical support of large, complex structured/unstructured data sets in order to extract business insights using statistical analysis methods (Decision tools, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting) and/or machine learning techniques with various tools including Open-Source methods. Using advanced coding solutions, provides analytical support for 2LOD internal fraud alert management and 2LOD external fraud functions. Strong project management skills and the ability to continuously multitask while meeting deadlines. Through direct and indirect oversight from the AntiFraud Group Manager, the position partners with dedicated 1LOD Fight Against Fraud teams and the business lines in the creation of enterprise key fraud risk indicators for reporting at various Risk Management Governance committees.

Essential Job Functions
• Analyzes and makes critical recommendations with enterprise level impacts to the 1st line Business Lines and the dedicated Fraud Prevention and Detection teams around best practices and processes for fraud scoring rules, strategies, and other business improvements. Identifies data trends and extrapolates results to report recommendations to reduce fraud activity.
• Collaborates in a lead advisory function with multiple areas in the Bank on complex fraud prevention projects requiring a mastery level of analytical support of large complex structured/unstructured data sets in order to extract business insights using statistical analysis methods and/or machine learning techniques with various tools including open source methods.
• Demonstrates mastery analytical knowledge and talent using various descriptive, predictive and prescriptive analytical methods.
• Manages projects leading small teams to support data analysis and concise reporting for new initiatives and other automation/business process improvement efforts.
• Makes recommendations to the Anti-Fraud Program management team of strategies for enhancing Program maturity, effectively executing budget allocation and establishing and maintaining Risk policies, procedures and processes to support the objectives of the Program.
• Credibly challenges 1st Line dedicated Fraud Prevention and Detection teams best practices and processes by solving the most complex analytical problems by identifying patterns in data and analyzing data metrics to diagnose problems with the goal of providing guidance for actionable next steps for reducing fraud activity and the associated losses at the Bank.
• Serves as the most senior data analyst advisory to the 1st Line in providing data driven challenge of the identification of risks and appropriate fraud prevention, detection and alert management controls in support of business strategy, technology changes and new activities.
• Provides mastery analytical support for Risk-managed employee behavioral monitoring alerting creating from scratch algorithms, predictive models, and forecasting often involving complex and intricate coding solutions and then determining the correct tool to use while automating long term solutions.

Other Job Duties:
• Provides credible challenge of the identification of risks and appropriate fraud prevention, detection and alert management controls established by the 1LOD in support for business strategy, technology changes and new activities
