24137,1327,Senior Data Analyst,Ingenio,United States,"Before we get started:

Here at Ingenio, we'd love to talk with you regardless of your qualifications or years of experience. If you believe you’d be a great fit for this role, we invite you to apply even if you do not meet all points on the job description...

Who we are:

Ingenio is a global media and technology company developing products that provide guidance on love, relationships, career, health, and life overall. We are passionate about connecting people with the world’s best advisors and content to empower everyone to live happier lives.

Together, Ingenio, adviqo and Barges offer the world's largest portfolio of over 25 marketplace and media brands in the spiritual and emotional wellness space – led by flagship brands such as Keen and Horoscope.com in the US, Questico and AstroTV in Germany, Purple Garden in Israel and Ukraine, The Circle in the UK, and Kang in France.

How you'll be impactful:

We are seeking a Senior Data Analyst to lead analytics on our digital content properties and empower our team to embrace data-driven decision-making. The ideal candidate is an experienced analyst with a breadth of experience across digital advertising, revenue forecasting, user segmentation, and A/B testing.

What you’ll be doing:
• Create, manage and maintain a centralized programmatic reporting interface
• Dive deep into our data to discover potential revenue opportunities, diagnose revenue-impacting issues and provide recommendations to senior leaders
• Partner with FP&A, BI, Programmatic, and Sales teams on revenue forecasting and budgeting
• Work with Product and Revenue Ops teams to evaluate the potential revenue impact from a proposed site/ad change, and provide recommendations and viable alternatives, as needed
• Develop new and effective ways to monitor and report on highly complex digital media inventory, particularly its consumption and monetization patterns
• Ensure quality assurance and accuracy across all programmatic partners and various data sources
• Build models that optimize internal referral logic to sister properties
• Support Marketing in analyzing social media and paid acquisition activities
• Support Product in analyzing changes to the UX of the site, app, store and subscription products
• Take ownership of Google Analytics (GA) and Firebase and be our SME
• Proactively explore user data, create segmentation models, and identify editorial opportunities
• Clearly communicate findings and actionable insights to teammates and executive leadership
• Partner with marketing to optimize (re-)engagement and monetization
• Partner with editorial team to target and measure engagement with custom content
• Partner with product to AB test site changes and maximize user experience
• Create dashboards and visualizations to monitor performance trends (Tableau)
• Identify and advocate for any tools necessary to get the insights needed

What you’ll need to be successful:
• 5+ years of experience as a data analyst / BI Dev
• Proven ability to frame and solve problems by extracting insight from raw data
• Proficient with SQL and at least one BI reporting tool (Tableau preferred)
• A curious mind and exceptional critical thinking skills
• Desire to learn new tools as needed: Firebase, AppsFlyer, GA, Optimizely, Mix Panel
• Willingness to challenge the status quo, ask questions, and roll-up sleeves to get things done
• Ability to work cross-functionally with a wide range of skillsets – engineers to creatives
• Bachelor’s degree and demonstrated interest in formal analytics training
• Experience with digital subscriptions a plus

Why Ingenio?

Our growing team of over 400 employees is powered by our diverse perspectives and company core values:
• We are humble. We believe the best result is achieved by leveraging others’ perspectives
• We think like owners. We make decisions that optimize for the greater good of the organization
• We challenge limiting beliefs. We are at our best when we identify and shatter status quo expectations

Perks & Benefits:
• Friendly, talented, collaborative and entrepreneurial team
• Premium medical, dental, and vision insurance
• Generous holiday and PTO policies
• 401k matching program
• Lunch
• Technology stipends
• Wellness allowance
• Training and development opportunities and allowance
• Fun and inclusive digital, and (in the future) in-person events
• Employee groups - DEI committee, fun committee, wellness group and more
• Flexible remote work

Ingenio is an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status",2022-02-14,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql']"
