24166,1356,Data & Reporting Analyst - REMOTE US,MassMutual,Anywhere,"The Opportunity

As a Data & Reporting Analyst you’ll have an opportunity to use your data analytic skills to provide a detailed understanding of how our business works. You will answer critical business questions such as “what happened and why?” as well as perform robust statistical analyses to understand “what will happen next?”, “when will it happen?” and “who will it impact?” to help our... leaders identify ways to optimize results. You may also be responsible for administering variable incentive compensations plans.

The Team

MassMutual has formed a dedicated third-party distribution channel, MassMutual Strategic Distributors (MMSD). MMSD’s strategy is to aggressively grow top line sales by expanding existing and establishing new partnerships with financial institutions (wire houses, banks, broker-dealers) and making significant investments in technology, sales, operations, marketing, and product development. Our strategy will be driven by dedicated teams across the enterprise where we will prioritize a dynamic, agile, and entrepreneurial culture.

The Impact

The key responsibilities will include but not be limited to the following:
• Deliver descriptive, diagnostic, predictive and prescriptive analytics to business stakeholders to drive action and decision making
• Translate complex business questions into problems that can be solved through data
• Lead efforts to continuously find ways to make processes automated and efficient, leading to more effective and timely output
• Provide ad hoc reporting design and support
• Prepare key statistics and daily/weekly/monthly updates and summaries to MMSD leadership team
• Provide “report outs” – summarizing and interpreting data in a manner that “tells a story”
• Leverage management data, prepare timely high-quality, clear, and succinct materials for weekly business meetings and other business execution needs, including senior or executive-level presentations, reports, and communications
• Work closely with the planning and strategy team, as well as senior leaders, to develop and produce reports which look to advance revenue and sales, analyze trends, and explore profitability across the MMSD segments
• Proactively identify and report out on any gaps, lapses, or opportunities to help progress MMSD strategy and business
• Work collaboratively with a team of analysts to support the senior leadership team’s vision and sales goals for MMSD
• Create supporting presentations and materials from a business/data analytics perspective
• Administer the Variable Incentive Compensation Program, accountable for the calculations of payments to eligible MMSD associates covered under the program agreed to by MMSD management and HR

Minimum Qualifications
• Bachelor’s Degree
• At least 3 years of experience processing, manipulating, validating, and analyzing large amounts of data
• Proven ability to utilize database technologies such as SQL server, Vertica, Teradata in a professional or academic setting
• Proven ability to deliver complex analysis in a digestible and actionable format in a professional or academic setting
• Proven ability to aggregate and make sense of large sets of data
• Outstanding analytical skills
