24245,1435,Data Scientist - Product,Channel Factory,United States,"Channel Factory provides intelligent marketing solutions for the next generation of contextual safety, suitability, and performance for brands and agencies. Our platform helps marketers implement, automate, and scale their marketing programs across the world’s largest video library, YouTube and emerging growth channels. We sit at the intersection of marketing and suitability and have a mission of... enabling the world’s top brands to consciously connect with the right audience in the right context, maximizing suitability and contextual performance.

Channel Factory embodies a strong start-up culture that values diversity, collaboration, and results. Our bias towards execution balances critical thinking, analysis, and pragmatic problem solving. We expect a lot from one another and value our thoughtful and intellectually curious company culture.

The Data Scientist is responsible for creating analytical solutions for data-driven marketing. The Data Scientist leverages supervised and unsupervised learning techniques to optimize all aspects of the marketing value chain (targeting, bid optimization, messaging, media preference, Text-to-Speech). Additionally, this role will have interdepartmental responsibility by supporting new product development and data best practices.

Responsibilities
• Develop repeatable automated “data wrangling” processes across multiple incoming data streams (performance, suitability, optimization, categorization, and more)
• Advise and develop on feature to create greater explanatory value from data sets
• Exploratory data analysis to determine trends with in the data which explain performance
• Build models to leveraging multiple algorithms (logistic regression, random forest, GBM, RNN, CNN, CHAID, etc)
• Conduct Text Mining (Sentiment Analysis, TF-IDF, etc) in relation to our suitability scoring
• Create code deployable as automated routines in production environments
• Model validation activities
• Enable supervised and unsupervised analysis of ad campaigns
• Build data visualizations to quickly communicate trends within campaigns
• Partner with client servicing teams to create presentations summarizing the results of campaign optimizations, highlighting key learnings & future actions
• Develop streamline solutions on data visualization that the Client Servicing team can employ
• Lead in marketplace analysis and trending to inform Strategists on pricing and Media buyers on buying tactics
• Partner with Design to develop and productize a client-facing visualization of campaign data & insights
• Establish statistically valid measurement practices to communicate unimpugnable campaign results
• Run ad-hoc analyses related to Product builds and Requirements to drive data-driven Product direction

Requirements
• Master’s degree in Statistics, Engineering, Economics, or Applied Mathematics
• 3 or more years of applied statistical analysis
• 3 or more years of experience with Python (Preferred) or R or Scala
• 3 or more years of experience with SQL
• For Python users with intermediate or better knowledge of scikit-learn or Keras, pandas, and NumPy, matplotlib or ggplot or boheh, and database interfaces
• For R users with intermediate or better knowledge of tidyverse (dplyr, tidyr, ggplot2, etc.), caret, gbm, randomForest, database interfaces (RODBC, dbi, RMySQL, etc)

Ideal Candidate Profile
• Natural curiosity about systems, data, and behaviors
• Independent self-starter with the ability to execute with limited supervision
• Effective communicator with the ability to convey complex ideas in simple general terms
• Resourceful in the development of solutions
• Experience with big data platforms (Hadoop, Spark, or Redshift)
• Experience in AdTech or data-driven marketing

Benefits
• Work with a leading startup in a high-demand industry, and you would be working with like-minded experts aiming to transform video targeting and buying operations
• Competitive salary
• Comprehensive medical benefits (Medical, Vision, Dental, and Life Insurance)
• Cell Phone & WiFi Reimbursement
• Gym stipend
• NatureBox credit for snacks
• Work-life flexibility – we value your contributions above all
