24313,1503,Senior Data Analyst I,Continental Resources,"Oklahoma City, OK","Job Summary

The Senior Data Analyst is primarily responsible for leading projects to automate manual processes and produce data driven insights for the team and other stakeholders across the organization. A successful candidate will also actively seek out and generate new and innovative ways to retrieve, visualize and analyze data across a variety of operational, geological and financial data... sources.

Serves as a resource for multiple projects across multiple work areas. Performs tasks to solve complex issues; may lead specific projects in areas of expertise. Fundamental knowledge of theories, principles and practices of Petroleum Engineering. Solves complex problems without precedent and/or structure; takes a broad perspective to identify solutions. Works independently, with guidance in complex situations.

Duties And Responsibilities
• Discover and troubleshoot data issues across sources, drive issues to resolution
• Create complex datasets, visualizations and tools
• Mentor and train staff in data management and analytics solutions; creates training content and executes across the team, department and company.
• Collaborate with varying levels of engineers, geologists and management to effectively gather data and build datasets for analytics, visualizations and reservoir modeling
• Own, maintain and enhance critical Spotfire Tools
• Own, maintain and enhance key Geographix projects for all basins
• Implement automated solutions to streamline manual team processes
• Perform data capture processes as necessary to support engineering and analytics efforts
• Personal commitment to inclusion and diversity
• Other duties as assigned.

Skills And Competencies
• SQL to retrieve data from systems, create integrated datasets, update data within systems and create data tables and views within CLR’s data warehouse
• Spotfire to enhance existing projects and create new projects using data from a variety of sources
• Understands or can learn the data models of Continental’s primary data sources including Aries, WellView, ProCount, SAP, Planning Analytics, eGIS, WLM, IHS and Enverus.
• Understands basic reservoir modeling principles and techniques
• Detail oriented with ability to organize and synthesize large amounts of data to generate high-quality, executive-level presentations in an efficient manner
• Understands E&P operations, drilling, completions, production, reservoir and geoscience data types
• Self-starter, with ability to work as part of a team or individually
• Advanced written and verbal communication skills
• Ability to quickly adapt and exemplify flexibility around process changes and shifting priorities
• Advanced skills with data, engineering and geoscience applications
• Advanced knowledge of data modeling and data integration principles and techniques
• Advanced programming skills capable of using all available techniques
• Drives results consistently, even under tough circumstances.
• Ability to prioritize multiple tasks with a no-job-too-big-or-small attitude
• Action oriented - Taking on new opportunities and tough challenges with a sense of urgency, high energy, and enthusiasm.
• Instills trust - Gaining the confidence and trust of others through honesty, integrity, and authenticity.
• Ensures accountability - Holding self and others accountable to meet commitments.
• Nimble learning - Actively learning through experimentation when tackling new problems, using both successes and failures as learning fodder.

Required Qualifications
• High School Diploma or GED
• Minimum of eight (8) years’ experience within the Oil and Gas industry working as a Data Analyst, Engineering Tech, Engineering Specialist, Business Analyst, Systems Analyst, IT Analyst or related role
• Advanced skills within Spotfire with the ability to use existing projects, inherit and enhance existing projects and create new projects leveraging multiple data sources
• Advanced skills in SQL with the ability to retrieve data from systems, create integrated datasets, update data within systems and create tables and views within CLR’s data warehouse
• An acceptable pre-employment background and drug test.

Preferred Qualifications
• Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited college or university in Management Information Systems, Data Analytics, Information Science/Management, Economics, Finance, Accounting or related degree.
• Experience in the engineering, geology and petrophysical suites of Geographix and Kingdom
• Coding skills in R or Python

Physical Requirements And Working Conditions
• Requires prolonged sitting, some bending, and stooping.
• Occasional lifting up to 25 pounds.
• Manual dexterity is sufficient to operate a computer keyboard and calculator.

Safety is a core value at Continental Resources, and we prioritize the health and safety of all employees and those who work around our facilities. As such, Continental Resources prefers for employees to be vaccinated against COVID-19.

Continental Resources, Inc. provides equal employment and affirmative action opportunities to applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or disability",2022-05-22,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sap', 'python', 'sql', 'r']"
24314,1504,Data Analyst II - Commercial Payments,Commerce Bank,"Kansas City, MO","About Working At Commerce

Wouldn’t it be great to build your career at a bank that’s known for helping people with their financial challenges? That’s exactly what you’d be doing when you join the team at Commerce Bank. We’re looking for teammates who are ready to do whatever it takes to help our customers with their everyday financial needs. You’d be helping yourself too, because Commerce has a... tradition of recognizing and rewarding team members for their talent, skills and contributions.

No wonder we’ve been an industry leader for over 155 years and have developed a reputation as a great place to work in the financial services world. If you’d like to be a part of a team and culture that is respected by its peers and in your community, we should talk. We’re always looking for the best and brightest.

About This Job

The Data Analyst provides reporting, business intelligence and analysis to the Commercial Payments Line of Business and functional department management. The analyst utilizes database programming (SQL), report design, Microsoft Access/Excel, Power BI, databases and other system tools to lead the business lines with the highest level of service in multiple areas including: sales strategy, business strategy, technical execution, and portfolio management. The incumbent should understand the business issue and its fit with enterprise goals in order to ascertain and consult insightful solutions. Project management skills are needed to develop requirements and project timelines. In addition, the position will require administering databases as well as a mind for automating repetitive tasks/reports and revision of those structures accordingly.

The ideal candidate will continuously ask what they can do to help. They will ask questions to understand customer needs and business goals and apply that understanding to define and evaluate multiple solutions. The ability to manage multiple projects concurrently while streamlining similar tasks across projects for maximum efficiency is expected. The candidate will display a sense of urgency in meeting deadlines and validate findings prior to presentation. The candidate will exhibit commitment and a sense of ownership by anticipating opportunities / issues and taking action to mitigate obstacles. Lastly, the analyst will evaluate emerging trends relative to current technical and leadership skills and request training to enhance those skills.

Essential Functions
• Develop and schedule releases for very complex relationship pricing model(s) and customer level profitability
• Develop new reports and dashboards ranging from sales metrics to financial trends to portfolio analysis
• Setup databases with various levels of complexity for aiding in the explanation of P&L financial variances
• Perform data management type initiatives which may require pulling and sending data from one, or more, system(s) or department(s) to another
• Ensure data cleanliness and accuracy within the database table/relationship structure
• Develop and implement databases, data collection systems/repositories for data analysis and consumption
• Plan and facilitate regular meetings with work group and leadership within the company
• Simplify very complex data to draw observations for all levels of management
• Create new ways to review data differently and articulate findings to management
• Coordinate efforts and track progress of multiple groups that are working on related projects or tasks
• Actively participate with other data team members to enhance department processes
• Provide quality assurance of imported data, working with quality assurance analyst if necessary
• Schedule, structure and facilitate working sessions to develop/build consensus on data items or terms with different applications or interpretations in different departments.
• Perform other duties as assigned

Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Required
• Intermediate knowledge of financial analysis, pricing, profitability and profit/loss statements
• Intermediate knowledge of visualization tools such as Power BI and Tableau
• Excellent facilitation and negotiation skills
• Ability to develop and manage relationships with wide variety of business units
• Ability to communicate technical information/concepts to non-technical audiences
• Strong analytical and critical thinking skills
• Ability to utilize best practices in data design concepts
• Ability to establish and meet deadlines consistently
• Strong meeting management skills that include scheduling, agenda planning, and decision summaries
• Motivated and organized self-starter with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities
• Inquisitive, agile and strong team player with excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills
• Ability to remain adaptable and resilient to all situations with an optimistic outlook and cast a positive shadow that is aligned with our culture and Core Values
• Intermediate level proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, Teams and Outlook

Education & Experience
• Bachelor’s or equivalent combination of education and experience required
• 3+ years of work-related experience in systems, data management, data science required
• Experience with business intelligence, data warehousing, statistical analysis or visualization platforms required
• Experience using querying and visualization tools such as Business Objectives, BI Tools, SAS, SQL, MS Access, etc. required
• Experience designing, managing and continually improving business processes preferred
• Experience developing organizational policies and procedures and implementing by building consensus and stakeholder commitment preferred
• Experience with application management including version control and handling large data sets and relational databases preferred
• Experience navigating data warehouses like Teradata or similar preferred

Location: 1000 Walnut St, Kansas City, Missouri 64106

Time Type:

Full time",2022-03-19,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'word', 'power_bi', 'sql', 'outlook', 'sas', 'excel']"
24315,1505,Data Analyst,"WOW! Internet, Cable & Phone","Home, KS","Job Description

The Data Analyst will be required to access and compile large amounts of data, analyze the data, interpret and quantify trends on the operational aspects of the customer care organization. The role will also need to effectively communicate concise findings and recommendations to various levels of WOW’s leadership. The Analyst will work on creating and/or enhancing various... analytical tools that will help improve the operational results and may also be required to develop requirements and perform testing on these analytical tools.

Duties And Responsibilities

Essential duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to those listed below:
• Responsible for providing data analyses for business operations for the customer care organization
• Gathers and analyzes data thoroughly to identify problems of varying complexities and provide business solutions; via data analysis, uncover the insights to the business that may be hidden in the data
• Create accurate and timely analyses on a wide variety of areas including operational performance, trend analysis, campaign performance, and subscriber behavior.
• Additional responsibilities may include offer forecasting and assist managers in developing and maintaining operational dashboards.
• Provide insight into and develop new ideas and approaches to improve operational results.
• Partner with cross functional teams such as Finance, Strategy, Business Analytics and Customer Care to understand enterprise trends, competitive environment and their impacts on subscriber behavior and provide conclusions and recommendations to business owners.
• Conduct trending analysis to identify improvements and understand the customer experience aimed at actionable business improvement
• Analysis efforts will include utilizing structured and unstructured data across different systems and platforms through various data manipulation, cleaning and merging techniques to deliver complex and or advanced statistical modeling analysis, actionable recommendations and meaningful insights
• Statistical analysis to identify correlations within the data
• Other duties as assigned

Qualifications

To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.

Education
• Bachelor’s degree from four year college or university; or at least one year of related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience

Experience
• Prefer candidates with degree in quantitative analysis, mathematics, economics or finance with prior experience in consumer services and products
• Prefer candidates with educational background or working experience with statistics
• Highly analytical and creative thinker
• Experience in preparing written project status reports and executive briefings required
• Highly disciplined self-starter with solid collaboration and communication skills who thrives on data, language and technology
• Must be self-directed, organized and detail oriented as well as have the ability to multitask and work effectively in a fast paced environment
• Excellent communication skills including an ability to communicate and work effectively with business managers and diverse cross-functional groups
• Ability to accommodate change and adapt accordingly
• Have participated or led data analysis in highly complex business problems
• Have developed executive level presentations that identify business trends, operational successes and opportunities based on transactional data

Computer Skills
• Skilled in Excel, Access, SAS and SQL
• Proficiency with word processing, excel spreadsheets, Power point presentations, Internet software, E-mail, Database software
• Must be able to use in-house billing and CRM systems in order to effectively produce metric reports

Physical Demands/Working Conditions

The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.
• regularly required to talk and hear
• required to use hands to type, handle objects and paperwork
• required to use close vision and be able to focus
• Must be able to perform computer functions and operate routine office equipment
• Must be able to sit or stand for extended periods of time
• Must be able to travel for business purposes on an occasional basis

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment

without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran",2022-10-20,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['spreadsheet', 'word', 'sql', 'sas', 'excel']"
