About This Job

The Data Analyst Intern will gain real world experience in a dynamic and supportive environment. You will get to be a member of the IT Project & Portfolio Management Office. The main purpose of this role is to assist with analyzing project data and gather requirements that will be used to increase productivity and the usability of our Portfolio and Agile Project Management Tools. The Data Analyst Intern will be expected to jump in and understand the meaning behind the data in the various data sources and accurately leverage the data for business decision making. This position will get the opportunity to assist with strategic build outs of custom Power BI reports and dashboards within our Portfolio and Agile Project Management Tools to improve the accuracy of internal and external reporting. This position will also contribute to the standardization and continuous improvement to mature the portfolio management and execution processes.

What You’ll Get
• Paid internship running from late May through early August with full time potential upon graduation
• Interaction and exposure to senior leadership
• Participate in weekly lunch-and-learns with other interns throughout the bank
• Partner with a data analytics mentor to advance your skills while owning real and meaningful work

Essential Functions
• Collaborate with the IT Project & Portfolio Management Office that supports the bank
• Partner with your peers and mentors to complete projects and duties
• Partner and communicate with various stakeholders to gather requirements for enhanced custom or automated reporting
• Perform data analysis and tracking of project data to assist in managing and forecasting projects and portfolios
• Understand, analyze, and use project and portfolio data to answer questions, spot patterns, resolve data issues, and solve business problems
• Perform other duties as assigned

Work Schedule
• Monday-Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm
• Hybrid (In-office and Remote)

Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Required
• Ability to apply strong analytical and complex problem solving and critical thinking skills
• Proficiency with Microsoft Excel including data mining and PivotTables and Outlook
• Working knowledge of Microsoft Power BI, Report Writer, or other business intelligence software
• SQL query development skills and understanding of relational databases.
• Motivated and organized self-starter with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities
• Inquisitive, agile and strong team player with excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills
• Experience with Azure DevOps and/or Planview Enterprise One is a plus
• Ability to remain adaptable and resilient to all situations with an optimistic outlook and cast a positive shadow that is aligned with our culture and Core Values

Education & Experience
• Pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Data Analysis or equivalent.
• preferred Junior or Senior standing
• Interns must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship

Location: 922 Walnut St, Kansas City, Missouri 64106

