24422,1612,"Internal Auditor and Data Analyst, Internal Audit",PSCU,Anywhere,"Join the people helping people.

For people drawn to serving others through their work, PSCU is a place to thrive, as we serve our credit union members best by taking care of each other first...

If you want to help shape an industry, challenge yourself, and invest in your own future, this is the place for you. PSCU is a highly accessible environment where you’re empowered to think on your feet, work from your heart, and discover the very best version of your professional and personal self. “Our Momentum. Your Moment.”

This application is the first step in seizing your moment.

Basic Function

This role is a hybrid position that will be responsible for both internal audit and data analytics functions. The Data Analyst and Internal Auditor will work as part of the Internal Audit team and split their time between participation in internal audits, and furthering the development of a continuous monitoring and analytics program within the Internal Audit department.

Within the capacity of an auditor, the individual will participate in the execution of Internal Audit activities including evaluating risks, testing controls, and reviewing processes related to the organization’s internal controls, department procedures, and compliance with regulatory rules and company policies. They will assist with the tracking of open audit findings and facilitate response generation, information gathering, testing of evidence, and escalation of prior findings with Audit Management.

In addition, the position will also be responsible for expanding the use of data analytics within the audit fuction. The role will be instrumental in the continued improvement of the internal control and governance processes via data analytics, reporting and continuous monitoring activities.

The ideal candidate will possess both strong audit expertise as well as technical knowledge and expertise in data mining, script and report writing, as well as continuous monitoring /auditing activities. Expertise in any of the following applications would be beneficial: Diligent/Highbond (Formerly ACL/Galvanize), IDEA, PowerBI, Certified Analytics Professional, Tableau, or similar business/data analytics software, tools and products.

Essential Functions & Responsibilities
• Perform internal risk assessments under the direction of Internal Audit Management.
• Identify key controls, control design, and/or control deficiencies through the development of a risks and controls matrix.
• Create process documentation, including process narratives and flow charts, to assist with audit planning and execution.
• Create audit program and testing procedures at the entity, process, transaction or application levels.
• Make recommendations on applying data analytics and continuous monitoring audit activities during the audit process.
• Assesses risks and internal controls by identifying areas of non-compliance; evaluating manual and automated processes; identifying process weaknesses and inefficiencies and technical issues.
• Partner with internal clients to define action plans for deficiencies identified. Monitor completion of action plans and, and provide support when needed or requested by Audit Management.
• Standardize and automate data preparation and reporting.
• Collect, process, ""clean"", analyze, and report on data from various internal and external applications and databases as well as other data sources when necessary.
• Identify and interpret trends or patterns in complex data sets.
• Train and develop data analytic skills within the Internal Audit team.
• Evaluate accounting and/or technical documentation, previous reports, data, flowcharts, etc.
• Create functional specifications and work closely with end-users to deliver business solutions.
• Identify, define, and implement process automation and/or workflow improvements.
• Perform other duties as assigned.

Physical Demands
• While performing the duties of this Job, the employee is regularly required to sit; use hands to finger, handle, or feel and talk or hear
• Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision
• Ability to occasionally lift/move up to 25 pounds
• Individuals with a disability who are otherwise able to perform the essential functions of the job may request a reasonable accommodation through the Human Resources department.

Supervisory Responsibility
• No

Position Specifications
• Bachelor’s Degree in Business, Information Technology, Mathematics, or related field required.
• Currently holds, or actively pursuing, an audit professional certification, such as CIA, CISSP, or CISA or equivalent audit credentials.
• Required to hold an audit certification(s) as condition of continued employment.
• Professional certification(s) in data analytics preferred.
• Three (3) years of experience in data analytics, audit or an audit-related function such as accounting, risk management, IT, or other business or operational position required. Advanced computer skills with various types of finance, accounting, database and analytics technologies, such as Query SAP, Oracle, Enterprise Data Warehouses and/or Data Lakes, and other audit software and databases such as Highbond/Galvanize -ACL / Analytics Exchange, PowerBI, IDEA, etc. required.
• Experience with payment systems and financial services related to the credit/debit card industry preferred.

Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities
• Demonstrate behaviors based on PSCU values: Excellence, Innovation, Leadership, Passion, Trust, and Diversity, Equity, & Inclusion
• Ability to establish relationships and rapport with all levels of personnel, including executive and other levels of management, company employees, vendors, clients and members
• Excellent teammate; Adds to team results by welcoming new and different work requirements; exploring new opportunities to make valuable contributions to the organization; helping others accomplish related job results as and where needed
• Strong understanding of financial services, systems, operational, and/or technology controls; knowledge of internal audit standards and practices; must have working knowledge of IT general controls
• Experience with financial institution regulatory standards such as NCUA, OCC, FFIEC, Nacha ACH, or related, a plus
• Advanced computer skills on MS Office including Microsoft word processing, presentation powerpoint, excel spreadsheets, and visio flowchart
• Project a professional demeanor and have the ability to handle confidential matters with utmost integrity
• Ability to work on your own initiative and as part of a team
• Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate effectively both verbally and written formats, including good presentation and report writing skills
• Ability to exercise discretion and good judgment in making decisions; strong problem solving, reasoning, and analytical skills; high attention to detail
• Project management and time-management skills, balancing multiple tasks and meeting deadlines, under pressure
• Strong Information Technology skills and working knowledge of SharePoint, a plus
• Ability to travel as needed, less than 25%

Pay Equity

The Typical Annual Hiring Range For This Position Based On Relevant Experience And Internal Equity Is

PSCU is committed to pay equity and a competitive benefits package.

$60,500.00

to

$88,700.00
• Note: The amount shown is based on full time annual salary and would be prorated based on role.

In addition this position is eligible for an incentive plan, based on performance.

Benefits

At PSCU, everything we do recognizes the fact that our employees are our most important asset. That’s why we are committed to a work/life integration that goes above and beyond to ensure that you have quality time at home with your family and/or to pursue outside interests and aspirations. We back this up with generous PTO, the opportunity to work remotely, flexible scheduling, and a management team that understands how to adjust when the unexpected curveballs of life happen.

Check out the comprehensive benefits PSCU has to offer that further solidifies our reputation as a company that just “gets it” when it comes to balancing life’s planned and unplanned events while equipping you with all the tools for growth.

