Children’s Minnesota is one of the largest pediatric health systems in the United States and the only health system in Minnesota to provide care exclusively to children, from before birth through young adulthood. An independent and not-for-profit system since 1924, Children’s Minnesota is one system serving kids throughout the Upper Midwest at two free-standing... hospitals, nine primary care clinics, multiple specialty clinics and seven rehabilitation sites. As The Kids Experts™ in our region, Children’s Minnesota is regularly ranked by U.S. News & World Report as a top children’s hospital. Find us on Facebook @childrensminnesota or on Twitter and Instagram @childrensmn. Please visit childrensMN.org.

Position Summary

The Sr. Data Analyst provides advanced analytic support to functional business and clinical areas in order to formulate actionable insights and strategies against departmental/organizational goals and business/clinical outcomes. The Sr. Analyst will drive the analysis of data from a variety of sources (e.g., the electronic health record, billing claims, cost reports, patient satisfaction surveys, etc.) to help deliver Value across its six domains: Effective, Timely, Efficient, Safe, Equitable, Patient Centered. The Sr. Analyst will design, build, and deliver comprehensive data solutions that guide decision-making, population health management, cost containment, and quality improvement strategies. The Sr. Data Analyst is responsible for leading the design, creation and automation of internal and external reports, creating executive-level dashboards, and presenting information to help leaders and stakeholders across the organization understand the operational and clinical impacts of the data. The Sr. Analyst has a deep understanding of effective data visualization practices and provides leadership and coaching to drive the organization toward data-driven management practices.

