The Business Intelligence Analyst works closely with the entire Analytics team and other business units to contribute to the development of the Member Insight product including defining the requirements and design of the product while maintaining data governance and data quality. This position supports data quality, data governance and data standards practices for the Analytics Team with a focus on Debit and Credit information. Customers could include all internal lines of business, partners and customers.

The Business Intelligence Analyst will work with the Analytics Solutions team to manage data as an asset and to ensure trusted quality data. The candidate will serve as a consultant related to using data effectively for process improvement, best practices, improved architecture, data interpretation and will also assist with training others on governed data sources. They will collaborate with members of various groups to identify the business needs, elicit, and draft high level requirements for end user analysis and semantic layers as well as be responsible for creating and maintaining data mappings & definitions.

Essential Functions & Responsibilities
• Validate and Analyze large data sets by profiling individual data points to determine data definitions & usefulness in analysis to end users becoming the subject matter experts on assigned data domains.
• Serve as authority for all information for assigned subject areas and strategic projects.
• Partner with stakeholders to elicit business requirements and provide research and analysis to aid in solving complex business scenarios with data.
• Analyze and prepare Requirements Documentation including but not limited to: Defining business requirements, business rules, data definitions, data transformations, end user reporting, and semantic layers.
• Prepare documentation for marketing releases and product releases.
• Validate and profile data to ensure proper accuracy.
• Drive process improvement for all data quality core processes to execute with simplicity, speed, quality and efficiency.
• Maintain business dictionary and data quality at the application/database level.
• Certify data and reporting to be accurate and consumable.
• Establish and build effective relationships with business customers and external customers.
• Develop an understanding and knowledge of key business functions related to specific data subject areas.
• Integrate all application / database technical metadata into the EMR for available capabilities.
• Work with the larger analytics team to ensure data is accurate and consumable for end users.
• Assure all technical metadata is connected to the business context along with Data lineage.
• Provide training or education to employees on governed data sources and metadata.
• Implement roles, responsibilities, procedures, processes and guidelines for respective applications/databases in compliance with enterprise business data standards.
• Ensure business information is properly used in operational environment.
• Proactively suggest improvements to Analytics operational process.
• Participate actively in Data and Analytics activities to improve department processes and procedures.
• Proactively enhances business semantics, maintaining metadata and ensuring data quality.
• Mentor Data Stewards in data analysis and design as well as their use of the Member Insight product.
• Contribute to the creation of training materials and CommunityVue reporting for the Member Insight product.
• Manage multiple priorities and deal effectively with senior management, staff members, clients, and vendors including doing in person or WebEx presentations.
• Perform other duties as assigned.

Position Requirements
• Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Science, Data Science, Applied Math Business Intelligence or a related quantitative discipline or equivalent combination of education and experience required.
• Four (4) years of experience within the payments industry in a Data Analyst or Business Analyst role with experience in investigating large data sets, identifying trends and creating meaningful insight required.
• Three (3) years’ product management or business consulting experience required.
• Experience in project management is a plus.

Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities
