24553,1743,Data Analyst & Researcher,BrightAction,Anywhere,"About BrightAction

At BrightAction we’re on a mission to empower people on climate solutions and help them take action at home and beyond...

Most people are worried about climate change (75% of Americans according to Yale research) and want to help, but are not sure where to start. It turns out we can all help - a lot. 40% of US carbon emissions come from 5 basic household activities we do every day. We now have solutions for all 5 that not only help with climate change, but also save families money, improve our health and create local jobs right away. We all have the power to help and make a difference on climate change! This is an all hands on deck moment. To reduce emissions and meet global goals it will take all of us - strong government policies, companies taking actions and all of us taking everyday actions to help move solutions forward.

BrightAction is an engagement platform that makes it simple, easy and fun to learn about solutions and take affordable actions that make an impact. We work with companies, organizations and cities to engage employees, members and residents on climate solutions. Our platform is data driven with an advanced calculator that tracks impact, provides custom user recommendations and makes participation fun with goals and challenges. Most importantly, we connect users to share, work together and support each other in taking action. Our platform provides customers custom branding and engagement tools to drive participation and make an impact on climate change. Join us on our mission to empower people on climate solutions!

The Opportunity

At BrightAction we have developed a best in class carbon calculator that provides our users localized and personalized estimates of their impact and savings from taking action. We are looking for a Data Analyst & Researcher to help identify new and expanded data sources and build our data sets and data model. This position is an expert in data research, acquisition and analysis and data management strategies. We are looking for someone who is a true “data geek” that is passionate about sourcing and utilizing the right data to create data tools to help empower users to take action on climate change and see the impact of their actions. Become an expert on global carbon calculations, a rapidly growing field and make a difference!

What you will be doing:
• Researching data sources and identifying the best data options to create robust carbon and savings data analytics
• Assessing data sources for attributes such as accuracy, availability and frequency of updates
• Managing data including building tools for data import and updates and ensuring data quality and accuracy
• Analyze data and data model to identify new data strategies and insights
• Develop strategies for data reporting and visualizations for customers and users.
• Collaborating with subject matter experts to develop new insights and contribute to the field

Requirements:
• 3+ years experience in data analytics role
• Strong quantitative skills, including research, analysis and utilization of large data sets
• BS required (or in progress), BS in Computer Science, Data Analytics, Mathematics or related field preferred
• Detail oriented with high standards of quality
• Strong work ethic and self-starter
• Experience with data modeling a plus
• Excel & SQL proficiency required, Python proficiency preferred
• English proficiency required

Part time, contract (approximately 10 hours/week). Remote position open to any U.S. location.

BrightAction is mission driven and has a positive work environment and creative, collaborative team. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion are part of our core values and are a priority in all of our activities from hiring to our company culture to our product design. BrightAction is an Equal Opportunity Employer and we encourage women, people of color, LGBTQ+ and individuals with disabilities to apply. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive, safe, and growth-oriented environment for all members of our team. Please submit a resume and cover letter to apply",2022-11-25,Part-time,data analyst,United States,"['sql', 'excel', 'python']"
