24822,78,Technical Analyst IV - Salesforce Data Integration Specialist ...,BOK Financial,"Tulsa, OK","Req ID:69042

Job Location:320 S. BostonTulsaOK...

Areas of Interest:Information Services

Colorado Base Salary Range:Not Available

BOK Financial (BOKF), Headquartered in Tulsa, Oklahoma, BOK Financial Corporation (NASDAQ: BOKF) is a top 25 U.S.-based financial services holding company with operations in ten states - Oklahoma, Texas, Arkansas, Arizona, Colorado, Kansas/Missouri, New Mexico, Nebraska and Wisconsin. The company began more than 100 years ago in Tulsa and has successfully diversified into a variety of industries, businesses and geographies. .
Bonus Type
Discretionary

Summary

At BOK Financial, our success starts with our incredible talent.Are you an experienced Technical Data Analyst who enjoys problem solving and learning? This is an opportunity to become involved in some major transformative projects and leverage new cutting- edge technology. Bring your passion for technical innovation. It's an exciting time to join us!

Job Description

As part of a growing team responsible for delivering one of largest transformational technology initiatives at the bank, you will be responsible for the evolving our most complex systems to meet future business needs using empiricism and validated learning. You will use your extensive data and technical expertise to focus on data integrations into and out of the Salesforce FSC platform, demonstrating an understanding of technical problems and solutions as you drive the evolution of our technical architecture.

Team Culture

We are one of many teams committed to delivering the best end to end sales and loan origination capabilities to our bankers by leveraging the Salesforce FSC and nCino Bank Operating System platforms. We are scaling out to multiple agile teams utilizing the Scrum and Nexus frameworks to achieve more together than we could on our own, and living out the scrum values each day. We are committed to create a diverse and sustainable environment where team members can be curious, collaborative, and grow, all while delivering fabulous business outcomes.

How You'll Spend Your Time
• You will work directly with all scrum team members to facilitate conversations, confirm understanding, test code, and provide fast feedback.
• You will work directly with all scrum team members to ensure stories are completed with the highest quality and the team achieves the sprint goal.
• You will work with product owners to understand new integration opportunities for data coming into or out of the Salesforce ecosystem.
• You will work with core loan system subject matter experts to deeply understand data models and define transformation logic.
• You will use ad-hoc SQL querying and other prototyping methods to confirm data assumptions and business rules are correct.
• You will use your analytical and deductive reasoning skills to determine root cause of defects in ETL code and develop solutions.
• You will use your creativity to develop integration and data flow diagrams to illustrate technical concepts to business stakeholders and team members.
• You will help configure and support our Salesforce org as a Salesforce and nCino Admin.
• You will utilize your vast knowledge of troubleshooting to take on incidents by participating in periodic on call rotations.
• You will help mentor junior analysts as you are the most knowledgeable in your space.
• You will apply your deep understanding of lean and agile principles to continuously improve our understanding, our products and our team.
• You will flex to do whatever is needed to help the team achieve the sprint and product goal.

Education & Experience Requirements

This level of knowledge is normally acquired through completion of (a/an) Bachelor's Degree in Information Technology or Computer Science or related field of study and / or 5-7 years of directly related experience in Technical Analysis, Data Analytics, or Bank Operations or equivalent combination of education and experience.
• Software integration, system integration, and technology used
• Strong data analysis and profiling abilities using SQL
• Familiarity with data integration design patterns (API, streaming, enterprise job schedulers, batch)
• Dashboards and Reporting Experience (Salesforce and PowerBI, preferred)
• Salesforce Admin (preferred)
• RDBMS principles and tools
• Tiered environments (e.g. development, testing, UAT, production, DR)
• Quality / Testing Methodologies and tools
• Lean and Agile methodologies (preferred)
• Ability to effectively plan time, method, manner and sequence of own work assignments
• Oral and written communication skills to effectively represent self and BOKF
• Demonstrated ability to establish and build healthy working partnerships with clients, vendors and peers.

Working Conditions & Physical Requirements
Office - Hybrid

BOK Financial is a stable and financially strong organization that provides excellent training and development to support building the long term careers of our employees. With passion, skill and partnership you can make an impact on the success of the bank, our customers and your own career!

Apply today and take the first step towards your next career opportunity!

If you are interested in a career with BOK Financial text ""BOKF"" to 25000 to engage with Olivia our virtual recruiting assistant.

BOK Financial is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities for training, compensation, transfer, promotion and other aspects of employment for all qualified applicants and employees without regard to sex, race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, genetic information or veteran status.

Please contact with any questions",2022-09-20,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'sql']"
24823,79,Data Analyst - Full-time / Part-time,Jiffy Trip,"Enid, OK","Are you looking to join a great company that is on the fast track for growth? Do you have a strong desire to serve others and exceed their expectations? Are you customer service driven? If so, you may be the person that we are looking for! Apply today!

Hammer Williams Company, the parent company for Jiffy Trip Convenience Stores, is celebrating our 50th anniversary and we are growing with an... expectation to double in size over the next several years. Our stores are currently located throughout Oklahoma and we are expanding into Arkansas with new stores expected to open later this year. With our company growth, we have a need to expand our IT Department and we are looking for the right person to join our team as a Data Analyst.

Description

The Data Analyst’s role is to design data modeling/analysis services used to mine enterprise systems and applications for knowledge and information that enhance business processes.

Responsibilities

Strategy & Planning
• Devise, develop, and deploy required data queries in response to business user needs.
• In conjunction with data owners and department managers, develop data models and protocols for mining production databases.
• Assist in the development of data management policies and procedures.
• Identify research questions, problem solve using data analysis, and communicate the results to various stakeholders

Operational Management
• Work with application development staff to coordinate the creation and management of data queries.
• Collaborate with unit managers, end users, development staff, and other stakeholders to integrate data management applications with existing systems.
• Provide and apply quality assurance best practices for data analysis services across the organization.
• Develop, implement, and maintain change control and testing processes for modifications to data models.
• Develop routines for end users to facilitate best-practice use of data management tools.
• Collaborate with database and disaster recovery administrators to ensure effective protection and integrity of data assets.
• Monitor data management system details within the database, including stored procedures and execution time, and implement efficiency improvements.
 
Formal Education & Certification
• College diploma or university degree in the field of computer science or statistics, and/or 2 years of equivalent work experience.
• Certifications in MSQL, AWS, Azure, Sysadmin strongly desired.

Knowledge & Experience
• Strong understanding of data models, structures, theories, principles, and practices.
• Working knowledge of data modeling tools such as ER/Studio, DbSchema, ConceptDraw or Erwin.
• Familiarity with data preparation, processing, classification, and forecasting.
• Working technical experience with relational database servers, including Msql, MySQL, NoSQL.
• Working knowledge of PowerBI or equivalent tools.
• Direct experience with data management techniques.
• Project management experience.
• Good understanding of the organization’s goals and objectives.
• Involvement in inter-departmental projects and experience communicating with various stakeholders
• Experience in the Convenience or QSR channels is a plus

Personal Attributes
• Good written and oral communication skills.
• Strong technical documentation skills.
• Good interpersonal skills.
• Ability to conduct research into data management issues, practices, and products as required.
• Ability to present ideas in a user-friendly language.
• Highly self-motivated and directed.
• Keen attention to detail.
• Proven analytical and problem-solving abilities.
• Ability to effectively prioritize and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment.
• Strong customer service orientation.
• Experience working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment.

Work Conditions
• On-call availability for 3-14 days per month.
• Sitting for extended periods of time.
• Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard, mouse, power tools, and to handle other computer components",2022-06-17,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'azure', 'mysql', 'aws', 'nosql']"
