24964,220,Contract Data Analyst - Now Hiring,AmerisourceBergen Corporation,"Sacramento, CA","Are you looking to make a difference in a patient's life? At AmerisourceBergen, you will find an innovative and collaborative culture that is patient focused and dedicated to making a difference. As an organization, we are united in our responsibility to create healthier futures. Join us and Apply today!

What you will be doing...

As of August 24, 2021, AmerisourceBergen requires all U.S. team members to be fully vaccinated and show proofof completed vaccine status at time of hire. If you cannot receive the COVID-19 vaccine due to adisability/medicalreasonor sincerely held religious belief you will be required to follow AmerisourceBergen's policy and process toapply for anexemption/accommodation.

POSITION SUMMARY:

Under direct supervision of the Director Provider Network Contracts, this position is directly responsible for developing and managing the data analytics for payer contracts. Conducts analysis and compilation of key business indicators that are tied to reimbursement strategies and tracks payer reimbursement following the implementation of new contracts and continuous monitoring of existing contracts. Assists with administering payer contracting operations and supports additional pharmacy programs as needed.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:

1. Responsible for designing, developing and implementing strategic contract analytics and reimbursement model(s) to identify area(s) for contract improvement and contract validation.

2. Accesses, analyzes and interprets all internal and external data sources to analyze reimbursement, gross profit, market position and market share to enhance contract negotiations and make objective, fact-based decisions.

3. Identifies trends in reimbursement and makes recommendations related to contracts, based on data-driven analysis.

4. Works directly with AmerisourceBergen data team(s) to define data requirements and reports needed to extract and compile data to measure payer compliance with contracts.

5. Works directly with AmerisourceBergen data team(s) to review external data feeds (e.g. IQVIA), to consistently improve methods to track and report contract related information.

6. Effectively communicates results and contract implications to management and internal departments.

7. Assists with the development of contract presentation materials for regional and national meetings, trade shows, and conventions.

8. Responsible for pre-negotiation preparations such as data gathering and contract analysis.

9. Participates in analysis to support negotiations with payers or proposals for new program opportunities.

10. Develops and maintains strategic relationships with peer-level contacts at PBMs or payers involved with retail pharmacy provider network contracting operations.

11. Monitors the approval process for contracts, identifies and resolves business issues that pertain to potential agreements.

12. Participates and supports development of overall objectives along with the long-term goals of AmerisourceBergen Corporation.

Participates in special projects and performs other duties as assigned
What your background should look like

EXPERIENCE AND EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:

Requires background in pharmacy benefit administration or PSAOs, retail pharmacy operations, and managed care with an understanding of pharmacy claims data and reimbursement terminology and methodology as well as the current and future business challenges pharmacies face. Broad training in fields such as business administration, economics, finance or similar vocations generally obtained through completion of a four-year bachelor's degree program and/or with at least five (5) years of experience in a PSAO, Managed Care organization or PBM environment preferred or equivalent work experience is required. Registered Pharmacy Technician designation desirable. Normally requires a minimum of 3 years related and progressively responsible experience.

MINIMUM SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE AND ABILITY REQUIREMENTS:

1. Pharmacy Benefit Management or PSAO background, preferably with pharmacy claims data, reimbursement and provider network contract experience.

2. Familiarity with NCPDP field formats, Maximum Allowable Cost pricing, 340B and Payor contract retail pharmacy reimbursement terms

3. Knowledge of ABC products, programs and services desirable

4. Ability to work under pressure to balance competing priorities and to meet time sensitive deadlines

5. Strong organizational and analytical skills; attention to detail

6. Ability to interpret complex material into easily understood analysis

7. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing; interacts with all levels of associates and management within and outside the organization.

8. Strong interpersonal skills

9. Excellent customer service management skills

10. Strong navigation of multiple systems and the consolidation of data from various sources

11. Strong computer skills necessary to operate effectively with company systems and programs

12. Contract document management (WORD, POWERPOINT) and advanced financial analytical skills (EXCEL) required.

13. Experience with relational databases and knowledge of query tools and/or statistical business intelligence software (e.g., Micro Strategy, AQT) is required.

14. Must have experience with extracting data from Salesforce or similar.
What AmerisourceBergen offers

We offer competitive total rewards compensation. Our commitment to our associates includes benefit programs that are comprehensive, diverse and designed to meet the various needs across our associate population.

Throughout our global footprint and various business units, we take a balanced approach to the benefits we offer. Many benefits are company-paid, while others are available through associate contributions. Specific benefit offerings may vary by location, position and/or business unit.
