24966,222,Data Business Analyst II - Full-time / Part-time,"Bass Pro, LLC","Springfield, MO","POSITION SUMMARY:

The Business Analyst II collects, interprets, and publishes data and analytics to drive actionable insight and value within the organization using statistical analysis, explanatory and predictive modeling, and data mining.The Business Analyst II determine best practices and develops actionable insights and recommendations for the current business operations, working directly... with the business partners to identify analytical requirements and priorities.The position may help to produce ad hoc data reports, and may assist in implementing or developing systems to capture business operation information and may occasionally guide less experienced and knowledgeable Business Analysts.

ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:
• Collects data through means such as analyzing business results or by setting up and managing new data assets to identify opportunities, highlight strengths, and provide recommended corrective actions.
• Monitors existing KPI metrics, develops new metrics, and identifies correlations and root causes.
• Transfers data into a new format to make it more appropriate for analysis.
• Creates new, experimental frameworks to collect data.
• Builds tools to automate data collection.
• Searches and analyzes large data sets to drive actionable intelligence and insights.
• Designs, creates, and presents data through visualization for business uses to accelerate information to action at scale.
• Correlates similar data to find actionable results.
• Develops programs, methodologies and reports for analyzing and presenting data.
• Invents new ways to define and measure program effectiveness and organizational productivity.
• Acts as a SME for BI tools and delivering training to team members on the usage of tools when necessary.
• ALL OTHER DUTIES AS ASSIGNED

EXPERIENCE/QUALIFICATIONS:
• Master's Degree in statistics, data science, business analytics, computer science, software engineering, or a related technical field, or an individual with 4+ years' experience of practical learning and experience in analytics or data science.
• Preference may be given to candidates who have experience in data analytics for manufacturing companies.

KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITY
• Knowledge of programming languages including SQL, Python, R, and Scala
• Familiarity with business intelligence tools (e.g. Domo, Tableau, Power BI)
• Strong statistical skills & working knowledge in application of skills
• Experience with big data technologies
• Advanced ability to perform exploratory data analysis
• Exceptional technical writing skills
• Ability to communicate complex data in a simple, actionable way both verbally and in writing
• Ability to visualize data in the most effective way possible
• Analytical and problem-solving skills
• Experience with machine learning and AI
• Familiarity with data management tools
• Ability to work independently and with team members from varied backgrounds
• Excellent attention to detail
• Strong influence and communication skills

TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS:
• N/A

PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:
• Regular computer work, and sitting
• Occasional walking, standing, and lifting up to 50lbs

INDEPENDENT JUDGEMENT:
• Develops objectives and general policies and procedures for a specific program or functional area of responsibility within general scope of established operational goals and plans. Day-to-day work and decisions do not require direction or review by immediate supervisor. End results are reviewed by supervisor.

