• Solicits information on enterprise direction, goals and strategies to inform development of Vendor Partner strategies related to Provider Networks and Provider Ancillary Programs.
• Understands key data and financial drivers and dynamics and uses this information to appropriately evaluate Partner expansion opportunities.
• Promotes recommendations for program strategies or enhancements illustrating the link to enterprise and business unit strategies and goals, reflecting awareness of the market context.

Building Relationships
• Establishes and maintains support from both internal and external key stakeholders within and across relevant business units to identify, then achieve, objectives and outcomes.
• Solicits advice, sponsorship and commitment across relevant parts of the organization to enhance the overall support of identified initiatives.
• Builds both formal and informal professional networks among relevant internal and external stakeholders and influencers, in a manner designed to maximize the success of Business Partnership Management.

Communication
• Is effective at conveying the product vision and other messages requiring action, in a way that brings people on board with the vision and builds their enthusiasm about fulfilling it.
• Manages up and down, in the sense of keeping everyone on the same page about what customer problems the Business Product is aiming to solve, what the vision is for how to do that, and where the organization is in executing that vision.
• Communicates business unit and product goals, objectives and priorities in a persuasive manner that builds support, agreement and commitment.
• Works effectively with and through others as a member of one or more teams focused on executing the product strategy.
• Assists with reconciling perspectives on product strategy and priorities into a consensus that all stakeholders can support.

Requirements
