24979,235,Senior Marketing Data Analyst - Now Hiring,"Government Employees Health Association, Inc. - GEHA","Lee's Summit, MO","GEHA (Government Employees Health Association, Inc., pronounced G.E.H.A.) is a nonprofit member association that provides medical and dental benefits to more than two million federal employees and retirees, military retirees and their families. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.

GEHA has one mission: To empower federal workers to be... healthy and well.

Offering one of the largest medical and dental benefit provider networks available to federal employees in the United States, GEHA empowers health and wellness by meeting its members where they are, when they need care. We serve our members with products they value and a personalized customer experience, sustained by a nimble and efficient organization.
GEHA is a leader in health services for federal employees and related customers, serving our chosen markets with low-cost offerings and best-in-class customer care, sustained by a nimble and efficient organization.

Facilitate Collaboration with internal stakeholders to identify opportunities to enhance member experience through GEHA's Provider Networks and Provider Ancillary Programs in alignment with our Vendor Partner strategies.

As part of the ACOE (Analytics Center of Excellence), this analyst with partner exclusively with the Sales and Marketing organization to define, forecast, execute, and measure brand initiatives. Ideally, the right candidate will have substantial experience in test design (A/B testing), evaluating outside factors (environmental, technological, competitive), understanding the impact on potential goals and outcomes, identifying the effects of multiple simultaneous tests and analyze, interpret and report results.

Works with key stakeholders across business and technology domains to develop and convey best testing opportunities with the purpose of learning, determining efficiencies and growth drivers.

Has a broad perspective that informs the business - from both customer insights and business model design - balancing these perspectives consistent with member impact, business profit and loss and/or other internal goals.

Considers enterprise priorities, strategies, goals, emerging technologies, industry trends and economic viability across the relevant Business Partner portfolio.SKILLS

Skills

Outcome-Driven Orientation
• Strong data analytics background. Proactively engages sales and marketing leadership to recommend effective test and implementation across initiatives. Understands the impact of test and learn, can project expect data-based outcomes and scaling opportunities.

Business Acumen and Enterprise Knowledge
• Solicits information on enterprise direction, goals and strategies to inform development of Vendor Partner strategies related to Provider Networks and Provider Ancillary Programs.
• Understands key data and financial drivers and dynamics and uses this information to appropriately evaluate Partner expansion opportunities.
• Promotes recommendations for program strategies or enhancements illustrating the link to enterprise and business unit strategies and goals, reflecting awareness of the market context.

Building Relationships
• Establishes and maintains support from both internal and external key stakeholders within and across relevant business units to identify, then achieve, objectives and outcomes.
• Solicits advice, sponsorship and commitment across relevant parts of the organization to enhance the overall support of identified initiatives.
• Builds both formal and informal professional networks among relevant internal and external stakeholders and influencers, in a manner designed to maximize the success of Business Partnership Management.

Communication
• Is effective at conveying the product vision and other messages requiring action, in a way that brings people on board with the vision and builds their enthusiasm about fulfilling it.
• Manages up and down, in the sense of keeping everyone on the same page about what customer problems the Business Product is aiming to solve, what the vision is for how to do that, and where the organization is in executing that vision.
• Communicates business unit and product goals, objectives and priorities in a persuasive manner that builds support, agreement and commitment.
• Works effectively with and through others as a member of one or more teams focused on executing the product strategy.
• Assists with reconciling perspectives on product strategy and priorities into a consensus that all stakeholders can support.

Requirements
• Bachelor's Degree in relevant area or equivalent work experience.
• Additional years of experience may be considered in lieu of education
• 5 years of relevant work experience with demonstrated product research and analytic evaluation success.
• Ability to lead cross-functional teams and coordinate across multiple teams to achieve common objectives.
• Ability to quickly understand and synthesize business goals and objectives and help stakeholders operationalize the future-state.
• Strong communication skills and the ability to communicate appropriately at all levels of the organization.
• 5 years of experience with SQL.
• Experience with delivering data in at least one visualization tool like PowerBI or Tableau.

Preferred
• Experience within the healthcare industry.
• Demonstrated experience executing with minimal guidance to programs and projects on the direction needed to produce specific business outcomes.

#GEHA

#LI-Remote

Work-at-home requirements
• Must have the ability to provide a non-cellular High Speed Internet Service such as Fiber, DSL, or cable Modems for a home office.
• A minimum standard speed for optimal performance of 30x5 (30mpbs download x 5mpbs upload) is required.
• Latency (ping) response time lower than 80 ms
• Hotspots, satellite and wireless internet service is NOT allowed for this role.
• A dedicated space lacking ongoing interruptions to protect member PHI / HIPAA information

How we value you
• Competitive pay/salary ranges
• Incentive plan
• Health/Vision/Dental benefits effective day one
• 401(k) retirement plan: company match - dollar for dollar up to 4% employee contribution (pretax or Roth options) plus a 6% annual company contribution
• Robust employee well-being program
• Paid Time Off
• Personal Community Enrichment Time
• Company-provided Basic Life and AD&D
• Company-provided Short-Term & Long-Term Disability
• Tuition Assistance Program

Please note that the salary information is a general guideline only. GEHA considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and business considerations when extending an offer.
The annual base salary range for this position is $83,300 - $116,700 USD.

GEHA is an Equal Opportunity Employer, which means we will not discriminate against any individual based on sex, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, age, military status, genetic information, veteran status, pregnancy, marital status, gender identity, and sexual orientation, as well as all other characteristics and qualities protected by federal, state, or local law. GEHA will not discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their compensation or the compensation of another employee or applicant. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. Our diversity drives innovation deepens connections and strengthens our organization.

GEHA is headquartered in Lee's Summit, Missouri, in the Kansas City area. We recognize the importance of balance and flexibility and offer hybrid and work-from-home options for many of our roles.

