25111,367,Electronic Data Interchange (EDI) Analyst,ZELIS,United States,"The EDI Data Analyst is responsible for the overall Electronic Data Interchange (EDI) systems and processing at Zelis Healthcare Inc. The Analyst's role is to develop, coordinate, implement, and communicate the organization's initiatives for EDI systems. The EDI Analyst will act as a liaison between business users, the Application development technical team, and trading partners to deliver... cost-effective, high-quality electronic exchange of information.

Use EDI notepad and other technology tools to review X files for issues, including but not limited to: balancing, structure, syntactical, data type and content errors; then develop and execute strategies to solve them. Troubleshooting activities include querying our database using SQL Management Studio to review stored values and/or using a text editor to manually review data files sent to Zelis by our Payer clients
Support Payer and Provider client implementation activities by generating 835s files, reviewing their content and then presenting your findings to Zelis clients
Respond to inquiries regarding 835 issues, claims, payments, and/or clearinghouse activities
Work closely with other departments on communication issues related to customer and third-party vendor connectivity
Communicate with vendor contacts to identify file issues and then disseminate the resolutions to the provider or payer to maintain compliance with all HIPAA and Zelis data security standards
Understand Zelis Payment products, protocols, systems and processes.
Support multiple client projects simultaneously
Must be proactive to ensure proper follow up and completion of projects.
Must maintain a professional demeanor in sensitive situations.

PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE/QUALIFICATIONS:
Must have Healthcare industry knowledge - preferably provider billing and/or claims payment
Experience writing and executing queries in Microsoft SQL Server Management Studio
Must have high technical aptitude
Have worked on assignments that are complex in nature in which judgment, critical thinking and initiative are required to accomplish the objectives of the assignment
Have successfully completed work tasks with minimal oversight
Have successfully managed and prioritized multiple tasks
Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines.
Must have excellent communication and presentation skills to effectively interface with the Operations staff, and external representatives from the payer and provider communities.

EDUCATION:

4-year college degree or equivalent technology, 835 and/or Healthcare experience

WORK ENVIRONMENT:
Walking, standing and sitting.
Long periods of computer usage.
Handling - seizing, holding, grasping and fingering of objects, tools and controls.
Reaching
Vision - close vision
Office Setting
Moderate noise level.
May be required to work on off hours and weekends

As a leading payments company in healthcare, we guide, price, explain, and pay for care on behalf of insurers and their members. We're Zelis in our pursuit to align the interests of payers, providers, and consumers to deliver a better financial experience and more affordable, transparent care for all. We partner with more than 700 payers, including the top-5 national health plans, BCBS insurers, regional health plans, TPAs and self-insured employers, over 4 million providers, and 100 million members, enabling the healthcare industry to pay for care, with care. Zelis brings adaptive technology, a deeply ingrained service culture, and a comprehensive navigation through adjudication and payment platform to manage the complete payment process.

Job Type: Full-time

Pay: $85,000.00 - $110,000.00 per year

Benefits:
401(k)
Dental insurance
Flexible spending account
Health insurance
Health savings account
Life insurance
Paid time off
Vision insurance
Schedule:
8 hour shift

