26017,1273,Patient Safety Data Analyst,R & K Enterprise Solutions,United States,"Patient Safety Data Analyst (PSDA) JBSA - Lackland-San Antonio, TX R&K Enterprise Solutions, Inc. (R&K) is a certified Service-Disabled Veteran Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) with core capabilities in Mission Support, Engineering and Logistics, Cybersecurity and Intelligence, Environmental and Emergency Management, Exercise and Training, and Defense Healthcare in support of our Defense... Intelligence, and Federal Civilian customers. R&K supports the Defense Health Agency (DHA) and the Chief of Air Force Patient Safety, who has responsibility within the Air Force Medical Service (AFMS) for managing the Air Force (AF) Patient Safety Program (PSP). The DHA PSP is dedicated to providing safe, effective, evidence-based healthcare to beneficiaries. It seeks to develop a healthcare organization where proactive risk identification, data-driven assessment, and reliable processes are the foundation for safe care. R&K supports the DHA PSP by providing expertise and assistance in accomplishing the PSP objectives within DHA, AF Major Commands (MAJCOM) and Military Treatment Facilities (MTF). R&K supports the DHA by providing highly qualified and experienced patient safety professionals at numerous MTFs and by providing training and training materials to foster a workplace-based safety cultural transformation, guided by our experts in patient safety. Title: Patient Safety Data Analyst (PSDA) Location: JBSA Lackland-San Antonio AFB, TX Duration: Permanent/ Full-Time Clearance: Tier 1 (NACI) Investigative Clearance / Background Investigation Start Date: Upon Approval Duties: The PSDA The PSDA duties will include: 1. Work with DHA PSPC to ensure that the AFMS meet its responsibilities as prescribed in AFI 44-119 Chapter 2 and DoD Manual 6025.13 Enclosure 8. This specifically includes support in the development of the MTF’s monthly and annual reports, PRAs and RCAs. 2. Work with MTF PSPC to collect and review all annual appraisals on the adequacy of organization-wide PS activities/policies/procedures ensuring an effective PSP across the AFMS. Assist in development of DHA-level annual AFMS PSP analysis. 3. Collaborate with MTF PSACs on items/issues related to risk identification, risk assessment, and risk control. These functions include, but are not limited to: ECONS, PI, IF, FM, Safety, MLC, MEMO, MERC, IM/IT, Education and Training, Pharmacy and Therapeutics, and Bioenvironmental Engineering. 4. Work with PSPC to ensure all MTF events are reported according to AF and DoD instructions. Contractor personnel shall monitor the reporting process, analyze events, take appropriate action, and consult with DHA risk, credentials and PI managers as appropriate. 5. Collect, collate, analyze, and display data from MTF event reviews, RCAs, PRAs, and other sources to prepare lessons learned to the MTF and AFMS. Disseminate information to appropriate consultants and enlisted and officer SMEs for PS improvement purposes. 6. Serve as expert on the use of analytical tools, e.g. flowcharting, statistical process control, etc., in PS activities. 7. Work with DHA PSPC to develop proactive approaches to enhance and sustain PS by providing best practices to the MTF PSPC, developing creative approaches to control risk, and apply successful safety principles from other agencies. 8. Produce monthly analyses of PSR and/or RCA events, PS trends, and lessons learned. With input from AFMRA SGHQ leadership, staff will produce two (2) 1-2 page analytic summaries for distribution to AFMS MTFs each quarter. Quarterly PS briefs may be included in this total. Staff will also provide analytic summaries and analyses for DHA-led Performance Management Forums, AF/SG driven data queries, and DHA- driven data queries. Requirements: The PSDA candidate shall meet the following qualifications: 1. A Bachelor’s degree in Healthcare Administration (HA), BA, IS, or equivalent degree programs that include training in data analysis and statistical analysis. 2. Four (4) years of experience at a healthcare facility level. 3. Proficient skills in Microsoft suite of tools including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Understanding of Microsoft Access, Visual Basic, and SQL. Experience with relational databases, visual report design tools, quantitative and qualitative data analytics and data manipulation is required. 4. Proficient skills with statistical tools is critical – if not proficient, Contractor should train PSDA on statistical analysis techniques at Contractor expense. 5. The ability to work independently, organize time, and manage multiple projects simultaneously. Attention to detail and the ability to effectively communicate patient safety concepts to leadership and AFMRA staff.. 6. Familiarity with the AAAHC and/or TJC’s accreditation standards, process, PS initiatives and goals as appropriate. 7. Knowledge and experience with RCA and PRA are necessary. If the employee does not have this training, Contractor will have six (6) months to send employee to this training at Contractor expense. 8. Effective writing and presentation skills. 9. Tier 1 (NACI) Investigative background must be obtained and maintained R&K Enterprise Solutions, Inc. is an equal opportunity affirmative action employer committed to cultural diversity and compliance. All qualified women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply for R&K job vacancies. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law",2022-03-12,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['word', 'visual_basic', 'powerpoint', 'sql', 'outlook', 'excel', 'r']"
