26775,2031,"Group Manager, Community and Field Marketing",Imply,"Burlingame, CA","Job Description

At Imply, we are on a mission to help developers become the new heroes of analytics. Our unique database, built from Apache Druid, enables them to develop the next generation of analytics applications. With Imply, developers can build without constraints as our database lets them create interactive data experiences on streaming and batch data with limitless scale and at the best... economics.

Backed by leading investors including a16z and Bessemer Venture Partners, Imply is on a fast growth trajectory - disrupting the $100B database market - with customers including Salesforce, Reddit, and Intercontinental Exchange. Come join our team of disruptors, pioneers, and innovators!

The Role:

The Growth Marketing team at Imply is looking for a highly intelligent and versatile leader to own our Global Field Marketing, Event Marketing, and Community Marketing functions. This is a unique opportunity within the world of enterprise software, as it encompasses both pipeline generation as well as open-source community building. Because of the unique nature of this role, this leader will be part of the Imply marketing leadership team and gain significant visibility to Imply sales and marketing leaders.

A successful candidate will be organized, ambitious and creative, and ultimately able to drive the success of our open-source based business through a wide range of field, event and community marketing activities. The ideal leader will have a strong understanding of open-source and developer-based business models, or the willingness to learn from leaders in the field.

Responsibilities:
• Hire, manage, retain and grow a global team of 3-5 field, event and community marketing managers
• Formulate and execute on a successful Imply presence across key industry, partner, and open-source community events as well as Imply-hosted events
• Have a strong, data-driven mindset around pipeline generation and community building
• Build strong partnership with sales leadership and account executives to understand what is happening in the field and make recommendations to the larger organization
• Build strong partnership with the developer relations team to understand the Apache Druid community and drive the growth and success of the community

Requirements:
• 7-10+ years of B2B field and/or community marketing experience
• Proven experience in building and leading teams
• A strong track record of success, demonstrated through meaningful impact on pipeline and/or community growth
• Strong working knowledge of the marketing technology landscape of B2B and account-targeted platforms and tools
• An understanding, or willingness to learn how to succeed in an open-source and developer-based business

Bonus Points:
• Experience in hyper growth organizations

What we offer:
• 100% Paid Medical, Dental and Vision Benefits
• 401(k) Program
• Fertility Coverage
• Pet Insurance
• Dependent Care FSA
• Mental Health Support
• Life and AD&D Insurance
• Unlimited Paid Time Off - USA Only
• Wellness Stipend
• Home Office Equipment Reimbursement
• Pre-Tax Commuter Benefits

Don't meet every single requirement? Studies have shown that certain minority groups are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every qualification. At Imply, we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace. If you're excited about this role but your past experience doesn't align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or for other roles in the future.

Imply is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, gender identity or expression, marital status, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, race, religion, pregnancy, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances.

Please note, applications and candidate submissions are subject to our privacy policy and, for California residents, the CCPA terms available at https://imply.io/privacy.

—

Attention: Imply Applicants

Due to reports of phishing, we're requesting that all Imply applicants apply through our official Careers page at imply.io/careers. All official communication from Imply will come from email addresses ending with @imply.io",2022-06-14,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
26776,2032,Product Information Management (PIM) Data Analyst,Fluke,Anywhere,"Our vision is to transform the customer experience with industry leading self-service digital tools driven by rich data. We need your help to build and maintain our database and enable best in class solutions with data. You are responsible for executing a structured approach to the collection, creation, and maintenance of master product data in our content management and PIM system supporting the... Business and digital team of Hengstler-Dynapar in the EMEA and US region. You will be a Power User responsible for the integrity of the organization's master product data systems. You will drive data integrity through data governance, change management, data ownership, and quality assurance.

You will be accountable for maintaining and managing the product information in our content management and PIM systems. You will work Business and digital team of Hengstler-Dynapar. to ensure data is available to be consumed by customer facing systems such as online systems including website, ecommerce and site search systems and offline assets such as product datasheets and catalogs. You will also partner with internal subject matter experts such as product management and engineering to understand key attributes for all product types, collect and implement attribute data for all SKUs.

This is a remote role with limited travel

Core Responsibilities:
• Be the Power User and advocate the use of centralized data/PIM platform
• Acquire and maintain product data from multiple data sources. Manages and executes data requests in support of business processes, new product sales initiatives
• Drives excellence and ensures continuous improvement in quality of data through cleansing and best practices for data construction
• Make data available for use in CMS and front-end website systems by partnering with web developers, agencies, and IT
• Reports KPIs related to material master data management and drives a system of actions to complete requests in accordance with Data management process
• Understand, adapt, and improve document management process to enable more efficient data updates and partner with stakeholders to establish standards, governance, and system administration where no processes are in place
• Upload images and product documents into asset management system with all necessary metadata to maintain system search standards
• Create, review, edit, and upload product content/media with a goal of achieving complete and quality data for all product groups
• Works collaboratively as a data steward within teams to ensure clear understanding of business requirements that are managed in concert with PIM data
• Work with regional teams to ensure that data translations are completed within the required timeframe and to a high standard.

Support and train stakeholders and local users on centralized data platform

Requirements:
• Bachelor's degree and at least 2 years of experience in e-commerce or PIM systems with a strong track record in working in ecommerce/digital space. Preference given to previous experience with major PIM solutions such as Akeneo, Salsify or Perfion",2022-03-10,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
26777,2033,Business Sales Data Analyst,Wilbert Funeral Services,"Overland Park, KS","Job Description

Summary...

Supports processes and conducts activities that are vital to the sales leadership team that exceeds the learning and performance needs of the Sales organization.

Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.
• Analytics that support the development of the Sales Revenue Plan (In Total, Sales Group, Customer Data, Product Segmentation, etc…)
• Reporting and analytics that support the development of the Sales OPEX Budget, including Business Plan and Rolling Financial Forecast (RFF) for Revenue & OPEX. Supports the strategic and budgetary processes for the sales organization; develops recommendations for operational budgets as well as sales forecasts by customer segment for sales management. Extensive communication and coordination will be required within all areas of the business
• Implements predictive analytics to forecast sales results, providing management with the information and time required to make any necessary changes.
• Analytics and reporting that supports the Sales Quota Setting Process. Develops recommendations of territory quotas for sales management for review and approval. Ensures the accuracy and integrity of the quota system.
• Support and analytics of the Rep Compensation Processing (commissions, bonus & expense reimbursement) including both goal setting and payment aspects. Ensures the administration of the sales incentive compensation plan as well as reporting changes in compensation costs compared to sales results, and rep behavioral changes impacting compensation to sales management.
• Produces the necessary supporting analytics for the sales management team to evaluate, prioritize and determine the effectiveness of the strategic market and competitive initiatives.
• Producing the monthly Strategy Deployment package. Participate in the monthly policy deployment process by producing the insights discovered through analytics and assembling those insights into a consistent message.
• Support and maintenance of the Sales Call Management System & Sales Reporting process
• Analyze requests through proprietary software. Ability to pull information from various resources, most importantly Syspro, CRM, and other internal database sources.
• Assist in the publication of sales operations policies and procedures.
• Work with sales representatives to identify opportunities for improvement and attend sales meetings where appropriate.
• Other ad-hoc analyses and special assignments as required

Supervisory Responsibilities

This job has no direct reports at this time.

Qualifications

To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions.

Education and/or Experience
• Bachelor's degree (B.A. or B.S.) from a four-year college or university; and a minimum of two to three years of experience in Finance or Accounting; or an equivalent combination of education and experience.

Strategic Skills

Ability to determine opportunities and threats through comprehensive analytics of historical and future trends. Ability to create value through analytics, develop a consistent and flowing message from the insights gained from analytics.

Computer Skills

To perform this job successfully, an individual should have knowledge of Database software; Human Resource systems; Internet software; Spreadsheet software; Microsoft Office (Excel & PowerPoint Focus).

Certificates, Licenses, Registrations

None

Other Skills and Abilities

None

Other Qualifications Preferred

Knowledge of company salespeople, products, and services.

Effectively interact with sales management.

Language Skills

Ability to read and interpret documents such as financial reports, sales data, and market analysis. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence. Ability to speak effectively with groups of customers or employees of the organization.

Mathematical Skills

Ability to calculate figures and amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, circumference, and volume. Ability to apply concepts of basic algebra and geometry.

Reasoning Ability

Ability to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form. Ability to deal with problems involving several concrete variables in standardized situations.

Physical Demands

The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions.

While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand; walk; sit and talk or hear.

Work Environment

The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions.

The noise level in the work environment is moderate.

Primary Competencies

To perform the job successfully, an individual should demonstrate the following competencies:

Analysis/Decision Making - Uses logic and insight to solve difficult problems and create effective solutions; uncovers hidden problems; is excellent at analysis; looks beyond the obvious and seeks the root cause of problems; makes decisions in a timely manner, under tight deadlines and pressure; able to make tough decisions; supports calculated risk-taking; influences others to build support for decisions; includes others (as appropriate) in decision making.

Action/Results Oriented - Achieves high level, sustainable performance and results; is bottom-line oriented; steadfastly pushes self and encourages others to grasp ownership for achieving timely, quality, agreed upon results; is highly energetic; not fearful of acting with less than complete data and planning; seizes opportunities and acts upon them; displays a sense of urgency.

Customer Orientation - Understands and meets the expectations and requirements of internal and external customers; gets first-hand customer information and uses it to meet customers' needs by providing the highest quality products and services; acts with customers in mind; develops effective relationships with customers and gains their trust and respect.

Communication - Presents ideas in a style that is clear, fluent, and to the point; keeps the attention of others; clearly articulates the key points of an issue; takes recipients' perspectives into consideration when communicating; listens to and understands views of others; knows who needs what information and communicates information in a concise, timely and straight forward fashion; not afraid to communicate difficult messages.

Team Player - Supports team efforts; cooperates and works well with others in the pursuit of team goals; builds group cohesiveness by emphasizing team objectives and reinforcing cooperation; creates strong morale in his/her team and across functions; shares win and successes; brings a feeling of participation and belonging to the team.

Adaptability - Effectively responds to change and is comfortable with ambiguity; manages conflicting priorities; comfortably handles risk and uncertainty; learns quickly when facing new problems; open to change; analyzes both successes and failures for clues to improvement; enjoys the challenge of unfamiliar tasks.

DISCLAIMER: The above information on this job description has been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed by the employee within this classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to this job.

