Job Description

This position is responsible for analyzing and transferring various electronic invoicing data into the correct format and internal coding, to enable uploading utilizing the Universal Flex Bill Import Tool. Also responsible for communicating internally and externally on a variety of billing issues regarding electronic data capture for Telecom, Utility and Waste billing, as well as providing support for team projects and technical issues.
Function
• Manages bill payment process for Telecom, Waste and Utility invoices that can go through the UFBI (Universal Flex Bill Import) file import tool, including working with many different types of vendors' proprietary software; to download, extract and manipulate the data for payment/reporting.
• Analyzes invoicing data to categorize charges using Engie Insight's internal coding system.
• Analyzes, researches and resolves complex problems related to electronic invoicing data and file loading.
• Sets up templates in Excel or Access when new data formats arrive, to create efficiencies with the upload process.
• Reviews exception reports that detail problems with invoice data uploads.
• Responsible for tracking the receipt, entry and distribution of the electronic files to ensure that optimal cycle times for bill processing are met.
• Manipulates, analyzes, and interprets large data sets.
• Communicates/collaborates internally and externally on a variety of billing issues.
• Handles increasingly difficult and complex issues.

Do you tick all the boxes?

We are looking for talented and motivated people to create the future of sustainability transition. Join a rewarding and flexible work environment that encourages innovation and creativity and help us meet the energy challenges of today and tomorrow.
• BA/BS in Business Administration/Finance/Mathematics/MIS or Computer Science preferred, or related experience.
• Database experience required.
• Strong analytical and quantitative skills.
