27177,371,"Director, Business Analysis and Insights (Corporate Real Estate...",Walmart,"Bella Vista, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

Are you looking for a great opportunity to join Fortune #1 and play a key role in the development and delivery of the new Home Office campus real estate data strategy? Corporate Affairs is hiring a Director, Corporate Real Estate (CRE) Data and Analytics for who will take ownership of CRE data strategy, architecture, and data product delivery strategy. In this role, you'll work with stakeholders in corporate real estate to understand their needs for key insights and metrics related to the operation and delivery of the new Walmart Home Office campus and corporate real estate portfolio.

You'll Make An Impact By:
• Leading the development of the CRE data and analytics strategy for the new Home Office campus that aligns to, supports, and enables corporate real estate objectives.
• Collaborating with stakeholders in CRE operations and CRE campus experience to confirm and capture business data requirements, reporting objectives, and timelines.
• Contributing to the development comprehensive Corporate Real Estate tech, platform and data strategies that deliver operational and experiential value to the Corporate Real Estate business and to Associates.
• Partnering with key stakeholders inside of Walmart Corporate Real Estate to ensure that CRE data strategy, platforms, and tools align to business requirements and enable business objectives.
• Partnering with Global Tech and other technology stakeholders to maintain alignment with broader Walmart enterprise tech/digital strategy and to implement workplace technology solutions.
• Leading definition of key CRE data requirements and objectives that enable delivery of CRE priorities.
• Contributing to the development of an evolving technology and data strategy that will be a key enabler of individual, team, and organizational activities, inclusive of a roadmap for foundational, enabling, and experiential technologies and tools, including smart building and digital / workplace technologies and standards, building management solutions, reservation systems, workplace apps, sensors, automation, etc.
• Routinely monitoring the adoption and effectiveness of the CRE solutions.

You'll Sweep Us Off Our Feet If:
• You have experience with Corporate Real Estate data sources such as BMS solutions, IWMS platforms, Space Management solutions, and/or Employee/Tenant mobile platforms.
• You have experience leading the planning and development of business data strategy, definition of key reporting capabilities for business metrics and key performance indicators.
• You have experience developing reporting and data driven insights in support of sustainability and energy efficiency goals.
• Experience with Data Analytics or Business Intelligence tools and techniques.
• You have had success operating in highly dynamic environment where guiding policies may not exist.

Minimum Qualifications...

Outlined below are the required minimum qualifications for this position. If none are listed, there are no minimum qualifications.
• Experience building and leading high performing teams
• Experience gathering, identifying, defining, and communicating requirements
• Experience consulting and advising business partners utilizing detailed analysis
• Experience leading data strategy development, data analytics platform or reporting implementation,
• Experience and proven track record delivering successful analytics and insights programs with measurable and significant business impact

Preferred:
Bachelor: Business Administration, Information Systems, Analytics, Computer Science

Specialization: Business Analytics, Data Insights, Business Intelligence, Data Science, Real Estate

Minimum Qualifications...

Outlined below are the required minimum qualifications for this position. If none are listed, there are no minimum qualifications.

Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business, Analytics, Statistics, or related field and 5 years' experience in data analytics, project management, business, or related area OR 7 years' experience in data analytics, project management, business, or related area. 3 years' experience using intermediate functionality of Microsoft Office. 4 years' supervisory experience.

Preferred Qualifications...

Outlined below are the optional preferred qualifications for this position. If none are listed, there are no preferred qualifications.

Consulting, Working on cross-functional teams or projects

Masters: Business

Project Management - Project Management Professional - Certification, Six Sigma - Certification
