27194,388,"Senior Manager I, Business Support - W+ Data Analytics and Reporting",Walmart,"Tontitown, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

About Walmart+

Walmart+ is a membership program that brings together valuable in-store and digital benefits like no other retailer can. With membership benefits like Free store delivery, Free shipping with no order minimum, Mobile scan & go in-store, Rx for less, and Member prices on Fuel, Walmart+ helps our members save time & money.

Specific Responsibilities Include

As a Senior Manager, Data Analytics and Reporting, analyze and ensures accuracy of information by creating, maintaining, and evaluating data; analyzing financial data, key performance indicators, and metrics; evaluating trends and reviewing results for accuracy; utilizing financial models, plans, and tools; and conducting analyses for special and recurring projects.

Collaborating with internal and external business partners to build a consistent and accurate strategy for using data-driven insights; and providing expert advice and guidance on the application of best practices.

What you'll Do

Skills and Experience
• Organize data-driven analysis and insights to help support business strategies by evaluating ongoing analytical needs;
• Serving as the analytics subject matter expert; reporting data-based insights in a uniform manner; monitoring and reporting on business strategies;
• Provide customer service and reporting in area of responsibility by providing reports and communicating results, preparing information and supporting documentation; supporting key business processes; serving as an information resource; providing guidance and recommendations based on defined policies and practices;
• Support relationships with key stakeholders to deliver solutions and support; and resolving issues, answering questions, obtaining information, and providing documentation.
• Provide and supports the implementation of business solutions by building relationships and partnerships with key stakeholders; identifying business needs; determining and carrying out necessary processes and practices; monitoring progress and results; recognizing and capitalizing on improvement opportunities; and adapting to competing demands, organizational changes, and new responsibilities.
• Producing clear and impactful visualizations in support of complex cases
• Provides recommendations to business stakeholders to solve complex business issues through data.
• Interpret data, analyze results and provide ongoing reports on looker.
• Develop and implement Big Query tables and looker reports on GCP.
• Identify, analyze, and interpret trends or patterns in complex data sets.
• Good to have capabilities - like filter and ""clean"" data by reviewing reports and performance indicators to locate and correct code problems
• Work with management to prioritize business and information needs
• Locate and define new process improvement opportunities
• You have experience in tools like Power BI, Tableau, Tableau Prep, BigQuery

Professional Traits
• Working with quickness and urgency
• Having effective verbal and written communications skills.
• Attention to detail
• Making complex and difficult matters simple and easily understood
• Multitasking and using good judgment in prioritization of tasks
• You're someone who can execute, with strong discipline and organization skills; someone who gets things done
• You have strong analytical skills to interpret insights coming from various initiatives and have a mindset for continuous learning and improvement.
• Proven working experience as a data analyst or business data analyst
• Technical expertise regarding data models, database design development, data mining and segmentation techniques
• Strong knowledge of and experience with reporting packages (Business Objects etc), databases (SQL etc), programming (ETL frameworks)
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy
• Adept at queries, report writing and presenting findings

