27195,389,"Manager II, Business Intelligence and Reporting - Pricing",Walmart,"Gravette, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

Every Day Low Prices (EDLP) is the cornerstone of our business and our focus on prices has never been stronger. We are looking for an entrepreneurial problem solver who enjoys sourcing and executing solutions. Be a part of an innovative team that is developing pricing strategies, building industry analytics and implement their recommendations at a scale that only Walmart can.

What You'll be doing: Focus on improving Walmart's leadership position in Pricing by delivering actionable insights across your business unit.
• Apply Business Acumen: Ability to disaggregate and translate complex business issues into actionable projects. Take initiative to identify and solve problems while comfortable providing recommendations to your cross functional partners.
• Execute Strategic Pricing Initiatives: Execute pricing strategies designed by you and your team based on deep understanding of how pricing is connected to the business goals and what competitive pressures are affecting the market.
• Collaborate with Merchants: Partner with the business functions, creating actionable insights for merchants and buyers, based off your industry expertise, pricing strategies and data tests.
• Data Source Identification: Proactively explore datasets, representing your industry group, and working with cross functional product teams to identify and test the suitable sources of data.
• Data Processing & Quality Management: Uses tools such as SQL Server, Teradata, Google Cloud Platform, Tableau, and Alteryx to wrangle data as needed. Test and validate data quality and applicability to the business.
• Data Visualization & Storytelling: Generate appropriate graphical representations of data. Seeks constant improvement and education around how merchants perceive data and use it to make decisions.
• Excellent People Skills: Ability to cultivate relationships up, down and across the organizational chain. Collaborate with both internal and external teams to achieve company goals. Demonstrate quick and effective problem-solving skills, and strong work ethics.
• Develop retail pricing strategies of low to moderate complexity based on volume, product lines, competition, or category penetration for assigned categories
• Utilize Walmart pricing systems to develop, improve, or modify strategy to maximize profit margin; ensuring strategies meet category and company objectives; and recommending promotion pricing strategies.
• Provides supervision and development opportunities for associates by training, mentoring, assigning duties, and providing recognition.

The above information has been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed in the role. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities and qualifications required of employees assigned to this job. The full Job Description can be made available as part of the hiring process.

Minimum Qualifications
• Bachelor's Degree in the fields of Economics, Accounting, Finance, Business, Marketing, or related friend AND 2 years' experience in Merchandising, Retail Pricing, Sourcing, Operations Management, Finance, Marketing or related area
• OR 4 years' experience in Merchandising, Retail Pricing, Operations Management, Finance, Marketing, or related area.

Preferred Qualifications:
• Experience in data analysis, statistics, or a related field
• Entrepreneurial spirit - must be a self-starter with an innovative mindset
• Excellent problem-solving skills including the ability to structure a problem, disaggregate issues, identify root causes and recommend solutions
• Ability to accomplish work in a fast-paced and dynamic work environment
• Excellent with Microsoft Office Suites (e.g. Word, Excel, PowerPoint)
• Solid understanding of financial, economic and general business concepts and terminology
• Excellent written and verbal Communication and cross functional relationship management Skills
• Professional attitude, team player, work standards and service orientation
• Understanding of SQL, Python, R, or Alteryx languages

