27348,542,Data Analyst III,Walmart,"Hayward, CA","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

About the Team

As a part of the Walmart Last Mile Delivery organization, you will contribute to the success of our Transportation Network! Why? Because Sam Walton founded our company with the belief that the customer is #1. It is not just a belief, but our way of doing business. With our Last Mile Delivery Team at the forefront of retail transformation you can work on a team that is ultimately focused on delighting our customers, saving them both time and money in unexpected ways. As the biggest player in the game, we trust our associates to innovate the future of Last Mile Delivery!

The Forecasting and Analytics team within the Last Mile Delivery organization mainly focuses on collaborating with various teams and analyzing data from various disparate sources to provide guidance on the future state and for solving complex business problems. You will manage complex data, collaborate with various teams, and work with operational and cross-functional partners to translate high level business strategy into estimates which will guide both strategic/tactical planning and daily operations.

If you are motivated by complex, purposeful challenges, this role, with the world's largest retailer, could be the fit you have been looking for. Do you possess any of the following skills and experience?
• Supply Chain or eCommerce domain knowledge
• Collaborative analytics and project management to improve business operations
• Data processing and data quality validation to ensure the best possible data inputs are driving systemic solutions, experience in SQL, advanced Excel and Tableau
• Experience in cross-functional and ambiguous situations

You'll make an impact through the following job functions:
• Forecasting - Develop and improve detailed forecasting frameworks to guide decision making and daily operations. Communicate, collaborate and align with various internal and external teams to improve the frameworks
• Prescriptive Data Analytics: Perform in-depth and detailed data analytics on large, complex, disparate datasets to investigate business problems, distill the complex analytics into easily understandable data visualizations to facilitate critical decision making and prescribe/recommend optimal actions
• Continuous Improvement: Continuously improve processes by utilizing the best practices in data analytics and standardizing the data inputs, processing, validation and visualization
• Cross Functional Collaboration: Build strong relationship with various teams and cross functional partners by constant-effective communication, understanding their business problems and requirements in detail and recommending/implementing optimal solutions
• Modeling: Develop and improve existing models. Continuously improve the modeling frameworks by mirroring the real world through assumptions and approximations but balance the speed to solution as well

About You
• You understand transportation or supply chain, whether in Retail ecommerce environment or similar industries
• You are a problem solver and creative thinker: you think about finding the best solution that will work in days, instead of the perfect one that requires weeks.
• You learn and adapt quickly, and are excellent at working on multiple cross-functional projects concurrently
• You have excellent general modeling and data processing skills.
• You are customer-centric in spirit and in execution.
• You work well with ambiguity
• You have strong technical skills in data analytics and visualization- SQL, advanced Excel, Tableau, Power BI etc.; Preferred- Knowledge and skills in any programming languages to automate data analysis

