27354,548,"Analyst II, Business Analysis And Insights - Tableau, SQL, Excel",Walmart,"Farmington, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

Who we are...

The Walmart Facility Services is employing skilled technicians, local to Walmart stores nationwide, to manage the property maintenance needs and serve as a point of contact to store retail staff. Third party contract vendors are additionally aligned as a supplement for work that cannot be performed by the local technician. Every year approximate 2.5 million work orders are created, over 800 capital projects completed, and a financial plan of 5 billion dollars is managed.

What you'll do...

Assist a large regional field team to review and react to facilities maintenance work orders in a timely manner. The team is working to improve store satisfaction through work order self-performance, quick response time, and prompt total work order completion. This role is primarily administrative and will require an organized and detail oriented individual. Project management, data handling, and written email communication is a daily function. This individual will work alongside a few peers who have the same function but supporting different geographical territories.

Responsibilities Include...
• Collaborate directly with project stakeholders (product, design, engineering, business) to develop and drive Infrastructure services overall goals
• Define frameworks and execute program roadmaps and schedules for multiple workstreams
• Identify and manage critical path workflows and cross-functional dependencies; collect and analyze project metrics to manage initiatives and drive accountability; identify and resolve bottlenecks
• Escalate and communicate program related issues to mitigate risks
• Own and drive stakeholder engagement for quarterly business planning process, KPI definition, executive updates, and agile practices
• Evaluate the effectiveness of assigned programs and initiatives to improve efficiency and cost-effectiveness with participating stakeholders
• Support development of executive level presentations and perspectives

You will sweep us off our feet if you...
• You are detail oriented, driven, and responsible
• You have a sense of curiosity and ownership to processes and projects
• You are proficient with Excel pivot tables and basic functions like v-lookup and if statements.
• Adapt quickly with a demonstrated ability to prioritize work and flex where needed
• Build trust based, strong relationships with internal and external partners

Benefits & Perks:

Beyond competitive pay, you can receive incentive awards for your performance. Other great perks include 401(k) match, stock purchase plan, paid maternity and parental leave, PTO, multiple health plans, and much more.

