27822,1016,"Senior Paralegal III, Tech & Data Regulatory",Walmart,"Bella Vista, AR","Position Summary...

What you'll do...

Imagine a position that combines your skills as a paralegal with your love of technology. Imagine an opportunity that positions you as a trusted partner to attorneys who work at the world's largest retailer. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment and enjoy solving problems and working collaboratively toward a solution, you'll find that being a part of our Legal division is a move that brings with it tremendous growth potential and exciting new challenges.

Join the Tech and Data Regulatory Team within Digital Citizenship as a Senior Paralegal III, Tech and Data Regulatory. In this role, you will provide paralegal support to the attorneys who are responsible for counselling leading-edge technology matters that power Walmart's global business, which serves as a center of subject matter expertise on data privacy and information security issues. In fulfilling your duties, you will partner cross-functionally with key stakeholders both within and outside of Digital Citizenship, keeping the ethical use of data and responsible use of technology at the forefront of your work.

You'll make an impact by:
• Providing support for team projects, including helping attorneys to develop, operationalize, and update standard operating procedures, policies, best practices, and trainings.
• Liaising with other members of Digital Citizenship and Walmart business teams on legal matters.
• Drafting, proofreading, and updating team presentations, policies, and templates.
• Assisting with outside counsel management, including the opening/closing of outside counsel matters and reporting.
• Assisting with team budget and annual planning submissions.
• Helping attorneys with caseload management, including the assignment of matters to team members, maintaining executed copies of contracts, and migrating historical contracts to approved document management systems.

You'll sweep us off our feet if...
• You have experience as a paralegal supporting the work of attorneys either in-house or at a law firm.
• You are comfortable with technology and the world of online retail commerce.
• You have some knowledge of data privacy and information security issues.
• You are familiar with outside counsel management systems (Passport) and with contract management tools (Ariba, Coupa).
• You are organized, detail-oriented, and calm under pressure
• You are process-minded and look for opportunities to streamline for improved efficiency and effectiveness
• You have strong communication skills to interact with senior leadership and stakeholders.
• You have experience working with cross-functional teams

Preferred Location: Bentonville, AR.

Dallas, TX; Hoboken, NJ; Sunnyvale, CA will also be considered.

The above information has been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed in the role. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities and qualifications required of employees assigned to this job. The full Job Description can be made available as part of the hiring process.

Benefits & Perks: Beyond competitive pay, you can receive incentive awards for your performance. Other great perks include 401(k) match, stock purchase plan, paid maternity and parental leave, PTO, multiple health plans, and much more.

Equal Opportunity Employer: Walmart, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer - By Choice. We believe we are best equipped to help our associates, customers and the communities we serve live better when we really know them. That means understanding, respecting and valuing diversity- unique styles, experiences, identities, ideas and opinions - while being inclusive of all people.

Who We Are Join: Walmart and your work could help over 275 million global customers live better every week. Yes, we are the Fortune #1 company. But you'll quickly find we're a company who wants you to feel comfortable bringing your whole self to work. A career at Walmart is where the world's most complex challenges meet a kinder way of life. Our mission spreads far beyond the walls of our stores. Join us and you'll discover why we are a world leader in diversity and inclusion, sustainability, and community involvement. From day one, you'll be empowered and equipped to do the best work of your life. careers.walmart.com

