27932,1126,"Senior Data Analyst, Incentive Compensation",Mariner Wealth Advisors,"Overland Park, KS","As a key member of the Incentive Compensation team, the Senior Data Analyst, Incentive Compensation will be a leading contributor to the execution of the firm's variable compensation plans, policies and processes. With broad system and top data tool access, they will be responsible for managing and helping to refine processes around data sourcing, calculation, validation and reporting. Candidates... with deep attention to detail, ability to problem-solve and have an enjoyment of process-oriented tasks and projects which optimize operations will thrive in this role.

If you are looking to build your career with a firm that puts the client first by providing 360° advice designed to last, then Mariner Wealth Advisors is the right firm for you. We actively nurture the next generation of professionals, give back to the community and focus on building a diverse culture where everyone genuinely loves where they work and has the support needed to meet their career goals.
• Ownership of quarterly and ad hoc calculation processes from sourcing large volumes of data across multiple CRM and billing platforms to the calculation and validation of results utilizing best-of-breed data tools and techniques (30%)
• Requires validation of data formatting, rule compliance and verifying payee licensing and eligibility requirements
• Responsible for reporting and data visualization, including sales tracking and complex calculation of compensation payments; recurring and an hoc leadership data analysis (10%)
• Build relationships and engage with the field while distributing compensation reporting, responding to payee and manager inquiries regarding compensation eligibility, calculations and trend analysis (10%)
• Partner with other HQ departments to ensure data quality, identifying process improvement opportunities (20%)
• Own the administration of compensation software and troubleshooting, ensure excellence in data integrity and quality (10%)
• Deliver training and education on compensation plans and user software to provide understanding and clarity to payees and managers (5%)
• Manage the process for requested updates to assign and credit sales and service commissions to payees using Salesforce CRM software (10%)
• Thoroughly document plans and processes (5%)
• Bachelor’s degree in business, math/accountancy, or data science fields of study, preferred

Skills & Knowledge
• 3+ years similar experience as a data or financial analyst
• Administration of variable compensation plans in a service industry, a plus
• Understanding of revenue sources, financial reporting, and analysis
• Client First mentality; service-oriented
• Deep analytical skills
• Attention to detail and conscientious about accuracy
• Strong communication and interpersonal skills with ability to engage in discussions with individuals regarding their compensation
• Experience with technical writing/process documentation, preferred
• Critical thinking and resourceful problem-solving abilities
• Advanced MS Excel capabilities
• Experience with compensation/commission systems/technology, such as Xactly, preferred
• Experience with data ETL and visualization tools, such as Alteryx and Tableau, preferred
• Basic understanding of programming languages or ability to learn, such as SQL, a plus
• High aptitude to leverage technology solutions and applications

We welcome your interest in being a part of the Mariner Wealth Advisors team. We offer associates an innovative and challenging place to work with camaraderie and teamwork. We have a growth-oriented, entrepreneurial culture that respects people and values talent, experience and ambition.

