27959,1153,"Business Analyst, Senior - Data Analytics: 100% Remote US",Varis,"Kansas City, MO","This is a 100% fully remote role. Work virtually from anywhere in the Continental U.S.

Varis is a well-funded and fast-growing technology startup that focuses on digital commerce software-as-a-service and procurement and is owned by The ODP Corporation (NASDAQ: ODP). We are innovation driven, customer centric, and ready to transform eProcurement and business-to-business (B2B) Marketplaces. Our... culture is focused on a bold vision, launching the simplest (yet still valuable) solutions to learn, then either failing or scaling fast as we iterate towards our product goals.

Joining us now is a ground-floor opportunity to shape our limitless future. You will see and feel the direct impact of your work, be surrounded by passionate people, learn how to be an entrepreneur, and be at the center of a highly dynamic business model with tremendous individual and collective potential.

Apply quickly by emailing your resume here: data_business_analyst__8c2d867b5us@iris.greenhouse.io

What You'll Do
• We are looking for a Senior Business Analyst for our Business Planning and Strategy team. As a Senior Business Analyst, you will work closely with Product Managers, Program Managers, Business Operation Managers, and Software Developers to generate actionable insights that guide operational excellence and product development.
• Your work will have a direct impact on decision-making and strategy for our team. You will support this initiative by developing business metrics and reports, analyzing current processes to provide solutions for improvements, and helping executive leaders make key business decisions.
• The successful candidate will communicate effectively across teams and levels while balancing the needs and requirements of internal and external customers. We seek an individual who is motivated by a fast-paced and highly entrepreneurial environment.

Key Responsibilities:
• Own the design, development, and maintenance of ongoing and ad-hoc metrics, reports, and analyses, that drive key business decisions
• Gather and analyze data for potential business expansion
• Prepare and present results of analysis and reports along with their relative impact(s) to the business to all levels of management.
• Create reports, dashboards, and visualizations with business intelligence tools (excel, visualization tools, and SQL), to understand business performance
• Participate in strategic & tactical planning discussions
• Coordinate with different departmental teams to produce better business outcomes
• Collaborate with the product manager on roadmap planning and prioritization

What You'll Need
• Bachelor's degree in Business, Engineering, Statistics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Supply Chain or a related field
• 7+ years in corporate operations.
• 3+ years of relevant experience in a business analyst/data analyst/statistical analyst role.
• 2+ years of experience with business metrics reporting for corporate functions like finance/sales etc.
• Experience in supporting C-level is a big bonus.
• Excel modeling.
• Experience in developing requirements and formulating business metrics for reporting, familiarity with data visualization tools like PowerBI and Tableau.
• SQL proficiency, can write basic SQL queries
• Knowledge of DAX is desirable
• Excellent communication (verbal and written) and interpersonal skills with both technical and business audiences.
• Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, prioritization, planning, and task delegation.
• Strong critical thinking and problem-solving.
• Ability to display complex data in a simple, intuitive format and to present findings in a clear and concise manner
• Ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with Sales, Finance and Executive teams
• Domain knowledge of eCommerce/indirect procurement/Saas is desirable
• Proven ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment.

The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by associates assigned to this classification and are not intended to be a complete list of all required responsibilities and skills. Other duties and special projects may be assigned per business needs. Job descriptions are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Varis is wholly owned by The ODP Corporation, which is the legal employer of Varis associates. ODP is an Equal Opportunity Employer.

Benefits and Perks:
• 100% permanent remote work in the United States
• Medical / dental / vision, AD&D, and Life Insurance
• Paid Time Offer (PTO) and company paid holidays
• Health Saving Account (HSA)
• Long Term Disability and Short-Term Disability
• 401(k) matching program
• Discounted auto, home, and pet insurance
• Retirement savings plan rollovers
• Banking services
• Military leave
• Employee Assistance Program (EAP)
• Regular pay for funeral/memorial service observance
• Discounts on Office Depot/Microsoft/Apple products and services
• Opportunity for professional growth and career advancement

Varis is wholly owned by The ODP Corporation, which is the legal employer of Varis associates.

The ODP Corporation is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities in all employment practices. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, citizenship status, marital status, age, disability, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by law. We will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records in alignment with the City & County of San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance",2022-01-08,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'dax', 'power_bi', 'sql', 'excel']"
27964,1158,Program Management Data Analyst,Citi,United States,"The Institutional Clients Group (ICG) Operations and Technology Organizational Program Management Office (OPMO), has visibility into the full book of work across ICG O&T. The ICG O&T book of work has more 5,000+ programs and projects that are executed on an annual basis driving Citi's Mission to Be the Best for Our Clients. The OPMO works across all the ICG O&T lines of business to ensure the... book of work is executed in an efficient, effective, and controlled manner. The team is responsible for a wide range of activities including but not limited to Governance, Program Management & Oversight, PM related Training and Reporting - all done in partnership with the ICG O&T lines of business. The ICG O&T OPMO has an opening for a Program Management Analyst. The candidate will be part of the Health Check function within the ICG O&T OPMO.

The Health Check is a PMO best practice developed by ICG O&T. It is a proactive control process and a critical service of the OPMO that is provided to ICG O&T's most critical strategic and safety and soundness programs. The purpose of the Health Check is to have an independent assessment of how well active program and project work efforts are performing. The candidate will be responsible for executing the Health Check program reviews, identifying, and tracking opportunities for improvement resulting from the Health Check, issuing a Health Check Report that proactively and impartially illustrates the well-being of the program, discussing results with the PM and offering guidance as needed, and monitoring all required remediation actions through completion. The role will partner heavily with Program and Project Managers across all levels of management as well as with the larger OPMO team and senior management. The role also brings opportunities to work on special projects and process improvements across the OPMO. The role will also require knowledge of Program and Project Management fundamentals and understanding of the SDLC and technology methodologies such as Waterfall and Agile.

This position provides a platform for continued development and visibility across a global organization as well as exposure to management and other functions.

Key Responsibilities:
• Perform independent Health Check Assessments of ICG Technology & Operations Programs, to meet Annual PMO Health Check Assessment/Review Targets.
• Execute the Health Check process against established criteria and recommend solutions for improvement.
• Analyze Health Check criteria element data to grasp issues, draw conclusions, and identify trends/patterns to properly assess the well-being of ICG Technology & Operations programs.
• Create Health Check Reports that proactively and impartially illustrates the well-being of programs.
• Monitor all required remediation actions for ICG Technology & Operations programs through completion.
• Assist with Health Check Program & Project Tracker updates and Health Check Analysis Template changes/enhancements (including Requirement Documentation, design & testing).
• Help with Health Check Scoping Process (including maintenance & updates to Scoping Database, Macros and Pivot tables).
• Support Health Check Metrics generation & results communication (including maintenance & update of Health Check Metrics Macros & Pivot tables).
• Take an active role in the continuous improvement of the ICG O&T Health Check processes and assist with design & implementation of process efficiencies & automations within the Health Check function.
• Support the transition of Health Check processes to SAS platform (including requirements Analysis/documentation, solution design & testing).
• Support other ICG O&T OPMO functions and special projects (as needed), including support of PQA/Spot Check Reviews on Monthly/Quarterly basis.
• Develop a thorough understanding of the ICG O&T Program and Project Management Procedure as well other PM guidelines.
• Drive PM adherence to standards, guidelines, and project management best practices.
• Actively engage and maintain robust collaboration with Program and Project Managers across multiple lines of business and support them with any ad hoc PM related queries.
• Interface with the broader ICG O&T OPMO team on PM Framework topics.
• Support any PMO audit or regulatory queries, as needed.

Qualifications:
• Bachelor's/University degree or equivalent experience.
• 5+ years of work experience in PM or PMO role with proven success in project execution
• Good understanding of Project Management Concepts with knowledge of Waterfall and Agile technology methodologies.
• Ability to analyze data and grasp issues, draw conclusions, and identify trends.
• Attention to detail to ensure precision of data and overall quality of outputs.
• Strong communication skills in English.
• Strong written skills in English.
• Strong organizational skills.
• Strong interpersonal skills to maintain effective, mutually beneficial relationships with members of the ICG O&T Program and Project Management community.
• Ability to support multiple work streams, work under tight deadlines and shift from one task to another on short notice as priorities change.
• Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and SharePoint.
• Prefer strong skills working with MS Excel PivotTables & Macros and ability to learn new tech tools.

