27979,1173,Data Analyst 2,Humana,"Tulsa, OK","Description

Do you seek to truly understand complex problems and how to solve them with data? Do you love the idea of taking raw data, turning it into compelling insights, and using the results to make informed decisions? By joining our team, you'll be a part of a group of analysts that are focused on delivering robust solutions to our business partners, and who play a key role in uncovering... hidden insights within huge amounts of data.

Responsibilities

As part of the Pharmacy Analytics and Consulting team, you will leverage complex data to support modeling and process improvements by using business expertise and analytics. These actionable insights will support our internal partners to drive business strategy and decisions.

Additional responsibilities will include leveraging knowledge of data, applying analytical methodologies, and collaborating and communicating complex results with clinical partners while following established guidelines/ procedures. You will be expected to exercise considerable latitude in determining objectives and approaches to solving challenges within both new and evolving assignments, making decisions on moderately complex to complex issues and regularly working without direct guidance.

Required Qualifications:
• Bachelor's degree, preferably in quantitative field
• 1-3 years of data analysis experience or relevant coursework
• Experience with statistical methodologies, exploratory data analysis, and using data to drive business outcomes, strategy, and decisions
• Programming/ Coding Experience (Python, SAS, R, and SQL)
• Knowledge of Microsoft Office applications
• Consultative problem-solving experience
• Excellent written and verbal communication
Preferred Qualifications:
• Masters or PhD in quantitative field
• Data visualization platforms such as PowerBI, QlikView, Tableau, or similar tools.
Additional Information

Scheduled Weekly Hours

40

Humana complies with all applicable federal civil rights laws and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or religion. We also provide free language interpreter services. See our",2022-02-28,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sas', 'sql', 'power_bi', 'r', 'python']"
27983,1177,Business Analyst/Healthcare Data Analyst,Alakaina Foundation Family of Companies,United States,"The Alaka ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) is looking for a Business Analyst/Healthcare Data Analyst to support the Defense Health Agency. Preferred locations are San Antonio or TX, Falls Church, VA, however this position can be remote as well.

Alaka ina has partnered with the Defense Health Agency (DHA) to deliver world class, data-driven decision science analytics of military... healthcare operations and the delivery of healthcare services worldwide. Alaka ina and its partners will lead with way for DHA to expand its current analytical services to incorporate leading-edge technologies and advanced skills.

Successful candidates will have an extensive background in the Military Healthcare System, in-depth knowledge of the Military Healthcare data marts, experience developing healthcare delivery standards, and analyzing operations at both the headquarters and military treatment facility levels.

JOB DESCRIPTION:

Access, validate and analyze information about the MHS population by developing, validating, and linking various medical, safety, environmental, occupational and personnel databases.
Aggregate and analyze population health data to respond to questions from the various Congressional inquiries, DoD senior leaders, Service-specific Headquarters agencies, and the MTFs.
Coordinate and attend meetings for Service and Enterprise/Tri-Services groups and record/report/ communicate back to Government leadership items of discussion especially relevant to Analytics.
Collaborate with DHA and other applicable agencies to link program data with other health and personnel data to support a longitudinal database.
Conduct financial on Business Case Analysis (BCA) associated with government programs.
Conduct research and perform analysis (including development/use of predictive models for improving clinical operations and evaluating clinical currency, efficiency, and productivity) to support a variety of clinic practices initiatives focused on improvement of clinical operations.
Coordinate and arrange for program data transfer from DHA, MCSCs, MTFs, and other users of various programs.
Identify, troubleshoot, and conduct data import, analysis, and display errors from multiple data sources.
Provide analytical support regarding the integration, access, and development of data to support the documentation, comparative analysis, and outcomes analysis necessary to demonstrate the efficacy of clinical pathways designed and implemented in the MTFs.
Provide data analysis and decision support using research expertise as well as literature review/evidence-base to develop clinical and business measures and prototypes of health information technology (IT) tools, programs, procedures, services, or databases to support DHA's goal of building a managed healthcare system that considers and optimizes safety, quality, cost, and access.
Provide technical expertise in the areas of prevention, managed care, medical readiness issues, health promotion, clinical safety and quality, and other health Service-related issues in order to support the DHA's vision of becoming the healthiest and highest performing segment of the US.
Research, develop, analyze, monitor, and report annual Performance Plans.
Research, identify and apply, when available, national/standardized benchmarks and thresholds to DHA/MHS metrics as appropriate or the Contractor shall identify reasons why the established benchmarks/thresholds/methods are not appropriate/relevant.
Support the Government as the lead clinical and business information resource in the documentation, plan, design, build, implementation, and maintenance of clinical and business information systems for the DHA and its internal/external customers.

REQUIRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:

Demonstrated knowledge of CHCS and/or M2 file and MHS data table structures; Minimum of 3 years' experience data mining and conducting detailed analysis within the Military Health System (MHS) Data Warehouses.
Expert level skills in SQL or SAS.
Demonstrated knowledge of internal MTF processes related to the execution of health care, e.g., admissions/dispositions process, patient scheduling and appointing, financial reimbursements through Third Party Collections, and outpatient and inpatient throughput.
Demonstrated knowledge of medical coding practices and processes (ICD-9/10 and CPT/HCPS).
Five (5) years of technical experience in data presentation software and concepts associated with presentation of quantitative information.
Five (5) years demonstrated ability conducting thorough and comprehensive system-wide business case and return on investment (ROI) analysis for healthcare operations within the DHA, MHS, Veterans Administration (VA) or private sector.
Five (5) years of experience in communicating and writing complex concepts and their effects/impacts on the target environment, such that a lay audience is capable of understanding.
Five (5) years of experience using MHS Medical Expense and Performance Reporting System (MEPRS) / Defense Medical Human Resources System Internet (DMHRSi), Manpower, Program Objective Memorandum (POM) processes, Finance, and Referral Management/Access to Care.
Five (5) years of experience with integration of performance planning goals to meet the objectives of the DHA.
Proven ability to identify and implement solutions to improve data quality (medical coding, MEPRS usage).
Three (3) years' experience working in a leadership role within Resource Management, Group Practice Management, or TRICARE Operations.
Ability to acquire skills/capabilities necessary to meet growing needs/demands of systems/software/hardware.
Ability to critically examine and evaluate, problem-solve.
Ability to deliver products on time, on schedule, within budget. Flexibility and ability to adapt to rapidly changing and often time-constrained environment.
Able to read, write, speak, and understand English.
Demonstrated ability to communicate analytical discoveries and appropriate recommendations/mitigation strategies effectively and clearly to all levels of customers including Senior DHA leadership.
Demonstrated ability to organize/participate/lead working groups to develop analytic products and byproducts or to develop/understand processes leading to effective optimization of analytic efforts.
Demonstrated ability to provide accurate and timely analytical products containing well-reasoned and cogent discussion points providing leadership with substantiated options or courses of action.
Demonstrated ability to undertake and complete multiple tasks with multiple deadlines simultaneously.
Demonstrated advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office products PLUS additional software/hardware skills and capabilities.
Proven ability to synthesize disparate data from multiple sources and coalesce into an accurate and useful analytic product, incorporating Service and MHS strategic goals for use by leadership in both tactical and strategic decision making.

DESIRED SKILLS:

Minimum of 10 years' experience within the Military Health System (MHS)

DEGREE/EDUCATION/CERTIFICATION REQUIREMENT:

Master's Degree in Healthcare or Business Administration, Economics, Accounting, Management, or 8 years of equivalent health care work experience.

CITIZENSHIP/SECURITY CLEARANCE REQUIREMENTS:

Tier I background check or National Agency Check with Inquiries (NACI) Equivalent
U.S. Citizenship Required

The Alaka ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) is a fast-growing government service provider. Employees enjoy competitive salaries; a 401K plan with company match; medical, dental, disability, and life insurance coverage; tuition reimbursement; paid time off; and 11 paid holidays.

We are an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. We are proud to state that we do not discriminate in employment decisions on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, or disability status. If you are a person with a disability and you need an accommodation during the application process, please click here to request accommodation. We E-Verify all employees.

The Alaka ina Foundation Family of Companies (FOCs) is comprised of industry-recognized government service firms designated as Native Hawaiian Organization (NHO)-owned and 8(a) certified businesses. The Family of Companies (FOCs) includes Ke aki Technologies, Laulima Government Solutions, Kūpono Government Services, and Kāpili Services, Po okela Solutions, Kīkaha Solutions, LLC, and Pololei Solutions, LLC. Alaka ina Foundation activities principally benefit the youth of Hawaii through charitable efforts which includes providing innovative educational programs that combine leadership, science & technology, and environmental stewardship.

For additional information, please visit",2022-06-06,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sql', 'sas']"
