28062,1256,Business Intelligence Analyst NOT REMOTE,Security Service Federal Credit Union,United States,"What You Will Do:

Supports the design, implementation, operation, and maintenance of data and analytical pipelines for the Payment Services operational, executive, and control/monitoring dashboards. Monitors, tracks, and reports on Payment Services organizational statistics, including daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly and yearly KPIs. Applies data mining and statistical methods on data sets to... extract actionable insights. Creates easy to understand visualizations to communicate information extracted from data to support all departments operational requirements in Payment Services. Performs ad-hoc data analysis per business user's request. Understands and maintains multiple data sources and streamlines the reporting process. Produces and distributes a variety of dashboards and other reports to payment services leadership and executive teams which reflect current and historical volume. Identify opportunities to create and enhance the reporting of the control and monitoring process dashboards and efficiency measures. Develop tracking tools, enhance spreadsheet and database functionality. Creates forms, templates, logic functions and macros in support of the data collection efforts to capture operational data points from all back-office teams in Payment Services. Helps develop, gather, and document basic technical data for the departments reporting processes. Communicates critical information to internal and external customers in compliance with clearly defined requirements. Provide analytical and research support for company projects and objectives as directed by management. Research, develop, and implement a coordinated data and reporting strategy to ensure regulatory adherence for the Payment Services Departments internal and external control monitoring process. Implements controls and monitoring processes to identify risks and issues within workflows and conducts periodic auditing of all Payment Services workflows and update accordingly. Establish, develops and maintains departmental policy and procedures documents for controls and monitoring. Completes any other job-related duties needed to help drive to our Vision, fulfill our Purpose, and abide by our Organization's Values.

Our Core Values:

All employees should demonstrate our SSFCU core values -- Caring, Innovative, Honest, Fair and Dedicated -- while providing enthusiastic, professional, and courteous service to SSFCU members and employees.

Additional Information:

We are an EEO Employer that provides equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, color, age, religion, protected veteran or disability status, or genetic information.

What We Require:

Bachelor's degree in business administration, finance, accounting, economics, computer science or equivalent education and/or experience. Minimum of five (5) years in the financial services industry. Must be experienced and proficient in Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Visio, Access and VBA. Demonstrate working knowledge of pivot tables, string functions, lookups, macro development, and code development in VBA. Experience in participating in multiple projects and ability to work with minimal supervision showing creativity, innovation, motivation, initiative and professionalism. Experience compiling large volumes of data into usable formats. Excellent time management and organizational skills. Experience with Data Analysis and Visualization of Power BI Dashboards. Experience with data integration of Power BI with external data sets and systems. Strong SQL Skills (complex queries on relational databases, stored procedures, automation)

Ideal Candidate Will Have:

Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills. Knowledge of federal regulations including but not limited to Regulations E, Z, CC, J, AA, UCC article 4, NACHA rules/regulations as well as Monarch experience and use of Fidelity applications. Outstanding leadership, teamwork, inter-personal, facilitation, organizational, process, listening and communication skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines. Ability to utilize business process, data management and information systems skills to create, design and implement tools that improve workforce effectiveness and management decision making. Exceptional knowledge of Advanced Excel and VBA Macros. Expert understanding of Power BI, or Tableau. Ability to write and execute data analysis expressions, queries and functions in Power BI. Advanced knowledge of databases, statistics, and data mining.

Who We Are:

Security Service Federal Credit Union is an industry leader who has built a reputation of innovation, strength, and stability. We pride ourselves on discovering and developing employees who have exceptional character and a genuine passion for helping others. In return, we deliver a comprehensive total rewards package that supports the financial, physical, and emotional wellbeing of our employees.

What We Offer:

SSFCU offers a comprehensive total rewards package. Benefit options include medical, dental and vision insurance; health savings and flexible spending accounts; company paid employee life insurance; supplemental life insurance plans; supplemental insurance plans for hospital and critical accident; short term disability; company paid long term disability; paid sick and safe leave, paid vacation, 401K match with immediate vesting, tuition reimbursement, employee tenure and award programs, access to an on-site fitness center or gym membership reimbursement program. Employees can participate in our award-winning Total Wellbeing program focusing on physical, financial and emotional wellbeing. We invest in our communities through our Volunteer Corps and in you, through ongoing growth and development opportunities",2022-01-13,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'spreadsheet', 'power_bi', 'visio', 'sql', 'vba', 'excel']"
28064,1258,Institutional Credit Management - Lending Data Analyst - Vice...,Citi,United States,"The Institutional Credit Management (ICM) group is looking for a Data Quality Analyst to join its Wholesale Lending Credit Risk (WLCR) data team. ICM has been established with the objective to provide an integrated end-to-end credit underwriting, identification, measurement, management and monitoring for the wholesale credit businesses across the enterprise. This is an exciting opportunity for an... experienced, action-oriented, highly motivated individual looking to thrive and build a career in a highly visible, challenging, dynamic, and growing team in a front-office division.

The WLCR Wholesale Lending data team within ICM is responsible for monitoring and resolving Wholesale Lending data quality issues, for owning data remediation efforts of known issues, and for owning 1st Line data quality reporting and detection.

Responsibilities:
• Build subject matter expertise on Citi's wholesale lending products and data architecture
• Assist the team in establishing operating standards and KPIs/metrics for the Data Quality program
• Draft business requirement documentation supporting effective data quality monitoring and measurement
• Navigate and manage complex data infrastructure supporting WLCR dependent processes including data analysis, modelling, and reporting requirements
• Assist the team in the implementation of data quality measurement methodologies and controls within the WLCR infrastructure
• Contribute to developing an operating model for data quality rules governance, implementation, and monitoring
• Prepare impact assessments of data quality issues and track the progress of systemic solutioning
• Perform analytical assessments of data quality concerns within credit risk systems which include multiple layers of enrichments and coded logic

Qualifications:
• 7+ years experience in a large financial institution
• Familiarity with loan products
• Familiarity with wholesale lending credit practices
• Intellectual curiosity, analytical, and conceptual thinker
• Proactively seeks and develops new opportunities
• Excellent analytical, interpretive, and problem-solving skills
• Demonstrated technical, diagnostic, and troubleshooting skills working with technology
• Excellent communication, motivational, and interpersonal skills
• Proficiency with Cognos, Tableau, and other data visualization tools/technologies

Education:
• Bachelor's/University degree

