28115,1309,Senior Data Analyst,GEHA,"Lee's Summit, MO","GEHA is a leader in health services for federal employees and related customers, serving our chosen markets with low-cost offerings and best-in-class customer care, sustained by a nimble and efficient organization.

An Executive Order was released stating that federal contractors must require COVID-19 vaccinations for all US employees. As a company that works on federal contracts, we have a legal... requirement to comply with the executive order, if it is enforced.

Within Analytics function this position is responsible for the development of analytical insights for all business units. Responsible for mentoring other Data Analysts. Serves as a lead liaison to business units for analytical support and is a super user of analytic solutions supported by the Analytics division. Requires expert level knowledge of enterprise accepted reporting, data and systems.

Please note that the salary information is a general guideline only. GEHA considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidates work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and business considerations when extending an offer.

The annual base salary range for this position is $78,539 - $109,961 USD.

SKILLS

Mentor for other Data Analysts that deliver analysis and insights in order to support all business functions and enterprise level initiatives.

Responsible for analytic request intake, prioritization and tracking.

Develops reports, data files and dashboards based on request requirements through direct interaction with business units.

Conducts research and analysis to provide insights and results back to business and senior management.

Expert level knowledge of enterprise accepted analytical and data sources in order to satisfy business requests and maximize efficiency. Responsible for working with manager to lead ongoing communication and planning with Data and Solutions teams within Analytics Division in order to fully support business functions.

Create new insightful metrics to help enterprise track and analyze data.

Foster team culture to promote strong documentation writing.

Requires a Bachelors degree in Healthcare, Business Administration, Computer Science, Statistics or a related discipline.

Requires six plus years of experience in Data Analytics or Data Management role (internally or at another company).

Prefer experience in healthcare.

Prefer experience managing staff

