28126,1320,Lead Finance Data Analyst,J&J Family of Companies,"Jefferson City, MO","Lead Finance Data Analyst - W

Description...

Johnson & Johnson Financial Solutions & Technology (FS&T) is recruiting for a Lead Finance Data Analyst, SigniFi EPM Business Architect, to develop the strategic FP&A technology solution architecture for the global enterprise. This role will be located in New Brunswick, NJ or other remote location in the US.

Caring for the world, one person at a time, has inspired and united the people of Johnson & Johnson for 125 years. We embrace research and science bringing innovative ideas, products and services to advance the health and well-being of people. Employees of the Johnson & Johnson Family of Companies work with partners in health care to touch the lives of over a billion people every day, throughout the world.

With more than $93 billion in 2021 sales, Johnson & Johnson is the world's most comprehensive and broadly-based manufacturer of health care products, as well as a provider of related services, for the consumer, pharmaceutical, and medical devices markets. There are more than 265 Johnson & Johnson operating companies employing approximately 132,200 people and with products touching the lives of over a billion people every day, throughout the world. If you have the talent and desire to touch the world, Johnson & Johnson has the career opportunities to help make it happen.

This position will provide financial data design support to Financial Reporting & Analytics. This team is focused on reshaping the way we work as a finance team for reporting, planning & analytics for JNJ Finance function. This position provides the opportunity to contribute to a highly visible and strategic enterprise initiative for the corporation. In addition, this role will provide the individual the opportunity to help shape global process transformation and efficiency within Enterprise FP&A.

Responsibilities
• Design and maintain the data model for enterprise EPM technology solution architecture for financial workstreams and lead data design team in Enterprise-wide initiatives.
• Partner closely across the SigniFi workstreams to drive coordinated solution designs and ensure end-to-end design objectives are met.
• Drive continuous improvement in Enterprise EPM/planning technology in support of the overall finance technology strategy.
• Collaborate with cross-functional business leaders, including IT to ensure tech solutions address business requirements and effectively enable finance stakeholder to deliver business insights.
• Govern SigniFi Common Information Model (CIM) design in Finance Data Hub Platform for Finance workstreams.
• Work with IT team as the Data Design Process Owner and to document change requests in support of product enhancements.
• Partner & integrate with the Data Governance team to help define data standards with extended CIM elements during the project and help define data quality matrix for extended CIM master data maintenance
Qualifications
• A minimum of a Bachelors Degree is required, Major in Finance or IT are preferred
• A minimum of 5 years of working experience is required
• A minimum of 3 years relational database management/data model/data warehouse experience is required
• Strong understanding of financial process knowledge is required
• SQL experience is required
• Strong technical systems background (Alteryx, SAP ERP (finance), Data Warehouse, MDM) or equivalent technologies is required
• Experience documenting best practices and enforcing strong governance in a team is required
• A commitment and passion for continuous integration, improvement, and using automation to ensure stable deliverables is required
• Strong Project Management Skills or experience leading implementations is preferred
• Experience supporting business partners within the Finance organization is preferred
• The position will be located in New Brunswick, NJ or remote at other US locations, and will require up to 10% travel
At Johnson & Johnson, were on a mission to change the trajectory of health for humanity. That starts by creating the worlds healthiest workforce. Through cutting-edge programs and policies, we empower the physical, mental, emotional, and financial health of our employees and the ones they love. As such, candidates offered employment must show proof of COVID-19 vaccination or secure an approved accommodation prior to the commencement of employment to support the well-being of our employees, their families and the communities in which we live and work.

For more information on how we support the whole health of our employees throughout their wellness, career and life journey, please visit .

Johnson & Johnson is an Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability.

Primary Location NA-US-New Jersey-New Brunswick

Other Locations NA-United States

Organization Johnson & Johnson Services Inc. (6090)

Job Function Finance

