28142,1336,CoxHealth Data Analyst - Infection Prevention Services,CoxHealth,"Springfield, MO","Summary
• Job Summary The Data Analyst is responsible for the daily activities related to collecting, storing, analyzing, and reporting data to support the Infection control program. This position supports the IP Facilitators in completing all required infection reporting, completes facility-wide reporting, and manages reporting of communicable diseases to the appropriate health department. The... program is designed to protect the overall health of patients, families, visitors, staff (paid or volunteer) and physicians who visit or work in one of our CoxHealth locations.
• Job Requirements Education Required: Associate Degree in a healthcare related field Preferred: Bachelor's degree in a Healthcare Related Field Experience Required: 2 years' experience with computer systems, program management, or statistics Preferred: Infection Prevention program analysis Skills Communication Data abstraction and Electronic Medical Record Navigation Data analysis and interpretation of microbiology laboratory results Public reporting systems Health care associated infection prevention Licensure/Certification/Registration Preferred: Certified Healthcare Data Analyst (CHDA) or Certified Infection Control (CIC)

Additional Information

Job Benefits & Perks!
• Tuition reimbursement up to $1200 per year
• Additional Educational Assistance programs available
• Health/Dental/Vision
• Retirement with employer match
• 20% tuition discount on most classes at Cox College
• On-site Daycare with extended hours, holidays and weekends
• Employee Discount at CoxHealth Fitness Centers
• Pharmacy delivery to your unit
• On-site Employee Health services
• Opportunity to earn referral bonuses of up to $5,000 per hire for certain positions
• 1906 Employee Store
• Cafeteria discount

If you would like more information about job benefits & perks, please feel free to email us @ hr-recruitment@ or visit",2022-07-05,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
