28146,1340,Problem Management Business Data Analyst Intern,Corporate,"Columbia, MO","You could be the one who changes everything for our 26 million members as an Intern at Centene. During this 12-week program, you'll learn more about Centene and how we're transforming the health of the community, one person at a time.

Position Purpose...
The main function of the Problem Management Business Data Analyst Role will be to support Centene Problem Management processes related to Incident and Problem data analysis and reporting. Typical daily duties include attending meetings and recording key takeaways, developing reports and presentations. The ideal candidate for this role will have a good blend of technical and soft skills, strong deductive reasoning capabilities, and communicate with a high degree of efficiency.

• Consult with various stakeholders and leadership to determine report requirements, design layout and format, identify and extract data
• Analyze and report on IT Problem and Incident data to identify trends and opportunities to help Senior Leaders evaluate current health and identify opportunities for improvement
• Continually work to expand upon and improve the efficiency and accuracy of all metrics reporting process and procedures related to Problem and Incident management
• Assist in coordination and compilation of data required for recurring and ad hoc reports
• Review, update, create process documentation related to the Problem practice and reporting
• Apply academic knowledge and learn new skills by contributing to various projects
• Research various legal, regulatory, and other topics within functional area and industry
• Attend training and development presentations to enhance professional competencies

Education/Experience:
High school diploma or equivalent. Must be enrolled in an undergraduate program at an accredited university or college, preferably in a field related to the hiring department through the internship period. Business, MIS, CIS, Data Analytics, Applied Math, Computer Science, or other related fields of study preferred.

Centene is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity, and values the ways in which we are different. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or other characteristic protected by applicable law",2022-04-05,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
28148,1342,Business Analyst III (Healthcare Analytics),Corporate,"Kansas City, MO","You could be the one who changes everything for our 26 million members. Centene is transforming the health of our communities, one person at a time. As a diversified, national organization, you'll have access to competitive benefits including a fresh perspective on workplace flexibility.

Position Purpose: Evaluate data and insights from extensive and integrated data sets to enable data-driven... decision making to reduce overall cost of care and improve clinical outcomes for members. Work collaboratively with key business stakeholders to identify areas of value, develop solutions, and deliver insights.

- Support business initiatives through data analysis, identification of implementation barriers, and development of documentation and project planning.
- Perform detailed analysis on assigned projects, recommend potential business solutions and assist with implementation
- Identify ways to enhance performance management and operational reports
- Support identification of and incorporate organizational best practices into business applications and processes
- Lead problem solving and coordination efforts between various business units
- Assist with formulating and updating departmental policies and procedures
- Serve as a subject matter expert on assigned functions, products, or analytic domains in support of strategic objectives
- Provide process and requirements guidance to junior analysts

Education/Experience
Bachelor's degree in business, economics, statistics, mathematics, actuarial science, public health, health informatics, healthcare administration, finance or related field or equivalent experience. Master's degree preferred. 4+ years of experience business process, data analysis, or requirements analysis. Healthcare, analytics delivery, project management, and/or IT experience preferred. Working knowledge of SQL/querying languages. Preferred knowledge of programmatic coding languages such as Python and R. Knowledge of basic statistical, analytical, or data mining techniques including basic data modeling, trend analysis, and root-cause analysis preferred. Ability to integrate, validate, and reconcile data from multiple sources as well as design and construct analysis tools that extract, prepare, analyze, and store/present results to support business needs. Preferred knowledge of modern business intelligence and visualization tools including Microsoft PowerBI. Direct Knowledge of FACETS system / Greenplum database a plus.

Our Comprehensive Benefits Package: Flexible work solutions including remote options, hybrid work schedules and dress flexibility, Competitive pay, Paid time off including holidays, Health insurance coverage for you and your dependents, 401(k) and stock purchase plans, Tuition reimbursement and best-in-class training and development.

Centene is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity, and values the ways in which we are different. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or other characteristic protected by applicable law",2022-01-11,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['power_bi', 'python']"
28152,1346,Senior Business Systems Analyst (Remote),EDWARD JONES,"Freeburg, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.
US Remote

Team Overview:
The Operational Data Product teams within Digital Product Management are looking for business analysts to join our delivery teams. Business Analysts will review, analyze and evaluate end-user needs as defined by strategic goals of the product team, along with querying and analyzing data, to create user stories and system specifications for Operational Data Stores (ODS) and/or Master Data Management (MDM) in partnership with our Data Stewards and Data Owners to align with the firms Data Governance policies.

What You'll Do:
• Create, maintain and review business process models, data flows, prototypes, business requirements, use cases and test cases.
• Perform data analysis that facilitates the transformation of complex data/information into actionable insights to support highly complex business processes using agile methodology.
• Execute and present written and verbal business systems impact analysis resulting in identification of new data solutions with moderate impact.
• Liaison between product team and stakeholders (data owners/stewards, other product teams, data governance) to proactively identify opportunities to create, maintain, enhance or integrate data usage by new and existing systems.
• Serve as a technical and functional data subject matter expert for multiple product epics at the same time.
• Understanding of cross divisional systems and impacts of change.
• Generate communication, process and educational plans to mitigate the disruption of change.
• Mentors less experienced members of the team.
What Experience You Need:
• Bachelor's degree or relevant experience required.
• 4 years experience designing and implementing functional systems and data in a structured process.
• Previous experience with Agile methodology (user storying creation and refinement, defining user acceptance criteria) and tools such as Jira, Aha
• Technical proficiency with tools to identify, collect and analyze data such as SQL Developer, Data Studio, or TOAD.
• Ability to document new and existing business process flows and research data definition to develop expertise or promote data usage efficiency.
• Ability to summarize moderate to highly complex business cases, system information and concepts and clearly and effectively communicate to cross divisional leadership using verbal, written and presentations skills.
• Advanced knowledge of standard Business System Analyst principles and practices.
• Associate must have the ability to work independently and in a team environment, multi-task and work with leader to prioritize assigned tasks/projects.
• Strong relationship management, interpersonal and negotiation skills.
• Advanced troubleshooting skills to investigate, resolve and escalate problems. Identifies need for technical assistance to help in problem resolution.
• Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office tools to provide working system prototypes and scenario modeling.
• Advanced understanding of evolving firm reporting technology platforms
