28167,1361,Workday Reporting/Data Analyst,Corporate,"Jefferson City, MO","You could be the one who changes everything for our 26 million members. Centene is transforming the health of our communities, one person at a time. As a diversified, national organization, you'll have access to competitive benefits including a fresh perspective on workplace flexibility. Position Purpose: Responsible for analytic data needs of the business unit. Handle complex data projects and... acts as a lead for other Data Analysts. Provide advanced analytical support for business operations within Workday and external reporting.
Extract, load, model, and reconcile large amounts of data across multiple system platforms and sources within Workday.
Review data to determine operational impacts and needed actions; elevate issues, trends, areas for improvement and opportunities to management.
Develop reports and deliverables and make recommendations to management
Model data using MS Excel
Assist management in driving business decisions based on data
Ensure compliance with federal and state deliverable reporting requirements by performing data quality audits and analysis.
Assist with training and mentoring other Data Analysts.
Assist with determining work load and related activities for other Data Analysts
• This position is offering a one time sign on bonus*

Education/Experience: Bachelor's degree in related field or equivalent experience. 6+ years of statistical analysis or data analysis experience. Workday experience Required. Workday Reporting, Prism Analytics and Integration knowledge. Modules: Core HCM, Recruit, Benefits and Comp are a plus to know. Healthcare experience preferred but not required. Advanced knowledge of Enterprise Reporting and Analysis within Workday and Microsoft Office applications, including Excel and Access. Experience managing projects or heavy involvement in project implementation.

Our Comprehensive Benefits Package: Flexible work solutions including remote options, hybrid work schedules and dress flexibility, Competitive pay, Paid time off including holidays, Health insurance coverage for you and your dependents, 401(k) and stock purchase plans, Tuition reimbursement and best-in-class training and development.

Centene is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity, and values the ways in which we are different. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or other characteristic protected by applicable law",2022-12-07,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['excel']
28171,1365,Senior Data Analyst Manager,Tyson Foods,"Springdale, AR","Job Details:

The Senior Data Analyst position requires knowledge of the biological, physical, and engineering sciences that make possible safe and wholesome food products; of food industry facilities, methods, processes, equipment capabilities and limitations; and of relevant laws, regulations, and governmental oversight. This position is responsible for involvement with the planning... development, implementation, and administration of systems for the acquisition, storage, and retrieval of data within the data-based applications and business systems for the internal/external users of the portfolio of the Product Development Management (PDM) systems used across the Enterprise. The Senior Data Analyst may also have responsibility for designing, developing, and implementing training materials including facilitator guides, participant guides, job aids, and computer-based training/learning options. The Senior Data Analyst operates as an internal consultant to IT project teams to provide analysis and definition of data requirements; development and administration of data standards; policies, and procedures; development and implementation of data mining programs; evaluation and recommendations on new database technologies; and ensuring the rigorous application of information security/information assurance policies, principles, and practices in the delivery of data management services. The Senior Data Analyst performs duties with wide latitude for the exercise of independent judgement to perform responsible work of considerable difficulty requiring somewhat extended professional and technical training and experience which has demonstrated important attainments and marked capacity for independent work. Additionally, the Data Manager needs to have knowledge of, and skill in, applying network principles and concepts; systems administration methods and procedures; customer support principles; IT security principles; troubleshooting methods; and utilize communication methods and techniques in providing guidance to our internal/external customers.

REQUIREMENTS:
Collaborate with IT staff and other technical staff to ensure that the delivered solution and/or system(s) meet the needs of the business.
Proactively analyze and resolve software, system, or application errors in a timely and accurate fashion.
Provide status reports as requested and escalate items to decision makers as needed.
Create and maintain documentation for systems and procedures related to the deliverables expectation.
Train customers and other team members on usage of systems and solutions.
Identify cross-functional opportunities to automate the execution of repeatable tasks and simplify system workflows.
Demonstrate problem-solving skills within area of responsibility and adjacent technology areas.
Build, maintain, and improve systems to support business processes.

EDUCATION:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD in related field of study. Equivalent work experience may be acceptable.

EXPERIENCE:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD with a minimum of 2 years relevant experience. No degree with a minimum of 4 years relevant experience.

COMPUTER SKILLS:
Requires strong PC skills including Microsoft Office, project management system(s), graphic management system(s) and all other web-based discipline specific systems.

COMMUNICATION SKILLS:
Requires robust collaboratory and relational ability to work cross-functionally across the Enterprise, with external customers, and consultants. Positive customer service and a team approach are required.

SPECIAL SKILLS (if applicable):
Critical thinking and problem-solving skills required. Strong time-management and organizational skills needed.

SUPERVISORY:
None

TRAVEL:
3+ Trips Per Year

Relocation Assistance Eligible:
Yes

Work Shift:

1ST SHIFT (United States of America)

Hourly Applicants ONLY -You must complete the task after submitting your application to provide additional information to be considered for employment.

Tyson is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, national origin, color, religion, age, genetics, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability or veteran status.

CCPA Notice. If you are a California resident, and would like to learn more about what categories of personal information we collect when you apply for this job, and how we may use that information, please read our CCPA Job Applicant Notice at Collection, click here ",2022-12-14,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
28172,1366,ERP Master Data Analyst,LUFKIN INDUSTRIES,"Claremore, OK","Job Purpose

Responsible for the Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) master data for the organization related to planning, procurement, inventory management. Ensure all master data hierarchies are properly associated. Provide accurate and useful information to assist management in decision-making through understanding master data interdependencies and how master data is leveraged to drive business... processes and support our business relationships. Collaborate with internal departments to improve processes and identify opportunities for innovation that utilize master data and other business information.

Key Accountabilities
• Provide support for the Sourcing (S2P) to Pay process, MRP Planning and Master Data Management as directed
• Understand the system impacts of hierarchy structures to support business processes, facilitate automation opportunities, data analysis and maintenance
• Identify, research and prioritize master data additions and modifications that impact business performance and processes
• Collaborates with Planning, Procurement, Engineering, Manufacturing and Product Line teams to understand ERP data requirements and ensure process are clearly defined
• Gatekeeper for the Item Master module in JDE/ERP System
• Ongoing JDE data governance review for accuracy and consistency including but not limited to Commodity Codes, HTS Codes, Product Family and Cost Coding.
• Conduct training for employees as needed/directed by Supply Chain Systems & Process Manager.
• Assist in JDE systems rollout to new business units.
• Support for internal and external audits (ISO, API, SOX, etc) as directed. • Other duties as required.
Required Education & Preferred Certifications
• At least 5 years of experience within the function in a manufacturing setting
• Bachelor's degree or equivalent work experience
Required Knowledge / Skills
• Knowledge of forecasting and planning processes
• Strong oral and written communication skills.
• Strong analytical, organizational, and interpersonal skills.
• Ability to coordinate several projects simultaneously.
• Performs duties with the highest degree of accuracy
• Ability to work under pressure in a fast-paced environment
• Able to accept precise direction and work in a closely managed relationship
• Flexible/able to work additional hours when needed
• Technically proficient with all MS Office Suite Applications; ERP System (JDE preferred), Power BI or ReportsNow.
Lufkin's proud past extends back to the early 20th century when the Lufkin Foundry manufactured railroad and sawmill equipment. The company expanded soon after by pioneering oilfield pumping units in the 1920s. Today, Lufkin is a world leader in its field, providing precision-engineered oilfield equipment, products, and services to customers around the globe.

Lufkin Industries is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law",2022-03-17,Full-time,data analyst,United States,['power_bi']
28173,1367,Data Analytics Engineer,EDWARD JONES,"St Thomas, MO","At Edward Jones, we help clients achieve their serious, long-term financial goals by understanding their needs and implementing tailored solutions. To ensure a personal client experience, we have located our 15,000+ branch offices where our more than 7 million clients live and work.

In a typical branch office, a financial advisor meets with clients and receives branch office support, so they can... focus on building deep relationships with clients. Headquarters associates in St. Louis, Tempe and Mississauga provide support and expertise to help U.S. and Canada branch teams deliver an ideal client experience. We continue to grow to meet the needs of long-term individual investors.
Team Overview:

We are currently seeking a Data Analytics Engineer to join our rapidly growing Mobile Center of Excellence (MCOE). The Data Analytics Engineer will be focused on partnering and collaborating with our product teams responsible for developing and delivering mobile apps to our client and branch teams.

The successful candidate will have proven experience in collaborating with product owners, business analyst and UX researchers to identify and define events to tag and track using analytics tools and platforms (i.e., Google Analytics, Firebase, Pendo Mobile, Data Studio, Tableau).

The Data Analytics Engineer will build dataset representations that allow the mobile product teams to understand and evaluate user behavior and interaction data captured. They will use a combination of business strategy and technical data knowledge to translate complex information into clear and helpful visual analytics dashboards displaying key metrics to support business decisions related to product development, delivery, and adoption strategies to deliver great mobile user experiences.

What You'll Do:
• Maintain a strong understanding of division results and key business drivers, as well as an understanding of key business strategies and priorities, apply business knowledge to analytic approach to address business questions
• Build and maintain a strong knowledge of data sets available to the analyst. Extract, cleanse and transform data to support analysis needs. Pressure test and validate logic and outputs against known sources and business acumen. Proactively identify data quality issues.
• Provide actionable insights to support business decisions, primarily by performing root cause, exploratory, sensitivity and scenario analysis, hypothesis testing, economic modeling, and data visualization to identify patterns, trends, and insights etc. on ambiguous business problems.
• Independently generate and incorporate insights into a cohesive story that clearly addresses product team questions. Effectively communicate with product teams, 3 rd party partners and non-technical audiences regarding analytic ideas, approach, key takeaways, and actionable insights.
• Develop and manage business relationships with project team members and leaders across the organization. Consult with product and portfolio owners to identify opportunities for leveraging data & analytics to drive business outcomes.
• Document, monitor, and proactively recommend improvements to processes and controls related to areas of responsibility.
• Lead the development and monitoring of KPIs and benchmarks. Must be able to communicate results to senior leaders.
• Prioritize and execute multiple tasks/projects and adjust to changing priorities.
• Communication: Communicate with product owners, business analysts, UX researchers and designers, and key executives through both verbal communication and visual representations.
What You'll Need:
• Bachelor's Degree with an emphasis in business, economics, math, engineering, or analytics preferred or 5 years+ business experience in marketing, finance, data analytics, or relevant field.
• Strong analytical, critical, and systems thinking.
• Requires conceptual knowledge of theories, practices, and procedures within a job discipline.
• Requires expanded conceptual knowledge in own job discipline and broadens capabilities.
• Data analysis: Require an understanding of data analysis principles and formulas. Possess data analysis skills to create effective, accurate and concise models that communicate the information and meaning of a dataset.
• Data engineering: Ability to develop software that collects, sorts and structures data. Uses these ideas and skills to create efficient software to display and communicate complex data.
• Data modeling: Experience creating data models to generate accurate models and communicate effectively through visual representations.
• Tools: Use data analytics tools and platforms to capture and create visual dashboards and reports on mobile user behaviors and interactions.
What Will Set You Apart:
• Previous analytical related experience is preferred. Financial services industry experience is a plus
• Advanced Degree or Certification preferred
• Experience with Google Analytics - GA-4
• Experience with Data Studio
• Experience with Mobile Applications
• Experience with Tableau
