28222,1416,Data Analyst - Target Marketing at Microsoft - 18 Month Contract...,Inviso,United States,"Are you an experienced Data Analyst ready to partner with the Global Demand Center (GDC) marketing team to direct how Microsoft competes globally? Cloud technologies have disrupted the marketplace and are now part of a fast-paced, exciting industry. This is your opportunity to be at the center of the action and make an impact as a Targeting Strategy and Operations analyst with Microsoft's Account... Based Marketing team.

As a Data/Process Analyst, you will have the opportunity to collaborate with partners across the marketing ecosystem to drive the insights that refine and evolve ABM marketing programs. You possess the technical and analytical capability to work with the data as well as the attention to detail to ensure accuracy and completeness in the operational aspects of this role. You are eager to learn more about the operational aspects of marketing from both the business and technical perspectives.

Job responsibilities will include:

Working with business stakeholders to define targeting requirements for marketing campaigns
Using a variety of tools and dashboards to pull data and prepare market sizing analyses
Creating target lists and managing processes for distributing to appropriate stakeholders
Acting as an interface between business stakeholders and BI teams to supply business requirements
Collaborating with stakeholders to re-design operational processes to reduce manual steps
Creating documentation and helping socializing process changes

Required Skills - Must have all of the following:

Experience in analysis or finance supporting sales or marketing, marketing technology management, or marketing business management
Ability to work in a fast paced, constantly changing environment.
Must have experience and strength in working with business stakeholders to ask the right questions, be customer facing and be able to talk with both technical and non-technical audiences, able to track down who has the data or the answer needed.
Experience coordinating and working with data engineering teams
Extremely strong collaboration, communication, and follow-through skills
Motivated, highly entrepreneurial, and comfortable with ambiguity in a dynamic environment
Must have experience documenting processes to enhance the team's value in the organization

Technical requirements:

Power user / very advanced with Excel and Power Pivot.
Comfortable with either Power BI or SQL.
Experience working with very large (several million rows) data sets, able to manipulate, extract and analyze data.

Desired Skills - not required, but very helpful

Experience with marketing campaign / customer analytics and intelligent targeting
Azure Synapse. modeling, and Starlight
Experience as a Technical Project Manager, planning, managing stakeholders, milestones, status reporting, and process documentation
Writing SQL queries, doing analysis, writing reports, generating data and seeing the problems with the data
Experience with account-based marketing and/or marketing campaign analytics / datasets.
Understanding Marketo data, and/or GDCs use of that data
Dynamics, BizApps, Modern Workplace or Azure marketing experience at Microsoft
Business analysis and reporting experience within Microsoft (Microsoft work experience)

ABOUT INVISO: Inviso is a premier consulting firm that delivers business solutions through Software Asset Management (SAM), Office 365 and Azure (Cloud), Modern App Dev and Business Intelligence, Staffing, and Marketing. We are an entrepreneurial, agile organization with a broad range of business experience and talents, and a laser focus on adding value to our customers. With headquarters in Seattle and additional locations around the world, we assist hundreds of customers across the globe",2022-06-04,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['sql', 'excel', 'azure', 'power_bi']"
