28306,1500,Business Analyst Financial Planning and Analysis VA Remote,Beacon Building Products,United States,"Job purpose

This technical role on the Corporate Business Analytics FP&A team will help create complex data models, algorithms, and dashboards to be used companywide to support our data-informed strategy. This role will leverage millions of data points across dozens of sources to deliver new insights to our business leaders. This role will focus mostly on sales reporting and insights...

The ideal candidate would have direct experience building complex data models within Tableau Prep, Desktop and producing relevant dashboards. While focused on sales primarily this role will also support the entire analytics team. To succeed in this role a candidate should be highly versatile, curious, and experienced with using data analysis tools to answer business questions.

Duties And Responsibilities
• Translate business requirements into data models, dashboards, and diagnostic tools for leadership consumption
• Create data models that join disparate data sources for relevant KPIs and dashboards
• Support the larger business analytics team from a technical development spanning sales, purchasing, inventory, pricing, and marketing analytics
• Partner with business stakeholders to develop and implement relevant KPIs
• Build demand planning / predictive sales models using Machine Learning (ML) and Artificial Intelligence (AI)
• Apply various data analysis techniques such as regression, Monte Carlo simulation, factor, cohort, cluster, time series, and sentiment analysis to drive insights
• Act as a subject matter expert to help upskill existing workforce and expand data fluency
• Prepare monthly / quarterly data sets as needed to support external business reporting
• Participate in special projects as requested

Qualifications
• Bachelor of Science degree in computer science, business, finance, statistics, analytics, or related field
• Minimum 3+ years of experience working in data science and / or analytics
• Strong analytical skillset and technical experience with Tableau mandatory
• Familiarity or direct experience with Alteryx, SQL, Python, or R preferred
• Hands on experience building and validating data models
• High degree of self-initiative and curiosity to answer leadership questions
• Ability to be a collaborative business partner and cultivate strong cross-functional relationships
• Experience within a commercial / retail (B2B or B2C) enterprise a plus

Working conditions
• Minimal travel requirements as needed for business purposes
• Work assignments may be completed remotely and/or available company offices within respective markets

Physical Requirements
• Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer and/or keyboard
• Heavy methods of verbal and auditory communication via phone, virtual calls, and/or email",2022-05-16,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'sql', 'r', 'alteryx', 'python']"
28307,1501,Senior Data Analyst (Manager),Tyson Foods,"Springdale, AR","Job Details:

The Senior Data Analyst position requires knowledge of the biological, physical, and engineering sciences that make possible safe and wholesome food products; of food industry facilities, methods, processes, equipment capabilities and limitations; and of relevant laws, regulations, and governmental oversight. This position is responsible for involvement with the planning... development, implementation, and administration of systems for the acquisition, storage, and retrieval of data within the data-based applications and business systems for the internal/external users of the portfolio of the Product Development Management (PDM) systems used across the Enterprise. The Senior Data Analyst may also have responsibility for designing, developing, and implementing training materials including facilitator guides, participant guides, job aids, and computer-based training/learning options. The Senior Data Analyst operates as an internal consultant to IT project teams to provide analysis and definition of data requirements; development and administration of data standards; policies, and procedures; development and implementation of data mining programs; evaluation and recommendations on new database technologies; and ensuring the rigorous application of information security/information assurance policies, principles, and practices in the delivery of data management services. The Senior Data Analyst performs duties with wide latitude for the exercise of independent judgement to perform responsible work of considerable difficulty requiring somewhat extended professional and technical training and experience which has demonstrated important attainments and marked capacity for independent work. Additionally, the Data Manager needs to have knowledge of, and skill in, applying network principles and concepts; systems administration methods and procedures; customer support principles; IT security principles; troubleshooting methods; and utilize communication methods and techniques in providing guidance to our internal/external customers.

REQUIREMENTS:
Collaborate with IT staff and other technical staff to ensure that the delivered solution and/or system(s) meet the needs of the business.
Proactively analyze and resolve software, system, or application errors in a timely and accurate fashion.
Provide status reports as requested and escalate items to decision makers as needed.
Create and maintain documentation for systems and procedures related to the deliverables expectation.
Train customers and other team members on usage of systems and solutions.
Identify cross-functional opportunities to automate the execution of repeatable tasks and simplify system workflows.
Demonstrate problem-solving skills within area of responsibility and adjacent technology areas.
Build, maintain, and improve systems to support business processes.

EDUCATION:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD in related field of study. Equivalent work experience may be acceptable.

EXPERIENCE:
Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD with a minimum of 2 years relevant experience. No degree with a minimum of 4 years relevant experience.

COMPUTER SKILLS:
Requires strong PC skills including Microsoft Office, project management system(s), graphic management system(s) and all other web-based discipline specific systems.

COMMUNICATION SKILLS:
Requires robust collaboratory and relational ability to work cross-functionally across the Enterprise, with external customers, and consultants. Positive customer service and a team approach are required.

SPECIAL SKILLS (if applicable):
Critical thinking and problem-solving skills required. Strong time-management and organizational skills needed.

SUPERVISORY:
None

TRAVEL:
3+ Trips Per Year

Relocation Assistance Eligible:
Yes

Work Shift:

1ST SHIFT (United States of America)

Hourly Applicants ONLY -You must complete the task after submitting your application to provide additional information to be considered for employment.

Tyson is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, national origin, color, religion, age, genetics, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability or veteran status.

CCPA Notice. If you are a California resident, and would like to learn more about what categories of personal information we collect when you apply for this job, and how we may use that information, please read our CCPA Job Applicant Notice at Collection, click here ",2022-12-23,Full-time,data analyst,United States,[]
28314,1508,Business Intelligence Analyst NOT REMOTE,Security Service Federal Credit Union,"Kansas City, MO","What You Will Do:

Supports the design, implementation, operation, and maintenance of data and analytical pipelines for the Payment Services operational, executive, and control/monitoring dashboards. Monitors, tracks, and reports on Payment Services organizational statistics, including daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly and yearly KPIs. Applies data mining and statistical methods on data sets to... extract actionable insights. Creates easy to understand visualizations to communicate information extracted from data to support all departments operational requirements in Payment Services. Performs ad-hoc data analysis per business user's request. Understands and maintains multiple data sources and streamlines the reporting process. Produces and distributes a variety of dashboards and other reports to payment services leadership and executive teams which reflect current and historical volume. Identify opportunities to create and enhance the reporting of the control and monitoring process dashboards and efficiency measures. Develop tracking tools, enhance spreadsheet and database functionality. Creates forms, templates, logic functions and macros in support of the data collection efforts to capture operational data points from all back-office teams in Payment Services. Helps develop, gather, and document basic technical data for the departments reporting processes. Communicates critical information to internal and external customers in compliance with clearly defined requirements. Provide analytical and research support for company projects and objectives as directed by management. Research, develop, and implement a coordinated data and reporting strategy to ensure regulatory adherence for the Payment Services Departments internal and external control monitoring process. Implements controls and monitoring processes to identify risks and issues within workflows and conducts periodic auditing of all Payment Services workflows and update accordingly. Establish, develops and maintains departmental policy and procedures documents for controls and monitoring. Completes any other job-related duties needed to help drive to our Vision, fulfill our Purpose, and abide by our Organization's Values.

Our Core Values:

All employees should demonstrate our SSFCU core values -- Caring, Innovative, Honest, Fair and Dedicated -- while providing enthusiastic, professional, and courteous service to SSFCU members and employees.

Additional Information:

We are an EEO Employer that provides equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, color, age, religion, protected veteran or disability status, or genetic information.

What We Require:

Bachelor's degree in business administration, finance, accounting, economics, computer science or equivalent education and/or experience. Minimum of five (5) years in the financial services industry. Must be experienced and proficient in Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Visio, Access and VBA. Demonstrate working knowledge of pivot tables, string functions, lookups, macro development, and code development in VBA. Experience in participating in multiple projects and ability to work with minimal supervision showing creativity, innovation, motivation, initiative and professionalism. Experience compiling large volumes of data into usable formats. Excellent time management and organizational skills. Experience with Data Analysis and Visualization of Power BI Dashboards. Experience with data integration of Power BI with external data sets and systems. Strong SQL Skills (complex queries on relational databases, stored procedures, automation)

Ideal Candidate Will Have:

Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills. Knowledge of federal regulations including but not limited to Regulations E, Z, CC, J, AA, UCC article 4, NACHA rules/regulations as well as Monarch experience and use of Fidelity applications. Outstanding leadership, teamwork, inter-personal, facilitation, organizational, process, listening and communication skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines. Ability to utilize business process, data management and information systems skills to create, design and implement tools that improve workforce effectiveness and management decision making. Exceptional knowledge of Advanced Excel and VBA Macros. Expert understanding of Power BI, or Tableau. Ability to write and execute data analysis expressions, queries and functions in Power BI. Advanced knowledge of databases, statistics, and data mining.

Who We Are:

Security Service Federal Credit Union is an industry leader who has built a reputation of innovation, strength, and stability. We pride ourselves on discovering and developing employees who have exceptional character and a genuine passion for helping others. In return, we deliver a comprehensive total rewards package that supports the financial, physical, and emotional wellbeing of our employees.

What We Offer:

SSFCU offers a comprehensive total rewards package. Benefit options include medical, dental and vision insurance; health savings and flexible spending accounts; company paid employee life insurance; supplemental life insurance plans; supplemental insurance plans for hospital and critical accident; short term disability; company paid long term disability; paid sick and safe leave, paid vacation, 401K match with immediate vesting, tuition reimbursement, employee tenure and award programs, access to an on-site fitness center or gym membership reimbursement program. Employees can participate in our award-winning Total Wellbeing program focusing on physical, financial and emotional wellbeing. We invest in our communities through our Volunteer Corps and in you, through ongoing growth and development opportunities",2022-12-07,Full-time,data analyst,United States,"['tableau', 'spreadsheet', 'power_bi', 'visio', 'sql', 'vba', 'excel']"
